  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Construction of 500 Housing Units at Dematagoda under Resettlement Programme  (Phase II) Award of the Contract for Piling Work",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3830",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- under the Environmental Improvement Programme of the Beira Lake Restoration Project about 1000 families in unauthorized occupation  were identified for relocation and with this in view,  the Government commenced a 1000 Housing Units Programme at Dematagoda in 2009.  Under Phase I of the project, construction of 320 Housing Units has been completed in December 2009 and they have been allocated to occupants of underserved settlements in the Slave Island area. \r\n\r\n\tUnder Phase II of the Project, it is proposed to construct 500 Housing Units in two, ten storeyed buildings at Dematagoda. On a proposal made by H.E. the President, on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC) which evaluated the Bids, Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract for piling works of these 500 Housing Units at Dematagoda for the cost of Rs.198.88 million. The project is to be funded by the Urban Development Authority."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Census of Population and Housing - 2011 to cover the entire Island after 30 years - Department of Census and Statistics",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3831",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- On the basis of a Memorandum submitted by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval has already been granted to hold the 14th Census of Population and Housing in the year 2011 and the Director General of Census and Statistics has been directed to make necessary arrangements for same.   The main feature and importance of this census is that it will be the first time since the census of population and housing held in 1981, that a census is being held to cover the entire Island, including the Northern and Eastern Provinces after 30 years.  Modern technology is to be utilized for the compilation of data for the first time and Cabinet approval was granted for same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Establishment of a Minimum Criteria for Procurement of Liquid Milk from Dairy Farmers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3832",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by the Minister of Livestock and Rural Community Development Hon. Arumugan Thondaman in keeping with the Budget Proposals for 2011, Cabinet approval was granted to increase the minimum purchase price of fresh milk at farm gate to Rs.50/- per ltr. to promote milk production.  The country has reached 35% self-reliance in local milk production and it is envisaged to become self sufficient in 2016, thereby saving a considerable amount of foreign exchange spent for the importation of milk powder."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Removing of all Duty Levies on Importation of Dairy Animals for Breeding purposes and Dairy Equipment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3833",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Government has observed that a well planned programme is essential to increase the number of high yielding cattle population to upgrade the country's milk production level.  The country needs to have additional 100,000 high yielding cows to be reared under intensive farming, for it to increase milk production and achieve self sufficiency.  The Import Duty and VAT have already been removed on importation of dairy animals for breeding purposes and also for dairy equipment.  Cabinet approval was granted for the removal of the Port and Airport Development Tax (5%) and Nation Building Tax (2%) on such imports."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Water Supply Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3834",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- II (JICA Loan No.SL-P 93) Kalu Ganga Water Supply Project [Phase I Stage II] Tender for Laying of  PVC Pipes, Fittings, Specials and DI Valves and Accessories for the Distribution Systems in Kesbewa East / West, Jamburaliya and Piliyandala - Miriswatte Areas  - this project has already been approved by the Cabinet for implementation.  Stage II of this project will meet the demand for pipe borne water for the people in the areas of Kesbewa, Borelesgamuwa, Gonapola, Kahapola, Polgasowita, Ingiriya, Handapangoda, Diyagama, Piliyandala, Panadura East and Magammana.  This will serve a population of about 49,000 in these areas by 2012. The project is being funded by the Japanese Government through Japan  International Cooporation Agency (JICA).  On a proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply and Drainage Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena, Cabinet approval was granted to award the tender for the laying of PVC Pipes, Fittings, Specials to M/s. Isuru-PND Joint Venture, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee consisting of 3 Secretaries of Ministries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Procurement of 02 Nos. of 31.5 MVA, 132/33 KV Power Transformers Vavuniya Grid Substation Augmentation Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3835",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bid No.TRP/PM/VGSP/10/01 - Cabinet approval was granted to a proposal by the Minister of Power and Energy Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, based on the recommendation made by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, to procure the transformers required for this project from the successful bidder M/s. Tirathai Public Company Limited of Thailand at a cost of US$ 890,000.00 and LKR 2,200,000.00. \r\n\r\n   \tImprovement of Infrastructure Facilities in Universities  - Minister of Higher Education Hon. S.B. Dissanayake submitted 4 proposals to construct new buildings and to expand the infrastructure facilities in Universities and the Cabinet decided to request the Chairman, University Grants Commission to submit a comprehensive Medium Term Programme for the improvement / enhancement of infrastructure facilities of the Universities for the next 10 years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-01-05",
    "description": "Completion of the rapid programme for establishing one thousand (1000) fully equipped secondary schools within a period of 04 years",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3836",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal made by the Minister of Education Hon. Bandula Gunawardena to implement a National Programme for establishing 1000 fully equipped secondary schools was approved by the Cabinet. Funds have already been received from the Asian Development Bank for the development of 100 such schools. The contract for planning and supervision is to be awarded to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB) and construction work will be awarded on Open Competitive Bidding basis. Medium and Small Scale contractors in the locality / respective provinces will be given preference in this process."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Establishment of National School of Business Management",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3837",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- the National Institute of Business Management (NIBM) is a self financing institute providing education, training and consultancy services for the public and private sectors in Sri Lanka.  At present it admits around 3000 students per intake and trains more than 10,000 students annually.  This institute has been granted Degree Awarding Status by the University Grants Commission in 2009. On a proposal made by the Minister of Youth Affairs and Skills Development, Hon. Dullas Alahapperuma, Cabinet approval was granted in principle for the establishment of a Business School affiliated to NIBM in the name of National School of Business Management.  A 50 acre block of land in Pitipana, Homagama owned by the Urban Development Authority (UDA) has been identified to set up this National School.  Detail proposals on this project will be submitted by the Ministry of Higher Education to the General Treasury for evaluation in the first instance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Bid for Hosting the Proposed Commonwealth Games 2018 to be held at Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3838",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Government intends to act as the host country to hold the Commonwealth Games - 2018 and it proposes to select Hambantota as the venue.  On a proposal made by the Minister of Sports, Hon. Mahindananda Aluthgamage, Cabinet approval was granted to proceed with the initial measures taken on this matter."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Conservation Neelagiri Maha Seya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3839",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Neelagiri Maha Seya is situated in the Lahugala forest reserve in the Ampara District in the Eastern Province.  It has been identified as the largest Stupa in the East.  Even though this place is of immense religious and archaeological importance, no development activities have taken place for the last 30 years due to terrorist activities which prevailed in the area.  Since the area has now been cleared of external threats, on a proposal made by the Minister of National Heritage, Hon. (Dr.) Jagath Balasuriya, Cabinet approval was granted in principle for the rehabilitation work in the area and to open Neelagiri Maha Seya to the general public as an archeological site in the near future.  Initial expenditure for rehabilitation work will be met from the financial provision allocated to the Department of Archeology for the year 2011 and the balance will be provided by the Government through the Medium Term Budgetary Framework 2012 - 2014."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Development of Hambantota and Nuwara Eliya  District General Hospitals under the Netherlands Assistance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3840",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Government of the Netherlands has pledged the Government of Sri Lanka concessionary financial assistance through the Rabobank International of the Netherlands for the construction of two new hospitals at identified locations in Hambantota and Nuwara Eliya, including the supply of necessary medical and other equipment, installation, training etc.  The proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC) and the Project Committee (PC), to award the contract to a construction company in Netherlands for a total cost of Euro 86.49 million and to enter into a loan agreement with the Government of the Netherlands to execute the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Development of Mahagama Silica Quartz Deposit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3841",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Vein Quartz or Silica Quartz, as known commercially, is a mineral commodity found in Sri Lanka.  Limited quantities of high purity (more than 97%) Vein Quartz Deposits are scattered in various parts of the country.  This mineral is being used in high-tech industries such as manufacturing of crystal tableware, laboratory glassware and high-end camera lenses etc. Cabinet approval was granted in principle for the proposal made by the Minister of Environment Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, for the development of Vein Quartz Deposit in Mahagama, as it would encourage foreign investment and provide employment opportunities domestically for nearly 600 persons.  A detailed project proposal for the purpose will be submitted by the Ministry of Environment to the General Treasury for evaluation."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Purchase of Soya Beans for Thriposha Production",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3842",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Management of the Thriposha Project which was handled by the Ceylon Tobacco Company up to 31.12.2010, is now being handled by the Government Owned Company registered as Sri Lanka Thriposha Limited.  On a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Cabinet approval was granted for the purchase of the requirement of Soya Beans for Thriposha production from the earlier suppliers at the rate of Rs.95/- per kilo, subject to the conditions stipulated by the General Treasury, failing which, to purchase the total stock of 1557 Mt of Soya Beans presently with the Paddy Marketing Board, at Rs.95/- per kilo."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Deyata Kirula Exhibition 2011 - Supply of Water",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3843",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- parallel to the Deyata Kirula Exhibition, action is being taken by the Department of National Water Supply and Drainage, on a proposal by the Minister of Water Supply and Drainage, Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena, to upgrade the Buttala Water Supply Scheme and work in connection with same is in progress.  A number of roads in the Moneragala District are being widened and resurfaced and since the existing pipe network falls under the carriageway, Cabinet approval was granted to relocate the pipe lines away from the carriageway.  The total cost of the project is Rs.175 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Tender for the Supply of 140,000 Vials of Rabies Vaccine",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3844",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Worldwide Tenders were called to purchase this vaccine and on the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, Cabinet approval was granted to award the above procurement to the lowest responsive bidder M/s. Sanofi Pasterur S A of France, at a total cost of US $861, 000.00.   Cabinet also decided that the Ministry of Health should take action to develop a mechanism in consultation with Local Authorities to reduce the menace of  stray dogs."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding concluded with the Great Socialist People?s Libyan Arab Jamahiriya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3845",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka and Libya being pioneers of the Non-Aligned Movement have closely cooperated within the moment.  Sri Lanka has been the largest black tea supplier to Libya with a market share of over 90% of total tea imports to that country.  H.E. the President visited Libya in April 2009, which was the first by a Sri Lankan Head and the Libyan Leader agreed to provide US $500 million as a financial cooperation package for the development projects in Sri Lanka, including development works in Hambantota and Northern and Eastern Provinces.  On a proposal made by the Minister of External Affairs,  Hon. (Prof) G.L. Peiris, covering approval of the Cabinet of Ministers was granted for three Memoranda of Understanding signed between the two countries, during the visit of H.E. President in 2009, which will further enhance cooperation in economic, technical and cultural fields in both countries."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "CATIC Grant Skyline Hotel and Rainbow Multifunction Complex in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3846",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- China National Aero Technology Import and Export Corporation (CATIC) intends to purchase about 7 acres of land around Galle Face Green area, close to the land already assigned for Shangri-La Hotels Lanka (Pvt) Ltd., to build a multifunction complex comprising a five star hotel and a shopping mall.  The total investment on this project will be nearly US $500 million.  The proposal made by the Minister of Economic Development,  Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, to proceed with the project proposal, was approved by the Cabinet.  The planned development in this area has already attracted another investment of around US $500 million from Shangri-La Hotels Lanka (Pvt) Ltd., which proposes to built a 500 room hotel, residencies and shopping complex to be completed by 2013.  The total foreign investment on these two projects will be  around 1000 million and would assist developing Colombo as a Middle Income Commercial City and also to accommodate nearly 2.5 million tourists expected by 2016."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-12-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-01-12",
    "description": "Recent Floods",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3847",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Cabinet also discussed in detailed the recent floods which affected many parts of the Island, including the Central Province, North Central Province and Northern and the Eastern Provinces. The Minister of Disaster Management, Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, briefed the Cabinet on the immediate measures taken to provide relief to the victims, on the direction of H.E. the President.  Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena and the Minister of Justice, Hon. Rauff Hakeem, extended gratitude to H.E. the President for the speedy steps taken to provide relief to victims in the flood affected areas of the country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-20-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-01-20",
    "description": "Annual Blood Donation Programme - 2011",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3848",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- a large quantity of blood is required daily for hospitals throughout the country depending on the requirements of patients.  The Blood Bank receives around 1370 pints of blood per day from the donors through its 82 branches located throughout the Island with the National Blood Transfusion Centre at Narahenpita as its Coordinating Centre.  Almost the same quantity of blood is issued to patients daily.  With the view to streamlining the process, on a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Cabinet approval was granted to implement a planned programme for blood donation commencing in 2011 to get the participation of all Government Institutions and Statutory Bodies in this campaign."
  },
