    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Strengthening the Health Care System in Northern Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3858",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Northern Province  consists of 5 Districts namely, Jaffna, Mannar, Vavuniya, Kilinochchi and Mullaitivu.  The majority of the population is Sri Lankan Tamils and this population was heavily affected by terrorist activities which prevailed for a period of nearly 30 years and as a result most of the health institutions in the Districts were damaged.  Since the commencement of the re-settlement process in the Northern Province, many development activities in healthcare institutions have been carried out with donor assistance.  On  a proposal made by the Minister of Health, Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, for the improvement of facilities and renovation work in hospitals in these Districts, Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has pledged its assistance in a sum of Rs.150 million, for the following: \r\n\t* Construction of Regional Training Centre, Jaffna    - cost  Rs.50.0 million. \r\n\t* Provision of Medical Equipment to the Intensive Care Unit at District General Hospital,Kilinochchi - cost Rs.25.0 million. \r\n\t* Construction of Nursing Quarters at District General Hospital, Kilinochchi - cost Rs.45.0 million. \r\n\t* Construction of Blood Bank at District General Hospital, Vavuniya - cost Rs.30.0 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-01-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-01-25",
    "description": "Development Project for the South Eastern University of Sri Lanka - Phase I - B",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-01-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kuwait Fund for Arab Economic Development has agreed to provide a loan of  Kuwait Dinars 3 million (approximately US $10.5 million to finance the implementation of the above project. The objective of this project is to develop essential academic infrastructure and introduce new demand driven degree programmes to meet  the national needs of the country. The project consists of 2 phases, namely, phase I - A  and Phase 1 - B costing US$ 7.0 million and 12.0 million respectively. Phase 1 - A is now being implemented and of the total cost of phase 1 - B, US $10.5 million will be financed by the Kuwait fund and the balance of US $1.5 million will be borne by the Government of Sri Lanka. The proceeds of the loan will be utilized to complete construction of buildings for the Faculties, Student hostels and for the  development of infrastructure facilities such as roads, water supply, electricity, sewerage and waste management system and supply of furniture and educational equipment."
  },
  {
