    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Financing and Rehabilitation of the Road Section from Dambulla to Habarana on Ambepussa - Kurunegala - Trincomalee (A6) Road by International Construction Consortium (Pvt) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3880",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- the Habarana - Kantale (44 Km) road section of the Ambepussa - Kurunegala - Trincomalee (A6) Road has been recently rehabilitated under Asian Development Bank Funding.  The road section from Ambepussa to Dambulla (91 Km) on (A6) road has been earmarked for rehabilitation and improvement under World Bank Funding.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, on the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Review Committee, Cabinet approval was granted to award the contract for rehabilitation of the remaining section of the road from Dambulla to Habarana (21.5 km), to the above Construction Consortium.  The rehabilitation of this section of the road will facilitate easy access to tourist destinations in the East Coast."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-02-09",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of National Highways with Concrete Surfacing through Domestic Contractors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3881",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- since it has been observed that concrete roads are more durable and require less maintenance than the roads constructed with bitumen, it has been decided that rehabilitation / construction of roads and highways in future should be with concrete surfacing where it is viable.  Accordingly, the Road Development Authority has selected 600 Km of highways for rehabilitation through domestic contractors, as a pilot project.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to call for technical and financial proposals from eligible domestic contractors for rehabilitation of roads by using concrete surfacing and for appointment of a Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC) and Project Committee (PC) to evaluate the proposals submitted."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
