    "description": "Damages to the Water Supply Schemes by Recent floods which occurred in the North Central/Northern and Eastern Provinces and Remedial Measures",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3894",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Water Supply Schemes and Systems in the Districts of Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Ampara, Trincomalee, Batticaloa and Vavuniya were badly affected due to the recent floods. Cabinet observed that arrangements have been made by  Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena, Minister of Water Supply and Drainage, to provide drinking water to the people of the affected area through bowsers, where necessary and also to disinfect the well using bleaching powder with the assistance of health authorities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2011-02-15",
    "description": "Buyer's Credit Facility of US$ 24,928,046.88 from the Exim Bank of China to Finance Lighting Sri Lanka Uva Province (Uva Udanaya) Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3895",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a request made by H.E. the President, the Government of China has agreed  to provide the above credit facility through the Exim Bank of China to meet 85% of the cost of the project. The proceeds of this facility will be utilized to provide 100% electricity coverage in Monaragala and Badulla Districts which will in turn improve the economic and social conditions of the people in the Uva province. Cabinet approval was granted to enter into this loan agreement."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-15-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2011-02-15",
    "description": "Importation of Dairy Animals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3896",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has already been granted for the importation of 4500 Dairy Animals (pregnant heifers) from Australia to develop the farms at Bopaththalawa, Nikaweratiya and Siringapatha belonging to the National Livestock Development Board (NLDB) over a period of 5 years for a total sum of US$ 28,537,185.  This project is to be implemented in two phases. Negotiations have been completed to obtain loans for the purpose from Netherlands and Australia to finance the project. On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to enter into loan agreements with the relevant Banks in Netherlands and Australia and to onlend the proceeds of the loans to the National Livestock Development Board to be utilized for the purpose."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "International Livestock and Poultry Exhibition 2011",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3897",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by Hon. Arumugan Thondaman, Minister of Livestock and Rural community Development, arrangements are being made by the Ministry to hold an International Poultry and Livestock Exhibition at the BMICH from 7th to 9th July 2011.  The exhibition will consist of a Trade Fair and a Scientific Conference focusing on development,  expansion and introduction of new technology for improving the poultry and livestock development in Sri Lanka. More than 150 foreign and local officials are expected to participate in this event which will be open to the public daily from 11.00 a.m. to 9.00 p.m.  This will be an ideal platform for all stakeholders of the industry such as livestock producers, animal breeders, feed producers, students, equipment and pharmaceutical manufacturers and other service providers.  Cabinet approval was granted in principle to conduct this event."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "Waste Water Disposal System for Ja-ela/Ekala and Ratmalana/Moratuwa Stage I - Phase II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3898",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- this project for which Cabinet approval has already been granted, is being implemented with financial assistance provided by the Government of Sweden (SIDA) supplemented with funds from the Government of Sri Lanka.  The works contract for the implementation of the project has been awarded to a Sweden Joint Venture at a total cost of US $90.65 million and Sri Lanka Rupees 181.02 million.  The consultancy services of the project has been awarded to M/s. SWECO International AB of Sweden at a total cost of SEK 26.57 million.  On a proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply and Drainage Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena, Cabinet approval was granted to increase the total estimated cost from Rs.12.8 billion to Rs.16.15 billion and also to seek additional grant funds to meet the cost.  Government contribution is expected to increase from Rs.2.4 billion to Rs.5.1 billion.  The project will be completed in 2013."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "Implementation of effective and well targeted District Development Plans",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3899",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- On a proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, Minister of Public Administration and Home Affairs, the Ministry has prepared a methodology for the preparation of District Development Plans to be implemented effectively through District Secretariats. This will pave the way to utilize District/Divisional mechanism in order to achieve expected development targets at the level of each Divisional, District and at National level, with the political leadership in the District taking the lead role.  Cabinet approval was granted for the implementation of the above with  the coordination of the Ministry of Economic Development and the Ministry of Finance and Planning.  The purpose is to ensure the efficiency of service delivery and also to expedite implementation of development activities in the District."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "Purchasing of two Nos. Ultra Heat Temperature (UHT) treated Milk Processing Plant for Milco (Pvt) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3900",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures are being taken by the Government to increase local milk production and processing with the view to save valuable foreign exchange being spent to import milk powder and also to uplift the living standard of the dairy farmers in the country. There has been a significant increase in the production of milk in the recent years. The production in 2006 which was 192 million litres increased to 233 million litres in 2009. The milk collection too has increased to 125 million liters in 2009. The government has noticed that the main issue at present is the preservation of  processed milk in polythene which lasts only for 3 days. On a proposal made by Hon. Arumugan Thondaman, Minister of Livestock and Rural Community Development, on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, Cabinet approval was granted for the purchase of  two Ultra Heat Temperature (UHT) treated milk processing plants for Milco (Pvt.) Ltd. which is a Government concern to be installed at the Factories in Polonnaruwa and Colombo.  This will enable Milco (Pvt.) Ltd. to produce UHT processed liquid milk in pouches (not in Tetra Packs) with long  shelf life of 30 - 40 days to be marketed at an affordable price  to the consumer in both urban and rural areas."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "Implementation of Greater Kurunegala Water Supply and Sewerage Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3901",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- out of a total population of 1.45 million in the Kurunegala District, about 150,000 are concentrated in the Kurunegala Town and its immediate suburbs.  During the past two decades commercial and industrial activities in the area have increased rapidly.  As such, there is an urgent need to provide safe drinking water for the people in the area and also to provide proper waste water disposal facilities and the above project has been designed to address this issue.  Accordingly, based on the recommendation made by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC) assisted by the Procurement Committee (PC), Cabinet granted approval to the proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply and Drainage Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena,  to sign the contract with M/s. China Machinery and Equipment Import & Export Corporation (CMEC) for a total sum of US $ 77,304,242.00 and domestic funds amounting to Rs.3,198,600,000.00 to be provided by the General Treasury."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-02-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-02-23",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding to conduct a feasibility study to develop a special zone for heavy industry in Trincomalee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3902",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-02-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- there is a growing enthusiasm for private foreign investment in infrastructure development after the dawn of peace in the country.  One such proposal is to construct an industrial zone at Sampur in the Trincomalee District by a multinational consortium from Australia with partners from Brazil.  The proposed industries to be located in this zone include Coke Plant, Iron Ore Palletizing Plant, Manufacturing Plant and Machinery, Sugar Refinery etc.  Investment for Phase I of the project will be US $700 million.  On the proposal made by H.E. the President on the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Review Committee, Cabinet approval was granted for the Consortium to conduct feasibility studies and submit their reports.  The feasibility of the project proposals will be examined by a Special Committee comprising of Senior Public Officers."
  },
