    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval was granted to provide various assistance to this category of farmers, including following:\r\n\r\n*\tseed paddy up to a maximum of 01 ha. free of charge, to farmers whose crops were totally damaged; \r\n*\tseeds for other field crops up to an extent of 0.2 ha. free of charge to farmers whose crops were damaged; and \r\n*\tprovision of financial assistance at the rate of Rs.4,000/- per 0.4 ha. through the Ministry of Economic Development, for re-cultivation purposes. \r\n\r\n\r\n\tThe cost of these assistance has to be met within the financial allocation of Rs.33 billion approved by the Cabinet on 09.02.2011, on the basis of a Cabinet Paper on   \"Impact of recent Flood - A Framework for relief and recovery programme for the Flood Affected Districts\"."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-03-08",
    "description": "Proposed Agreement between European Community and the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka on certain aspects of Air Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3909",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- the present practice has been for Sri Lanka to  enter into Bi-lateral Air Services Agreements to cover foreign civil aviation activities. However, a situation has now developed within the European Union of its Member States having under the process of European Integration agreed to align the key areas such civil aviation in accordance with the European Community Law. Under the circumstances, it has become necessary to amend the relevant Air Services Agreements. Since there are  26 countries to be covered and amending the Air Services Agreements individually would be a tedious process, on a joint  proposal made by Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris, Minister of External Affairs and Hon. Piyankara Jayaratne, Minister of Civil Aviation, Cabinet approval was granted to sign a Horizontal Agreement for the purpose between the European Community and the Government of Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-03-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-03-08",
