    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- in December 2010 Cabinet has approved a proposal to draft a Bill to amend the Finance Act No.78 of 1988 with a view to providing for a strong governance framework to regulate finance business.  The purpose of this effort is to update the law with the developments in technology in keeping with international best practices to combat unauthorized deposit taking businesses and to ensure the stability of the financial sector.  Some of the salient features of the Bill are - \r\n\r\n\t\t*\tacceptance of deposits without authority is made an offence;\r\n\t\t*\tdefinition of \"deposit\" is introduced; \r\n\t\t*\tenhanced examination/investigative powers;\r\n\t\t*\tenhancement of supervisory action on licensed finance companies;\r\n\t\t*\tenhanced public disclosure;\r\n\t\t*\tenhanced penalties.\r\n\r\n\tThe proposal made by H.E. the President to present the  relevant Bill in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
