    "description": "Hosting the Proposed Commonwealth Games 2018 to be held at Hambantota - Submission of Guarantees",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by Hon. Mahindananda Aluthgamage, Minister of Sports, Cabinet approval was granted to provide an assurance to the Commonwealth Games Federation that in the event Sri Lanka wins the bid to host the Commonwealth Games in Hambantota in 2018, the Government of Sri Lanka will meet any financial requirements found necessary for the purpose."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Proposed Amendments to the Banking Act, No. 30 of 1988",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3962",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- several developments have taken place in the domestic banking sector and in banking practices throughout the world, which has necessitated to consider further amendments to the Banking Act which was last amended in 2006.  The proposed amendments will streamline and strengthen the regulatory and supervisory framework for licensed Banks to be in line with the best global standards and practices.  The proposal made by H.E. the President to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare amending legislation for the purpose was approved by the Cabinet.  Some of the salient features of the proposed amendments as follows:\r\n\r\n*\tintroduction of a definition to \"significant management interest\" in respect of ownership in licensed Banks and to empower the Monetory Board to issue directions to these Banks in that respect;\r\n*\tintroduction of a dispute resolution mechanism with respect to non-registration of shares due to inability to establish the beneficial interests of such shares;\r\n*\tremoval of exemption granted for the Subsidiaries of licensed Banks to use the word \"Bank\" as part of its name; \r\n*\trepeal of provisions pertaining to numbered accounts; and\r\n*\tenhancement of penalties to be in line with present trends."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Amendments to the Licensing of Shipping Agents, Freight Forwarders, Non Vessel Operating Common Carriers and Container Operators Act No.10 of 1972",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3963",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- this Act has been enacted in 1972 to provide for the regulation and control of carrying on the business of a Shipping Agent.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to amend this Act to incorporate suitable provisions to empower the Minister in-charge of the subject of Shipping, inter alia, on the following:\r\n\r\n*\tto regulate fees charged by sectors under the purview of this Act;\r\n*\tto stipulate minimum requirements pertaining to paid up capital of the respective sectors; and\r\n*\tto specify minimum standards for financial responsibility and operational viability of the respective sectors.\r\n\r\n\tThe relevant Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman will be presented to Parliament for approval."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Re-development of 2600 underdeveloped Dhamma Schools in view of the 2600th Anniversary of the Buddha's Enlightenment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3964",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- there are about 10,000 Dhamma Schools registered at the Department of Buddhist Affairs and the number of students receiving Dhamma education is about 18 lakhs.  The Department of Buddhist Affairs has identified Dhamma Schools with less facilities in Pradesheeya Sasanarakshaka Balamandalayas throughout the island and has prepared a priority list of Dhamma Schools that should be developed very early in each Balamandala area.  On  a proposal made by Hon. D.M. Jayaratne, Prime Minister and Minister of Buddha Sasana and Religious Affairs, Cabinet approval was granted to develop 2600 such underdeveloped Dhamma Schools throughout the island, in keeping with the Sambuddhathwa Jayanthi Celebrations in 2011."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Restoration of Wilakandiya Tank",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3965",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- this tank is situated in the Mahiyangana Divisional Secretary's Division in the Badulla District. This is said to have been constructed by king Walagamba and later left abandoned after its breach.  On a proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, Cabinet approval was granted for the restoration of this tank at an estimated cost of Rs.81 million from the funds allocated to the Ministry for the year 2011.  After the restoration work is completed, about 500 acres of land will be available for cultivation purposes.  It is proposed to cultivate paddy covering the total area of 500 acres during the Maha season and during the Yala season, irrigation facilities will be provided for cultivation of paddy as well as other field crops such as maize, chillies, ground nut etc."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Development and Expansion of Fishnet Factory of Northsea Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- this is a 100% government owned fishnet factory situated in Jaffna which manufactured about 300 Mt. of fishnets per annum and was damaged during the conflict situation in the area during the last 3 decades.  Fishing  industry has been a major economic activity and  a source of livelihood in the Northern Region during the past, where about 18,500 fishermen are engaged in fishing in the region.  The sea food production in 2010 was 20,740 Mt. and is expected to be increased up to 25,000 Mt. per annum.  On a proposal made by Hon. Douglas Devananda, Minister of Traditional Industries and Small Enterprise Development, Cabinet approval was granted to develop and expand this fishnet factory at Gurunagar, Jaffna with financial assistance from the Government of India at a cost of Rs.152 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Implementation of a Pilot Project to Improve the Easy Accessibility and Sustainability of Financial Facilities to Rural Communities for obtaining the Electricity Service Connection",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- with the view to facilitate  the provision of electricity to low income household categories and Samurdhi beneficiaries, Cabinet approval has already been granted  for a Scheme to recover the electricity service connection charge up to a maximum limit of Rs.30,000 for such categories, by the Ceylon Electricity Board in 48 equal monthly installments.  On a proposal made by Hon.Patali Chapika Ranawaka, Minister of Power and Energy, Cabinet approval was granted to implement a micro credit based electricity connectivity programme with a grant of US$3.5 million from the Asian Development Bank to provided financial assistance to those who would not be eligible to obtain a loan under the CEB-Samurdhi Programme.  Under this programme, a pilot project has been designed to be implemented in three Districts, namely Hambantota (Southern Province), Ratnapura (Sabaragamuwa Province) and Ampara (Eastern Province)."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-04-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-04-27",
    "description": "Land Alienation Policy to Promote Development Activities of the Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=3968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-04-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a joint proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management; Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, Minister of Economic Development; and  Hon. Janaka Bandara Tennakoon, Minister of Lands and Land Development, Cabinet approval was granted to streamline the procedure of land alienation / disposition so as to ensure that there is a consistent policy on the extent of land that would be made available by the Government and Government Agencies to specific sectors, in the national interest.  Under the proposed procedure - \r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for agricultural purposes will be strictly on lease basis for a period not exceeding 35 years;\r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for industrial purposes will also be strictly on lease basis for a period not exceeding 35 years;\r\n\r\n*\tland alienation for tourism will be on the basis of 99 year lease and the extent of land will be 30 acres or less; and\r\n\r\n*\tin case of land required for agricultural or industrial purpose on investments over US $20 million, a suitable long term tenure will be considered."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
