  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-05-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-05-11",
    "description": "Guidelines for the provision of relief to the public at disaster and for the restoration of such affected areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4001",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-05-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- the disaster situation experienced in the country at the beginning of this year caused a severe impact on essential infrastructure facilities and livelihood of the people in a number of Districts throughout the country.  On a proposal made by H.E. the President, Cabinet approval was granted to streamline the process of providing facilities in disaster situations.  Implementation of this procedure will be as follows: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n*\tImmediate disaster relief such as cooked meal allowance, dry rations, assistance for kitchen utensils, tools and equipment, expenses for funerals and for injured persons - to be provided by the Ministry of Disaster Management through the District Secretaries, at enhanced rates. \r\n\r\n*\tDisaster rehabilitation relief such as subsidies for cultivation, assistance for self employment and for housing rehabilitation - to be implemented by the Ministry of Economic Development, through the District Secretaries, in consultation with the relevant Ministries such as Agriculture, Housing and Provincial Councils.\r\n\r\n*\tRestoration of major infrastructure - this work will be handled by the respective line Ministries."
  },
