    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-06",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Madu Church is situated in the Mannar District and during the festival season of the \tChurch nearly 450,000 people visit and encamp in the Church premises.  A water shortage is experienced during the festival period and additional water is supplied by bowsers by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board.  To overcome this situation, a project proposed by Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena, Minister of Water Supply and Drainage,  to  be implemented in two stages, for the improvement of water supply in the area, was approved by the Cabinet. Stage I of the project costing Rs.101.4 million to be implemented in 2011 will consist of the following: \r\n\r\n\t  \t*\tImprovements to existing water intake and pumping station.\r\n\t  \t*\tImprovements to internal distribution system.\r\n\t  \t*\tProvision of additional stand-posts.\r\n*\tConstruction of additional tube wells and establish bathing points with multiple showers. \r\n\r\n\tStage II of the project costing Rs.403.8 million to be implemented from 2012 - 2014, \twill consist of the following:\r\n\r\n\t\t*\tPumping facilities.\r\n\t\t*\t12 Km water transmission pipe line.\r\n\t\t*\tElevated storage tank.\r\n\t\t*\tAdditional distribution system.\r\n\t\t*\tWater purification facility."
  },
