    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Construction of the proposed Indigenous Community Museum Transformation into a Living Indigenous Community Museum",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4107",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- even though the concept of a Living Museum is rather strange to the Sri Lankan, this has been successfully implemented in many countries of the world. Under this concept action will be taken to exhibit the manner in which incidents of historical importance are being activated live in the form they took place in the past.  Under this project, while the infrastructure facilities of a selected part of the Dambana locality would be developed in a manner that would highlight the traditional lifestyle of the Indigenous Community, action would be taken to rebuild 15 houses in the traditional manner. It is also expected to promote tourist attraction through this programme. The above proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Jagath Balasuriya, Minister of National Heritage utilizing Rs.22 million for the purpose from the funds provided to the Ministry for 2011, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-07-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Implementing Housing Project for Tsunami affected people in Sainthamaruthu Divisional Secretariat Division in Ampara District as Owner Driven Housing Construction Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4108",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- a grant of US $6.2 million was received from the Government of  Bolivian Republic of Venezuela in 2005 to construct houses for the Tsunami affected people in the above area and 199 houses constructed by the State Engineering Corporation utilizing these funds have been handed over to the beneficiaries in 2010.  The proposal made by Hon. Basil Rajapaksa, Minister of Economic Development, to construct 200 houses under the above project for the remaining 200 beneficiaries, in the reclaimed Government land at Karawahuwatta, Sainthamaruthu, utilizing the balance funds from the above grant, with unskilled labour component being provided by the beneficiaries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-07-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2011-07-27",
    "description": "Financial Assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for the implementation of Pura Neguma - Local Government Enhancement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4109",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-07-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- on a proposal made by H.E. the President, loan negotiations are to be held with the Asian Development Bank on the 03rd and 04th August 2011 to obtain financial assistance in a sum of US $59 million (approximately Rs.6.5 billion) to improve the Local Government Infrastructure and Service Delivery through implementation of the Pura Neguma - Local Government Enhancement Project.  The total investment for the project is US $68.77 million, which includes a loan of US $59 million from the Asian Development Fund and Government contribution of US $9.77 million.   The project will provide capital grants to selected Local Authorities for eligible sub-projects such as, water supply and sanitation, drainage, solid waste management, roads and bridges, improvement of maternity and healthcare centres, public markets etc.   Cabinet approval was granted to enter into a loan agreement with the Asian Development Bank for a loan of US $59 million for the above project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
