    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- the proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health to award the construction of a building for the installation of a M.R.I. Scanner Unit at the Lady Ridgeway Children's Hospital, Colombo, to the State Engineering Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Annual  Report of the State Pharmaceuticals Corporation (SPC) for the year  2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4176",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- SPC is the sole importer of healthcare items to the Medical Supplies Division of the Ministry of Health, which in turn supply these items to all government hospitals.  It has the largest distribution network covering the entire island, including the North and the East.  During the year 2009, SPC has recorded the highest turnover of Rs.13,321 million, which is an increase of 8.8 million as against the previous year.  The turnover in the open market during the year has been Rs.3,331 million as against the 2008 turnover of Rs.2,934 million.  Profit after tax from the open market operation was Rs.318 million in 2009 as against Rs.362 million in 2011. The above report submitted by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health, was approved  by the Cabinet for presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Annual Reports of the State Timber Corporation for the years 2008 and 2009",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4177",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "-  the \tCorporation has increased its income from Rs.3141 million to Rs.3581 million, the\tgross profit from Rs.1210 million to Rs.1351 million and the net profit from Rs.647\tmillion to Rs.810 million, in 2009.  It contributed Rs.1635 million to the National\tIncome in 2009.  With the view to protect natural resources for the benefit of the future\tgeneration, the Corporation has instituted an island-wide tree planting programme to\tpromote developing the forest cover in the country. The above report submitted by\tHon. Anura  Priyadharshana Yapa,  Minister  of  Environment, was  approved by the\tCabinet for presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Annual Report of the National Apprentice and Industrial Training Authority (NAITA) for the year 2008",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4178",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- training provided by NAITA could be broadly categorized as follows:\r\n\r\n*\tEnterprise Based Apprenticeship Training - under this programme, trainees are attached to an enterprise throughout the training period to earn skills by doing.  This programme provides skills specific to the enterprises to which apprentices are attached according to a training guide prepared by NAITA in consultation with the employer.  \r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n*\tInstitutional / Centre Based Duel Apprenticeship Training - in this system, trainees are directly enrolled to the National Level Training Institutes for a specific period of institutional training followed by an on-the-job training component in public or private sector industrial organizations. \r\n\r\n*\tIn Plant Training - this offers training for undergraduates of the Engineering Degree Courses at Moratuwa, Peradeniya and Ruhuna Universities and Diploma Courses conducted by the Universities and other tertiary level educational institutions. \r\n\r\n*\tOn-the-job Training - NAITA conducts a programme of 06 months duration for students of other vocational training institutions.  \r\n\t\r\n\tIn 2008, NAITA has recruited 25875 apprentices for different modes of training.  The \tabove report submitted by Hon.Dallas Alahapperuma, Minister of Youth Affairs and \tSkills Development, was approved by the Cabinet for presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2011-09-07-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2011-09-07",
    "description": "Supply of Locally Produced Whole Milk Powder for the Thriposha Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=4179",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2011-09-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Thriposha is a nutritious food distributed free of charge to the malnourished children, pregnanat mothers and breast feeding mothers under a national programme. Whole Milk Powder is a main raw material use for Thriposha production. The proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, Minister of Health to purchase 187 MT. of Whole Milk Powder from 06.08.2011 up to 31.12.2011 at a cost of Rs.100.79 million was approved by the Cabinet.  Purchase of the quantity of Milk Powder required for this programme for 2012 is to be made through competitive bidding from domestic milk food manufacturers, following tender procedure."
  },
  {
