    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-01-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- the government has given high priority to increase the local milk production to cater to the demand in the country.  Out of the 4500 heads of cows proposed to be imported under Phase I, 2000 have already been imported from Australia. It has been planned to import the balance 2500 from Australia and develop the infrastructure facilities of the Ridiyagama Farm in Hambantota under Phase II of the project in 2014.  Negotiations have already been concluded to obtain credit facilities from a Bank in Netherlands for the importation of the balance 2500 cows referred to above, and an additional 20,000 high quality cows in keeping with the Budget Proposals for 2014.  The proposal made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning, to enter into loan agreements for the purpose with the relevant Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-01-13-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2014-01-13",
    "description": "Implementation of the Farmers' Pension Scheme and Social Security Benefit Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5371",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-01-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- this Scheme is being implemented by the Agricultural and Agrarian Insurance Board under the Farmers' Pension and Social Security Benefit Scheme Act, No.12 of 1987.  The total number of members who joined this Scheme is 959,254 and as at 01st  January 2014 the number entitled to receive pension benefits is 128,659. In keeping with the budget proposals, 2014, action will be initiated to effect the payment of the new Pension Scheme for farmers,  the salient features of which are as follows:\r\n\r\n*\tpension to be paid at the age of 64 years, subject to a minimum monthly pension of Rs.1,250/- and a maximum pension of Rs.5,000/- during the entire lifespan of the retired farmers;\r\n\r\n*\tRs.1000 million allocated initially from the 2014 budget and similar allocations to be made annually during the next few years;\r\n\r\n*\tmeasures to be taken for long term sustainability of the Farmers' Pension Fund through contributions from farmers;\r\n\r\n*\tcontributors for the previous Farmers' Pension Scheme to be absorbed into the new Scheme and make pension payments; and\r\n\r\n*\tto give legal effect to the amendments through a Gazette Notification.\r\n\tThe above proposal made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
