    "doc_id": "2014-09-18-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2014-09-18",
    "description": "Appropriation Bill for the Financial Year 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5719",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "-  the General Treasury has conducted Budget discussions with Ministries, Provincial Councils and other stakeholders and accordingly budgetary provisions have been made taking into consideration of the total resources available in the medium term 2015?2017, giving priority for timely completion of on going development activities and new development projects identified for implementation during the medium term, based on the priorities identified during the above discussions.  Within the medium term 2015?2017, the total estimated revenue of the Government for 2015 is Rs.1,713 billion and total Government expenditure for 2015 is estimated to be Rs.3,053 billion.  The expected fiscal targets to be achieved in 2015 under the medium term 2015?2017 are as follows:\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t                      2014     2015\t   2016\t      2017\t\r\n\t*\tPublic Investment (% of GDP)                  6.0\t   6.5\t     6.5\t       6.5\r\n\t*\tBudget Deficit (% of GDP)\t             5.2\t   4.4        3.6        3.0\r\n\t*\tTotal Public Debt (% of GDP)\t           75.0     71.0      68.0      65.0\r\n\t*\tEconomic Growth Rate                              7.8       8.2        8.3        8.4\r\n\t*\tInflation\t\t\t\t\t  6.0\t   5.5\t     5.0         5.0\r\n\r\n\tThe proposal made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance and Planning, to proceed with the related activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-09-18-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2014-09-18",
    "description": "Implementation of Construction of Headworks of Thalpitigala Reservoir Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5720",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Thalpitigala Reservoir Project envisages the construction of a 45.7 m. high dam across Uma Oya at Thalpitigala and the reservoir will have a capacity of 15.6 million cu.m.   It will provide improved irrigation water for 810 hectares in the Bathmedilla Scheme currently served by water from Vela Oya and supplemented by diversion from Uma Oya.  This will ensure meeting drinking water supply requirements and irrigation requirements at Menipe and Bathmedilla Anicuts among downstream water users in the area.   The project also envisages the construction of a hydro?power station with a capacity of 2 x 7.5 MW that will generate 51 GWh of hydro?power annually to feed the National Grid.  The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to award the above construction works as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-09-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2014-09-30",
    "description": "Creation of a mechanism for regulation of Programmes implemented with the objective of ensuring mutual friendship and trust among communities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5721",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-09-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- in the recommendations made by the Lessons Learnt and Reconciliation Commission (LLRC) special emphasis has been made on promoting coexistence among communities. Various Government Institutions are implementing programmes and projects based on the recommendations of this Commission from national level to regional level.  The following proposals made by H.E. the President in this regard were approved by the Cabinet:\r\n\r\n*\tto appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee on Social Reconciliation and Coexistence among Communities presided over by H.E. the President and comprising of Hon. Ministers to monitor and facilitate the implementation of the LLRC recommendations aimed at strengthening of coexistence among communities; and\r\n\r\n*\tto appoint a Committee of Officers comprising of Ministry Secretaries and presided over by the Secretary to the President who functions as the Chairman of the Committee which supervises the implementation of the recommendations of LLRC to assist this Cabinet Sub?Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2014-09-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2014-09-30",
    "description": "Construction of an Additional Building for the Office of the Leader of the Opposition in the same premises that presently houses his office",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5722",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2014-09-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has already been granted for the construction of an additional building for the Office of the Leader of the Opposition in the premises of No.30, Sir Marcus Fernando Mawatha, Colombo 07, presently used as his Colombo Office. The proposal made by Hon. D.M. Jayaratna, the Prime Minister, to increase the total cost estimate of the project from Rs.28,400,000.00 to Rs.56,280,036.49 due to price escalations etc., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
