    "doc_id": "2015-03-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-03-12",
    "description": "Draft Bill on Right to Information",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5980",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Government indents to draft and submit a Bill on Right to Information which enshrines provisions to ensure the right of the public to official information of the Government and to appoint a Commission for the purpose, with the intention to give effect to better implementation of democracy and good governance in the country and thereby to create an ethical society free of corruption in Sri Lanka.  \tAccordingly, action has been taken to prepare a preliminary draft for the Bill by a Committee appointed for the purpose in association with the Ministries of Mass Media and Parliamentary Affairs; Public Administration, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Democratic Governance; and Justice and Labour and also  taking into consideration of the views of journalists, veterans in the legal field, representatives of the Non Governmental Organizations and Public Officers.  The proposal made by Hon.Gayantha Karunathilaka, Minister of Mass Media and Parliamentary Affairs, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation based on the above preliminary draft, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-03-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-03-12",
    "description": "Proposed Administrative Procedure for granting Dual Citizenship",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, Minister of Public Order, Disaster Management and Christian Affairs, to grant dual citizenship under a new Administrative Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet.  Accordingly, individuals who satisfy at least one of the following qualifications are eligible to apply for dual citizenship: \n\n \t\t*\twho possesses professional or educational qualifications;\n*\twho owns immovable property worth of Rs.2.5 million or above;\n*\twho has a fixed deposit of Rs.2.5 million or above for a period of three (03) years in any Bank approved by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL);\n*\twho has fixed deposit of US$25,000 or above in NRFC/RFC/SFIDA accounts for a period of three (03) years in a Commercial Bank approved by the CBSL;\n*\twho has invested US$25,000 or above for three (03) years in a Treasury Bond or a Security Investment Account; and\n  \t\t*\ton attaining the age of 55 years.\n\n\tFurther, the spouse or unmarried children under the age of 22 years of the applicant are also eligible."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-03-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2015-03-12",
    "description": "Implementation of Vessel Monitoring System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=5982",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The incumbent Government has decided to take prompt actions to regain the European market for fisheries products  of Sri Lanka and the foreign exchange back to the country giving due consideration to the observations of the Indian Ocean Tuna Commission and the European Union, while giving preference to the views of the fisher community regarding the issues in the fisheries sector including the lifting of the ban already imposed on fish exports to the countries in the European Union. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.Joseph Michael Perera, Minister of Home Affairs and Fisheries, to purchase 1,500 transponders and distribute them among the fishermen free of charge and to complete the process in that regard by August 2015, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
