    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6022",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to recruit a team of retired police officers to the Anti-Corruption Committee Secretariat for a period of 03 months on temporary basis in order to assist the carrying out of the activities of the Anti-corruption Committee Secretariat expeditiously and efficiently, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Recognition of INTERPOL Travel Document in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6023",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Criminal Police Organization (ICPO) of which Sri Lanka is also a member, has introduced a special travel document to enable the officers of the INTERPOL and the law enforcement officers who travel abroad to conduct transnational investigations pertaining to the official duties of INTERPOL, to obtain visas expeditiously.   At present, 72 member countries of the ICPO, including several Asian countries such as Malaysia, Maldives, Pakistan, Nepal, Afghanistan, Laos, Philippines and Singapore have recognized this special travel document. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Public Order and Christian Affairs, to enter into an Agreement for the recognition of said Special Travel Document, as per the request made by ICPO and to authorize the Inspector General of Police to sign the said Agreement on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Implementation of 100 Day Programme to provide land ownership and proper housing to Plantation Workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6024",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is declared in the 100 Day Programme that the action will be taken to provide land ownership and proper housing to plantation workers instead of their current confinement in line rooms. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to implement the measures identified to be followed for the said purpose with the concurrence of all relevant stakeholders, to provide the estate workers each with a plot of land in extent of 07 perches, to provide them with a bankable document for those lands and to take back the houses constructed under different schemes and given to the beneficiaries, but subsequently transferred to third parties illegally and vest the said houses with the Estate Worker Housing Co-operative Societies without providing compensation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "National Policy on Cancer Prevention and Control",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6025",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cancer is identified as one of the major diseases reported in Sri Lanka in recent times.  The cancer incidence rate which was 37.6 per 100,000 persons in the year 1985 has been increased to 74.2 per 100,000 persons by the year 2005.  This shows an increasing trend in cancer frequency in Sri Lanka. The  10 most common cancer types in Sri Lanka are the cancers of breast, oral cavity, esophagus, cervix, lungs, thyroid, colon & rectum, lymphoma, ovary and leukemia.  The National Health Policy of Sri Lanka and the Health Master Plan  2007-2016 have recognized the prevention and control of cancer as part of  a broader concept of the Non-Communicable Disease prevention.  Accordingly, the National Policy and  Strategic Framework encompassing all actions to minimize the difficulties faced by the public due to cancer, presented by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Sri Lanka National Policy on Alcohol Control",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6026",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Alcohol consumption is identified as a significant contributor to the global burden of diseases and it is also listed as the prime risk factor that leads to premature deaths and disabilities reported in low and lower middle income countries.  As reported, the Cirrhosis mortality rate among male in Sri Lanka is 33.4 per 100,000, which is the highest in the world.  Alcohol is strongly related with large number of suicides and deliberate self-harm prevail in the country. It is also a cause for domestic violence that prevails within the families. As such, a complex relationship subsists between alcohol consumption and poverty in Sri Lanka.  The necessity of having an effective national policy on alcohol control has been identified  by all other stakeholders inclusive of the Ministry of Health and Indigenous Medicine and the National Mental Health Committee. Accordingly, the Sri Lanka National Policy on Alcohol Control presented by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Special Cardiac Surgery Programme for underprivileged Children at Lady Ridgeway Children Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6027",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The structural problems of the heart prevail at the birth are known as \u201cCongenital Heart Defects\u201d and it is estimated by now that approximately 2,500 to 3,000 children are born with congenital heart defects in Sri Lanka annually, and out of which around 2,000 children have to undergo corrective surgeries.  Currently about 900 children undergo similar surgeries at the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for Children every year and only a small number of surgeries are performed at Teaching Hospital, Karapitiya and Sri Jayawardenapura General Hospital.  At present, there are thousands of children waiting in the lists till their opportunity comes for the surgery, but most of them succumb to their illness or develop irreversible complications while waiting for surgery.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to implement a programme for \u201cafter working hours cardiac surgery\u201d at the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for Children as the best possible measure can be taken to perform above surgeries without further delay with the financial sponsorship of the \u201cGift of Life International\u201d, an organization relates to Rotary Club, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Hosting of the 37th Asian Conference on Remote Sensing in Sri Lanka during October - November, 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6028",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Conference on Remote Sensing held annually to explore the possibilities of using the latest technology on surveying and mapping and it is a prestigious annual event organized by the Asian Association on Remote Sensing and its host country.  It is held in rotation in the countries within the Asia Pacific Region to promote Remote Sensing Technology and its applications.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. M.K.A.D.S. Gunawardana, the Minister of Lands, to host the 37th Asian Conference on Remote Sensing in Sri Lanka, during the months of October and November,2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Transfer of Lands for the Second Phase of the Hambanthota Port",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6029",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Second Phase of the Hambanthota Port Project, 491.5 hectares of lands have been identified for acquisition and these lands are to be utilized for the Port development activities and as well as for the creation of industries related to the Port.  There are about 400 families presently residing in these lands which are to be acquired  and the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga,  the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to provide them with alternative lands and compensation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Amendment to the Intellectual Property Act, No. 36 of 2003 to enhance the protection given for Geographical Indications of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6030",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to make necessary regulations under the Intellectual Property Act, No.36 of 2003 and to draft pertinent amending legislations to prevent the detriment caused to the country due to the fraudulent use of the Trade Names and to safeguard the interests of the producers and exporters of Ceylon Tea, Pure Ceylon Tea, Sri Lanka Tea, Pure Sri Lanka Tea, Ceylon Cinnamon, Pure Ceylon Cinnamon, Sri Lanka Cinnamon, Pure Sri Lanka Cinnamon etc. accepted as attributed to Sri Lanka alone, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Consultancy Services for Broadlands Hydropower Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6031",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Power and Energy, to award the Contract for consultancy services of Broadlands Hydropower Project, to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau, as per the recommendation of the Project Committee appointed for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-04-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2015-04-08",
    "description": "Proposed Driver Training Track and the Vehicle Parking Area to be constructed at Werahera Office Premises of the Department of Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6032",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-04-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Practical tests related to driving licenses issued by the Department of Motor Traffic are conducted on district basis and the practical tests pertinent to Colombo district are conducted at its office premises at Werahera.  Werahera Office receives about 10,000 applications per month for the above practical tests and presently, such practical tests are being done on the main road.  Conducting these practical tests on the main road is a difficult task and other countries of the world practise different developed methods for this purpose.  As such, the construction of a driver training track is identified as a prioritized matter to be implemented expeditiously. The proposal made in this regard by Hon. R.M.Ranjith Maddumabandara, the Minister of Internal Transport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
