    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Modernization of Infrastructure Facilities of Multi Storeyed Housing Schemes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6256",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, Minister of Housing and Samurdhi, to renovate the public roads and rain water drainage systems in the following 13 Housing Schemes where 1700 families reside, at a cost of Rs.143.29 million, under the Programme of Modernization of Infrastructure Facilities of Multi Storeyed Housing Schemes in Colombo City, was approved by the Cabinet. \r\n\r\nBolamesawatta Housing Scheme\r\nVeluwanarama Housing Scheme\r\nElvitigala Housing Scheme\r\nMallikarama Housing Scheme\r\nCentral Road Housing Scheme\r\nKammalwatta Housing Scheme\r\nJumma Masjid Housing Scheme\r\nDissanayakewatta Housing Scheme\r\nAluth Mawatha Housing Scheme\r\nDias Place Housing Scheme\r\nBloemandhal Housing Scheme\r\nSt. James Street Housing Scheme\r\nAluthkada Housing Scheme"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Project on Construction of Defence Headquarters Complex at Akuregoda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6257",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- An Officials' Committee has been appointed, by the Cabinet to investigate into the activities of the Defence Headquarters Complex which is being constructed at Akuregoda, Battaramulla, and to report on same.  The attention of the Cabinet was drawn to the following facts mentioned in the Officials' Committee Report, with regard to a company to which the consultancy services of this project have been awarded, that is,  \r\n\r\n*\tthe company has been selected without calling competitive bids; \r\n\r\n*\tthe company has been registered under the Registrar of Companies and under the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects, only after it has been selected  for consultancy services; \r\n\r\n* \tthe  authorities concerned have not entered into a formal Agreement, to obtain services of the said company; \r\n\r\n* \tit has been decided to pay the said company Rs.606.032 million in cash, for the consultancy services of the entire project; Although, the company has been paid Rs.509.926 million as at 2015-05-31, (83% of the total payment) it has only completed 30.02% of the entire work of the project as of now. \r\n\r\n\tThe Cabinet decided to investigate into the above facts mentioned in the Officials' Committee Report pertaining to the Consultancy Services Company and to take legal action, on the findings of the  said investigation, as appropriate."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Resettlement of Families affected due to acquiring of lands for Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Agricultural Development Project - the increase of families due to the delay of the project - Revision of benefits including approval of alternative proposals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6258",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "Moragahakanda - Kaluganga Agricultural Development Project was commenced in 2008 and it has been identified that the 1,747 families of 12 Grama Niladari Divisions in Naula Divisional Secretary's Division and 907 families of 11 Grama Niladari Divisions in Laggala Pallegama Divisional Secretary's Division will be affected in the implementation of the said project. However, the following issues have arisen due to the delay in the implementation of the project by 8 years:   \r\n\r\n*\tSince the new marriages have taken place within the families to be affected, another 224 families have been added to the earlier number, as families to be affected. \r\n\r\n*\treluctance of the newly added families, to leave the area \tand settle down in Medirigiriya. \r\n\r\n*\tthe expression of unwillingness by 345 families which consented to settle down in Medirigiriya in the year 2007 to go and live in the said area.  \r\n\r\n*\tthe alternative lands have to be provided with the newly added families who have expressed their unwillingness to settle down in Medirigiriya area. \r\n\r\nThe proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripla Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment,  to acquire the lands identified to be given to the famiies to be added under above project belonging to the Government Owned Plantation Companies situated in the relevant area and suburbs, to pay compensation for the lands owned by such families and to provide assistance for building houses in alternative lands, as a remedy to solve the above issues, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Establishement of a Wastewater Management System for the Negombo town area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6259",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As far as Sri Lanka wastewater management sector is concerned, only 2.4% of the Sri Lankan population is connected to a collective wastewater management system and the vast majority of the population uses individual sanitation systems.  In reality, most of the existing collective systems are out dated and poorly maintained.  This has decreased their efficient functioning. Therefore, under treated wastewater is discharged into drainage channels and this has brought adverse consequences for both the public health and the environment. Considering the prevailing situation, the 'Sanitation and  Hygiene Initiative for Towns' (SHIFT) Project has been initiated to establish three collective wastewater management systems for Negombo, Galle and Kelaniya - Peliyagoda areas.  \r\n\r\n\tUnder first phase of this project, it is expected to establish a wastewater management system for the Negombo Urban Area at a cost of Euro 107 million and the Agence Francaise De Development (AFD) has agreed to provide a financial facility of Euro 76 million for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, to enter into an agreement with AFD of France, for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Archaeological Heritage Management in the Rajagala Archaeological Reserve",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6260",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Rajagalatenna Ancient Ariyakara Viharaya situated in the Uhana Divisional Secretariat Division of the Ampara District of the Eastern Province is considered to be established by the King Lajjitissa.  The ruins of this monastery which is believed to be a combination of a Pabbatha Vihara and a forest monastery type are scattered in an area of 1,025 acres.  The ashes of the great Arahath Mahinda is said to be interred in a Stupa found in the premises. The Rajagala Archaeological Project is being carried out as a joint project of the Department of Archaeology and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura since 2012, to arrest the deterioration process of the archeological remains in this monastery and to conserve them in order to secure them sustainably in the future and for the developemnt of the Heritage Tourism Programme. \r\n\r\n\tThe total estimated cost of this project is Rs.323.8 million and the sum spent on the project  up to the end of 2014 amounts to Rs.55.5 million including the funds provided for by the American Embassy Fund and the University of Sri Jayawardenapura. The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and the Minister of Policy Planning, Economic Affairs, Child, Youth and Cultural Affairs, to obtain a sum of Rs. 268.3 million required for the completion of these project, from the Government Consolidated Fund,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Agreement on Exemption from Visa Requirements for Holders of Diplomatic and Official / Service Passports between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Kazakhstan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6261",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The purpose of entering into this Agreement is to further strengthen the friendly relations between two countries and to simplify the relevant procedures to facilitate the movement of citizens of Sri Lanka and Kazakhstan between the two countries. The permission is granted for the Nationals of States of one Party, holders of valid diplomatic or service/official passports to enter, leave and transit through the territory of the  State of the other Party without obtaining visas for a period of thirty (30) days, through this Agreement. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Public Order and Christian Affairs, to enter into the above Agreement between Sri Lanka and Kazakhstan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Development Project of National Hospital Health Square \u2013 Providing Houses for the unauthorized settlers in Bosevanawatte",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6262",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cardiology Unit of the Sri Lanka National Hospital provides an invaluable patient care service to the heart patients of the country.  However, the building complex where the Cardiology Unit is housed is very old and the space available in the building is not at all sufficient, in considering the services currently provided by the Unit.  As such, the health staff as well as the patients under go excessive difficulties.  As a remedy, the Cardiology Unit should be extended,  but the prevailing land is inadequate for the purpose.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to utilize the adjacent land called 'Bosevanawatte' to improve the required facilities of the Cardiology Unit, by providing the unauthorized settlers reside in the said land with the alternative houses from a Multi-storeyed Housing Project is being constructed at another place under the Urban Regeneration Project of  Urban Development Authority, in lieu of the 63 housing units of the said unauthorized settlers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Purchasing of Plasma from the National Blood Transfusion Service in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6263",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- No substitute has yet been found for blood and the blood necessary for transfusion is obtained from the donors.  Although, blood used to be transfused as \u201cwhole blood\u201d up to recent times, the situation has now changed. If one unit of blood could be separated accurately as recommended, there is a possibility of deriving up to four components out of it.  As such, a patient can be given only the portion of blood he needs and the balance components can be given to other patients who need them.  The National Blood Transfusion Service (NBTS) collects 100,000 litres of Plasma, annually, from the donors and after the separation of components the NBTS utilizes only around 60,000 units out of them for the clinical use.  Since the facilities are not available with the NBTS to separate a large number of components there is the possibility of providing the balance quantity of 40,000 litres which is currently discarded,  to the companies which possess the technology of producing Plasma Protein.  Although, the situation is such, the Plasma Protein requirement of Sri Lanka is imported from the foreign companies / institutions which produce Plasma Protein incurring a heavy expenditure.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medicine, to give the excess quantity of Plasma for Plasma Protein production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Protocol of Phytosanitary Requirements for the Export of Banana from Sri Lanka to China between the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine of China and the Ministry of Agriculture of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6264",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Banana is being cultivated successfully in Sri Lanka as if suits with the climatic and environmental conditions prevail in the Country and it is a crop which could be used to meet the local food requirements and to generate export income. There is a healthy potential for the exportation of banana to China through developing trade relations with China, a friendly country of Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to enter into an Agreement with the General Administration on Quality Supervision, Inspection and Plant Quarantine of China, enabling Sri Lanka to export banana to China complying with laws and regulations on phytosanitary requirements and to provide information on banana cultivation lands and localise packing houses, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Incorporating the Divi Neguma Social Security Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6265",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Samurdhi Social Security Fund established under the Samurdhi Programme which commenced with a view to alleviating poverty of the low income earners is implemented with effect from 1st January 1997 and its  objective is to extend financial assistance to Samurdhi beneficiaries beset with unexpected problems during their journey towards economic development. As of now, 1,478,288 families receive monthly Samurdhi subsidy and a contribution of Rs.45/- out of it is debited to this Fund.  Having taken into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Samurdhi, to incorporate the said Fund, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to operate the said Fund as a Trust under the Trust Ordinance until it is formally incorporated."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the Government Analyst\u2019s Department of Sri Lanka and the National Forensic Service of the Republic of Korea",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6266",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to sign a MOU between the Government Analyst's Department of Sri Lanka and the National Forensic Service of the Republic of Korea to extend cooperation on matters as follows, was approved by the Cabinet: \r\n\r\n*\tPromotion of the standards of the Forensic testing of the Government Analyst's Department in order to achieve excellence in the process of investigations into criminal matters in Sri Lanka; \r\n\r\n*\tInstallation of new methodologies for the advancement of laboratory testing in the field of forensic science including new researches,   examination of questioned documents, forensic toxicology, analysis of narcotics, firearms and explosives  and the most modern analysis of DNA; \r\n\r\n*\tSharing the knowledge on testing methods pertaining to criminal investigations, the knowledge of the experts in the field, theoretical and practical knowledge in the conduct of criminal investigations; \r\n\r\n*\tExchange of knowledge mutually through workshops, seminars, training programmes and meetings conducted by experts; \r\n\r\n*\tGranting assistance in the purchase of state-of-the-art laboratory equipment and tools; and  \r\n\r\n*\tEnsuring the international level of \"Accredited Testing Samples\" and the standards of the laboratories in the Government Analyst's Department."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "\u2018Sri Lanka Expo 2016\u2019 to be held from 15th - 17th September, 2016 at the BMICH, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6267",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Organizing of International Expositions to showcase the country's export capabilities while facilitating Sri Lankan producers, exporters and service providers to meet the prospective international buyers, partners and potential investors is one of the strategic promotional tools. In the back-drop of the special political and economic developments taken place recently in the country, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen,  the Minister of Industry and Commerce to hold the 'Sri Lanka Expo - 2016' from 15th - 17th September 2016 at BMICH, Colombo, enabling concerned parties to obtain valuable business experience with a combination of events such as  expositions, seminars, meetings, programmes conducted simultaneously and visits to factories, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-08-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2015-08-05",
    "description": "Investigation on Corruptions, Mal-administration and Irregularities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6268",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-08-05",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by the Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Internal Transport to consult the Attorney General's Department, to institute legal actions against the responsible institutions and persons, in accordance with the Report pertaining to the following matters submitted by the Special Investigation Committee appointed by the Secretary to the Ministry, on a directive made by the Minister of Internal Transport, to make investigations into corruption, maladministration and irregularities said to have been taken place during the past five year period in the Ministry and its affiliated institutions and to avoid occurrence of such situations in future, was approved by the Cabinet:  \r\n\r\n*\tNon-recovery of a sum of Rs.142 million for the buses hired by the Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB), for the presidential election-2015.  \r\n\r\n*\tNon-receipt of the discount offered in procuring 2,200 new buses for the SLTB. \r\n\r\n*\tLoosing the anticipated quality and the import duty concessions to the SLTB when purchasing spare parts. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of private buses under SLTB logo. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of 20 luxury buses imported for the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting, by the Road Development Authority. \r\n\r\n*\tIssues with regard to enormous cost and the estimates in the construction of the Northern Railway Line. \r\n\r\n*\tSubmission of estimates with an enormous cost in the construction of the Matara - Kataragama Railway Line. \r\n\r\n*\tVesting and leasing out lands owned by the Railway Department, to the external institutions and persons,  deviating from the formal procedure. \r\n\r\n*\tOperation of rail carriages/special trains with private sector participation and loses incurred in the operation of the Vice Roy special train. \r\n\r\n*\tSale of scrap iron deviating from the accepted procedure."
  },
  {
