  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-16-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2015-09-16",
    "description": "Appointment of Advisors to Hon. Ministers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6293",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Secretary to the Cabinet having drawn the attention of the Cabinet of Ministers the need to have a policy decision with regard to the appointment of Advisors/Consultants and making payments to Advisors/Consultants so appointed, the Cabinet decided as follows: \n\nto consider only the experts who possess an in depth knowledge of the subject matter and functions of the Ministry and are viewed by the Minister as persons who can provide advise that cannot be expected from serving senior officers of that Ministry, for appointment as advisors to Ministers. \n\nonly one Advisor/Consultant could be appointed to each Minster, but however, a maximum of only two Advisors/Consultants could be appointed to the Minister of a Ministry which has a wide purview and entrusted with two or more portfolios, subject to the approval of the Cabinet.  \n\n\nIn making monthly payments to the Advisors/Consultants so appointed, the attention should be focused on their fulfillment of a   high level of  academic  or professional qualifications pertaining to the subject matter of the relevant Ministry, on their contribution in pioneering programmes or projects of an innovative nature pertaining to the subject matter of the relevant Ministry, on themselves being persons who have held senior positions in the private sector drawing very high remuneration immediately prior to the appointment or who have held  senior most positions in the public service."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2015-09-22",
    "description": "Minimizing Waste in the use of Public Funds",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6294",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. Prime Minister having focused the attention of the Cabinet that the Government should demonstrate its commitment for frugality in spending public funds, the Cabinet decided to take action as follows to minimize waste in the use of public funds: \n\nthat, foreign travels undertaken by Cabinet Ministers, State Ministers, Deputy Ministers, all other elected Representatives and Public Officers should be restricted as far as possible.\n\nthat, when undertaking foreign travels of essential nature, restriction of the members of the delegation, only to those whose participation is absolutely necessary at such events. \n \nthat , after a formal assessment on the security to be provided to the dignitaries, people's representatives and officials at present, who have been provided with security escort, to take action to reduce the  security staff and the number of vehicles provided to them to a bare minimum. \n\nthat to make applicable all the above mentioned guidelines to the Provincial Authorities, Defence Forces, State Owned Enterprises, Statutory Boards and Government Owned Companies as well."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2015-09-22",
    "description": "The Establishment of a Joint Committee for Consular Affairs between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6295",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The formal diplomatic relations between Sri Lanka and United Arab Emirates (UAE) has commenced in 1979 and in recent years, the relationship has developed, encompassing a number of fields such as employing Sri Lankan employees, culture and education, in addition to trade and investment. Presently, about 250,000 Sri Lankans are employed in the UAE and Sri Lanka anticipates to further extend the existing partnership with the UAE to create more employment opportunities for Sri Lankans, especially in the 'Skilled Category'. At the first session of the Joint Commission between Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates held on 26th and 27th of January 2014 at Dubai, the two parties have agreed to establish a Joint Consular Committee, with a view to providing consular protection and assistance to the citizens of both countries.\n\tThe objective of the establishment of this Committee is to strengthen and develop the cooperation in the Consular field between the two countries.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to sign the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on the Establishment of a Joint Committee for Consular Affairs between the Democratic Republic of Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates and also to take appropriate action for the effective implementation of  the MOU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2015-09-22",
    "description": "Registration of Vehicles of Ministries, Departments and Government Institutions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6296",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet noted the information submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance with regard to the vehicles owned by each Ministry, Department and other Government Institutions. \n\t\n\tAccordingly, the Cabinet further noted that the registered vehicles owned by the Ministries, Departments and other Institutions of the Government are 59,160 in number and out of these vehicles, a considerable number is found still being used by the Ministers, Deputy Ministers, Members of Parliament and who were engaged in various capacities in the last regime, but not functioning any more in such positions.  As such, the Cabinet decided to instruct the Secretaries to the Ministries, to take necessary action to retrieve the Government owned vehicles which are still being used by various persons without official entitlement, without delay."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2015-09-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2015-09-22",
    "description": "Programme on renovation of 25,000 houses to mark the World Habitat Day - 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6297",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2015-09-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- United Nations Organization has declared the first Monday of the month of October every year as the 'World Habitat Day'.  Accordingly, this year's World Habitat Day falls on Monday the 05th of October and the theme followed this time is \"Public Spaces for All\".  \n\n\tIt has been observed by the Ministry of Housing and Construction that there are many families reside for a long time in houses where only the preliminary construction work has been done and without having plastered the walls, in the housing construction process being implemented in various parts of the country and as a result issues have arisen such as reduction of economic value of houses, weakening of the strength of the houses by exposing them to elements of weather and causing  health problems like respiratory failures of  children and elderly living in these houses. \n\n\n\tAs such, in simultaneous to the World Habitat Day Celebration, the Ministry of Housing and Construction anticipates to implement a series of  islandwide programmes, in association with the institutions affiliated to the Ministry, other public institutions and organizations. The period from October 5th to 12th is to be declared as the \"Habitat Week\".  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to implement the proposed programmes under the direction of the Ministry, to mark the World Habitat Day \u2013 2015, to select 25,000 houses comprised of 1,000 from each district of which walls need to be plastered and to obtain Rs.250 million to implement the renovation programme through providing only the building materials worth of Rs.10,000/- maximum for each selected house, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
