    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Power & Renewable Energy of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry for Economic Affairs and Energy of the Federal Republic of Germany on Co-operation on Sustainable Development in the Energy Sector of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6552",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to sign the Memorandum of Understanding for the Co-operation on Sustainable Development in the Energy Sector of Sri Lanka, consists of the development of electricity generation projects in  renewable energy, research and development in relation to enhancing  renewable energy electricity absorption capacity into the national electricity grid, development of the plants and equipment used in the renewable energy based electricity generation, manufacturing of such plants and equipment with the use of local raw materials, introduction of  clean technologies for thermal power generation, training and education in relation to renewable energy development, between the Ministry of Power & Renewable Energy of Sri Lanka and the Ministry for Economic Affairs and Energy of the Federal Republic of Germany, during the state visit of H.E. the President, to the Federal Republic of Germany, on the 16th and 17th February of this year, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "Implementation of the Food Production National Programme (2016 - 2018)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6553",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the observations made at the meeting chaired by  H.E. the President, held with the representatives of the private sector who engaged in business activities related to agriculture and food production sector, in order to successfully implement the Food Production National Programme, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to implement the proposals of making mandatory the obtaining of clearance from the Department of Agriculture when importing any crop being promoted for cultivation under this programme, by an importer, to Sri Lanka as a consumer item, prior to ordering such items; if the said crops are imported at the instances where the local production is inadequate, the provision of opportunities to the private companies as well as the institutions who engaged in promotion of crop cultivation under the above National Programme, to import such crops as consumer items; in order to ensure that the each food product so imported as consumer items possesses health safeness and high standard, introduction of a new methodology to examine the quality of such goods, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "The National Strategic Plan to Monitor and Combat Human Trafficking - 2015 - 2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6554",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'Human Trafficking' which is often described as 'modern - day slavery' is a heinous crime condemned by the civilized world.  Sri Lanka ratified the United Nations Protocol  to Prevent, Suppress and Punish Trafficking in Persons, especially Women and Children (Palermo Protocol) in 2015.  The Protocol acts to prevent and combat trafficking in persons, to provide for the physical and psychological recovery and reintegration  of victims of trafficking and to promote co-operation among states, in order to meet those objectives. Accordingly, recognizing the importance of following a multi-stakeholder approach to prevent the heinous crime of human trafficking, the 'Five Year National Strategic Plan to Monitor, Combat Human Trafficking (2015-2019)' developed by the National Anti-Human Trafficking Task Force, submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "Project for Issuing of Internationally recognized 'Continuous  Discharge Certificate' and  'Certificate of Competency' for Sri Lankan Seafarers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6555",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- There is a high demand for Sri Lankan Seafarers, from the  International Shipping Companies, because of their knowledge, skills and positive attitudes.  Sri Lankan Naval Captains, Officers, Marine Engineers and other Technical officers are presently employed in mega ships of  several companies and Sri Lanka derives a considerable amount of foreign exchange on their earnings. It is a legal requirement for the Sri Lankan Seafarers to obtain the 'Continuous Discharge Certificate(CDC)' and 'Certificate of Competency(COC)' issued by the Director General of Merchant Shipping, to engage in their occupations.  In comparison with the certificates issued to their Seafarers by the developed countries, the quality of the certificates issued to the Sri Lankan Seafarers should be further upgraded to be complied with the International Standards. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to implement a project to issue a 'Continuous Discharge Certificate' and a 'Certificate of Competency' which possess recognition at international level, incorporating bio metric information, to the Sri Lankan Seafarers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "Construction of 4,000 Houses for the Plantation Community in the Uva and Central Provinces, under the Indian Government Grant Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6556",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per a Memorandum of Understanding signed by the Governments of Sri Lanka and India in the year 2012, the arrangements have been made to construct 4,000 houses for the plantation community in the Uva and Central Provinces, within the next three years from 2016-2019.  As the first phase of this endeavour, the preliminary activities related to the construction of 1,134 houses have been completed and activities pertaining to the construction of the rest of the 2,866 houses also have been commenced.  Each house is to be constructed in a land area of 7 perches with a floor area of 550 square feet and the total cost to be incurred for a house would be Rs.1,120,000.00.  In selecting beneficiaries  for this purpose, the priority is given to the families who live in landslide affected and landslide prone areas and the families living in the fire affected line-rooms.  Accordingly, in order to proceed with this project, the proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding which clearly outlines the  responsibilities and the functions of the respective parties, between the Governments of India and Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "UNITERRA Volunteer Co-operation Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6557",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- UNITERRA is a volunteer co-operation and international development programme which is jointly implemented by the World University Service of Canada (WUSE) and the Centre for International Studies and Co-operation (CECI) in Canada. It has been planned to implement this programme in Sri Lanka, during the period of 2016-2020, and the proposed programme will be implemented in relation to the sectors of  Tourism & Hospitality and Apparels. The Government of Canada will spend an amount of Canadian dollars 2.7 million for this programme to be implemented covering about 80,000 beneficiaries, during the period of 2016-2020. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding with the Government of Canada, for the implementation of the above programme in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-02-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-02-03",
    "description": "The Framework Arrangement between the Government of  the\tRepublic of Korea and the Government of the Democratic Socialist\tRepublic of Sri Lanka, concerning loans from the Economic\tDevelopment Cooperation Fund of the EXIM Bank of Korea from\t2016-2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6558",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-02-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to further strengthen the friendship and the economic cooperation between the two countries, the Government of Korea has agreed to grant an aggregate commitment amount in Korean Won not exceeding the equivalent of US$ 300 million to Sri Lanka, from 2016 to 2018, through the Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF) of the Export Import (EXIM) Bank of Korea, to finance the mutually agreed projects by the two Governments.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of  National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Framework Arrangement  with  the Government of Korea, to obtain the said loan amount, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
