    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Reaping the harvest in the Maha Season 2015/2016 has already commenced and the Paddy Marketing Board has made arrangements to purchase paddy in 19 Districts during this Season, in accordance with the Government's Policy on purchase of paddy. Accordingly, the proposals made by Hon. P. Harrison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to purchase paddy directly from the farmers by the Paddy Marketing Board, under the Paddy purchasing programme of the Government in the Maha Season 2015/2016, to implement the programme in the relevant Districts with the  assistance of the District Secretaries/Government Agents, to pay Rs.50/- per kg for 'Keeri samba', Rs. 41/- per kg for 'Samba' and Rs.38/- per kg for 'Nadu' purchased by the Board and purchase paddy from the farmers engaged in the paddy cultivation during the Season, subject to a maximum\tquantity of 2,000 kg from each, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-02-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2016-03-02",
    "description": "Obtaining vehicles for Government Agencies under the Operating \tLeasing Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6609",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government spends a considerable amount of money for the purchase of vehicles for public institutions as well as for the maintenance of such vehicles due to the high repair costs and administrative delays. It has been proposed through the Budget - 2016 to introduce an 'Operating Leasing Scheme' to obtain vehicles for the vehicle pools of the Government institutions and the officers of the Government institutions and public enterprises entitled to have official vehicles, in order to avoid the weaknesses in the existing system, to reduce the amount of money spent by all public institutions for the maintenance of a large number of vehicles and to increase the efficiency of the Leasing industry in the country while promoting the same. Under this system, a portion of the vehicles required for the Government will be obtained on the option of 'Use and Return' on a 60 month fixed rental basis from the eligible suppliers who provide vehicle rental services, selected through the Government Procurement procedure, and the lessor will bear the expenses of Insurance covers, revenue licenses, all repair  costs and the other relevant expenses, and the Government will bear only the expenses for the drivers and fuel. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to implement the above methodology of obtaining vehicles under the proposed Operating Leasing Scheme, incurring an optimal costs saving to the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Ecosystems Conservation and Management  Project (ESCAMP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6610",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although Sri Lanka has been ranked as a global bio-diversity hot spot, the ecosystem and the bio-diversity of the country have been confronted with serious threats. The prime objective of the Government is to direct Sri Lanka towards a sustainable development that ensures the conservation and management, while empowering environmental safety. The objective of this project is to strengthen the capacity of the Government Institutions and the General Public, for the improvement of the sensitive ecosystems in selected areas, demonstrating models on human-elephant co-existence and the sustainable consumption and conservation of natural resources. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement this project during the period of 2016-2021, utilizing a loan facility of US$ 40 million to be obtained from the World Bank and Rs.473 million to be provided by the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Issuance of  Passenger Permits for the Expressway",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6611",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Tender procedure to select bus operators, for the issuance of passenger permits in the expressway was introduced and under that procedure the permits were issued to the persons who have submitted the highest bid and therefore the ordinary bus owners were deprived of the opportunity of providing transport services in the expressway. Accordingly, an Officials' Committee was appointed by the Cabinet, to submit an alternative methodology for the purpose. On the recommendations of the said Committee, also with the approval of the Cabinet, the criterion to be followed in issuing passenger permits for the expressway and the marking scheme related thereto were implemented. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to implement the recommendations of the Cabinet Sub-Committee, appointed to submit recommendations for the introduction of a more transparent methodology, avoiding the shortcomings evident in the previous procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Implementation of  Pre-paid Card System for Public Transport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6612",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The use of Information Technology Solutions for the qualitative development of the Public transport service has become popular in many countries today. Among these solutions, the use of an electronic charging system has become very popular and the ability to charge the relevant fee accurately from the passengers, receipt of due income by the bus owner, avoidance of issues such as settling balances (due to not possessing coins) are among the advantages of this system. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to introduce a system of electronic charging for the passenger service buses, via pre-paid cards, in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Information and Communication Technology Agency, Sri Lanka Transport Board, National Transport Commission, Private Bus Owners, State Banks and IT Companies, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "National Expressway Authority Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6613",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to publish the National Expressway Authority Bill drafted to provide for the establishment of National Expressway Authority for the construction, management, development and maintenance of expressways in Sri Lanka, to   ensure a safe, efficient and an environmental friendly movement of vehicles on the expressways, and to entrust the powers and functions connected thereto, in the Gazette and thereafter to present same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Investment in the 'Commonwealth Small States Trade Financing Facility'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6614",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM) which was held in Malta in November, 2015, the Commonwealth along with Sri Lanka, India, Mauritius and Malta had announced the setting up of a new Fund as 'Commonwealth Small States Trade Financing Facility', to promote trade and investment flows, particularly for small and developing countries of the Commonwealth. The objective of this Fund is to promote trade flows to and from the small States of the Commonwealth.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to invest a sum of US$ 1.5 million, as an 'Anchor investor', in the said Fund, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Financial Assistance for the implementation of Anuradhapura Integrated Urban Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6615",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Anuradhapura, which belongs to the 'Cultural Triangle' of Sri Lanka holds a special significance due to its archaeological specialty and the number of sacred places of Buddhist worship found therein. At the same time, it is the economic and administrative hub of the North Central Province and is a destination which has gained the  attraction of the local and foreign tourists. Presently, a population of more than 51,000 reside in the city limits of Anuradhapura, where a high growth is anticipated in time to come. Therefore, it is proposed to create a balanced growth and co-development between the sacred city and the new town areas of Anuradhapura, under the Strategic Cities Development Project implemented by the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development, while preserving its cultural and natural heritage.  The improvement of the city water drainage system, provision of public transport facilities, traffic management and the enhancement of public space are anticipated to be carried out through this project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement the Anuradhapura Integrated Urban Development Project, under the Strategic Cities Development Project being implemented and the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to enter into a loan agreement with the Agence Francaise De Developpment (AFD), to obtain a credit facility of Euro 52 million, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Implementation of Small and Micro Industries Leader and Entrepreneur  Promotion  Project - SMILE III - Revolving Fund Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6616",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Granting loans to small and medium size entrepreneurs including those who engaged in the production of import substitutes, value added goods and goods produced using modern technology for the export market, with a view to uplifting high yielding industries within macro-economic framework of the Government and to all those  small and medium size industrialists who are not covered by other loan schemes, is undertaken by the above Loan Scheme. As per the requests made by the small and medium industrial entrepreneurs, who are the recipient beneficiaries of this loan scheme and the participating loan institutions who implement this loan scheme, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to increase the maximum subsidiary loan limit up to Rs.25 million, provided under the present General Loan Scheme and to increase the re-financing ratio for the subsidiary Loans provided  to the participating credit institutions, by the Government, up to 100%, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Allocation of Land at Kalutara to the Kalutara Bodhi Trust for a Public Car Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6617",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to legally transfer the block of land known as 'Diyambathalawa' of 33.75 perches in extent, situated in between the two bridges across the Kalu Ganga, in the Kalutara city, in Galle Road to which the Kalutara Bodhi Trust  has already paid  compensation and the interest related thereto in respect of the transfer of the said land and the possession had been transferred to the said Trust, to the Kalutara Bodhi Trust, by the Urban Development Authority, for the enhancement of the parking facilities of the pilgrims who daily arrive at the Kalutara Bodhi, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Obscene Publications Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6618",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is of paramount importance to safeguard children from the adverse effects which could result from their exposure to obscene publications. The provisions contained in the Penal Code and the Obscene Publications Ordinance of 1927 are  inadequate to deal with that regard, especially in the present social context. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to bring in a new Act on obscene publications, in place of the existing legal provisions, in order to provide for the prohibition of obscene publications using children, prevention of keeping child pornography through use of computer systems and for the avoidance of exposure of children to visuals on sexual activities using computer as a medium, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Obtaining Allocations for the Payment of Compensation for the lands acquired for the Second Stage of the Hambantota Port Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6619",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of the Phase II of this project is nearing completion by now and therefore, the joint proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, Minister of Ports and Shipping and Hon. Sagala Rathnayake, Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to obtain the provisions required for the payment of compensation, in respect of the lands acquired for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Allocation of at least 25% of the provisions for women, from  the Projects implemented for Rural Economic Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the recommendation of the Cabinet Sub-Committee appointed to study the proposal submitted previously for the use of at least 25% of the provisions earned by the projects implemented for the development of the rural economy, for women, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) K.D.M. Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to use at least a minimum of 25% of investments made for the identified rural development projects implemented by the various Ministries, in the interest of women, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Ratification of United Nations Convention on the Use of Electronic Communications in International Contracts: Amendments to Electronic Transactions Act, No. 19 of 2006",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka signed the United Nations Electronic Communications Convention (UN-ECC) on 07th July, 2015 and thus Sri Lanka is the second country in Asia and the first country in South Asia to ratify this Convention. The purpose of this Convention is to offer practical solutions for the issues related to the use of electronic means of communication in connection with international contracts. The proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication and Digital Infrastructure, to amend the Electronic Transactions Act, No.19 of 2006, for the implementation of this Convention in Sri Lanka, which provides necessary facilities to promote Sri Lanka as a hub for e-commerce, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Construction of the New Courts Complex, Matara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Courts Complex, Matara is housed in buildings of over 100 years old, within the premises of Fort of Matara. It has become necessary to house all the Court buildings, comprising of a Civil Appellate High Court, a Provincial High Court, three District Courts, two Magistrate's Courts and a Labour Tribunal under one roof and for this purpose, a portion of land from the land called Kotawilawatta, situated in Matara has been identified.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to construct the Courts Complex, Matara, at a cost of Rs.1,119.5 million, with a Juvenile Magistrate's Court, a Commercial High Court, a Bank, a Post Office, Rest Rooms and Library for Lawyers, a Community Correction Office, a Legal Aid Office and Family Counselling Office, in addition to the above Courts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-09-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-03-09",
    "description": "Extension of the Agreement on Colombo Port City Development Project with the Government of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the environmental issues that have arisen, the activities of the  Colombo Port City Development Project has been suspended since February 2015 and a comprehensive and formal Environmental Impact Assessment Report on the Project was called for. The Cabinet Committee on Economic Management has recommended to allow the re-commencement of the activities of the Colombo Port City Development Project, subject to certain matters to be resolved in future and within the fixed limits and conditions indicated in the said Report. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickramasinghe, the Prime Minister, to extend the Agreement entered into with the relevant Project Company by the Government of Sri Lanka, for a further period of six (06) months from 15th March 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Agreement on Global Climate Change and National Strategic\tAccord (National Contribution towards minimizing Global\tTemperature)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Excessive burning of fossil fuels, industrialization, urbanization, deforestation and environmental pollution have paved the way to the increase of global temperature and it has been predicted that the global temperature is likely to rise by 4 degrees Celcius (4\u00b0C) by the end of this Century. The climate changes that occur due to the increase of global temperature will cause adverse effects to the sustenance of mankind. As per the Paris Agreement entered into at the 21st Session of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCC), which was held in Paris,  France from 30th November to 11th December 2015, it has been agreed not to exceed the global temperature by another 2 degrees Celcius (2\u00b0C)  from the present temperature level by 2100 and to maintain the same below 1.5 degrees Celcius (1.5\u00b0C).  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of  Mahaweli Development and Environment, for Sri Lanka to sign the Paris Agreement in concurrence with the above to formulate the policies and plans relevant to implement the set of proposals for the reduction of Green House Gas emissions  as designed for the contribution of Sri Lanka as per the said Agreement, to draft legislation for the establishment of the 'Climate Change Commission of Sri Lanka' and to implement the ''Blue Green Beautiful Lanka' Programme, in 10,000 villages, during the period of 2016-2020, in collaboration with the community organizations, with a view to creating eco-friendly 'Green Smart Villages', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Establishment of the Wildlife Management Units",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka looses more than 50 human lives and 200 wild elephants  annually, due to the elephant-human conflict and a trend is developing where in addition to elephants, other  animals such as leopards,  crocodiles and monkeys have conflicts with humans. As such, in order to control this situation, plans are being launched by the Department of Wildlife Conservation, and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to establish Wildlife Management Units covering the wildlife areas where wildlife-human conflicts are mostly reported, to take prompt measures by visiting relevant places immediately, when a such incident is reported, was approved by the Cabinet in principle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "The Report of the Cabinet Sub-Committee appointed to submit the recommendations on relocation of families living in high risk areas prone to landslide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Cabinet Sub-Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, was appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers, to study and report issues pertaining to the relocation of families living in high risk areas prone to landslides and expediting of the construction of houses for the persons who have been affected due to landslides. Accordingly, the implementation of the recommendations submitted, giving attention to  matters such as identification of the number of families settled at landslide risk prone areas, resettling them in other places, provision of facilities to convert the disaster affected persons back to normalcy,  re-establishment of  public places such as schools situated in high risk prone areas, in stages, on priority basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "World Expo 2017 - Astana, Kazakhstan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'World Expo' exhibition is  held biennially in major cities of the world, under different themes and this year's exhibition is scheduled to be held in Astana, Kazakhastan from the 10th of June to 10th of September, 2017, under the theme of 'Future Energy'. The Republic of Kazakhstan has invited Sri Lanka to take part in the said exhibition. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to appoint a Commissioner General to organize the Sri Lanka's participation at this exhibition and to provide the opportunity for the small and medium sector producers of horticulture and related products in Sri Lanka, to be involved in the Exposition through an accepted methodology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Restructuring of Lanka Sathosa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6628",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- In August 2014, Lanka Sathosa  imported 257,853 metric tons of rice, on a bank loan of Rs.14,078 million and due to the failure in selling the stock of rice as expected, it has become impossible to settle the loan obtained. By now a sum of Rs.5,742 million has been settled and further Rs.8,754 million together with the outstanding interest is to be settled. A sum of Rs.17,000 million has been spent for the importation of this stock of rice including port charges, demurrages, transportation and warehouse costs. It has been identified that 3,048 Metric tons of rice from the presently remaining stock is unfit for human consumption. It seems that the anticipated income from selling the remaining stock of rice, will not be sufficient to settle the outstanding loan amount and to have the working capital required to continue the daily operational activities of Lanka Sathosa. Accordingly, in order to avoid this situation, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, Hon. Malik Samarawickrama, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to provide the  funds required to meet the urgent working Capital requirement and to pay the outstanding loan due to the state banks by Lanka Sathosa, from the General Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Strategic Cities Development Project - Development of Jaffna City",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The main objective of the Strategic Cities Development Project is  to develop a system of environmentally sustainable and well-linked cities. The development of  the cities of Kandy and Galle as strategic cities, with relevant facilities has already been commenced under this project, on loan facilities, obtained from the World Bank. Jaffna city too has been identified as an appropriate city to be developed under this programme and  therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to proceed with the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Allocation of a block of land developed for a Tsunami Housing Scheme at Kalmunai Town to the National Housing Development Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Kalmunai Town can be described as one of the most affected towns from the Tsunami disaster that occurred in the year 2004. The families displaced from the said disaster have been resettled in a three storied housing complex comprising of 174 housing units, which was constructed utilizing a sum of money given by a private donor, in a plot of land purchased by the Urban Development Authority, for the resettlement of displaced families. The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to allocate the relevant land as a free grant to the National Housing Development Authority (NHDA) by the Urban Development Authority, enabling the NHDA to legally allocate the said housing units to the residents of such housing units through issuing deeds to them and also to take necessary measures to manage common amenities of the said housing scheme, providing solutions  to the issues encountered by the residents due to absence of a proper mechanism for the maintenance of this housing scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "The programme of  Providing Rs.20,000/- to obtain nutritional foods for expectant mothers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6631",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to give birth to a physically and mentally healthy child and for the elimination of low birth-weigh child births from Sri Lanka, a programme of providing nutritional food in a value of Rs.20,000/- to expectant mothers for a period of 10 months, including the final 06 months of pregnancy period and the first 04 months of the lactation period, is being implemented by the Government since March 2015. It has been recommended  to introduce a new methodology, to enable the expectant mothers to select food of their preference and choice and to further simplify the present methodology. It would provide expectant mothers with the opportunity of getting nutritional food, for a period of 10 months from any of the easily accessible business institutions, subject to a maximum of Rs. 20,000/- per month, which have been registered in the Divisional Secretariat. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to implement the proposed new methodology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "The Contract for Consultancy Service for Reviewing of Design and Construction Supervision of Headworks of Moragahakanda Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6632",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The projects of Moragahakanda and Kalu Ganga have been identified as projects that provide strong contribution towards the provision of water for the agricultural activities, supply of electricity and  the development of the livelihood of the people of the area and by now, a considerable quantity of work has been completed. Presently 60% of the head work of Moragahakanda project has been completed and it has been planned to complete the construction  work by March 2017. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the Contract for Consultancy Services for reviewing of design and construction supervision of the head work of this project, to the Mahaweli Consultancy Bureau, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Development of infrastructure facilities of the Universities of Kelaniya, Visual and Performing Arts, Moratuwa, Rajarata, Sri Jayawardenapura, Colombo and the University of Colombo School of Computing",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6633",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Development of infrastructure facilities of Universities and Higher Education Institutions is essential to produce professionally competent graduates who par  with the existing development needs of the economy of the country and cater to the needs of the international job market. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to implement the proposed 09 projects of developing the infrastructure facilities of the Universities of Kelaniya, Visual and Performing Arts, Moratuwa, Sri Jayawardenapura, Rajarata, Colombo and the University of Colombo School of Computing, at an investment of Rs.1,706.9 million, during the period of 2016-2019, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Construction of an Administrative Building for the Ministry of Higher Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6634",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the building facilities found in the Ministry of Higher Education  which is presently situated in a state land in Ward Place, Colombo 07, are inadequate for the present day service requirements, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to demolish a building more than 25 years old and to make use of the premises for the construction of a new Administrative Building consisting with eight (08) floors and  a floor area of 64,255 sq.ft., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Tender for Supply, Installation & After - Sales Services of 01 No. MRI Scanner for the National Hospital of Sri Lanka (NHSL)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6635",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The MRI Scanner presently installed at the National Hospital is about 15 years old and as such, it is essential to procure a new MRI Scanner for the National Hospital.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faizal Casim, the Acting Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the Tender for Supply, Installation and After Sales Services of 01 No. MRI Scanner for the NHSL, to the lowest responsive bidder, as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Construction of a New Building for the Divisional Secretariat, Homagama",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6636",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Divisional Secretariat, Homagama is the one which comprises the most number of Grama Niladhari Divisions and covers the largest area out of the thirteen (13) Divisional Secretariat Divisions in the Colombo District. The extent of this Divisional Secretariat Division is 11,815.5 hectares and the number of families residing there is around 60,425.  The pensioners residing in the area are around 10,000 and the total population there is around 250,000. Adequate facilities are not available in the building where the Divisional Secretariat is housed presently and therefore, with a view to providing a more efficient and an effective service to the general public, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to construct a three (03) storied building for the above Secretariat , at a cost of Rs.286.66 million,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Construction of the District Secretariat Building, Mullaitivu - Stage - II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6637",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mullaitivu belonging to the Northern Province is a district where the lives of the people have been worst affected by the Tsunami and the protracted conflict. Although, a large number of development activities are in progress under the supervision of the District Secretary, to uplift the living conditions of the people of the district, the limited space available in the District Secretariat has become an obstruction to carry out such development activities efficiently and effectively. Accordingly, with a view to providing the services of the District Secretariat under one roof, in order to provide a better service to the people of the district, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to carry out the construction work of  the Stage II of the District Secretariat, Mullaitivu at an estimated cost of Rs.328 million,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Stator Replacement - Victoria Power Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6638",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Three Generators are being operated at the Victoria Power Station and such  machines have been in use for over 30 years.  The technical experts in the field have recommended that the said machines have to be repaired without delay, if further efficient service is to be obtained from these machines. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the Tender for the replacement of the Stator of Unit 3 Machine of Victoria Power Station, to the bidder recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Greater Colombo Wastewater Management Project - Stage-II -  Design Supervision and Management Consultancy Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6639",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Greater Colombo Drinking Water and Wastewater Management Project and the Development Investment Programme are being implemented with the objective of streamlining the Wastewater disposal process and improving the public health of the residents of the Greater Colombo area. The Asian Development Bank has provided financial facilities to the Government of Sri Lanka for Stage-II of the Programme and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to award the Contract for Design Supervision and Management Consultancy Service, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Consultant Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-16-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-03-16",
    "description": "Eco-systems Conservation and Management Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6640",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the implementation of the Eco-systems Conservation and Management Project during the period of 2016 to 2021, with a view to improving the management of Eco-systems in identified areas, to formulate mechanisms to create co-existence between the elephants and humans and to provide benefits to the people through the sustainable use and protection of natural resources, by developing the capacity of the government institutions as well as of the people has already been approved by the Cabinet.  The International Development Association (IDA) of the World Bank has shown its interest to provide funds for the said project and the World Bank has agreed to provide a loan facility equivalent to US$ 45 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations with the IDA for the implementation of this project and to enter into a relevant Financing Agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Implementation of a Waste Management Project in the Matara   Municipal Council and the areas under the purview of the Matara Pradeshiya Sabha",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6641",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- A project for establishing a centre for disposing waste in a proper manner and a plant for generating electricity power using bio-gas produced from waste, in Matara, Kotawila area, had been planned  concurrent to the Deyata Kirula 2015, the National Development Exhibition. With the suspension of the Deyata Kirula, the National Development Exhibition, the project activities too came to a standstill. Therefore, the proposal made by H.E the president Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the suspended Waste Management Project, expeditiously, for the purpose of solving the irregular waste disposal problem of Matara Municipal Council and the areas under the purview of the Matara Pradeshiya Sabha,with the assistance of the private sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Financing of Polgahawela, Pothuhera and Alawwa Integrated Water Supply Project, Kundasale - Haragama Water Supply Project and Aluthgama, Mathugama and Agalawatta  Integrated Water Supply Project through the Local Banks",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6642",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The cabinet of Ministers has already granted approval, to implement the Water Supply Project of Kundasale-Haragama and the Integrated Water Supply Projects of the Polgahawela, Pothuhera and Alawwa; and Aluthgama, Mathugama and Agalawatta. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Prime Minister, Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic affairs, to authorize the National Water Supply and Drainage Board to obtain the funds through the local banks to implement the Projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Construction of a rail track from Kurunegala to Habarana via Dambulla to be implemented under \u2018Let\u2019s Awaken Polonnaruwa\u2019 District Development Programme (2016 - 2020)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6643",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the 5 year plan of \u2018Let\u2019s Awaken Polonnaruwa\u2019 District Development Programme (2016-2020) which includes development projects for the enhancement of the living standards of the people living in Polonnaruwa and other adjoining districts, the project for the construction of a rail track from Kurunegala to Habarana via Dambulla, 80 km in length has been identified as a priority. This project envisages to provide a safe, fast and a cheap mode of transport to the people of the Eastern and North Central Provinces and also the linking of the Dambulla Economic Centre to the Railway Network which will greatly facilitate the achievement of district development targets and objectives.  The Peoples' Republic of China has agreed to contribute to the implementation of this project and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation to appoint a project staff for speedy action to complete the project and to acquire the lands required for the identified trace of the  rail track, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Payment of Compensations and gratuity - The Department of Divineguma Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6644",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The joint proposal made by Hon. S.B Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment and Welfare and Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, for obtaining funds required for payment of Compensation and gratuity, in stages, for the officers who served in the institutions that were amalgamated to form the Department of Divineguma Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Amendments to the Companies Act, No. 07 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6645",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Companies Act, No.07 of 2007 provides for the Incorporation of  Companies, Administration and Management, Amalgamation, Liquidation and Settlement of Company Disputes etc; and it has now been in operation for a period of nearly 10 years.  Based on the Auditor General's Report, all three versions of the Act were reviewed  by the Advisory Commission appointed to advise the Minister regarding the implementation of Company Law and certain provisions were identified for expeditious amendment. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce to amend the Companies Act, No.07 of 2007 incorporating the proposed amendments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Horana Town Centre Improvement Programme - Implementation of the Horana Bus Stand Development Project - Stage II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6646",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Development Plan prepared by the Urban Development Authority for Horana Town has identified the issues regarding the inadequacy of infrastructure, traffic congestion and improper land use pattern in the Central Business Area and the basic requirements for the development of the city. To upgrade the Central Business Area, it is absolutely necessary to develop the existing bus stand with adequate parking space for the large number of buses operating to and fro to provide the necessary facilities for the people who come to the city. Stage I of this bus stand has already been completed and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development to proceed with Stage II of the bus stand development project which includes small scale shop spaces, sanitary facilities, bus shelter access facilities  and access road improvement facilities at a cost of Rs.182 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Proposed Social Welfare Centre at Mattakkuliya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6647",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to construct a Social Welfare Centre at Mattakkuliya with a view to creating a good day-to-day life for the under privileged and the low income groups living in the Colombo North Urban Area. The building which is proposed to be constructed by the Urban Development Authority in collaboration with the Colombo Municipal Council will have child and maternity clinics, healthcare centres, e-channeling, a library, a gym, carom, chess etc; and common office facilities. The construction of the building will be completed within one year and after completion the ownership of the building and its management will be vested with the Colombo Municipal Council.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development to implement the project for the construction of the proposed Welfare Centre at Mattakkuliya at a cost of Rs.250 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Payment of annual contribution to the Centre for Alleviation of Poverty through Sustainable Agriculture (CAPSA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6648",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The centre for Alleviation of Poverty through Sustainable Agriculture (CAPSA) is a sub-institution governed by the United Nations' Economic and Social Commission and the main objective of the institution is to provide policy inducement for member countries for the upliftment of the living standard of the rural people living on secondary crops and carrying out development activities on agriculture and research to alleviate poverty.  Sri Lanka as a member of this centre has obtained the services pertaining to agricultural development and gained various other benefits. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture to continue to pay the annual membership fee as a member of this centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Bill to amend the Mediation Boards Act, No.72 of 1988",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6649",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has already granted approval, to increase the limit of monetary value in respect of disputes to be referred to compulsory mediation, from Rs.250,000/- to Rs.500,000/-. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon.(Dr) Wijayadasa Rajapaksha, the Minister of Justice, to  publish the draft bill in the Government Gazette and present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Purchasing a Land for the Ministry of Parliamentary Reforms and Mass Media",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6650",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Parliamentary Reforms and Mass Media, to purchase a plot of land of 40 perches, located at the new Parliament Road, Battaramulla at a cost of Rs.31.5 million, from the Urban Development Authority, since it is beneficial to construct a Government owned building, to house the Ministry of Parliamentary Reforms and Mass Media, which is presently functioning in a private building at Pelawatta, Battaramulla on a monthly rental of Rs.630,000/-, as per the recommendations of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "The Accelerated Program for the development of Middle Income Housing & Infrastructure",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6651",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- A five year programme for providing houses for the middle income wage earners in urban and sub-urban areas, in all districts, has been launched with the assistance of the private sector, and it would be implemented within the next five years. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to establish a Programme Coordination Unit for the efficient implementation of the programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "The Re-launching of the Village Reawakening (Gam Udawa) Program",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6652",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-03-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The programme 'Gam Udawa', which was launched successfully in the 1980s as an innovative strategy to reach the poor and under privileged people, in every nook and cranny of the country for the upliftment of their living standards, was implemented on the basis that shelter is fundamental to  physical, psychological, social and spiritual well-being of the people.  However, the implementation of 'Gam Udawa' was abandoned during the middle of 1990s. The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to restore this integrated development effort, which had evolved around the development of human settlements and followed with the 'Gam Udawa' Exhibition, covering a few electorates at regional level, effective from this year, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-03-23-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-03-23",
    "description": "Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act of the United States of America - entering into an Inter-Governmental Agreement with the Internal Revenue Services of the United States of America",
