    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- A necessity has arisen to provide for the Registration of Persons who are missing and their whereabouts unknown, especially those who are reported missing in the course of, consequent to, or in connection with the conflict in the Northern and Eastern provinces and/or its aftermath or in connection with the political unrest, and/or civil disturbances, and due to enforced disappearances. Such registration and issuance of 'Certificates of Absence' to the relatives of such missing persons will enable their relatives  to manage the properties and assets of the missing person, temporarily obtain provisional guardianship of children of the missing person, make applications for the benefits under the social welfare schemes and make representations before the relevant authorities and make requests on behalf of the missing person. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to  amend the Registration of Deaths (Temporary Provisions) Act, No.19 of 2010, with a view to issuing the 'Certificates of Absence' regarding missing persons or for the cancellation of the Certificate of Absence in the event of the missing person being found to be alive or deceased or the  issuance of a certificate of death with regard to the person concerned, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-07-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-06-07",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding for Cooperation between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Turkey on Diplomatic Training, Exchange of Information and Documentation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6813",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of entering into the above agreement is to  strengthen and consolidate the close and friendly relations between Sri Lanka and  Turkey, through the development of mutually beneficial cooperation on diplomatic training, the exchange of information and documentation on international law and other academic disciplines that are relevant to the practice of diplomacy and international relations, in the spheres of political, economic, cultural or otherwise. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to enter into the above  Memorandum of Understanding between the Foreign Ministry of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Foreign Ministry of the Republic of Turkey, during the forthcoming visit of Hon. Mevlut Cavusoglu, the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Turkey to Sri Lanka in June 2016, pertaining to diplomatic training and exchange of information and documentation, was  approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-07-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-06-07",
    "description": "Disposal of garbage accumulated in certain areas of the Western Province due to the recent floods",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6814",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government informed the Cabinet that the Joint Mission Programme initiated to dispose the garbage accumulated in certain areas of the Western Province expeditiously, including the Kolonnawa Divisional Secretariat Division, due to   recent floods, in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Army, Civil Security Department, Provincial Council of Western Province, Local Government Authorities, Department of Agrarian Development and Sri Lanka Land Reclamation & Development Corporation, was implemented successfully during the past 7 days disposing of around 5,440 Tons of garbage, during the period and that it has been decided to extend the implementation period of the above Joint Mission Programme up to 2016-06-12, as around 2,000 Tons of accumulated garbage is yet to be disposed."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-07-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-06-07",
    "description": "Housing Development Programme for families suffering from renal failure and living in abject poverty",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6815",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Joint proposal made by H. E. the President Maithripala Sirisena and Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to initiate and implement a Housing Programme with the basic infrastructure facilities for the families suffering from renal failure and living in  abject poverty, in view of the 'National Housing Week' commencing from the National Housing Day which falls on 23rd June, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Extradition Treaty between Sri Lanka and Ukraine",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6816",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, with the objective of strengthening the cooperation between the two countries on extradition of criminals back to their motherlands, was approved by the Cabinet. This would provide Sri Lanka with the opportunity of requesting the authorities of Ukrain, to transfer the persons who have engaged in illegal acts in the country and sought refuge in Ukraine."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Renovation of the 'Seth Sevana' Government Elders Home at Mirigama and the construction of Water Tank for the Home",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6817",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The ageing population of Sri Lanka constitutes 12.4% of the total population at present. The ageing population of Sri Lanka is rapidly increasing and it is anticipated that it would exceed 24.8% by the year 2041. When considering the increase of elderly population day by day, it is necessary to provide them with the opportunity of spending their lives with self-respect and dignity. The 'Seth Sevana' Elders Home at Mirigama, in which 265 elders presently reside, was established to commemorate Right Honourable D.S. Senanayake, and it is the largest elders home located in the Western Province and maintained by the Government. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment and Welfare, to obtain financial provision for preliminary repairs including the water supply of the Elders Home, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Project for Computerization of subjects of the Department of Labour for enhancing transparency and efficiency of its activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6818",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The responsibility of enforcing service conditions, employment terms and  employee welfare measures enacted by the Government from time to time, in compliance with the charters and recommendations of the International Labour Organization, to safeguard the human rights of employees and also protect them against occupational hazards, lies with the Department of Labour. With a view to computerizing the main subjects of the Department, the activities relating to designing of a computer software (Labour Inspection System Application - LISA) had commenced in the year 2010 with the assistance of the International Labour Organization.  The basic objectives of the above programme are to obtain accurate data, to prevent the occurrence of duplication in inspecting  institutions, to enhance the efficiency and transparency of the Department and to formulate an employee progress review system.  The Cabinet of Ministers noted the information submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations to the effect that after obtaining the staff and the infrastructure facilities necessary, the programme is to be completely undertaken and implemented by the Department of Labour by August 2016."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Implementation of the SAARC Agreement on Trade in Services (SATIS)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6819",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Leaders of the Member States, during the  16th SAARC Summit held in Bhutan in 2010 signed the SAARC Framework Agreement on Trade in Services (SATIS), as a further step towards expanding the regional trade to the services sector. To give effect to the Framework Agreement on SATIS, the Schedules of Commitments have to be finalized by the Individual Member Countries.  Sri Lanka falls within the Category-I, namely the Category of non Least Developed Countries and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to include new areas of operatorless Rental/Leasing Services relating to ships and land transport in the Schedules of Commitments, in addition to the areas of Communications Services, Financial Services and Tourism and Travel related Services to which Sri Lanka has already agreed in the Doha Round of World Trade Organization and to open such services under the SATIS Agreement and to make necessary requests to the relevant Government Institutions, for the implementation of the Agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Agreement on Economic Cooperation between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Bulgaria",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6820",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The total trade turnover between Sri Lanka and Bulgaria, which is a  Member State of the European Union has increased up to US$ 7.75 million in the year 2015.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to sign an Agreement on Economic Cooperation between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Republic of Bulgaria,  to search for new ways and means to enhance trade, investment and  economic ties between the two countries and to have an inter-governmental mechanism to enhance cooperation between the two countries in identified new fields, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Commemoration of 94th International Co-operative Day",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6821",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Co-operative Movement can be described as a movement built by the people by themselves for the purpose of enhancing their economic and social well-being. The commemorative activities of the International Co-operative Day have been carried out by the United Nations Organization since 1975.  The International Co\u2011operative Day of this year falls on 2nd July and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to declare a 'Co-operative Week' from 25th June to 2nd July 2016 and to celebrate the Co-operative Day which falls on 2nd July 2016 at the  Nelum Pokuna Theatre, in collaboration with the members of the Movement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Allocation of Land for Construction of the Approach Road to the Dedicated Economic Centre at Veyangoda from the Veyangoda Town",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6822",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Dedicated Economic Centre at Veyangoda established in the year 2007 consists of 70 business units and 06 stores and it is a highly important business centre for the trade and consumer community of the area.  Since the present approach road for the Dedicated Economic Centre is situated at a considerable distance from the Veyangoda Town, the consumers are reluctant to visit the Centre and also as there is no approach road to the Centre from the Nittambuwa - Katunayake Main Road, which runs close to the Centre, the lorry owners who use the said road for the transportation of vegetables and other items from various places such as Dambulla, Welimada, Nuwara-Eliya are also reluctant to come to the Centre. This state of affairs has adversely affected the development of the Centre and therefore, to avoid this situation, the joint proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce and Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to allocate the 40 perches of land belonging to the Food Commissioner's Department situated in the area, to construct a convenient approach way  providing direct access to the Economic Centre, from the Katunayake - Nittambuwa Main Road, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Amendment to the Provincial Councils Elections Act, No.02 of 1988",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6823",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the present Government's policy towards the increase of  female representation at least by 25% in the political decision making process, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to publish the Provincial Councils Elections (Amendment) Bill prepared to incorporate provisions in the Provincial Councils Elections Act, No.02 of 1988 to include not less than 30% of the total number of candidates whose names appear in the nomination paper submitted by each political party or independent group in respect of each Provincial Council to consist of female  candidates, in the Government Gazette and thereafter, to present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Resettlement of Internally Displaced Families reside in the Welfare Centres",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6824",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is noted that by the end of March 2016, 251,000 internally displaced families who were affected by the conflict have been resettled in the  Northern and Eastern Provinces.  However, there are over 14,000 families yet to be resettled in those areas.  Presently, 1,109 displaced families reside in the 31 welfare centres in the Tellippalai Divisional Secretary's Division and it is reported that 641 families out of these families are landless. In regard to the resettlement of these landless families, the District Secretary, Jaffna has identified 65 hectares of land belonging to the Kankasanthurai Cement Corporation. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to release the above mentioned land identified for the purpose of resettling 400 landless families residing welfare centres at Tellippalai and to transfer the said land in favour of the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Allocation of Land for Establishment of a Tyre Factory at Gonapola, Horana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6825",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The annual income earned by Sri Lanka from the export of Pneumatic and Retreated Rubber Tyres and Tubes amounts to US$ 471 million and that has been accounted as 61.9% of the total rubber exports. Therefore, in order to further enhance the industries in this field, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrama, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to provide necessary facilities to commence a tyre manufacturing plant with a production capacity of 03 million tyres per annum, as a BOI project, with an investment of US$ 75 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "The development of the Airport at Palaviya in Puttalam",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6826",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The availability of an efficient internal air transport system which integrates the entire country with the international airports is essential for a country. In addition to the two international airports available in Sri Lanka at Katunayake and Mattala presently, there are 14 domestic airports of different sizes at Ampara, Anuradhapura, Baticaloa, Hingurakkgoda, Palali, Iranamadu, Koggala, Katukurunda, Palaviya, Ratmalana, Sigiriya, Trincomalee, Weeravila and Vavuniya so as to cover 07 out of the 09 Provinces in the Island.  The Budget - 2016 has proposed  to establish three new domestic airports in the districts of Badulla, Kandy and Puttalam under public-private partnership, especially for the promotion of tourism in such Districts.  With a view  to developing the tourism industry prevalent in the Kalpitiya area which is becoming a tourist destination, simultaneously, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to develop the Palaviya Airport which is currently non-utilized, acquiring a land of  26 hectares in extent, at an estimated cost of Rs.750 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities at the Universities of Peradeniya, Kelaniya, Colombo, Jaffna, Rajarata, Visual & Performing Arts, Eastern and the Institute of Agro-Technology and Rural Sciences of the University of Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6827",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has given a high priority to develop the available space and infrastructure of the State universities, to fulfill the requirements of the present students and also of the future students who expect to follow the Technology Degrees and other Degree Courses. By the end of the year 2016, it is expected to enroll 1825 students to follow the Technology Degree Courses while the University Grants Commission has taken steps to enroll students at an average annual growth rate of 5 % from the year 2017 onwards. Instructions have already been issued to commence these Degree Courses in future in other Universities as well.  Accordingly, with a view to producing competent graduates to cater to the international job market and the existing development needs in the economy, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to improve the infrastructure facilities such as faculty buildings, computer units, libraries and research buildings in 08  universities, at an estimated cost of Rs.484 million in the year 2016, Rs.3,381 million and Rs.1,074 million in the year 2017 and 2018 respectively,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Awarding contracts for Eighteen (18) Civil Work Contract Packages in the Provinces of North Central and the North Western and the Kalutara District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6828",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank funded Integrated Road Investment Programme is implemented with a view to improving the access routes  between rural areas and socio-economic centres.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the 18 contract packages relevant to the civil work of 18 road sections scheduled to be implemented for the rehabilitation and improvement of rural roads so as to cover all the Districts of North Central and the North Western Provinces and also the Kalutara District, under this programme, as per the recommendation made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Reintroduction of Capital Gains Tax (CGT) Regime",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6829",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the last few decades, there has been a massive increase in the private capital of the country. The increase in prices of lands attributable to the large infrastructure developments such as road development carried out through Government funds have enabled the land owners to make significant capital gains free of taxation. This has resulted in an increase in the inequality of income distribution.  In order to rectify this situation, the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management has agreed to reintroduce the Capital Gains Tax and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Chairman of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management, to draft a New Capital Gains Tax Regime, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-14-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-06-14",
    "description": "Annual Report of the Ministry of Finance - 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6830",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of Section 13 of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.03 of 2003, the Minister of Finance is required to submit a Report on the Final Budgetary Position (Annual Report) to Parliament and to the public before 31st of May of the subsequent year.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to present in Parliament, the Annual Report of the Ministry of Finance for the year 2015, containing the updated information of the Government's Fiscal Position, consisting of 13 Chapters, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Strengthening of the Co-ordination between the Provincial Councils and the Line Ministries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6831",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- At the commencement of the Cabinet Meeting with the participation of the Chief Ministers of Provinces, the difficulties encountered in  implementing the activities of Provincial Councils efficiently and effectively were discussed and during the discussion attention was paid to  matters such as recruitment of teachers for schools under the Provincial Councils, filling of the vacancies of principals and teachers, the difficulties encountered when obtaining the resources necessary for Provincial Councils and waste disposal management.  Emphasis was also laid on the necessity of implementing development projects with a close co-ordination between the Provincial Councils and the Line Ministries.  \n\nAs per the methodology introduced through the 2016 Budget proposals, the budgetary provisions for the Provincial Councils are allocated through the Expenditure Head of the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government.  At the previous Cabinet Meeting held with the participation of the Chief Ministers of Provinces, it had been decided  to adopt the methodology previously followed till the end of the year 2015, instead of the new methodology. Accordingly, the Cabinet granted approval to amend the Appropriation Act, No.16 of 2015, to enable the General Treasury to allocate provisions directly to each Provincial Council."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "'Project on Construction of Defence Headquarters Complex at Akuregoda' \u2013 (Presenting the Report of the Committee appointed to inquire into the Consultancy Firms and related Payments",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6832",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Officials' Committee appointed to investigate into the matter concerning the consultancy firms and the related payments of the Defence Headquarters at Akuregoda, has observed that the Cabinet has not been informed of the accurate facts regarding the selection of consultancy firms and making relevant payments to such firms.  Accordingly, as per the recommendation made by the said Committee, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, not to obtain the services of the private firm which provided consultancy services for the construction of the project hereafter and to review the consultancy fee made to the said firm, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Amendment of the Sri Lanka Buddhist and Pali University of Sri Lanka Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6833",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Identifying the challenges and the limits faced by the Sri Lanka Buddhist and Pali University and also with a view to safeguarding the future safety of the University, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to amend the the Sri Lanka Buddhist and Pali University Act, No. 37 of 1995, to suit the present global trends, without any prejudice to the objectives of the Act and also to achieve them in a more realistic manner, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Implementation of Wastewater Disposal Infrastructure for Chilaw Town and the Puttalam Town and the Wastewater Disposal  System for Maharagama -  Boralesgamuwa Areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6834",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The joint proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply and Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to implement the project for the development of Wastewater Disposal Infrastructure for the Chilaw Town and the Puttalam Town and the Wastewater Disposal System for Maharagama -  Boralesgamuwa areas, and to obtain a loan of US$105 million from the EXIM Bank of China on concessionary terms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Obtaining Technical Assistance for the Implementation of Weliwita Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6835",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to obtain technical assistance of the International Finance Corporation (IFC) of the World Bank Group for the construction of the Weliwita Water Supply Project, which is the first ever water supply project constructed in Sri Lanka under the Public - Private Partnership Basis, and to appoint a Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC) and a Project Committee for the implementation of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Recommencement of the Construction Activities of Walasmulla Sathi Pola",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6836",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of Walasmulla Sathi Pola, has been completed up to the foundation level and it has been temporarily halted due to non-availability of funds for the project.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to continue the remaining construction activities of the project, with the assistance of the Construction Unit of Sri Lanka Army, who conducted the preliminary construction activities of the project, subject to an estimated cost of Rs.50 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Conducting the 3rd Meeting of Expert Group on Natural Rubber \tPrice Stabilization of the Association of Natural Rubber Producing \tCountries (ANRPC) in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6837",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to facilitate the holding of the 3rd Meeting of the Expert Group on Natural Rubber Price Stabilization of the Association of Natural Rubber Producing Countries, which is an international organization comprising of 11 natural rubber producing member countries, including Sri Lanka, in the year 2016 in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "The  Accelerated Programme for the Development of Middle Income \tHousing & Infrastructure",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6838",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the approval granted by the Cabinet, the project proposals have been called for the implementation of the Project of the Development of Middle Income Housing and Infrastructure, in eight (08) plots of land, belonging to the National Housing Development Authority (NHDA), situated in different areas of the Island, with the participation of local and foreign investors and the developers. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted the information/matters submitted by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, that, it has been recommended by the Steering Committee appointed to implement this project, to implement the housing projects in the areas of Panadura, Homagama (Jalthara Stage II), Yakkala and Ragama and to recall project proposals for the housing projects in the areas of Kundasale, Homagama, Galle and Nittambuwa."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Developing Jetty Facilities in the Jaffna Peninsula and Suburban \tIslands to transport Passengers and Cargo safely",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6839",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- People living in islands suburban to Jaffna peninsula including Delft and Nagadeepa use boat transport services for their day to day necessities. In addition to that, the tourists who visit religious places also use boats as their mode of transportation.  However, due to problems such as lack of sufficient and secure boat services, available facilities in the jetties being at a minimum level and the existing light house being in a condition which deserves renovation, have caused obstacles/impediments to the coastal passenger transportation. As a solution to this situation,  the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranathunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to develop and regulate the coastal passenger transportation activities through the Director General of Merchant Shipping and to introduce appropriate  amendments to the Boat Ordinance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Utilization  of the provisions required for conducting the National Pirivena Day Festival",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6840",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contribution rendered by the Pirivena Education, for the Buddhist Education and Culture in Sri Lanka is immense. At present, 64,606 of lay and clergy students receive education from 750 pirivenas which have been organized as Mulika Pirivenas, Maha Pirivenas and Vidyathana Pirivenas, 6,495 lay and clergy teachers are engaged in teaching in such institutions. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to conduct the Pirivena Day Festival which is held annually to appreciate the service rendered by pirivena institutions and their teachers as well as the creativity skills of  pirivena students, this time at the Getambe Stadium, Kandy on 16th, 17th and 18th July 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Relocation of City-centered Prisons to Interior Areas with more Space",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6841",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has recognized the necessity of undertaking urgent reforms in the prisons with a view to converting prisons into correction centers.  Under this programme, the priority has been given to relocate  the city-centered prisons in the less populated areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. D.M Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to entrust preparation of design and consultancy activities pertaining to the relocation of Colombo, Galle, Matara, Badulla, Trincomalee and Batticaloa Prisons, to Government owned Construction Agencies,  as recommended by the Committee appointed to expedite the prison relocation activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Meeting of Heads of National Law Enforcement Agencies (HONLEA), Asia and Pacific Region",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6842",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) functions as the main and premier body in investigating into the global illicit drug racket and the supervision of the implementation of the international treaties on drug control is carried out by the Commission on Narcotic Drugs (CND). The Meeting of Heads of National Law Enforcement Agencies (HONLEA),  Asia and Pacific Region, which functions as a subsidiary body of the Commission, deals with the new trends and matters pertaining to drugs within Asia and Pacific Region and it also provides the opportunity of exchanging views and knowledge on law enforcement against illicit drug rackets. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Rathnayake, the Minister of Law and Order and Southern Development, to provide relevant facilities to hold/conduct the above Conference in Colombo, from 22nd to 28th October 2016, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Establishment of a Domestic Airport in Badulla District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6843",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Domestic airports are located in all the other provinces of Sri Lanka, except in the Uva and Sabaragamuwa Provinces. It takes more than\t06 hours at least, to travel from Colombo to Badulla by a vehicle and\tthat time can be restricted to 25 minutes by way of flights and the establishment of an airport in the Badulla district will serve immensely for the promotion of tourism in the area and the development of  cultivation of economic crops for export purposes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to establish a domestic\tairport at Bandarawela in the Badulla district, was approved in principle by the\tCabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Supply of Medical Equipment and Services for the Epilepsy Unit\tat the National Hospital of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6844",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contracts for the supply of ward medical equipment and services to the Epilepsy Unit at the National Hospital of Sri Lanka, as per the recommendations made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Implementation of 2016 Budget Proposals - Construction of Cold \tStores",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6845",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The price fluctuation of fruits and vegetables, at different times of the year, including B onions\tand Potatoes, has caused adverse effects to the farmer as well as to the consumer.  Since the cultivation of crops in Sri Lanka\t occurs in terms of seasonal patterns, funds have been allocated through the 2016 Budget proposals for the provision of cold stores facilities, to ensure the continuous supply of harvest throughout the year.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to construct cold stores, as a pilot project, closer to the Dambulla Special Economic Centre for some selected vegetables and fruits, including B Onions and closer to the Keppetipola Special Economic Centre for some selected vegetables and fruits, including Potatoes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Central Expressway Project \u2013 obtaining consultancy services for\tthe construction of Section 2  from Meerigama to Kurunegala\t(39.91km) with a link from Meerigama to Ambepussa (9.3 km)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6846",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- A four lane Expressway with a length of 39.91 km from Meerigama to Kurunegala via Pothuhera will be constructed under Section 2 of the Central Expressway Project and a link road with 2 lanes in a length of 9.3 km from the Meerigama Interchange to Ambepussa will also be constructed. Therefore, the  proposal made  by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to initiate the procurement work required for selecting an appropriate Consultancy Company to provide the consultancy services for the supervision of these construction, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Financial assistance for disaster relief and recovery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6847",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet was informed by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to the effect that three (03) Bank accounts for the remittance of the financial donations received from local donors and five (05) accounts to deposit the donations received from foreign donors in different foreign currencies to provide relief to the people affected by the heavy floods and landslides which occurred in several districts of the island due to adverse weather conditions that prevailed in May 2016, have been opened and the funds accumulated into these accounts are credited daily, to the account opened in the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, in the name of the Deputy Secretary to the Treasury, to enable to be used for the relevant relief providing measures."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Obtaining a Credit of Special Drawing Rights (SDR) from the International  Development  Association (IDA) of the World Bank for the Competitiveness, Transparency and Fiscal Sustainability Development Policy Financing (DPF) Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6848",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Prime Minister, Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies\t and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Financial Agreement to obtain a credit facility being equivalent of US$ 100 million from the International Development Association (IDA), for the proposed programme of Economic Development in Sri Lanka, through the implementation of the identified reforms under three (03) sectors for the purposes of removing the existing impediments for the competition in the Private Sector, improving transparency and management in the Public Sector and developing government's fiscal sustainability, was approved by the\tCabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-06-21-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2016-06-21",
    "description": "Clearance of the debris of houses and garbage accumulated at Salawa area in Kosgama due to the emergency disaster situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6849",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-06-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The disposal of garbage accumulated in certain areas of  the Western Province due to the sudden disaster of floods that occurred in May 2016, has been implemented successfully and the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to employ around 20 tippers for a period of one (01) week, as per the request made by the Sri Lanka Army, utilizing the balance amount of funds allocated for the disposal of garbage accumulated due to floods, to clear the debris of the damaged houses and garbage, accumulated due to the sudden disaster which occurred  at  Salawa  area in Kosgama recently, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "'E-Motoring Project' - Department of Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6871",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The above project is expected to be implemented under three (03) components, namely the  preparation of an Electronic Documentation Management System for the Department of Motor Traffic, development  of the existing Vehicle Registration System and its database and the improvement of communication network.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to implement this 'E-Motoring Project' as a Build, Operate and Transfer (BOT) Project, as per the recommendation of the Cabinet Committee on Economic Management, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Proposals on the measures to be taken with regard to the damages caused to the houses of the residents of the area and business places due to the explosion of ammunition dump in Salawa Army Camp",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6872",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though any loss of civilian lives was not reported due to the explosion that occurred in the ammunition dump in Army Camp at Salawa, Kosgama on 2016\u201106\u201105, movable and immovable properties in 12 Grama Niladhari Divisions around the area have been damaged. Cabinet decided to provide necessary relief, as per the recommendations of the Ministerial Committee appointed under the Chairmanship of Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to examine on the payment of compensation for such damaged houses and business places. Accordingly, Rs.50,000/- per month is being paid to the families, whose houses and business places are damaged, until their resettlement in the said premises and up to now  of around 400 families have been paid Rs.50,000/- each. Since it may take several months to restore normalcy in Salawa and the surrounding area, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharashana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management,  to  provide a  monthly allowance of Rs.50,000/- each, to the rest of the families, whose houses were completely and partially damaged and are unable to resettle in their houses and to provide compensation in respect of the damages to the movable property expeditiously, as per the recommendations of the Assessing Committees appointed for the said purpose, was approved by the Cabinet.  \nIt was also decided by the Cabinet, to instruct the relevant authorities to expedite the activities of providing relief to the residents of the Western Province, including Kolonnawa, who were affected due to the flood disaster that occurred recently."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Construction of Traditional Indigenous Medical Research Hospital and Herbal Garden",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6873",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, a conspicuous tendency in Sri Lankans to move towards  the Ayurvedic and Indigenous medical treatments can be seen / witnessed. Since the traditional indigenous medical system is a precious medical system to be transferred to the present as well as future generations,  measures are being taken by the Government to take necessary action for its conservation and development. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to construct a traditional indigenous medical research hospital and a herbal garden, in associated with the 'Wedagama' model village in the Dompe Divisional Secretariat Division, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Stormwater Drainage Improvements within Western Megapolis Region",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though the Western Province accounts for only 5.7% of the total land extent of the country, it contributes more than 50% to the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and is an immensely important industrial, commercial and administrative centre in Sri Lanka. Five (05) major river basins of Sri Lanka, including Kalu and Kelani Rivers are located in the Western Province and hence, it will be vitally important to improve the existing infrastructure facilities to minimize the risk of frequent floods, in transforming the Western Region into a Megapolis on par with the international standards. As per now, around 30% of the activities of the Weras Ganga Stormwater Drainage and Environment Improvement Project have been completed. Accordingly, with a view to exploring long term solutions for the flood issues in the flood prone areas of the Western Province, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement 08 projects expeditiously, including the construction of two (02) small tunnels to enhance the capacity of disposal of stormwater to the sea and the construction of two (02) pumping stations to pump  stormwater to the sea,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Restructuring of Tea Shakthi Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6875",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to restructure the Tea Shakthi Fund, as recommended by the Officials' Committee appointed to submit the recommendations on the restructuring of the Tea Shakthi Fund and to improve the management of the twelve (12) factories belonging to the Tea Shakthi Fund, under the direct supervision of the Ministry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Establishment of the 'Engineering Council' to regulate the\tprofessional practice of Engineering in Sri Lanka by registering\tEngineering Practitioners",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6876",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Engineering professionals who qualify from different educational establishments in Sri Lanka and abroad, possess different levels of academic and professional competencies depending on the standard and level of the educational programmes they followed, practice Engineering at different levels. However, an accepted formal methodology for registering or granting licenses followed in respect of the professionals in the fields of Medicine and Law, who qualify similarly from different establishments, is  not pursued in respect of the Engineering professionals.  Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power & Renewable Energy and Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to publish 'the Engineering Council, Sri Lanka Bill' drafted for the purposes of establishing the 'Engineering Council, Sri Lanka', which shall be responsible for the maintenance of professional standard and conduct of engineering practitioners, registration of different categories of engineering practitioners and to provide for matters connected therewith or incidental thereto, in the Government Gazette and thereafter to submit same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Holding the United NationsVesak Day Celebrations in Sri Lanka in\tthe year 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6877",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It was proposed by Prof. Gunapala Malalasekara at the World Buddhist Congress held in Sri Lanka, in the year 1950, to the effect that the Vesak Day should be celebrated internationally and on a proposal subsequently made by Hon. Lakshman Kadirgamar, former Minister of Foreign Affairs of Sri Lanka, at the United Nations General Assembly in the year 1999, the tradition of celebrating the Vesak Day internationally was adopted. The United Nations Vesak Day Celebrations were held in Thailand, in the year 2016. Therefore, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, the Prime Minister, Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe and Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to hold the United Nations Vesak Day Celebrations and the Conference of the year 2017, on 12th and 13th May 2017, in Sri Lanka and to appoint a Committee to arrange the related activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Amendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No. 15 of 1979 \t(Rights of Detainees - Access to Legal Counsel)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6878",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to publish the Code of Criminal Procedure (Amendment) Bill prepared to provide for the acceptance of the right to retain and consult an Attorney-at-law of his choice at his own expenses by any person who has been arrested and detained in police custody, after recording his statements and prior to being produced before a Magistrate and provision of services of an Attorney-at-law of the Legal Aid Commission, to such person, in an instance where such person states that he is unable to retain and consult an Attorney-at-law at his own expense, in the Government Gazette and thereafter to submit the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Consolidation of Core Legislation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6879",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has become a complicated and difficult task to understand the laws/statutes enacted long ago, due to the frequent amendments made to such legislation.  In order to redress this situation, the Ministry of Justice, with the support of the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) works on to re-draft five (05) core pieces of legislation in three languages of Sinhala, Tamil and English and to consolidate the same. In considering the statutes of Evidence Ordinance, Criminal Procedure Code and Penal Code which fall under the purview of the five (05) core statutes to be consolidated under this programme, it has been apparent that there may be a potential of misunderstanding of certain words and expressions, by the public who refer such legislation, since certain words and expressions contained in such statutes are totally outdated in the present context. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to substitute or revise such words and expressions contained in the said statutes, so as to reflect and suit the contemporary language usage, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Amendment to Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act, No. 04 of 2015",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6880",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act, No.04 of 2015 was brought into operation on 16th May 2016. There have been requests to permit the giving of evidence under the said Act, from a remote location outside Sri Lanka, too.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to draft amending legislation to the Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime and Witnesses Act, No.04 of 2015, to provide for the victims and witnesses of a crime to record an evidence or a statement through audio-visual linkage, from anywhere outside Sri Lanka, without his personal attendance in Court, and to give such evidence through  Sri Lankan diplomatic Mission abroad, while ensuring the freedom and lack of any duress on the witness, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Enforcement of new Regulations in terms of the Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea (SOLAS)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6881",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the \u201cConvention for the Safety of Life at Sea\u201d (SOLAS), issued by the International Maritime Organization (IMO), in the year 1974, common and specific laws and regulations for the safety of life at sea, to be followed in the international merchant shipping affairs have been introduced. All the member states have agreed upon  to follow all these rules and regulations imposed with regard to the field of merchant shipping.  Accordingly, a Certificate detailing as to the gross mass of all the containers shipped, should be submitted, with a view to enhancing the security of the container ships, maintaining the stability/balance of the ships, storing the containers in a due manner and minimizing the environmental effects. However, no steps have been taken to issue a formal Certificate in this regard, though records of the gross weight of the export containers are kept at present.  Therefore, in order to provide for the said purpose, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to draft the Regulations prepared by the Merchant Shipping Secretariat, for the issuance of Certificates to container weight verifiers and container transporters, after having discussions with all the relevant stakeholders relating to the maritime affairs, through the Legal Draftsman and to publish the said regulations  in the Government Gazette and to submit the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Resettlement of Protracted Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) in the Northern Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6882",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Internal displacement due to conflict situation became a phenomena in Sri Lanka from the decade of 1980s and due to the said situation many  Sinhalese and Muslim families, in addition to the Tamil people, who lived in the Northern Province were internally displaced. Although the protracted IDPs commenced returning to their places of origin after conflicts were over, they could not be resettled productively, due to the lack of basic facilities. It has been identified that, for the housing requirement of the protracted returnees, 16,120 houses and 5,543 houses are required for Muslim families and Sinhalese families respectively. Due to the displacement their political rights, including the right to vote, have been adversely affected and they have to face difficulties in registering births and deaths, admitting children to schools and accessing the facilities offered by the Divisional Secretariat and other Government Institutions.  Accordingly, in order to facilitate the resettlement activities of the protracted displaced families in the Northern Province and to provide solutions for the issues  encountered by them in the said process, the approval of the Cabinet was granted to appoint a Task Force comprising of the Provincial Heads and Senior officials, under the Co\u2011chairmanship of the Ministers of Industry and Commerce; Provincial Councils and Local Government; and Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs to pursue action as per the recommendations of the said Task Force."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Development Projects on Rehabilitation & Resettlement 2016 : Development Projects implemented for the Resettled Families and Returnee Refugees in the Northern, Eastern Provinces and former threatened Villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6883",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- A special budgetary provision of Rs.14 Billion was allocated though the budget proposals 2016, for the implementation of Resettlement and Rehabilitation projects in the year 2016, for the conflict affected  areas in the Northern and Eastern Provinces and former threatened villages. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted the information submitted by Hon. D.M Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to the effect that the Ministry has implemented a number of development projects for the betterment of IDPs and returnee Refugees, including the construction of new houses, repair of partly damaged houses,  provision of sanitation facilities, supply of safe drinking water, relocation of families, provision of livelihood assistance for IDP resettled families and returnee refugees, renovation of roads and development of infrastructural facilities in the relevant areas, under the budget proposals - 2016."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Creating a Special Head in Annual Budget Estimates for the effective implementation of the Official Language Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6884",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sinhala and Tamil languages have been recognized as official languages by the Constitution of Sri Lanka and the right of the citizens of Sri Lanka to satisfy their service needs from any public institution in an official language of their preference has also been safeguarded.  Accordingly, all the public institutions in Sri Lanka, are bound to deliver their services in Sinhala and Tamil Languages in terms of the Official Languages Policy. Therefore, with the objective of facilitating the citizens to satisfy their service needs in an official language of their preference by the year 2020, the proposal made by Hon. Mano Ganeshan, the Minister of National Co-existence, Dialogue and Official Languages,  to allocate provisions by creating a separate object code in the Budget Estimates of the Ministries and Government Departments, from the year 2017, for the implementation of  the Official Languages policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Leasing of the Old Chancery Building of the Embassy of Sri  Lanka in Washington D.C.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6885",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Government owned building in Washington D.C., in which the office works of the Embassy of Sri Lanka in the United States of America were conducted until recently, is now vacant and therefore, it has been observed that, it would be better to utilize the said building in an economically productive manner beneficial to the Government of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to appoint a Technical Evaluation Committee, under the Chairmanship of the Sri Lankan Ambassador to the United States of America, to negotiate the terms and conditions pertaining to the leasing/renting of the said building and to proceed with the activities related thereto, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Kaduruwela Town Expansion Project - Phase I",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6886",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the end of the conflict situation, the economic activities in the area of Kaduruwela increased tremendously, and it has resulted in issues such as traffic congestion and parking issues; and due to the haphazard development, a number of environmental and social issues have emerged as well. The Urban Development Authority (UDA), having considered the said issues, has designed the Kaduruwela Town Expansion Project and a number of projects are to be implemented under the said programme. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the designing activities of phase 1 of the project, land development activities, construction of drainage system and land filling, to Sri Lanka Land Reclamation and Development Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-05-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-07-05",
    "description": "Maintaining a Pool of Elephants consisting of about 35 Tuskers / Male Elephants / Female Elephants under the Zoological Department to make them to participate in cultural activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6887",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Perahera culture in Sri Lanka has inherited a proud history and especially the splendid peraheras such as  Dalada Perahera  have  drawn the attention of the whole world. It has been observed that, participation of Tuskers and Elephants is essential to maintain the beauty, magnificence and sacredness of a procession. The obtaining of elephants for peraheras has become a problem when Dalada Perahera and other famous peraheras are held during the same period of time. It has been found difficult to have all the existing elephants participate in pageant occasions due to the ageing and musth of elephants.  Accordingly, with the objective of training elephants to take part in pageant activities, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to establish a pool of  tamed Elephants from Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage and Udawalawa 'Eth Athuru Sewana' if necessary, to a maximum of  35 Tuskers / Male Elephants/Female Elephants and maintain it as a unit of the Department of Zoology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Formation of an Institution for Nation Development with Civil-Military Coordination",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6888",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The knowledge and resources possessed by the Tri Forces of Sri Lanka can be utilized easily for nation building and they are prepared to bear the responsibilities in respect of the nation building mechanism using their knowledge on various fields.  As such, in order to make use of the resources, strength and training possessed by the Tri Forces for the overall national development and for the process of establishing peace, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to establish an Institution with Civil-Military coordination which functions on a mutual understanding with the civilian officers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Sri Lanka Sustainable Development Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6889",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Prime Minister, Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to publish the  Sri Lanka Sustainable Development Bill prepared for the implementation and  promotion of the National Policy and strategy on sustainable development in Sri Lanka, the establishment of a Sustainable Development Council and to provide for matters connected  therewith, in the Government Gazette and to present the same in Parliament for approval, after fulling the relevant other requirements thereto, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Introduction of a  Concessionary Period and a method of Concessionary Charges for the Applicants who delayed in applying for Registration of Transfer of Vehicles on the change of possession of motor vehicles",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6890",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tDue to usage of vehicles under the name of the first owner without the registration of the transfer where the ownership has changed for over a long period and circulation of vehicles among various persons on open transfer papers, the Government is deprived of a large amount of income including registration charges and this situation has caused many difficulties for the law enforcement institutions as well.  Although a method of delayed charges was introduced through the Motor Traffic (Fees) Regulations published in the year 2011, in a bid to minimize this trend, it is observed that the anticipated objectives have not been achieved.  As such,  the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to provide a concessionary period of three months for the vehicle owners who have not applied for registration of transfers within the specified time period, although the ownership has been changed, to register such transfers and in order to persuade such registration of transfers, to grant a concession on the additional fee levied in such instances, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Vesting of the Vocational Training Centre located at Nilaveli in the  Eastern Province with the Department of Divineguma Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6891",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tWith the objective of providing Vocational Training, the Divineguma Development Department implements various training programmes and practical workshops and such training programme and workshops are conducted at the training centres belonging to the said Department and at the Rural Development Training and Research Institute located at Borella.  However, the training workshops and lectures conducted by the Department for the beneficiaries who reside in the Northern and Eastern provinces, have to be conducted in Colombo and they encounter various practical difficulties in taking part in such workshops and lectures and the Department also faces various problems in providing them with accommodation facilities.  Therefore, in order to establish a Training Centre to conduct training programme to Divinaguma beneficiaries living in the Northern and Eastern Provinces, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment and Welfare, to vest the Vocational Training Centre Building situated in Gopalapuram, Nilaveli in the Trincomalee District, with the Department of Divineguma Development at a Government valuation of a sum of Rs.125 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities of the Universities of Sri Jayawardenapura, Sabaragamuwa, Jaffna, Kelaniya, Colombo, Peradeniya, Uva Wellassa and the South Eastern",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6892",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tIt has been planned to increase the number of students admitting to the Universities to follow Degree Courses under various subject streams annually by 5%.  As such, in order to provide facilities for the increasing number of students, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to commence the activities pertaining to the development of common infrastructure facilities in the Universities of Sri Jayawardenapura, Sabaragamuwa, Jaffna, Kelaniya, Colombo, Peradeniya and activities pertaining to the development of required infrastructure facilities to establish Information Technology (IT) Faculties in the Universities of Uva Wellassa, Sabaragamuwa and South Eastern, utilizing the financial provision of Rs.1,369 million allocated for the purpose in the year 2016, and to get the financial provisions required for the purpose in the years 2017 and 2018 from the General Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Implementation of the Tranche - 3 of the Greater Colombo Water and Wastewater Management Improvement Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6893",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to sign a Credit Agreement between the Government of Sri Lanka and the European Investment Bank, to implement the Tranche - 3 of the Greater Colombo Water and Wastewater Management Improvement Programme, at a cost of Euro156 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Obtaining a Technical Cooperation Grant of Euro 13 million from the  Federal Republic of Germany",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6894",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, to enter into an agreement for a Technical Cooperation Grant of Euro 14 million   agreed to be provided by the Federal Republic of Germany, during the visit of H.E. the President of Sri Lanka to Germany in February 2016, for the implementation of the 04 projects, namely the National Park and Buffer Zone Management Project in Wilpattu, the Vocational Training Project in the North and East, the Small and Medium sized Enterprises (SME) Sector Development Project and the Facilitating Initiatives for Social Cohesion and Transformation (FLICT) Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Payment Platform for Digital Commerce and easing of Digital Transactions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6895",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, the most convenient way adopted in the payment for goods and services by the public is the use of international credit cards such as VISA  Master Card, and American Express.  However, the adoption of such cards in Sri Lanka is still at a relatively low ebb due to various reasons including the  charges levied in such transactions.  When the value of a transaction is high, the charges levied by the relevant card scheme also rise, and the government institutions including Sri Lanka Customs, Department of Inland Revenue, Excise Department as well as the other businessmen are reluctant to use such cards.  As proposed by the Committee comprising of veteran senior officials in the relevant fields who studied the recommendations made by the Ministry of Finance and the Central Bank of Sri Lanka in this regard, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Finance, for the establishment of  a National Payment Platform as a methodology for the facilitation of digital commerce and online transactions for the Government Institutions of Sri Lanka, enterprises and citizens, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Relocation of the Welikada Prison",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6896",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Most of the Prisons in Sri Lanka are located in the middle of the relevant cities on lands which possess higher economic importance. Under the programme for relocation of Prisons situated island-wide, it is proposed to establish the Welikada prison and its sub units in a different location.  The Welikada Prison Complex is comprised of 04 sections segregated from each other and the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to acquire the land owned by the BCC Lanka Limited, situated in close proximity to the Supreme Courts Complex,  for the establishment of the Remand Prison where the suspects who have to be produced in Courts frequently are detained,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Allocation of Funds for the Development of Rural Infrastructure Facilities and Livelihood Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6897",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- A budgetary provision of Rs.13.3 billion has been allocated for the programme on Development of Rural Infrastructure Facilities through the Budget - 2016 and the project is being implemented at present. As such, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to implement a pilot project on development of rural infrastructure facilities and rural livelihood in the districts of Anuradhapura, Batticaloa and Polonnaruwa, targeting the communities which are not covered by the small scale infrastructure  development programmes implemented by various institutions, at national and provincial levels, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Scholarship Fund for the Technology Stream",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6898",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has provided a grant of Rs.100 million for the scholarship programme implemented for the students of low income families who follow the newly introduced Technology Stream of the G.C.E. (Advanced Level) and the said programme is implemented through the Department of Public Trustee.  However, since a considerable amount of the grant has to be spent on administrative matters, a situation has arisen where the anticipated objectives of the scholarship programme are not achieved. Therefore,  in order to make use of the relevant funds for the anticipated objectives, enabling a greater number of students to have the benefits, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to get the funds transferred to the Ministry of Education, which are currently credited to the Department of Public Trustee and thereafter to continuously implement this scholarship programme through an annual allocation from the Budget, under a relevant Expenditure Head of the General Treasury,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-07-12-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-07-12",
    "description": "Construction of a New Four Storied Building for the District Secretariat, Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=6899",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-07-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to award the Contract on the first phase of the construction of a new four storied building complex for the District Secretariat, Polonnaruwa, to the lowest substantially responsive bidder, as per the recommendation made by  the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
