    "doc_id": "2016-11-01-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2016-11-01",
    "description": "Construction of the North - Western Canal under the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Program",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7204",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The North-Western Province Canal Project is implemented under the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Program, with the objective of providing for 12,500 Ha of paddy land.  Under Phase-I of the Project, it is proposed to develop a length of 5.25 km in the Wemadulla Left Bank main canal up to the Nebadagahawatta Reservoir, and to construct a new sluice at Wemadulla and to construct a canal from the sluice 600 meters in length up to the Left Bank main canal.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the relevant contract, in accordance with the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-01-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2016-11-01",
    "description": "Supply of 06 Diesel Multiple Units with air conditioned passenger compartments to Sri Lanka Railways under the Indian Line of Credit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7205",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval for the procurement of 06 Diesel Multiple Units with air conditioned passenger compartments to the Sri Lanka Railways under the Indian Line of Credit, with the objective of providing a more efficient and comfortable train transport service to the people. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract, in accordance with the recommendations of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-01-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2016-11-01",
    "description": "Improvement of the Production Capacity of the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7206",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to expand the manufacturing capacity of the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation (SPMC), in order to provide good quality drugs in large quantities at lower prices to all hospitals in the country and also in a short period of time and save a considerable amount of foreign exchange. Accordingly, the Cabinet has already granted approval to implement a Project for the construction of new drug manufacturing plants with the necessary infrastructure facilities and modern equipment and in this regard, a loan facility of Japanese Yen 1,244 Million has also been provided.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract, in accordance with the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Creating a Special Unit in the Treasury for the Low Income Group  and the Middle Income Group under the Home Ownership Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7207",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government is expected to construct a total of 620,000 houses  consisting of 120,000 for the Low Income Group and 500,000 for the Middle Income Group by the year 2019, under the Low Income Group  and the Middle Income Group Home Ownership Programme. Treating this as a national priority, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to establish a Special Unit (Special Purpose) in the General Treasury, for obtaining the necessary approval expeditiously for the programme (SPV) allocating the required lands and provision of the necessary facilities to complete the project within the stipulated time frame, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Drafting a new Act to further strengthen the Coast Guard activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7208",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that the Department of Coast Guard, established by the Department of Coast Guard Act, No.41 of 2009, finds it difficult to carry out the functions expected of the Department within its existing organizational structure.  Accordingly, having taken into consideration the current needs, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to draft a new Act repealing the Department of Coast Guard Act, 41, of 2009, to further strengthen the Department of Coast Guard, as a law enforcement Institution of the Coast Guard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Provision of Funds for the implementation of the Katana Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7209",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for the implementation of the Katana Water Supply Project, aimed at providing safe drinking water to a majority of the populace living in the Katana Divisional Secretariat Division.  Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into Loan Agreements with the China Development Bank and the Bank of Ceylon for the provision of funds for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Provision of Funds for the implementation of the Thambuttegama Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7210",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for the implementation of the Thambuttegama pipe born Water Supply Project covering 42 Garama Niladhari Divisions comprising of Thalawa, Thambuttegama and Galnawa Divisional Secretary's Divisions aimed at providing safe drinking water. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into Loan Agreements with the China Development Bank and the Bank of Ceylon for the provision of funds for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Provision of Additional Funds for the Kaluganga Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7211",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work carried out in the Moragahakanda Reservoir under the Kaluganga Development Project, is expected to release 100 Cu.M. of irrigable water into the Moragahakanda Reservoir, annually and the development of a new irrigational area of 3,000 Ha, is due to be completed by the end of the year 2018.  Due to the unforeseen geological conditions and the changes in the subject area, the cost of the contract has been revised, accordingly.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into negotiations and a Loan Agreement with the Opec Fund for International Development (OFID), for the provision of a part of the additional funds so required, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding on Bilateral Consultations between Sri Lanka and Sudan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7212",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding on Bilateral Consultations between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Sudan (Northern Sudan), with a view to further strengthening the existing friendship and cooperation between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Extension of the Surgical/Medical Units in the Teaching Hospital - Karapitiya, Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7213",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Teaching Hospital - Karapitiya, Galle is the major hospital in the Galle District and it provides services to patients from the Districts of Matara and Hambantota of the Southern Province and as well as to patients from other Provinces.  This hospital consists of 60 wards with 1,838 beds and 24 Specialist Units.  The number of patients receiving treatment from this hospital and the number of surgeries done have  increased significantly, over the past several years. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon.(Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to increase the total number of beds in the hospital by 300 and to construct a 10 storeyed building with an Orthopaedic Ward to enable 130 additional surgeries to be done per week, a Plastic Surgery and Burns Unit, 02 Ear - Nose - Throat (ENT) Units, Gastro Enterology and Genito-Urology Surgery Units, a Rheumatology Unit, a Vitreo-Retinal Surgery Unit, and also a Paediatric Cardiology Unit, Nephrology, Neurology and Opthalmology wards with facilities for the treatment of children, at an estimated cost of Rs.1,401.7 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Development of Wijaya Kumaratunga Memorial Hospital at Seeduwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7214",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon.(Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, for implementation of the following two Projects for the Development of the Wijaya Kumaratunga Memorial Hospital at Seeduwa, was approved by the Cabinet. \n*\tfor expanding and modernizing the building consisting of the Hospital Office and the Clinics, at an estimated cost of Rs.35 Million; and \n\n*\tfor constructing a 06 storeyed building consisting of an Accident Ward and an Emergency Treatment Unit, Mdical and Surgical Wards, the 2nd Eye Ward, Diabetic Treatment Centre, Intensive Care Unit, Laboratory and X-ray Department, rooms for Doctors and accommodation facilities for Nurses, at an estimated cost of Rs.1,431 Million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Development of 100 Temples situated in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7215",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Most of the Buddhist temples in the Northern and Eastern Provinces can be identified as un-accesible temples with very low facilities.  Facilities for drinking water and the essential sanitary facilities in these temples are at a minimum level, in view of the limited number of families with the ability to support, the temples do not possess the financial capacities to upgrade these facilities.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Buddha Sasana, to implement a project for improving the sanitary facilities (toilet facilities etc.) in 100 selected temples with inadequate facilities situated in the Northern and Eastern Provinces, utilizing the Rs.20.25 Million donated by Rev. Ming Sheng, the Chairman of the Buddhist Association in the Gwandoon area  of China, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Guidelines for the maintenance of temporary shelters to provide protection for women victims of violence",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7216",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, in addition to legal assistance, counselling and medical services required for the women victims of violence in cases of domestic violence, rape and to sex trafficking, the need to maintain temporary shelters which provide relief for such women victims has also emerged.  The first shelter for women victims of violence  was established by the Government of Sri Lanka in the year 2012 and subsequently, several such centres have been established on a regional level. Further, such temporary shelters are maintained at private premises as well, with the assistance of government hospitals, the Police and Non-Government Organizations. As such, the Cabinet granted its approval for the Guidelines submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, for the maintenance of such shelters to provide protection for women who become victims of violence due to various reasons."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Upgrading the Printing Press in the Department of Examinations, Sri Lanka based on new technology",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7217",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka annually conducts over 270 examinations and the Press of the Department prints over 160 Lakhs of question papers including a large number of other documentation.  It has been  identified that the Press needs modernization if it were to print question papers with a high quality finish, devoid of defects and preserving the confidentiality it requires.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasa, the Minister of Education, for the purchase of printing machines of digital technology and equipment necessary for the press of the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka, at an estimated cost of Rs.530 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Re-calling of Nominations of the Pudukuduirippu and the Maritimepattu Pradeshiya Sabhas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7218",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The elections of the Pudukuduirippu and the Maritimepattu Pradeshiya Sabhas in the Mulativu District was scheduled to be held on 2011-03-17  but due to various reasons, the elections had to be postponed from time to time.  Although, the elections were postponed, the nominations submitted are in force even by now.  Hence, a necessity for re-calling nominations, has arisen due to demise of the candidate who have submitted nominations or the candidate exceeding the age of 35 years who when submitting nominations was below the age of 35 years. Further, the elections of the above local authorities should be held under the proportional representation system that existed then, in accordance with the provisions of the Local Authorities Elections Act.  However, it is observed that holding elections for these two local authorities would be appropriate under the mixed system of elections, since the delimitation activities of the wards of Local Authorities are almost at the final stage. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapaha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation providing for holding of elections for the above two local authorities under the mixed system of elections based on the ward system re-calling nominations and calling for fresh nominations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Resettlement of Landless Internally Displaced (IDP) Families residing in Welfare Centres",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7219",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures are being taken by the Government to accelerate the resettlement activities of the IDP families residing in the Welfare Centres.  There are, presently, 971 such families residing in the Welfare Centres in the Jaffna District and measures have been taken to resettle 462 families out of these 682 landless families, in alternative lands and there still have 220 families for whom lands remain to be identified for resettlement.  Since there is a scarcity of state lands in the Jaffna District, it has been proposed  to purchase private lands so as to provide 20 perches of land per family  in order to resettle the 220 families.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to allocate a maximum sum of Rs.88 Million, to purchase the private lands required for the purpose, through the District Secretary Jaffna, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Construction of Baddegama, Wanathawilluwa, Meegahathenna and Katupotha Police Stations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7220",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing a more efficient service to the general public, a programme for constructing Police Stations with new facilities is being presently implemented. Under this programme, in addition to the renovation of the existing Police Stations, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, for the construction of new buildings for the Baddegama, Wanathawilluwa, Meegahathenna and Katupotha Police Stations housed in rented out buildings or very old buildings, at an estimated cost of Rs.370.3 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "The Project for Construction of the Peradeniya Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7221",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although, it was planned to initiate the development activities in the year 2008 of the Peradeniya Police Station which is housed in an area, where there is a large local as well as foreign population, the construction work has not been carried out so far due to various reasons.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to launch the project for constructing a state-of-the art Police Station at Peradeniya to suit the present day needs, at an estimated cost of Rs.141 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Prohibition of Cinnamon imports to Sri Lanka and the Amendment of Re-export Procedures of Spices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7222",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Cinnamon has been able to acquire a long standing reputation due to its unique quality, aroma, taste, flavour and colour.  However, there has been reports recently of incidents of importing cinnamon to Sri Lanka from various countries and re-exporting same which has adversely affected the reputation of the Sri Lanka Cinnamon (Ceylon Cinnamon) in the global market.  Having taken this situation into consideration, the proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Primary Industries, to band the import of cinnamon to Sri Lanka from other countries and taking into consideration, the importance of reviewing the Re-export Procedure through Sri Lanka Ports, to appoint an Officials' Committee, to amend the scheme for Temporary Importation for Exporting Processing (TIEP),  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Construction of the Arrivals Passenger Terminal Building at the Bandaranayke International Airport (BIA), Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7223",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the construction of  the New Immigration Hall and the Electronic Mall, at the Arrivals Passenger Terminal Building at the BIA, Katunayake as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Expansion to the Departure Public Concourse at the Bandaranayke International Airport (BIA), Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7224",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the expansion of the Departure Public Concourse at BIA, Katunayake, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Supply of 10 Diesel Electric Locomotives to Sri Lanka Railways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7225",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing a more efficient Railway transport service to the people, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the procurement of 10 Diesel Electric Locomotives to the Sri Lanka Railway Department under the Indian Line of Credit, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Awarding of the contract for the construction of the section from Meerigama to Kurunegala of the Central Expressway Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7226",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Section 2 of of the Central Expressway starts from Meerigama and runs up to Kurunegala, a length of 39.29 km.  Considering the volume of work involved in the section, the contract has been divided into 04 civil work packages. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract of the 04 civil work packages, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities at the State Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7227",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has accorded high priority to develop the available space and the infrastructure facilities of the State Universities and to provide the students engaged in studies in these Universities with a qualitative higher education.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to implement the project for the development of infrastructure facilities of the Bhiksu University of Sri Lanka, the Universities of Wayamba & Ruhuna and also the Sri Palee Campus of the University of Colombo and the Trincomalee Campus of the Eastern University, at an estimated cost of Rs.2,670 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-08-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2016-11-08",
    "description": "Renovation of the Cardiology Unit of the National Hospital, Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7228",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cardiology Unit of the National Hospital of Sri Lanka provides an immense service to cure the heart patients with various types of cardiac complications, coming from all over the island.  Since the building complex where the Cardiology Unit of the National Hospital is housed is in a dilapidated condition, the Cabinet has already granted approval to renovate the building. After the commencement of the renovation activities, considering the new proposals made by the specialists attached to the Cardiac Unit, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, for installing of a Central Air condition Network for the building complex to enable successful surgeries to be performed on patients, carry out other repairs which are absolutely necessary and also to modernize the Cardiac Unit, at a revised estimated cost of Rs.186.32 Million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
