    "doc_id": "2016-11-29-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2016-11-29",
    "description": "Allocation of 100 Housing Units to the Sri Lanka Police from the \u2018Nila Sevana\u2019 Project at Wekunagoda, Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7288",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- \u2018Nila Sevana\u2019 Project at Wekunagoda, Galle is a project jointly carried out under a tripartite Agreement by the Board of Investment, Ministry of Public Administration and Management and the Private Sector. The proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayaka, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, seeking the allocation of Treasury Funds of Rs.333 to the Sri Lanka Police to provide 100 units from the said Project to the Police personnel such as Police Constables, Police Sergeants and Police Officers in the Inspector Grades serving in the Galle area needing housing facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2016-11-29-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2016-11-29",
    "description": "Procuring 1,000 new 40-46 seater (2x2) high back, buses for the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7289",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2016-11-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids were invited for repairing 1,000 old buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board but since the repairing cost of a bus, in accordance with the responses received was almost equal to the cost of procuring a new bus, it was found that repairing is not economically productive.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to suspend the project for the repairing of 1,000 buses and instead to purchase 40-46 seater (2x2) high back, 1,000 new passenger buses, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
