    "doc_id": "2017-07-04-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-07-04",
    "description": "Commemoration of the World Post Day 2017 - Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7882",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Arrangements have been made to hold the 143rd Anniversary of the  Commemoration of the World Post Day which falls on the 09th of October 2017 centered around the North Central Province. Accordingly, Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs informed the Cabinet that action has been taken to organize activities pertaining to holding of the National Commemoration of the World Post Day on the 09th of October 2017 in Polonnaruwa under the patronage of H.E. the President, and concurrent to the above, to renovate 34 Post Offices and Sub\u2011Post Offices in the Districts of Polonnaruwa and Anuradhapura with modern facilities, to conduct blood donation campaigns and social service projects at Divisional Level with the contribution and participation of all employees of the Postal Department and to carry out the evaluation programmes of a Postal Staff of 25,000 employees."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-04-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-07-04",
    "description": "Release of a block of land for an Integrated Solid Waste Management Project implemented by the Urban Council of Chillaw, Pradeshiya Sabha of Chillaw and Pradeshiya Sabha of Arachchikattuwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7883",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The daily collection of Solid Waste within the limits of the Chillaw Urban Council is around 18 to 20 Mt while within the limits of the Pradeshiya Sabha of Chillaw and Arachchikattuwa the Solid Waste collection daily amounts to around 06 to 05 Mt, respectively. These Solid Waste is disposed of in sites which are not scientifically developed for such dumping and as a result, environmental and societal issues have cropped up. As such, an integrated Waste Management Project has been planned to be implemented by these three (03)  Local Government Institutions for the management of the non\u2011degradable waste collected within their limits. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to vest a plot of land in extent of 05 acres out of the land called Manaweriyawatta, situated in the Karukkuliya Grama Niladhari Division within the Divisional Secretary's Division of Arachchikattuwa  belonging to the Land Reform Commission and presently possessed by the National Livestock Development Board, with the Chillaw Urban Council on a 30 year lease basis in order to implement the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-04-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-07-04",
    "description": "Acquisition of a land to the Sri Lanka Police for the construction of the  Bulathsinhala Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7884",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to vest a land in extent of 04 acres owned by the Horana Plantation Company situated in the Athura village in the Bulathsinhala Grama Niladhari Division with the Sri Lanka Police to construct a building to house the Bulathsinhala Police Station, presently functioning in a closed down school building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-04-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-07-04",
    "description": "Establishment of a Tamil Medium Secondary School in the Matugama town",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7885",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Matugama Educational Zone of the Kalutara District  there are 18 estate and other schools which provide Tamil Medium education. These schools are primary schools that conduct classes only from Grade 1 to 5. As such, there are no Tamil Medium schools in the Zone, suitable for the students to seek education for the Advanced Level standards and therefore, the Tamil Medium students have to often attend the schools either in the Kalutara or Horana Educational Zones. As for the students who follow the Advanced Lelvel Classes in Science and Maths subjects, they have to invariably attend to schools situated in the Beruwela or Darga town educational zones.  \n\n\nTherefore, it has been identified that it is essential to commence a secondary school in the Tamil Medium in close proximity with the Matugama town. \n\nAccordingly, taking into consideration the joint proposal made by Hon. Mano Ganeshan, the Minister of National Co-existence, Dialogue and Official Languages and Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, the Cabinet granted approval for the establishment of a Tamil Medium Secondary School in close proximity with the Matugama town with the corporation of the Ministry of Education and the Western Provincial Ministry of Education and to set apart a land in extent of about 05 acres for the purpose, from the Matugama Estate managed by the Namunukula Estate Company."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-04-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-07-04",
    "description": "Augmentation of water pipelines concurrent to the improvement of the Orugodawatta - Ambatale Road Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7886",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The augmentation of water distribution pipelines from Orugodawatta up to Kaduwela are required to be carried out concurrent to the development of the Orugodawatta - Ambatale Road Development Project. The Cabinet has granted approval to award the contract of this project for a sum of Euro 46.21 million at its  meeting held on 2017\u201103\u201121. While the Uni Credit Bank of Austria has consented to provide 85% of the required funds for the project, the People's Bank has expressed its willing to provide the balance  of 15%.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into the relevant loan Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
