    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The absence of a developed young agricultural community in the country to undertake agricultural activities using advanced technology, with entrepreneurial capacity  has been identified as a problem directly affecting the low productivity in the field of agriculture of the country.  Even though a considerable number of young people qualify annually from the Schools of Agriculture and from the Faculties of Agriculture in the Universities, majority of them drift away from the agriculture sector as a vocation, as a result of the field of agriculture being a non-profitable venture when compared to that of other fields and involvement in the agricultural sector is a hardly recognized vocation in the society. \n\nIt has been planned to implement a project to produce young agriculture entrepreneurs who could engage themselves in the commercial agriculture under the National Programme on Food Production, with a view to maintaining the contribution of the agriculture sector towards the country's national production at a high level. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to provide loan facilities to obtain resources inclusive of modern agricultural technological equipment for 100 young entrepreneurs selected from the Kurunegala District under its pilot project and on the basis of the success of the pilot project to implement the project with the participation of 1000 young entrepreneurs from the South Western, North Central and Eastern Provinces and at the next stage, with the participation of 10,000 young men and women agri entrepreneurs from all parts of the island, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Grant and Implementation Agreement between the Millennium Challenge Corporation and the Government of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7950",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Millennium Challenge Corporation (MCC) of the United States of America which is an agency for granting foreign aid operating aimed at long term economic development through the creation of economic growth of selected countries is due to arrange a grant of US$ 7.4 million to the Government of Sri Lanka within the next period of five years for the development of several important sectors conducive to the economic  progress of the country. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to enter into an agreement between the Millennium Challenge Corporation and the Government of Sri Lanka to obtain the said grant and for the implementation of the programmes under its purview, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Providing of hostel facilities for the Staff of the Defence Services Command and Staff College",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7951",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Annually, more than 130 local and foreign officers complete the training given by the Defence Services Command and Staff College established to train the staff officers of the Three Armed Forces and the Public Service to bear the responsibilities of high positions, direct operations and perform the duties entrusted to them efficiently.  Therefore, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to construct a three storey building and a four storey building to provide  hostel facilities for the Senior Non\u2011Commissioned Officers of the Three Armed Forces and for the Officers of other ranks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Phasing-out of Hydrochloroflurocarbon harmful to the Ozone Strata",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7952",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been working on minimizing the use of ozone depleting substance known as Hydrochloroflurocarbon, since 1989 and introducing ozone friendly alternative substances, in accordance with the agreements reached and the commitments made with the Vienna Convention and the Montreal Protocol on protection of the Ozone Layer.  Accordingly, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 16\u201108\u20112016 appointed a Technical Committee to submit short term and long term solutions for imposing limits on the import of  Hydrochloroflurocarbon chemical while also controlling the adverse effects likely to occur on the maintenance and repair of refrigeration and air conditioning systems which necessitate the use of Hydrochloroflurocarbon.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the implementation of the recommendations of the Committee along with the following recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet: \n\n\n*\tto impose a ban with immediate effect, on the import of used and reconditioned equipment falling within the category with the ozone depleting substances mentioned in the Montreal Protocol. including Refrigerators, Deep Freezers, Air conditioning Systems and Heat Pump Units, Water Coolers, Ice Machines, Vehicle Deep Freezers or Containers.  \n\n*\tto impose a ban with effect from 01\u201101\u20112018, on the importation to Sri Lanka of equipment or spares manufacturing or assembling in Sri Lanka using the Hydrochloroflurocarbon  exceeding the Global Warming Potential 100, and Ozone Depleting Potential 0.03. \n\n*\tto impose a ban with effect from 01\u201101\u20112021, on the importation to Sri Lanka, of equipment or spares manufacturing or assembling in Sri Lanka using the Hydrochloroflurocarbon not exceeding the Global Warming Potential 100, and Ozone Depleting Potential 0.03. \n\n*\tto make it mandatory to use Refrigerant Recovery and Recycling Machine with effect 01\u201101\u20112019 at all work shops which are engaged in  services, maintenance and repair of Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Systems to be incorporated as a condition, when issuing environment protection licenses."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Payment of compensation to the affected persons due to the acquisition of their lands for the Moragahakanda Project, which had been provided to them in lieu of their lands inundated by Wemedilla Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7953",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The people who were deprived of their lands at the acquisition of lands for the implementation of the Wemedilla Reservoir project covering the Divisional  Secretary's Divisions of Naula, Galewela and Dambulla in the Matale District were provided with lands from the Laggala - Pallegama Divisional Secretary's Division under the Kandepitawala reservoir scheme in the year 2008.  However, action has been taken to acquire the lands so provided once again for the Moragahakanda - Kaluganga development project, and as such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, for the payment of cash as compensation for 53 persons who were so deprived of their lands in lieu of alternative lands, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Preparation of a Methodology to conduct the practical tests pertaining to issuing of Driving Licenses in a more qualitative and productive manner",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7954",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Public criticisms have been leveled against the malpractices that occur due to the monopoly that exist in conducting the practical tests for issuing Driving Licenses and it has been pointed out that this situation acts as a barrier to producing disciplined drivers. When considering the road accidents that presently occur the negligence of the drivers and their lack of knowledge of the road rules further justifies the above mentioned situation. \n\nAs a solution to this state of affairs, a proposal has been made to identify  suitable parties to conduct these practice tests in addition to the Examiners of Motor Vehicles of the Department of Motor Traffic. Through this process, it is anticipated to conduct the practical tests in a more qualitative manner and through proper regulation to exert accountability. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to appoint an Officials' Committee comprising of the representatives of the relevant institutions to obtain a Report with recommendations for a suitable methodology to be adopted in this process, after a study, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Awarding of a new house as the super prize in 'Sevana' Lottery Draw",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7955",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- In addition to the 'Sevana' instant Lottery conducted by the National Lotteries Board, another Lottery draw named 'Sevana' has been released to the market to coincide to the National Housing Day which fell on 2017\u201106\u201123 and its maiden draw is due to be held on 2017\u201107\u201127. As the super prize of this draw, it has been proposed to award a new house with all modern facilities from a suburb of Colombo or close to another urban area. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Foreign Affairs to purchase new houses from an institution recommended by the Ministry of Housing and Construction and the National Housing Development Authority to be awarded as prices, and to make the relevant contribution of the sales revenue of this Lottery to the Sevana Trust Fund, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Manufacture of 100 special boats to salvage the lives of victims in situations of flood disaster",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7956",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- During flood disasters boats have to be used to salvage the lives of people and to distribute food and other basic amenities to the people caught in the floods.  In this respect, the inability to find the required number of boats and the non\u2011availability of the basic essential equipment in certain boats, was a major obstacle faced during the past flood situations. As a solution to this problem, the Sri Lanka Navy has manufactured a special boat which could be used during the flood disaster situations. This boat can be made use of during night time for search and salvage operations and also for relief activities and it consists of life saving jackets, flash lights, solar panels, first aid kits and communication equipments and it can accommodate around 10 persons at a time.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management to get such 100 special boats manufactured by the Navy and to identify high risk prone areas of flood disaster and station them in close proximity to such areas, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "National Health Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7957",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The existing National Health Policy is one which had been prepared in the year 1996 and as such, the need has arisen for the introduction of a new National Health Policy to address the present emerging problems. \n\nAccordingly, within a period of three (03) years from 2014 to 2016 a new National Health Policy has been designed with the participation of professional experts of all sectors of the Health Service, Professionals and the Professional Institutions. In this respect, the concept of the 'Universal Health Coverage' was taken into consideration for the introduction of the new Health Policy aimed at ensuring the rights of patients and social justice centered around the patients and the public.\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine for the approval of the said National Health Policy designed for a period of 10 years from 2016 to 2025 identifying the following major policy directions, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tStrengthening of services delivery for achieving the goals of preventive health. \n\n*\tprovision of an appropriate and accessible high quality curative care for all citizens of Sri Lanka.\n\n*\tPromotion of equitable access to qualitative rehabilitation care.\n\n\n*\tEstablishment of a planned methodology based on the service supply data to strengthen the methodologies of uninterrupted service supplies.\n\n*\tDevelopment of new strategies to minimize of out of pocket spending for patients and to reduce of financial risk.\n\n*\tEnsure a comprehensive health system through a better re\u2011structure including human resource management.\n\n*\tDevelopment of  a strategic partnership with all health care providers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Appointment of a Board of Administration for the Ranmihithenna National Tele-Cinema Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7958",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that it is essential to appoint a Board of Administration for the creative and efficient performance of the functions of the Ranmihithenna National Tele-Cinema Park and also to prevent unnecessary delays in the  decision making process. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to appoint a Board of Administration comprising of experts pertaining to the field and the representatives of the relevant institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Vesting of land for the Salawa Town Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7959",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the explosion of the Armoury at the Salawa Army Camp premises at Kosgama, last year, damages were caused to a number of public and private properties.  In accordance with the recommendations of the special Committee appointed to make recommendations for the re\u2011development of the township and the buildings damaged by the explosion, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to vest a land in extent of 04 Acres, 02 Roods, 24.40 Perches with the Urban Development Authority as a free grant, from the premises of the Salawa Army Camp,  with the concurrence of the Sri Lanka Army, for the expeditious commencement of the following projects, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tWidening of the main road to form four lanes\n*\tAllocation of land for the banks\n*\tConstruction of the Community Centre\n*\tConstruction of the Super Market\n*\tConstruction of 35 Nos. of shops\n*\tConstruction of a Children's Park and a Play Ground\n*\tConstruction of food courts"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Conducting of international level training courses and workshops by the  Irrigation Training Institute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7960",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that there is a possibility of building up an international demand for short term training courses in respect of the development which existed with the system of irrigational civilization of Sri Lanka and the allied subjects.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to provide the necessary facilities and to design an administrative and financial methodology to conduct international level training courses at the Kotmale International Training Institute for Irrigation and Water Management (KTI-IWM)  and the Galgamuwa Irrigation Training Institute with the collaboration of the institutions like the International Irrigation and Water Management Institute and the International Water Centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Amendment of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- As it has been identified that the appointment of Justices of the Peace for Administrative Districts instead of appointing them for a Judicial Zone, Judicial District or Division is more practicable and appropriate, the Cabinet has granted approval to amend section 45 of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978, with a view to making provision in that regard.   \n\nIn this context, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Justice, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for the amendment of Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 including the necessary provision to state that the Justices of Peace already appointed before the date of operation of this amendment shall be deemed to be appointed for the  relevant Administrative District containing the Divisional Secretary Division, in which their residences were situated at the time of the appointment and with the objective of implementing a code of conduct in respect of the Justices of the Peace to enable the Minister to make regulations for the suspension, cancellation and termination of the appointment of the Justices of the Peace, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Providing of relief to the People affected by Floods and Landslides Living in the plantation areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7962",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the floods and landslides that occurred in the month of May in 2017, in the Districts of Galle, Ratnapura, Kegalle and Hatton, approximately 872 families living in the plantation areas were severely affected and most of their properties were destroyed. The people so affected are now residing in temporary sheds and common shelters and as such, measures are needed to be taken to relocate and their infrastructure facilities renovated. \n\n\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of  Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to identify suitable land to construct new houses for the re-location  of persons so affected at a cost of Rs.500 million, to provide roofing sheets for the houses that were damaged, to construct toilets in affected plantation areas, to implement water supply projects, to provide with water tanks, and to upgrade the Child Development Centres damaged due to the disaster, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "The prevention of unauthorized dumping of solid waste in Colombo and the suburban areas and the emergency measures to be taken for controlling of the Dengue Epidemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7963",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval to prepare an operational mechanism  to minimize the issues faced due to haphazard disposal of solid waste informally in Colombo and the suburban areas. Accordingly, an Operational Office has already been set up in the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government,  integrating the Tri\u2011Armed Forces, and the Police including other Institutions and the said office receives a considerable number of complaints on a daily basis. The complaints reveal that the required  cooperation of the public is not forthcoming for the disposal of waste and  the haphazard disposal of waste takes place specially during the night. Accordingly, the Joint proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government  and Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development to implement the following steps decided upon to be carried out at the meeting held under the Chairmanship of the Prime Minister, was approved by the Cabinet: \n\n*\tinstallation of CCTV Cameras to observe the common sites where unauthorized waste is disposed of and to adopt a methodology to enable the officers of the Operational Office to monitor the images received from such cameras through mobile phones. \n\n*  making it compulsory to exhibit name boards containing all information pertaining to the construction sites in Colombo and the suburban areas, the names of the legal owners of such construction sites and the information regarding the contractor with other details. \n\n*  \tinstituting legal action against persons in their personal name working in such manner as to make way for mosquito breeding in schools, state institutions and other institutions. \n\n*  \tmake regulations under the Public Security Ordinance permitting the entry into premises which are under lock and key to conduct investigations and also to take legal action against such persons.   \n\n*\tto attach the required number of officers to the Operational Office to enable it to operate during the entire 24 hours and to provide such facilities in respect of the above."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Construction of the Academic and Administrative Building of the Nurses Training School, Kalutara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7964",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The has Government has decided to increase the intake of trainees for training in nursing in order to provide a qualitative health service. As such, it has been planned to construct a new academic and an administrative building for the Nurses Training School, Kalutara which functions presently within the National Institute of Health Sciences, amidst great difficulties. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for a sum of Rs.714.2 million (with tax), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Modernization of the Jaya Container Terminal of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7965",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The capacity of the Jaya Container Terminal which is fully owned and operated by the Sri Lanka Port Authority has to be modernized expeditiously in order to accommodate large ships. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to implement the modernization work of Phase V of the terminal, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Empowerment of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption is the  State Institution established in Sri Lanka for eradicating bribery and corruption. Certain investigations to be handled by this Commission are of a very complex nature and as such, it has been identified that providing modern technology support and updating the knowledge and enhancing the skills of the officers are essential for enhancing the efficiency of the Commission, the Bureau for Democracy, Human Rights and Labour Affairs of the State Department of the United States of America has agreed to provide financial support for this purpose. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena to enter into the relevant Memoranda of Understanding to obtain the grant of US$ 235,000 (approximately Rs.35.25 million) agreed to be provided by the above Bureau, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy Services to implement the Disaster Management Process in Sri Lanka more efficiently and effectively",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The tendency for natural calamities has been increased due to climatic changes and concurrently the man made disasters are also increasing.  Therefore, the need for a long term plan has arisen for the management of these disaster situations efficiently and effectively. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management,  to appoint an Expert Committee comprising of experts in the field, under the Chairmanship of the Minister of Disaster Management to get the necessary advice, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-07-18-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-07-18",
    "description": "Adoption of expeditious remedial measures to resolve the issues  associated with the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=7968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-07-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2017\u201106\u201127 appointed a Ministerial Sub\u2011Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera the  Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development and the State Minister of Mahaweli Development to examine and submit a Report to the Cabinet on the difficulties encountered by the residents of the area as a result of the construction of tunnels of the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Scheme. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development and the State Minister of Mahaweli Development, to implement the following recommendations expeditiously to provide relief for the difficulties faced by the residents of the area, as a result of the construction of tunnels of the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Scheme, subsequent to a visit to the relevant area and  discussions had with the relevant parties, was approved by the Cabinet: \n\n*\tHaving made a comprehensive study, to construct six (06) large deep wells associated with the suitable locations.\n\n*\tImplement a special programme to provide water tanks within the next two (02) weeks, to family units, if any, which have not been provided with water tanks so far; \n\n*\tRelease twenty (20) tractor bowsers in the possession of the Ministry of Home Affairs, to the District Secretary, Badulla expeditiously, for further strengthening of the water distribution process; \n\n*\tExpedite the process of the payment of compensation for the damaged properties. \n\n*\tEstablishment of a special unit by the National Buildings Research Institute for a more efficient service. \n\n*\tRelease of a financial provision of Rs.100 million expeditiously to the Provincial Council for the rehabilitation of the Rural Road Network of the affected areas. \n\n*\tStrengthen the 'Secretariat for Relief to Persons' already established to ensure that the relief activities are efficient. \n\n* \tReview of the progress of the relief measures once in two weeks or monthly. \n\n*\tAllocation of funds necessary for expediting the construction work of the proposed Bandarawela Multi Water Scheme from the Budget 2018. \n\n*\tRelease provision of Rs.100 million for the restoration of the affected small reservoirs.   \n\n*\tHand over of the possession of the lands identified to be re\u2011settled expeditiously to the Divisional Secretary, Bandarawela.  \n\n*\tProvide the necessary additional financial provision to renovate the affected schools expeditiously and put them in order.   \n\n*\tProvide a 2 year relief period for the affected families for the repayment of installments of housing and cultivation loans obtained by them. \n\n*\tImplement a special alternative livelihood development plan expeditiously in the affected areas. \n\n*\tAction to be taken by the Company in Iran to close the water spill in the tunnel. \n\n*\tFuture drilling activities of the project to be considered only on the recommendations of the International Experts and on the recommendations made by a Committee of Local Experts."
  },
