    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction work of Phase I of the four storey building constructed for the District Secretariat in Polonnaruwa is to be completed before the end of this year and to coincide with same, the construction work of Phase II of the project has to be commenced expeditiously.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs to award the contract for the  construction work of Phase II, taking into consideration the necessity to bring the various divisions of the District Secretariat of Polonnaruwa presently functioning in several locations, under one roof, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-01-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-08-01",
    "description": "Restructure of the ownership of the Hyatt Hotel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8005",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-08-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The policy of the government is to promote rapid, sustainable and inclusive economic development by improving competitiveness and the performance of the state owned enterprises under its control.  Accordingly, the government has planned to restructure the ownership of a several selected non\u2011strategic state owned enterprises. \n\nA further substantial investment has to be made, in order to develop it to its full  potential owned by the Grand Hyatt Hotel project constructed by the Canwill holdings (Pvt) Ltd. belonging to the Government Institutions namely the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation, Litro Gas Company and the Employees' Provident Fund. As there are other priority issues, incurring of further funds of the public institutions for a luxury hotel project of this nature which  serves foreign tourists and only a handful of high net worth individuals in Sri Lanka is not appropriate and as such, it has been decided to call for private investment for the project. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Public Enterprise Development, to appoint a Procurement Committee and a Technology Evaluation Committee to select suitable private investors to divest  the government owned shares of the Canwill Holdings (Pvt) Ltd. implementing the Grand Hyatt Hotel Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-08-01-021-en",
