    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Construction of a building complex for the National Institute of Social Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8124",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, to award the contract to construct a building complex on design and build basis for the National Institute of Social Development in the Seeduwa area, to the State Engineering Corporation of Sri Lanka, at a cost of Rs.818.63 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Construction of a five storey building at the School of Nursing, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8125",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- In providing a high qualitative health care service, the contribution of the Nursing Officers is of paramount importance. The Government has identified that the facilities of the Nurses Training School in Colombo have to be improved to fulfill the need of increasing the number of trained Nursing Officers with high skills and the knowledge of scientific and up to date information. The Nurses Training School in Colombo established in the year 1939 is one of the major Training Schools in the country and the facilities available there, at present, is sufficient only to train 100 Nurses annually. As such, it has been planned to construct a building consisting of five storeys to improve the facilities of the Nurses Training School in Colombo to enable around 600 Nursing Students to be trained annually. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract to the State Engineering Corporation with a view to implementing the project expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Supply and Delivery of New Tyre Kits to the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8126",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called for, under open competitive bidding to select a suitable institution for the supply and delivery of New Tyre Kits to the buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board and in response 02 bidders have submitted their bids. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract to M/s. Ceat Kelani International Tyres (Pvt) Ltd., for the supply of 33,672 tyre kits of different varieties, for a sum of Rs.1,115 million, as per the recommendation of the  Technical Evaluation Committee appointed to evaluate the prices and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-032-en",
    "num": "32",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "The Mixed Development Project  in the Land of Charlmers Granaries in Colombo Fort",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8127",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to establish a Multi-modal Transport Hub integrating all modes of transport in Colombo Fort and Pettah. As such, it has been decided to make use of the land of the Charlmers Granaries in extent of 9 Acres 3 Roods 27 Perches, belonging to the Urban Development Authority situated in front of the Fort Railway Station to carry out the necessary development activities under the project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to call for competitive bids under the Multi-madel Transport Hub Project to select a suitable investor to develop the land as a 'Gate to the City of Colombo', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-033-en",
    "num": "33",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Establishment of the Country Office of the International Fund (IFAD) for Agricultural Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8128",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Fund for Agricultural Development is a special agency of the United Nations dedicated to alleviate the rural poverty in the developing countries. The said agency which provided support for the implementation of the various projects in Sri Lanka since 1978 continue to provide the necessary support presently too, for the various agricultural development programmes.  In order to strengthen its operational activities carried out in Sri Lanka, the  fund intends to open a country office.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to sign an Agreement between the International Fund for Agricultural Development and the Government of Sri Lanka, for the establishment of its country office in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-034-en",
    "num": "34",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Tentative Programme for the Budget Debate for the Financial Year 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8129",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, presented the tentative programme for the Budget Debate for the Financial Year 2018 to the Cabinet and the Cabinet noted same. \n\nAccordingly, the budget speech for the financial year 2018 will be delivered on 09th November 2017 and  it has been planned to conduct the Parliamentary Debate on the Second Reading of the Appropriation Bill on 10th, 11th, 13th, 14th and 15th November 2017, to commence its Committee Stage Debate on 2017-11-16 and to conduct the vote of the Third Reading of the Appropriation Bill on 2017-12-09."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-035-en",
    "num": "35",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Appropriation Bill for the Financial Year 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8130",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Action has been taken to table the Appropriation Bill for the Financial Year 2018 in Parliament at the end of September 2017. The General Treasury has prepared these Budget Estimates, based on the Government policy priorities, taking into consideration the total resources which may be available for the Medium Term Budgetary Framework 2018 - 2020. Attention has also been drawn to the matters surfaced at the budget discussions with the Line Ministries and the Provincial Councils.  \n\nAccordingly, the total expenditure of the Government for the financial year 2018 has been estimated at Rs.3,982 billion. Authority need to be derived through the proposed Appropriation Bill to incur the expenditure amounting to Rs.1,977 billion from the said total amount, other than the expenditure to be incurred under laws passed by Parliament such as for servicing and repayment of public debt and payment of Widows/Widowers and Orphans Pension etc amounting to Rs.2,005.1 billion for the year 2018, from this Recurrent Expenditure is estimated at Rs.1,308.9 billion and the Capital Expenditure is estimated at Rs.668 billion. Further, the total estimated Government Revenue and the Foreign Grants for the year 2018, is estimated at Rs.2,175 billion and accordingly, Rs.1,813 billion has to be obtained as loans by way of domestic and international resources, including Rs.6 billion for the advanced accounts expenditure of the Government. \n\nThe proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2018 including the draft budgetary estimates, for approval in Parliament having published the same in the Government Gazette, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-12-036-en",
    "num": "36",
    "date_str": "2017-09-12",
    "description": "Museum of Traditional Technological Heritage and an Information Centre in Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8131",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The establishment of a Heritage Museum and an Information Centre which reflect the pristine traditional technology such as the past towns and garden designing, technological heritage, traditional irrigation and water supply systems, food preservation methods, mode of transport, architecture etc. different to that of a normal museum has been identified as a need of the time.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena and Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of Internal Affairs, Wayamba Development and Cultural Affairs, to establish a Heritage Museum and an Information Centre in Polonnaruwa which comprises of galleries designed to display the important milestones in the field of traditional technology and the period of governance from the pre-historic era to the present day, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on co-operation between Sri Lanka and Australia in regard to the prevention of various crimes committed across Borders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8132",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with a view to strengthening and for further promotion of the existing co-operation between Sri Lanka and Australia in regard to the prevention of human smuggling and other Transnational Border Crime. Through this, both parties will reap the  benefits of preventing human smuggling and movement of illicit goods, Border Management, promotion of regional and multilateral engagement related to Transnational Border Crime and the prevention of such other crimes beyond  human smuggling and other Transnational Border Crime by money laundering. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to sign the proposed MoU between the Ministry of Defence of Sri Lanka and the Department of Immigration and Border Protection of the Government of Australia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Securing of supplementary financial assistance for the completion of the construction work of the Mahamodara Maternity Hospital, Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8133",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Germany has agreed to provide further financial assistance required for the completion of the construction work of the Mahamodara Maternity Hospital, Galle which was damaged by the Tsunami disaster. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to negotiate and enter into a loan Agreement with the KfW (Kerditanstalt Fur Weideraufbau) Bank of Germany to secure the  supplementary loan facility up to Euro 13 million required for the completion of these development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Short term solutions for the unprotected railway level crossings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8134",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The policy of the Government is to provide systematic protection at every railway level crossing. Presently, action is being taken by the Government to install a Bell and Light protection system at unprotected railway level crossings and until then such activities are completed, it will be necessary to have Railway Barrier Operators to avoid accidents that may occur at such level crossings.  \n\n\n\n\n\tPresently, there are 687 railway level crossings throughout the country manned by the barrier operators employed with the intervention of the Sri Lanka Police. For each such crossing, three (03) barrier operators are employed and each person so employed is paid a monthly allowance of Rs.7,500/-. However, in the recent past, a considerable number of barrier operators have left the service due to the inadequacy of the allowance paid to them. \n\n\tTherefore, as a remedial measure, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to hand over the responsibility of handling the barriers throughout the day to be given over specifically to a single Member of the Samurdhi beneficiary family selected for the purpose for the payment of Rs.22,500/- for each barrier to the said Samurdhi beneficiary Family assigned with the task, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Improvement of the efficiency of the Railway operations through the introduction of the Global Positioning System (GPS) and providing train operation related information to the General Public",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8135",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has previously granted approval to improve the efficiency of the train operations by procuring a  train operating information system based on the Global Positioning System (GPS). It has been proposed to further expand the use of the Global Positioning System (GPS) for the improvement of the efficiency of the railway operations to cover a wide scope by connecting Colombo, Anuradhapura and Nawalapitiya control centres of Sri Lanka Railways, preparation of train charts automatically, generating all train operation related reports, analyzing the train delay monitoring system etc; and to provide the general public with the train operation related information. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to obtain the relevant operating system from the Ministry of Defence for a sum of Rs.31.8 million, in accordance with the proposal put forward by the said Ministry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Providing accommodation facilities for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8136",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to overcome the difficulties faced due to the insufficient office space in the Republic Building in Colombo 01 where the Ministry of Foreign Affairs is functioning at present, it is necessary to obtain an additional space of approximately 30,000 sqft. The proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to have the building adjacent to the Republic Building constructed in the Dutch era and used by the Civil Security Department until recently, renovated by the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Further payment of house rental allowance to persons whose dwelling houses had been damaged completely or found unsuitable for occupation being subject to the floods and landslides which occurred in May 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8137",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the floods, landslides and storms that occurred in the latter part of last May, a large number of people were subject to distress and in respect of the families who were evacuated due to the complete loss of their dwelling houses or found unsuitable for occupation or landslide high risk areas, the Government decided to provide a housing rental allowance of Rs.7,500/- per month for each family for a period of three (03) months to enable them to reside in rented out houses temporarily. Accordingly, 3,584 families affected in the Districts of Ratnapura, Galle, Matara, Hambantota, Kalutara and Colombo were provided with the housing rental for the months of June, July and August, 2017. \n\n\tThe preliminary activities for the resettlement of such families are already underway and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to extend the payment of the house rental now being paid for such families for a further period of three (03) months up until the completion of such activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Establishment of District Offices of the National Building Research Organization (NBRO) in high risk landslide-prone Districts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8138",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Building Research Organization is an institution which carries out all related activities of landslide investigations, mapping out disaster prone zones, awareness creation, early warning indication and issuance of Landslide Risk Assessment Certificate prior to all construction and development projects in the landslide-prone areas through its Head Office in Colombo and the district offices located in 09 landslide-prone districts.  \n\nIn view of the unprecedented increase of landslides and collapsing of slopes has  been observed, as never before, due to the climate change impacts and changing monsoon patterns that bring any heavy rains and in order to enable to provide services to the public in an efficient manner, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to construct permanent office buildings with modern laboratory facilities in the most critical two (02) landslide-prone Districts and thereafter as per the necessity, to provide such facilities in the other Districts as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Establishment of a State of the Art National Science Centre (NSC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8139",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- A science culture for a country is an essential factor to move towards a knowledge based society and economy. Establishment of fully fledged science centres in order to enhance the knowledge an understanding of science, technology and innovations of the general public are measures adopted by many countries around the world. \n\nAs such, it has been proposed to establish a National Science Centre with modern facilities in the country with the objective of providing the knowledge of science especially in school children, for paving the way for activities such as conducting experiments etc.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to construct a National Science Centre in the block of land allocated from the Technocity at Mahenawatta, Pitipana, Homagama, at a cost of Rs.2,550 million and in accordance with the international standards, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Entering into Collaboratives  with the European Organization for Nuclear Research (CERN)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8140",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has entered into a Collaborative with the European Organization for Nuclear Research (CERN), an institution which is engaged in high energy physics and related high tech scientific experiments, in May 2017.  This Collaborative will provide an opportunity for the professors and lecturers of the universities and the scientists of the country to have access to the laboratories of the organization and to liaise with the Organization and the Scientists of around 77 countries linked with the Organization and it will enable to educate the Sri Lankan student population and as well as for the progress of the local industries.   \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to enter into Collaboration Agreements and  to allocate a provision of Rs.250.45 million in the forthcoming 05 years for the activities related to the said Collaboratives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Science and Technology for Society (STS) Forum - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8141",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Science and Technology for Society (STS) Forum Sri Lanka' was first held in the year 2016 with the objective of achieving the benefits from the progress in the fields of science, technology and research in the developed world and  increasing the contribution of the knowledge on science, technology and research to the national development process and it has been possible to initiate the support of the Sri Lankan Scientists residing in foreign countries, towards the local science and technology projects. \n\n\tTaking into consideration the success of its first forum, it has been proposed to conduct the same for the second time with the participation of approximately 1,000 persons including the representatives of other countries and international organizations working in collaboration with Sri Lanka in this field, eminent Sri Lankan expatriate scientists, Government and Private sector technologists, innovators and university and school students. Identification of emerging technologies enabling economic development, science and technology innovations for Sustainable Development Goals are the themes scheduled to be addressed at the forum. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to conduct the 'Science and Technology for Society (STS) Forum Sri Lanka' in Colombo, in October 2018 for the second time, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Improving the Cancer Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital,  Karapitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8142",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cancer has become the second major cause of death in the hospitals of Sri Lanka.  Taking into consideration the recent increase in the number of Cancer patients, the Cancer Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital in Karapitiya, the major hospital in the Southern Province, which provides special treatment services to those patients, needs to be improved.   \n\n\tAs such, a ten storey building with OPD, Iodine Therapy Unit, Clinics, 03 Oncology Units, Onco\u2011Surgical and Pediatric Oncology Units, a Laboratory and Auditorium Facilities has been planned to be constructed, in order to expand the existing Cancer Treatment Service Facilities at the Hospital. An estimated cost of Rs.2,000 million is to be incurred in respect of same. The Charitable Organization, Colours of Courage Trust (COC) has come forward to provide its contribution for the joint implementation of this project and it is expected to utilize the financial aid collected by the organization by conducting trails throughout the country, for the purpose.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine and the Charitable Organization, Colours of Courage Trust (COC) to carry out the construction work of the proposed ten (10) storeyed building to expand the Cancer treatment facilities at the Teaching Hospital in Karapitiya, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Construction of a Cardiac Catheterization Laboratory with Auxiliary Clinical Services at the Provincial General Hospital in Badulla",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8143",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, there is a significant increase in the risk of the people being subject to heart diseases.  Therefore, it is essential to improve the facilities in the Cardiac Treatment Units of the hospitals.  The Provincial General Hospital in Badulla is the only hospital in the Uva Province, which provides specialized treatment services for heart diseases. Around 10,000 patients arrive in its Cardiology Clinics annually and about 1,500 out of them are admitted to the Cardiac Treatment Unit.  Even though more than 1,000 patients out of them are required to have Catheterization for diagnostic purposes, the facilities available at the hospital at the moment are inadequate for such a number. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to establish a Catheterization Laboratory with the relevant clinical treatment facilities and an Intensive Care Unit at the Provincial General Hospital in Badulla, at the estimated cost of Rs.698 million within the financial assistance of the Japan International Cooperation  Agency (JICA), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Establishment of the Anuradhapura Regional Office of the Ayurvedic Drugs Corporation of Sri Lanka, the Sales Centre and the Medicine Purchasing  Centre in one and the same building",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8144",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The requirement of establishing the Regional Office of the Ayurvedic Drugs Corporation of Sri Lanka, the Sales Centre and the Medicine Purchasing Centre located at different places in the Anuradhapura town, in one and the same premises, has been identified.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to vest the block of Government land and the abandoned building situated at the Public Stadium Mawatha in Anuradhapura, given on lease to M/s. Lanka Salusala Ltd.,  with the Ayurvedic Drugs Corporation of Sri Lanka, on a long term lease basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Development of hospitals in the Sabaragamuwa Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8145",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity of upgrading the healthcare facilities in the Sabaragamuwa Province  where around 9% of the total population of Sri Lanka are living  has been identified. As the Provincial General Hospital in Ratnapura and the District General Hospital in Kegalle, the major hospitals in the province are highly congested, it has been identified that it will be essential to develop the Base Hospitals of Mawanella, Karawanella, Balangoda and Kalawana and the  Divisional Hospitals of Rambukkana and Eheliyagoda where people can have easy access and have quality healthcare service. Accordingly, it is expected to establish different new clinics and treatment units and to increase the number of beds by 250 in each hospital. Therefore,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the proposed project at an estimated cost of Rs.1,547 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Construction of a new building complex for the Gampaha District Secretariat",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8146",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that the old building where the Gampaha District Secretariat is housed at present is not suitable to provide an efficient and effective service to the general public. The relocation of the Government and Semi-Government institutions, presently scattered in several places, within the District Secretariat premises would also result in minimizing the traffic congestion in the Gampaha town.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to construct a 07 storey building complex with approximately  200,000 square feet, at an estimated cost of Rs 2,960 million for the Gampaha District Secretariat, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Enhancing the provisions allocated for the State Award Ceremonies and other Commemoration Ceremonies organized by the Department of Cultural Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8147",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Fifteen various state award ceremonies and several commemoration ceremonies are annually conducted by the Department of Cultural affairs with a view to preserving, promoting and propagating the cultural heritage of Sri Lanka. Certain state award ceremonies are conducted continuously for more than a half century and this has been greatly helpful in cultural renaissance of high quality and standard. \n\nThe amount of the cash awards presented to the winners at these state award ceremonies has not been enhanced for a long period of time. Further, the organizational cost for these ceremonies too has gone up considerably and additional provisions are also necessary, since a few new state award ceremonies are being organized to be held in respect of major fields of Arts which have not been subject to appreciation up to now, at State level. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of Internal Affairs, Wayamba Development and Cultural Affairs, to enhance the provision of Rs.55 million presently set apart annually by the General Treasury up to Rs.100 million, for the state award ceremonies conducted to facilitate the Artists in different fields, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Allocation of blocks of lands from the Regional Industrial Estates to set up Industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8148",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Proposals have been called through paper advertisements to select suitable industrialists in order to invest in the industrial estates, with a view to promoting industries at regional level. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to allocate the blocks of land situated in Laksha Uyana, Trincomalee - Stage 2, Batticaloa, Mathugama, Homagama, Ratmalana, Millewa, Galigamuwa, Nalanda Ellawala, Buttala, Karandeniya, Bata atha, Dankotuwa, Puttalam, Nalanda and Ulapane Regional Industrial Estates, to the selected investors on lease basis as per the  recommendations of the Regional Industrial Services Committees which evaluated the project proposals submitted in this regard and the Ministry Project Evaluation Committee, to establish 26 Industrial Projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Allocation of a block of land to the Open University of Sri Lanka (OUSL) to establish the Ratnapura Study Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8149",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ratnapura Study Centre of the Open University of Sri Lanka has been proposed to be improved under the project 'One Regional Centre of the Open University for each Province'. The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to transfer a block of land of 01Acre 02Roods in extent, belonging to the Urban Development Authority, situated in the Ratnapura New Town, to the Open University of Sri Lanka as a free grant for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Development of a Recreational Beach Area from Colpetty to Dehiwala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8150",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the rapid development of the City of Colombo, it has become a necessity to develop a common beach area for the people living in the City of Colombo and the suburbs. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to develop a recreational beach area from Colpetty to Dehiwala for the public recreational activities and consequently, to mitigate the sea erosion and provide space required for the additional railway lines, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "New projects proposed to be implemented from the year 2018 for the performance of the Coconut Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8151",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 70% of the Coconut yield in Sri Lanka is used for domestic consumption and the remainder is used for coconut related industries. Sri Lanka has been successful in receiving an export revenue of Rs.84 billion in the year 2016 alone by exporting coconut kernel related products. The Coconut related industries need to be developed while protecting the local consumer as well as the coconut cultivator, due to the limited extent of land available for  coconut cultivation and the challenges due to various climatic factors.     Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of  Plantation Industries, to establish specially in the Northern and Eastern areas model coconut gardens to enhance the performance of coconut cultivation and  to establish a trained work force for the coconut sector from the year 2018, with the objective of increasing the coconut yield and the productivity in the coconut sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Utilization of abandoned and uncultivated paddy fields for Solar Power Generation Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8152",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The government has launched a programme to improve the contribution of the renewable energy sources for electricity generation in Sri Lanka and the priority has been given for electricity generation by solar power.  Under the 'Sooryabala Sangramaya' project, the opportunity has been given to any customers to generate electricity by solar power and derive an income by supplying the same to the National Electricity Grid. \n \nEven though there is a potential for solar power electricity generation in the Provinces such as Western and Sabaragamuwa where the demand for electricity is high in Sri Lanka, there are difficulties in acquiring the lands required for the purpose. An area of 3 - 5 acres is generally required for a land mounted solar power electricity generation project with the capacity of 1 MW. Accordingly,   the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to utilize the abandoned and uncultivated paddy lands in the Western and Sabaragamuwa Provinces for the solar power electricity generation projects with the concurrence of the Commissioner General of Agrarian Services and the other authorities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Implementing a formal Agricultural Insurance Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8153",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the difficulties faced by the farming community in recovering the damages caused to the agricultural crops due to the natural disasters, a proposal was made by the budget 2017 to implement a methodology for providing an insurance cover of Rs.40,000/- per acre initially for the 6 of crops of paddy, maize, soya, big onions, potatoes and chilli. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to put forward a suitable  mechanism in collaboration with the  National Insurance Trust Fund in order to  to implement the said insurance scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Development of identified infrastructure facilities associated with minor irrigation systems",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8154",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the magnitude of the  drought and the flood situations that occurred recently, it has been found that measures should be taken to minimize impacts of the climate change on the agriculture sector and to adopt to the situation. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to implement a project to develop farm access roads, enabling the  use of modern technology on the lands of small farmers in remote areas of the dry zone and to renovate the existing agro wells and encourage farmers towards water conserving farming, as recommended by the Inter Ministerial Committee of Experts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Amendment to the Code of Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions) Act, No.2 of 2013 (Rights of Detainees - Access to Legal Counsel)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8155",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet was granted previously to publish the draft Bill submitted to amend the Code of Criminal Procedure (Special Provisions) Act, No.2 of 2013 to ensure the right of a detainee in custody to access the services of a Legal Counsel   in the Government Gazette and to present it in Parliament for approval. Further, approval was also granted to present the amendments proposed in respect of the draft Bill at the Committee Stage in Parliament.  \n\n\tPrior to resubmitting the Revised Draft Bill in Parliament a series of discussions had been held with the Attorney General's Department, Sri Lanka Police, the Bar Association of Sri Lanka and the relevant stakeholders, and  the Revised Draft Bill, has been unanimously accepted. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to publish the said Revised Draft Bill initially to be operative for four (04) years, in the Government Gazette, to be implemented and subsequently, to present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Increasing of the daily food allowance paid to the student teachers undergoing training at the National Colleges of Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8156",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are 19 National Colleges of Education in the country for the purpose of training teachers required for schools and at present there are 12,558 resident student teachers undergoing training. These student teachers during the period of their residential training are paid a monthly allowance of Rs.3,500/- and it would be appropriate to increase the said allowance to meet  the present day trends. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to increase the monthly allowance up to Rs.5,000/-  and to grant this allowance to  the entire training period of 03 years including the internship as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Establishment of two new National Schools within the Municipal limits of Kurunegala and in the Wariyapola Town",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8157",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "-  There are 09 National Sinhala Medium Schools within the Municipal limits of Kurunegala and although 5,228 application had been received in the year 2016 for admission of children to year 01, it is only a number of 1,425 students who could be admitted to them. Similarly, there is only 01 National School in the Wariyapola town and out of the 503 applications received for the year 2016 for admission of children to year 01, only 240 applicants could be provided with the opportunity. \n\n\n\n\tTaking these circumstances into consideration, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to establish  02 new National mixed Schools for girls and boys in the Kurunegala  and Wariyapola electorates, consisting all facilities was approved by the Cabinet. Further, the Cabinet also decided that a National Policy should be formulated on the establishment of National Schools."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Amendment to the Pradeshiya Sabhas Act for the provision of welfare facilities to the Plantation Community",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8158",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has already granted approval to make amendments to the relevant provisions of the Pradeshiya Sabhas Act, No.15 of 1987 to enable the use of funds of the Pradeshiya Sabhas for the supply of the common amenities necessary for the plantation community. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government to publish the draft Bill (Amendment) prepared accordingly in the Government Gazette, to seek the views of the Provincial Councils in respect of  the said draft Bill and subsequently, present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "The Construction of the Human Performance Laboratory",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8159",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- For the purpose of achieving international success in sports, inherent talents and traditional training methods alone will not suffice but the use of modern technology and correct and updated training methods and dynamics are also essential.  In the international sports arena, the developed countries use the facilities of 'Human Performance Laboratories' which analyze the human motion and the structural shortcomings in order to keep the skills of the sportsmen/women at an optimal level by preventing sports injuries.  \n\nThe construction of such a Human Performance Laboratory has commenced in Sri Lanka as well and the activities pertaining to it will be completed this year.  This laboratory will provide immense assistance to keep the skills of the  sportsmen/women at an optimal level.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of Sports, to purchase the high tech  equipment needed for the laboratory and to commence activities to secure the  consultancy services of experts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Completion of the 2nd Phase of the new building of the National Sports Museum",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8160",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Activities pertaining to the establishment of the 'National Sports Museum' is in progress at the Independence Square in Colombo 07 with a view to conserving and exhibiting the sports related information and memorabilia of historic value.  This Museum will be provided with the galleries necessary to include the history of National Sports Associations, a data base of sports, records, live size vax statues of elite sportsmen/women who gained success at the international competitions. \n\nThis museum is scheduled to be opened in December 2017 and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of Sports, to obtain Treasury Allocations for the construction activities pertaining to its  2nd phase, for fixing interior decor and electronic equipment etc. and to obtain the past information related to sports like, films, TV programmes, photographs and documents from the relevant government institutions, to be preserved in the museum,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Eviction of encroachers in the land of the Kandy Hospital by providing housing facilities for the  Development of the General Hospital of Kandy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8161",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kandy Teaching Hospital with 2,402 beds is the second largest hospital in Sri Lanka.  The limitation of space has become a major obstacle for the future development activities of this hospital which provides treatment to around 1,600,000 patients annually. Although the extent of land belonging to the hospital is 58.4 acres and as a result of an extent of 23.7 acres being occupied by the encroachers, the development of facilities within the premises have been hampered. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Special Assignments,Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, for reacquisition of the said land required to carry out the development activities to be conducted under the Kandy Teaching Hospital development plan  and to construct a housing complex comprising of 66 houses in a separate area within hospital  land for the low income earning unauthorized settlers affected by the decision to evict such settlers and  allocate houses to  them, utilizing the provisions to be allocated to the Ministry for the year 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Obtaining the consultancy services for Designing of Bridges and Railway Lines from the Maradana Railway Station up to Maligawatte",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8162",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'The Colombo - Suburban Railway Project' will be implemented to cater to the demand of railway services by the year 2035 focusing attention on the development associated with Colombo and Suburban area of the railway network of Sri Lanka. The pre-feasibility  study of the project has been completed by now and is planned to construct of four (04) new railway lines from Maradana to Maligawatta has been recommended as a short term development proposal. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to obtain the consultancy services required to lay the new rail line, to widen the bridge at the school lane at Maligawatta and the pedestrian bridge at Maradana from the Road Development Authority along with the assistance of the experts of the Department of Railways, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-032-en",
    "num": "32",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "Improvement of the  Kaduwela - Athurugiriya Road and the Walgama - Athurugiriya Road",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8163",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to improve and rehabilitate the road section from  starting point to 9.5 km on the Kaduwela - Athurugiriya (B 174) and the  road section from starting point to 1.2 km (B 451) on the Walgama - Athurugiriya, utilizing a part of the loan received from the OPEC Fund for International Development (OFID) for the Western Province Road Development Project.  Accordingly, Bids have been called for the said construction work and  the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract for the improvement and rehabilitation of the said road sections to M/s. Hovael Construction (Pvt) Ltd., the lowest substantially responsive bidder, for a sum of Rs.1,065 million, in accordance with the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee and the Procurement Appeals Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-09-26-033-en",
    "num": "33",
    "date_str": "2017-09-26",
    "description": "The New Bridge Construction Project over the Kelani river -  Award of the contract for the construction of the Steel bridge section",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8164",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-09-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called from the local and international contractors for the construction of the Steel Bridge Section to be constructed under Package I of the New Bridge Construction Project over the Kelani river.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract for the construction of the said steel bridge section to the JMT Joint Venture of Japan comprising of M/s. JFE Engineering Corporation, Mitsui Engineering & Shipbuilding Co. Ltd. and M/s. TODA Corporation for a sum of Rs.31,539 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
