    "doc_id": "2017-10-10-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-10-10",
    "description": "Towns East of Polonnaruwa Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8267",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-10-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement a new water supply project so as to cover the towns east of Polonnaruwa which is being developed under the 'Rajarata Navodaya - Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa'. Through this project, it is expected to supply safe drinking water to a population of about 262,481 residing in Welikanda, Dimbulagala, Thamankaduwa, Lankapura, Hingurakkdoda and Elahera Divisional Secretariat Divisions.\n \nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the implementation of the  project to M/s China Harbor Engineering Company Ltd. for a sum of US$ 354 million, as recommended by the standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-10-10-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-10-10",
    "description": "Development of the Medical Ward Complex in the General Hospital, Kalutara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8268",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-10-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The General Hospital, Kalutara, which is the major hospital in the Kalutara District provides a great service in providing health care services for the people living in Agalawatta, Bulathsinghala, Horana, Bandaragama, Kalutara, Mathugama, Panadura and Beruwala. It has been proposed to construct a new 07 storey building for the medical ward complex with the objective of providing with more accommodation facilities for in-door patients.\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the  construction of this complex to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and the Engineering Services (Pvt.) Company for a sum of Rs.2,817 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-10-10-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-10-10",
    "description": "Procurement of 400,000 Nucleic Acid Testing Reagents used for Blood Tests",
