    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Regularizing the disposition of state lands and the prevention of encroachment in state lands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8394",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet appointed a Committee comprising of the officers of the relevant institutions relating to the subject of Land to study and report facts pertaining to the same, to prepare a formal methodology for regularizing the disposition of state lands and and the prevention of encroachment in state lands.  \n\nAccordingly, taking into consideration the recommendations made by the Committee and the facts submitted by H.E. the President and the Ministers of Defence; and Megapolis and Western Development in this regard, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, to implement the proposals submitted with regard to further strengthening of the existing methodology for the prevention of encroachment in State Lands and the disposition of State Lands, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Preparation of a legal framework to implement the National Land Use Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8395",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for the National Land Use Policy prepared by a Committee of Experts under the Sustainable Land Management Project and to enact legislation for its implementation. The absence of a National Land Use Policy to be enforced by law, has been identified as one of the major causes for the occurrence of disasters such as floods and landslides in the country in the recent times.  \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the required draft Bill, based on the said National Land Use Policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Export Crops Villages Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8396",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministerial Committee on Kandy City Development has identified the necessity of utilizing the lands owned by the state institutions situated around the Kandy area which have not been used productively to be made use of for re-cultivation or for ear-marked export oriented purposes.  \n\nAs such, a proposal has been made to implement a project named  'Export Crops Villages Project'.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Special Assignments and Chairman of the Ministerial Committee on Kandy City Development, to grant an extent of land of 400 acres situated in the Woodside Estate of the Medadumbara Divisional Secretariat Division identified as suitable, to be given on lease basis, under this project to the selected beneficiaries,to provide the necessary technical know how to carry out agricultural activities in these lands and to expand the activities of the project depending on its success, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Awarding of Contracts for Rebuilding and Pre-curing services for tyres of the buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8397",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contracts for providing the services for re\u2011building and pre-curing of tyres of the buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board over to 09 companies, as per the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC) and the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Upgrading the Old Kotte Road (Rajagiriya Section)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8398",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously for widening the Mahaiyawa tunnel, expanding the Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, making improvements to the Old Kotte Road (Rajagiriya Section) and constructing the drainage system in the Kurunegala City by using the available savings of the road projects carried out under the Programme for the Rehabilitation of National Highways funded by the local banks.  \n\nSince acceleration of the improvements to the Old Kotte Road (Rajagiriya Section) will ease the existing traffic congestion around the Rajagiriya roundabout, it has become necessary to complete the improvements to that section within a short period of time and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, for the Road Development Authority to complete the task by adopting the direct labour method, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Accelerating the Construction and Development activities of the Hospitals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8399",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the need to accelerate the development activities of the hospitals, a proposal has been made to entrust certain construction activities with the Government Construction Agencies, in order to overcome the delays that take place due to the adoption of the General Procurement Procedure. As such, taking into consideration a  proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, the Cabinet granted approval to entrust the construction activities of the Oral Health Unit in the Teaching Hospital in Karapitiya, the Specialized Pediatric Ward Complex in the General Hospital in Ampara and the New Building Complex in Ninthavur to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and the Central Engineering Services (Private) Limited., and the construction of the six storey building with an operation theatre in the Base Hospital in Horana to the State Engineering Corporation of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Purchase of Full Cream Milk Powder required for the Production of Thriposha",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8400",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Thriposha is a nutritious food supplement, distributed free of charge by the Ministry of  Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine to the children with malnutrition, pregnant mothers with nutrition problems and lactating mothers. The main raw material used for the manufacturing of Thriposha is full cream milk powder and from the year 2014 to 2017 the milk powder required for the purpose has been supplied by the M/s. Milco (Private) Limited. Considering the contribution that could be made for the local diary farmers in uplifting their economic well-being by continuing to purchase milk from Milco, which is a Government owned company engaged in the production of local milk products and the advantage of purchasing milk directly without intermediaries, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to purchase 600 MT of full cream milk required to manufacture Thriposha for the year 2018, for a sum of Rs.486 million (excluding tax), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "The Middle Income Housing Project at Elliot Place in Borella",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8401",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the design and construction contract of the proposed Middle Income Housing Project of 400 housing units at  Elliot Place in Borella, on design and built basis to M/s Yanjian Group Co. Ltd., for a sum of Rs.7,799 million, excluding tax, as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Implementation of the Global Promotion and Marketing Campaign for 'Ceylon Tea'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8402",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Tea Board has initiated a global promotion campaign for the 'Ceylon Tea' with the primary objective of sustaining the existing demand for the Sri Lankan Tea as 'Ceylon Tea', re\u2011building the image of pure 'Ceylon Tea' in the lost market and establishing the Sri Lankan Tea brands in the international market. Action will be taken in terms of the Government Procurement Procedure in this regard for selecting an agency for consultancy services for the media planning, scheduling and buying.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of  Plantation Industries, to select the Dentsu Grant (Pvt.) Ltd. as the Consultancy Agency in that regard, for a sum of Rs.219.89 million and for a period of three (03) years, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Consultancy Committee for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Provision of footwear for students in difficult, most difficult and remote schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8403",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Education is implementing the programme for the provision of a pair of footwear for the students in the difficult, most difficult and remote schools. Accordingly, footwear have been provided to 621,941 students in the year 2016 and a sum of Rs.592.2 million has been spent by the Government for the purpose. In implementing this programme, suppliers were selected through  a procurement process and they adopted a method of getting the sizes of the feet of the students to manufacture footwear to fit those sizes and distributed those footwear to the schools. Considering the lengthy period of about 6 months taken and the necessity of providing footwear to all school students at the same time, focus has been made to implement this programme by providing a gift voucher to the students in lieu of the above procedure in providing the footwear required for this year. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to implement the programme in this year by providing the students with gift vouchers to the value of Rs.1,200/- to Rs.1,500/- according to their grades, incurring an expenditure of around Rs.808.27 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Upgrading the Printing Press of the Department of Examinations in Sri Lanka with the new technology",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8404",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Examinations in Sri Lanka carries out the printing of the examination papers and documents necessary for conducting of about 270 examinations annually and most of the machines in use for the purpose are older than 30 years. The secrecy of the examinations can be safeguarded optimally by the introduction of the new technological methods and thereby, the confidence of the candidates on the examinations will also rise. The Cabinet has granted approval to improve its system  by using the Digital Printing Technology for the Printing Press of the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka. \n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to award the contract for upgrading the Printing Press of the Department of Examination of Sri Lanka by introducing the Digital Printing Technology to M/s Metropolitan Office (Pvt.) Limited, for a sum of US$ 2.9 million and Rs.15 million, excluding tax, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Installation of the Fuel Hydrant System and Upgrading of the Aviation Refueling Terminal of the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8405",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, to award the contract for the installation of the Fuel Hydrant System for the proposed new Apron - E implemented concurrent to the development activities of Phase II of the BIA and upgrading of the Aviation Refueling Terminal of the Bandaranaike International Airport to the Joint Venture of M/s WEC Engineers and Constructors Pte. Ltd., Singapore, M/s Pte. Wijaya Karya and M/s China National Chemical Engineering, for a sum of US$ 51.5 million, excluding tax and to secure the financial facilities necessary, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Installation of a Fuel Storage Tank in the Petroleum Storage Terminal of Kolonnawa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8406",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Adequate storage facilities should be provided for each petroleum product in order to maintain a stock of fuel in Sri Lanka sufficient at least for a minimum of 30 days and it has been estimated that an additional storage capacity for 100,000 MT is required.  As a preliminary measure, tenders have been called for to install a Petrol Storage Tank of 15,000 m3 at the Kolonnawa Terminal.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, to award the contract to install a Fuel Storage Tank with a capacity of 15,000 m3 with Internal Floating Roof at Kolonnawa, to M/s Indo East Engineering & Construction (Lanka) Pte. Ltd., for a sum of Rs.412.78 million excluding tax, in accordance with the recommendations of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Purchasing of 06 Armoured Vehicles required for the Special Task Force proposed for UN Peacekeeping Operations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8407",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to procure the vehicles and equipment required for the Special Task Force proposed for the UN Peacekeeping Operations. As such, bids have been called for, to purchase 06 Armoured Vehicles required to be used for the proposed programme.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to purchase 06 Armoured Vehicles for a sum of Rs.413.59 million, Rs.68.93 million being the unit price, including tax, from M/s Securatec Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd., in accordance with the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Construction of the Stage - II of the Accident and Emergency Medical Treatment Unit in the District General Hospital of Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8408",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The District General Hospital of Polonnaruwa is the major hospital which provides patient care services to the people living in the area.  As the presently available facilities are inadequate to provide accident and emergency treatment for the patients, the construction of the Accident and Emergency Medical Treatment Unit commenced in the year 2015. As of now, Stage\u2011I of the project for the construction of two storeys is nearing completion and is about to be handed over.  \n\n\n\n\tAccordingly, considering the necessity of commencing the activities pertaining to Stage\u2011II of the project expeditiously, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to hand over the construction work to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and the Engineering Services (Pvt.) Limited on Design and Built basis, for a sum of Rs.643.36 million, including tax, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Regulations in respect of the list of the Import Control and Banned Items and the list of the Export Control Items under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8409",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has been a member of the World Customs Organization since the year 1968 and the country is obligatory to implement the International Convention on Harmonized Commodity Description and the Coding System. Steps have been taken to update the new Harmonized Coding System in accordance with the sharp changes in the Patterns of International Trade and Technology and as such, the National Harmonized System has been amended as a Harmonized Coding System with eight digits.  \n\n\tIt is necessary to amend the Regulations (controlled items) published under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 pertaining to the import control, banned and export control items to coincide with the same.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to present the Gazette Extraordinary Notifications No.2044/40 and No.2044/41 dated 2017\u201111\u201109 published with amendments to those regulations, in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and the Republic of Korea on Investment Promotion",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8410",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Republic of Korea is regarded as an important country which makes Foreign Direct Investment in Sri Lanka and Korea has already made investments in over 70 companies of Sri Lanka. A number of other sectors have been identified where there is the potential for expanding the Korean investments in Sri Lanka and in this respect, it is appropriate to further strengthen the investment cooperation and collaboration between the two countries.  \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and the Republic of Korea to promote investment exchange between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Hosting of the First Annual Conference of Non-Communicable Diseases (NCD) of SAARC Countries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8411",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- All the countries in the SAARC region have faced the problem pertaining to the non-communicable diseases.  At the meeting of the Health Ministers of the SAARC countries, a proposal has been made that a conference of the SAARC countries be held to discuss the ways and means to solve the problem and to provide opportunities to exchange the experiences of the respective countries and to provide opportunities for the improvement of the prevailing methodologies for the control of the non-communicable diseases.   \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to host the said conference on the 9th and 10th of December 2017 in Colombo, Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Agreement to be signed between Sri Lanka and the Republic of Korea  on Cooperation in the fields of Culture, Arts, Education, Youth activities and Sports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8412",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to sign an Agreement between Sri Lanka and the Republic of Korea with a view to strengthening the mutual friendly relations existing  between the two countries and promoting cooperation in the fields of Culture, Arts, Education, Youth activities and Sports, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-11-21-032-en",
    "num": "32",
    "date_str": "2017-11-21",
    "description": "Supply of fertilizer for the Maha Season - 2017/2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8413",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-11-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to award the tender for procuring 72,000 MT of Urea required for the distribution of fertilizer for the Maha Season 2017/2018 by the Government Fertilizer Companies, to M/s JAT Holding (Pvt.) Ltd. which has successfully submitted the bid in this regard, for a sum of US$ 23.57 million being US$ 327.40 per MT, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Enhancement of the local dairy production by producing Young Dairy Farm Entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8414",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the non-production of the required quantity of liquid milk or milk powder inside the country for the consumption of the Sri Lankans, a large amount of foreign currency has to be disbursed annually for the importation of such dairy products. Therefore, focus of the Government has been made for enlisting the contribution of the Youth Community to enhance the dairy production capacity in the country adopting advanced scientific methods and technology.\n\n\tAs such, a proposal has been made to implement a programme for producing of Young Dairy Farm Entrepreneurs under the aegis of the National Programme on Food Production. Under this programme, it has been planned to select youth to be fully involved in dairy farming, provide them with technical knowledge and resources and, to build them up as entrepreneurs with the capacity of producing at least 100 litres of milk, per day. It is expected that it would be possible to raise the domestic dairy production to the optimal level, by establishing such 10,000 units of young entrepreneurs.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement its Pilot Project in the District of Kandy with the assistance of the Ministry of Rural Economy, the Central Provincial Council and the District Secretariat, Kandy and to implement the same in other areas based on its success, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Provision of funds for the implementation of the second phase of the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8415",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme funded by the Asian  Development Bank (ADB) has been implemented with the objective of developing the dry areas in the North Western, North Central and Northern Provinces by providing Mahaweli water to those areas. Under the first phase of this programme, the three (03) major investment projects namely, the Upper Elahera Canal project, North Western Province Canal project and Minipe Left Bank Canal Rehabilitation project, are implemented. \n\n\tA sum of US$ 210 million is due to be obtained from the ADB under the second phase of this Loan Agreement and it has been planned to use the same for the construction of a part of the Upper Elahera Canal  project with the tunnel, a part of the transfer canal linking Kaluganga-Moragahakanda of the Upper Elahera Canal  project, a part of the Mahakithula tunnel of the North Western Provincial Canal Project, Mahakithula and Mahakirula reservoirs and the feeder canal from Mahakithula to Mahakirula reservoir, and for the implementation of the environmental and social security activities in the aforesaid constructing areas. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to obtain the funds for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Granting of Concessionary Loans to students to follow Degree Programmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8416",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with a proposal made in the National Budget of 2017, the Government has launched a project to provide an interest free concessionary loan facility subject to a maximum limit of Rs.800,000 to facilitate the students who were unable to secure admission to the state universities due to the z-score method adopted, to follow the degree programmes offered by the Non-Governmental Degree Awarding Institutions. To coincide with this, the Cabinet approval has also been granted to provide a loan up to a Rs.1.1 million to the youth who have passed the G.C.E. (A/L) so as to cover their general expenses as well, to follow the Degree in Education Programmes from the non-governmental Higher Educational Institutes.  \n\n\tAs such, in addition to the expenditure to cover the course fee and the books through this loan to the youth who follow other Degree Programmes, a proposal has been made to add Rs.75,000/- for the other general expenses as well. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enhance the maximum amount of this loan granted under the programme to Rupees one million twenty five thousand (Rs.1,025,000) for a degree of 03 year duration and Rupees one million hundred thousand (RS.1,100,000) for a degree of 04 year duration, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Providing of facilities for the establishment of an Internationally recognized Business School in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8417",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has recognized the importance of taking modern and sustainable measures to achieve an expeditious economic growth by transforming Sri Lanka into a knowledge based economy.  As such, the Cabinet approval has been granted to establish a world recognized engineering school and a business school in Sri Lanka to provide the knowledge and the professional skill necessary to enhance the qualitative aspect of the workforce of the country. \n\nAs a result of discussions had with the renowned universities of the world, a proposal has been put forward by the Berkeley Haas Business School in California of the United States of the America to establish a Business School in Sri Lanka on a not-for-profit basis. The University expects to establish the proposed Business School as a regional hub of the Indian Ocean. The educational opportunities will be open to the bright students possessing skills and talents, irrespective of their financial background.\n\nThis business school has been planned to be established in the District of Gampaha and the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways and Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to provide for its initial planning activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Establishment of a 400 MW Natural Gas Power Plant in Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8418",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the importance of the introduction of natural gas as a resource for the energy generation field in Sri Lanka, deliberations have been made to establish a 400 MW Natural Gas Power Plant in Hambantota by the Governments of China and Sri Lanka jointly, on Government to Government basis. With the main objective of providing electricity to the industrial zone proposed to be established in Hambantota and avoiding the possible scarcity of electricity in future, it is due to be implemented as a special project. Accordingly, the  proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to set up this Natural Gas Power Plant and the Natural Gas Unloading Terminal between the China Machinery Engineering Corporation (CMEC) nominated by the Government of China and the Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) as a Joint Venture, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Securing Financial Aid from the Government of Hungary for the development Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8419",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Hungary has agreed to provide funds for the development of some of the projects implemented by the Government of Sri Lanka. Under this programme, concessionary loan facilities in a sum of Euro 149 million will be provided for, in respect of the following  projects through the Import and Export Bank of Hungary.\n\n\t1.\tBingiriya - Udubaddawa Water Supply Project (Euro 53 million)\n\n2.\tConstruction of Flyovers - Kohuwala, Kirulapona and Yangalmodara (Euro 52 million)\n\t3.\tElectronic Court Management System (Euro 32 million)\n\n\t4.\tRailway Level Crossing Protection Project (Euro 12 million)\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into an Aid Credit Framework Programme Agreement with the Government of Hungary in respect of the said loan facility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "The Bilateral Air Services Agreement between Tanzania, Rwanda, Azerbaijan, Poland  and Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8420",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to sign the proposed Air Services Agreements between Sri Lanka, Tanzania, Rwanda, Azerbaijan and Poland, presently, agreed upon at the official level and  subsequently to take appropriate measures for its entry into force, with a view to formalizing the Air Services between each country, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Enactment of Laws for the prevention of touting at the Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8421",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the difficulties faced by the air passengers due to various unauthorized touts being present at the common areas of the Bandaranaike International Airport, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to enact laws to control such activities. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to publish the draft Bill to amend the Civil Aviation Act, No.14 of 2010 in the Government Gazette providing for touting and for loading any baggage to vehicles by unauthorized persons at the Airport as offences under the Civil Aviation Act and for the arrest of such persons committing such offences and to file action in the Magistrate Court having the  jurisdiction over the area where the Airport is situated without the sanction of the Attorney General, and subsequently, to present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Teledrama, Film and Commercials Levy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8422",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the impact on the local teledramas and the film industry by dubbed foreign teledramas, films and commercials flowing into the country, it has been proposed in the budget 2017 to increase the 'Teledrama, Film and Commercial Levy' imposed on the teledramas, films and commercials dubbed in sinhala or tamil language. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Extraordinary Gazette Notification No.2044/21 dated 2017-11-07 published in terms of the provisions of the Finance Act, No.11 of 2006 amending the relevant levy, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Allocation of lands on Lease Basis for a farming project of Milkfish (Chanos Chanos)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8423",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the long line fishing method used for harvesting the major commodities of Sri Lankan fish exports such as Tuna and Bill Fish, Squids, Milkfish and Gold Strip Sardinella are used as baits. Though about 7,000 MT of baits are required for the purpose annually, only around 3,000 MT of the same is satisfied locally. Since, more baits have to be imported the price of the major domestic commodities of fish exports rise and causes adverse effects on imposing a competitive price for those products in the International Market.\n\n\tIt will be beneficial to produce milkfish (Chanos Chanos) at commercial level to be used as bait as well as for human consumption and it may lead to saving a some amount of foreign currency out of over of Rs.01 billion spent annually for the importation of baits.   The All Island Multiday Fishing Vessels Owners' Association has presented a project proposal for conducting intensive farming of milkfish. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to grant a block of land 12.14 hectares in extent located in Bangadeniya in the District of Puttalam, belonging to the National Aquaculture Development Authority of Sri Lanka (NAQDA), on lease basis, to the said Association for the implementation of the project by the National Aquaculture Development Authority of Sri Lanka as the Government Partner on Public-Private Partnership basis, subject to carrying out a specific environmental impact assessment, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Improvement of infrastructure road facilities for the plantation community",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8424",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the difficulty in accessing the facilities such as health,  education, safety water and other infrastructure, the life indicators pertaining to the plantation region are low when compared to the other areas of the country. As such, it is essential to improve the road development activities for easy access to such infrastructure facilities. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of  Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to rehabilitate the road section in the Hatton area leading from Brodack to Abbotsligh by mettalling and taring, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Improvement to the Existing Network Infrastructure at the Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8425",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need for the adoption of the state-of-the-art technologies to effectively carry out the essential administrative and parliamentary functions of the Parliament of Sri Lanka has been recognized. In this regard the e-Parliament project is implemented by the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka (ICTA).  In this respect, it is essential to improve the existing computer network infrastructure facilities and as such, the proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication and Digital Infrastructure, to adopt the Government Procurement Procedure to select an appropriate agency for the supply of the necessary equipment and the services, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Renovation and Reactivation of Myliddy Fishery Harbour",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8426",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the decade of 1980, the Myliddy fishery harbour situated in the Walikkamam area of Jaffna was a major fishery harbour which provided a significant contribution towards the fishery industry and it was considered unique due to the fact that it could be used even during the North East monsoon period. During the period of the conflict, the activities of this harbour was disrupted and with the re-emergence of a peaceful environment in the Northern Province, the fisheries  harbour and its 54 acre land has been released in July 2017 enabling it to be used for the fisheries industry. \n\n\tSince, the displaced people who were living in the area have returned to the area once again, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  to take measures to commence the renovation activities expeditiously in the Myliddy fishery harbour, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Upgrading of the National Holiday Resorts (NHR)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8427",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The national holiday resorts situated in Anuradhapura, Nuwara Eliya, Bandarawela and Katharagama and managed by the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority are very popular among the Public Officers and the domestic holiday seekers. As such, the proposal made by Hon.John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to redevelop the holiday resorts with a view to making those more attractive to tourists, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Construction of the Library Building Complex at the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8428",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award the contract of Phase-1 of the project for the construction of the Library Building Complex at the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka, to M/s CML-MTD Construction Ltd., for a sum of Rs.315 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Awarding of the contract for the External Work and the Land Development Work of the Modern Research and Development Complex (MRDC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8429",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to award the contract for the External Work and the Land Development Work of the Modern Research and Development Complex (MRDC) at the Industrial Technology Institute (ITI) situated in the Malabe area, to M/s. Ranasiha Lanka Construction (Pvt.) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.215.9 million as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Extension of the Surgical / Medical Units at the Teaching Hospital at Karapitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8430",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to extend the Surgical / Medical Units at the Teaching Hospital at Karapitiya in Galle, which is one of the major hospitals in Sri Lanka, in order to enhance its surgical and medical facilities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract of its construction, to M/s Subasinghe Contractors & Earth Movers for a sum of Rs.690 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy Services required for the Township Development Programmes to be implemented in 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8431",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the 'Sukithapurawara' Township Development Programme implemented by the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development, it has been proposed to implement 80 new projects in the year 2018. With a view to completing the new projects expeditiously, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to vest the contracts for the provision of consultancy services required according to the nature of each construction work, with the Urban Development Authority (UDA), Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), State Engineering Corporation (SEC), Sri Lanka Land Reclamation and Development Corporation (SLLR&DC), Provincial Road Development Authority (PRDA), Road Development Authority (RDA) and the Colombo Municipal Council (CMC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Construction of the Fair and the Commercial Building at the Kurusa Junction at Alubomulla in Bandaragama",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8432",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to construct a Fair, a Commercial Complex and a Multi-purpose building in the land belonging to the Bandaragama Multi Purpose Cooperative Society, located in close proximity to the Kurusa Junction at Alubomulla in Bandaragama along the Panadura - Horana main road. It is expected to construct 120 trade stalls under this project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement this project at an estimated cost of Rs.200 million under the 'Sukithapurawara' Township Development Programme and to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the said Cooperative Society for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Provision of Solar Power Systems to the Public Institutions under the  \tSoorya Bala Sangramaya Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8433",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Soorya Bala Sangramaya Programme, a project has been planned to provide Solar Power Systems to the Public Institutions. The Sustainable Energy Authority has identified such public institutions where the solar power systems can be installed for the purpose and tenders have been called for to select suitable institutions for the purpose of installing these solar power systems. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contracts for the installation of solar power systems in 63 Government hospitals, 13 Government schools and 01 Divisional Secretariat Division, to the institutions recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Construction of the Left Bank Main Canal of the Yan Oya Reservoir Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8434",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Yan Oya Reservoir Development Project, which is one of the major scale irrigation development projects implemented in Sri Lanka in the recent times, provides water to around 4,190 hectares of lands in the areas of the Districts of Anuradhapura and Trincomalee faced with scarcity of water for cultivation purposes. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources Management, to award the contract for the construction of the Left Bank Main Canal of the project, to M/s China CAMC Engineering Co. Ltd., (CAMCE), for  a sum of US$ 39.5 million on design and built basis, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Signing of the Shareholder Agreement for the commencement of the \toperational activities of the Port of Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8435",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to develop the Port of Hambantota by expanding its operations under the Public-Private Partnership, a Concession Agreement was signed on 29th July 2017 among the Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA), the Government of Sri Lanka, China Merchants Port Holdings Company Limited (CM Port), Hambantota International Port Group (Private) Limited (HIPG) and Hambantota International Port Services (Private) Limited (HIPS). Accordingly, International Port Group (Private) Limited (HIPG) and Hambantota International Port Services (Private) Limited (HIPS), the two unique services companies established for the development of the Port of Hambantota, have planned to commence its operational activities on 09th December 2017 on the terms agreed upon in the Agreement. \n\t85% of the Share Capital of the HIPG Company will be possessed by the CM Port Company or its affiliation and 15% of the same will be vested with the Sri  Lanka Ports Authority. Similarly, 58% of the Share Capital of the HIPS Company will be possessed by the HIPG Company and the rest of 42% will be vested with the Sri Lanka Ports Authority. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to sign the Shareholder Agreement prepared as a Supplementary Agreement to the Original Agreement among the relevant parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Managing the Public Expenditure for the Reconstruction of Properties Damaged due to the adverse weather",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8436",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The General Treasury has already provided an additional allocation of Rs.32 billion to restore the livelihood of the affected people due to drought, flood and adverse weather during the recent times and to rehabilitate the damaged properties. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to make use of the provisions which have not been utilized so far by various  ministries, so that the funds further required for the purpose, could be managed within the provisions which have already been granted, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Planning of Public Investments  Efficiently  and  the Programmatic Project Preparation Facility",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8437",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Programmatic Project Preparation Facility- PPPF has been designed to be implemented with the aim of achieving the desired objectives of improving the quality at the inception of projects implemented by the Government, improving the implementation mechanisms and enhancing the capacity of making project preparation documents within the different Government Agencies. Therefore,in order to secure US $ 4 million required for the purpose, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Financing Agreement with the World Bank, was approved with Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Granting Rs.50,000/- as house rent allowance further for the owners of the houses evacuated due to the Landslide which occurred at the Meethotamulla Garbage Dump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8438",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the first and second phase of the housing programme  to provide houses for those who were deprived of their houses and the families evacuated from their dwelling houses which were prone to high risk as a result of the landslides which occurred in the garbage dump at Meethotamulla in Kolonnawa on the 2017-04-14, have been provided with houses to 98 families  and another 72 families have been provided with alternative houses on 2017-11-08 under the third phase of the programme.\n\nThe families were given a monthly house rent allowance of Rs.50,000/- up to the month of August 2017 until they were resettled. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to grant the house rent allowance for the 72 families who were resettled for the last time for the period of two (02)  months up to August 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy Services for the Feasibility Study and the Detailed Design of Colombo Suburban Railway Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8439",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the Consultancy Services Contract for the   Feasibility Study and the Detailed Design of the project implemented with the objective of upgrading the railway system in Colombo and Suburban areas to M/s DOHWA Engineering Co. Ltd., and its partners for a sum of 256,030 Sterling Pounds, US$ 6,481,575 and Rs.379,213,616 as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Consultancy Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Performing of Emergency Heart Surgeries through Private Hospitals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8440",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As the two theaters of the Cardiology unit of the Colombo National Hospital, are under renovation, the heart surgeries performed there have been suspended. As such, the Colombo National Hospital is presently transferring the patients there over to the Sri Jayawardhanapura Hospital for heart surgeries, but it has not been an adequate measure to overcome the issue. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to make necessary arrangements to refer the heart patients over to the private hospitals where cardiology units are available, for emergency treatments, at Government expense and to expedite the renovation work of the Cardiology unit in the Colombo National Hospital, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-05-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2017-12-05",
    "description": "Short Term Measures for reducing the Cost of Living",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8441",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The disruption of cultivation in several seasons, due to the adverse climatic condition that prevailed has resulted in a considerable decline of food production in the country and has caused the escalation of prices of food items. Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister pointed out to the Cabinet that the general public are being severely inconvenienced due to the exorbitant prices of the food items especially such as rice, coconut and vegetables varieties and the Cabinet discussed the matter at length.   \n\n\tWith a view to controlling this situation, it was decided to take the following measures expeditiously to supply adequate essential food items to the market:\n\n*\tto facilitate any Private Institution or the Co-operative Wholesale Establishment (CWE) to import rice under the direction and supervision of the General Treasury;\n\n*\tto import the coconut kernel required for the coconut related industries and coconuts required for domestic consumption, under the supervision of the Ministry of Plantation Industries;\n\n*\tto appoint an Officials' Committee to submit proposals expeditiously on the further reliefs that could be provided, in addition to the reliefs already granted by the Government,  to the  farmers whose cultivation has been disrupted."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Construction of a new building for the Jaffna District Office of the Election Commission",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8442",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Twenty five Divisional Offices have been established at the level of Administrative Districts to facilitate in carrying out the statutory as well as the administrative functions of the Election Commission. Since the Jaffna Election Office functions within a limited space set apart from the Jaffna District Secretariat building with inadequate facilities, the need for the construction of a separate office building for same has been identified and for this purpose, a plot of land belonging to the Government within the municipal limits of Jaffna has already been allocated.\n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the present and future needs,              the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to construct a  4 storey building with a floor area of 18,425 sq.ft. for the Election Office of the Jaffna District and to secure funds amounting to Rs.97.7 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Obtaining the participation of the people to protect the forests in the Dry   Zones",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8443",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the census  and statistics data of the year 2010 the total land area of the Island is 29.7%. The importance of the participation of the people for forest management has been recognized by the National Forest Policy as well and the Department of Forest Conservation has introduced various strategies for the purpose.  It is essential to further implement the programmes of this nature with a view to increasing further the forest cover of the country and its sustainability. \n\n\tAs such, a proposal has been made to activate the 'Sri Lanka Community Forestry Programme' for the upliftment of the economic status of the community living closer to the forests and the protection of the forest. Under this programme, it is expected to take measures such as introducing livelihood methods to enhance the economic status of the rural community living in close proximity to the forests in the 17 Districts which represent the Dry Zone and the Intermediate Zone of Sri Lanka, providing the necessary training equipment for such purpose, activating home gardening and inducing the school going children to engage in forest conservation etc. Through this programme, it will be possible to provide direct economic benefits to over 20,000 persons and the conservation of about 30,000 hectares of forest land. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment,  to implement the above project at a cost of Rs.261.06 million, within the period from 2018-2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Continuation of the '1990 Suwaseriya' Emergency Pre-hospital Care Ambulance Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8444",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Emergency Pre-hospital Care Ambulance Service which commenced in the Southern and Western Provinces with Indian Grant Assistance is presently implemented successfully and the approval of the Cabinet has been granted to establish the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' by an Act of Parliament for the uninterrupted supply of the service. The Drafting of the Bill for the purpose is in progress.\n\n\tUnder Phase II of this initiative, the Government of India has agreed to provide an additional grant facility for the expansion of the above service in the other seven Provinces as well, by deploying 209 additional ambulances. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  to extend the period of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) entered into between the GVK EMRI Lanka (Pvt.) (GEL) Ltd. and the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine to continue the service uninterruptedly until the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' is established, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "The Establishment of a Vocational Training Centre for the Tourism Industry in the Nilaveli area of Trincomalee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8445",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Youth Services Council has planned to commence a training centre in the Nilaveli area of Trincomalee in the year 2018 for training the youth for job opportunities in the tourism industry. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to get 200 acres of land situated in the Nilaveli area vested with the Tourism Development Authority to be vested with the Ministry of National Policies and Economic Affairs for the establishment of the proposed training centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Development of the Royal Botanical Gardens at Peradeniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8446",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Royal Botanical Gardens at Peradeniya which is more than 196 years old is comprised of 147 acres of land where more than 3,500 plant species are conserved. This internationally acclaimed botanical gardens has an annual turnout of approximately 1.6 million local and foreign tourists and it has been planned to further improve the available facilities, considering the objectives of the spectators in regard to education, research and recreation. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to implement a project for the development of the Royal Botanical Gardens at Peradeniya within the next period of 05 years and to secure funds amounting to Rs.385 million necessary for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Providing relief to the affected persons due to the acquisition of lands  for the construction of a New Railway Track from Kurunegala to Habarana via Dambulla",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8447",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- An extent of approximately 300 acres will have to be acquired for the project for the construction of a new Railway Track 84 kms in length from Kurunegala to Habarana via Dambulla under the 'Awakening Rajarata' Presidential Programme - 'Let's Awaken Polonnaruwa' District Development Programme 2016 - 2020. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to follow the special procedure adopted in respect of the payment of compensation for the the acquisition of lands for large scale projects, with a view to carrying out the acquisition activities expeditiously without an interruption, in order to make a more justifiable compensation for the persons who are affected due to the acquisition of their lands, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Hydrology Study - Kalmunai Master Plan Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8448",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The task of preparing the Master Plan on Integrated Township Development in the areas of Kalmunai and Sammanthurai has been vested with the Ministry of City Planning and Water Supply and the plan is being prepared with the assistance of the University of Moratuwa. For the purpose, a comprehensive hydrological study needs to be carried out.  Out of this study, it is expected to create a suitable system to prevent the floods occurring due to the water-logging issue in the Kalmunai area.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with M/s Hydroinformatics Institute Pte. Ltd. of Singapore, to obtain the assistance of the Institute to carry out the Hydrological Study, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Providing compensation to persons who had private ownership of their lands which were damaged due to the landslide and those situated in the high risk zones at Meethotamulla, solid waste dump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8449",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- All persons who have expressed their willingness to accept alternative houses out of the house owners evacuated due to the damages and the high risk situation on account of the landslide of the solid waste dump at Meethotamulla, have been provided with such houses and the number of houses so provided is 170.  \n\n\tConsequent to this disaster, action has been taken to acquire lands where the damaged houses are located in the risk zone marked by the National Building Research Organization (NBRO) and 110 such land owners have been identified. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Anura Priyadharshana Yapa, the Minister of Disaster Management, to pay the assessed value of the lands and houses of those 110 land owners as compensation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Establishment of incubators in five districts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8450",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Rs.100 million has been allocated through the Budget proposals 2017, to establish an Innovation Accelerator Fund and to set up incubators in five districts to support startup. Accordingly, it has been designed to implement the Innovation Accelerator Fund under the Innovators Fund presently being operated and measures have been taken to set up incubators through the Universities of Peradeniya and Jaffna and the National Engineering Research and Development Corporation. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to allocate the funds required for implementing the proposed two projects to the Sri Lanka Inventors Commission, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Acquisition of Competencies on Nano-Satellite Technologies and Space Engineering",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8451",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The institute of technology KYUTECH, one of the National Universities of Japan, has implemented a programme, with the aim of granting capability of basic satellite technologies acquisition for the countries which have not  undertaken space faring. Thereby it provides experiences on the whole process of planning, designing, developing, fabricating, examining, launching and operating a Nano-Satellite. Under its first stage, a Satellite has been successfully launched to the orbit by a team of engineers representing the countries of Japan, Mongolia,Ghana and Bangladesh.\n\n\nTwo Engineers of the Arthur C. Clarke Institute for Modern Technologies (ACCIMT) have been selected for designing a  Nano-Satellite and launching it under the next stage of this programme and thereby it would be able for Sri Lanka to obtain knowledge and experiences of this field. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to enter into a Cooperative Research Agreement with the Japanese National University - Kyushu Institute of Technology (KYUTECH), Japan and the Arthur C. Clarke Institute for Modern Technologies (ACCIMT) on the participation in the Nano-Satellite programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Prescribing the Minimum Standards for the Medical Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8452",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Publishing of Minimum Standards on Medical Education under the Medical Ordinance, was a long felt need. The Sri Lanka Medical Council has drafted  the Minimum Standards required for the Medical Education so as to cover the relevant sectors of medical education such as the minimum qualifications required for university entrance, content in the courses for medical education, assessment of medical students, academic staff, resources and facilities for education, course reviews, updating the syllabuses continuously and administration and management. All the relevant stakeholders including the Sri Lanka Medical Council, the University Grants Commission and the Attorney General have reached consensus with regard to the regulation of standards. \n\nThe Cabinet has decided to treat that the minimum qualification required for every student for entry into a University of Sri Lanka to follow Medical Education to be a minimum of two (02) Credit passes and an Ordinary pass obtained at the G.C.E. (A/L) Examination for Biology, Chemistry and Physics, at one and the same sitting. \n\n Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to publish in the Government Gazette the Minimum Standards for Medical Education in Sri Lanka as Regulations under the Medical Ordinance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Governments of the Member States of the Indian Ocean Rim Association for the promotion of Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8453",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Indian Ocean Rim Association with the objective of driving innovation and competition among the member countries, has focused its attention to connect micro-enterprises and the informal sector with large companies and international value chains and thereby, to promote Small and Medium scale Enterprises. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, for a suitable authority of the Ministry of Industry and Commerce on behalf of Sri Lanka to sign the Memorandum of Understanding to be entered into between the member countries of the said Association, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Establishment of a Certification System on Health and Safety in the Textile and Apparel Products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8454",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is a complicated matter to identify the qualitatively right clothes for use out of the varieties of clothes found in the market. Attention must be paid on the health safety on the raw materials and the other chemicals used specially in the manufacture and pacing of fabrics  and the manufactures and consumers should be provided with adequate knowledge of this matter.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to make health and safety certification as a mandatory requirement for locally manufactured and imported textile and apparel products prior to gaining entry into the local market, to authorize the Sri Lanka Institute of Textile and Apparel as the agent responsible for certification, to decide relevant criterion with the assistance of the Sri Lanka Standards Institute and to make the process enforceable through the Consumer Affairs Authority, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Provision of Transport infrastructure facilities to the Colombo Port City - Construction of the underground Marine Drive Extension",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8455",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to adopt the Public-Private Partnership methodology for the construction activities of the infrastructure facilities of the proposed Colombo Port City. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement the project for the construction of the underground Marine Drive Extension as  an entry into the Port City from the Colpetty Railway Station up to Colombo Chaithya Road, with the Port City Project Company as a Public\u2011Private Partnership Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for the acquisition of lands for the development activities of the George Rajapaksha Playground at Weeraketiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8456",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Weeraketiya City Development Project, a land in extent of 0.3288 hectares has been acquired by the Urban Development Authority (UDA) for the development of the George Rajapaksha Playground. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to secure funds amounting to Rs.19.5 million required for the payment of compensation and the interest for the lands so acquired, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Authorization for the construction of a new Brackish Water Shrimp Farm in the Puttalam District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8457",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Brackish Water Shrimp Farming is the main commercial aquaculture activity presently carried out in Sri Lanka and  in the Puttalam District alone where it is found more popularly there are 1,320 shrimp farms in an extent of 4,500 hectares.  The main source of water supply for these farms is the Dutch Canal that connects Chilaw, Puttalam and the Mundalama lagoons. Taking into consideration, the adverse effects caused to the industry due to exceeding of its maximum limits of water intake and the non availability of an adequate water source to open up farms, the usage of new lands for shrimp farming in the District was terminated in the year 2003.  \n\nBy now the usage of water in the Dutch Canal is carried out sustainably by providing water on a seasonal time table.  Similarly, the semi intensive farming method presently adopted under a low stocking density in place of the high intensive farming method has prompted for new proposals being made to open up shrimp farms in the Puttalam District.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to take up project proposals which could be assured to have high potential with the objective of promoting shrimp farming industry in the Puttalam District under the high intensive farming method only, under a strict regulatory method, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Implementation of Joint Ventures centered around Fishery Harbours and Anchorages under the Fishery Harbour Village Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8458",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The attention of the Government has been focused to create a new business community, generate new employment opportunities and increase the fishery products export revenue with the use of the facilities found in the Fishery Harbours and obtaining the participation of the people living closer to the Fishery Harbours, by establishing the value added fishery products and services with the corporation of the private sector investors as well.\n\n\tAccordingly, the approval of the Cabinet has been granted to obtain the assistance of the local and foreign investors for the diversification of the  fishery harbour operations under the Fishery Harbour Village Programme. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to create service facilities and the improvement of infrastructure facilities associated with all fishery harbours of Dikkowita, Modara, Galle, Cod Bay and Oluvil and facilities pertaining to the repairs of fishery and non-fishery vessels, to support tourism by improving the infrastructure facilities in close proximity to all fishery harbours and anchorages, the construction of solar power and wind power plants inclusive of the implementation of several other projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Promoting Ceylon Tea in the People's Republic of China",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8459",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Owing to the qualitative aspect of Ceylon Tea, an opportunity has been created to popularize Ceylon Tea within China which inherits a deeply rooted culture for tea.  Since the Chinese people shows a trend towards consumption from green tea up to black tea, it has been recognized that the introduction of a formal procedure to popularize black tea of Sri Lanka in the Chinese market is appropriate.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of  Plantation Industries, to prepare a specific procedure for the purpose subsequent to discussions with the relevant institutions in the the People's Republic of China and to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding for conducting tea auctions in China, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Enhancing the Performance of State Plantation Companies",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8460",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are 49,654 hectares of land under the custody of the State Plantation Companies and the direct employment opportunities provided by the companies are 16,373. The weak financial position, excessive of statutory obligations, outdated agricultural practices, inefficient management practices and different external factors have resulted in long term under-performance of these plantation companies.\n\nTherefore, a proposal has been made to implement a performance enhancing process of these plantation companies through the introduction of modern technology and crop varieties, optimum utilization of land and natural resources, access for private investments, institutional development and providing solutions for difficulties faced by those who are engaged in the plantation sector. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Public Enterprise Development, to implement the proposed project in respect of the Janatha Estates Development Board (JEDB), Sri Lanka State Plantations Corporation (SLSPC), Elkaduwa Plantations Limited (EPL), Gal-Oya Plantations and the Sri Lanka Cashew Corporation (SLCC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Obtaining an alternative land from Kundasale in Kandy for the 'Nilasevana' housing project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8461",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct a Housing Complex in the Kundasale area in Kandy under the 'Nilasevana' Housing Project implemented as a Public-Private Partnership Project, with a view to providing houses to Public Officers. Since the land allocated for the purpose is situated adjacent to the Meditation Centre, it has been decided to implement the project in another location, taking into consideration the hindrances that could be caused to the activities taking place at this religious site.\n\nAs such, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Maddumabandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management and Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to allocate a block of land situated in the Mahawatta village in the Kundasale area as an alternative land, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Development of the Port of Kankesanthurai",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8462",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Port of Kankesanthurai located 15 km in North to the City of Jaffna was a Port constructed for the transportation of raw materials required for the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory. Cargo Vessels below 2,500 tons can be operated at this Port which is around 06 metres in depth. Since this Port is located in close proximity with Indian Harbours, there is a potential of connecting this with the international shipping activities, enhancing regional industries and developing the same as a Regional Harbour providing the services required for the Northern and North Central Provinces.\n\nAccordingly, the Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) has designed plans for the rehabilitation of the breakwater of the Port of Kankesanthurai, construction of a new jetty in order to expand its commercial operations. It has been decided to establish a Warehouse and to construct an Administration Building. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to transfer a land in extent of 50 acres required for the purpose, from the Sri Lanka Cement Corporation, over to the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Upgrading the Milk Production Network in Jaffna",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8463",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that the need for milk is more than 5,000 litre per day in Jaffana town and the surrounding areas. Consumption of liquid milk is also hiking up and therefore, in order to fulfill the need, it is imperative that the facilities be upgraded for the management of milk production.\n\nAs such, it has been planned to purchase machines to pasteurize milk and  hand over these machines to the YARLCO milk processing factory of the Jaffna District Development Cooperative Society so as to expand and strengthen the liquid milk and milk related production network in the Jaffana District. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Prison Reforms, Rehabilitation, Resettlement and Hindu Religious Affairs, to implement the proposed project at an estimated cost of Rs. 59.8 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Obtaining Specialized Consultancy for the Sri Lanka Police Reforms",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8464",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Reforming of the Sri Lanka Police so as to suit the present and future goals is a timely need. A Committee comprising of experts of the relevant field was appointed for the purpose of making recommendations and the said Committee has stressed the need for the transformation of the Sri Lanka Police service into a dignified profession which upholds the principles of Good Governance. \n\nAs such, it has been decided to secure the services of an experienced consultant to implement the recommendations made by the said Committee. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to seek the assistance of the British National Sir Hugh Orde, a British National with vast expertise on Police Reforms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Providing of an Information and Communication Technology System for Blocks 06 and 07 in the Akuregoda Defence Headquarters Complex Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8465",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to award the construction for the provision of an Information & Communication Technology System for Blocks 06 and 07 in the Akuregoda Defence Headquarters Complex, to M/s VS Information (Pvt.) Ltd., at a sum of Rs.372.06 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Supply of uniform and other clothing materials for the Tri-Forces, Department of Civil Security and the National Cadet Corps",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8466",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The uniforms and other clothing materials required for the Sri Lanka Army, Sri Lanka Navy, Sri Lanka Air Force, Department of Civil Security and the National Cadet Corps are supplied by calling quotations from the Local Textile Manufacturers. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to purchase the uniforms and clothing material required for the year 2017, from the local textile manufacturing institutions recommended by the Domestic Textile Allocation Committee, at the cost of Rs.1,887.8 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Calling for Bids for the construction of an Airport Hotel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8467",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing a better service to the air passengers and tourists, two investors have been provided with blocks of land for the construction and maintenance of two hotels with Star Class in two blocks of land located in the Katunayake Bandaranaike International Airport, belonging to the Airport and Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) Limited (AASL). However, due to the failure of pursuing action by those investors in terms of their proposals, it has been decided to call for Requests for Proposals (RFP) once again, in respect of those blocks of land. \n\n\tAs such, proposals have already been called upon for the construction of a 4-Star Airport hotel in one of the blocks of land and the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to call for proposals to select a suitable investor for the construction and maintenance of a 2-Star Airport Hotel in the other block of land, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Improvement to the Passenger Terminal Capacity of the Interim Terminal Building at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8468",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The design capacity of the passenger terminal building of the  Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) is 6 million air passengers per annum.  However, 9.5 million air passengers have been handled in the year 2016 and this number continuous to increase annually. As such, in order to increase the annual  passenger handling capacity up to 15 million a project for the construction of a new passenger terminal has been initiated. \n\nIt is expected that the construction activities of the terminal can be finalized around the year 2022 and until such time, in order to address the congestion of the air passenger traffic, as an intermediary solution,  it has been proposed to construct a pre-fabricated passenger terminal.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to take necessary action to finalize the construction of a pre-fabricated building by the end of year 2018, to facilitate 400 departing passengers in an hour at peak hours, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Management of the Warehouse Complexes being constructed in the Districts of Polonnaruwa, Killinochchi and Ratnapura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8469",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a solution for the decline of prices of agricultural products due to the glut situation of such products in the market during the harvesting period, the Government has implemented a project for providing high quality storage facilities to the farmers to store their agricultural crops. Under this project, action has been taken to construct 03 warehouse complexes in the Districts of Polonnaruwa, Kilinochchi and Ratnapura at the cost of Rs.600 million. Out of them, the construction of the warehouse at Ratnapura has already been completed and the construction work of the other two warehouses is due to be completed by early 2018. \n\nIt has been identified that it would be appropriate to assign the management of these warehouse complexes with an external party, on the basis of a monthly fee. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to assign the contracts for the management of warehouses at Polonnaruwa, Ratnapura and Kilinochchi, to the Regional Development Bank with experience in this regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Purchase of equipment required for the construction of four New Grid Substations at Nawalapitiya, Ragala, Wewalwatta and Maliboda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8470",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to interconnect the electricity generated in the mini hydro power plants with the main electricity transmission system, the Ceylon Electricity Board has planned to construct four (04) Grid Substations at Nawalapitiya, Ragala, Wewalwatta and Maliboda and the related transmission lines. Its construction activities are implemented under 03 packages and under the package 02 of them, the essential equipment are purchased as Lot A and Lot B.\n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the purchase of equipment under Lot A in package 02 to M/s Siemens Ltd., for a sum of Rs.297.2 million and the contract for the purchase of equipment under Lot B to M/s Ceylex Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.122.9 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Purchase of two Pilot Launches for the Sri Lanka Ports Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8471",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has become necessary to purchase two (02) Pilot  Launches for the Sri Lanka Ports Authority, to provide efficient navigational services to the vessels arriving at the Port of Colombo. For this purpose, a financial allocation of Rs.500 million has been made out of the funds of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to purchase two (02) Pilot Launches by calling for International Competitive Bids, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Introduction of the Electronic Government Procurement (e-GP) to the Public Procurement System in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8472",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the benefits to be achieved by the institutions of both public and private sectors, by enhancing the transparency of the Public Procurement System, monitoring and regulating the procurement process, deriving large scale economic benefits through integrated procurement, treating the suppliers equally and by creating a competitive platform for them, the Electronic  Procurement System needs to be introduced without delay.  The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to introduce the Electronic Procurement System to the Public Procurement System in Sri Lanka, on the recommendations submitted by the working group appointed for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-032-en",
    "num": "32",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "The Report of the Officials\u2019 Committee appointed in terms of the Cabinet decision dated 2017-10-03 on 'Procurement of Vehicles for Government Agencies'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8473",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 03rd October 2017 decided to appoint an Officials' Committee, under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the President, to examine the issues that have surfaced in implementing the 'Operational Leasing Method' which is presently being adopted for procuring vehicles for the Government Institutions and submit recommendations. Accordingly, approval of the Cabinet was granted to implement the following recommendations made by the said Committee.\n\ni. \tProcurement of vehicles required for political authorities such as  Ministers, State Ministers and Deputy Ministers through the Direct Purchase method.\n\nii. \tProcurement of vehicles required for the Senior Officers of the Government through the Financial leasing  method.\n\niii. \tFurther following the Operational Leasing Method for Double Cabs for heavy usage and high maintenance and vehicles with several passenger seats.\n\niv. \tOperating a formal procedure for the productive use of vehicles of the Government Institutions by the Comptroller General of the General Treasury.\n\nv.  \tThe Chief Accounting Officer of the relevant Ministry to ensure that an officer is entitled to a single vehicle in terms of a formal approval. \n\nvi.  \tGranting priority to procure vehicles with Hybrid engines and taking action for the disposal of vehicles over 10 years, considering their high maintenance cost."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-033-en",
    "num": "33",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Expediting the restoration activities of the seven storeyed building of the District General Hospital in  Negombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8474",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract for the restoration of the seven storeyed building of the District General Hospital in  Negombo has been vested with the State Development and Construction Corporation (SD&CC) in the year 2015. It has been observed that the said restoration activities are moving at a slow pace and as a result, the patients and the hospital staff are faced with a number of difficulties. As such, in accordance with the request made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, the Cabinet granted approval to obtain the services of the Sri Lanka Army for expediting the said construction activities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-034-en",
    "num": "34",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "Leasing out of the Port property and the Common Amenities to commence the operational activities of the Hambantota Port",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8475",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the conditions laid down in the Concessionary Agreement  singed on the 29th of July 2017 to develop the Hambantota Port by expanding its operational activities under the  Public-Private Partnership (PPP) initiative, the Port property and the common amenities should be given over to the Hambantota International Port Group (Pvt.) Ltd. (HIPG) and the Hambantota International Port Services Company (Pvt.)Ltd.(HIPS) on lease basis, in order to commence the operational activities of the Port. \n\n\tThe Lease Agreements pertaining to the lease of the Port property and the common amenities were signed earlier and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to issue instructions to the relevant State Institutions in regard to the implementation of the Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-12-035-en",
    "num": "35",
    "date_str": "2017-12-12",
    "description": "The strike initiated by several categories of employees of the Department of Sri Lanka Railways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8476",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet discussed at length about the difficulties faced by the general public owing to the strike initiated by several categories of employees of the Department of Sri Lanka Railways. Accordingly, with a view to finding a satisfactory solution to meet the demands put forward by the relevant trade unions, the Cabinet decided to appoint the following Ministerial Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon.(Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Special Assignments, to conduct discussions with the representatives of the relevant trade unions and make recommendations without any delay for resolving the salaries and other professional issues of the railway employees and  an Officials' Committee comprising of the relevant officers to assist in its deliberations. \n\n*\tHon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama,\n\tMinister of Special Assignments - (Chairman);\n\n*\tHon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne,\n\tMinister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine;\n\n*\tHon. Ranjith Maddumabandara,\n\tMinister of Public Administration and Management;\n\n*\tHon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, \n\tMinister of Education."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Amendment to the Firing Ranges and Military Training Act, No.24 of 1951",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8477",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The firing ranges established in the country are presently provided by the Ministry of Defence for training only to the Tri-Forces and the Sri Lanka Police. It has become a timely requirement to utilize these firing ranges for providing the training on firearms and explosives more formally to the persons recruited as security officers to the private security agencies, state banks, public institutions and the semi-government institutions and the sea marshals deployed for the protection of merchant vessels.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to amend the Firing Ranges and Military Training Act, No.24 of 1951, to make enable to utilize the said firing ranges for the purpose intended, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Establishment of the 'Institute of National Security Studies' of Sri Lanka by an Act of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8478",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka, is strategically positioned geographically, with a risk of its being vulnerable to both traditional and non-traditional security threats. As such,  the 'Institute of National Security Studies of Sri Lanka' was established in the year 2016, as a think tank dedicated to work as the central repository  of knowledge on national security, for deliberations inclusive of the Government,  private sector and the civil society to make enable to discuss and take action on the issues identified pertaining to the national security and stability and the measures that could be adopted in that regard.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to establish the Institute of National Security Studies of Sri Lanka by an Act of Parliament to enable formally to achieve the said objectives and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill providing the necessary provision in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2017-12-19-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2017-12-19",
    "description": "Control of Forest Fires in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8479",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2017-12-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Forest fires is attributed as one of the major causes for the decline of natural forest cover in the country. There are no natural forest fires in Sri Lanka and it has been observed that all fires that emanate in the forest areas are due to the negligence or deliberate actions of human beings. Cattle owners, specially set fire on the grass lands with the objective of getting tender grass and these fires spread into forest resulting forest fires. Hunters set fire to the forests to hunt animals and the chena cultivators set fire to the forest to clear the land for cultivation. Further, the fire used by the labourers who work on the railway tracks, fires set by some villagers on their lands bordering the forest boundaries and cigarette buttes and matches discarded by the passers-by etc. result in negligent fires and some people set fire to the forest for pleasure as well.   \n\n\tDestruction of flora and fauna and the destruction of their habitats, due to forest fires in the dry zone such as  the exposure of soil and erosion during the subsequent rainy season, the blocking of streams and rivers and siltation of reservoirs reducing their water storage capacity, release of Carbon Dioxide to the atmosphere are several adverse effects that result due to forest fires.  In the year 2016 alone 2,945 hectares of forest lands have been subject to forest fires.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President, Maithripala Sirisena in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, with the objective of controlling and preventing forest fires, to implement a series of programmes to cover the whole Island for the establishment of fire belts to prevent the spread of fires, establishment of fire extinguishing emergency responsive units associated with areas where fires occur frequently and including public awareness of the matter, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
