    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish the South Asian Regional Intelligence and the Coordination Centre (SARICC) in Sri Lanka to coordinate and to exchange intelligence information among the countries in the region, with a view to eliminating organized crimes and the drug menace in the South Asian Region. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Law & Order and Southern Development, to establish the said centre in Sri Lanka and to accommodate it  temporarily in the premises of the National Dangerous Drugs Control Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-20-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-02-20",
    "description": "Amending the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Act, No.31 of 1980",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the timely requirements, it has been proposed to amend the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Act, No.31 of 1980. Accordingly, the Voluntary Social Service Organizations (Registration and Supervision) Amendment Bill has been prepared, taking into consideration the recommendations made by the Parliamentary Select Committee which studied the operation of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations and its impact as well as the views of the relevant stakeholders including the Financial Intelligence Unit of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. \n\n\tThe objectives of making the proposed amendment are to provide for the registration of all the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to establish the National Secretariat for Non\u2011Governmental Organizations as a Statutory Body which is the authorized institution for the regulation and supervision of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to promote the mutual co\u2011operation between the State and Non\u2011Governmental Organizations, to recognize the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations in the effort to fulfill the common development requirements of the country, to strengthen and empower the civil society, to facilitate the effective operation of the Non\u2011Governmental Organizations and to ensure the transparency and accountability on its Finance, Policies and Management. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mano Ganesan, the Minister of National Co\u2011existence, Dialogue and Official Languages, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and to present same thereafter in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
