    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8664",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- When the National Audit Bill was taken up for discussion at the Cabinet meeting held on 20\u201102\u20112018,  the proposed Bill was referred to the Committee appointed under the Chairmanship of Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Special Assignments, to examine the observations submitted by the Minister of Finance and Mass Media and the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, and to make recommendations, if any further amendments are necessary for the proposed Bill. \n\n\tAccordingly, the Cabinet having noted the recommendations made by the said Cabinet  Sub\u2011Committee, decided to grant approval to the National Audit Bill subject to including the amendments proposed in the recommendations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Health and Medical Service Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8665",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the recent past, a significant increase is shown in the non\u2011communicable diseases such as the cardiovascular and strokes among the people of the country. Of the deaths caused, 75% are due to non\u2011communicable diseases and the major cause for about 40% is heart diseases. As such, the focus of the Government has been directed to improve the health and medical service facilities needed specially for the prevention of  heart diseases, and  providing treatments in that regard. \n\n\tUnder this programme it has been proposed to implement a project with the objective of improving such treatment services in the General Hospitals of Anuradhapura, Kandy, Kurunegala, Badulla and Trincomalee and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has agreed to provide funds for this purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations with JICA to obtain a loan of  Japanese Yen 10,639 million for the implementation of the project and to enter into the relevant loan Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-02-27-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2018-02-27",
    "description": "Supply of Chemical Fertilizer for Paddy Cultivation in the Yala Season - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8666",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The supply of fertilizer is necessary from the oncoming first week of the month of April for around 500,000 hectares of paddy expected to be cultivated during the Yala season of 2018. Since, it is difficult to import and distribute fertilizer prior to the said time period following the normal procurement procedure for purchasing fertilizer, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to adopt an expeditious procurement procedure and select a suitable supplier by calling for competitive bids and to issue Treasury Guarantees to the two state owned Fertilizer Companies namely, the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Limited and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Limited for purchasing fertilizer, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the implementation of the Giridara Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8667",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for the implementation of the Giridara Water Supply Project which has been identified as a priority project by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board (NWS&DB), which has been designed with the objective of  addressing the drinking water issues in the Dompe Divisional Secretariat Division covering 18 Grama Niladhari Divisions, at a cost of Rs.513.28 million.\n\n\tProposals have been called from local banks to secure the funds necessary for the project and in this respect, it has been decided to obtain the required loan from the People's Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to authorize the National Water Supply and Drainage Board to enter into a Loan Agreement with the People's Bank to secure the necessary funds, amounting to Rs.513.28 million for the implementation of the Giridara Water Supply Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Listing of Census Units",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8668",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Census and Statistics (DCS) conducts the listing of Census Units such as, housing units, collective living quarters and non-housing units island-wide based on the census of population and housing. The List is taken  as the Sampling Frame, in respect of all surveys conducted by the Department. From the year 2012 in which the last census of population and housing was conducted, the Sampling Frame has been considerably changed up to now due to the reasons such as disasters which took place during the period and the new settlements. Since these data are used for disaster management and achieving the Sustainable Development Goals in addition to duly carrying out the surveys of population and housing, it is essential to have updated information.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposals made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct the listing of Census Units in the year 2018 covering the entire island and  subsequently, at two year intervals, thereafter, with the collaboration of the district and divisional administrative mechanisms as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Raising Funds for the construction of the Multi-model Center in Makumbura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8669",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction activities of the Makumbura Multi-model Centre is in progress at present. It is expected to provide a more efficient and cost effective public transport facilities through the transport center constructed with the amalgamation of  the transport modes from railway to long distance and local bus services.\n\nIt has been estimated that, Rs.306.79 million will be incurred  to prepare an operational mechanism required for transport management, operation and maintenance  of the Multi-model Transport Centre and providing necessary information for the commuters. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, for the proposed construction of the Makumbura Multi-model centre by utilizing the remaining unused balance of the credit facility obtained from the Japan International Corporation Agency,  for the  activities of Phase 2 of the Outer Circular Highway Development Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Installation of the Railway Level Crossing Protection Systems and formation of  Project Management Units to expedite the rehabilitation of the Northern Railway Line",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8670",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The length of the Sri Lanka Railway Network is 1,450 km and there are all together 1,337 railway cross roads. Out of the above, 520 have already been protected, pursuant to the provisions set apart from the Budget 2018 and measures are being taken to install Railway Level Crossing Protection Systems for another 400 railway cross roads.  Further, a proposal has been made to implement a project to construct railway cross roads so as to cover all the remaining railway cross roads under the financial assistance of the Government of Hungary.  \n\n\tFurther, action has been initiated to rehabilitate the railway track from Maho Junction to Omanthai, and to construct a double track and installation of signaling system from Polgahawela to Kurunegala under the financial assistance of India with the objective of operating trains at 120 km per hour in the Northern railway line so as to reduce the time taken to reach from Jaffna to Colombo by 40 minutes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, for the establishment of Project Management Units to implement the projects expeditiously and to implement the installation of Level Crossing Protection Systems under the financial assistance of the Hungarian Export and Import (EXIM) Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Amending the Labour Laws for the protection of the rights of domestic workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8671",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though there are no statistics available pertaining to the domestic workers employed in Sri Lanka, it is clear that a large group of such workers are so employed. Since the prevailing labour laws are insufficient for the protection of the rights of such domestic workers, it is found that the worker community is faced with disadvantageous situations like employment for lower salaries, inability to obtain  leave and the non availability of social security. Since the domestic workers are excluded from the application of the Industrial Disputes Act, the Employees' Provident Fund Act and the other Labour Acts, the Department of Labour is unable to intervene to protect the rights of such workers.\n\n\tThrough the \u201cNational Action Plan for Human Rights of 2017 - 2021\u201d the need for the protection of the rights of the domestic workers has also been identified.  As such, considering a proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour, Trade Union Relations and Sabaragamu Development, the Cabinet granted approval in principle for enacting legislation required to protect the rights of the domestic workers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Implementation of the Small and Medium Scale Enterprises Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8672",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The programme implemented by the Government with the objective of securing funds for the capital and as well as the working capital requirements of the small and medium scale entrepreneurs, provides funds subject to a maximum Rs.50 million with a 10 year repayment period. Under this loan scheme, loan facilities are provided for business start up or the expansion of the existing businesses. Ten public and as well as the private sector banking institutions participate in this loan assistance programme and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to enter into the relevant loan Agreements with those participatory financial institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Extension of the Polduwa by-pass road from 'Suhurupaya' to 'Koswatta Junction'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8673",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The traffic congestion in the Kaduwela-Colombo road has become intense due to the rapid development taking place in the Battaramulla area and as a solution to the problem, it has been identified as necessary to construct a by pass road from the Polduwa Junction to Koswatta Junction circumventing the Battaramulla town.  The construction activities of the access road from the Polduwa Junction to 'Suhurupaya' has already been completed and the Cabinet approval has also been granted to extend this road up to  Udumulla Junction as a 2 lane road.\n\tConsidering the increasing traffic congestion in the Battaramulla area, it is proposed to extend this road up to the Koswatta junction. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to develop the Polduwa by-pass road about 4 km in length as a 4 lane road up to the Koswatta junction, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Lease of 2 land lots in the Muthurajawela sand filled area for the Logistics related activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8674",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Muthurajawela area in Wattala has been identified as a part of the Logistics Zone being constructed under the Megapolis Plan of the Western Province. The land in extent of 400 acres developed in the area by the Sri Lanka Land Reclamation and Development Corporation (SLLR&DC) through sand nourishment, has been alienated for various projects.\n\n\tApplications have been called by way of publishing paper advertisements to lease out two remaining land lots for logistic purposes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to lease out the said two land lots to John Keells Logistics (Pvt.) Ltd., the highest bidder for the purpose, for a period of 30 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Controlling of the floods in the Colombo and Kolonnawa areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8675",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kolonnawa Canal Diversion Scheme (KCD) has been identified as a major development activities under the Metro Colombo Urban Development Project, carried out aimed at mitigating of floods. Under this project, it is expected to widen the existing canals to flow down the storm water in the Colombo area during the periods of low water levels in the Kelani River and also to make arrangements to mitigate the flood condition occurring in the Kolonnawa area during the periods of high water level in the Kelani River.\n\n\tAs such, it has been planned to reconstruct the flood gate structure across the Kiththampahuwa Canal closer to the outfall on Sedawaththa - Ambathale Road  and to remove the bottlenecks to the canal flow and to conduct the gabion bank conservation activities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement the project with the assistance of the Officers of the Department of Irrigation and the Climate Resilience Improvement Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Amendments to the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8676",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need for amending the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005 introduced with a view to eliminating domestic violence has now arisen, when considering the problems observed during the implementation of the Act during the last 12 years. The Committee comprising of all stakeholders appointed to examine the matter after obtaining the views of the General Public as well, has submitted its recommendations for amending the Act.  \n\n\tAccordingly, proposed amendments include the increase of the categories of persons who can institute legal action on behalf of an adult person or children, subject to domestic violence, simplifying the process of filing an application, removing of the requirement of mandatory counseling in order to ensure the protection of an aggrieved party, amending the existing method of followup action, implementation of temporary protection orders effectively. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to amend the  prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005 incorporating the said amendments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Obtaining suitable lands to Local Authorities for Solid Waste Management",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8677",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Local Authorities are faced with the difficulty of obtaining suitable lands  in disposing of solid waste for Solid Waste Management adopting environmentally friendly methods. Even though lands have been released to some Local Government Authorities for disposing of waste, the development of those lands as sanitary landfills has been barred due to non-awarding of the legal ownership of those lands.\n\nTherefore, as agreed to by at the discussion held on this matter with the participation of all relevant stakeholders, the joint proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms and Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government to formally vest the lands already set apart to the relevant Local Government Authorities for disposing of waste and to acquire the land lots belonging to the Land Reform Commission and the State Plantation Corporation and those possessed by the Regional Plantation Companies on long term lease basis under the Land Acquisition Act, which has been found as suitable for the disposal of waste by developing them as sanitary land fills and to allocate the same over to the Local Government Authorities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Construction of the Kaluganga - Moragahakanda Transfer Canal (KMTC) under the Upper Elahera Canal Construction Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8678",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Design and Build Contract for the Transfer Canal comprising of two tunnels 8km in length from the Kalu Ganga Tank to Moragahakanda Tank, open canal way, aqueducts and the associated structures, which fall under the purview of the Upper Elahera Canal Project is implemented under the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the construction contract to Sinohydro Corporation Limited of China, for a sum of Rs.6,111.91 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Procurement of Catering Services for Passenger Lounges of the Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8679",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Airport & Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) Limited operates  four (04) Passenger Lounges at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), Katunayake and one (01) Passenger Lounge at the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport (MRIA) for the passengers of the Business Class, First Class and Special Categories. It is essential to provide high quality catering services to the local as well as the foreign air passengers receiving the services of these Lounges. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract to M/s Sri Lankan Catering Limited affiliated to the Srilankan Airlines, which has the potential for the purpose, for a forthcoming period of 03 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Construction of public institutions utilizing the cost effective NERD technology",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8680",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Engineering Research and Development Centre of Sri Lanka (NERDC) is carrying out research activities pertaining to cost effective  technologies of construction of buildings and also take measures to spread the outcome of such research among the public. Presently, school buildings, laboratories for hospitals, buildings or clinics and stores residential buildings for the forces and various types of houses have been constructed in various parts of the Island utilizing these cost effective technologies. If this method is adopted from the planning stage, at least a minimum of 20%- 25% of a financial saving could be had from the total cost of construction and also there is the possibility of minimizing the use of timber, sand and metal. The use of this technology for the construction of buildings has also been recommended by the Construction Industries Development Authority.  \n\n\tTaking into consideration, the above and making provision for the use of the cost effective method for the construction of buildings required for public institutions, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to award  the consultancy services, designing and construction of such buildings directly to the National Engineering Research and Development Centre of Sri Lanka (NERDC), subject to a maximum of Rs.50 million, deviating from the procurement procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Procurement of 100MW of Supplementary Power to ensure uninterrupted power supply in the County",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8681",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the inadequate rain fall that prevails, the fall of water level of the reservoirs could be expected within the next 06 months and it has been identified that this could be an obstruction for an uninterrupted supply of power. As such, the approval of the Cabinet has been granted to purchase supplementary power of 100MW through a short term power purchase agreement and in the meantime, bids have been called adopting the International competitive bidding for the purpose.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy,  to purchase a 56MW power supply from M/s Aggreko International Projects Limited at the rate of Rs.28.063 per KW hour and to purchase a 44 MW power supply from M/s Hayleys Aventura (Pvt.) Limited & SES Smart Energy Solutions Fzco at the rate of Rs.28.367 per KW hour for a period of 06 months, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Construction of the Vavunathivu Solar Power Plant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8682",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the Solar Power Plant with a 10MW capacity proposed to be built in Valachchanai area is to be connected with the Vavunathivu grid sub\u2011station, it will be named as the 'Vavunathivu Solar Power Plant'.  Bids have been called for, for the construction of the said Solar Power Plant and 17 institutions have submitted their bids in this regard. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract to Build, Own and Operate the 'Vavunathivu Solar Power Plant' to M/s Ex-Pack Corrugated Cartons (Pvt.) Ltd., which has submitted the minimum cost at the rate of Rs.11.86 per KW hour, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Purchasing of 100 Waste Transport Vehicles (Compactors) for formalizing of the transportation of waste by the Local Authorities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8683",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that 341 additional waste transport vehicles are required for the Local Authorities to carry out the waste disposal efficiently and effectively.  Out of this number, action is in progress to obtain 190 waste transport vehicles under the Korean Loan Aid facility.  A further number of 100  waste transport vehicles are proposed to be purchased expeditiously with domestic funds and for this purpose bids have been called.\n\n\tConsidering the recommendations of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC) and the Procurement Appeal Board, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to award the contract for the supply of 100 waste transport vehicles (Compactors)  with a capacity of 6 cubic meters, to M/s ZXY Hong Kong Co. Limited of China, for a sum of Rs.622.13 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Establishment of the Faculty of Medicine in the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8684",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The University of Sabaragamuwa established as a National University in the year 1996, is presently, a University comprising of 7 Faculties. In accordance with the policy of the Government to expand the medical education, a sum of Rs.1,250 million has been set apart from the Budget of 2018 to commence the Medical Faculties of the Universities of Wayamba, Moratuwa and Sabaragamuwa. Under this programme, it has been planned to commence the Medical Faculty of the  University of Sabaragamuwa in 2018 with the admission of 75 Medical Students. The construction of a building for the Medical Faculty has been planned in the year 2019 and until then building accommodation facilities have to be sorted out.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the then Minister of Higher Education and Highways with the concurrence of the present Minister as well, to vest the land and the building complex located close to Batuhena school in Ratnapura - Colombo main road belonging to the Auditor General's Department formally with the Ministry of Higher Education and Highways with a view to conducting the activities of the Faculty, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Enactment of a New Act in respect of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8685",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted, in principle, to amend the laws pertaining to Bribery or Corruption and pursuant to the said Cabinet approval, action is being taken to amend the Bribery Act, No.11 of 1954.  The power of instituting prosecutions in respect of the offences under the Bribery Act and the Declaration of Assets and Liabilities Law, No.1 of 1975 has been vested with the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, established by the Act, No.19 of 1994. \n\n\tIn terms of Article 156A(1) of the Constitution as amended by the 19th Amendment to the Constitution, provisions should be made to vest the CIABOC with the power to conduct investigations on its own motion or on a complaint made to the Commission by another individual pertaining to an allegation of  bribery or corruption and to institute prosecutions  on the same and to implement the International Conventions relating to the prevention of corruption to which Sri Lanka is a party.     \n\n\tFor this purpose, it has become apparent that it would be more appropriate to introduce a new Act for the establishment of CIABOC as an independent entity by further strengthening the same instead of amending the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption Act, No.19 of 1994. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new Bill for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Office for Reparations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8686",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Pursuant to the policy decisions as approved by the Cabinet from time to time where gross violation of Human Rights or Humanitarian Law which occurred, in the following instances, the necessity of having an independent institution  has been recognized for the purpose of providing reparations for the same:\n\n(i)\tIn the course of the conflict which took place in the Northern and Eastern Provinces in the past or its aftermath; or\n\n(ii)\tIn connection with political or civil disturbances; or\n\n(iii)\tIn the course of systematic violations of the rights of individuals, groups or communities of the people of Sri Lanka; or\n\n(iv)\tDue to enforced disappearances as defined in the 'International Convention on Protection of All Persons from Enforced Disappearances'.\nTherefore, a proposal has been made to establish an 'Office for Reparations' by law to which requests for reparations can be submitted by Sri Lankans belonging to all ethnic and religious groups including the civilians in the adjoining villages who were amidst those conflicts and affected by such incidents and including the families of the Police and the Security Forces. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill necessary for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Implementation of the Paddy Purchasing Programme of the Government (PPPG) in 2017/2018 Maha Season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8687",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Rural Economy, to obtain Rs. 500 million from the General Treasury, to implement the Paddy Purchasing Programme of the Government, through the Paddy Marketing Board in the districts where paddy harvest has been received in excess of consumption requirements of the 2017/2018 Maha Season, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-06-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-03-06",
    "description": "Resolving the Academic Issues of the Medical Students of the South Asian Institute of Technology and Medicine (SAITM)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8688",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Committee under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the Ministry of the Defence, has been appointed to introduce a suitable methodology for the admission of  the medical students of the SAITM to the Medical Faculty of the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University, with a view  to resolving the issue that cropped up relating to the admission of medical students to SAITM and awarding medical degrees to them. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to implement the following recommendations in the report made by the said committee, having examined the issue and  conducted negotiations with  the relevant parties, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tAdmission of only the students who are currently studying at the Faculty of Medicine of the SAITM to the  Faculty of the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and awarding of the MBBS Degree for those who successfully complete their degree programme.\n\n*\tThe Government to provide the capital and recurrent expenditure required for the maintenance of academic study programmes of the said students and the Recurrent expenditure required for the maintenance of hospital services of the Kotelawala Defence University."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "Execution of the Strategic Plan relevant to Sri Lanka in the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8689",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka, in collaboration with the United Nations World Food Programme (WFP), has successfully completed a large number of various programmes since the year 1968. The following objectives are expected to be achieved by the implementation of the the strategic programmes planned by the Government of Sri Lanka in collaboration with the World Food Programme (WFP), during the period from 2018 - 2022  in accordance with  the United Nations Sustainable Development Framework. \n\n*\tSupply of food all year round for the people affected by crisis situations;\n\n*\tSupply of food all year round for the children of school going age in the food insecure areas;\n\n*\tImprovement of the nutrition of children under 5 years, adolescent girls and women of the reproductive age, by the year 2025;\n\n*\tStrengthen the livelihood of easily vulnerable communities and the smallholder farmers to develop the ability of facing the risk situations;\n\nThe World Food Programme  has expressed its willingness to provide US$ 46.8 million for the implementation of the said strategic plan. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding with the World Food Programme to obtain the grant aid and to get the strategic plan executed through the relevant line Ministries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "Project for the establishment of the Neonatal and Obstetrics Reference Centre for the De-Zoysa Maternity Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8690",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approval has been granted for the establishment of the Neonatal and Obstetrics Reference Centre for enhancing the qualitative aspect of the Neonatal treatment services provided by the De Zoysa Maternity Hospital and for securing funds for the purpose. Negotiations have been conducted to secure funds from the Government of France for this purpose and considering the obstacles and the delay in obtaining the said funds, a decision has been made to consider the alternative sources of loans. \n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to secure a loan of EURO 17.99 million from the Standard Chartered Bank and EURO 8.45 million from the Sampath Bank and to sign the relevant agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "The Implementation of a Health Assessment Programme for migrants who visit Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8691",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Migration Health Policy was declared by Sri Lanka in the year 2013 and accordingly, appropriate measures have to be taken to prevent the threat posed on  public health with the diseases that could enter the country due to migration. Sri Lanka receives around 40,000 long-stay or resident visa applications annually and it is identified that around 60% of them are from migrant workers arriving from the countries with a higher risk level relative to the public health in Sri Lanka. Currently, there is no process to assess their health level status of these migrants and no incentive programmes is also in place for them to obtain a health insurance cover during their stay in the country to cover their health expenditure.  \n\nTherefore, it has become necessary to take some expeditious measures in this regard. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine representing Sri Lanka and the International Organization for Migration (IOM), to establish and implement a Health Assessment Programme for Residence Visa Applicants, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "Alternative Sources of Financing - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8692",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- As proposed by the Budget 2018, the maximum borrowing limit of the Government for the year 2018 is Rs.1,895 billion. It is estimated that within the first quarter of the year, around US$732 million will be required for foreign loan debt servicing and repayments. In the context of the existing global conditions and the difficulties that would emerge in future, in securing funds at a lower cost, it has been observed that it would be beneficial to pay and release the Sri Lanka Development Bonds which are to be matured in the year 2018, with a relatively higher cost by securing funds expeditiously, under the prevailing Fixed Interest Ratios. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Eran Wickramaratna, the Acting Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to secure funds for the purpose, up to a maximum of US$ 300 million, from the Bank of Ceylon and the People's Bank through their Foreign Exchange Banking Units or the Offshore Banking Units, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "Mullaitivu Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8693",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Mullaitivu Water Supply Scheme has been designed covering 09 Grama Niladhari Divisions of the Maritimepattu Divisional Secretariat Division in the Mullaitivu District with the objective of providing  safe drinking water for around a population of  7,430  living in the town of Mullaitivu and the suburban areas (around 1,500 families). Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of the Mullaitivu Water Supply Scheme to the Joint Venture of M/s Ceylex Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd. and Prathibha Industries Ltd.,  India, for a sum of Rs.894.74 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
