    "doc_id": "2018-03-20-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-03-20",
    "description": "Granting loans at concessional interest rate for the damaged businesses  due to conflicts  in the Kandy District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8705",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to provide relief to rebuild the damaged businesses in the Kandy Administrative District which occurred due to the conflicts that took place in the first week of March 2018.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Public Enterprise and Kandy Development, to grant loans at 2% concessionary interest rate under the 'Athwela Loan Scheme' to re-build such damaged businesses in the Kandy District, subject to the relevant terms and conditions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "The Association of Accounting Technicians (AAT) of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8706",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Association of Accounting Technicians of Sri Lanka which was established in the year 1987 has been registered as a company limited by guarantee under the Companies Act and at present, it has become one of the prominent accountancy and training institutes in Sri Lanka. A proposal has been made to incorporate the said Institution by an Act of Parliament, in order to produce the required competent Accounting Technicians for the Small and Medium Enterprise sector by further expanding the activities carried out by the Institution. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Securing of Additional financing for the Kaluganga Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8707",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Construction work of the Kaluganga Reservoir has commenced in the year 2014 and the work is expected to be completed by December 2018. Due to the unforeseen geological conditions identified in the Bund, the necessary revisions of the design done accordingly have led to an increase of the cost of the contract by US$ 50.5 million. Out of the shortfall of funds, the Saudi Fund for Development has agreed to provide an additional loan of approximately US$ 16 million to cover the shortfall.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct negotiations to obtain the said loan and to enter into the relevant agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Securing of loan facilities for the implementation of the Thalpitigala Reservoir Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8708",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The total estimated cost of the Thalpitigala Reservoir construction project is US$ 174 million and the Cabinet has granted approval to obtain a loan from the EXIM Bank of China to cover 85% of same. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain a loan of US$ 26.1 million from the People's Bank to cover 15% of the balance project cost and to enter into a loan agreement in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Establishment of the 'National Railway Museum of Sri Lanka' at the historical site of the Colombo Terminus Station at Maradana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8709",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Several attempts have been made to establish a railway museum of international standards in Sri Lanka to attract the general public, the students and the railway enthusiasts. However, due to inadequate resources and proper methodologies, the two(02) railway museums which have been established presently in Maradana and Kadugannawa do not function properly.  Therefore, it has been planned to establish a railway museum by rehabilitating the buildings of the Colombo Terminus Station and the buildings close by, in Maradana under a new railway museum project.\n\nIt has been found that more than hundreds of small and large railway related artifacts with historical value are available in proper condition for exhibition and by attracting local and foreign tourists to the new museum, the Department of Railways can also earn a considerable amount of revenue. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to establish 'Sri Lanka National Railway Museum', was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Value Enhancement of Sri Lankan Timber Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8710",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "When analyzing  the development of the other various industries in Sri Lanka, the Timber and the Timber Based Industry indicates a comparative downward trend or slow progress in comparison with other industries. The need for the sustainable development of the Timber and the Timber Based Industry of Sri Lanka a fair balance between the protective and productive capacity of the forest has been recognized. For this purpose, obtaining of membership by Sri Lanka of the International Tropical Timber Organization (ITTO) for Forest Conservation which promote conservation and sustainable management and the  use and trade of tropical forest resources and marketing, and the establishment of a Timber Innovation and Design Centre in Moratuwa where there are a large number of wood based manufacturing producers, has been planned.    \n\n       \tThe proposed  Timber Innovation and Design Centre would pave the way for the timber manufactures to develop first class timber and to develop Moratuwa area as one of the magnificent design centres with the assistance of the State Timber Corporation and the design groups of the University of Moratuwa. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Science, Technology and Research and the relevant institutions and the Universities, to implement the said proposals, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Vesting of a plot of land to establish the office of  Payagala Medical Officer of Health (MOH)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8711",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Considering the number of hospitals and the offices of the MOH situated in the area of the National Institute of Health Sciences in Kalutara, the establishment of a MOH office in Wadugoda, Payagala has been identified as essential for the purpose of according due attention to child and maternal health and implementing programmes to take follow-up action to prevent the non communicable diseases such as diabetes, heart diseases, high-blood pressure as well as dengue prevention in the area.  It is considered that the premises where the Wadugoda Primary School was situated which remains closed since the year 2004 is highly appropriate for this purpose.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to vest the said land with the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to establish the Payagala MOH Office, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Introduction to Sri Lanka a methodology for the transplantation of the organs of the persons diagnosed for brain-death",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8712",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Presently, the transplantation of the organs of the persons diagnosed for brain death is a surgical operation conducted globally, for a period of time. The organs of the brain dead persons connected to a ventilator in an intensive care unit can be so transplanted. There is the possibility of transplanting specially, the kidneys, heart, liver, lungs, pancreas, parts of the digestive system as well as parts of the eye, skin, veins, heart valves, ligaments and bones.\n\n\tApproximately,  750 - 1,000 are buried without retrieving organs as a result of not having an opportunity to give their consent for donating organs before their death. It is the responsibility of the Government to provide for opportunities for the people willing to donate their organs after death. Australia, France and Lebanon carry out this activity using their national data network and the countries like the United Kingdom have provided several opportunities of registration of their data network for the donation of organs through the internet, telephones, short messages etc.\n\n\tMotor traffic accidents has become a major cause for brain death and it is estimated that, approximately, more than 2,500 people die of road traffic accidents every year. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to design and implement a national programme for within Sri Lanka transplanting organs after death and to prepare an organ donor registration data network inclusive of future course of action, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Adoption of Innovators to Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8713",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Budget of 2018 proposed to provide the opportunity for new inventors to enter into industries and the objective was to absorb the University Graduates and NVQ Certificate Holders with a registered Patent or a viable business idea.  The industry will adopt the innovators and to support this cause, the Government will bear 50% of their monthly salary subject to a Rs.50,000/- per month up to a maximum of 24 months and in addition the cost of Patent in Sri Lanka and counseling on Patenting.      \n    \nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement the project inclusive of the determination of criteria to select the candidates and partner companies, to appoint a Steering Committee to take necessary measures to implement the Project and to take measures to ensure success of the initiatives including the  selection of candidates, the entities, matching the candidate to the entity and other activities of the proposal and also to appoint a Technical Committee to assist the Steering Committee, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Holding of a Presidential Media Award Ceremony for Media Personnel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8714",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The necessity of identifying the multiple talents and skills of the media personnel and while appreciating their skills, evaluate and guide them in the  appropriate way to create professional media personnel and motivate them and to empower the entire media sector in order to build a just society and to induce the media personnel to create a progressive media culture, has been recognized. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media,  to hold a  Presidential Media Award Ceremony annually from 2018 onwards to appreciate the mission and the contribution made by Sri Lankan Media Personnel, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Amending the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017 to provide for Transitional Provisions and to avoid the practical impediments in the implementation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8715",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017 will be in force from April, 2018. Under this, the transitional provisions necessary to be provided to the tax payers such as claiming the unexpired losses, capital allowances, tax holidays etc., which had been granted by the previous Inland Revenue Act, have to be issued by way of Regulations. Further, in order to avoid the practical impediments which may arise in the implementation of the new Act certain provisions in the Act require amendments. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to amend the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017 for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Nation Building Tax (Amendment) Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8716",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to amend the Nation Building Tax (NBT) (Amendment) Bill incorporating the following amendments proposed by the Budget 2018, was approved by the Cabinet:\n\n*\tImposing the NBT on liquor in addition to the other existing taxes applicable to liquor;\n\n*\tRemoval of the NBT from the following services and articles;\n\n(a)\tEquipment that enables advanced technology agriculture  practices, including green houses, poly tunnels and material for the construction of green houses;\n\n(b)\tCoconut oil and other coconut related products;\n\n(c)\tGem Stones imported for the purpose of re export after cutting and polishing;\n\n(d)\tNon motorized equipment and accessories for water sports such as Rowing, Kayaks, Canoes, Kite Surfing  and Diving;\n\n(e)\tNon powered equipment and accessories for aero sports such as Hang Gliding, Ballooning, Dirigibles, Parachutes and Para Gliders;\n\n(f)\tServices provided by the Sri Lanka Deposit Insurance Scheme;"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "The draft Bill of the Sri Lanka Light Rail Transit System",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8717",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Action is being taken by the Government to implement a project on Light Rail Transit System (LRT) to establish an efficient and effective passenger transport system in the Colombo Megapolis area. Under this 7 LRT lines have been planned to be constructed and in this respect priority has been given to the LRT line running within Colombo and the LRT line extending towards Malabe from Boralle via Battaramulla. It is expected to commence the operation of the Colombo Light Rail (CLR) system by the year 2025.\n\n\tIn accordance with the agreement with the Japan International Corporation Agency (JICA) which provides funds for the construction of the proposed 2 roads the regulatory frame work relating to the above has to be drawn up before commencing the construction of the said 2 roads. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to establish a legal entity for the regulation on management of the proposed LRT, to provide for relevant legal provision and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the Sri Lanka Light Rail Transit System Bill, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Establishment of Development Review Committees for the implementation of the Sacred Areas Development Plans",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8718",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The need for the improvement of facilities available for the pilgrims and the visitors who visit the sacred areas around the Island has been identified. In this respect, it is important to develop the sacred areas in a formal manner with a proper administrative mechanism and guidance. Accordingly, with a view to developing the sacred areas according to a well prepared plan, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to establish Development Review Committees in Anuradhapura, Kataragama, Seruwavila, Matale Aluviharaya, Mahiyanganaya, Kelaniya, Kotte, Devinuwara, Muthiyanganaya and Tissamaharamaya with  the authority delegated for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Replacement of the Plantation Management Monitoring Division with the Plantation Regulatory and Compliance Agency",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8719",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The lands acquired by the Land Reform Commission in terms of the Land Reform Laws, were vested with the Janatha Estates Development Board and Sri Lanka State Plantation Corporation and later they were leased out to 23 Regional Plantation Companies for a period of 53 years with effect from 1992. Monitoring activities of the ownership rights of the Government in such companies were carried out by the Plantation Management Monitoring Division of the Ministry of Plantation Industries. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of  Plantation Industries, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for the establishment of a Plantation Regulatory and Compliance Agency with sufficient monitoring powers to safeguard the interests of the Government for the remainder of the lease period of 28 years in place of the existing Plantation Management Monitoring Division, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Supply of electricity to the State Vesak Festival of 2562nd  Year of Buddhist Era",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8720",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The approval of the Cabinet has been granted to conduct the State Vesak Festival this year at the historical Bingiriya Rajamaha Viharaya in the Kurunegala District. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to secure the funds further required for the supply of electricity to the Bingiriya Rajamaha Viharaya, where the main function will be conducted and the surrounding areas, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Establishment of a Divisional Office in Kurunegala for the Department of Buddhist Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8721",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Taking into consideration the special religious activities and the significance of the places of worship, two divisional offices of the Department of Buddhist Affairs have been established in the districts of Kandy and Rathnapura. Important places of worship are located in the North, North Central and North Western Provinces. In the above Provinces, 54 places of worship where the  administrative activities are being directly carried out by the Department of Buddhist Affairs and a total of 2,364 temples are located. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to establish a divisional office of the Department of Buddhist Affairs in the Kurunegala District, in order to fulfill the official duties and related services to the places of worship and temples, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Protection of Human Dignity and Social Harmony Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8722",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Presently, it has become imperative to device measures to  suppress the surreptitious efforts emerging and the incident of harassment, revenge, intimidation and threat through electronic media to create social unrest and   the religious and communal disharmony among the general public, damaging the human dignity and social harmony.\n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice, to formulate legislation to enable to take action against the efforts made to violate the privacy of each individual and to create religious, racial or communal disharmony among the general public treating them as offences, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Re establishment of the Sri Lanka National Book Development Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8723",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Sri Lanka National Book Development Board, having established in the year 1972, on a recommendation made by the UNESCO to achieve the objectives of formulating and implementing a National Policy pertaining to the functions inclusive of improving and encouraging the habit of reading and referring books among public, writing and producing books, was abolished in the year 2012 and its functions were taken over by the National Library and Documentation Services Board. However, taking into consideration the necessity of having a separate entity to achieve the objectives and carry out the  functions in a more effective manner, which were expected to be performed by the Sri Lanka National Book Development Board, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to re establish the Sri Lanka National Book Development Board which was abolished in the year 2012, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "General Education Modernization Project (funded by the World Bank)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8724",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Along with the globalization and the rapid progress in the technology, it has been recognized that the General Education will lay the foundation for producing the human resource of a country to suit the economic and social activities. Accordingly, in order to suit the future requirements of Sri Lanka, the World Bank has given its concurrence to grant a concessionary loan of US$ 100 million for the implementation of a General Education Modernization Project, for modernizing and enhancing the quality of General Education. As such, to befits needs of the present labour market, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to implement the proposed project with a view to developing human capital with skills and training, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Technical Education Development Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8725",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The technology subject stream for the G.C.E.(Advanced Level) was introduced in the year 2013 and in the first phase of the project, the teaching of the subject stream commenced in 251 schools. With a view to further expanding the opportunities for learning the technology subjects, it has been planned to introduce the technology subject stream in 1,500 schools by the year 2019. Since this stream is inclined towards practical activities the schools where this stream is to be taught should essentially be equipped with modern technology and training of teachers for teaching the subjects should essentially be done. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to implement the Technical Education Development Programme with the assistance of the OPEC Funds for International Development (OFID) to achieve the said objectives, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Implementation of the Small Scale Infrastructure Development Projects at Local Level",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8726",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "In accordance with the Local Government Elections held under the new Electoral System there is an elected representative for each ward of a Local Authority and therefore, it is important to provide him / her also as representatives with an opportunity to take part in the identification of the infrastructural needs of the respective ward. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils and Local Government, to develop an appropriate mechanism to avoid issues that would crop up in the implementation and duplication of work, giving priority to the proposals so identified, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Formulation of a Joint-Programme for the Administration of Provincial and District Sports Complexes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8727",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "A project is being implemented by the Government to construct 09 Provincial Sports Complexes and 16 District Sports Complexes, covering the entire Island with a view to creating rural athletes who will excel in international events through the establishment of sports infrastructure facilities. Under this project, 04 Provincial Sports Complexes constructed in areas such as Anuradhapura, Badulla, Trincomalee and Kandy as well as 05 District Sports Complexes constructed in areas such as Kalutara, Matara, Polonnaruwa, Batticaloa and Jaffna, have been vested with the public.  It is anticipated to finalize the construction of the other Sports Complexes also, within this year.\n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of                              Sports, to formulate a proper mechanism for the formal administration of these Sports  Complexes, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Presentation of Regulations made by the Minister of Sports under section 34(1) of the Convention against Doping in Sports Act, in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8728",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Dayasiri Jayasekara, the Minister of Sports, to present the Gazette Notification issued, incorporating the Anti-Doping Regulations (Prohibited List) No.3 of 2017 made by the Minister of Sports in terms of section 34(1) of the Convention against Doping in Sports Act, No.33 of 2013, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Construction of the Main Canal from Nebadagahawatta to Mahakithula Reservoir Inlet Tunnel of the North Western Province Canal Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8729",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the contract for the construction of the Main Canal from Nebadagahawatta to Mahakithula Reservoir Inlet Tunnel of the North Western Province Canal Project under the Mahaweli Water Securities Investment Programme to China State Construction Engineering Corporation Limited, for a sum of Rs.5,505.28 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "The Development of the Kandy Suburban Railway (KSR) as a solution to minimize the traffic congestion in the Kandy Metropolitan Region (KMR)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8730",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The population in the Kandy district is around 1.4 million and out of which about 150,000 are the residents of the Kandy Metropolitan Region. Daily inflow of vehicles to the KMR is about 55,000 and the 3 access roads available are not at all sufficient for the fulfillment of the present and the future  transport requirements and the roads cannot be further widened due to extensive urbanization. Due to this reason, a proposal has been made to implement a Kandy Suburban Railway Development Project to minimize the acute traffic congestion prevalent in Kandy and the Asian Development Bank has expressed its willingness to provide loan assistance for the purpose.  Accordingly, the information submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to the effect that proposals have been called from appropriate institutions to obtain consultancy services necessary for the followings road development activities, was noted by the Cabinet.    \n\n*\tIncreasing the railway traffic capacity of the main line from Rambukkana to Kadugannawa;\n\n*\tConstruction of Double Lines from Kadugannawa to Katugastota or Wallegagama (Matale Line);\n\n*\tRehabilitation of the track section from Katugastota to Matale;\n\n*\tImprovement of the traffic capacity in the section from Peradeniya junction to Gampola."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Development of the rural roads in the Uva Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8731",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to award 15 contracts for the improvement of rural roads of a length of 557.31 KM in the District of Badulla in the Uva Province and 488.78 KM in length in the Monaragala District under the second Integrated Road Investment Programme funded by the Asia Development Bank as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "The Ambathale Water Treatment Plant Expansion Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8732",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "It is expected that the daily water demand of the Colombo district will increase up to 863,602 m\u00b3 of water by the year 2020.  Therefore, it has been planned to increase the water purification capacity of the Ambathale Water Treatment Plant by 50,000 m\u00b3 of water per day. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to implement the Ambathale Water Treatment Plant Expansion Project treating it as a priority project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Sanitation and Hygiene Initiative for Towns (SHIFT) Project for the Southern and Western Provinces of Sri Lanka - Design and Supervision Consultancy Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8733",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Sanitation and Hygiene Initiative for the Towns in the Southern and Western Provinces of Sri Lanka will be implemented with the funds of the French Agency for Development and the Government of Sri Lanka. Improvement of the management capacity of the large scale sewerage system of the Water Supply and Drainage Board and the implementation of the Galle Unawatuna and Kelaniya Peliyagoda sewerage systems will be undertaken by this project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for Designing and providing consultancy services to the Joint Project established by the M/s Cabinet D'ETUDES MARC MERLIN and SWECO Denmark A/S Green Tech Consultants (Pvt) Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Procurement of new components for the Gas Turbine at the Kelanitissa Combined Cycle Power Station (KCCPS)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8734",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to procure the essential components required to be re installed in the Gas Turbine at the Kelanitissa Combined Cycle Power Station after operating a specific period of time, from GE BHEL-GE Gas Turbine Services (Pvt.) Ltd. in India, the local agent of the General Electric Company, the original equipment manufacturer, for a sum of Rs.582 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "The Extension of the agreements of the Private Plants from which the Ceylon Electricity Board currently purchases power",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8735",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The total installed capacity, of the the Ceylon Electricity Board currently, is 4086 Megawatts. The hydro power plants that have been generating 1,391 Megawatts of power have been limited due to the drought experienced during the last two years. Since the power plants constructed presently, are due to be completed during the period between 2019 and 2022, the need has arisen to make a temporary programme to get electricity until the year 2020.  Accordingly, considering the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee (CANC), the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to extend the power purchase Agreements entered into in 2018 and due to expire in the near future to be extended to enable to purchase electricity further from the power plants belonging to ACE Power from Matara, Embilipitiya and Sapugaskanda for a further period of three (03) years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Construction of the Moragolla Hydro Power Plant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8736",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Under the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme, the procurement activities of the construction of the  Moragolla Hydro Power Plant with a capacity of 30.2 Megawatts are implemented in three Lots. Out of this, under the first Lot, civil works consisting of road construction, office construction, irrigation system and quarters for employees are due to be constructed and a sum of US$ 5.21 has been set apart for the purpose. Accordingly, the 7 bids have been received from the bids called for this procurement, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract to the bidder V V Karunaratne & Company, the lowest bidder for a sum of Rs.1,109.4 million, (without VAT) as recommended by the  Procurement Appeal Board (PAB) and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-032-en",
    "num": "32",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Obtaining a Re insurance Cover for Agricultural Crop Insurance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8737",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Measures have been taken by the Agricultural and Agrarian Insurance Board to implement an agricultural crop insurance scheme proposed in the Budget Proposals of 2018. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to award the re insurance scheme to cover the said insurance scheme to Renaisance Re Lloyds Syndicate Company, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-033-en",
    "num": "33",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Feasibility Study on the North Port Development Project of the Port of Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8738",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Considering the need to perform a feasibility study for the development of the Port of Colombo towards the Northern side by the Government of Sri Lanka for the development activities of the transport sector, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to call for  Expression of Interest (EOI) and Request for Proposal (RFP) to select and appoint an appropriate consultancy agency for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-034-en",
    "num": "34",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Carrying out the Rehabilitation activities of the Kankesanthurai Harbour",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8739",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "In accordance with the development policy framework of the Government, the rehabilitation of the Kankesanthurai Harbour for commercial purposes as a self sustainable Commercial Port has been identified to be one of the major projects under the North East Economic Corridor Concept. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to undertake the rehabilitation of the existing brake water and the construction of the new Jetty  of the Kankesanthurai Harbour by the Sri Lanka Ports Authority utilizing the funds of the Line of Credit provided by the Government of India, and to appoint the Procurement and Technical Evaluation Committees for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-035-en",
    "num": "35",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Additional Financing for Rural Bridges Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8740",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The need to construct approximately 400 bridges to upgrade the economic development in the rural areas and to reduce the provincial disparities has been identified. The currently ongoing project implemented to construction 1,210 bridges is in the final stages of completion, with over 1000 bridges completed and about 200 more to be completed.\n\n         \tConsidering the requests received from the different Provinces for the immediate completion of the bridges to improve the rural connectivity, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to extend the  periods of the relevant loan agreements to obtain the additional provisions required for the construction of 250 more bridges from the same agencies that funded for the original projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-036-en",
    "num": "36",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Augmentation of Kotugoda, Kolonnawa, Padukka, Horana Dehiwala and Madampe Grid Substations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8741",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "Taking into consideration the recommendations made by the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Procurement Committee, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contracts to M/s ABB India Ltd., for a sum of Rs. 2,214.16 million, to upgrade the Kotugoda, Kolonnawa, Padukka, Horana, Dehiwala and Madampe Grid Substations under the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-037-en",
    "num": "37",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Amending the Fertilizer Subsidy Policy to be effective from the Yala Season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8742",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Fertilizer Subsidy Programme, which provided fertilizer to the farmers, with effect from the Yala Season in the year 2016 was determined to be in the form of a cash grant and the same is being implemented during 4 seasons consecutively, since the Yala Season, 2016 up to now. Under the programme, measures were taken to remit to the bank accounts of the farmers a sum of Rs.25,000/- for two hectares of paddy cultivation in one season and a sum of Rs.10,000/- once a year, for one hectare of selected other field crops such as potatoes, onions, capsicum, corn and soya.\n\n\tConsidering the matters which arose while reviewing the Cash Grant Policy for the purchase of fertilizer, the Government has focused its attention on making arrangements to purchase the direct fertilizer such as Urea, T. S. P. , M. O. P. and Ammonia Sulfate as required by the farmers for a concessionary price determined in the open market, based on the recommendations to be applied in respect of each crop, covering all crops in lieu of the Cash Grant Programme.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to provide a bag of 50 kg of direct fertilizer such as Urea, T. S. P. and M. O. P. at a concessionary price of Rs.500/-, to the paddy cultivators for one season subject to a maximum of 5 acres through the Department of Agrarian Development, to formulate a mechanism to enable to purchase a bag of fertilizer of 50kg required by the farmers who cultivate other crops at a concessionary price of Rs.1,500/- from the open market, to contribute  Rs.675/- per season by the Government, to an Insurance Scheme on behalf of a farmer, providing a compensation of Rs.40,000/- per acre for the loss of crops such as paddy, potatoes, corn, soya and onions due to natural causes, as proposed by the Budget 2018, and to implement these proposals with effect from the Yala Season 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-038-en",
    "num": "38",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Presenting the Draft Bill of the General Sir John Kotelawala National Defence University to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8743",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The General Sir John Kotelawala Defence Academy established  in terms of the Sir John Kotelawala Defence Academy Act, No.68 of 1981, as amended by Sir John Kotelawala Defence Academy (Amendment) Act, No.27 of 1988, General Sir John Kotelawala Defence Academy (Amendment) Act, No.30 of 1990 and Sir John Kotelawala Defence Academy (Amendment) Act, No.50 of 2007, functions as a Defence University which provides Academically, Professionally qualified Military Officers to the Tri Forces and higher education opportunities to local and foreign students. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to repeal the above Acts and to enact a new Act namely, the General Sir John Kotelawala National Defence University, to further expand the academic activities of the University and to enhance its functions and the mission as a National Defence University. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to publish the Draft Bill so formulated in the Government Gazette and to present same subsequently, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-03-27-039-en",
    "num": "39",
    "date_str": "2018-03-27",
    "description": "Naming a different day for the May Day Commemoration activities falling within the 'Vesak Sathiya' of 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8744",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-03-27",
    "decision_details_body": "The Vesak Poya of 2018 has fallen on the 29th of April and the week succeeding the said date has been named as the 'Vesak Sathiya' and preparations have been made to conduct religious programmes Islandwide to commemorate the Three Noble Events associated with the Vesak Poya Day. Since 1st of May being the International Labour Day, also falls within the said 'Vesak Sathiya', a proposal has been made by the Most Venerable Chief Prelates of the Three Nikayas to make alternative arrangements to commemorate the May Day enabling the General Public to participate in the programmes scheduled for the 'Vesak Sathiya' without any obstructions.\n\n\tAccordingly, a request is made to all Trade Unions and the Political Parties to make arrangements to hold their ceremonies and programmes pertaining to the May Day on the 7th of May. As such, the Cabinet decided to cancel the holiday which falls on the 1st of May and instead declare 7th of May as a holiday."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Amendment of Chemical Weapons Convention Act, No.58 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8745",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Chemical Weapons Convention Act, No.58 of 2007 has been enacted in order to implement the provisions of the Convention relating to the prohibition of the development, production, stockpiling and the use of chemical weapons and their destruction in Sri Lanka. In terms of the provisions of the Act, the relevant subject matter Minister named for the implementation of the provisions of the Act, is the Minister of Industry and Commerce. \n\nSince the National Chemical Weapons Convention is a subject matter directly relevant to the National Security, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the Chemical Weapons Convention Act No.58 of 2007 incorporating the Minister of Defence as the Minister in\u2011charge of  the subject, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Proposed Amendments to the Law relating to Central Banking in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8746",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need has been identified to amend the Monitory Law Act relating to the establishment of the Central Bank and the other relevant laws and regulations for improving the Governance of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka in order to strengthen the independence of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Through these amendments it is expected to take appropriate measures to facilitate the adoption of a Flexible Inflation Targeting on the monitory policy framework to ensure sustainable price stability in Sri Lanka and to strengthen the financial sector oversight. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to update the laws relating to the functions of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Providing a monthly allowance to the Senior Citizens of over 100 years of age",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8747",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The existence of an elderly population of over  100 years of age, in a country is considered a benchmark which reflects a country's development in the health sector. It is identified that, presently, there are approximately 350 elders in Sri Lanka over 100 years of age. \n\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. S.B. Dissanayake, the Minister of Social Empowerment, Welfare and Kandyan Heritage, to pay a monthly allowance of Rs.5,000/- to all citizens over 100 years of age, with a view to ensuring security and welfare of their lives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Amendments to the Maternity Benefits Ordinance, No.32 of 1939 and the Shop and the Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act, No.9 of 1954",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8748",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need to take corrective measures to remove the discrepancies in the  Maternity Benefits Ordinance, No.32 of 1939 relevant to the payment of maternity benefits to a female worker during her confinement and the Shop and the Office Employees (Regulation of Employment and Remuneration) Act, No.9 of 1954 has been recognized. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. W.D.J. Seneviratne, the Minister of Labour, Trade Union Relations and Sabaragamu Development, to publish the two draft amendment Bills prepared by the Legal Draftsman in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present them in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Strengthening the Corporation in Science and Technology among the countries associated with the Bay of Bengal  Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8749",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the second summit of the BIMSTEC held in India in the year 2008, it was decided to establish a Technology Transfer Facility in Sri Lanka for the member states of the BIMSTEC. Through this facility it is proposed to exchange experiences among the member states in regard to biotechnology, nanotechnology, information and communications technology and space technology and to strengthen the corporation among member states for capacity building. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Susil Premajayantha, the Minister of Science, Technology and Research, to sign the Memorandum of Association and securing the funds required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Vesting of a land for the construction of  a Playground and a Community Centre at Badanagoda in Beruwala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8750",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine,to vest a portion of land in extent of 127.6 perches from the land called Pallegodawaththa managed by the Namunukula State Plantation Company for the construction of a playground and a community centre at Badanagoda in Beruwala for the use of the people living in the area around Grama Niladhari Divisions of Galpoththawila and Punsalamulla belonging to the Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Beruwala and Dodangoda, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Public Sector Efficiency Enhancement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8751",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The World Bank has agreed to provide Sri Lanka with a loan facility of US$ 60 million while the European Union has agreed to provide with a grant approximately US$ 10 million for institutional strengthening and the capacity  building of the public sector institutions pertaining to the public financial management. Focusing on the following, with the utilization of these funds it has been planned to implement the Public Sector Efficiency Project (PSEP), strengthening the efficiency of the public investment and debt management improving the operational efficiency of the budget execution and the procurement process, strengthening the Governance transparency and the  efficiency of the public services, and the sustainable public sector skill development and capacity building and public participation. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to provide the facilities necessary for the implementation of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Procurement of Vehicles  for the Government Institutions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8752",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for procuring of vehicles for the use of  Government Institutions under the methods of Outright Purchase, Operational Leasing and Financial Leasing. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to issue Circular Instructions indicating the criteria to be adopted when procuring of vehicles adopting each method, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Amendments to the Companies Act, No.7 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8753",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that certain amendments have to be made to the existing Companies Act, No.7 of 2007 to maintain the Business Index of Sri Lanka on a high level with a view to promoting the investment activities of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to amend sections 5, 9 and 10 of the Companies Act No.7 of 2007 to enable the Registrar of companies to notify the general public regarding the incorporation of a new company providing certain information of the relevant company and to eliminate publishing a public notice regarding the incorporation of a new company, and to empower the Registrar of companies to make order for any company to change the name of the company, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Amendments proposed to the Consumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 2003",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8754",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Consumer Affairs Authority has been established under the provisions of the Consumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 2003. The main objective of this is to provide the consumers with the proper protection through the regulation of trade and the prices of goods and services and to protect traders and manufactures against unfair trade practices and the restrictive trade practices. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to amend the Consumer Affairs Authority Act, eliminating the short comings identified in the implementation of the Act for the last fifteen years commencing from 2003 and also while complying with the laws and regulations adopted in the developed and developing countries to protect the consumer and the trade competition in accordance with the new global marketing trends, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Development of the Bloemendhal Area for Port related logistics",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8755",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that the Bloemendhal area in Colombo needs to be developed for the Colombo Port related logistics and the commercial and residential development purposes with the expectation to improve the cargo operation activities of the Port of Colombo and to improve its efficiency and it will enable to make the local import and export activities effective. Through this initiative, action will be taken to ensure a more protective environment devoid of health hazards to the community living around Bloemendhal in under facility houses.  \n\n\tFurther, it has been planned to carry out the construction of such work as the the expansion of the Authentication Centre at the Sri Lanka Customs, Urban Recreational Garden and the Kimbula Ela Water Retention area as well as the improvement of additional railway line facilities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to carry out these development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Improvement of the Productivity of the Tea Smallholders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8756",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 64% of the Tea Smallholdings accounts for the total extent of tea lands in Sri Lanka and it provides more than 76% of contribution for the total tea production of the country. As a strategy for further improving the Tea Smallholding Sector, the Budget 2018 has allocated Rs.250 million for the improvement of the productivity of the Tea Smallholders. Under this, it has been designed to implement 3 major projects namely, the introduction of modern machines for the effective application of fertilizer for tea cultivation, provision of equipment required for encouraging the adoption of correct agricultural practices and the rehabilitation of the rural access roads to supply the infrastructure facilities for the sale of qualitative green leaves. \n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of  Plantation Industries, to provide fertilizer applicator each to 1,456 Tea Smallholder Development Societies in each tea cultivating areas, to provide  equipment such as Spray Machines, Pruning Machines and Forks needed for cultivation and to rehabilitate the rural access roads to facilitate transportation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Enforcement of the Additional Protocol to Sri Lanka's Safeguards Agreement with the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8757",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka placed her signature to the Treaty on Non\u2011Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons (NPT) in the year 1970 and in terms of the binding effect of the Treaty, Sri Lanka has entered into an Agreement with the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) on the 06th of August 1984 on application of safeguards. The main objective of this initiative is to ensure through a verification mechanism, non\u2011diversion of Nuclear material and technology from peaceful use to Nuclear weaponization.  With a view to further strengthening of the safeguard system for collecting information of the Nuclear Fuel Cycle and its supporting elements, a proposal to sign an Additional Protocol between the member states of the relevant Agreement and the International Atomic Energy Agency has been adopted in the year 1997 and by May 2017, 129 countries have singed the protocol.  \n\nDemonstrating the dedication by Sri Lanka for utilizing the Nuclear Materials and Technology only for peaceful purposes, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to take necessary action to implement the provisions in the protocol within Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Establishment of Technical Collaboration in the field of Agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8758",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to enter into an Agreement to foster Cooperation in Education and Research for Long-term Technical Collaboration between  the Sri Lanka Council for Agricultural Research Policy functioning under the purview of the Ministry of  Agriculture and the Michigan State University (MSU) of the United States of America, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the  Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration (SLIDA) and the   Institute of Public Enterprises of (IPE) India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8759",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration responsible for promoting the skills  and the capacity building of the officers of the All Island Services of the Public Sector is in the process of expanding its relations with the recognized Foreign Educational Institutes, with a view to improving the learning and development capacity. Under this programme, a proposal has been made to enter into a MoU with the Institute of Public Enterprises of India which is a recognized Educational Institute in India.  \n\nThe Agreement will cover the areas such as joint training programmes, exchange of expertise, student, academic activities, management consultancy activities and joint research. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management, to enter into the proposed MoU, with the objective of providing public services more efficiency through the development of the capacity building of the public sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Development of Infrastructure Facilities in the Ruhuna and the Wayamba Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8760",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has given priority to increase the accommodation and infrastructure facilities in the State Universities.  Under this programme, it has been planned to develop the infrastructure facilities in the Ruhuna and the Wayamba Universities using the provision set apart by the budget of 2018.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Higher Education and Highways, to construct a building for the Medical Faculty and the construction of the Nautical Study Centre Building at the Faculty of Engineering of the University of Ruhuna and to construct the technological faculty building at the University of Wayamba, \twas approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Construction of the small Boutique Hotel  associated with the Waters Edge Hotel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8761",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Waters Edge Hotel Ltd. has been successful in securing a profit of Rs.240 million in the year 2017 and as such, focus has been made to further improve the operational activities and the physical infrastructure facilities of the hotel. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to construct a small Urban Boutique Hotel for the Waters Edge Ltd. consisting of 48 rooms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Procurement of Locomotives to Transport Solid Waste from Kelaniya to Aruwakkalu",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8762",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has been granted to implement the project for the disposal of Municipal Solid Waste collected in the Colombo City region limits to a Sanitary Landfill constructed in the Aruwakkalu Area in Puttalam. For this purpose, 04 railway engines and carrier wagons have to be procured to transport Solid Waste from the Kelaniya railway Transfer Station to the Aruwakkalu area. \n\nSecuring locomotives for this purpose through a new procurement process will take a considerable length of time. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to couple the requirement of 04 railway locomotives for the purpose, with the ongoing procurement process commenced by the Department of Sri Lanka Railways for securing railway engines for the Department, with a view to implementing the project expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Upgrading the Fishing Fleet to increase fish production and to enhance the quality of fish landings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8763",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet has granted approval for the implementation of a project for  upgrading the Fishing Fleet to increase fish production and to enhance the quality of fish landings. The budget of 2018 has allocated a sum of Rs.400 million for this project. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, for the production of 23 fishing boats on the basis of the beneficiary making a contribution of 50%, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Resolving of the current issues of the Oluvil Port for the immediate commencement of its operational activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8764",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Although the Oluvil port developed at a cost of euro 45 million, was opened in the year 2013, it has not been possible to commence its commercial operations, due to the siltation of of the harbour basin. Furthermore, the sea erosion of coastal area to the north of Oluvil Port has progressively advanced and it has adversely affected the livelihood of the fishermen in the area. The need to take action for the immediate commencement of the commercial operations of the Oluvil Port by resolving the issues concerned has been identified. The proposed solution is dredging the coastal area south to the Oluvil harbour and   sand nourishment of the coastal area north to the harbour and it has been estimated that it would incur an expenditure of US $ 15 million. \n\n        \tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to carry out the relevant dredging activities by securing Foreign Aid and to purchase a suitable dredger for such purpose under the Government Procurement Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement between Sri Lanka and Russia on Military Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8765",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to enter into an Agreement on Military Cooperation, between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Russian Federation, with a view to enhancing the bilateral military cooperation for strengthening mutual trust and international security, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Implementation of the Pilot Project for the creation of Young Agrarian Entrepreneurs in the districts of Kurunegala and Puttalam",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8766",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement a project under the 'Food Production National Programme' to create entrepreneurs who will be able to involve in agriculture at commercial level, with a view to improving the local food production.  As a pilot project, it has been planned for 100 selected young entrepreneurs in the Kurunegala District, to be provided with concessionary loan facilities to procure resources including modern technology in agricultural equipment. Taking into consideration the prevailing weather condition in the Kurunegala District and the interest already shown by the agricultural entrepreneurs in this regard, in the Puttalam district, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the pilot project including the district of Puttalam as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Construction of Rain Water Drainage Tunnels in the New Mutwal and Torrington Areas under the Metro Colombo Urban Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8767",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct a drainage tunnel system in Mutwal and Torrington areas under the Metro Colombo Urban Development Project, for the  control of floods. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract to M/s China Petroleum Pipeline Engineering Co. Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Enforcement of the law against those who disseminate false information and publish defamative statements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8768",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet decided to intimate to the Institutions such as, the Ministry of Finance and Mass Media, Law & Order and Telecommunication, Digital Infrastructure and Foreign Employment and Telecommunication Regulatory Commission to make recommendations to the Cabinet regarding the measures that could be taken within the existing legal framework against the persons utilizing the Social Media networks, various websites including electronic media and electronic & print media who disseminate false information and publish defamative statements."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-03-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-04-03",
    "description": "Expediting the payment of compensation for those who were affected due to the unfortunate incidents that took place mainly around Kandy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8769",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet decided to instruct the relevant authorities to expedite the payment of compensation to the persons who were affected and the properties damaged due to the unfortunate incidents that took place mainly around Kandy in the first half of the month of March."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Upgrading health facilities in the identified hospitals of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8770",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement a project for the construction of buildings for the identified hospitals and to provide them with medical equipment with a view to enhancing the facilities of health services in Sri Lanka. As previously planed, it has not been able to obtain loan assistance from the EXIM Bank of China. \n\nHowever, considering the need to implement this project expeditiously, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into loan agreements in order to secure US$ 72.25 million which covers 85% of the total project cost from the Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation Limited in Hongkong and the balance sum of US $ 12.75 million which covers the remaining 15% of the cost from the People's Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Popularizing the Sustainable Development Goals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8771",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the year 2015, Sri Lanka has committed  to implementing the United Nations Agenda 2030 designed to achieve Sustainable Development Goals by 2030. In this connection, the Sri Lanka Sustainable Development Act, No.19 of 2017 comprising of the relevant provisions is in force with effect from 2017\u201110\u201103. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, to request all State Institutions to incorporate the National Strategies to be adopted by State Institutions in their institutional plans in achieving the Sustainable Development Goals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Introduction of the standardized (plain) packaging for tobacco products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8772",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a result of the direct and indirect harm caused by the use of tobacco, it has been estimated that the death toll in Sri Lanka annually exceeds 25,000. The programmes implemented for the prevention of the use of tobacco and alcohol throughout the past have resulted in reducing the use of tobacco among the adult males in Sri Lanka from 29% in 2011 up to 24% by 2015. The expectation of the Government is to reduce the tobacco usage up to 15% in the next 4 years to prevent the 6,000 deaths. In this respect, as one of the strategies adopted for discouraging of smoking, a proposal has been made to introduce 'Standardized Packaging' to minimize the attractiveness of packaging of all tobacco products. \n\tIn this, only two colours or black and white can be used for tobacco products packaging and anything other than the information specified or mandated by the Government such as trade name, product name, quantity of the product and health warning or any symbol will not be permitted to be exhibited on these packaging. It has been a proven experience in other countries that this strategy has helped in minimizing the sale of tobacco to a considerable level. As such, with a view to providing legal provisions to introduce 'Standardized Packaging' for all tobacco products placed for sale in the country, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the National Authority on Tobacco and Alcohol Act, No.27 of 2006 or to prepare draft legislation to enact regulations under the Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Strengthening of  the Primary Healthcare Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8773",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though there exists around 970 primary level hospitals in Sri Lanka, there is a trend among the general public to bypass this network of hospitals and to move towards the hospitals providing treatments at tertiary level. Owing to this trend, a heavy congestion has been created in such hospitals providing treatments at tertiary level. Besides, the need has arisen to enhance the local Healthcare service due the increase of the elderly population, growth of non\u2011communicable diseases, dynamic illness patterns etc. As such, a proposal has been made to establish an advanced Health Service System, to enable the general public to have access to those facilities easily by linking the closest hospitals providing specialized treatment services, as forums.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the 'Policy providing Healthcare services with the objective of Universal Health Coverage', prepared inclusive of the following components, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tto identify one family doctor each to cover per 5,000 of the population and to further strengthen the institutions providing Primary Healthcare services to facilitate the prevention of illnesses;\n\n*\tto provide the Medical Practitioners with the initial training required for carrying out the functions in the field of Family Medicine and for  strengthening the first contact care services;\n\n*\tto ensure that all patients are provided with treatments at the Primary Healthcare Institutions and to encourage to refer those patients to secondary and tertiary hospitals with Specialist Doctors appropriately, in  a timely manner;\n\n*\tto provide a Personal Health Record to every citizen, with a unique heath identification number and to further strengthen the Health Information Management System;\n\n*\tto ensure the attribution and the utilization of human resources in the health sector productively;\n\n*\tto establish a method of obtaining distant assistance from Specialist Doctors to help the doctors providing Primary Healthcare within the relevant forums, in order to enhance their clinical skills."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Introduction of a New National Policy pertaining to the Fisheries and Aquaculture Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8774",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The draft on the New National Policy pertaining to the Fisheries and Aquaculture Sector has been prepared by the Ministry of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, having sought the views of all stakeholders including the fishermen, aquaculture farmers and exporters and academics and the general public, in accordance with the approval granted by the Cabinet to formulate such a policy. \n\n\tThe new policy has focused on the sustainable management of the fisheries industry and aquaculture farming with equitable distribution of benefits. The policy provides provisions for engagement in the fisheries industry in accordance with the International Standards, elimination of illegal fishing, introduction of appropriate new technology, minimizing of the post harvest  losses, increasing of the national fish consumption, promotion of fish product exports and enhancing the socio-economic status of the fisher community. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to present the proposed new National Fisheries and Aquaculture Policy in Parliament, to seek the views of all Members of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Increase of aquaculture production through conservation and development of the aquatic ecosystems associated with lagoons and inland waters of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8775",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- There is a high probability for the sustainable utilization of the natural lagoon system, estuary related areas and the small and medium scale internal waters in the wet zone with surplus of water which is not used for temperate grasslands and agricultural purposes the fishery industry in the country. Therefore, the Budget - 2018 has allocated Rs.1,000 million to implement a project to improve the fish production through conservation and development of the aquatic ecosystems associated with lagoons and inland waters of Sri Lanka. \n\n\tThe objectives of the project are to improve the fish production, generate new employment opportunities, promote tourism related industries, enhance the rural economy by implementing the fish product processing and value addition projects and to increase the foreign currency earnings.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to implement the project to cover 18 lagoons and 300 inland tanks in the wet zone, giving priority to the lagoons of Puttalam, Nayaru, Arugambay, Panama and Rekawa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-04-10",
    "description": "Agri-Irrigated project adaptable to Climate Changes (2018 - 2024)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8776",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 470,000 acres of paddy lands are cultivated under the small tanks, anicuts and irrigational channels situated in the dry and intermediate zones of the Island which is about 25% of the total cultivated paddy lands of the country. This provides livelihood means to about 384,000 farmer families. Since these paddy lands are prone to climatic changes easily 1,493 small tanks scattered in 87 cascades located in 09 dry zone districts have been identified for rehabilitation to resist the adverse effects of the climate changes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Agriculture, to implement a project under the World Bank Aid during the period from 2018 to 2024, with a view to enhancing the productivity of the cultivated lands falling under the said tanks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
