    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Implementation of the Sri Lanka Integrated Border Management (IBM) Strategy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8785",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The border protection and management is highly important, in order to maintain the national security and safety of the country effectively.  This has become a matter of paramount importance especially with the increase in the cross border movement of both people and goods. As such, the National Border Management Committee has been established in the year 2016 to act as the principal coordinating body within the Government for border management.\n\t\n\tThe Committee has prepared a formal Integrated Border Management (IBM) Strategy and Action Plan, identifying the responsibilities and functions of the various inter\u2011agencies engaged in boarder protection, to establish an effective border management in the country, in accordance with the international standards.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to implement the Strategy and the Action Plan under the grant aid provided by the Government of Australia through the International Organization for Migration (IOM), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Enactment of the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8786",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to expand the pre-hospital care ambulance service presently being operated in the Western and Southern Provinces under the grant facility of the Government of India, to the other Provinces as well and to establish the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' for the administration of the said service. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to publish the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman, incorporating the provisions required for the purpose in the Government Gazette and to present it subsequently, in  Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Securing of Funds for the proposed Technical Education Development Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8787",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The Government has found the need to upgrade the work force in Sri Lanka  to suit the changing demand for emerging technologies and skills in the country. Therefore, considerable changes have been made to the education system in Sri Lanka during the recent past, focusing on vocational skills.  In this respect, the technology subject stream was introduced for the G.C.E. (A/L) from the year 2013 and action should essentially be taken for providing the required modern infrastructure facilities for the practical activities and training of teachers.  For this purpose, it has been planned to implement the proposed Technical Education Development Programme at a cost of US $ 60.7million.\n\nThe OPEC Fund for International Development (OFID) has agreed to grant a loan facility of US $ 50 million for the implementation of the project and the balance sum of US $ 10.7 million will be borne by the Government of Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a loan agreement with the OPEC Fund for International Development (OFID), to obtain a loan of US$50 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Primary Healthcare System Strengthening Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8788",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "Even though the management of child and maternity health services and communicable diseases has achieved its success on account of the free health service, further challenges such as the growth of the aged population and the spreading of non\u2011communicable diseases due to unwholesome foods and bad health practices, have to be dealt with. At the Primary Healthcare level, more attention has to be focused on communicable diseases such as Dengue fever, Tuberculosis and H.I.V./AIDS, in addition to non\u2011communicable diseases. Due to this reason, it has become a timely requirement to develop the Primary Healthcare service facilities in Sri Lanka and accordingly, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement the 'Policy providing Healthcare services aimed at Universal Health Coverage', formulated in that regard.\n\n\tUnder this, it has been designed to implement a Five Year Project for the empowerment of the Primary Healthcare System identifying the deficiencies in the Primary Healthcare system prevailing in the country to enable to provide a comprehensive and qualitative health treatment service. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the proposed project by the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine in collaboration with the Ministry of Provincial Councils and Local Government, utilizing the funds of US$ 200 million as agreed to by the World Bank to provide under concessionary terms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Upgrading the functions of the Institute of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology (IFMT)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8789",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The Institute of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology (IFMT) of the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, performs a significant role in  conducting autopsies. A proposal has been made to implement a programme with the collaboration of the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) with a view to enhancing the quality of the operations of the said Institute through standardization and centralization of  autopsy associated operations and training of non\u2011medical staff. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to sign a Letter of Agreement between the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine and the International Committee of the Red Cross in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
