    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Signing of an Agreement on the Exchange of Sugarcane Breeding Material between Sri Lanka and Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8793",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "Under a collaboration undertaken between 3 Agricultural Research Institutes in Pakistan and the Sugarcane Research Institute of Sri Lanka in the year 2010, the exchange of commercial varieties of sugarcane breeding material for sugarcane plant improvement through modern breeding technologies and training of young agricultural scientists have been carried out.\n\n\tConsidering its success, a proposal has been made to have a new Memorandum of Understanding on the exchange of sugarcane breeding material between the Sugarcane Research Institute of Sri Lanka and the Sugarcane Research and Development Board and the Sugarcane Research Institute in Faisalabad, Pakistan. Under this programme, an opportunity is created to obtain new sugarcane varieties to Sri Lanka and to engage in joint research activities with the Agricultural Scientists of Pakistan.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to sign the proposed Memorandum of Understanding between the relevant institutes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Development of means of livelihood associated with Model Villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8794",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "Under the model village programme implemented by the Ministry of Housing and Construction, the impoverished and low income families who have neither a house of their own nor a suitable plot of land for the construction of a house, is provided with a state land and a loan facility up to a maximum of Rs.500,000/- to construct a house. Under this programme, the work pertaining to 596 model villages have commenced from the year 2015 up to now and out of which 54 model villages have already been vested with the beneficiaries.  \n\nFor the sustainable upliftment of this community, in addition to providing houses, it is essential to develop their income as well as their livelihood. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to appoint a Steering Committee comprising of the officers of the relevant institutions for the introduction of home gardening, small scale animal husbandry, domestic industries and self employment activities in the model villages, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Allocation of lands for 'Semata Sevana' and 'Grama Shakthi' Model Villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8795",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "When strengthening of the low income communities through socio\u2011economic empowerment, the Government by the implementation of the 'Semata Sevana' and 'Grama Shakthi' Model Villages programmes has taken measures to resolve their issues with regard to their basic need of housing. In order to achieve the target under the programme for the construction of 2,500 model villages by the year 2020, it is imperative that around 650 model villages are constructed  annually. \n\nFor this purpose, the allocation of lands Island-wide has to be done expeditiously. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to establish an Officials' Committee under the Co\u2011Chairmanship of the Secretary to the Ministry of Housing and Construction and the Secretary to the Ministry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms and comprising of the representatives of the relevant Ministries and institutions  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Appointment of Consultancy Service Agencies for the Construction of the new buildings of the Sri Lanka Police",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8796",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "A sum exceeding Rs.1,000 million is allocated annually to the Sri Lanka Police, for the construction of new buildings and for the improvement and renovations pertaining to the existing buildings. Taking into consideration a proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration and Management and  the Minister of Law & Order, to select a consultancy service agency for the new building construction projects of the Sri Lanka Police during the period from 2018 to 2020, approval of the Cabinet was granted to obtain the  services intended from the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), State Engineering Corporation and  the Department of National Buildings."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Sale of Mineral Products of the Lanka Mineral Sands Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8797",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The Lanka Mineral Sands Ltd. sells its main mineral products such as Ilmenite, Rutile, Zircon, Hi Ti Ilmenite etc. through the International Competitive Bidding Procedure. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to sell 17,800 metric tons of mineral sands of different types to the highest bidders who have submitted their quotations, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Entering into a long term Contract for the purchase of 7,000,000 barrels of Crude Oil",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8798",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "It has been decided to purchase crude oil necessary under the term contracts, to ensure the uninterrupted supply to the Sapugaskanda Oil Refinery of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation for its continuous operation. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development to award the contract to M/s Swiss Singapore Overseas Enterprises Pte. Ltd. for the purchase of 7,000,000 Barrels of Murban Crude Oil required for a period of 8 months from the 01st of April 2018 for a premium value of US$ 1.69 per crude oil barrel, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Construction and augmentation of the Biyagama 220/33 kV Grid Substation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8799",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction and augmentation of the Biyagama 220/33 kV Grid Substation implemented under the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme, to M/s ABB India Limited for a sum of Rs.1,434.11 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Purchase of the machinery required for enhancing the performance of the Department of Government Factory",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8800",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The Department of Government Factory is a pioneering institution which supplies Mechanical Engineering Services to the public and private sector and especially, its Heavy Fabrication and Mechanical Workshop provides large structures and the necessary engineering products and services required for the irrigation sector. With the development of the country's irrigation industry, the demand for the construction, fixing and refurbishing of irrigation water management sluice gates is in the increase and to meet the demand it has been identified that the production capacity of the workshop has to be enhanced. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to purchase a Plano Miller and a Computer Numerical Control (CNC) Machine which could be operated by computer required for the Heavy Structural Machinery Division, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-04-24-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-04-24",
    "description": "Entering into Three (03) Term Contracts to Purchase Refined Petroleum Products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8801",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-04-24",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, to enter into Three (03) Term Contracts with the relevant suppliers to purchase 4,650,000 Gas Oil (Diesel) Barrels, 2,080,000 Jet A\u20111 Gas Oil Barrels and 1,275,000 Gasoline (Petrol) Barrels required for a period of eight (08) months from the 15th of March 2018, as recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SSCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Drafting of a new Immigrants and Emigrants Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8802",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "Cabinet has granted approval to enact a new Act reviewing the Sri Lanka Immigrants and Emigrants Act No.20 of 1948, taking into consideration, the timely needs. As such, a Committee comprising of Experts conversant with the subject has been appointed to study the subject specific matters. The Department of Immigration and Emigration has prepared a Report, pertaining to the provisions to be included in the new Immigrants and Emigrants Act  based on the recommendations of the said Committee. \n\nAccordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of  Internal Affairs and Wayamba Development, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new Immigration and Emigration Bill incorporating the provisions proposed in the said Report, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Grant and Implementation Agreement between the Millennium Challenge Corporation, USA and the Government of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8803",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The Cabinet has granted approval to obtain a US$ Grant of 7.4 million to be awarded to Sri Lanka by the Millennium Challenge Corporation (MCC) which is a foreign grant aid agency of the United States of America for the development of several important sectors towards the advancement of the  economic growth of Sri Lanka within the forthcoming period of five years, and also to sign the Agreement pertaining to it. Subsequently, the said corporation has also agreed to award Sri Lanka an additional grant of US$ 2.6 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to obtain the additional grant and to sign the Agreement made between the Millennium Challenge Corporation and the Government of Sri Lanka in respect of the implementation of the programmes under same with a revised total grant of US$ 10 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Regulating the Registration of International Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8804",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "As a result of the non-formulation of laws and regulations pertaining to the registration, accreditation and regulation of international schools, there is a tendency of establishing an unlimited number of international schools below standards island\u2011wide along various informal methods of registration. Since the children who receive the education from these schools form more than 95% of the Sri Lankan nationals, it should be ensured that they receive a quality education to suit the needs of the country. When requesting the Sri Lankan community living abroad to return to Sri Lanka to contribute to the development process of the country and attracting the foreign investors into the country, the availability of standardized international schools is an essential factor and an absolute necessity.\n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, the Cabinet granted approval to resume the registration of international schools under the Companies Act, on the recommendations of the Ministry of Education until such time that a formal legal framework is formulated. The Cabinet further decided to appoint a Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee to study and make necessary recommendations and establish legal provision for the registration, accreditation, regulation, quality assurance and monitoring and making it mandatory for the training of the teachers of those schools and for teaching of the subjects of Sinhala, Tamil, Religion and History for the Sri Lankan students receiving their education in the international schools."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the field of Tourism between Sri Lanka and Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8805",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to promote Cooperation in  the field of Tourism between Sri Lanka and Pakistan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "The proposed Health System Enhancement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8806",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "It has been planned to enhance the health system of the North Central, Central, Sabaragamuwa and the Uva Provinces under the proposed health system enhancement project to be implemented  under the  Asian Development Bank (ADB) Assistance and funds of the Sri Lanka Government. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to establish Project Management Units under the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine and the  relevant provincial level, for the implementation of the project and to recruit the necessary staff for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Establishment of Joint Ventures by the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation (SPMC) of Sri Lanka with investors to promote the manufacturing of pharmaceuticals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8807",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "With the uplifting of the pharmaceutical manufacturing industry in Sri Lanka, a considerable amount of foreign exchange incurred for the import of pharmaceuticals, could be saved. Hence, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to identify the investors with the potential of supplying  pharmaceuticals of high quality to the Government Hospitals in an efficient manner and to establish Joint Ventures between the investors and the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation of Sri Lanka.\n\nWith a view to granting legal authority to the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation of Sri Lanka, to enter into the Joint Ventures, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to amend the orders issued under the State Industrial Corporations Act, No.49 of 1957, published in the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.456/21 dated 1987\u201107\u201104, as recommended by the Attorney General, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Construction of a Three-storey Rehabilitation Centre and providing it with equipment and the implementation of a three-year Training Programme in the Teaching Hospital, Jaffna",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8808",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "Teaching Hospital, Jaffna is a major tertiary Health Service Centre in Sri Lanka and provides the clinical training required to the undergraduates at the Faculty of Medicine of the University of Jaffna. In the year 2017, 39,390 surgeries have been performed at the hospital and out of those, around 12,486 are orthopedic surgeries requiring post\u2011operative rehabilitation care. It has been identified that the infrastructure facilities and staff training at the hospital should be improved, in order to provide quality rehabilitation care services.\n\nIt has therefore been proposed to construct a three-storey rehabilitation centre at the Teaching Hospital, Jaffna, to provide it with equipment and to implement a three year training programme to enhance the skills of the relevant staff. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to implement the  proposed project at a cost of Rs.605 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Implementation of the 'Women Entrepreneurship Finance Initiative",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8809",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "Taking into consideration the importance of motivating women entrepreneurs, a proposal has been made to implement a loan scheme known as 'Women Entrepreneurship Finance Initiative Grant Programme'. It has been planned to implement the loan scheme under the second phase of the Small and Medium-sized Enterprises Line of Credit Scheme presently in force, utilizing the financial assistance of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) has agreed to provide. Loans will be provided to the women entrepreneurs who satisfy the following conditions and an amount of 20% - 30% of the loan will be given as a non\u2011repayable grant:\n\n\nI.\tthe requested loan should be Rs.750,000/- or more and 51% or more of the relevant business institution should be owned by women; or\n\t\nII.\tthe loan for which the request is made should be Rs.750,000/- or more and the following three conditions must be fulfilled;\n\n- \tthe minimum of 20% of the institution must be owned by women.\n\n- \tthe Chief Executive Officer or the Chief Operations Officer should be a woman.\n\n- \tthe women representation where the Director Boards exist, must be a minimum of 30%.\n\nAccordingly, giving priority to the less developed areas such as Uva, Sabaragamuwa, North and East, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement the loan scheme through 10 financial institutions island\u2011wide, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Conducting of the Regional Symposium on Sustainable Development Goal  -'Life below Water' (Blue SDG) on 21st and 22nd June 2018 in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8810",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "It has been found that, the fisheries industry is able to contribute a great deal in achieving the goals coming under the Sustainable Development Goals of the United Nations such as eradication of poverty etc. As such, the importance of being prepared collectively in facing challenges and achieving the Life below Water or Blue Sustainable Development Goals has been emphasized. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the then Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development also taking into consideration the concurrence given by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the present Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, to host a Regional Symposium on  Blue Sustainable Development Goals with the participation of the representatives of the coastal nations of the region on 21st and 22nd of June 2018 in Sri Lanka and to obtain the donor award of Rs 3.48 million granted by the Government of Norway, in order to cover the expenditure incurred for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Amending the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act, No.25 of 2002",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8811",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act, No.25 of 2002 provides for combating trans\u2011national  crimes and strengthening the prevention of crimes or internal investigation and confiscating the crimes proceeds. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to amend the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act, No.25 of 2002, for identifying the offences relating to Money Laundering and the necessity of criminalizing the offences related to bribery outlined in Article 16 of the Convention of the United Nations against Bribery and Corruption and the recent developments  pertaining to computer systems and data related criminal offences, reflecting the international obligations of Sri Lanka in the present context. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to publish the Amendment Bill so formulated in the Government Gazette and to present the same, subsequently, in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Strengthening of the National Equipment and Machinery Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8812",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The  National Equipment and Machinery Organization was established in the year 1992 as a remedial measure taken to address the dearth that existed in machineries required for the construction sector to implement the regional development projects expeditiously. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to obtain a loan facility on a Treasury Guarantee, in order to secure the working capital required to expand the entrepreneurial affairs of the Organization, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Establishment of a Single Window Investment Facilitation Taskforce (SWIFT) for providing investment services in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8813",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "At present, the investors who envisage to commence their operational activities in Sri Lanka, are supposed to obtain around 14 approvals/permits provided by various Government Institutions. The lengthy period taken for the purpose results in discouraging the investors. Even though the Board of Investment (BOI) of Sri Lanka functions as the Coordinating institution, constraints have come up in making the process efficient, due to various obstacles found in the other relevant Government Institutions. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to establish a Single Window Investment Facilitation Task Force with proper coordination and a mechanism for follow\u2011up action and regulation as a remedial measure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Supply of a Air Traffic Management System, for the Bandaranaike International Airport at Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8814",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the supply and Commissioning of a Air Traffic Management System for the Bandaranaike International Airport at Katunayake to M/s Thales Air Systems S.A.S., France, as recommended by the  Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Implementation of the Colombo Suburban Railway Efficiency Improvement Project (CSREIP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8815",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "In providing an efficient passenger transportation service to the general public by improving of the Public Transport Service, the Government has identified the development of the Railway Service of the country as a priority. Accordingly, action has been taken to commence the development activities of the suburban railway system connecting the Colombo city with other areas under the 'Colombo Suburban Railway Project' implemented under the financial assistance of the Asian Development Bank (ADB). A proposal has been made to implement the following few small scale projects required for the improvement of the railway efficiency through 'Colombo Suburban Railway Efficiency Improvement Project (CSREIP)' to be implemented under this project:\n\n*\tImplementation of a modern Ticketing and Seating Reservation System,  replacing the existing ticketing and seating reservation system;\n\n*\tInstallation of a new system for providing radio telecommunication services to the railway passengers;\n*\tExpansion and reconstruction of the School Avenue railway bridge at Maligawatta, Colombo;\n\n*\tConstruction of the Colombo Train Control Centre and the Railway  Operations Centre;\n\n*\tDevelopment of the training activities of the Sri Lanka - German Railway Technical Training Centre, including the new technology, systems and methodologies;\n\n*\tProviding a Machinery and Carriage Repair workshop for the Railway Mechanical Engineers' Department at Ratmalana;\n\n*\tEstablishment of 02 Housing Schemes for the resettlement of families living in the railway reservations.\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to implement the Colombo Suburban Railway Efficiency Improvement Project (CSREIP) which includes the above sub projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Purchasing of drugs required for the treatment of diabetic patients",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8816",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the supply of 1,350,000 vials of Biphasic Isophane Insulin injections, a medicine used for treating the diabetes patients, to M/s Novo Nordisk A/S, Denmark, for a sum of US$ 2.55 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Design, Construction and Financing of the Super Structure Work of the Housing Project at Kimbula Ela Watta, Madampitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8817",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract for Design, Construction and Financing of the Super Structure Work of the Housing Project at Kimbula Ela Watta, Madampitiya, which comprises of 472 low income category housing units, to M/s CML-MTD Construction (Pvt.) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.2,247 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Purchasing of a Multi Beam Echo Sounder to carry out Hydrographic Surveys for mapping out the ocean belt of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8818",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The drawing of Nautical Charts for Sri Lanka from the Colonial times up to date is done by the United Kingdom and since the Charts thus prepared are owned by them, they derive a colossal sum of money out of the sale of such charts. It is imperative that every ship which sails across the shipping route of Sri Lanka should use the printed and electronic nautical charts of the ocean belt of Sri Lanka and when considering the large number of commercial ships which sail across the shipping route of Sri Lanka, annually, the country can derive a huge income.\n\n\tAlthough, there are trained human resources available, the constraint for mapping out of the ocean belt of Sri Lanka is the non-availability of modern technological equipment with the Sri Lanka Navy Hydrographic Division. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the then Minister of  Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to purchase a Multi Beam Echo Sounder for the country's only institute available for designing of Nautical Charts established in the National Aquatic Resources Research Development Agency, with a view to mapping out the ocean belt of Sri Lanka with an updated network of hydrographic surveys and to call for international bids for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet, taking into consideration the concurrence given by  Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the present Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Implementation of 03 Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) Power Plants as Joint Venture Projects with the Governments of Japan, India and China and the Government of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8819",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "China, Japan and India have expressed their willingness to sponsor to establish 03 Liquefied Natural Gas (LNG) Power Plants in Sri Lanka on Government to Government basis. Taking into consideration the increase in demand for  Renewable Energy after the year 2021 and the recommendation of the National Economic Council, the proposal made by the Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to take future measures necessary for the construction of a 400 MW LNG power plant in the Hambantota area, with the collaboration of the Government of China, a 500 MW LNG power plant with the collaboration of the Government of Japan and a 500 MW LNG power plant with the collaboration of the Government of India, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Presentation in Parliament of the Annual Report of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka for the Year 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8820",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The Annual Report of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) is formulated in accordance with the provisions contained in the Monetary Law Act incorporating the information on the economic status of Sri Lanka, the status of the CBSL and the monetary policies and measures adopted by the Monetary Board within the year. \n\n\tAccording to the 2017 Annual Report of the Central Bank, even though the economic growth has reduced up to 3.1% in the year 2017 in the midst of adverse climatic conditions and the other effects caused in that regard, the unemployment ratio has further declined up to 4.2%. Sri Lanka has succeeded in reporting a surplus in the overall Balance of Payments (BoP) amounting to US$ 2.1 billion in the year 2017 and the Gross Official Foreign Reserves have increased up to US$ 8 billion. The increase of the Tax revenue of the Government as a percentage of the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) is a considerable victory. By the year 2017, the per capita income of the country has reached US$ 4,065. The Annual Report of the CBSL for the year 2017 has pointed out the importance of formulating policies aiming at the progress of the general public and the sustainable implementation of the reforms with a long term vision, in achieving the economic and development challenges of the country. As such, Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media submitted the Report to the Cabinet and the same was approved by the Cabinet for its presentation in Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Public Sector Efficiency Project (PSEP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8821",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The European Union (EU) has agreed to provide a grant of Euro 10 million, to strengthen the Government Institutions functioning in respect of the Public Finance Management and its capacity building and approval of the Cabinet has been granted to pursue future action with regard to obtaining those funds. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to enter into the relevant Grant Agreement and to authorize the Secretary, Ministry of Finance and Mass Media to sign the same on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Construction of the Old Kelaniya Railway Bridge",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8822",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The Government has identified the need for developing the railway infrastructure facilities in keeping with the increasing number of passengers traveling by train and the need for increasing the speed of the trains.  As such, the Government has launched a project to reconstruct the Old Kelaniya Railway Bridge, constructed in the year 1881, to suit the present trends. It has been estimated that Euro 9 million will have to be incurred for the project. The UniCredit Bank of Austria AG has expressed its willingness to grant an interest free loan to cover the entire cost of the project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct loan negotiations with the UniCredit Bank of Austria AG to obtain the said credit facility and to enter into the relevant loan agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Release of Lands in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8823",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "Private and Government lands in extent of 4,992.84 acres in the Northern and Eastern Provinces used by the three forces during the conflict situation and which are not further needed, have already been released to their original owners with the consent of the Ministry of Defence.  The Sri Lanka Army has agreed to further release 522 acres of private lands in the Northern and Eastern Provinces to resettle the displaced community presently living in the welfare centres or in the residences of their friends and relatives, amidst much difficulties. \n\nAccordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, and Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to allocate the funds of a sum of of Rs. 866.71 million, required for the purpose of relocating the army camps presently existing in the private lands when releasing such private lands, to the Sri Lanka Army, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-09-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-05-09",
    "description": "Appointment of an Expert Committee on the Impact of the use of Glyphosate",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8824",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-09",
    "decision_details_body": "The Cabinet appointed an Officials' Committee comprising of experts, to make a study to confine the use of Glyphosate only in respect of the Plantation Sector subject to restrictions, taking into consideration the adverse effects caused on the Plantation Sector of the country due to the decision taken by the Government to impose a prohibition on the use of Glyphosate as a pesticide.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to permit the use of Glyphosate only for tea and rubber cultivation for a period of 36 months, under strict control, subject to the establishment of a proper monitoring mechanism for over use and misuse of Glyphosate and prevention of leakage of Glyphosate to water sources, as recommended by the Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Supply of Firefighting Vehicles / Equipment for the Colombo Municipal Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8825",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Owing to the increase in population and the limited land space available building complexes with multi\u2011storyes are being constructed in the city of Colombo and its suburbs. In order to ensure the safety of these properties and the occupants of these buildings it has been proposed to supply fire fighting equipment and vehicles with the objective of increasing the capacity of the fire fighting unit of the Colombo Municipal Council. \n\n\tThe UniCredit Bank of Austria, A.G. has agreed to provide an interest free loan of Euro 10.5 million for securing the funds necessary for the purpose.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct negotiations to obtain the loan and enter into the loan Agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the supply of Medical Equipment required for the Medical Faculties of Rajarata and Eastern Universities and the Faculty of Allied Health Science of the University of Peradeniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8826",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The standard of the health care status of Sri Lanka is higher in comparison to the other countries of the region. The free education system and the free health services prevalent in Sri Lanka have greatly impacted towards this situation and the aim of the Government is to provide a higher quality free health and education. In this contest, a proposal has been made to provide the medical equipment required for the Medical Faculties of Rajarata and the Eastern Universities and the Faculty of Allide Health Science of the University of Peradeniya. The UniCredit Bank of Austria, A.G. has agreed to provide a loan of Euro 4.9 million to meet the expenditure required for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into the relevant loan agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Securing of Funds for the implementation of the Primary Health Care System Strengthening Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8827",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Owing to the high quality and the efficiency of the health care system, it has been possible for Sri Lanka, to achieve satisfactory standards in various health care indicators. However, a new trend has emerged in the increase of the number of deaths caused by non\u2011communicable diseases and as well as infectious diseases. The need also has arisen for the provision of health facilities for the gradual increase of the aging population.  Therefore, the strengthening of the primary Medical Care System in Sri Lanka has become an essential factor.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the Cabinet has already granted approval to implement a project for strengthening of the primary heath care system.  The International Bank for re-construction which is an institute affiliated to the World Bank has agreed to provide the US$ 200.0 million required for the purpose. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into a financial agreement with the World Bank to obtain the loan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Construction of 300 Low Cost Housing Units adjacent to the  the Madhu Church in Mannar",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8828",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Out of the Sacred places in Sri Lanka the Madhu Church is a destination held in high esteem and it is a place for worship and honour of local, foreign Catholic devotees and as well as other devotees. \n\t\tConsidering the inadequacy of the accommodation facilities available during the festive seasons,  a proposal has been made to construct 300 housing units for the use of the tourists and the devotees who visit the Madhu Church.  The Government of India has agreed to grant a financial sponsorship of Rs.300 million for the implementation of this housing project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Government of Sri Lanka and India to obtain the financial aid, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Establishment of the Amaradeva Aesthetic and Research Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8829",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval to establish an institute by the name of 'Amaradeva Aesthetic and Research Centre' by an Act of Parliament, to preserve the musical culture introduced by the late Dr. Pandith W.D. Amaradeva known as the legendary music icon of Sri Lanka for the future generations, treating same as national heritage in gratitude to him.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to publish the draft Bill of the Amaradeva Aesthetic and Research Centre prepared by the Legal Draftsman, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present it in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Appointment of new members to the Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism (AML/CFT) National Coordinating Committee (NCC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8830",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Financial Intelligence Unit  (FIU) in Sri Lanka was established in 2006 under the Ministry of Finance and with the introduction of the National Anti\u2011Money Laundering (AML) and Countering the Financing of Terrorism   Policy, it was renamed as the Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism National Coordinating Committee (NCC). \n \n\tWith the development of technology, the financial crimes becoming complex from day to day and the coordination with various Government institutions has become an essential factor in order to face them successfully. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to expand the composition of the National Coordinating Committee of the Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism, for the inclusion of the Commissioner General of Inland Revenue, the Commissioner General of the Department of Excise, Director General of Commission to Investigate Allegation of  Bribery or Corruption and the representatives of the   Ministry of Defence and the Ministry of National Policies and Economic Affairs, as well,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Granting of loans at a concessionary interest rate for the damaged business properties in the Kandy Administrative District as a result of the conflicts that occurred",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8831",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet on 2018\u201103\u201120 granted approval to grant loans at a concessionary interest rate to revive the damaged businesses as a result of the conflicts that occurred in the Kandy administrative district in the first week of March 2018 at a concessionary rate of 2% interest, subject to the relevant conditions and the stipulations of the 'Athwela Loan Scheme'. However, the maximum loan amount granted by the loan scheme is around Rs.500,000/-. When considering the extent of damages caused to the business places the maximum loan amount appears to be inadequate. \n\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Public Enterprise & Kandy City Development, to increase the maximum loan amount up to Rs.1 million granted under the 'Athwela Loan Scheme' at a concessionary rate of 2% interest for the business places so damaged, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Upgrading the Health facilities in the Estate Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8832",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are more than 220,000 families living in the Estate Sector of the country.  90% of the labour force in the Estate Sector constitute of women and the nutrition status of the children and the pregnant mothers living in those areas are at a low ebb when compared with the rest of the areas in the Island. As such, the necessity of giving priority to upgrade the health facilities in the Estate Sector has been identified. Presently, there are about 450 Estate Dispensaries under the estate management and a proposal has been made to enhance the health status of the estate sector by upgrading of the said Dispensaries.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to integrate the Estate Health Network with that of the Government to enable the people of the Estate Sector to obtain the health services conveniently in the manner the services as   provided by the Government to the people of the other Rural and Urban Areas and to vest all the Estate Health Institutes now implemented under the Estate Management with the Government in Phases, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "The National Survey for identification of Risk factors of the non-communicable diseases in stages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8833",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Survey STEPS is conducted for identifying the data in stages on risk factors that contribute to the non-communicable diseases with the objective of collecting the data necessary to determine the spread of non-communicable diseases and for the preparation of plans for deciding the prevalence and the prevention and control of the non\u2011communicable diseases. Since the year 2003, this National Survey is conducted once in every 05 years and preparations are underway to conduct it once again in the year 2018.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to conduct the National Survey STEPS Island-wide at an estimated cost of Rs.50 million, in the month of August in the year 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Project for the Implementation of an Emergency Air and Technical Rescue System for Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8834",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish an Emergency Air and Technical Rescue System for Sri Lanka which responds expeditiously to transport the affected persons by air to the closest hospital for treatment from the scene of the accident when a sudden accident occurs. According to the project proposal, presented by a non\u2011profit organization in Germany known as Bijorn Steiger Stiftung, it has been planned to provide the services of an emergency rescue system with 8 helicopters and 25 technical rescue vehicles during an emergency. The estimated cost of this project is Rs.190 million and the sum will be provided as a long term soft loan.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to appoint a Project Committee and a Negotiation Committee to make a feasibility study on the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and Korea for the development in the field of Navigation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8835",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to sign a MoU between the Ministry of Ports and Shipping of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries of the Republic of Korea with a view to exchanging  technological information between the two countries for the development of the field of navigation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Amendment to the Intellectual Property Act, No.36 of 2003 to introduce  exemptions in respect of Copy Right provisions by reproducing and distribution of published printed material to enable the visually impaired or otherwise print disabled people to use the print media",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8836",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Marrakesh Treaty administered by the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) has provided guidance to the member states to introduce a series of exceptions to relax the limits imposed on copy right provisions for facilitating access in regard to the reproduction and distribution of the published printed works to enable the persons with disability for using the printed material.\n\n\tThe Cabinet has granted approval in the year 2016 to amend the Intellectual Property Act, No.36 of 2003 prior to ratifying the Marrakesh Treaty incorporating a series of exemptions in regard to the existing copy right provisions. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to publish the draft (Amendment) Bill to the Intellectual Property Act,  No.36 of 2003 in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Use of the  'Soranawatta' Land at Horana for a middle class housing project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8837",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although, it was planned to use Soranawatta' Land at Horana to relocate the Welikada prison and the relevant institutions, the arrangements pertaining to the relocation process has been suspended due to the demands made by the local community and the political leaders of the area. As such, action is being taken to identify another plot of land suitable for the relocation of the prison. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to make use of the Soranawatta' Land at Horana to construct a housing project for the middle income earners and improve the related facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "The project for the construction of the Wind Power Plant in Mannar",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8838",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the present context, global focus has been diverted for alternate sources of electricity and the generation of electricity by using renewable energy has become a costly and environmentally uncongenial process. As a result, electricity generation with wind power and solar power is spreading globally. Being an Island in the Indian ocean and situated in a region where there is  wind blowing, there is ample wind power available in Sri Lanka for the generation of electricity.\n\n\tCabinet has granted approval for implementing large scale wind power plants   to develop them as Wind Power Parks and as a first step of the venture, the preliminary activities necessary have been taken, by now, for the construction of a 100MW wind park in the Mannar Island.  The funds required  for the purpose is due to be granted by the Asian Development Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to implement the construction of 100MW wind park in the Mannar Island along with the other infrastructure facilities necessary, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Amendment to the Sri Lanka Bhikku University Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8839",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Bhikku University, established with the objective of imparting the Buddhist monks with knowledge required for the furtherance of Buddhism, is presently carrying out a significant mission in the higher education sector in Sri Lanka.  A proposal has now been made to amend the Bhikku University Act, No.26 of 1996 incorporating provision to provide opportunities for the laymen as well to follow post graduate degree courses in view of the great keenness shown not only among the Bhikkus but also the laymen relating to the Buddhist education, also inclusive of several   amendments important in the current context,  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the then Minister of Higher Education and Highways to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft amending legislation for the purpose also taking into consideration the concurrence given by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the present Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Hosting of the 5th International Conference of the International Association of Theravada Buddhist Universities (IATBU)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8840",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Association of Theravada Buddhist Universities (IATBU) implemented globally for the enhancement of the Buddhist education, has become a global network that coordinates the higher educational institutions which provides the student community in understanding and following Buddhism documented in Pali Texts. Its 5th international conference has been scheduled to be held on the three days of 27th 28th and 29th of November 2018 centering Colombo and Anuradhapura. \n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to host this conference in Sri Lanka under the patronage of the Sri Lanka Buddhist and Pali University in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Bhiksu University, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Construction of an auditorium for the Sri Lanka Social Security Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8841",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Social Security Board is implemented with the objective of granting pensions and social security benefits to all state sector employees who are not entitled to pension rights. When the promotional activities of this institute are carried out, the need for an auditorium to conduct training of divisional officers, to hold seminars etc. has been felt. For this purpose, the Cabinet granted approval to provide the funds to upgrade the upper floor of the Head Office of the Sri Lanka Social Security Board as an auditorium."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Revision of the name of the National Institute of Social Development as the 'Sri Lanka School of Social Work'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8842",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Institute of Social Development is the only State Institute in Sri Lanka which provides education pertaining to social work. The institute which commenced in 1952 as the 'Institute of Social Work' has subsequently been named as the 'Sri Lanka School of Social Work'. Under Act No.41 of 1992 this institute has been established as a Higher Educational Institute by the name of National Institute of Social Development. Accordingly, the institute conducts higher educational courses pertaining to various subjects related to Social Work and also Counseling, Child Care, Elder Care, Community based Correction, Conflict Management, Leadership, Communication Skills and Project Management.\n\n\tThe proposal made by the experts who represent the Universities and most of those engaged in various professional fields pertaining to social work, is that when the programmes conducted by this institute is introduced to Government and Non-Governmental Institutes and also to the community at large, the name denoted by 'Sri Lanka School of Social Work' has a better professional recognition than the name of 'National Institute of Social Development'. Considering these facts, the Cabinet granted approval to change the name of  'National Institute of Social Development' and rename the institute as 'Sri Lanka School of Social Work'."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Alienation of lands vested in the Land Reform Commission to outsiders and institutions on Lease Basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8843",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of the Land Reform Act No.01 of 1992 the alienation of lands vested in the Land Reform Commission for commercial and agricultural purposes should be done with the approval of the subject Minister. However, it has been decided in the year 2011 that the approval of the Cabinet should be obtained for the purpose, in all instances except in exceptional situations.\n \n\tThe Cabinet decided that the Minister in-charge to whom the subject of Land Reform Commission is assigned may select the beneficiaries for the alienation of land up to a maximum of 05 acres, subject to a mechanism being used to select the suitable persons in a more transparent manner based on the recommendations of a Senior Officials' Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Providing sponsorship to 13 Government approved unaided private schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8844",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to urbanization and the increase in population there is a tremendous competition for admission of children to national and provincial schools in Sri Lanka and the need to resolve this social problem with Government mediation through expanding the educational opportunities, has been identified. It would enable to ensure a high quality standard of education by facilitating those Government approved private schools where the national syllabus is implemented under the supervision of the Ministry of Education, thereby providing a reliable alternative solution for the national issue for the parents when admitting a child  to a school. \n\n\tPresently, there are 80 Government approved private schools registered under the Ministry of Education and the Government provides all such schools with benefits such as school uniforms and text books free of charge.  Out of which the Government provides aid to 36 schools for the payment of teacher salaries. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to expand this sponsorship further and grant aid for 13 selected private schools which do not receive Government aid with ability to provide the children with qualitative and competitive education to be treated as Government sponsored schools based on the criteria of the Ministry of Education, was approved y the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Implementation of Development Programmes in the Mannar District concurrent to the  Meela'd-Un-Nabi Celebration - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8845",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mannar district has been selected to conduct the major celebrations of the   Meela'd\u2011Un\u2011Nabi - 2018 and its major event is scheduled to be conducted at the Muslim National School. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs, seeking the active co-operation and support of the Central Government, the Northern Provincial Council and the other institutions, in order to implement the development activities proposed to be carried out concurrent to the   Meela'd\u2011Un\u2011Nabi Celebration to develop the common amenities and the infrastructure facilities of the Muslim people who have been resettled in their places of origin after being displaced and living in welfare camps for a long period of time, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Granting of permission for the operation of Currency Exchange Counters in the Arrival Terminal of the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), at Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8846",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to avail the permission for maintaining the operation of Currency Exchange Counters in the Arrival Terminal beyond the Customs area at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), Katunayake, to the Commercial Bank of Ceylon PLC, Sampath Bank PLC, Thomas Cook Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd., Bank of Ceylon and the People's Bank, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Construction of Mulankavil Water Supply Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8847",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Mulankavil Water Supply Scheme, it is expected to provide safe drinking water to nearly ten thousands of people residing in Mulankavil area in the Kilinochchi District. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the above contract for the construction of the said water supply scheme, to the Joint Venture of M/s Ceylex Engineering (Pvt) Ltd., and Prathibha Industries Limited, for a sum of Rs.608.49 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Construction of the Hambantota 220/132kV Grid Substation and Augmentation of the existing  Hambantota Grid Substation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8848",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction of the Hambantota 220/132kV Grid Substation and augmentation of the existing  132/33 KV Hambantota Grid Substation, under the Green Power Development & Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme, to M/s Chint Electric Co., Ltd., for a sum of Rs,1866.49 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Awarding the contract for the construction of Wellamankara Fishery Harbour",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8849",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has been granted earlier to construct the Wellamankara Fishery Harbour with two breakwaters with 4 meters deep and 700 meters long to provide all service facilities for fishery boats of 40 to 60 feet in size engaged in the fishery industry. \n\n\tThe proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the then Minister of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Development, to award the contract for the construction of the said fishery harbour to M/s R R Construction (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.1,862.25 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), also taking into consideration the concurrence given by the present Hon. Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Construction of Pulathisi  Market Complex and Agro-Economic Centre at Kaduruwela, Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8850",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to construct a market complex consisting of 58 sales outlets in an area spread over 8 acres under the 'Pibidemu Polonnaruwa' National Programme by the year 2019 to provide facilities for the farmers in Polonnaruwa to sell their agricultural products and to provide facilities for the people of the area to buy such products. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to award the contract for the construction of this market complex with an agro- economic centre, food court, children's park, a vehicle park and other common amenities as well to the Central Engineering  Consultancy Bureau, for a sum of Rs.623.2 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Resolving the educational problems of the students of the Medical Faculty of the South Asian Institute of Technology and Medicine - SAITM",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8851",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet granted approval on 2018-03-06 to implement a methodology in accordance with the recommendations made by the Officials' Committee Chaired by the Secretary to the Ministry of Defence pertaining to the absorption of the students of the South Asian Institute of Technology and Medicine engaged in studying medicine to the Institute of General Sir John Kothalawala Defence University. Subsequently, discussions were held on 2018\u201105\u201109 presided over by H.E. the President and with the participation of the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs on 2018\u201105\u201110 in regard to the legal and practical problems arisen when implementing the approved methodology. \n\n\tThe joint proposals made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena in his capacity as the Minister of Defence; and Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legal provision with regard to the implementation of the following recommendations pertaining to the absorption of the medical students of the SAITM into the Faculty of Medicine of the Kothalawala Defence University, as decided at the said discussions, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tOut of the students who have registered with the SAITM institute from 15th September, 2009 up to 15th of May 2017 to the course of study in medicine only, the students who have fulfilled the basic qualifications to be admitted to the Medical Faculties in the State Universities to be absorbed into the Faculty of Medicine of the General Sir John Kothalawala Defence University. \n\n*\tGranting authority to the Board of Management of the said University to stipulate the requirements and conditions for the absorption of the said students to the General Sir John Kothalawa Defence University.\n\n*\tOut of the students absorbed into the General Sir John Kothalawa Defence University from the SAITM institute, the students who pass the relevant examination of the Sir John Kothalawa Defence University will be awarded the degree of the said University."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Purchasing of dates  required to be distributed amongst Islamic devotees during the Ramalan festival",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8852",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is a religious practice amongst Islamic devotees to consume dates at the breaking of the fast during the Ramalan festival. As such, it is usual for the Government of Saudi Arabia to provide the requirement of dates to the Government of Sri Lanka as a donation for the consumption of the Islamic devotees during this period. However, this year the Government of Saudi Arabia has not made any donation of dates to Sri Lanka but has received a stock of 03MT of dates from 03 private donors.\n\n\tTherefore, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, and Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs, to purchase the additional stock of 250 MT of dates from the Cooperative Wholesale Establishment (CWE) required to be distributed during the Ramalan festival amongst the Islamic devotees through the mosques specially centered around the Muslim families beset with financial difficulties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Scheme for providing the  Kerosene subsidy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8853",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet on 2018-05-09 approved the implementation of the 'Pricing Formula System' for the petroleum products and accordingly, instructions were given to the relevant institutions to design a proper scheme to grant a kerosene subsidy to the low income families with no access to electricity and the small scale fishery community using mechanized boats who will be affected due to the increase in fuel price. \n\n\tAs such, taking into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to take necessary action in keeping with the amount of increase in the price of kerosene to provide the subsidy for kerosene,  implemented up to now also in the future."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-15-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2018-05-15",
    "description": "Revision of bus fares in keeping with the increase in fuel prices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8854",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Requests have been made by the Bus Associations for the revision of bus fares in keeping with the fuel price increase effective from 2018-05-11. The Official Committee working on the revision of the bus fair policy considering the recommendations made by the National Transport Commission and also that bus fairs are revised in the month of July every year, has made its recommendations  as to the manner in which the bus fairs should be revised.\n\n\tAccordingly, the Cabinet granted approval to increase the bus fairs by 6.56% with the minimum charge being Rs.10/- effective from 2018\u201105\u201116."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Obtaining Membership of the International Coral Reef Initiative by Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8855",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka is unique out of the countries with tropical coral reefs which is an environmental system containing bio diversity. More than 193 species of hard corals are reported from the sea belt around Sri Lanka and it has been estimated that more than 900 species of shore fish diversity exist associated with those coral reefs. These coral reefs provide an economic contribution towards fisheries, tourism and ornamental fish industry while also providing an environmental contribution through the mitigation of sea erosion and acting as a buffer to protect the sea belt from surge water. As of now, there is an imminent danger of the destruction of coral reefs due to human activities as well as natural phenomena such as cyclones and Tsunami. \n\n\tBy obtaining the membership of the International Coral Reef Initiative (ICRI) acclaimed as an International Organization which functions with the objective of protecting the coral reef resource, focus is made to derive the further benefits of the international partnerships for the conservation of coral reefs.     Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to obtain the membership of the ICRI,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and Rwanda on Cooperation in the field of Defence and Security",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8856",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to enter into a MoU between Sri Lanka and  Rwanda with a view to encouraging, facilitating and promoting military cooperation and providing a structure for capacity building, cooperation in Defence  and  Security, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Obtaining private investment on Public Private Partnership(PPP) Basis for construction of the buildings for the Public Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has to spend a large sum of money from the annual budgetary allocations for the construction of Government buildings such as schools, universities, hospitals and offices and also consume time and funds to construct and maintain such buildings. As such, focus has been made to find the possibility of obtaining private sector investments for the construction of Government buildings to enable the Government funds to be utilized for other priority activities.  \n\n\tA proposal has been made to adopt the Public Private Partnership Model to construct the new Government buildings in the fields of education, higher education, skills development & vocational training and health.  According to this method, the private investor will construct a building for a Government institute and after a lapse of a period of 15 to 20 years, the Government will acquire the building.  During this period the maintenance of the building will be carried out under the Public Private Partnership basis and the Government will pay the guaranteed rental to the private investor.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to take action to call for proposals from private investors under the said system in relevance to the above fields to construct the buildings required by the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Increase of the subsidy provided by the Government for the 'Sisu Seriya', 'Gemi Seriya' and 'Nisi Seriya' Bus Passenger Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8858",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has introduced 'Sisu Seriya' and 'Gemi Seriya' projects  respectively, to provide bus passenger transport services to school students and the students of Universities, Technical Institutions and other similar Institutions on concessionary rates and also to provide bus services to the general public living by the non\u2011profitable rural routes. The 'Nisi Seriya' project is also implemented to ensure the reliability of the night final turn and the dawn first turn. \n\n\tIt is essential to further encourage the implementation of these bus passenger services and accordingly, considering the timely cost, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to increase the concessionary cost granted by the Government for these bus passenger services, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Establishment of Bonded Warehouse facilities for selected Industries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Budget proposals of 2018, a proposal has been made for granting of tax relief in the import of capital goods for pharmaceutical manufacturing industry, dairy production industry, solid waste management and renewable energy production enterprises and providing facilities in order to eliminate delays in Custom clearance.\n\n\tBy this, it is expected to develop said sectors by providing relief to the local investors who are engaged in the importation of capital goods for the establishment or expansion of the said industries. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to introduce  a method of bonded warehouse facilities to provide new investments to expand the industries of the pharmaceutical manufacturing, dairy production, solid waste management and renewable energy production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Conducting of the Co-operative Conference on Asian Press Councils in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8860",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Press Council takes action to conduct awareness workshops and seminars aimed at creating a positive media culture in the country, and to secure the press freedom as well as the rights of the public. In this context, it has been proposed to host the Asia Press Council Cooperative Conference in Sri Lanka, considering the benefits accrued such as the promotion of cooperation among Press Councils and the Media Councils in the countries of the South Asian Region, creating awareness of global trends and expanding the training opportunities for professional journalists and the trainee journalists.\n\n\tAccordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to host the proposed Asian Press Council Cooperative Conference in October 2018  in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Entering into a new Agreement in regard to providing access to the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) to observe the places of detention in the Country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8861",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) has been operating in Sri Lanka since the year 1989 and it conducts excellent relations at professional level with all relevant public institutions. According to a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signed with the then representation of the Ministry of Defence, an opportunity has been provided to the Committee to visit the persons detained in Sri Lanka Prisons and the places of detention. The Committee ensures that all detainees are treated humanly and brings to the awareness of the relevant authorities the matters where attention is needed. With the change of environment following the conclusion of the armed conflict, a proposal has been made by the Committee to enter into a new Agreement in regard to carrying out the observation activities and the visits of the Committee to the places of detention conducted in Sri Lanka. \n\n\tWhen the prison network of Sri Lanka is designed in accordance with the international standards, obtaining the wide international experiences the Red Cross Committee has gained and its expertise, is really important to Sri Lanka  in order to improve the status of the detention places of Sri Lanka and the manner in which the detainees are treated. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to sign the Agreement proposed for cooperation and humanitarian activities in between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka and the International Red Cross Committee to benefit the detainees deprived of their liberty, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and Australia on Recognition of Certificates issued to the Sailors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8862",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- For a Naval Officer with a Certificate of Competence to serve in a vessel registered under the flag of a foreign country, it is mandatory that he obtains  a Certificate of Recognition from the country in which the relevant vessel has been registered, in addition to the Certificate of Competency.  For the issuance of such certificates there should be a convention or Memorandum of Understanding entered into between the relevant states and Sri Lanka has already signed such agreements with 32 foreign countries.\n\n\tBy entering into such agreements, employment opportunities will be open to a large number of Sri Lankan Naval Officers with Certificate of Competency to serve in foreign vessels. The Government of Australia has expressed its willingness to enter into an agreement with the Government of Sri Lanka on the issuance of these certificates. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Samarasinghe, the Minister of Ports and Shipping, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding pertaining to the recognition of certificates of maritime proficiency, with the Government of  Australia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Introduction of a Fertilizer Subsidy Scheme starting with the 2018 Yala cultivation season for paddy farmers using organic farming methods",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8863",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the method of granting fertilizer subsidy to the farmers in the form of cash, implemented from the 2016 Yala Season onwards, there was the option of using the subsidy by the farmers for the purchase of chemical fertilizer or organic fertilizer for their cultivation. However, with the granting of chemical fertilizer again to the farmers on a subsidized price from 2018 Yala Season onwards, this programme is now being implemented and this had not provided any relief to the farmers who cultivate using organic fertilizer.  \n\nAs such, taking into consideration, the importance of encouraging organic cultivation,  the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture to identify the farmers who are engaged in the organic farming in each season and the actual extents of land to be cultivated at the Grama Niladhari Division level and credit the relevant financial subsidy in their bank accounts and make the necessary adjustments in each season based on the variations in the price of chemical fertilizer, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Five (5) programmes implemented under the  Presidential Task Forces to be integrated into the society through the 'Model Village' Housing Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8864",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Programme initiated for the construction of 2500 new model villages by the year 2020 through the National Housing Development Authority  by the Ministry of Housing and Construction has been implemented. By now, the work of 700 model villages has commenced and out of which 60 houses have already been constructed and handed over to the beneficiaries. It has been found that, by implementing the National Programme for Kidney Disease Prevention, National Programme for Environmental Conservation, National Programmes for Food Production and Drug Prevention National Programme as well as Let's Protect Children' national programme, at the model village level, it would be possible to achieve the desired objectives effectively. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to appoint a National Steering Committee, to coordinate the required resources and relevant institutions to implement the intended programmes through the Model Villages Programme, and report its progress to the Cabinet, once in every 06 months, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Traditional Brick and Mortar Type Permanent Housing Programme for conflict affected families in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8867",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has been granted to construct 50,000 Traditional Brick and Mortar Type Houses to the families affected during the conflict of Northern and Eastern Provinces.  For this purpose, proposals were called for from the contractors and out of such proposals, the proposals presented by the United Nations Human Settlements Programme (UN-Habitat), the United Nations Office for Project Services (UNOPS),  Habitat for Humanity Sri Lanka and the Sri Lanka Red Cross Society (SLRCS) led non\u2011profit oriented humanitarian organizations consortium with 3 options, has been recommended by the Negotiation Committee appointed by the Cabinet as being most advantageous. \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to take future action in accordance with the proposal made by the said consortium to construct 25,000 of the said type of houses in the Districts of Jaffna, Kilinochchi, Mannar, Mullaithivu, Trincomalee and Batticaloa under Phase 1 of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Construction of 40,000 permanent houses for the low income families resettled in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8868",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- When providing a permanent solution to the housing problems of the displaced and affected persons due to the conflict which existed in the Northern and Eastern Provinces of Sri Lanka, a large scale housing project has to be implemented with the intervention of the Government. The proposal made prior to this for the construction of 65,000 prefabricated houses for the purpose was not implemented due to the opposition of certain parties. The recommendation made by the National Building Research Organization (NBRO) for the construction of houses using the concrete panel technology, as an alternative has been acclaimed by the people and the Political Representatives of those areas.  \n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to construct 40,000 permanent houses of 650 sq.ft. for the low income families resettled in the Northern and Eastern areas using the concrete panel technology, within a period of two (02) years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "e Motoring Project of the Department of Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8869",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for designing an information technology solution for the e\u2011Motoring Project of the Department of Motor Traffic under Build, Operate and Transfer basis, to 'Face Technologies & Metropolitan Joint Venture', as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Implementation of the 'Suraksha' Health Care Insurance Scheme for School Children during the period 2018/2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8870",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- An insurance scheme has been implemented under the 'Suraksha' Health Care Insurance Scheme for all school children between the age of 05 - 19, in accordance with the Budget proposal 2017 and accordingly, a health care insurance certificate valued at Rs.200,000/- will be provided for every child. The Insurance Scheme will grant up to Rs.100,000/- for indoor patients treatments and Rs.10,000/- for outdoor patients treatments. The Insurance Scheme is presently  implemented by the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation and provisions have been allocated to implement the said Insurance Scheme during the year 2018/2019 as well.\nAccordingly, taking into consideration, a proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, pertaining to the selection of a suitable insurance institution, to take measures to call for proposals from Government Insurance Institutions and to select an Insurance Institution which will provide more benefits to the school children, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-22-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-05-22",
    "description": "Revision of bus fares in keeping with the increase in fuel prices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8871",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the demand made by the Bus Associations to revise the bus fares in keeping with the increase of fuel prices from 2018\u201105\u201111, the Cabinet granted approval at its meeting held on 2018\u201105\u201115 to increase the other bus fares by 6.56% while keeping the minimum fare of Rs.10/- static. However, the Bus Associations made representations to the effect that the increase of bus fare is inadequate and the Government has also agreed that certain value fluctuations in the price mechanism on which the annual bus fare revision is based should be amended to suit the present day values. \n\n\tConsidering these factors, the Deputy Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation     and the Deputy Minister of Finance and Mass Media had made discussions with the Bus Associations. According to the agreement reached at the discussion, and taking into consideration the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, the Cabinet granted approval to increase the minimum charge of Rs.10/- up to Rs.12/- and the other bus fares by 12.5% with effect from 2018\u201105\u201122, subject to the condition that no revision of bus fares will be made during the forthcoming period of two years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Emergency Pre-Hospital Care Ambulance Service in Sri Lanka '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' - Implementation of Phase II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8872",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- As of now, action is being taken to establish '1990 Suwaseriya' Pre-Hospital Care Ambulance Service by an Act of Parliament. Under its second Phase, it has been planned to expand the said ambulance service, presently being implemented in Western and Southern Provinces to the other Provinces in the Island as well. The Indian Government has expressed its willingness to grant a credit facility of US $15.02 million for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to bear the relevant tax expenditure to be incurred for the second Phase of the said ambulance service by his Ministry, until the '1990 Suwaseriya Foundation' is established, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Implementation of the Budget Proposal of 2018 on the Middle Income Housing Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8873",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with a proposal in the Budget of 2018, the Middle Income Housing Loan Scheme is implemented with the objective of supporting the first time home buyers to obtain a house from the Middle Income Housing Loan Scheme implemented by the National Housing Development Authority and the Urban Development Authority. It has been found that the demand for housing cannot be fulfilled expeditiously through the housing projects implemented by the Government, as a result of the non\u2011availability of adequate extents of lands and the time taken for the  completion of the construction activities.\n\nAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to expand this housing loan scheme to make enable the first time home byres of the middle income category to purchase houses from the private sector as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Programme was introduced to Sri Lanka in the year 2010, in order to provide opportunities to the public sector officials of the executive grade to undergo Master Degree programmes in prominent universities in Japan. By now, 135 officers have got the opportunity to follow studies under two frameworks in this programme. In response to a request made by the Government of Sri Lanka, the Government of Japan has expressed its willingness to continue this programme for the ensuing 4 years, uninterruptedly. Under this programme, it has been proposed to provide 15 scholarships for Post Graduate Degree courses each year and 02 Scholarships for the Doctorate degree for the next 4 years. \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs,  to sign an Agreement with the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) to obtain a grant of Japanese Yen 265 million, in order to implement the proposed Human Resources Development Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Providing relief to the Beach Seine (Madel) Fishers of Kalametiya who were adversely affected by the construction of the Kalametiya Fishery Harbour",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8875",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a result of the construction of Kalametiya Fishery Harbour and the Breakwater, the traditional beach seine fishing industry in the area was hampered and it has adversely affected  28  beach seine fishers and 644 of their dependents. It has been found that a significant loss of annual income has been sustained by the Madel owners. In this regard, a proposal has been made to provide 36ft multiday boats at a cost of Rs. 7.8 million, to the 28 Madel owners, separately instead of monitary compensation. Accordingly, considering the above factors, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to provide 36 ft.  multiday boats to each 28  Madel owners, separately and a 50% of the total cost to be borne by the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Amendment to the Customs Ordinance to facilitate the 'Single Window' implementation to improve Ease of Doing Business Index",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8876",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is essential to improve the efficiency and the simplicity of the trading process for the improvement of the Business Climate and the Investment Climate of the Economy of Sri Lanka and as such, it has been proposed to implement the pre\u2011arrival clearance and paperless customs process prior to the importing process. This will reduce the costs and time of the Traders during the clearance process and Ease of Doing Business Index will improve. \n\nTherefore, a proposal has been made to amend the Customs Ordinance by incorporating provisions to that effect. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft the proposed amendments to the Customs Ordinance to be included in the (Amendment) Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Management of waste within the Harbours in the Coastal Zone of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8877",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approximately, 30% of the total population of Sri Lanka lives associated with the sea coast where several major economic related activities including the fisheries industry and the tourism industry are carried out. As a result of the improper management of the waste generated, sea pollution in the zone has reached a high level and posed a severe threat to the public health.  Accordingly, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment and the then Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to set up a Waste Management Committee with the representation of all institutions engaged in waste management activities in the coastal zone and to provide a mechanism to take action strickly against the persons polluting the coastal zone, under the Dengue Prevention Act, the National Environmental Act and the Marine Environment Protection Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "National Programme for the expeditious grant of deeds to the General Public",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8878",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Government Policy of granting all citizens the ownership of land,  a National Programme for the distribution of 1 million Permits / Grants to the people residing in state lands has been initiated. The main programmes under the above have been conducted in the districts of Polonnaruwa, Moneragala, Galle and Anuradhapura.  It has been planned to conduct the main programmes relevant to the remaining 21 districts and 03 programmes in each district at divisional level within the period from May to December of 2018. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, to allocate additional Funds from the Treasury to the Land Commissioner General's Department for the implementation of this programme, in all districts and at divisional level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Establishment of the New Villages Development Authority for Plantation Region",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8879",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. U. Palani Digambaram, the Minister of  Hill Country New Villages, Infrastructure and Community Development, to publish the New Villages Development Authority Act, in respect of the Plantation Region, prepared incorporating provisions for the establishment of the New Villages Development Authority, in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Procurement for the Supply, Installation, Testing and Operation of Railway Level Crossing Protection",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8880",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract for supply, installation, testing and operation of 25 Double Line and 175 Single Line Level Crossing Protection Systems inclusive of the requirement of Training was awarded to a consortium consisting of M/s N\u2011Able (Pvt.) Ltd. and M/s Uni Consultancy Services of the University of Moratuwa. The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to extend  the duration of the project by a period of 12 months taking into consideration the various issues that have cropped up in the implementation of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Procurement of services of International Forensic Audit Firm/s for Forensic Audits/Investigations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8881",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Report furnished by the Commission of Inquiry appointed by His Excellency the President to investigate into the alleged irregularities said to have been committed in the issuance of the Central Bank Treasury Bonds, after its investigation, has recommended to conduct different Forensic Audits in respect of the matters specified thereto. A proposal has been made to obtain the services of an independent firm/s with a an exellent performance and expertise in the field and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to appoint a Consultancy Procurement Committee to select a suitable audit firm, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Productive utilization of the savings of  contingencies allocated for the Rural Bridges Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8882",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to construct 35 rural bridges at the same rates indicated in the original contract agreements by utilizing the savings of contingencies allocated for construction of bridges in the rural areas and construction of temporary bridges with a length of 36 meters for each Province. However,  it has been proposed at the National Steering Committee Meeting, that it would be more appropriate to construct 15 additional bridges in the most essential flood affected locations instead of 09 temporary bridges at provincial level as previously proposed.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils, Local Government and Sports, to construct 15 steel bridges in the most essential flood affected locations, instead of constructing 09 temporary bridges at provincial level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Training of Unemployed Graduates on Staggered Basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8883",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the need to provide employment for unemployed Graduates, measures will be taken to call for all unemployed graduates under 45 years of age who have submitted their applicaions, for an interview. It has been planned to recruit  5,000 graduates in July 2018 and 15,000 in September 2018 for training. During the training period, they will be provided with a monthly allowance of Rs.20,000/-. It has also been planned to train the rest of the graduates in the year 2019 on staggered basis.\n\t\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to implement the programme for training of unemployed graduates and recruit the graduates who will fulfill the qualifications in terms of the Service Minute of the Development Officers, to fill the vacancies of the post of Development Officer, out of those who complete the training, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Hosting of the 18th International Conference of the Parties to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Fauna and Flora - (CITES)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8884",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to host the 18th International Conference of the Parties to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Fauna and Flora (CITES) from 22nd May to 03rd June 2019 in Sri Lanka. Even though, the responsibility of organizing this conference was vested with the then Ministry of Sustainable Development and Wildlife, it has since been entrusted to the Ministry of Buddhasasana by the Gazette Notification No.2064/26 dated 2018\u201103\u201128.  \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to sign the Memorandum of Understanding on hosting of the conference in Sri Lanka, to be entered into with the CITES Secretariat, on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Emergency Measures necessary for the control of the influenza epidemic spreading in the  Southern Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8885",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "Nearly 2,000 patients of suspected influenza have been admitted to the hospitals of the Southern Province within the past 02 months and it has been reported that 11 patients have died during the period. The Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine has taken numerous measures for the control of the disease, including provision of emergency treatment services and setting up of places for segregating patients. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mohomed Casim Mohomed Faizal, the Acting Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to provide the additional medical equipment, other equipment and facilities without delay, to be supplied to the relevant hospitals expeditiously, for further strengthening the measures taken up for the prevention of  spreading the disease within the Province and the adjacent areas, in accordance with the instructions of H.E. the President, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-05-30-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-05-30",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer to be distributed under the Fertilizer Subsidy of the Government - 2018 June",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8886",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "Chemical Fertilizer is imported by the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd. and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizers Ltd., to be supplied to the farmers. With a view to distributing the required fertilizer in the month of June 2018 under this programme, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, to purchase 6,000 MT of Muriate of Potash at US$ 311.74 per 01 MT from M/s Valency International Trading (Pvt.) Ltd. of Singapore, and 18,000 MT of Urea at US$ 280.90 per 01 MT from M/s Agri Commodities & Finance FZE of Abu Dhabi, as recommended by the Procurement Appeal Board (PAB), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the implementation of the  Primary Health Care System Strengthening Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8887",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- A consensus has been reached with the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) of the World Bank for securing funds in a sum of US$ 200 million required for the implementation of the Primary Health Care System Strengthening Project designed for strengthening the health care protection network of Sri Lanka, with special emphasis on the primary health care services. Accordingly, the Cabinet was informed by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to the effect that it has been agreed to implement this project within a period of 5 \u00bd years and settle this loan in 33 years with a grace period of 06 years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Expansion and improvement of Daycare facilities for children",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8888",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need for taking measures for the expansion and improvement of Daycare facilities for children having been drawn to the attention of the Cabinet, prior to this, by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, a Committee comprising of the representatives of the institutions of the relevant field, was appointed by the Cabinet, to make the necessary recommendations in that regard to the Cabinet.     \n\nAccordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, and Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to take the necessary steps to implement professional training programmes offering a relevant NVQ level for childcare givers with the consensus of  the relevant stakeholders, to encourage the youth to follow the child care courses through the provision of soft loan facilities under the Government loan schemes and to introduce a concessionary loan scheme up to a sum of Rs.02 million for the youth trained in the process, to establish daycare centres, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Promotion and Implementation of the 'Enterprise Sri Lanka' Interest Subsidy Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8889",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the budget proposals of 2017 and 2018, the 'Enterprise Sri Lanka' Interest Subsidy Loan Scheme is implemented by the Ministry of Finance and Mass Media in collaboration with the state and private banks, foreign financial cooperation institutes and the other participatory institutes. Through this programme it is expected to build a business paradise in Sri Lanka, using the innate entrepreneur expertise of the Sri Lankans. Under this programme consisting of 11 interest subsidy loan schemes, 3 refinancing loan schemes inclusive of 2 financial and non\u2011financial schemes, concessions are provided under 16 schemes. Accordingly, funds over Rs.30 billion have been provided by now to entrepreneurs of around 12,405 in number. The Government has set apart Rs.5,250 million for the year 2018 for the payment of interest subsidies alone in respect of the loan schemes, implemented under the programme and the Government expects the generation of 50,000 new employment opportunities, through the creation of a capital of nearly Rs.60,000 million. \n\t\n \tWith a view to popularizing the programme further among the general public, it is expected to implement it as a national level promotional programme, under the theme '2025 vision' along with the other development programmes of the Government once in every three (03) months covering all Provinces of the country in the hope of providing the necessary guidance to expand the products of the entrepreneurs up to the international level. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to establish a Secretariat in the Ministry of Finance and Mass Media to coordinate the activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Obtaining the Membership of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) by Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8890",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- This Multinational Forum was established in the year 1992 to enhance cooperation towards promoting peace, security and stability in the Asian region.  As of now, Sri Lanka is working as an observer country of this conference where 26 countries including India, China and Russia have obtained the membership. China which holds the current Chairmanship of the Conference has invited Sri Lanka to obtain the full pledged membership of the conference and thereby, Sri Lanka has got the opportunity to further develop interaction with all member states. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, for Sri Lanka to obtain the membership of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Provision of the State of the Art Medical Equipment",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8891",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, cancer has been identified as the second major cause of death in Sri Lanka owing to diseases. There is a tendency for patients with a sound financial position to seek treatment from centres in foreign countries due to the lack of advanced facilities of modern technology in Sri Lanka to control the disease. If there is a possibility of the early detection of the disease, its development in more than 1/3 of the patients could be prevented but around 70% of all cancer cases in the low and middle income countries are diagnosed after being too far gone and as a result, the deaths of cancer cases have increased. \n\t\n\tHaving taken the situation into consideration, it has been proposed to implement a project to procure and install a 3 Tesla MRI Scanner at the National Cancer Hospital, Maharagama for early detection and diagnosis of the disease  and a Gamma Knife Package and a PET/CT Scanner at the Teaching Hospital in Kandy. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to obtain a comprehensive proposal from Odelga Med G.m.b.H, Austria  and to conduct loan negotiations with the UniCredit Bank of Austria to secure the funds required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Introducing 'Health' as a Compulsory Subject for GCE (O/L) Examination",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8892",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the latest statistics available, around 75% of the deaths that occur in Sri Lanka annually are attributed to non-communicable diseases. Further, it has been revealed that 72.5% of the total population do not consume enough vegetables and fruits and that around 44% of the female population do not engage in sufficient physical exercises. In order to avert this situation and to lead a healthy lifestyle, a proper awareness on health is essential. Nevertheless,  health as a subject is taught in schools only from the year six and the year nine as a compulsory subject and it is not mandatory for the G.C.E. (O/L) examination.\n\t\nAccordingly, taking into consideration the proposals made by the Expertise Committee on Educational Reforms to the effect that the subject of 'Health and Physiology' should be taught in schools as a compulsory subject up to the G.C.E. (O/L) examination from the next revision of the school syllabi, to be made in the year 2023, the Cabinet granted approval to implement the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, after obtaining the recommendations of the National Education Commission which is the authority on policy decisions with regard to the revision of the school syllabi."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Presenting the progress of the Programme for Control of Weligama Coconut leaf Wilt and Rot Disease",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8893",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to prevent the damage caused to the coconut cultivation, as a result of the Weligama coconut leaf wilt and rot disease prevalent in the Southern Province, the approval of the Cabinet had been granted prior to this to continue to implement the Programme further from 2018 to 2020. Under this programme, steps are taken for the identification of sick trees, marking for removal, spreading awareness of the disease, supply of alternative economic crops and for the development of facilities for the generation of coconut varieties resistant to the disease and for the payment of Rs.3,000 per coconut tree removed, as compensation to land owners. In this context Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries informed the Cabinet that 832 infected coconut trees had been removed during the first quarter of the year 2018 and that a further 819 coconut trees have been identified for removal under this programme."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "The Development activities to be effected within the Central Cultural Fund (CCF) Project Office premises in Polonnaruwa, to coincide with the  ' Re awakening Polonnaruwa ' Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8894",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to develop the adjacent region of the sacred city of Polonnaruwa as a world heritage zone under the 'Re\u2011awakening Polonnaruwa' Project. As such, it has been planned to renovate the 19th Century building  where the project office of the Central Cultural Fund in Polonnaruwa is established, as a Heritage Management Centre, Archaeological Information Centre and a sales and Exhibition Centre for local foods and industrial products, to be attractive to both local and foreign tourists while preserving its cultural identity. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to construct a two storey market complex expeditiously, consisting of 22 small sales centres to replace the sales centres which have to be removed due to the development of the Colombo - Batticaloa main road running in front of the said building,  concurrent to the development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Implementation of Case Management Guidelines to prevent children from all Forms of Violence",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8895",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Over two decades have elapsed, since Sri Lanka had signed the convention on the 'Rights of the Child' and the Government has taken a large number of measures to ensure the protection and security of children.  While performing the activities pertaining to the protection of children from all forms of violence, it is imperative that the officers dealing with such activities carry out their services in accordance with the principles of child rights.  As such, guidelines to be adopted in such circumstances have been prepared under the name of  'Case Management Guidelines to Prevent Children from all Forms of Violence' by the Department of Probation and Child Care Services.\n\n\n\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women and Child Affairs, to implement these Guidelines as the National Guidelines when taking action with regard to children and to implement, direct and monitor such guidelines by the officers in charge at all administrative levels, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Sri Lanka's accession to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, Stockpiling, Production and Transfer  of Anti personnel Mines and on their Destruction: (APMBC) Ottawa Convention",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8896",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval for Sri Lanka to accede to the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, stockpiling, production and transfer of Antipersonnel Mines and on their Destruction: (APMBC) Ottawa Convention. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms,  to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft enabling legislation to give effect to the provisions of the APMBC, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Provision of a packet of milk to School Children",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8897",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The programme of providing a packet of milk to school children from Grade 1 to Grade 5 of the selected schools in the morning, covering the students in the special educational units as well, is implemented up to date, uninterruptedly from the year 2013. Under this programme, a packet of milk containing 150 ml produced by the Milco Private Limited and purchased by the Government for a market value of Rs.30/-is given over to school children. Through this programme, it is anticipated to create a viable student generation minimizing the nutritional problems of school children. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to continue to conduct this programme further, even under the presently higher market price of a packet of milk, treating the importance of conducting the programme uninterruptedly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Centre of e Content Development for Computer Assisted Teaching",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8898",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- A project proposal has been prepared by the Ministry of education to formalize  information technology education and the use of information technology for education in Sri Lankan schools and action will be taken to provide computers and accessories to all provincial Information Technology Resource Centres and to establish two communication technology information centres each at the Nilwala National College of Education premises and the Addalachchenai National College of Education premises and also to establish a National e\u2011Content Development Centre at the Narangala Estate premises in Kuliyapitiya.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to secure funds amounting to US$ 56.9 million through the Korean EXIM Bank from the Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF) and the Abu Dhabi Fund, for the implementation of this project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Preparation of a Master Plan for the Hambantota District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8899",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to set up a Special Economic Zone in Hambantota, in collaboration with the Government of China and for this purpose, China Harbour Engineering Corporation has been nominated by the Government of China. Under this, the construction of Sri Lanka - China Logistics and the Industrial Zone in Monaragala and Hambantota Districts are scheduled to be carried out under 03 stages. It has been decided that it would be appropriate to prepare a Master Plan for the Hambantota District, in order to ensure that a well planned urban development is carried out in the area concurrent to the development activities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Youth Affairs, Project Management and Southern Development, to establish a consultancy service institute for the purpose and to set up a Project Management Unit for the coordination of the said project and also to provide the required facilities for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the areas of Digitalization between Sri Lanka and Finland",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8900",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication, Digital Infrastructure and Foreign Employment, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the fields of Digitalization so as to cover the areas of  Cyber Security, E-Government, Digital Services and Critical Online Communication Methods, between Sri Lanka and  Finland during the official visit of the Deputy Minister of Economic Affairs and Employment of Finland, to Sri Lanka from 10th to 13th June 2018, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Introduction of a new Act to make the Sri Lankan labour force the shareholders of the economy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8901",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Labour, from its inception up to now has enforced 61 Acts related to the Service Conditions, Social Protection and Occupational Hygiene and Safety of Workers and out of them only 27 Acts are being practically implemented, at present. As several discrepancies seem to have been found between certain service conditions in these Acts, it has been proposed to make a single Act pertaining to the conditions of employment without prejudice to the existing labour rights, with a view to averting the discrepancies encountered when implementing them. By this Act, it is expected to introduce flexible service conditions to get the inactive labour population in Sri Lanka to  contribute to the economic development. \n\t\n       \tAccordingly, the  the proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, to introduce a new Act in respect of employment replacing the Wages Boards Ordinance, Shop and Office Employees Act, the Employment of Women, Young Persons and Children Act and the Maternity Benefits Ordinance, without any prejudice to the labour rights enforced by the labour laws already imposed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Procuring of 500 New Buses for the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8902",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although 7,257 buses are required according to the transportation time table of the Sri Lanka Transport Board, to fulfill the passenger requirements, only 6,000 buses have been operated in service due to the shortage of buses. 1,560 buses of the fleet of  buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board are more than 15 years old, and since they constantly succumb to technical failures, the Board has not been able to provide a dependable service to fulfill the passenger requirements. Annually about 500 buses have to be removed from the fleet due to expiry of the life span and accidents. Considering these issues, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to procure  400 New Buses with 50-54 High Back Seaters to be deployed  for  passenger services in urban routes and 100 New Buses with 32-35 Seaters to be used for the passenger services in the rural routes, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Purchasing of Surgical Rubber Gloves",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8903",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the supply of 31,041,000 locally manufactured Sterile Surgical Rubber Gloves made of rubber latex (in various sizes) for single use, powdered, in pairs, sterile packed in peel open package for surgeries, to M/s Sisili Project Consortium (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.1,199.9 million, in accordance with the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Purchasing of Medical Examination Gloves",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8904",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the supply of  79,430,000 locally manufactured unsterile Medical Examination Gloves made of Rubber latex (in various sizes), used in medical examinations, to M/s Sisili Project Consortium (Pvt.) Ltd., for a sum of Rs.448.3 million, in accordance with the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Implementation of the Beira Lake Intervention Area Development Plan and the Bank Protection",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8905",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Urban Development Authority has planned to develop the area surrounding the Beira Lake as a tourist attraction destination, preserving its natural beauty. Under this programme, the necessity of implementation of projects pertaining to the establishment of a Linear Park around the lake, development of the surrounding lands of the lake and the infrastructure facilities have been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to take necessary action to conserve the lake bank prior to commencing the said development activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Procurement of Container Carrier Wagons and Container Boxes to transport solid waste from Kelaniya to Aruwakkalu",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8906",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- he Cabinet has granted approval previously, to construct a Municipal Solid Waste Sanitary Landfill Disposal Facility at the Aruwakkalu area in Puttalam and the contract in that regard has already been awarded. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to commence the procurement procedure to procure  34 container carrier wagons and 94 container boxes to transport the solid waste collected in the selected municipal areas in Colombo up to Aruwakkalu area, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-05-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-06-05",
    "description": "Construction of buildings for the use of the Ceylon Electricity Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8907",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct eight housing complexes and a dormitory comprising of 24 rooms, available with all facilities for the Engineers in the Lakvijaya Power Plant in Puttalam. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction, to M/s George Steuart Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., in accordance with the recommendation of the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Establishment of the Office for Reparations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8908",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has been granted to draft legislation to establish an Office for Reparation to identify suitable persons for reparation and to carry out the reparation activities pertaining to the payment of compensation to those who were harmed due to getting caught in conflict situations, political unrest, civil commotion, forcible disappearance and various other causes, in a more formalized and a transparent manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to publish the draft Bill for the establishment of the  office for Reparations prepared by the Legal Draftsman in the Government Gazette and   subsequently, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Amendment to the National Environmental Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8909",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Environmental Act, No.47 of 1980 provides the legal framework for the coordination of all sectors related to the environment of Sri Lanka, at national level and the Central Environmental Authority has been established as the fundamental institution for implementing the functions pertaining to the Act.  Even though, this Act has been amended in several instances to suit the timely needs, the necessity for amending the Act has been recognized in order to find solutions for the present environmental issues as well as those that may arise in future.  \n\t\n\tAccordingly, in order to face current and future issues successfully, especially with regard to water pollution caused by factories, urban waste related issues and issues caused by illegal constructions, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft necessary legislation to amend the National Environmental Act, No.47 of 1980, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the purchase of Railway Locomotives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8910",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet had been granted previously, to purchase 12 Railway Locomotives for the Sri Lanka Railways with the objective of improving the Upcountry Railway Line operations. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into an Agreement to secure a sum of US$ 48.67 million as funds necessary for the purpose, from  the Standard Chartered Bank with the collaboration of the Export Development Canada, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Issuance of title deeds to the re-settlers under the Awarakotuwa Relocation Project at Muthurajawela",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8911",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Muthurajawela Development Project which was implemented in the year 1994, the squatters who were residing in the marshy area of the land were relocated in a section of the said land subsequent to its development.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to issue title deeds for the families identified after a survey done with regard to granting of title deeds to the occupants of these lands, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Providing Samurdhi Subsidies to 150,000 low income families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8912",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, around 1.38 million people are provided with benefits under the Samurdhi Subsidy Programme. However, it has been reported that families who have been resettled in the Northern and Eastern areas and are not presently Samurdhi beneficiaries as well as a large number of low income families living in the other areas of the country, identified as deserving the Samurdhi benefit, do not receive the said subsidy.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Social Empowerment, to expand the Samurdhi subsidy facility for a further  150,000 low income families, with the recommendations of the relevant District Secretaries and Divisional Secretaries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Implementing the 'Sampath Piyasa' programme in the model villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8913",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Action is taken to ensure the entitlement of a land, a housing unit and a settlement to the low income or poverty stricken families who do not possess a plot of land to construct a house, by the model villages programme implemented under the National Housing Programme implemented by the Ministry of Housing and Construction. Accordingly, it has been possible for the beneficiaries of the 75 model villages vested with the community under this programme, to achieve considerable progress in the implementation of drug prevention, health promotion and home gardening programmes. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to establish a 'Sampath Piyasa' unit introduced by the Central Environmental Authority in every Model Village to make it possible for the disposal of non degradable waste collected in the villages in an environment friendly manner, with the support of the Presidential Task Force on Environmental Conservation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Payment of Special Compensation for the properties damaged due to the incidents that took place in the Beruwala, Aluthgama Areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8914",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Action has been taken by the Government to grant the maximum compensation payable under the existing regulations for the properties damaged due to the civil commotion that took place in the year 2014 in the Beruwala and Aluthgama areas in the Kalutara District. As such, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to allocate a sum of Rs.185.9 million to enable the further payments recommended by a Special Valuation Committee appointed by the District Secretary in order to compensate for the damages caused to furniture and other equipment that have not been covered so far, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Purchase of 160 Passenger Coaches",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8915",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the contract for the purchase of 160 Passenger Coaches, under the Indian Line of Credit, with the objective of further improving the passenger services provided by the Sri Lanka Railways, to M/s RITES Ltd., for a sum of US$ 82.63 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Establishment of the Cost Estimate Review Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8916",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- When contracts are awarded pertaining to infrastructure development projects by the Government, it has been found that most are awarded for a sum that exceeds the Engineer's Estimate and that during the implementation of the projects, frequent cost increases take place. Therefore, the introduction of a proper mechanism to rectify this situation and the guidance of procurement entities in the preparation of realistic cost estimates, have been recognized as a timely need.\n\t\n\tAs such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to establish a Cost Estimate Review Committee comprised of the relevant officers under the Ministry of National Policies and Economic Affairs to review the total cost estimates and contract price variations of the infrastructure development projects within the authority of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committees, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Deltota Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8917",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to make a request to M/s M-U-T GambH Austria for the issuance of project proposals for the implementation of the Deltota Water Supply Project which is a priority project included in the master plan of investment of the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Sale of Mineral Sands of Lanka Mineral Sands Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8918",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Lanka Mineral Sands Limited is a state venture implemented under the supervision of the Ministry of Industry and Commerce, which is mainly engaged in mining, separating and selling of Ilmenite, Rutile, Zircon and Hi-TI Ilmenite. The company has called for prices to sell 25,000 MT of Ilmenite and the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to sell the said stock of Ilmenite at US$ 145.25 per 01MT, to M/s Rescom Mineral Trading FZE established in Dubai in the United Arab Emirates as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Award of contract for the consultancy services for the implementation of the projects in the Uva Province under the Second Integrated Roads Investment Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8919",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "The Asian Development Bank has expressed its willingness to provide a sum of US$ 900 million as funds for the implementation of the Second Integrated Roads Investment Programme and the Cabinet has granted approval to implement the said programme in the Northern, Eastern, Uva and Western Provinces. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development, to award the contract for  consultancy services for the implementation of the projects in the Uva Province inclusive of the construction monitoring and contract management to the joint venture of M/s Pyunghwa Engineering Consultants Institute in Korea and M/s Consulting Engineers and Architects Associated (Pvt.) Company, for a sum of Rs.1,154.8 million, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Consultancy Procurement Committee (CACPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Improvement of the road sections from Bibile to Chenkalady and  Padiyathalawa to Tampitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8920",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "The Saudi Fund has provided loan facilities for the rehabilitation and  improvement of the road section from Bibile to Chenkalady, 86.75km in length. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development to award the following 02 contract packages under the project, to M/s Consulting Engineers & Contractors (Pvt.) Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet.\n\t\t\n*\tRehabilitation and Improvement of the Bibile to Padiyathalawa road section, 29 km in length, for a sum of Rs.2,389.07 million.\n\t\t\n*\tRehabilitation and Improvement of the Padiyathalawa to Tampitiya road section, 30 km in length, for a sum of Rs.2,295.63 million."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Appointment of a Task Force to direct, coordinate and monitor the development programmes in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8921",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "Subsequent to the cessation of the conflict which existed in the Northern and Eastern Provinces, several projects have been implemented for Socio Economic Development of the areas. However,  it is observed that the projects have not been sufficiently effective in raising the living standards of the people of the area. As such, the information furnished by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to the Cabinet to the effect that he has taken measures to appoint a Task Force to review, coordinate, operate and monitor the development programmes implemented in the Northern and Eastern Provinces by various Government Institutions, comprising of the Hon. Prime Minister, Provincial Governors, Chief Secretaries of Provinces, Officers of the Armed Forces and the Police in charge of Provinces and all relevant stakeholders under his Chairmanship, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Reduction of the Price of Kerosene",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8922",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "Previously, the Government had decided to increase up to a certain extent, the price of kerosene that had been provided at a relatively concessionary rate in comparison with the high prices in the world market. Accordingly, the proposals made by the Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs and the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to reduce the price per litre of kerosene increased up to Rs.101/- down to Rs.70/-, considering the requests made by the small scale mechanized fishing boat owners who use kerosene for their boats and the low income families who use kerosene for lighting, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-12-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-06-12",
    "description": "Annual Report of the Ministry of Finance - 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8923",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "In terms of the provisions of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.03 of 2003, the Minister of Finance is required to table a 'Final Budgetary Position Report' in Parliament, for information of the Parliament and the general public. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to table the Annual Report of the Ministry of Finance pertaining to the financial year 2017, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Draft Bill on 'Secured Transactions'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8924",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously, to repeal the Secured Transactions Act, No.49 of 2009 and to draft a new Bill to enable Small and Medium Entrepreneurs to leverage a large part of their assets as 'surety bonds' in obtaining credit for improving their enterprises. It has also been proposed to amend the Prescription Ordinance, Trust Receipts Ordinance, Mortgage Ordinance, Finance Leasing Act, No.56 of 2000, Inland Trust Receipts Act, No.14 of 1990, Companies Act, No.7 of 2007 and the Registration of Documents Ordinance, along with the proposed draft Bill. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to amend the said Acts and to table the Draft (Amendment) Bills in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Development of 06 Mini Milk Processing Centres in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8925",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to secure the funds necessary for the development of 30 milk collecting centres and 06 milk processing centres in the areas of Kaduwela, Attanagalla, Polonnaruwa, Batticaloa, Wariyapola and Wennappuwa with the expectation of enhancing the income level of dairy farmers through the increase of the capability of producing fresh milk in the rural areas, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Promotion of Domestic Air Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8926",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Expression of Interest calling of proposals by the National Agency for Public Private Partnership (NAPPP) for the operation of scheduled domestic air services according to a given time table, 05 institutes have submitted their proposals and the said proposals have been evaluated by a Committee comprising of the Director General of Civil Aviation, the Chairman of the National Agency for Public Private Partnership and the Executive Director of the Airport and Aviation (Sri Lanka). Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs and Hon. Ashoka Abeysinghe, the Acting Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to call for applications from the relevant air services institutes for issuing licenses for operational activities, subject to taking action in accordance with the recommendations of the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Bilateral Consultations between Sri Lanka and Thailand pertaining to Air Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8927",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Delegations representing Sri Lanka and Thailand Aeronautical Authorities held discussion with regard to the air services plans of the two countries at the Civil Air Services Conference held in December 2017 in Colombo. The 2 parties reached consensus with regard to the  air services agreement scheduled to be signed between the two countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ashoka Abeysinghe the acting Ministers of Transport and Civil Aviation,  to enter into force of this Agreement and to implement it effectively, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Granting of Ports and Airports Development Levy Tax Concessions on High tech Automated Machinery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8928",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Gazette Notification issued under the Ports and Airports Development Levy Act, No.18 of 2011 for granting a 75% tax concession in respect of the High tech Automated Machinery used for the production activities of the domestic production industry, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Report on Public Sector Cadre for the First Quarter of the Year 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8929",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the decision taken previously by the Cabinet, the changes taking place in the Public Sector cadre due to the recruitment, transfers, vacation of posts, dismissal, retirement, resignation and death of officers in all public institutions should be updated and maintained and such information has to be submitted to the Cabinet, for consideration. In accordance with the Note submitted by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, 9,851 personnel have been newly recruited to the public sector and 7,755 public officers have left office due to retirement, resignation, vacation of post, dismissal or death, during the first quarter of the year 2018. Besides, the Provincial Councils have employed 7,840 persons outside the approved cadre and the necessity for all public sector institutions to adhere to a national policy on salary has also been pinpointed. The above information submitted by the Note to the Cabinet was noted by the Cabinet and  the Cabinet also emphasized the fact that the Heads of the Institutions are held accountable for the recruitment of employees outside the approved cadre without specific approval."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Mixed Development Project for the Chalmers Granary Land at Pettah",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8930",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to develop the Chalmers Granary Land at Pettah as a Mixed Development Project. Although proposals had been called for the Project accordingly, investors have not submitted proposals even by the due date. Considering the deliberations had with the investors who showed interest in the project when proposals were called for the purpose, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to provide the opportunity of submitting alternative proposals for the payment of the land value when the Chalmers Granary Land at Pettah is used for Mixed Development Projects and  to introduce a process for the evaluation of such proposals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Amendment to the Sri Lanka National Freedom from Hunger Campaign Board Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8931",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to amend the title of the Act as National Food Promotion Board Act, with a view to updating the Sri Lanka National Freedom from Hunger Campaign Board Act, No.15 of 1973 to suit the current trends. In this respect, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, to draft a Bill incorporating the further amendments necessary to be made in the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman, in order to further strengthen the activities of the agricultural community and the institutions engaged in such activities, to publish same in the Government Gazette and subsequently, present the Bill in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Conducting the Workshops on 'Innovative Technologies for Increasing the Agricultural Water Productivity' and 'Smart Agriculture Extension Models' in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8932",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to conduct  two workshops on 'Innovative Technologies for Increasing Agricultural Water Productivity' and 'Smart Agriculture Extension Models' in Sri Lanka organized jointly by the Asian Productivity Organization and the Ministry of Agriculture with a view to enhancing the productivity in the industrial and agricultural fields of member states. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, to conduct a 5 day workshop commencing from 2018\u201107\u201123 to 2018\u201107\u201127 on 'Innovative Technologies for Increasing Agricultural Water Productivity' for encouraging towards healthy water resources management and a 5 day workshop commencing from 2018\u201109\u201117 to 2018\u201109\u201121 on 'Smart Agriculture Extensions' to make a study of the 'Smart Agriculture Extension Models and Methodologies' which are suited for member states, in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Increasing  the Production of Local Big Onions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8933",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though the big onion cultivation which is very popular among the farmers of the dry zone and had been spread over an area of 7,000 hectares by 2014, it has been reduced up to 2,000 hectares by 2017 due to the price changes that occurred in the market and the climatic conditions. However, the Government has focused its attention on matters such as the inability of marketing the big onion seeds of farmers, the prevention of the farmers refraining from the cultivation of big onion and safeguarding of the local seed producers. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, to purchase 5,000 kgs. of seeds from the seed stocks available with the local big onion seed producers and cultivate newly 1,000 hectares of lands during the Yala season of 2018, for the Government to purchase a further 2,000 kgs. of   big onion seeds and stock them for the seed requirement in the next season, to intervene in securing a price of Rs.70/- to Rs.80/- per kilograms to the local producers and to revise the import taxes accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Construction of Volley ball and Basket Ball play grounds in the National Police Academy at Katana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8934",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Police Academy at Katana has been established with a view to enhancing the knowledge, skills, attitudes and vocational skills of the police officers. Five training courses are conducted daily in this academy and around 300 trainees attend the courses and  out of them, a majority participate in  training being resident in the academy. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to construct 02 Volley Ball and Basket Ball play grounds to facilitate the said trainees to be engaged in sports, physical exercises and physical fitness activities in order to spend their leisure time productively, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Required amendments to the Establishments Code in accordance with the provisions of the Right to Information Act, No.12 of 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8935",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "Under the Right to Information Act, No.12 of 2016, providing of information in possession of the public institutions to the people is effective with effect from 03rd February 2017.  It has been identified that when the provisions of the Act is enforced by the public officers, certain provisions found hitherto pertaining to the provision of information to the public in the Establishments Code have to be revised.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to make the required amendments in Volume II of the Establishments Code, taking into consideration the views of the Public Service Commission, provided for by way of Circular instructions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Social Integration of the Gramashakthi Livelihood Development Programme through the Model Village Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8936",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The model villages programme implemented under the Ministry of Housing and Construction could be utilized for the social integration of the Gramashakthi Peoples' Movement carried out under the guidance of His Excellency the President through which the capability of the livelihood  development of the rural people could be gained by empowering them collectively. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to implement the Gramashakthi Peoples' Movement centred at the model villages, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Establishment of Educational Institutions for the Buddhist Dasa Sil Matha",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8937",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present there are approximately 4,000 Dasa Sil Matha residing in Sri Lanka and their educational activities are being carried out by several educational institutions which function at voluntary level without Government assistance. Presently, necessary measures are being taken to amend the Pirivena Education Act, No.64 of 1979, in order to provide the said institutions with the assistance and the sponsorship required thereto by the Government. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, Minister of Education, to register the institutions which provide education to Dasa Sil Matha as \u201cEducational Institutions for Buddhist Dasa Sil Matha\u201d and provide the said institutions with necessary facilities until the amendments are made to the above Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "National HAJ Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8938",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Around 7,000 - 1,0000 applications are made by the Muslim Devotees to the Department\tof Muslim Religious and Cultural Affairs per year to take part in the Hajj Pilgrimage. However, since the annual quota received by Sri Lanka to take part in the Hajj Pilgrimage is limited from 2,200 to 3,400, it is found to be an extremely difficult task to choose the pilgrims and tour operators.  Accordingly, a proposal has been made to draft an Act to regulate the activities related to the Hajj Pilgrimage. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. M.H.A Haleem, the Minister of  Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation for this purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "The Action Plan of the Spices and Allied Products Marketing Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8939",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Action Plan submitted by the Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, to develop the Spices and Allied Products by the Spices and Allied Products Marketing Board and to promote the services with a view to enhancing the quality, organic products, upgrading the technology and research studies for promoting them locally and internationally, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Amending the Institute of Personnel Management Sri Lanka Act, No.24 of 1976",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8940",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Institute of Personnel Management Sri Lanka representing 1,500 full time members professionally qualified in the field of Human Resources Management, was founded in 1959 and has been incorporated by the Institute of Personnel Management Sri Lanka Act, No.24 of 1976. The Cabinet has granted  approval previously to amend the Institute of Personnel Management Sri Lanka Act, substituting its name as the 'Charted Institute of Personal Management Sri Lanka'. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, to publish the Draft (Amendment) Bill prepared in that regard, in the Government Gazette and subsequently present it in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Establishment of a Cyclotron Plant in Sri Lanka to operate PET CT Scanners in Government Hospitals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8941",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Tests are carried out by the PET CT Scanners to reveal the functioning of the tissues and organs of the Human body and for such tests, a radioactive drug  known as FDG 18 is used. A Cyclotron Plant is required to manufacture this radioactive drug. The service of a PET CT Scanner is essential for the purpose of observing the cancer related growth, to assess the response and to provide accurate treatment of cancer patients. As of now, only one such PET CT Scanner is available in a Private Hospital in Sri Lanka and about Rs.150,000/- is charged to obtain an examination report and an exorbitant sum has to be paid for the radioactive drug FDG 18 as well, used for the purpose. A PET CT Scanner has been commissioned at the National Hospital of Sri Lanka and another such scanner will also be commissioned at the Apeksha Cancer Hospital, Maharagama, in future.  The radioactive drug FDG 18 will be needed for those scanners as well in the future. If the PET CT Scanners  are to be used successfully and effectively in the country, it is absolutely essential to have a Cyclotron Plant in Sri Lanka.  As a remedial measure, M/s Access International (Pvt.) Ltd. has submitted a proposal to commission a Cyclotron Plant in Sri Lanka, subject to entering into a purchase agreement within a specific time period. Taking into consideration the importance of the proposal, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to appoint a Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee to evaluate the said project proposal and conduct negotiations in respect of same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Procurement of Locomotives to transport solid waste from Kelaniya to Aruwakkalu in Puttalam",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8942",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The management of the solid waste collected in the urban areas of Sri Lanka has become a major issue and as a solution to the problem, a project for constructing a sanitary landfill has been initiated in Aruwakkalu area in Puttalam for disposing of the urban solid waste. Under this project, waste has to be transported by trains from Kelaniya to Aruwakkalu for which it is necessary to procure 04 railway engines, 34 container carrier wagons and 94 container boxes. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to purchase 04 railway engines required for the purpose, from M/s Dongfang Electric International Corporation of China, for a sum of US$ 8.27 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy services for the  review of plans and supervision of constructions of the proposed Thalpitigala Reservoir Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8943",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement the Thalpitigala Reservoir Project to meet the water scarcity of the Bathmedilla Scheme in Uma Oya lower valley by the construction of the Uma Oya Multi\u2011Purpose Project. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to obtain the consultancy services for the  review of plans and supervision of constructions of the project from the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-19-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-06-19",
    "description": "Amendments to the relevant Tax Legislation for providing tax reliefs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8944",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-19",
    "decision_details_body": "Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to amend the Value Added Tax (VAT), Nation Building Tax (NBT) and the Economic Service Charges (ESC), for the maintenance of a stable Government Revenue. However, taking into consideration the requests made by various stakeholders, it has been found that it would be appropriate to remove certain taxes so imposed. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to amend the relevant legislation to remove the Value Added Tax (VAT) imposed on the Medical Consultation fees, channeling fees and the fees paid to the Medical Practitioners, to relieve the construction services provided under the construction agreements entered into before 01st August 2017 from the Nation Building Tax (NBT) and to release the unrealized foreign exchange benefits of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka from the Economic Service Charges (ESC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "Construction of a four storey building with state of the art facilities for the Administrative functions of the Kalutara Police College",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8945",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Police College in Kalutara which extends over an area of 209 acres provides facilities to train over a 1000 police officers, at a time, from the post of Police Constable to the rank of Assistant Superintendent of Police.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to construct a four storey building with state of the art facilities in place of the building presently used for the Administrative functions of the said training courses, with inadequate facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "National Evaluation Policy (NEP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8946",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government implements around 1,300 diverse development projects through out the country annually and out of such projects, about 1/3 could be considered as large scale projects implemented utilizing an expenditure exceeding Rs.500 million. In addition to these projects, a large number of small and medium scale development activities are also implemented in the country at provincial, district, divisional and local authority levels. However, due to the absence of a formal evaluation process on the outcome of those projects, it has been difficult to assess their productivity and analyze properly the impact caused by  them and their long term effect on the lives of the community. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Youth Affairs, Project Management and Southern Development, to implement the draft National Evaluation Policy prepared with the contribution of the relevant stakeholders and experts, as a remedial measure to overcome the situation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "The commencement of the preliminary construction work of the Cardiac and Critical Care Complex of the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for children",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8947",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval to the proposal made by the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine to carry out the project for the construction of the Cardiac and Critical Care Complex of the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for children as a Joint Venture with the coordination of the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine and the Ministry of Defence and to deploy the Sri Lanka Navy to undertake its construction work. In accordance with a proposal made by the Minister of Defence subsequently, approval of the Cabinet has been has been granted to carry out certain construction activities through external sources which cannot be handled by the Sri Lanka Navy.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to award the contract for the construction of the Pile Foundation of the Cardiac and Critical Care Complex of the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for children to M/s Nawaloka Piling (Pvt.) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.99.67 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "Construction of an Airport Hotel at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) in Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8948",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ashoka Abeysinghe, the Acting Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to award the procurement for the Establishment and Operation of an Airport Hotel in a land owned by the Airport and Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) Ltd. (AASL) at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), Katunayake to the consortium of M/s Thilanka Hotels (Pvt.) Ltd. and Striders Corporation, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "The procurement for the supply of Inflight Entertainment material and Guide 'Onboard' for Air Flight Passengers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8949",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Public Enterprise & Kandy City Development, to award the procurement for the Supply of Inflight Entertainment (IFE) Material and Inflight Entertainment Guide 'Onboard' in the SriLankan Airlines to M/s Inflight Dublin Ltd. for a period of three (03) years effective from 2018\u201110\u201101 for a sum of US$ 5.92 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "Wandurapeenu Ella Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8950",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In a study made by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, it has been revealed that the construction of the Wandurapeenu Ella Reservoir is the most suitable alternative for providing drinking water to the Kurunegala District as well as to make it a better storage for all of the water supply schemes carried out adjacent to the Daduru Oya Basin. M/s Tata Projects Ltd. of India has made an Expression of Intent to make a feasibility study in respect of the construction of the proposed reservoir. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between M/s Tata Projects Ltd. and the National Water Supply & Drainage Board to carry out the said feasibility study, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "Construction of a 1500cum capacity water tower and the Transmission and Distribution network in the Naiwala area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8951",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for the construction of a 1500cum capacity water tower in the Naiwala area under the Gampaha, Attanagalla, Minuwangoda Integrated Water Supply Project and laying of the required water pipes for transmission and distribution activities and the installation of other accessories, to the Joint Venture of M/s Ceylex Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd. and Prathiba Industries Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "Obtaining of consultancy services for the implementation of the  Northern Province Sustainable Fisheries Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8952",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The North and Eastern Regions cover around 2/3 of the coastal belt of Sri Lanka and the fisheries industry has been recognized as an industry which would contribute largely for the development of livelihoods of these areas. As such, the Asian Development Bank (ADB) has agreed to provide financial assistance in a sum of US$ 158 million, for improving the infrastructure facilities essential for the promotion of the fisheries industry in those areas inclusive of the entire infrastructure facilities required. Under this, it has been planned to construct two (02) fishery harbours in Point Pedro and Pesalai and an anchorage at Mandaitivu in Jaffna as well. It has been also identified to improve eight (08) fishery ferries in the Jaffna and Mannar Districts, six (06) fishery landing sites in the Mullaitvu District and three (03) fishery ferries in the Kilinochchi District.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, to take necessary action to select consultancy firms needed for the project implemented under three basic components namely, the construction and development of fishery harbours, anchorages and landing sites, and aquaculture and the livelihood development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-06-26-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-06-26",
    "description": "The Committee for updating the fuel oil prices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8953",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-06-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously, to introduce a price formula for fuel oils based on the cost and make it effective from 2018\u201105\u201111 and to update the fuel oil prices from the 5th day of the third month based on the international prices that prevailed in the preceding two months. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to establish an Officials' Committee comprising of the officials of the Treasury and the Ministry of Petroleum Resources Development to implement the price formula in a more transparent manner and to update the  price of Petrol and Diesel used in vehicles, on the 5th day after after every third month,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Project to Check the quality of internal water sources of the country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8954",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Excessive use of pesticides and chemicals in agricultural activities has resulted in the deterioration of the quality of water in the water sources which has adversely affected for the existence of humans and animal lives. Further, information has been received to confirm the speculation that the chronic kidney disease spread presently in certain provinces of the country, is attributed to the deterioration of the quality of water used for drinking purposes. As a solution, it has been found necessary to identify the causes of water pollution by testing the quality of water in the water sources, take measures to avoid that causes and also create awareness among the students and the public on the impact it causes. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the 'Folllow-up project to check the quality of internal water sources of the country' for a period of 02 years from 2019 to 2020 by the Central Environmental Authority, by incurring a sum of Rs.44.9 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Implementation of the 'Clean Air 2025 Action Plan'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8955",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has implemented several programmes to control the air pollution that existed in the atmosphere  of the Colombo metropolitan area and the suburbs, for a considerable period of  time. Under the guidance of the Air Resources Management Centre which was established to facilitate for the management of the quality of air, The 'Clean Air 2000 Action Plan' has been  implemented uninterruptedly, subject to appropriate amendments.\n\nThe 'Clean Air 2025 Action Plan' has been prepared with the objective of  managing the quality of air in Sri Lanka at a optimum level for the next few years. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the said plan and to appoint a Steering Committee to monitor and regulate the implementation of such plan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Women's wellbeing Survey - 2018/19",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8956",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Provisions pertaining to the safety and empowerment of women have been provided in the Constitution and in many other Acts. Accordingly, programmes pertaining to the empowerment of women are being implemented by the Government jointly  in collaboration with Non-Governmental Organizations.\n\nHowever,  due to the information pertaining to the lower percentage of women in the labour market in Sri Lanka, gender based violence and domestic violence against women, circulating in the society through unofficial statistics, the need for official statistics has surfaced to understand the real life situation of women. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct a National Level survey on the women's wellbeing by the Department of Census and Statistics, utilizing the donor facility of Rs.26.9 million, to be granted by the United Nations Population Fund(UNFPA) and to publish its report, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Securing Funds for the construction of the Central Expressway section from Pothuhera to Galagedara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8957",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to construct the Central Expressway by further expanding the existing Expressway network, in order to link Colombo and Kandy via Pothuhera. Through this, an uninterrupted connectivity will be created from down South of the Island to Kandy, linking the Port, Airport  and Commercial Cities and several provinces of economic importance. Arrangements have been made to construct phase 3 of the Central Expressway, the section from Pothuhera to Galagedara 32.5 km in length under the Japanese Banks financing. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into an Agreement with the MUFG Bank Ltd. of Japan to secure funds amounting to Japanese Yen 100 billion required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Obtaining Technical Assistance required for the Urban Development Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8958",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- By carrying out feasibility studies on Urban Development Projects and preparing detailed designs and strengthening the institutional capacity pertaining to performance and implementation of procurement activities for expediting the project activities, it is expected to strengthen the project preparedness through the proposed urban project preparatory facility. Under this, the start\u2011up efficiency of the projects for the development of 25 secondary towns implemented under the Ministry of Provincial Councils, Local Government and Sports and the projects for the development of 04 Strategic Cities implemented under the Ministry of Megapolis and Western Development, will be enhanced.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain the technical assistance loan of US$ 10 million from the Asian Development Bank for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Securing funds for the implementation of the Science and Technology Human Resource Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8959",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has decided to focus more on science and technology education to meet the evolving demands of the economy for human resource with knowledge on technology and innovation. For this purpose, the Government has planned to implement the Science and Technology Human Resource Development Project at a total investment of US$ 165 million.  Under this project, 03 technological faculties at the Universities of Kelaniya, Rajarata and Sabaragamuwa as well as an Engineering Faculty at the University of Sri Jayewardenapura will be established. Through this, it is expected to orient graduates with extensive knowledge on modern technology and interest on entrepreneurship and equipped skills to suit the present labour market. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to take appropriate action to obtain the foreign funds of US$ 145 million required for the implementation of the project, from the Asian Development Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Obtaining  funds required for the implementation  of Northern Province  Sustainable Fisheries Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8960",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement the Northern Province Sustainable Fisheries Development Project to promote investments and livelihood opportunities in the fisheries sector in the Northern Province and thereby sustainably increasing  the production in the Province. Under this project, it has been planned to construct two fishery harbours at Point Pedro and Pesalai; one anchorage at Mandative in Jaffna District; 23 landing sites in Jaffna, Mannar, Mullativu and Kilinochchi Districts. In addition, for the development of aquaculture, a sea cucumber hatchery, a mud crab hatchery and a sea weed tissue culture have been scheduled to be constructed in Mullativu, Mannar and Jaffna respectively. With a view to expanding this project among the local communities of the area and women, it is expected to develop the infrastructure facilities in selected 141 Grama Niladhari Divisions and provide access to credit for the re\u2011plantation of Kadolana, create awareness of credit facilities, establish three model enterprises in partnership with the private sector to generate employment opportunities and  provide the communities impacted due to the prolonged conflict with psycho\u2011social trauma support.\n\nA sum of US$ 201.02 million is scheduled to be invested by the Government with the assistance of foreign loans for this Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain the foreign loan of US$ 174 million from the Asian Development Bank required for the implementation of this project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Obtaining funds for the implementation of Port Access Elevated Highway Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8961",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Port Access Elevated Highway Project is proposed to link the Colombo - Katunayake Expressway to the Colombo Fort and the Port via the New Kelani Bridge. This project will help to minimize the traffic congestion prevailing around the port and the city and provide trade logistics as well. Under this project, it is scheduled to construct the 5.3 km Port Access Elevated Highway from New Kelani Bridge to Galle Face with a dedicated ramp to Colombo Port. Further, upgrading the existing port access road to six lanes and installing the electronic troll collection system have also been proposed. In addition, it has also been planned to relocate 49 places of the port affected due to these constructions and to establish a maritime facilitation center.\n\nThe total investment of US$ 360.2 million is expected to be made by the Government for this Project out of which US$ 300 million is to be obtained as a foreign loan from the Asian Development Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to obtain said loan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Project for promoting the right to information among the various communities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8962",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Right to Information Act, No.12 of 2016 is implemented to enable the public to access the information in possession of Public Authorities. The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement a project utilizing the funds donated by the Swiss Confederation, to promote the right to information guaranteed by the said Act specially among the people in the conflict and remote areas and the officers serving in the said areas,  to create awareness in the manner in exercising the  right to information and to further enhance the training provided for the officers in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Development of a framework and Infrastructure Financing to Support   Public - Private Partnerships",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8963",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Agency for Public-Private Partnership (NAPPP) has been established for the purpose of attracting foreign direct investments and accelerating economic growth through a robust Public-Private Partnership programmes. The said Agency has identified approximately 35 Public-Private Partnership projects for implementation.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement a programme with the funds from the Word Bank to support the Public-Private Partnership programmes in Sri Lanka and provide facilities required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Hosting the Water and Development Congress 2019 of the International Water Association(IWA) and the Exhibition on Sustainable Solution for Water Security in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8964",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to host the Water and Development Congress and  Exhibition organized every two years by the International Water Association, in Colombo in the year 2019. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply,  to host the proposed congress and exhibition in Sri Lanka in September, 2019 considering the benefits to be achieved for the professional development of those interested in this field, Water and Environmental professionals, engineers, chemists, regulators and policy makers, and the service to be provided, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Allocation blocks of Land from the Regional Industrial Estates to set up \tIndustries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8965",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tThe Regional Industrial Estates have been established with the objective of promoting the industries at regional level and the selection of investors anticipating to establish industries, will be performed by the Regional Industrial Services Committee and the Project Evaluation Committee of the Ministry. Accordingly, considering the direct employment opportunities to be generated with a total investments exceeding Rs.4 billion from such industries, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to allocate blocks of land from the Industrial estates located in areas of Puttlam, Noorani, Bata Atha, Nalanda, Nalanda Ellawala, Laksha Uyana, Raigampura and Millewa, for a lease period of 35 years, to the investors selected, as per the recommendations of those Committees, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Providing facilities to the private sector engaged in the field of agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8966",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has identified the necessity of obtaining the contribution of the private sector in order to improve the agriculture productivity and enhance the quality of such agricultural products. As such, the proposal  made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of Agriculture, to establish an Inter Ministerial Coordinating Committee to facilitate the private sector engaged in the field of agriculture to perform successfully in the global business environment as well as to provide agricultural products of high quality to consumers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Development of the infrastructure facilities in remote villages where Samurdhi beneficiaries are living",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8967",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though various programmes have been implemented by the Department of Samurdhi Development for the economic empowerment of the Samurdhi beneficiaries, it has been found that the expected result from these programmes could not be achieved due to inadequate accessibility facilities to bring their products to the market, limitations pertaining to the water supply facility required for cultivation activities, lack of places required for marketing the products and the absence of service centres to seek technical facilities and enhance the quality of products and the insufficient infrastructure facilities.\n\nAs a remedial measure, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Social Empowerment, to implement a special programme for improvement of such infrastructure facilities in rural villages situated in the Northern, Eastern and hilly areas as well as in the districts of Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Moneragala and Hambantota where the poverty exists at its highest level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Restructuring of the Department of Government Factory (DGF)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8968",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Government Factory (DGF) is a Department which possesses the competency in carrying out the mechanical, engineering work and installation activities with high quality required for the development activities and various Government Institutions for a longer period of time.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to appoint a committee to obtain recommendations to restructure the Department in order to further continue as an independent institution and grant approval for the mechanical, engineering work and installation activities required for the institutions of the Public Sector to be performed by the Department of Government Factory under direct contract method, until the proposed restructuring activities are completed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Cultivating Ayurvedic Medicinal Herbs at the model village level and selling to the Ayurvedic Drugs Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8969",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The model village housing programme which functions under the Ministry of Housing and Constructions addresses the housing problems of beneficiary families and empowers such beneficiaries in view of making them productive partners of the national economy. As such, for a model village comprising 25 housing units, a land extent of two acres in addition to the land allotted for the houses have been reserved for collective cultivation of beneficiaries. Similarly,  Cultivation of ayurvedic medical plants have been initiated in 77 model villages which have already been vested with the beneficiaries and ayurvedic medical plants are expected to be introduced for the proposed 2,500 model village as well. This programme will also minimize the import cost borne by importing ayurvedic drugs and enhance the income level of the beneficiaries. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to establish a Steering Committee for launching the programme of promoting the cultivation of ayurvedic medicinal herbs within the model villages, was approved by the  Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Ensuring the proper functioning of the rental housing market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8970",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- An Experts' Committee has been appointed to submit recommendations pertaining to the functioning of rental housing market at an optimum level considering the requirement of providing rental housing at a price affordable to those moving to the city due to the urbanization, employees and young families.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to draft necessary legislation to ensure the proper functioning of rental housing market taking into consideration the matters such as regulation of rental housing market, increase the provision of rental housing and designing such houses at a rate affordable to the women and elders as per the recommendation of said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Expediting the Digitalization of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8971",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Creating a 'Digital Sri Lanka' which leads the way towards a digital economy has been identified as a priority area in the policy and economic development plan. In this instance, providing the service receivers with broadband connections has been recognized as a vital aspect. Even though, Fibre-To-The Premises has been recognized as an important medium to increase broadband penetration in the areas of service receivers, a high cost have to be incurred in respect of same. However, the development of technology has enabled the broadband to share the same infrastructure with electrical power. Accordingly, mutually sharing the infrastructure by the electricity distribution licensees and the licensees of telecommunication service providers, enables to expand electricity and broadband connections at considerably lower cost with high standard technology. The Joint Proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication, Digital Infrastructure and Foreign Employment, and Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to appoint a Committee comprising of expertise in the field to examine all aspects relating to the subject  and submit proposals in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Preparing a National Policy for Primary Industries in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8972",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures have been taken to prepare a national policy for primary industries with the objective of the primary industry sector actively contributing in  achieving the government goal of enhancing the export earnings and strengthening livelihood of the people through the promotion of investments. Promotion of competitiveness and productivity in the primary industry sector, research and development, enhancement of entrepreneurial capacity, increase of global market share, entire economic growth through the market diversification and export promotion is expected to be covered by this policy. Accordingly, the National policy for primary industries was submitted by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, for information of the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding on Strategic Economic Partnership \tbetween Thailand and Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8973",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and Thailand covering the sectors such as investments, agricultural development, promoting and facilitating the fisheries industry, promoting the tourism industry and expanding and promoting information technology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-03-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-07-03",
    "description": "Developing the Gem Street Demuwawatha, Ratnapura as an International Gem Street and Constructing the Gem Tower",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8974",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approval has been granted previously to develop the Gem Street Demuwawatha, Ratnapura as an International Gem Street and to construct a Gem Tower with the objective of constructing a specific centre for  providing all the required services efficiently for the gem and jewelry sector under one roof within the Ratnapura city and to attract buyers for medium scale entrepreneurs. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to construct a four storied building at a land in extent of 22 perches located at Limewatta, Demuwawatha Street, Ratnapura and to establish business places, gem laboratory and banking, export and customs facilities therein, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
