    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and \tFinland for cooperation in the field of Health",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8988",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Social Activities and Health of the Republic of Finland for enhancing the cooperation between the two countries on the matters pertaining to the Health Sector for adopting Digital Technology, Dental Care, development of Medical Equipment and Hospital Infrastructure facilities, Genomics, Blood Plasma Fractionation, Diagnostics, Medical and Health Care Education and Non\u2011Communicable Diseases, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Amendments to the National Institute of Plantation Management Act, No.45 of 1979",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8989",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to amend the National Institute of Plantation Management Act, No.45 of 1979, so as to transform the National Institute of Plantation Management as an institution which creates professionals with high competency required in the field of plantation and awards skills oriented plantation management degrees, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Introduction of a Fixed Rate of CESS on Bulk Tea Exports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8990",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- CESS calculation on Bulk Tea is being carried out at present and accordingly, the said calculation is computed on a monthly basis, at the rate of Rs.10/- per kg or 2.5% of the Colombo Tea Auction average prices which ever is higher. Presently, CESS paid by the Tea exporters is approximately 20% per kg. of tea and accordingly, the tea exporters have encountered several difficulties such as the difficulty in finalizing the bulk tea prices in advance as the CESS rates is computed on monthly basis and delay in submitting export prices. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to introduce a fixed CESS rate of Rs.10/- per kg for bulk tea exports, as a remedial measure for the issue, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Reserving of lands to Establish the Natural Gas Power Plant at  Kerawalapitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8991",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that, establishment of Power Plants that utilize Natural Gas as the fuel, is more appropriate to meet the increasing demand of electricity in Sri Lanka. Accordingly, approval of the Cabinet has been received to establish two Natural Gas Power Plants of each 500 MW, as a joint venture project between India and Japan.  Kerawalapitiya area has been identified as the most suitable area to construct the Natural Gas Power Plants considering the facts such as the close proximity to the Colombo City and Suburban areas, appropriate location to build to receive the important natural gas terminal, availability of cooling water as well as the availability of the open lands to build power plants. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to vest a state land in extent of 110 acres situated at Kerawalapitiya to the Ceylon Electricity Board subsequent to a proper environmental assessment, for the construction of the proposed Natural Power Plant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Obtaining of Technical Consultancy Services for the successful implementation of the Empowerment of Programmes for the Samurdhi Beneficiaries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8992",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- An Entrepreneurs Motivation Programme named ''One Country One Product'', ''OTOT- One Tambon One Product'' for selling high standard local products within the country is conducted in Thailand very successfully. As such, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Social Empowerment, to enter into an agreement between the Thailand International Cooperation Agency, in the Ministry of Affairs of the Kingdom of Thailand and the Ministry of Social Empowerment of Sri Lanka for obtaining technical consultancy in the implementation of the empowerment programmes for the promotion of the economic viability of the Samurdhi beneficiaries through the said programme conducted in Thailand, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Obtaining the active contribution of the Tri Forces for Control of Drugs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8993",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Narcotic Bureau of the Sri Lanka Police and the Divisional Police perform a yeoman service to control the rapidly spreading drug menace within the country which has engulfed the elders as well as youth community with harmful effects  with the assistance of the Special Task Force of the Sri Lanka Police and the Tri\u2011 Forces as well where necessary.  It has been found that, obtaining of the active contribution of the Tri\u2011Forces would be appropriate to control the drug menace more successfully. It has been found that, the control of drug trafficking could be made more effective by vesting the officers who engage in drug control operations with more powers. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, and Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to draft the Drugs Control (Special Provisions) Bill, vesting certain powers recommended by the Attorney General with the Tri\u2011Forces for a determined period of time to control drugs menace more successfully, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Programme for the construction of new houses for the displaced families in the Welioya  Area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8994",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to implement a special project to address the housing problem of 1,000 displaced families who lived in the villages of Helambawewa, Mayawewa, Sapumaltenna, Gajabapura, Hansawila and Namalpura in the Welioya Divisional Secretary's Division. Under this programme, construction work of 1,084 houses was initiated and out of them 994 housing units have now been completed. The construction work of the balance 90 houses is being completed.  Another 256 families who lived in the area and left due to the conflict situation, having returned to the area, are living in temporarily built houses with in adequate facilities. Having also considered the request made by such families to assist in the construction of houses for them also under the said housing project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to construct houses for them as well under the said project, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Facilitating newly constituted Local Authorities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8995",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Revising the limits, 10 new Local Authorities have been constituted as the previous Ambagamuwa Pradeshiya Sabha Authority Area as Ambagamuwa, Maskeliya and Norwood Pradeshiya Sabhas, the Nuwara Eliya Pradeshiya Sabha Authority Area as Nuwara Weediya, Kotapola, Agarapathana Pradeshiya Sabha, the Thamankaduwa Pradeshiya Sabha Authority Area as two   Pollonnaruwa Municiple Council and Pradeshiya Sabha newly, Bandaragama Pradeshiya Sabha Authority Area as two Bandaragama and Millaniya Pradeshiya Sabha newly. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils, Local Government and Sports, to secure a sum of Rs.540 million to provide the new Local Authorities with the essential facilities with a view to providing Public Services expeditiously through the newly constituted Local Authorities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Development of the Deniyaya Weekly Fair",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8996",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Youth Affairs, Project Management and Southern Development, to improve and develop the  Deniyaya Weekly Fair which is present in a dilapidated condition as a trade complex with 80 to 120 shops inclusive of a new road net work around the  trade complex and proper sanitary facilities with a view to providing necessary facilities for daily commuters of 25,000 arriving in the Deniyaya town, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Establishment of an Elephant Retention Centre to retain the two elephants living in the Sinharaja Reserve",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8997",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The damage caused by the two elephants presently remaining in the Sinharaja World Heritage Reserve, to the lives and properties of the villagers living closer to the said reserve is gradually increasing. In this background, the attention of the Government has been focused to take expeditious measures to protect the two elephants and the lives and the properties of the villagers living closer to the Reserve. Accordingly, the proposal made by Field Marshal Hon. Sarath Fonseka, the Minister of Sustainable Development, Wildlife and Regional Development, to reserve and maintain an area of land in extent of 36 hectares situated in the Parugala area of the Dolekanda Grama Niladhary Division in Kalawana with environmental conditions suitable for the retention of the two elephants, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Purchasing of Gas Cylinders used by the Litro Gas Lanka Ltd., for the distribution of Gas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8998",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Lakshman Kiriella, the Minister of Public Enterprise & Kandy City Development to purchase 656,298 of LP Gas Cylinders (of different sizes) with safety valves used by the Litro Gas Lanka Ltd., for distribution purposes, from M/s Mauriya Udyog Ltd., in India for a sum of Rs.2,057.1 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Construction of the Stage II of the Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital in Jaffna",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=8999",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- As Stage II of the Construction of a five storey building for the Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital in Jaffna, the construction activities of the 2nd floor up to the 5th floor of the said building has been planned to be constructed. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the construction work of Stage II of the Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit at the Teaching Hospital in Jaffna to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and the Central Engineering Services Private Limited, for a sum of Rs.1,224.6 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Construction of a Ten Storey Building at the Provincial General Hospital in Badulla",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9000",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Provincial General Hospital in Badulla equipped with 1,493 beds and 41 wards, is the largest Health Service providing institution in the Uva Province. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to implement an Accident and Emergency Care Project, and to construct a Cardiac Catheterization Laboratory with Auxiliary Clinical Services at the Hospital. Accordingly, a proposal has been made to construct a new ten\u2011storey building in the hospital premises to establish surgical/medical ward facilities and cardiac treatment facilities as well as the proposed Accident and Emergency Care Unit. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the contract for the construction of the ten\u2011storey building to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB), with an investment of Rs.3,958.2 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Implementation of the Light Rail Transit Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9001",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The introduction of a Light Rail Transit System for the establishment of an effective and productive transport service within the Colombo Megapolis area is one of the major components in the Western Region Megapolis Master Plan.  Under this, it has been planned to construct 07 Light Railway Transit Lines and out of them, the line which links Colombo Fort area with other major cities and the line extended to the area of Battaramulla and Malabe have been identified as priority roads.\n\t\n\nDue to the high congestion in these areas, the Government of Sri Lanka has requested financial assistance from Japan to construct these lines as two elevated Light Railway Transit Lines. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to implement a Light Rail Transit Project with 16 stations and a Depot 17km in length, from Malabe to the Multi Model Transport Hub (MMTH) in Colombo Fort, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Construction of the Ambathale Water Pumping Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9002",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ambathale Water Pumping Station Project due to be implemented with a view to providing a qualitative water supply service, is a sub project identified under the Metro Colombo Region Development Project.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract for the Design and Building of the Ambathale Water Pumping Station to M/s SALCON ENGINEERING BERHAD of Malaysia for a sum of Rs.1,181.5 million (excluding tax), as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Supply of LED Lamps (Light Emitting Diode Lamps) for a concessionary price to  electricity consumers who consume less electricity",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9003",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the National Programme for the Demand Side Energy Management, it has been planned to distribute LED Lamps among the consumers who consume  less electricity on a concessionary basis with a view to encouraging the popular use of the efficient LED Lamps. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the tender for the supply of 10 consignments of 1 million LED Lamps for a sum of Rs.169.6 million per consignment to M/s Rang Dong Light Source & Vacuum Flask Company, in Vietnam, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Construction of  the Kokilai Bridge",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9004",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "Construction of a new bridge and approaches across Kokilai  Lagoon provides the people living in Trincomalee and its suburbs with an easy access to Jaffna and through which the distance of travel from Mullaitivu to Trincomalee will be reduced by around 80 km.  Accordingly, the Joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, and Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development, to award the Contract for the construction of Kokilai Bridge and approaches across Kokilai Lagoon on Mullaitivu - Kokilai - Pulmudai road, to Bilfinger MCE Slany s.r.o of Czech Republic for a sum of Euro 48.8 million as per the Cabinet decision made in 2014 in this regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Printing of School Textbooks to be distributed free of charge among the \tschool children for the year 2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9005",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to deliver the school textbooks scheduled to be distributed to the schools prior to 2018-11-04 free of charge to the school children for the year 2019.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to award the contract for the printing of 39.7 million copies of school text books  in 419 categories to 27 local printing institutions  for a sum of Rs.3,473.1 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-07-10-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-07-10",
    "description": "Supply of 120,000 Bottles of Human Albumin Solution - 50ml",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9006",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-07-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the procurement for the purchase of 120,000 bottles of  Human Albumin Solution BP/PH EUR, 20% in 50ml, a drug used for the treatment of kidney patients, to M/s Shire Singapore Pte. Ltd. for US$ 2.82 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC) and the Procurement Appeal Board (PAB), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
