    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to vest the block of land in extent of 49.80 perches with the Police Department, to set up the Police Station in Kottawa, which has been vested with the Urban Development Authority (UDA) by the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for the vehicles damaged due to the explosion at the Salawa Ammunition Storage",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9097",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The explosion which occurred in the Salawa Ammunition Storage at Kosgama has caused damages to many movable and immovable properties in the area and the Government has taken measures to pay  compensation due for houses, business places, and other various properties so damaged. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to pay  compensation for the vehicles damaged by the said explosion but which have not been provided with the due compensation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Providing new accommodation for the Department of Cultural Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9098",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that the Department of Cultural Affairs maintained at the Sethsiripaya Building at Battaramulla does not have adequate facilities to accommodate its staff of about 170 and the artistes and  other persons coming from various parts of the Island for the activities pertaining to the 12 institutions affiliated to the said Department. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to vest the building premises at Kappetipola Mawatha where the Department for Registration of Persons was then located, with the Department of Cultural Affairs to relocate the Department of Cultural Affairs at the said  premises, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "The Northern Province Sustainable Fisheries Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9099",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement the Northern Province Sustainable Fisheries Development Programme, which consists of 03 components such as construction and development of a fishery harbour, anchorages and landing sites, aquaculture development and livelihood development, with financial assistance of US$ 174 million to be provided by the Asian Development Bank within the period of 2018 - 2024. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, to allocate an equal amount of US$ 27.22 million as the Government contribution for this project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "The Draft Bill for the recovery of damages pertaining to the death of a person",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9100",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to publish the Bill to provide for the recovery of damages pertaining to the death of a person caused by a wrongful act, omission, negligence or default of another and for other matters connected thereto, prepared with the clearance of the Attorney General, in the Government Gazette and to submit the said Bill, thereafter, in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Providing  a pair of shoes for the school children",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9101",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A programme for providing gift vouchers to 648,151 students of the difficult, the most difficult and the isolated schools in the remote, the most remote and the isolated areas to buy shoes, was successfully conducted in the year 2017. It was found that these children were provided with an opportunity to purchase  a pair of shoes at their choice through this programme and it was a huge economic relief for their parents as well. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to continue to implement this programme for the year 2018 as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for the people and those whose properties were affected due to political victimization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9102",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The joint proposal made by the Ministers of Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara,  Public Administration & Management and Law & Order; Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, Justice & Prison Reforms; Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to secure the necessary provisions for the payment of compensation in accordance with the  recommendations made by a Committee formed for the payment of compensation for the persons who lost their lives, were injured and those whose properties were damaged due to various political reasons, and pay and settle such compensation in the year 2019 itself, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "National Occupational Safety Week 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9103",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the National Occupational Safety Week which falls from the 01st of October until the 06th of October various activities and awareness  programmes have been planned to be conducted island-wide by the public and private sector institutions. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, to hold the National Occupational Safety and Health  Seminar on the 02nd of October in Colombo and the National Occupational Safety and Health Award of Excellence at the National level, withing the said week was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Calling for bids for the operation of Currency Exchange Counters in the Departure Walkway at Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) in Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9104",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to call for bids from the financial institutions approved by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka to increase the currency exchange counters in the Departure Walkway at Bandaranaike International Airport up to 06 and to conduct such services uninterruptedly from the year 2019 for the convenience of the finance and foreign exchange activities of the tourists who use the Bandaranaike International Airport in Katunayake, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Commissioning of the Railway level crossing protection system",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9105",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- There are 1,337 Railway level crossings within Sri Lanka and out of those the protection system functions only in 520. In addition, action is being taken to install protection systems in another 400 level crossings. The Hungarian Government has agreed to provide financial assistance for the Supply, Installation and Commissioning of the balance 417 level crossings. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to call for proposals from M/s. Muszer Automatika Ltd. recommended by the Government of Hungaria for the implementation of this project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Ambathale Water Supply System Improvement and Energy Saving Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9106",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ambathale Water Supply System Improvement and Energy Saving Project has been identified to be implemented under the Greater Colombo Water & Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme with financial assistance by the Asian Development Bank (ADB). Through this project, it has been planned to carry out the renovation and re-establishment of the water pipe lines of the Ambathale Water Treatment Plant, installation of the machinery and to introduce an automated system for the water pumping process and to construct a tank of 8,000 m\u00b3 in capacity. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the contract for designing and building of the project to M/s Zongnan-SZSG JH JV, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Entering into term contracts to purchase Refined Petroleum Products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9107",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to maintaining the petroleum stocks at an optimal level, it was decided to enter into 02 term contracts for purchasing refined petroleum products within a period of ten (10) months from the 01st of September 2018 up to the 30th of June 2019. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Petroleum Resources Development, to award the procurement contracts for purchasing the petroleum products to M/s Gulf Petrochem FZC of the United Arab Emirates, as recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SSCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Securing the services of a suitable company for the maintenance and operational activities of the Mehewara Piyasa building",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9108",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The construction process of a 32 storey building named as the \u201cMehewara Piyasa\u201d for accommodating the Ministry of Labour and all other institutions functioning under its purview, under one roof with a view to rendering a more effective quality service to the clients, has now reached its final phase. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, for securing the services of a competent external institution for the maintenance activities of this building due to the scarcity of trained staff for the proper maintenance of a building of this nature, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Sultanate of Oman on Visa Exemption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9109",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of  Internal Affairs & Wayamba Development, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding on Visa Exemption for holders of diplomatic, Special, Service and Official Passports, between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Sultanate of Oman, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Promoting Sri Lanka as an attractive destination among the Tourists",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9110",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A digital advertising campaign has been designed to be implemented to promote Sri Lanka as an attractive destination among the tourists in the countries of United Kingdom, Germany and France. Accordingly, with a view to implementing the digital advertising campaign specific for each country under the government procurement procedure, the proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to award the procurement to the Digital Spring Limited of the United Kingdom for a sum of  US$ 703,480, to the Media Consulta International Holdings AG of Germany for a sum of US$ 697,770.92, and to the  Interface Tourism of France for a sum of US$ 706,460, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-14-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-08-14",
    "description": "Appointing a Special Commission to review the Salaries of the Public Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9111",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that, it is a timely need to take measures to settle the problems pertaining to the salaries of the entire public sector after having studied the existing salary structures, and taking into consideration the dire difficulties to be faced by the general public and the adverse effects caused to the economy due to various groups in the public sector resorting to trade union action from the recent times to enhance their salaries and payments.  In order to  find immediate solutions, to avert this situation, the Government has focused its attention to appoint a Special Commission comprising of experts with the knowledge and experience in each sector in the Public Service. In this context, the rectification of salary anomalies in the Railways has been identified as a subject matter of the Commission. Accordingly, the Cabinet agreed on the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to request H.E. the President to appoint a Special Commission to review the salary structures in addition to the functions of the  National Salaries and Cadres Commission."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Amendments to the Forest Conservation Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9112",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Focusing special attention on the bio-diversity, soil, water, cultural, religious, historical and aesthetic value, it has been found necessary to amend the Forest Conservation Ordinance presently in force for the achievement of the objectives of forest conservation for the betterment of the future generation, preserving the mineral resources in the forest reserves, further strengthening of the powers assigned to the Forest Conservation Officers, promoting the productivity of the forests and strengthening of the contribution provided by the forests for the welfare of the rural community. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to draft a Bill to amend the Forest Conservation Ordinance incorporating the relevant amendments so as to effectively and productively implement the Forest Conservation Legal Framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Climate Change Mitigation Action Support Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9113",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka is bound to contribute to the global effort for mitigating the emission of Greenhouse gases which has been the cause for climate changes with the ratification of the Paris Agreement by Sri Lanka in the year 2016 under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) for  mitigation of the emission of Greenhouse gases.  For this purpose, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to submit a series of extensive activities which may mitigate the emission of Greenhouse gases in the 05 major sectors namely  energy, transport, industry, waste and forests to be the local contribution. In order to achieve these goals so determined locally, it is required to identify the quantity of the Greenhouse gases emitted from each of the above sectors. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to obtain the Grants due to Sri Lanka in order to implement the relevant project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Imposing orders to stop land reclamation and destruction of wetlands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9114",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- An Officials' Committee has been previously appointed by the Cabinet for obtaining the recommendations necessary to impose a temporary prohibitory order to immediately stop land reclamation and destruction of wetlands in the Colombo Metropolitan Region and to take appropriate measures to declare wetlands as protected zones and the preservation of same.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the following recommendations made by the said Officials' Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. \ni\tto impose a prohibitory order preventing all types of land reclamation and constructions in the Colombo Metropolitan Region for any other purpose other than the constructions necessary to be done which are of  national importance and the constructions identified under the Transit Railway Line Network.\n\nii\tto direct the Director General of Wildlife to declare the wetlands, other than the areas recognized adjacent to Kimbulaela and Diyawanna oya in which the development activities have already been initiated, as protected areas."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Construction of a new Conference Hall for the Joint Services Language Training Institute at Kotmale",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9115",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to construct a new Conference Hall with the State of the Art facilities which could house around 150 trainees at one given time, in place of the old Conference Hall now being used with inadequate facilities at the Joint Services Language Training Institute at Kotmale, which provides training in various languages to the officers of the Tri Forces and the Police,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Establishment of a temperature controlled Warehouse at Dambulla to store Agricultural Produce",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9116",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to establish a Warehouse in close proximity to the  Economic Centre at Dambulla with a temperature controlled facility on an investment of Rs.475 million to enable the small and medium scale farmers engaged specially in the cultivation of fruits and vegetables to store their produce in a state of freshness for a long period.  Since the availability of a continuous market could be guaranteed for the crops harvested seasonally, a stable price could be maintained for such crops by minimizing the price fluctuations of the products.  The Government of India has agreed to grant Rs.300 million out of the said investment. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to secure the funds necessary for the establishment of a temperature controlled Warehouse at Dambulla and to formulate a mechanism for the management of same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Health System Enhancement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9117",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to implement a project with an investment of US$ 60 million for the enhancement of the primary healthcare, to strengthen healthcare and prevention, formulation of policies in that regard and capacity building in the Uva, Sabaragamuwa, Central and North Central Provinces.  It has also been further proposed to obtain a grant of US$12.5 million and a  concessionary loan of US$37.5 million from the Asian Development Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into the necessary agreements to secure the relevant funds, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Issuance of Sovereign Bonds",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9118",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka has been issuing International Sovereign Bonds since the year 2017 to finance the annual budget and the said Bonds issued up to the year 2018 have been United States denominated Dollars. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to appoint an Officials' Committee comprising of the relevant institutions, to study the possibility of gaining access to the International market with denominated Yen, Renminbi and Euro, for export diversification and attracting Foreign Direct Investments (FDI) within the current economic activities in anticipation of managing the budget financing at a low cost, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Implementation of an Inland Water Transport project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9119",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to maintain an Inland Water Transport across the canals from Battaramulla to Wellawatta, from Fort to Union Place via Beira Lake, from Mattakkuliya to Hanwella across Kelani river and other waterways, as a Public\u2011Private Partnership project. The Minister of Megapolis and Western Development informed the Cabinet that as an initial step before the commencement of the implementation of the said project under a Public\u2011Private Partnership model, to implement a pilot project from Fort to Union Place via Beira Laka for a period of two (02) years with the assistance of the Sri Lanka Navy and that arrangements have been made to purchase the required vessels and construct jetties, and those contents were noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Amending the name of the Institute of Post Harvest Technology (IPHT) as 'the National Institute of Post Harvest Management (NIPHM)'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9120",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Institute of Post Harvest Technology (IPHT) established in the year 2000, is an institution which carries out the post harvest technical research and development activities from the harvesting stage of the crops to the value addition leading to consumption. As such, with a view to performing the technical, research development and regulate activities on the post harvest of Sri Lanka more efficiently and effectively, the proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, to amend the name of the Institute as 'the National Institute of Post Harvest Management (NIPHM)', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Enhancing the productivity of rubber cultivation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9121",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that the productivity of rubber cultivation in Sri Lanka is comparatively lower when compared to the other Asian Countries which are engaged in the same industry. As a long term solution, it has been identified that it would be appropriate to remove the low harvesting old cultivation which has exceeded its life span and re\u2011cultivate the rubber plants generated from new clones which provide a large harvest. However, taking into consideration the excessive cost to be incurred for the re\u2011cultivation of rubber, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to increase the concession provided to new rubber cultivation from Rs.150,000/- to Rs.300,000/- per hectare and the concession provided for the re\u2011cultivation of rubber from Rs.175,000/- to Rs.350,000/- per hectare, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Providing the necessary facilities to enhance the productivity of the Coconut Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9122",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Of the total extent of the coconut lands in the country 84% has been identified  as small scale coconut lands of less than 20 acres in extent. As such, with a view to converting the coconut industry into more profitable and stable industry through minimizing the production cost by enhancing the productivity of the small scale coconut lands, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, for seeking allocations required to provide coconut tree climbing devices, Mini Tillers used for fertilizer application, Red Weevil pheromone traps, Grass Cutters, Power Sprayers and Mini Choppers for chopping various parts of the coconut tree, to the coconut land owners and the members of the Kapruka Societies, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Providing facilities to enhance the productivity of the Tea Small Holdings",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9123",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to provide relief measures, to distribute equipment among the tea smallholders and to enhance the connected rural infrastructure facilities to increase the productivity of the Tea Smallholdings. Further, it has been found that, it would be more appropriate to enhance the tea productivity by ensuring the uninterrupted tea production by the Tea Smallholders, adopting agricultural practices such as proper land preparation, pruning, weeding, standard maintenance of tea bushes, proper application of fertilizer, avoiding soil erosion and ample supply of water during dry seasons. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to implement a programme for distributing the equipment required to adopt the proper agricultural mechanisms relating to the tea cultivation among the tea smallholders at an investment of Rs.250 million and to distribute 10,000 water tanks, 3,500 water pumps and 4,500 sprayers among them under the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Amendments to the Debt Conciliation Ordinance, No.39 of 1941",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9124",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to amend the Debt Conciliation Ordinance, No.39 of 1941 by increasing the membership of the Debt Conciliation Board and revise the selection criteria of the Chairman, members of the Debt Conciliation Board and the members of each Branch. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to publish the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman in the Government Gazette and present the same thereafter in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Establishment of a new Trilingual Mixed National School in the Nanuoya area in Nuwara Eliya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9125",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to further upgrade the educational facilities available in the Nuwara Eliya District, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to establish a fully fledged new Trilingual Mixed National School, in the Nanuoya area, with an investment of Rs.800 million to conduct classes from Grade 6 to Grade 13 and to secure the facilities required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Establishment of a new Trilingual National School in Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9126",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish a new Trilingual National School in Colombo to provide the female students of all ethnic groups with the education in three languages. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to establish this as a Trilingual National School with an investment of Rs.900 million at the Wellawatta area and to secure the necessary facilities for the school, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Establishment of 5,000 Export Production Villages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9127",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish 5,000 Export Production Villages in the country under 02 stages, with the objective of promoting the primary products of farmers within the integrated process in order to accelerate the value added products of the primary products to suit the export market. The products suited for each village will be chosen based on the abundance of resources in them and it has been planned to provide training in the activities such as, securing funds required for farmers, technology, efficient resource utilization, farm management, harvesting, packaging and transportation and arrangements are made for them to gain access to the domestic and international markets. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, to implement this programme under the  project for Research, Development and Promotional Programme for export development implemented under the Ministry of Social Welfare and Primary Industries and establish 1,000 Export Production villages within 300 Divisional Secretariat Divisions under its first stage, implement this project within the period of 2018 to 2020 and improve the total number of villages up to 5,000 in stages, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Construction of the new two storey hospital buildings for the Southern Naval Hospital of the Sri Lanka Navy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9128",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Naval Hospital of the Southern Naval Command is located at Boossa and the hospital provides medical facilities for about 4,200 Navel personnel attached to the said Command and their family members. Accordingly,  the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to secure the further required funds for the construction of the 02, two storey buildings equipped with modern facilities in place of the old buildings with inadequate facilities in which this hospital is maintained at present, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Providing building facilities for the accommodation of the staff of the Naval Hospital Complex",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9129",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Navy General Hospital which consists of 684 navel personnel provides medical facilities for about 450 persons per day including  the navel personnel of the Sri Lanka Navy, the retired navel personnel and their family members. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to construct a permanent four storey residential building to facilitate the accommodation of the naval personnel taking into consideration the difficulties faced by them due to the absence of such permanent accommodation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Procurement of an Accounting and Treasury Management System to be used for the Employees' Provident Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9130",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Collection of Employees' Provident Fund amounting to around Rs.2,000 billion, maintenance of accounts, payment of benefits, investment of the excess funds and the preparation of financial statements of the funds, are done by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Since it has been found that it would be appropriate to replace the existing computer system associated with a new system for the accounting and treasury management activities of this fund, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to carry out the procurement activities for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Development of the Borella Ayurveda Hospital as a Teaching Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9131",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the project for the Development of the Borella Ayurveda Hospital as a Teaching Hospital, the construction of a new ward complex is underway. The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, for the supply of electricity, the construction of the Water and Sewage System to initiate healthcare services expeditiously in the said building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Procurement for the construction of the Renal Care Unit at the General Hospital in Badulla",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9132",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the procurement for the construction of the Renal Care Unit at the General Hospital in Badulla to provide specialized care for the patients suffering from Chronic Kidney Diseases of Unknown Aetiology to M/s Orient Construction Company (Pvt) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.668.2 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Procurement for the construction of the Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit at the Ashroff Memorial Hospital in Kalmunai",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9133",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to award the procurement for the construction of the Accident and Emergency Treatment Unit at the Ashroff Memorial Hospital in Kalmunai to M/s Link Engineering (Pvt) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.926.5 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9134",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, for the approval to procure 54,000 MT of Urea (Granular) at the rate of US$ 305 per MT and 6,500 MT of Urea (Prill) at the rate of US$ 325 per MT from Agri Commodities and Finance and 15,000 MT of Triple Super Phosphate at the rate of US$ 334.1 per MT from Swiss Singapore Overseas Enterprises, required by the Ceylon  Fertilizer Company Limited and Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company limited for the production of Chemical Fertilizer for the month of September, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Awarding of the contract for the construction of the Grid Substation under the National Transmission and Distribution Network Development and Efficiency Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9135",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement a project consisting of 04 packages to develop and improve the efficiency of the national electricity transmission and distribution network. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction and improvement of Grid Substations in the areas of Kirindiwela, Battaramulla, Biyagama, Kotmale, Veyangoda, Padukka, Kosgama, Seethawaka, Thulhiriya, Ratmalana, Pannipitiya, Kolonnawa, Athurugiriya, Polpitiya, Ukuwela, and Naula, to the Joint Venture of the  Mitsubishi Corporation and Ceylex Engineering (pvt) Ltd., under its second package, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement for the Establishment of a Biotechnology Laboratory",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9136",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Memorandum of Understanding has been entered into between Sri Lanka and the Science and Technology Ministry of the Government of China previously, for the establishment of a Joint Biotechnology Laboratory in Sri Lanka.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Science, Technology, Research, Skills Development & Vocational Training and Kandyan Heritage, to sign the second Agreement including the terms and the conditions agreed upon for the implementation of the project for strengthening of the technical cooperation between the two parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Bringing back to normal the reservoirs and the agricultural wells in the North Central Province dried up due to the dry weather conditions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9137",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that nearly 12,000 cultivation wells and approximately 2,000 reservoirs used to take drinking water in the North Central Province have dried up due to the prevailing dry climatic conditions. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, for the construction of common new drinking water wells to be resistant to drought, excavation of the dried up cultivation wells,  excavation of wells in the dried up reservoirs and renovation of the drinking water wells to be carried out by the farmer organizations through the Divisional Secretaries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-21-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2018-08-21",
    "description": "Renovation of the National Art Gallery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9138",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approved to set apart a provision of Rs.42 million required in respect of the renovation activities in the National Art Gallery identified as needed to be done expeditiously, taking into consideration the matters submitted to the Cabinet by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Stabilization of the Mt. Lavinia to Angulana Coastal Stretch and the Sand Bar at the Kalu Ganga Outfall which has been subject to erosion",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9139",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted in principle previously to stabilize the Coastal Stretch from Mt. Lavinia to Angulana under the Southern Colombo Sand Catchment Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to stabilize the Coastal Stretch from Mt. Lavinia to Angulana using the Sand Engine Methodology and to restore the sand bar at the Kalu Ganga outfall eroded due to the recent floods, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Improvement of the facilities needed to support the Public - Private Partnerships in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9140",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to secure funds amounting to US$ 25 million from the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) of the World Bank for the improvement of a structure to assist the Public\u2011Private Partnerships and for provision of infrastructure financing to support the Public-Private partnerships programme.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct negotiations in that regard and enter into the relevant loan agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Holding the State Christmas Festival - 2018 under the patronage of the  Mannar Diocese",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9141",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Action has been taken to hold the State Christmas Festival,  every year, under the patronage of a Catholic Diocese and the patronage and guidance of the Bishop of the respective diocese. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to hold the State Christmas Festival - 2018 under the patronage of the Mannar Diocese with the theme as 'The Nativity of Jesus and the Splendor of Christmas', with a view to promoting reconciliation and spiritual awakening among the people in Mannar where there is a multi\u2011national community, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Hosting of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) Annual Meeting - 2021 in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9142",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to communicate the Asian Development Bank; a long time development partner of Sri Lanka, the intention of hosting the Asian Development Bank Annual Meeting - 2021 in Sri Lanka and to appoint a National Monitoring Committee and Sub\u2011Committees for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Amendments to the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration Act, No.9 of 1982",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9143",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to make amendments to the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration Act, No.9 of 1982, incorporating the necessary amendments to suit the present needs of the functions and the administrative structure of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "New Projects proposed to be implemented from the year 2019 for the performance of the Plantation Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9144",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Through the export of products associated with tea, rubber and coconut, an income of Rs.457.85 billion could be generated in the year 2017 and it has been found that various research, services and methodologies should be enhanced in order to generate more income. For this purpose, it has been planed to implement projects for the production of hybrid coconut seeds, the production and distribution of the predatory Mites for the control Mite damages and the construction of productive and highly efficient modern smoke houses.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to secure the provision needed for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Systematic diagnostic assessment of the chemical disaster risks in Sri Lanka by the National Building Research Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9145",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Through a study conducted by the National Building Research Organization (NBRO) it has been confirmed that most of the accidents related to chemical substances in Sri Lanka occur on account of being unaware of those substances,  the non\u2011maintenance of the premises using such substances, the lapses on the supervision and the misuse of the technologies. Considering the requirement of preparing a formal disaster management framework as a remedial measure to address this situation, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to conduct a Systematic diagnostic assessment of the chemical disaster risks in Sri Lanka between 2019 - 2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Formalization of investments of the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9146",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The objective of the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund is to create higher education opportunities for underprivileged youth and provide facilities and enhance them in respect of same. The National Wealth Cooperation Limited and the National Wealth Securities Limited established under the full ownership of the Mahapola Fund make investments on strengthening the Mahapola Main Fund. In view of the negative impact caused to the Mahapola Fund due to the activities of the said companies and to regularize the investments of the said Fund,  the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to liquidate the said companies and invest all the funds belonging to the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund, only in state banks and Central bank bonds, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Amendments to the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund Act, No. 66 of 1981",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9147",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, to amend the title of Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund Act, No.66 of 1981 which regulates the Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship providing the students in the Government higher education institutions with funds for their education, as Lalith Athulathmudali Mahapola Higher Education Scholarship Trust Fund Act, No.66 of 1981, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Revision of the Nutrition Allowance of the Scholarship holders of the  Sports Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9148",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sport Schools have been established with the objective of producing athletes at national and international level by selecting students who display talents for sports and providing them with proper training. As such,  the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education, to increase the monthly Nutrition Allowance provided to a student from Rs.2,500/- to Rs.5,000/-, with a view to providing the students who engage in training in these schools with sufficient nutrition, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Conducting the Asia-Pacific Region Annual Conference on Express Mail Service (EMS) - 2019 in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9149",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, the Minister of Posts, Postal Services and Muslim Religious Affairs, to conduct the Asia-Pacific Region Annual Conference on Express Mail Service (EMS) - 2019 in Sri Lanka, in September 2019 with the participation of foreign representatives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "The project for upgrading the infrastructure facilities at the Industrial Engineering Training Institute (IETI) in Katubedda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9150",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Industrial Engineering Training Institute (IETI) in Katubedda offers Three year full time courses at National Vocational Qualification (NVQ) Level 4 in the fields of Electrical, Construction, Wood Work and a one year course in the Computer Application. It has been planned to increase the annual intake of students to the institute which offers courses suited to the job market by enhancing its facilities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Science, Technology, Research, Skills Development & Vocational Training and Kandyan Heritage, to call for a comprehensive project proposal to upgrade the institute with an investment of Rs.2,400 million by obtaining financial assistance from an Austrian Soft Loan Scheme; and to secure foreign donor assistance for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Kolonnawa Canal Diversion Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9151",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement the  Kolonnawa Canal Diversion Scheme with a length of 4.8 km under the Metro Colombo Urban Development Project, under four sub sections with an investment of Rs.3,000 million. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract to carry out the construction activities to be implemented under its Stage 3, to the E &C - RR Joint Venture, for a sum of Rs 1,004.4 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Construction of 08 rural bridges for the betterment of the beneficiaries of the model villages in the Hambantota district",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9152",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to construct the 08  rural bridges under the 'Nagamu Purawara' programme namely, the bridge across the Rambukwewa Weligatta ara, the bridge across the Muwanwewa Weerawila ara, the Diyabendi bridge across Pannegamuwa and Abhayapura, the bridge across Ambalanthota Liyangastota and Bedigantota, the Malalaara, Ranmuduwewa bridge in the Thanamalwila road, the bridge between Rubberwatta and Uduwila, the Katuwana Keselwatta bridge and the bridge across Lunugamwehera right bank,  for the housing beneficiaries of the model villages being initiated in the underdeveloped villages of the Hambantota district in order to provide easy access to the urban common amenities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-08-28-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-08-28",
    "description": "Naming the year 2018 as the National Food Production year",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9153",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena made the Cabinet aware that action will be taken to issue circular instructions for all the relevant Government institutions to focus attention on re\u2011cultivating the abandoned paddy lands, making use of all other cultivable lands for cultivation purposes and  producing the seeds and planting materials required for the crop cultivation, with a view to giving a fresh start to the agricultural activities which had declined due to adverse weather conditions such as drought and floods that occurred in the past years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Reconstruction of Sri Lanka Maha Viharaya in Nepal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9154",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Maha Viharaya situated in the vicinity of the Lumbini Sacred Area in Nepal where the birth of the Gautama Buddha took place is a place of worship of the Buddhist pilgrims. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to provide necessary provision for the further reconstruction activities to be carried out in the Sri Lanka Maha Viharaya with a view to developing the said sacred area as a place of worship which demonstrates the flourishing of the Theravada Buddhism, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Introduction of a transit card which could be used in bus and rail transport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9155",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to modernize the Public Transport Service of Sri Lanka and for the convenience of the commuters, it has been planned to introduce a transit card system through an electronic payment methodology.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to facilitate the implementation of a Framework for a Standardized common card required in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Establishment of an Industrial Zone for the Small Scale Entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9156",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to develop small scale industries in the areas utilizing the extent of the land of 100 acres where the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory had been situated. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to develop the said land as an industrial zone for the small scale entrepreneurs, under an investment of around Rs.998 million, with all infrastructure facilities needed for industries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Implementation of the Tharapuram Co-operative Village Programme in the Mannar District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9157",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously for the development work carried out under the Tharapuram Co-operative Village Programme in the Mannar District. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to construct a Convention Centre as the next stage of the multipurpose building under construction, utilizing the provision set apart under the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Amending the Companies Act, No.7 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9158",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has focused its attention to amend the Companies Act, No.7  of 2007, considering the present trends and the requirements.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to publish the amendments made to sections 5, 9 and 10 of the Act in the Government Gazette enabling the Registrar of Companies to notify the general public on the incorporation of a new Company and to direct a Company to change its name  in order to achieve a higher grading in the Ease of Business Index of the World Bank for Sri Lanka and to present the same, thereafter, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Providing permanent building facilities for the Nuwara Eliya Regional Office of the Tea Small Holdings Development Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9159",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing permanent building facilities in place of the building on lease where the Nuwara Eliya Regional Office of the Tea Small Holdings Development Authority is functioning presently, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to establish the said Office in a building situated in a block of land in extent of 0.0452 hectares in the Kotmale New Town after renovation and to allocate the required funds for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Amendments to the Tea Research Board Act, No.52 of 1993",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9160",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to amend the Tea Research  Board Act, No.52 of 1993. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to publish the Bill prepared, incorporating the provisions to widen the functions of the Board on formulating the environmental security measures, specific provision pertaining to the issue of research outcome to various parties, to make provision to prevent the inconsistencies between the Tea Research Board Act and other related law and to reconstitute the composition of the Board of Directors of the Tea Research Board, in the Government Gazette and to present the same thereafter, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Supply of drinking water to the people in the Jaffna Peninsula",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9161",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Joint Proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, and Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to implement the drinking water supply project utilizing the water resource in the Vadamarachchi Lagoon, at an investment of Rs.2,000 million, for the supply of safe drinking water to the people in the Jaffna Peninsula, in accordance with the feasibility study made on the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Reduction of the landslide vulnerability through mitigation measures",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9162",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement a project to identify the landslide vulnerable    areas and unstable slopes in the hilly areas to minimize the possible disastrous situations due to climatic changes resulting from extreme bad weather conditions. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to implement the said project at an investment of US$ 104 million and secure the funds required for the purpose from the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Amendments to the Convention against the Illicit Traffic of Narcotic drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, No.1 of 2008",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9163",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka has signed the United Nations Convention of 1988 against the Illicit Traffic of Narcotic drugs and Psychotropic substances and with a view to executing the responsibility bounded by international obligations, the Convention against Illicit Traffic of Narcotic drugs and Psychotropic substances Act, No.1 of 2008 has been enacted. However, prevention of illicit trafficking and use of these substances has become a serious challenge locally and as well as internationally. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to  amend the Convention against Illicit Traffic of Narcotic drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, No.1 of 2008, by establishing a code of laws, which enables to face the situation squarely, locally and internationally, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the establishment of the South Asian Regional Intelligence and Coordination Centre on Transnational Organized Crime (SARICC-TOC)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9164",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish the Co-ordination Centre in Sri Lanka for the project on \u201cStrengthening of law enforcement on Drugs in South Asia\u201d conducted by the South Asian Regional Office of the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between Sri Lanka and India, Nepal, Maldives, Bangladesh and Bhutan which are the member countries of the said Centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Introduction of a system for the standardization of the Geographical names",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9165",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sinhalese and Tamil languages,which are the Official Languages of Sri Lanka, comprise of non\u2011romanized alphabets. Since the correct Sinhalese/Tamil pronunciation is not produced when the geographical names of such as, villages, towns and rivers in Sri Lanka are written using English characters, writing in English characters in accordance with a standardized system to produce the correct pronunciation is known as the Romanization System. This system is already being used to write geographical names in the Tamil language. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, the Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, to propose the use of Romanization System for writing the geographical names in the Sinhalese language to enable the use of such names internationally and to propose the same, at the United Nations Conference on Standardization, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "The Project for the Correction of Drug Addictive Offenders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9166",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- A pilot project, has been implemented within the North Western Province to preclude drug addictive offenders from drug addiction through corrective measures and making them engaged in self employment opportunities enabling their economic stability. The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to secure the provisions required to implement the said project in the North Western, Southern, Sabaragamuwa and Eastern Provinces as well, from the year 2019 onwards, based on its success, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Tourism Promotion",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9167",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to implement programmes for promoting Sri Lanka as an attractive destination among the tourists in the global level in order to attract tourists of developed countries with a high purchasing power and to retain them for a longer period of time in the country. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to implement the said tourism promotion programmes by the Ministry of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs as recommended by the committees comprising of the representatives of the relevant institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Digital Advertising Campaign for Tourism Promotion",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9168",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "-  Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to implement a digital advertising campaign to  promote Sri Lanka as an attractive tourist destination among the tourists in the United Kingdom,Germany, France, India and China. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. John Amaratunga, the Minister of Tourism Development and Christian Religious Affairs, to award the contracts for the implementation of the said digital advertising campaigns for India and China to Havas Media India Private Limited and to M/s Ionic Media  respectively as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee and the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Supply and delivery of new Tyre Kits for the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9169",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation,\tto award the procurement for the purchase of new Tyre Kits in various sizes required for the buses of the Sri Lanka Transport Board to M/s. Ceat Kelani International Tyres (Pvt.) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.1,124.14 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Establishment of Standing Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committees to accelerate  the implementation of projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9170",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to appoint Senior Officials such as Secretaries to the State Ministries, Additional Secretaries, Chief Financial Officers as members of  the Standing Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committees in order to expedite the procurement decision making process, to accelerate the projects inclusive of development projects implemented by the  Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Mirigama Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9171",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement the Mirigama Water Supply Project, with a view to supplying water to Mirigama, Kaleliya, Kandalama and to a section of the proposed Mirigama Industrial Zone. A feasibility study has been conducted by M/s China Aero Technology International Engineering Corporation (CATIC) in this regard, and the said Corporation has submitted a project proposal for implementation. As such, the Joint Proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs and Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to appoint a Committee to evaluate the said proposal, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Housing Project with 450 Housing Units at Cyril C. Perera Mawatha at Bloemendhal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9172",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to award the contract of the Housing Project with 450 Housing Units at Cyril C. Perera Mawatha at Bloemendhal to M/s Access Engineering PLC, for a sum of Rs.2,737.35 million as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9173",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mahinda Amaraweera, the Minister of  Agriculture, for approval to procure 38,500 MT of Urea (Granular) at the rate of US$ 309.60 per MT from Liven Agrichem Pte. Ltd., 20,000 MT of Muriate of Potash at the rate of US$ 329.50 per MT and 7,500 MT of Triple Super Phosphate at the rate of US$ 317.25 per MT from Agri Commodities and Finance, required by the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Limited and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Limited for the procurement of Chemical Fertilizer for the month of October, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-04-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-09-04",
    "description": "Vesting of Dr. Neville Fernando Hospital with the Sri Lanka Air Force",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9174",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a solution to the conflict which prevailed for a length of time at the SAITM Medical Faculty, around 900 medical students who were studying at the faculty had been absorbed into the Sir John Kotelawala Defence University.  Considering the proposal presented for vesting Dr. Neville Fernando Hospital  affiliated to the SAITM Medical Faculty with the Sri Lanka Air Force, the proposal made by Hon. Maithripala Sirisena, the Minister of Defence, for the appointment of a Official Committee to conduct negotiations in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Middle-Income Housing Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9175",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to expand the Middle\u2011Income Housing Loan Scheme enabling the middle income earners of both the public and private sectors who purchase a house for the first time from the middle income housing projects to obtain a concessionary loan from the National Savings Bank.   Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to take into  consideration the age limits generally adopted by the Banks instead of the age limits that prevailed previously to apply for this loan scheme and also to enable to facilitate more beneficiaries to purchase houses from projects implemented by the private sector  as well, was approved by the Cabinet.  Pertaining to this matter, as proposed by H.E. the President, it was also decided to lower the eligibility criteria relating to the monthly income level for this programme."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Completion of the construction work of the Public Library Building in Batticaloa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9176",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction work of a new building in place of the 50 year old building where the present Public Library of Batticaloa is located is now underway. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to secure Rs.169.97 million required further to complete the construction work of the said building from the Budget of the  year 2019, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Implementation of the Sustainable Punyagrama Programme Islandwide towards a Righteous Society",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9177",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sustainable Punyagrama Programme with temple as a centre point is being conducted by the Ministry of Buddhasasana, with the objective of implementing the concept of the village and the temple in a more realistic way and creating a village comprising of an economically sound community  empowered with virtues. Through this programme the community life is to be activated based on the village temple being in the forefront and in accordance with the Buddhist values, customs and cultural concepts which prevailed in the past, but which are deteriorating at present. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, considering the success of the 50 programmes conducted last year to implement this programme in 250 villages covering all the Districts in the Island within the coming year and centering the other religious places as well, making aware the other Ministries to implement the programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "The re-printing activities of the Buddha Jayanthi Publication Series by the Ministry of Buddhasasana",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9178",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The translation activities of the Pali Thripitikaya into Sinhala language commenced to commemorate the 2500 Buddha Jayanthi and by the year 1989 the publication series have been completed. The Ministry of Buddhasasana has made plans to print this publication series in a more formal manner and publicize in future. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana, to undertake the responsibility of editing and printing of the Tripitaka Publication Series by the Ministry of Buddhasasana, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Amendment to the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act, No.27 of 2005 to increase the income level of the Sri Lanka Transport Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9179",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that a considerable amount of daily income receivable to the Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB) is lost due to various malpractices. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft necessary legislation to amend the Sri Lanka Transport Board Act, No.27 of 2005, by incorporating the necessary amendments to increase the level of income through the prevention of such practices, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Islandwide citizens Awareness Programme on the Right to Information",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9180",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka, being one of the countries which have ensured the right to information of the public, possesses the third best Right to Information Act in the world. Accordingly, the Government has focused its attention to declare the period from 21st to 28th September as the Information Week to make aware the public of using the right to information for the public welfare to coincide with the International Day of Right to Information which falls on 28th September while naming the year 2018 as 'Year of Public Awareness'. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to implement the mobile service on Right to Information as 'Right to Information to the Village' under this programme and to make aware the students of the same by conducting various competitions covering all schools Islandwide, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Enhancing the coverage of 'Vasantham TV' Channel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9181",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The television channel 'Vasantham TV' has been launched by the Independent Television media network for the Tamil speaking community and during its first phase, services were provided to the viewers covering Colombo and suburban areas. Subsequently, it has been extended to Jaffna, Eastern Province and Kokavil area. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to extend the broadcasting facilities with an investment of Rs.304 million enabling the Tamil viewers living in the other parts of the Island as well the facility to watch the programmes in this Channel, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Health Research Council",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9182",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft necessary legislation for the establishment of the 'National Health Research Council' at national level for regulation, co\u2011ordination, monitoring, development and management of Health Researches, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Upgrading of the Provincial General Hospital - Ratnapura as a Teaching Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9183",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to accommodate the first intake of medical students which consists of 75 undergraduates for the Faculty of Medicine of the Sabaragamuwa University at the end of the year 2018. The need has arisen to upgrade the Ratnapura General Hospital as a Teaching Hospital with a view to providing the said medical students with clinical training. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to upgrade the Provincial General Hospital in Ratnapura as a Teaching Hospital in order to function as the hospital affiliated to the new Faculty of Medicine of the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Organizing the 71st  National Day Celebration",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9184",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs, to appoint a sub-committee comprising of 13 people's representatives chaired by  the Hon. Prime Minister to prepare the relevant programme and organize and monitor necessary arrangements pertaining to the 71st National Day Ceremony which falls on 04th  February, 2019, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Disposal of ash dump accumulated at the ash yard of the Norochcholai Coal Power Plant in an eco-friendly manner",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9185",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures have to be taken immediately to dispose the ash dump accumulated as a by product of coal combustion of the Norochcholai Coal Power Plant to prevent the harmful impact caused to the public in surrounding villages and the environment. As a step of this process, it has been decided to provide ash for making eco-friendly products by using them. As such, according to a proposal presented to make bricks by using ash, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to dispose the ash within the ash yard of the Coal Power Plant to carry out productions without disposing them to the environment, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Drafting a new Act to give effect to the National Fisheries and \tAquaculture Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9186",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- National Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No.2 of 1996 which is presently in force has been amended at various instances and according to the present economic, social and environmental trends, it has been identified that further amendments should be made to the said Act. As such, \tthe proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, to draft a new Act incorporating the provisions to regulate, conserve and develop the fisheries industry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Construction of 1,200 houses in the Northern and Southern Provinces under the Semata Sevana Gramashakthi Model Village Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9187",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has extended a financial assistance of Rs 600 million for the construction of 600 housing units in 25 villages of the Northern Province and  600 housing units in 25 villages of the Southern Province  under the Semata Sevana Gramashakthi Model Village Project conducted by the Government Island wide. Accordingly, the construction of the said villages is being carried out at present.  As such, in terms of the concurrence given by the Government of India for financial assistance under the same project in constructing of another 600 housing units in the Northern Province and 600 housing units in the Southern Province, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to implement the said project, to enter into a  Memorandum of Understanding in that regard and to appoint a Steering Committee for the project implementation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Installation of Solar Power Panels in Model Village Housing Schemes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9188",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of uplifting the economic well being of the people residing in the model villages implemented Islandwide by the Ministry of Housing and Construction, it has been proposed to implement a project to install Solar Power Panels in the said Model Villages with the participation of private entrepreneurs, under the Soorya Bala Sangramaya project presently being implemented by the Government. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to call for  proposals to select suitable investors for the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Agreement for the Transfer of Sentenced Persons between Sri Lanka and the Kingdom of Thailand",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9189",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to present the Agreement entered into between Sri Lanka and Thailand on the Transfer of Sentenced Persons, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Enactment of Legislation for the Prevention of Animal Sacrifices",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9190",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although animal sacrifice which is considered an ancient religious practice, it is still carried out publicly in certain Hindu temples, it has been observed that the majority of the Hindu devotees do not accept that practice. At present, the Government of India has banned the animal sacrifice in the Hindu temples. As such the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to enact legislation to ban animal and bird sacrifices carried out in the Hindu temples or its precincts in Sri Lanka as well and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation based on the draft prepared for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Integrated e-Land Registry (e-LR) Project for improving Registering Property Mechanism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9191",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The e-Land Registry has been initiated with the objective of elevating the position of Sri Lanka in the Ease of Doing Business Index by improving the  access to land information by investors when registering a property. The current process of registering a property takes 51 days and consists of 09 steps. Through the implementation of the e-Land Registry project, it is expected to reduce the said duration up to 05 days and 02 steps. The programme has been planned to be implemented in the Western and Southern Provinces in the year 2018. As such, the Joint Proposal made by Hon. Vajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Home Affairs and Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to secure the required provision for the future implementation of the said project Island Wide, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Regulation of the Boat building Industry and providing infrastructure facilities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9192",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to improving the Boat building industry in Sri Lanka, feasibility study is expected to be carried out to construct the Boat launching pad, slipway, repair facilities and the breakwater in Weligama, Kapparathota for facilitating the preparation of a regulatory framework for the purpose and for providing the necessary infrastructure facilities to the existing boat builders to continue with their industry. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to secure the required provision for the continuation of the project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Construction of the Intake Structure of the Bandarawela, Diyathalawa and Haputale Integrated Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9193",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Bandarawela, Diyathalawa and Haputale Integrated Water Supply Project has been planned to be implemented to address the present and the future water needs of the residents of the 63 Grama Niladhari Divisions affected by the implementation of the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Project.  Accordingly, the Dayabara Reservoir which is being constructed under the Uma Oya Project has been identified as the water source of the said  project.  Presently, the construction work of the Dayabara Reservoir is nearing its completion and as the Intake Structure of the Reservoir has to be constructed before filling the Reservoir, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to award the said contract to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau / Central Engineering Services (Pvt.) Ltd., and also to secure the funds required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Development of the Hambantota and Nuwara Eliya District General Hospitals under the Financial Assistance of Netherlands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9194",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the projects on construction of the Hambantota and the Nuwara Eliya District General hospitals and the supply of the necessary equipment for those hospitals have commenced from the year 2012 under the financial assistance of  Netherlands, the inability to complete the projects up to date due to various reasons has resulted in escalating the expenditure to be incurred in respect of the required equipment for the hospitals considerably. However, considering the necessity of fulfilling the requirements of the residents of the area expeditiously, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to obtain the necessary approval and secure funds to provide modern equipment according to specification,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Construction of the Mathugama, Galle, Beliatta, Matara and Pallekele Grid Substations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9195",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish 90 Solar Power Plants to connect to the central electricity system all over Sri Lanka under the Soorya Bala Sangramaya Programme. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy, to award the contract for the construction of 05 Grid substations in Mathugama, Galle, Beliatta, Matara and Pallekele out of the Grid substations to be constructed to be connected to the solar power electricity system, in accordance with the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Development of infrastructure facilities at the Rajarata, Colombo, Ruhuna and Eastern Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9196",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- As it has been planned for the gradual increase of the intake of students to the State Universities, the Government has planned to increase the infrastructure facilities at the Rajarata, Colombo, Ruhuna and Eastern Universities in order to provide more qualitative infrastructure facilities for the students of these Universities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, for the development activities such as the construction of a Laboratory complex including Lecture halls for the Faculty of Agriculture of the Rajarata University, the construction of canteens at Mihintale Student Hostel Premises, the construction of  Stage I of the New Arts building of the University of Colombo, the development of infrastructure facilities of the new Faculty of Healthcare Sciences at the Eastern University, the construction of Stage I of the Faculty of Allied Health Science building of the University of Ruhuna and the renovations at the main building premises of same, with an investment of Rs.3,690.42 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Construction of the buildings necessary for the establishment of the Faculty of Medicine of the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9197",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish the Faculty of Medicine of the Sabaragamuwa University in a 20 acre land situated in close proximity to the General Hospital  of Ratnapura with an investment of Rs.5,015 million. Considering the urgent need of commencing the activities of this Faculty of Medicine, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, the Minister of Higher Education & Cultural Affairs, for the construction of the Clinical building for the Medical and the Para Medical Faculty and to secure the funds necessary for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Rehabilitation and Improvement of the road section of 27.75km from Tampitiya to Chenkalady under the Badulla-Chenkalady Road Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9198",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Badulla-Chenkalady Road Improvement Project is implemented under 03 main stages with the financial assistance of the Saudi Fund for Development (SFD). The proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development, to award the contract for the rehabilitation and improvement of the road section from 249.8 km to 277.55 km from Tampitiya to Chenkalady in the Badulla-Chenkalady Road as its 3rd stage, at a sum of Rs.2,837.43 million, without VAT, to Maga Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Facilities to promote women's employment in the field of Technical and Vocational Education and Training",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9199",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide a grant of US$ 3 million for the provision of required facilities to promote self-employment among  female trainees in the field of Technical and Vocational Education and Training, guide women towards the male-dominated employment fields and widen the women's access towards emerging employment opportunities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Science, Technology, Research, Skills Development & Vocational Training and Kandyan Heritage, to enter into an Agreement with the Plan International Australia to implement the relevant  project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "The Proposed Counter Terrorism Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9200",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to publish the draft Bill for the Counter Terrorism in the Government Gazette, which has been drafted with the objective of protecting the people of Sri Lanka from terrorism and the terrorism associated activities after discussions with all relevant stakeholders, and to present it in Parliament and further amendments if any, necessary for the Bill to be considered at the Committee Stage of the Bill in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Empowering Youth with leadership skills",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9201",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of empowering youth to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) in Sri Lanka, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement a programme namely 'Project for empowering youth with leadership skills to spearhead accountability for achieving the Sustainable Development Goals in Sri Lanka' under 03 major stages through the 'Sustainable Development Division' of the Presidential Secretariat and to secure the required provision for the purpose through the 2019-2021 Medium Term Budgetary Framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-11-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2018-09-11",
    "description": "Construction of rural bridges for the well being of the beneficiaries of the model villages in the Hambantota District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9202",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to commence the construction of the 04 projects under the 'Nagamu Purawara' programme namely the Yaya bridge along the Walasmulla - Pallekanda road, the bridge across the Urubokka Oya in Medagoda Kumbukmulla, the bridge connecting Thalunna and Andupelena and the bridge extension of Pahala Beragama to facilitate easy access to the urban facilities for the housing beneficiaries of the model villages implemented in the villages with inadequate infrastructure facilities in the Hambantota District, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "National Food Production Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9203",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to implement the National Food Production Programme with the objective of reducing the foreign exchange spent for the importation of food by producing all food items which can be produced locally of good quality. However, it has been difficult to achieve the expected targets of this programme due to the bad whether condition that prevailed in the country during the recent past. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to extend this programme up to the years 2019 and 2020 which includes renovating tanks  Island wide, promoting new technological methods among farmers, empowering persons engaged in agricultural, fisheries and livestock fields as entrepreneurs, promoting the renewable energy usage in the said fields, uplifting local milk production and encouraging relevant research work in the field of food production, and to provide necessary funds for that purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Obtaining International Scientific, Technical and Financial Assistance to mitigate Adverse Impacts of Climate Change",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9204",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The importance of building relations with international institutions to implement the activities in an integrated manner to mitigate the Adverse Impacts of Climate Change and meet national obligations on the international environmental agreements has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to enter into Host Country Agreements with Green Climate Fund (GCF) and the International Council for Research  in Agroforestry (ICRAF) and communicate the interest in obtaining the membership of Global Green Growth Institute (GGGI) and ratify the establishment agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Strengthening Elder Care Facilities in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9205",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been projected that the elderly population in Sri Lanka will be doubled from the current level and reach the level of 24.8% of the total population by the year 2041.  However, it has been observed that the access of the elderly people to the formal mechanism of social protection is very limited. Accordingly, as a remedial measure, the joint proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs and Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, to introduce a methodology to establish Day Care Homes for elders with family, permanent stay homes for elders without family and wards in state hospitals under the care of Geriatric Specialists for elders who are severely disabled or bedridden and to implement necessary programmes to train around 10,000 elder care givers to cater the growing demand in the field of elder care and to implement the necessary programme and provide necessary facilities for same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Bilateral Air Services Consultation  between Sri Lanka and Luxembourg",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9206",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation, to enter into a bilateral agreement between Sri Lanka and Luxembourg on air services pertaining to transportation of passengers and cargo according to the agreement reached between the relevant parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Amendments to the Finance Bill - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9207",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Finance Bill prepared to facilitate for the implementation of the various proposals submitted through the Budgets of the years of 2016, 2017, and 2018 by the Government, has been presented in Parliament. Taking into consideration the requests made by different parties on the implementation of the said proposals, it has been observed that it would be appropriate to include the  amendments during the Committee Stage of the Bill in Parliament since it  requires some amendments to implement the above proposals effectively. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the Finance Bill by revising various taxes, dates on implementation of certain provisions and other administrative provisions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Madhu Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9208",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Shrine of Our Lady of Madhu with a history of more than 400 years, is a sacred place of devotion not only of the Catholics but persons belonging to other religions as well. In order to provide a regular water purification facility, for the Water Supply system presently used to provide water to the pilgrims arriving to this sacred place, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning and Water Supply, to implement the Madhu Water Supply Project by using the Madhu reservoir to enable to generate 1,000 cubic meters of water per day, with an investment of Rs.554 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the Establishment of a Bilateral Consultation Mechanism between Sri Lanka and Laos",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9209",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding to strengthen the existing bilateral relations between Sri Lanka and Laos and for the mutual co\u2011operation on regional and international matters, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Establishment of an Industrial Zone for Small Entrepreneurs by utilizing the land belonging to the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9210",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish an eco\u2011friendly Industrial Zone in a land area of 330 acres out of the land where the Kankesanthurai Cement Factory was situated and not being used for production purposes as of now and to develop 100 acres under its first phase in the year 2019. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to select  suitable investors for the development of the relevant infrastructure facilities and to commence industries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Recommencement of the manufacturing activities of the Paper Mill at Embilipitiya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9211",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- M/s Korean SPA Packaging (Pvt.) Ltd. has submitted a proposal to recommence the manufacturing activities of the Paper Mill at Embilipitya, which is presently defunct, after renovating its plant machinery and infrastructure facilities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to allocate this Mill to the M/s Korean SPA Packaging (Pvt.) Ltd., on lease basis, for the manufacturing of industrial grade paper required for packaging items, with an investment of Rs.1,200 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Establishment of an Industrial and Technological Development Super Zone at Raigama in Kalutara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9212",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to generating new employment opportunities and upgrading the living standards of the rural community, the proposal made by Hon. Rishad Bathiudeen, the Minister of Industry and Commerce, to establish the Industrial and Technological Development Super Zone with an investment of Rs.346 million in a block of land in extent of 24 acres in the Neuchatel Estate at Horahena in Millaniya, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Renovation of the Railway Bridge in Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9213",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found necessary to construct a new railway bridge after demolishing the narrow bridge constructed via Galle - Matara railway bridge crossing the Moda Ela due to the barrier it causes for efficient flood conveyance.  As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to secure funds required for the construction of a temporary railway bridge and a railway track  for transportation purposes until the proposed bridge is constructed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Developing systems for building assessment and condition reporting",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9214",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Building Research Organization has designed to introduce a 'system for building assessment and condition reporting' to ensure the protection of the occupants of the building and the neighborhood by assessing the structural integrity of the buildings, deterioration of the building elements due to time, repair and retrofitting of buildings and providing suitable technical recommendations. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to secure funds required to promote the said system, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Development and Rehabilitation of Fishery Harbours, Anchorages and Landing Sites Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9215",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The  Development and Rehabilitation of Fishery Harbours, Anchorages and Landing Sites Project has developed Seven Fishery Harbours, a Boat Yard, two Landing Sites and three Anchorages by now. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Vijith Vijayamuni Zoysa, the Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development and Rural Economic Affairs, to secure funds and other facilities to develop the projects including upgrading and developing of Balapitiya, Suduwella, Dodanduwa, Hambantota and Mailady fishery harbours; Negambo Lagoon Development Project and the construction of Welipatanwila, Dehiwala, Rekawa and Mawella anchorages which have been identified to be further carried out under the said project, during the period from 2018 - 2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Supply of equipment for the Research Unit of the Sri Lanka Anti-Doping Agency",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9216",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, the Minister of Provincial Councils, Local Government and Sports, to supply laboratory equipment for the Research Unit of Sri Lanka Anti-Doping Agency, with the objective of preserving the clean and spiritual sport by minimizing the risk of the Sri Lankan Athletes who participate in National and International level tournaments being alleged on the usage of  prohibited substances, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Expediting the demining activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9217",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- National Demining Programme was initiated in the year 2002 in the conflict affected areas and accordingly a land area of 137 square km has been cleared and handed over for resettlement activities by now. It has been designed to complete the demining activities by 2020, by implementing the said demining programme in an another land area of 28 square km in  Northern, Eastern and the North Central Provinces. As such, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to secure facilities required for the Demining Unit of the Sri Lanka Army engaged in the said activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Granting National Vocational Qualification Level 3 (NVQ 3) Certificate for 10,000 Cinnamon Peelers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9218",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, to prepare a programme for granting  National Vocational Qualification Level 3 (NVQ 3) certificate for 10,000 Cinnamon Peelers for carrying out the cinnamon peeling process with accurate technical usages and to secure other facilities required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Submission of the regulations made on the factory conditions in terms of  the Factories Ordinance, in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9219",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Factories Ordinance has been enforced  by the Department of Labour in order to inspect the factories enabling to maintain the occupational safety protect, the health and welfare of the employees. Taking into consideration the need for effective enforcement of the law on the factory conditions, the proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, to present 05 Regulations made in terms of the provisions of  the Factories Ordinance on the Registration of Factories and Approval of Factory Buildings, Registration of Steam Boilers, issuance of Certificates for examination of Steam Boilers  and other Pressure Vessels, protection of workers from excessive noise and General Standard of the lights of the Factories, for approval in Parliament and thereafter publish the same in the Government Gazette, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Implementing the Recommendations submitted by the Office on Missing Persons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9220",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Office on Missing Persons has made its recommendations by the Interim Report submitted on 5th  August 2018  on the legal reforms to be effected with regard to the steps to be taken in relation to the legal obligations for reparation and to ensure the non-occurrence of such incidents. Further, recommendations have been made on implementing Financial Assistance Programmes, Debt Relief Programmes, Housing Development Programmes, Educational Support Programmes, Vocational Training and Livelihood Development Programmes for the affected parties.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee comprising of another 10 Ministers, under the Chairmanship of Hon. (Dr.) Wijayadasa Rajapaksa, to study the said recommendations and propose appropriate future course action and to secure facilities required to implement the  recommendations of the said Sub\u2011Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Productive Use of Stand - by Generators in Government Institutions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9221",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that the  Stand - by Generator of Government Institutions used in emergency situations can generate about 200 MW of power. Accordingly, it has been observed that, it would be a profitable alternative, if  the above Stand-by generators could be used to feed the National Grid, rather than generating power through diesel power plants. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to grant permission to the Ceylon Electricity Board to purchase electricity generated from the Stand-by generators of Government Institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Implementation of the Electronic Immigration Gate System (e-Gate System) at Bandaranayake International Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9222",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that the installation of the e-Gate System as an alternative to the services being provided by the Immigration and Emigration Officers at the Airport will regulate the arrival and departure immigration clearance process. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Nimal Siripala de Silva, the Minister of Transport and Civil Aviation and Hon. S.B. Navinne, the Minister of  Internal Affairs & Wayamba Development to install the e-Gate System consisting of  10 units at the Bandaranaike Interantional Airport with an investment of Rs.260 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Vocational Training Institute at Hingurakgoda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9223",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-09-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish a  National Vocational Training Institute at Hingurakgoda with a view to providing employable skills to the rural youth. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Sarath Amunugama, the Minister of Science, Technology, Research, Skills Development & Vocational Training and Kandyan Heritage to award the said contract to M/s Gemco International BV, the Netherlands at a sum of Euro 35 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-09-18-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-09-18",
