    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has decided to provide relief measures further required to the people  affected by the severe dry weather conditions, due to  not being able to engage in cultivation activities. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to provide relief measures for total 451,224 families, comprising of the farmer families who cultivate paddy and other crops and could not cultivate the last three seasons consecutively due to dry weather conditions, families who could not engage in inland fishing industry and lost their livelihood due to dry weather conditions and the labour families engaged in agriculture, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-02-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2018-10-02",
    "description": "The Parliamentary Programme for the Budget Debate - 2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9265",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, informed the Cabinet that it has been proposed to present the Budget (Budget speech/the second reading of the Budget) in Parliament on 05th November, 2018 and the Second Reading Debate from 07th to 14th November and the Committee Stage debate (the third reading of the Budget) from 15th November to 08th December, in accordance with the Parliamentary Programme pertaining to the Financial Year 2019."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-02-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2018-10-02",
    "description": "Construction of rural bridges for the benefit of the beneficiaries in model \tvillages in the Hambanthota District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9266",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to implement 06 projects, pertaining to the  construction of the bridge across Kirama Oya in Katuwana, Batagassa, Youth Service Bridge across Kirama Ara in Handugala, Kammale Ferry Bridge across Urubokka Oya in Katuwana, bridge across Thundoala connecting Kohamporuwa and Siyambalamuraya, bridge across Kirama Oya in Beliatta along the Angulmaduwa - Aranwela road and fly over across Tangalle - Kadurupokuna road under the 'Nagamu Purawara' Programme to facilitate the beneficiaries of the model villages which are to be commenced in the villages with inadequate infrastructure facilities in the Hambantota District, for them to gain easy access to the \tcommon urban amenities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Strengthening the functioning of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9267",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption plays a vital role in maintaining and improving the fiscal discipline in the Public sector. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the Training Programme formulated to provide specialized   training to the Officers of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption with a view to strengthening the state economy by further improving the fiscal discipline, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Amending the Parliament (Powers and Privileges) Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9268",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister, to amend the Parliament (Powers and Privileges) Act, to declare and define the privileges, immunities and powers of Parliament and its Members, to secure the freedom of speech and debate or proceedings in Parliament, to provide for the punishment for the breaches of Parliamentary privileges and to provide protection to persons employed in the publication of Papers, Minutes, Votes or Proceedings of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Minimizing the damages caused to the Environmental systems due to the                   fragmentation of lands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9269",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several issues have emerged in fragmentation of lands for housing constructions; other purposes and commencing housing projects due to the non adherence of guidelines and the procedure for approval to be followed to minimize the adverse impacts caused to the environment, even though such procedures are in existence. Therefore, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, on the measures to be taken for the optimum utilization of state and private lands by minimizing the said issues, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Promotion for the establishment of  network of Temperature Controlled Warehouses/ Cold Storages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9270",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his\tcapacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to launch a\tproject for the promotion of private investments for the establishment of a\tnetwork of Temperature Controlled Warehouses/Cold Storages in crop\tproducing and fishing areas as a remedial measure to the severe issues faced by \tthose who cultivate fruit and vegetable as well as fishermen and other\tsmall and medium scale producers in post production operations in view of\tminimizing the fluctuation of prices of such production, was approved by the\tCabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Construction of Rural Bridges",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9271",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has identified the need to construct 4,000 rural bridges in order to improve the economic development of the rural areas and to minimize the disparities existing in the Divisional development between Provinces.  In this context, 1,000 bridges have been constructed by now under the Rural Bridges Construction Project with foreign financial assistance. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to enter into Agreements to secure the additional funds necessary for the construction of a further 250 rural bridges under the original project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Census of Population and Housing - 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9272",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Census and Statistics has planned to conduct the next census of population held once in 10 years, in the year 2021. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to conduct the listing stage of the census of population and housing in the year 2020 and the enumeration and data dissemination stages in the year 2021, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Improvement of call connectivity of mobile phone calls and efficiencies in data transfers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9273",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mobile Operators are faced with the challenge of supplying a more qualitative service to their customers due to lack of antenna coverage for the mobile phones in Colombo and other areas. Accordingly, as a solution for the issue, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies and Economic Affairs, to formulate a mechanism to install roof top antennas in strategic locations of Colombo and the suburbs with the approval of the Telecommunication Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Report on Public Sector Cadre for the Second Quarter of the year 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9274",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Report on public sector cadre for the second quarter of the year 2018 submitted by  Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, was presented for the attention of the Cabinet. In terms of the information contained in the said Report, the Cabinet noted that 1,370,885 persons are employed in the public sector comprising of Ministries, Departments, Provincial Councils, Public Corporations, Statutory Boards and Government owned Companies by the second quarter of the year 2018,  that officers in the cadre of certain Public Corporations and Boards are engaged in projects for  more than 05 years without formal approval and that the attention of the Government should be focused when taking decisions on creating additional posts in the education and the health sectors in the public sector in a situation where the contribution of the private sector in the education and the health sectors has rapidly increased."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Obtaining approval for the Gazette Notifications published under the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9275",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Gazette Notification No.2079/32 published to revise the customs duty imposed on the importation of Beedi Leaves, to create new National Sub Division Customs Codes to identify the foods with artificial sugar and the Gazette Notification No.2080/42 published to grant duty free concessions under the Free Trade Agreement in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notifications published under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007, for the approval of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9276",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Eight (08) Gazette Notifications issued during the period from 31st May 2018 to 07th September 2018, to amend the Special Commodity Levy ratio  in order to keep stable the market price of essential food items, provide goods to the consumer without a shortage, protecting the local farmers, facilitating the consumers to pay a consolidated levy instead of various types of taxes and to extend the period for Special Commodity Levy at the same rates, for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Approval for the submission of the Gazette Notifications under the Excise \t(Special Provisions) Act, No.13 of 1989",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9277",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Excise (Special Provisions) Act, No.13 of 1989, any Notification issued by the Gazette Notifications issued under the said Act, should be presented in Parliament within 04 months from the date of publication of such Notification. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to present the Gazette Notification No.2079/58 to revise the Excise duty imposed on the amount of sugar added in some sweetened beverages, the Gazette Notification No.2080/31 for removing the condition to release motor vehicles from the Sri Lanka Customs on or before 30th April 2018, the Gazette Notification No.2082/11 for the revision of Excise duty on Cigarettes and the Gazette Notification Nos.2082/10 and 2083/2 for the revision of Excise Tax on motor vehicles with an engine capacity below 1000 CC, which have been issued by now, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Loan scheme for the installation of the Rooftop Solar Power Generation Systems under the Solar Power Generation Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9278",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposed loan scheme will be operated for supporting the 'Sooryabala Sangrama Programme' implemented with the objective of supplying 200MW by the year 2020 and 1000 MW by the year 2025 to the national grid through the installation of the Solar Power generation systems on every household and commercial / factory buildings. As such, it has been proposed to provide financial assistance under this programme for the installation of Solar Power generation in households and commercial / factory buildings. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to secure the necessary funds for the implementation of this project and to enter into sub loan agreements with the participatory financial institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Introduction of a new Bill to substitute the Sri Lanka Code for the Protection, Promotion and Support of Breastfeeding and marketing the designated products",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9279",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been ensured that breastfeeding contributes strongly for the achievement of optimum physical health, nutrition and the cognitive development in children and to reduce malnutrition as well as the prevention of non\u2011communicable diseases in later life. Sri Lanka is also one of the first countries of the world that adopted the International Code on Breast Milk substitutes according to the World Health Convention in 1981 and has gained the first place in  breast feeding status according to the Report of the World  Breastfeeding Trend Initiative. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a new Bill with a strong legal frame, to address the issues caused by the milk food industry for the infants and children, the promotion of commercial complementary foods and also for the prevention of the spread of unhealthy food habits, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Construction of a Palliative Care Centre in Anuradhapura to provide care for the Patients with Kidney Disease and Cancer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9280",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Shanthi Foundation' in Australia has agreed to construct a Palliative Care Centre in the Anuradhapura town as a donation for the terminally ill patients with Chronic Kidney Disease and Cancer. Under the proposed Centre, it has been planned to construct a Palliative Care Unit for the indoor patients, Out Door Patient Clinics, a Home based Palliative Care Unit and a Training and Research Unit. In this context, a Memorandum of Understanding has been signed between the 'Shanthi Foundation' in Australia and the Ministry of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine for the establishment and the maintenance of the proposed Palliative Care Centre. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition and Indigenous Medicine, for the establishment and maintenance of the said Palliative Care Centre, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Construction of the proposed Multipurpose Building adjoining the Beach Park at 'Crow Island', Mattakkuliya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9281",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to providing space to persons living in the Crow Island area of Mattakkuliya for their public activities, it has been proposed to construct a Multipurpose building adjacent to the Beach Park constructed therein, with the assistance of the World Bank. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Lasantha Alagiyawanna, the Acting Minister of Megapolis and Western Development, to construct the Multipurpose building with a floor area of 14,500 sq.ft. in a land of 65 perches in extent, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Cooperation between Sri Lanka and China",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9282",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka and China entered into a mutual cooperation for the betterment of the plantation industry of both countries. The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding to develop tea, rubber and coconut in the plantation sector as the first step of the said cooperation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Formulating a methodology for the frugal consumption of electricity",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9283",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Electricity access in Sri Lanka has been developed up to 100% and  required measures have been taken by the Government to provide electricity during the 24 hours uninterruptedly. However,  the cost incurred for generating electricity can be minimized with the frugal consumption of electricity and thereby reducing the fuel consumption incurred annually. As such, the Joint Proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Ranjith Siyambalapitiya, the Minister of Power and Renewable Energy and Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Mass Media, to appoint an Officials' Committee with the Chairmanship of the Secretary, Ministry of Power and Renewable Energy to propose a practical mechanism for the frugal consumption of electricity, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Rehabilitation of Feeder Tanks under Giant's tank",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9284",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Giant's Tank in the Mannar District which has 162 feeder tanks expands over an area of 3,800 hectares. For almost 03 decades, maintenance and rehabilitation works in feeder tanks of the Giant's tank have not been properly carried out due to the conflict situation which prevailed in the past.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Duminda Dissanayake, the Minister of Irrigation and Water Resources & Disaster Management, to secure required funds for the rehabilitation of 40 feeder tanks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Renovation of 'I, H and N' buildings of the Anderson Flats",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9285",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- A total of 144 housing units of 'I,H and N' buildings consisting of 48 housing\tunits in each building are used as official quarters of the Inspectors of Police\tand the junior grade officers. These houses are nearly 50 years old and\taccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the\tMinister of Public Administration & Management and Law & Order, to secure\trequired funds for immediate renovation of these buildings, was approved by\tthe Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Extending the beneficiary base of the 'Sonduru Piyasa' Concessionary Loan Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9286",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and\tConstruction, in order to extend the beneficiary base by increasing the\texisting floor area of the house to be eligible under 'Sonduru Piyasa'\tConcessionary Loan Scheme from 1000sq.ft. to 1500sq.ft., was approved by \tthe Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Social Integration of the Export Village Programme through the Model Village Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9287",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that the persons living in the Model Villages can reach the economic and environmental development through the Export Village Programme implemented by the Government. The livelihood development facilities can be provided to the beneficiaries by providing planting material, knowledge and other technical assistance to those living in such Model Villages, required for the collective cultivation of selected export crops or the assistance required in the commencement of a manufacturing industry. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing and Construction, to implement the Export Village Programme in the Model Villages, in association with the Ministry of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Amending the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 for the appointment of Justices of the Peace for Administrative Districts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9288",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to publish the draft Bill prepared by amending the section 45 of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 by incorporating provisions to enable the Justices of the Peace to be appointed for the Administrative Districts instead of the Judicial Zones, Districts and Divisions which was adopted in making such appointments, in the Government Gazette and to present the same thereafter in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Renovation of the Courts Complexes and the Official Residences",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9289",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Colombo Commercial High Court building and the building of the Judicial Services Commission are maintained in old building complexes of historical value and the immediate renovation has been identified in view of their antiquity. The judicial official residences in Colombo as well as the buildings belonging to the District/Magistrate's Courts in Chilaw have also been identified as buildings which require immediate renovation. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to have such construction activities carried out by the government construction institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Stabilization of the land prone to landslide risk where the Kegalle Court Complex is located",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9290",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The land where the Kegalle Court Complex is located comprising of buildings of more than 80 years seems at risk of landslide. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to secure funds for the stabilization of the land preventing such risk, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-025-en",
    "num": "25",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Release of land in the Northern and Eastern Provinces for resettlement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9291",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Action is being taken to release the private lands to the owners of such lands taken into custody of the Tri\u2011Forces during the period of conflict in the Northern and Eastern Provinces. In terms of the above, it has been planned to release a block of land 23 acres in extent in Mullikulam, Mannar, a block of land 53 acres in extent in Mullivaikal, Mullaitivu held in the custody of the Sri Lanka Navy and a block of land 03 acres in extent in Thoppur, Trincomalee where the 224 Brigade Headquarters of the Sri Lanka Army has been established, to their original owners. Also, in order to enable the people to be resettled in those areas to maintain sustainable livelihood activities, 03 small tanks so identified are to be renovated while developing the infrastructure facilities in such areas and handing them over to the original owners. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. D.M. Swaminathan, the Minister of Resettlement, Rehabilitation, Northern Development & Hindu Religious Affairs, to re\u2011establish such facilities enabling to release the lands being occupied by the Tri\u2011Forces and to secure the funds required for the development of infrastructure facilities in the areas, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "The development project in the Kataragama Sacred Area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9292",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is identified that vehicle parking facilities, sanitary facilities, drainage facilities, solid waste disposal facilities and lodging facilities in the Kataragama town should be further improved, for the convenience of the local and as well as foreign pilgrims who visit the sacred area of Kataragama to pay their homage. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayake, the Minister of Youth Affairs, Project Management and Southern Development, to implement the development project in the Kataragama sacred area providing with facilities such as common amenities, police posts, vehicle parks, protective walls, rest rooms and improved road networks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "National Information and Cyber Security Strategy of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9293",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to implement the Cyber Security Strategy over a period of 05 years from 2019 - 2023. This strategy aims at creating a resilient Cyber Security Eco System that will enable the Citizens of Sri Lanka and other parties to improve their livelihoods by deriving the benefits of digital technologies.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, the Minister of Telecommunication, Digital Infrastructure and Foreign Employment, to implement the Cyber Security Strategy designed with the participation of the experts in the field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "National Policy for the Senior Citizens of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9294",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Out of the total population of Sri Lanka 12.4% or 2.6 million people are in the age category of senior citizens over 60 years and by the year 2020, it is anticipated that the population will increase to about 16.3%. The government has adopted various measures for the welfare and the protection of the elderly population. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Social Welfare and Primary Industries, to implement the National Policy prepared for the livelihood  development and the protection of the rights of the elderly people in collaboration with the relevant institutions to develop the situation further, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-029-en",
    "num": "29",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Implementation of the National Information Technology initiative for export development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9295",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Budget of 2018 had proposed to provide the necessary facilities for the Export Managers of the Information Technologies/Exporters in the Business Process Management, by the implementation of an export growth initiative as a promotional strategy for the development of exports within a period of 03 years from the year 2018 to 2020. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to implement the Information Technology Initiative Programme so designed, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-030-en",
    "num": "30",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Setting up a Business Centre in Jaffna for empowering new entrepreneurs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9296",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to bring about a sustainable development in the Northern area by creating entrepreneurs equipped with information technology and generating new employment opportunities and income sources. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrema, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to set up a centre in Jaffna with the financial assistance of the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of India to empower the new entrepreneurs to provide required services, enabling the professional services, enterprises and entrepreneurs to easily and cost effectively set up their offices, so as to have quick access to the export market, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2018-10-16-031-en",
    "num": "31",
    "date_str": "2018-10-16",
    "description": "Amending the Shrama Vasana Fund Act, No.12 of 1998",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9297",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2018-10-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravindra Samaraweera, the Minister of Labour & Trade Union Relations, to publish the draft bill drafted to amend the Shrama Vasana Fund Act, No.12 of 1998 so as to make provisions for further promotion of the Shrama Vasana Lottery which contributes to the Shrama Vasana Fund that provides diverse relief to the employees of Sri Lanka, in the Government Gazette and present the same thereafter in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
