    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-07",
    "decision_details_body": "Approval was granted at the Cabinet meeting held last week for the preparation of the Annual Budget for the year 2019, with a view to strengthening the Government Fiscal Consolidation Programme which is being carried out presently and to enable to achieve the mid term Government fiscal targets planned to be attained by the year 2021. As such, it has been planned to re\u2011present a new Appropriation Bill incorporating the Government expenditure as well scheduled to be incurred under the Vote on Accounts during the first 04 months of the Financial Year 2019.\n\nIn accordance with the Appropriation Bill so drafted, the expenditure to be incurred for general services amounts to Rs.2,312 billion comprising of Rs.1,436 billion for recurrent expenditure and Rs.876 billion for capital expenditure. In addition, Rs.2,232 billion has been set apart for the expenses already authorized to be charged on the Consolidated Fund such as Public Debt Servicing and Widows and Orphans Pensions. Similarly, inclusive of a provision of Rs.06 billion for the Government Advance Account, the total expenditure anticipated to be incurred for the year 2019 is Rs.4,550 billion. According to the prevailing tax rates structure, the Government revenue and the foreign grants for the year 2019 will be around Rs.2,390 billion. Further, the total borrowing requirement from both foreign and domestic sources will be Rs.2,160 billion. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media, to present the draft Appropriation Bill for the year 2019 in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-07-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-01-07",
    "description": "Granting of relief to the people in the Northern Province affected by the floods",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9421",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the inclement weather conditions which affected the Island by the activation of the North East monsoon during the past days, 123,862 persons of 39,895 families in 13 Divisional Secretary's Divisions including Kilinochchi, Mullaitivu and Jaffna in the Northern Province have been affected and 474 houses have been completely destroyed while 4,522 houses have been partially damaged in the Kilinochchi and Mullaitivu Districts. The required funds and materials have been released to the District Secretaries to grant an advance of Rs.10,000/- for the house owners to do the necessary renovations and cleaning required to be done urgently, until the completion of the payment of the due compensation after a proper assessment. Similarly, action is also being taken to provide a dry ration for a period of two weeks for the affected families until their lives are brought back to normal. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranjith Madduma Bandara, the Minister of Public Administration & Disaster Management, to secure the funds necessary to provide further relief for those affected due to the said disaster situation, to carry out the renovations of the damaged infrastructure facilities and common buildings and also for the damages caused to agricultural crops and livestock, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-14-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-01-14",
    "description": "High Priority Economic and Social Empowerment and Infrastructure Development Projects in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9422",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the lapses in the development in the Northern and Eastern provinces for a period of more than three decades, a special project has been proposed to be implemented to accelerate the development in those areas by improving the economic and social infrastructure facilities and facilitating the livelihood development. Accordingly, the programmes will be implemented in such sectors paying special attention towards agricultural, industrial, fisheries and service sectors. It has also been scheduled to provide facilities related to livelihood under this project such as rural roads, anchorages and landing sites, jetties, accesses between islands and main islands, agricultural equipment, agro wells, fishing boats and engines, self\u2011employment related equipment and technology, market facilities, storage and related infrastructure facilities.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to secure a sum of Rs.2,000 million for the expeditious implementation of this project through the 04 sectors of economic infrastructure facilities, social infrastructure facilities, livelihood and self\u2011employment and small industries and enterprises, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-01-14",
    "description": "Entering into 06 Memoranda of Understanding between Sri Lanka and Philippines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9423",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet was granted to the proposals submitted for the purpose of entering into 06 Memoranda of Understanding specified below in view of the Bilateral Friendship, Cooperation and Development during the visit of         H. E. the President in Philippines. \n\n\tMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the field of Tourism \u2011 The proposal made by Hon. John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs, to enter into a bi\u00adlateral Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) in the field of tourism between Sri Lanka and Philippines on improvement of the cooperation in Research & Development, Education and Training, tourism promotion programmes, investments and the other sectors as determined by both parties. \n\n\nImprovement of the cooperation in the field of foreign employment \u2011 The proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, Minister of Telecommunication, Foreign Employment and Sports, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Philippines and Sri Lanka for the improvement of the co\u2011operation in the fields of welfare and protection of rights of workers, enhancement of productivity, working standards and professional health and security, providing training for migrant workers and certification and legal aid for safeguarding the workers rights between both countries. \t\n\nMemorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Cooperation in the Field of Higher Education \u2011 The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Wate Supply and Higher Education, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Commission on Higher Education of the Republic of the Philippines and the Ministry of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education of Sri Lanka with a view to strengthening the cooperation in the field of Higher Education between the two countries. \n\t\nEntering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) covering agriculture and the related fields \u2011 \nThe proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Philippines and Sri Lanka for the improvement of the cooperation in the fields of crop cultivation, fisheries industry, livestock control and poultry farming, agri\u2011processing and value addition, distribution and marketing of products.\n \nProviding facilities for the Researchers of the National Agricultural Research System (NARS) to follow foreign Postgraduate Degree Courses \u2011 The proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Los Banos University of the Philippines, to provide for the researchers of the NARS with facilities to follow foreign postgraduate degrees. \n\nEnhancement of cooperation between the two countries in the field of defence \u2011 The proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and Philippines on the enhancement of cooperation in the fields of defence, military education and training, exchange of defence delegations, joint exercises, goodwill visits and conference"
  },
