    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet of Ministers had been granted previously to declare the Tripitaka which includes all preachings of Buddha as a National Heritage of Sri Lanka and to officially declare the same by the Government and reprint the Tripitaka and other related work under the supervision of the Ministry of Buddhasasana. Accordingly, on 05th January 2019, the Tripitaka was declared as a National Heritage at the Matale Alu Viharaya. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to move a resolution in Parliament to confirm  the declaration so made and the necessity to take appropriate action to declare the Tripitaka as a World Heritage, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Second National Action Plan of the Open Government Partnership (2018 - 2020)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9441",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Open Government Partnership is a multilateral initiative that is aimed at securing a concrete commitment from the Governments on policies to promote transparency, empower  citizens, fight corruption and harness new technologies to strengthen governance. Under the Open Government Partnership (OGP), all  the participating countries are obliged to develop an Action Plan inclusive of their voluntary commitments spanning for 02 years. Approval of the Cabinet had been granted previously for the implementation of the First 02 year Action Plan of the OGP (2016-2018) of the Government of Sri Lanka.  \n\nThe Second National Action Plan has been prepared consisting of 14 transformative commitments and 61 milestones ranging from enhancing the rights of the disabled community, promoting accountability through asset declarations and provision of improved services for disaster management. With the implementation of the Second National Action Plan, it is anticipated that it will enhance the citizens participation in the governance processes and transparency and thereby increasing the accountability of the Government towards its citizenry. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the Second National Action Plan (2018-2020) in collaboration with the relevant Government Institutions and to appoint an Inter Ministerial Steering Committee to monitor the progress and to provide guidance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Police Reforms",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9442",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Police Reforms Committee comprising of the experts was appointed to make recommendations for reforming the Sri Lanka Police, in order to update the present police methodologies and performance to cater to the present trends, relatively to the public demand for an efficient and accountable professional police service. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to implement the Police Reforms Action Plan containing the recommendations made by the said Committee in the areas of improving  professionalism and standards of the Sri Lanka Police, enhancing accountability and transparency, practicing and upholding human rights, preventing and controlling crime and reducing fear of crime and increasing the public trust and confidence in the Police, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Renovation of the three storey building where the Ahangama Police \tStation is housed",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9443",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ahangama Police Station, which extends its services to the people living in 35 Grama Niladhari Divisions, encounters difficulties while providingservices due to the dilapidated condition and non renovation for a long period of the three storey building in which the police station is housed. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to allocate Rs.33.4 million for the renovations and improvements required to be carried out in the said building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Further extending of the financial facilities provided under the 'Enterprise Sri Lanka' Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9444",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that there is a great demand for the loan schemes implemented under the Enterprise Sri Lanka programme due to the  concessionary terms and conditions of such loan schemes. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media, to implement this programme covering the groups such as migrant workers with the anticipation of concessionary housing loans, private bus owners with the expectation of deploying luxury city buses instead of normal buses, investors who are looking forward to constructing and improving elderly care centres and three-wheeler owners willing to change over to the taxi service that have not so far been covered by the loan schemes implemented under this programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Amendment to the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002 for the provision of tax reliefs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9445",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Value Added Tax (VAT) exemption that was applicable on certain goods and services including importation of air crafts and accessories, sawn timber and fabrics and sale of condominium housing units has been removed under the Value Added Tax (Amendment) Act, No.25 of 2018. However, considering the requests made by the relevant stakeholders in these fields, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media, to amend the Value Added Tax (VAT) Act enabling to re-introduce the tax exemptions imposed on importation of air crafts and accessories, sawn timber and fabrics and locally manufactured Rice Bran oil and with a view to protecting the Government revenue and enable the Minister to determine and prescribe by regulation the basis for the imposition of VAT on certain goods,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Obtaining approval of Parliament for the Gazette Notifications published \tunder the Revenue Protection Act, No 19 of 1962",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9446",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Gazette \tNotifications issued under the Revenue Protection Act, No 19 \tof 1962, revising the import duty should be presented in Parliament for \tapproval. As such, the proposal made by Hon.\tMangala Samaraweera, the \tMinister of Finance & Mass Media to present the Gazette Notifications No. \t2079/32, 2092/8 and 2097/36 issued for introducing new H.S code \tand duty \tenabling to receive concessions to the local manufactures in \tlevying import \tduty and revising the import duty on petrol for the adjustment of the fuel price \tin the \tcountry relatively to the decrease in fuel price in the international \tmarket, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Paddy Purchasing Programme for Maha Season 2018/2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9447",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Harvesting of paddy for Maha Season 2018/2019 is due to be commenced and  it has been planned to implement the Paddy Purchasing Programme in 18 districts during this season in order to maintain a price stability for paddy and to ensure a reasonable price for the paddy farmers. As such paddy is to be purchased under a guaranteed price of Rs 41.00 per kg of Samba paddy varieties and  Rs 38.00 per kg of Nadu paddy variety. Accordingly, the proposal  made by Hon.P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to secure funds required for the Paddy Marketing Board to implement the Paddy Purchasing Programme for the Maha Season, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Reimbursement of the cultivation losses caused by the 'Fall Armyworm' Pest under the Compulsory Cultivation Insurance Scheme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9448",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the Fall Armyworm menace which is rapidly spreading in the major agricultural areas of Sri Lanka from recent times, the farmers have to face an unexpected economic loss. Under the present Compulsory Insurance Scheme, an Insurance Cover is not available for cultivation losses caused by this kind of  pest calamity and therefore, the farmers have to obtain the Insurance Cover under an additional cover through the payment of a small premium. However, it is observed that, a majority of farmers who have commenced cultivation in the Maha Season of 2018/19 have not obtained this additional Insurance Cover and as such, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to reimburse the cultivation losses caused by the Fall Armyworm Pest under the Compulsory Cultivation Insurance Scheme and to secure the additional provision required for the purpose from the Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Simplifying the Scheme for Registration of Exporters",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9449",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is observed that a long procedure has to be followed for the registration of Exporters under the registration process currently adopted by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board which has been introduced in 1985 for the registration of Exporters since it has be to operated by collaborating with 06 different agencies and that a period from 01 to 03 weeks is taken for the registration of exporters.  At the same time, studies have shown that a further period of 02 weeks to 04 weeks is required in addition to the period given above for enterprises which need permits or licenses for the Export activities.  In order to make the registration process convenient, the Sri Lanka Export Development Board has already taken steps to prepare a mechanism in collaboration with the institutions such as the Sri Lanka Customs and the  Department of Inland Revenue which operate similar databases with exporter details. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Malik Samarawickrama, Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade, to revoke the registration scheme presently adopted by the Sri Lanka Export Development Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Plant and Design Build Contract for the Civil, Machinery and Electricity \t(M&E) Work of the Valachchenai Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9450",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education, to award the Plant and Design Build contract for the civil, machinery and electrical work of the Valachchenai Water Supply Project to be implemented covering the 06 Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Koralaipattu, Koralaipattu West, Koralaipattu Central, Koralaipattu South, Koralaipattu North and Eravurpattu to M/s China Geo Engineering Company Limited & M/s China National Aero Technology International Engineering Corporation \u2011 JV, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee (CANC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Construction of a Vehicle and Powertrain Laboratory at the Department of Mechanical Engineering of the Faculty of Engineering, University of Moratuwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9451",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to construct a Vehicle and Powertrain Laboratory at the Department of Mechanical Engineering of the Faculty of Engineering, University of Moratuwa, with a view to facilitating the emerging needs of the local automobile industry, establishing a state of the art and automotive laboratory, producing engineers well equipped with modern knowledge and conducting the research, survey and development capabilities related to the automotive environmental issues. The Raiffeisen Bank International AG of Austria has given its concurrence to provide concessional financing for this project under a soft loan scheme. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education, to obtain a detailed project proposal from M/s AVL List GmbH who is the sole Austrian Manufacturer and supplier operative in this field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Procurement for the Supply of 12,000 MT of Maize required for Thriposha Production",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9452",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine to award the contract for the purchase of 12,000 MT of Maize, which is one of the main ingredients used for manufacturing Thriposha for Sri Lanka Thriposha Limited, to M/s KST Evergreen (Pvt)Ltd., for a sum of Rs 670.8 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Kalu Ganga Development Project for the prevention of flood and restraining  Salinity intrusion and  for the Supply of Drinking Water to the Hambantota District by diverting Kalu Ganga",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9453",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- A feasibility study has been carried out to implement the Kalu Ganga  development project at an investment of Rs 123 billion, with the main objective of preventing the damages caused in the Ratnapura and Kalutara districts due to the overflowing of the Kalu Ganga during the rainy season, restraining salinity intrusion in the supply of drinking water caused by the flowing of salinity up to 18 km upstream from the river mouth and providing drinking water to the Hambantota district, by diverting Kuda Ganga, which is a tributary of the Kalu Ganga. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development to call for proposals for Expression of Interest from the International Construction Companies which can implement the project with foreign investment, to call for project proposals from eligible construction companies and to appoint Cabinet Appointed Committees to evaluate them, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-22-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-01-22",
    "description": "Provision of drinking water for model villages and reawakened \tsettlements \tin Chronic Kidney Disease of Unknown Etiology (CKDU) \taffected areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9454",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet had been granted previously to utilize the funds allocated to the model village and reawakened settlements project to provide drinking water to the said villages in the CKDU affected areas. In this respect, the joint proposal made by Hon.Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Wate Supply and Higher Education and Hon.Sajith Premadasa, the\tMinister of Housing,  Construction  and  Cultural  Affairs,  to  implement  the\tproject for improving the Kirindi Oya water treatment plant, enabling to\tprovide drinking water for 703 families in 18 model villages located   in Lunugamwehera and Thissamaharama Divisional Secretariat Divisions in the Hambantota District, with an investment of Rs. 298 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Controlling of the quantum of waste accumulated in the coast and the ocean through waterways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9455",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been revealed that 90% of the waste accumulated in the coast and the ocean is generated on account of human activities and industries carried out on land and as a result of which, many social, economic and environmental issues have emerged. Action is being taken to obtain the 'Blue Flag' Certificate issued by the Foundation for Environmental Education of Denmark pertaining to the coastal line of Sri Lanka which is treated as an international standard for the assurance of the quality of the coastal line. In addition, it is also necessary to maintain a clean coastal line and ocean for achieving the goal of attracting 4 million of tourists to Sri Lanka by the year 2020 as the coastal and ocean related areas provide around 70% of the contribution to the in\u2011bound tourism industry while safeguarding the place secured by Sri Lanka as the world's best tourism destination. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to implement the programmes at District level for the maintenance of waterways free of waste, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Forest plantation for timber production",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9456",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the timber requirement in Sri Lanka increases on an annual basis and in order to coincide with this, it has been proposed to increase the productivity of the forest plantation presently carried out for timber and establish new forest plantation. Lands in extent of 500 hectares have been identified in the Districts of Vavuniya, Kilinochchi, Mullaitivu and Mannar for the establishment of the new forest plantation. Through the implementation of this project, it is expected to generate employment opportunities at divisional level and contribute for the control of global warming by upgrading the forest layer, in addition to meeting the demand for timber. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment, to secure the funds required for the implementation of this project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Accelerated implementation of the resettlement activities in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9457",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has focused its attention to carry out the resettlement activities expeditiously in the Northern and Eastern Provinces affected due to conflicts by establishing permanent shelter, sanitation facilities, water supply and economic infrastructure facilities such as roads and electricity connections and educational and health facilities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to construct 4,750 housing units under the owner driven housing programme, to improve the essential economic and social infrastructure facilities in such areas and to upgrade the Thickkam Distilleries for the revival of palmyrah related industry, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Adopting the concept of Managing for Development Results (MfDR) as a planning and management technique at the Public institutions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9458",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The developed as well as the developing countries adopt the concept of Managing for Development Results (MfDR) as a modern planning and management technqiue in their public sector management cycle. Through this cycle, the Public management activities are conducted aiming at Key Performance Indicators (KPI) targeted towards the National Sustainable Development. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to institutionalize the process of Managing for Development Results (MfDR) as an initiative in 05 Ministries and 02 Provincial Councils in the form of a pilot project andadopting this concept covering all Public institutions based on its success, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Development of the Palaly (Kankesanthurai) Airport for the operation of Regional Commercial Flights",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9459",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need to develop the Palaly Airport has been recognized for the operation of internal commercial flights with a view to promoting the tourism industry. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to make use of the Palaly Airport for the operation of internal commercial passenger flights according to a schedule and to carry out the development activities required for the Palaly Airport expeditiously by the Sri Lanka Air Force at an investment of Rs.1,950 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Payment of Compensation to the persons affected by the construction of the Kandy Multimodal Transport Terminal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9460",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The project for the construction of the Kandy Multimodal Transport Terminal has been identified for implementation under the Strategic Cities Development Project. The project which is to be implemented at an investment of Rs.11,700 million, is expected to contribute towards the establishment of an environmental friendly transport system that enhances the quality of life of the people in the Kandy City and its cultural heritage. However, it has been found that implementation of this project would deprive the livelihood of 820 persons including businessmen engaged in different entrepreneurial activities in the area. Therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development, to pay compensation as recommended by the Entitlement Assessment Committee appointed to determine the exact compensation amounts to be paid to the persons affected by the said Project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Providing facilities to improve the productivity of the Tea and Coconut Smallholder Sectors",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9461",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that the contribution made by the Tea and Coconut smallholder Sectors to the total tea and coconut production towards the sectors is being increased during the past few years and it has also been identified that there is a tendency for further increasing the said contribution. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries to allocate the funds required to increase the productivity of Tea and Coconut smallholder Sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Modernization of the Seed and Planting Materiel Supply System of the Department of Agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9462",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Certified seed and planting materiel of paddy, other field crops and vegetables are received from 27 seed farms and the Contract Seed Production Programmes functioning under the Seed and Planting Material Development Centre. However, it has been found difficult to achieve the targets for the production of basic seeds due to the lack of proper irrigation facilities, lack of mechanization, inadequate storage facilities, poor transportation facilities and the limited essential structural facilities available in the farms for production activities. Therefore, a proposal has been made to carry out the functions such as mechanization of seed processing, establishing a combined drying and processing complex at Mahailuppallama, Ampara and Aluttarama farms, purchasing new technical equipment to select other food crop seeds for Palwehera and Bataatha farms, establishing four seed stores in Rahangala, Seethaeliya, Bataatha and Ampara farms, improving of the transportation system in Seed and Planting Material Development Centres and extending the Lak Krushi dealers' network island-wide. As such, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to allocate Rs.335 million required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Food safety enhancement through the establishment of a Sustainable Agriculture Development Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9463",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Centre of Excellence for Organic Agriculture (CEOA) at Makandura conducts research and technology transfer on organic agriculture and organic fertilizer while the Regional Agriculture Research and Development Centre (RARDC) at Makandura conducts research in several other sectors such as crop improvement and plant nutrition. It has been found necessary to establish an Eco-friendly Agriculture Development and Research Centre at present and as such, the proposal made by Hon.\tP. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to secure funds required to establish the Sustainable Agriculture Development Centre amalgamating the said two centres, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Ensuring the quality of Seeds and Planting Materials",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9464",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that the use of quality seeds and planting material will increase the quantity of the harvest from 15% -20%. Therefore, it has been planned to provide the farmers with processing equipment and services necessary for producing quality seeds, facilities required for the improvement and proper maintenance of mother plant gardens, the ways of popularizing new plant varieties and approved imported planting materials, ensuring the quality of seeds and planting materials that are available in the market and adopting the multi-dimensional media propaganda methods to educate the farmers and producers and expanding the activities of planting material production industry. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to secure funds required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Strengthening of the mechanism for implementing and regulating the \tControl of Pesticides Act, No.33 of 1980",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9465",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The task of regulating the use of pesticides in Sri Lanka is carried out by the Control of Pesticides Act, No.33 of 1980 as amended by the Acts No.06 of 1994 and No.31 of 2011. The number of pesticide products has been increased considerably up to about 700 which prevailed at 70 in the year 1983 when this Act came into operation. Similarly, it has been found necessary to update the management \tof pesticides to coincide with the world trends and the development taking place in the pesticide industry. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural \tEconomic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development to secure funds required for the purpose of strengthening the process of protecting the quality of pesticides compositions to ensure that they conform to the requirement regarding pesticide residues in food crops, ensuring food safety and protection of the \tconsumer from pesticide residues and expanding international recognized conformity analysis facilities, disseminating world trends in agricultural produce and good \tagricultural practices in the country, developing the requisite data systems and administrative structures required for the effective implementation of field monitoring not only the pesticides in agricultural sector but also in other sectors related thereto, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Enhancing the food safety through the establishment of a National Level \tAnalytical laboratory",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9466",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to establish a laboratory with modern facilities with a view to regulating the inputs and excessive usage of chemical fertilizer, organic manures and pesticides and monitoring the residues and contaminant levels in food, soil and water. At the same time, it has been proposed to improve the  investigative capability of the laboratory by providing laboratory equipment and facilities, conducting laboratory accreditation and quality assurance, educating the safe and correct use of agricultural inputs and to provide training in the use and issue of agro\u2011chemicals and fertilizers. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to set apart funds required for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Entering into Bilateral Air Services Agreements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9467",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to enhancing the international cooperation in relation to the Air Services, the proposal made by Hon. Arjuna Ranatunga, the Minister of Transport & Civil Aviation, to sign the initialed Air Services Agreements with Afghanistan, the State of Qatar, the State of Israel, and Zimbabwe by an accredited representative of Sri Lanka thereafter implement the said agreements enabling to contribute to the development process of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Amendment to section 45 of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9468",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of section 45 of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978, the power to appoint Justices of the Peace to Judicial Zones, Districts and Divisions has been vested with the Minister in charge of the subject of Justice. Accordingly, Justices of the Peace will be appointed to serve in a judicial zone, district or division as appropriate, taking into consideration the place where such person to be appointed to the said post resides. However, taking into account the difficulties faced by Justices of the Peace in identifying their Judicial Zones due to changes that take place from time to time, the Cabinet approval had been granted previously to amend section 45 of the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 enabling to appoint Justices \tof the Peace for Administrative Districts in place of Judicial Zones, Districts or Divisions. As such, the proposal made by Hon.(Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to publish the draft bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present it in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Establishment of a Tamil Medium National School in the Kelaniya\tEducation Zone",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9469",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mano Ganesan, the Minister of National Integration, Official Languages, Social Progress and Hindu Religious Affairs, to establish a Tamil Medium Hindu National School in the name of Arun Maanikkawaasagam Hindu College in the Kelaniya Education Zone utilizing the property to be vested with the Ministry of Education by way of a Deed of Gift by the Arun Prasanth Foundation with a view to uplifting the educational standard of the Tamil medium students in the Wattala area in Gampaha, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Implementation of the High Priority focused Road Development Projects in the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9470",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has focused its attention for the rehabilitation of the road network in the area and for further enhancing the livelihood of the people living in the Northern and Eastern Provinces and providing them with the necessary facilities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, in his capacity as the Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to award the contract for the rehabilitation of the roads belonging to the Provincial Road Development Department of the Northern Province to the CEC-NEM Joint Venture, the contract for the rehabilitation of the roads belonging to the Local Government Department of the Northern Province to M/s KDE Weerasinghe & Co. Pvt. LTD., the contract for the rehabilitation of the roads belonging to the Road Development Authority within the Eastern Province to the Consulting Engineers & Contractors Pvt. Ltd., the contract for the rehabilitation of the roads belonging to the Provincial Road Development Department of the Eastern Province to Nawaloka Construction Company Pvt. Ltd. and the contract for the rehabilitation of the roads belonging to the Local Government Department of the Eastern Province to M/s Sinohydro Corporation Limited, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Development of the Infrastructure facilities at the Kelaniya, Sri Jayawardenapura, Sabaragamuwa and Moratuwa Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9471",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has focused its attention for the development of the infrastructure facilities of the universities with a view to further enhancing the qualitative aspect of the field of Higher Education. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education, for the implementation of the projects for the construction of a 4 storey hostel building for the students of the University of Kelaniya, construction of 3 stories as Stage I of the project for the 7 storey multi-functional building at the University of Sri Jayawardenapura, Stage I of the project for the construction of the faculty building complex of the Faculty of Agriculture of the Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka, attending to the balance work left at the lecture hall building of the Faculty of Architecture and at the multi\u2011functional building of the Faculty of Engineering at the University of Moratuwa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Improvement of the Horana - Padukka and Habarana - Valachchenai Transmission Network",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9472",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development, to award the contracts for the construction of the Transmission Line of 25 km in length between Horana and Padukka and the Second Circuit Stringing of the Habarana - Valachchenai transmission network, under the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme implemented for the strengthening of the transmission network of the Ceylon Electricity Board, to M/s China National Electric Engineering Co. Ltd., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "The contract for the construction of Transmission Lines and Capacity Enhancement under the National Transmission and Distribution Network Development and Efficiency Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9473",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Transmission and Distribution Network Development and Efficiency Improvement of the electricity Grid has been planned to be implemented under 4 components. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development, to award the contract for the project for construction of Transmission Lines and Capacity Enhancement planned as its component 3, to M/s Kinden Corporation and M/s Kalpatharu Power Transmission Joint Venture of Japan, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Increasing the Handling Capacity of the Coal Yard of the Lakvijaya Power Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9474",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The usage capacity of the coal yard of the Norochcholai Lakvijaya Power Plant is about 742,421 MT and it is sufficient only to store the coal requirement of 3 months. Therefore, it has been planned to increase the storage capacity of the Plant up to 1.21 million MT enabling it to fulfill the coal requirement for 6 months. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development, to award the contract for the purpose to M/s China Machinery Engineering Corporation of China, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-01-29-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2019-01-29",
    "description": "Construction of new paddy stores of the Paddy Marketing Board (PMB) and renovation of its existing stores",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9475",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-01-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- The attention of the Government has been focused to develop the infrastructure facilities in the field of agriculture while improving the agricultural sector, for providing relief to the farmers. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, for the construction of 2 State-of-the-Art paddy stores in the Beliatta and Meegahajandura areas with a capacity of 2,000 MT and to renovate 39 old paddy stores spread over the Island, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Implementation of the National Action Plan for Combating Corruption",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9478",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to formulate a National Action Plan to eradicate corruption, considering the necessity for the implementation of a National Plan applicable in general in regard to all Public Sector Institutions as well as the other institutions for combating bribery and corruption. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to implement the National Action Plan, during the period of 2019\u20112023, formulated for combating bribery and corruption, taking into consideration the views and proposals of all relevant stakeholders, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Implementation of the National Drug Prevention Programme 'A Country Free of Drugs'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9479",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The drug menace has adversely affected the well-being of the society both economically and socially. The National Drug Prevention Policy and the Action Plan was implemented with a view to providing a lasting solution to the drug menace and 'the Country Free of Drugs' programme to create a Nation Free of Drugs is being successfully implemented with the coordination of the Presidential Task Force on Drug Prevention and the contribution of the Sri Lanka Police, the National Dangerous Drugs Control Board and the other relevant institutions. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to  further expand the activities pertaining to 'the Country Free of Drugs', by the establishment of a National Authority for  Rehabilitation of the Persons addicted to drugs and to import modern technology equipment capable of detecting toxic drugs and usage, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Improvements to the building where  the Police Recruitment Division and the Police Information Technology Division are housed",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9480",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Police Recruitment Division and the Police Information Technology Division are housed in the building at the Sri Sambuddha Jayanthi Mawatha, Kirulapone where the Vilasitha Nivasa was situated earlier. In order to prevent the challenges that have to be faced while being engaged in the disposal of official duties, as a result of this building not being renovated for a long time, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to secure a provision of Rs.126.8 million within the Medium\u2011term Budgetary Framework for 2020-2022, to improve and carry out a complete revamp of the building inclusive of the construction of a rain water and waste water drainage system and the re\u2011construction of the water supply system, the sewerage and drainage system and the electric control system, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Providing relief to the personnel of the Tri Forces who have retired from service or vacated their posts as a result of the disability due to terrorist activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9481",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval previously to provide relief to 1,573 members of the Tri\u2011Forces who have retired from service after having completed the due period of service as a result of disability caused due to   terrorist activities and due to lowering of the disability to 50%. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as  the Minister of Defence, to provide relief to a further number of 792 retired similar members of the Tri\u2011Forces as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Providing a plot of land to expand the accommodation facilities of the Ceylon German Technical Training Institute (CGTTI)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9482",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ceylon German Technical Training Institute initiated in the year 1959 under German Aid, currently offers 11 full time courses in the field of Auto Mobile Engineering and allied fields and enrolls around 600 trainees annually. In addition, 42 short\u2011term courses are conducted and around 2000 full time course trainees and a number exceeding 2500 part\u2011time course trainees follow training. This institute is located presently in a land in extent of around 13 acres and it has been planned to provide training opportunities to around further 150 trainees by extending the activities of this institute an establishing new workshops, class rooms and laboratories etc., As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development, Vocational Training & Skills Development and Youth Affairs, to obtain the plot of land situated adjacent to the said institute in extent of 4 acres and 15.5 perches belonging to the Urban Development Authority on lease basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Establishment of a Methodology for the selection of Beneficiaries for Welfare Programmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9483",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to establish a database on welfare beneficiaries in order to create a more transparent system for the selection of beneficiaries eligible to receive benefits under various welfare programmes implemented within the country.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media, to refer the Regulations drafted under section 27 of the Welfare Benefits Act, No.24 of 2002 to the Legal Draftsman, including the provisions such as, the mode of application for obtaining benefits, establishment of  Selection Committees and Appeal Committees, eligibility for such appointments, the responsibilities of such committees, the methodologies to be adopted for ensuring the accuracy of the information provided in the applications, the mode of admission of beneficiaries  to the programme and the procedure adopted in dealing with Appeals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Construction of the Kokilai Bridge and approach roads across Kokilai Lagoon on Mullaitivu - Kokilai - Pulmudai Road",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9484",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to develop  the Mullativu - Kokilai - Pulmudai Road to provide land connectivity on the coastal belt between the Eastern Province and the Northern Province. It is anticipated that the distance between Mullaitivu and Pulmudai will be reduced by around 100 km by the proposed bridge to be constructed across the Kokilai Lagoon. Further, it is proposed to obtain the financial facilities from the CSOB Bank of Czech Republic and a Local Commercial Bank for this project. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media, to conduct loan negotiations with the said Banks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "The Agreement between Sri Lanka and the Government of Ukraine in respect of Taxation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9485",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media to enter into the Agreement at the Government level which is initialed by now at official level, between Sri Lanka and Ukraine for the avoidance of double taxation and prevention of Fiscal Evasion on income in line with the Government Policy for enhancing mutual economic relations between Sri Lanka and Ukraine, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Implementation of the Projects for the years 2019 - 2021 utilizing the grants provided by the Global Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9486",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Global Fund has been established to provide funds for the programmes carried out with the objective of preventing the three infectious diseases namely, HIV AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria which have become a serious health problem affected globally. The Ministry of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine has entered into Agreements to obtain grants worth of US$ 76 million and out of which utilizing US$ 61 million, several projects have been implemented. The Global Fund has allocated a grant of US$ 12.3 million for the period from 2019 - 2021. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine to secure the grant, pertaining to the Agreement entered into, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Implementation of Kolonnawa Strom Water Drainage and Environment Improvement Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9487",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Kolonnawa drainage basin comes under the flood threat annually due to the urbanization that occurred during the last four decades and the absence of an insufficient drainage system in the area. This has become a negative factor  to the future investment planning and for the improvement of infrastructure facilities and economic development. Therefore, measures should be taken to develop Kittampahuwa, Salalihini Mawatha and Danduthota Canals which directly connect to the Kelani river and control the unauthorized constructions and encroachments. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development to implement the Kolonnawa Strom Water Drainage and Environment Improvement Project during the period from 2019 to 2022, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Upgrading the diploma course conducted by Sri Lanka School of Animal Husbandry at Kundasale to obtain the National Vocational Qualification (NVQ) Level  5 and 6",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9488",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- As it is essential to achieve the National Vocational Qualification for all technical courses by the year 2020, all requirements pertaining to the development of syllabi teaching and training modules and the improvement of National Competency Standards have been finalized enabling to upgrade the two year Animal Husbandry Diploma Course conducted by the Department of Animal Production & Health to obtain the National Vocational Qualification (NVQ) Level 5 and 6. Accordingly, it is expected to upgrade the said course as the two and a half year Higher National Diploma in Livestock Production Technology Course. As such, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development to secure funds required for the establishment of an e-learning facility with the required infrastructure and upgrading the training farm and the infrastructure facilities for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "The National Housing Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9489",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been previously granted to revise, the National Housing Policy presently being used so as to reflect within the Vision of the present Government and to focus more attention towards  the issues such as urbanization, impacts of natural disasters and implementation of the concept of Sustainable Human Settlements Development. Accordingly,  the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, \tMinister of \tHousing, Construction and Cultural Affairs on the revised National Housing Policy taking also into account of the assignment of subjects presently to the Ministries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Awarding of the Contract regarding the Supply of Liquefied Petroleum Gas for the year 2019/2020 to the Litro Gas Lanka Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9490",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Litro Gas Lanka Limited is a Government owned company which owns a 70% market share of the Island's Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG), engaged in importing, storing, filling, marketing and selling LPG. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance & Mass Media to award the contract for the procurement of 350,000 MT of LPG as to M/s Oman Trading International Ltd. for the said company to fulfill the country's market needs, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Procurement for the Construction of Buildings for the Outdoor Patients Division, Laboratory, Radiology Unit and Wards at the National Institute of Infectious Diseases (IDH) in Angoda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9491",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to develop the National Institute of Infectious Diseases in Angoda as a state\u2011of\u2011the\u2011art centre which conducts treatment of infectious diseases and training and research activities. In this context, it is proposed to develop it as a Health Service Centre of Excellence with an Outdoor Patient Division, Wards, Clinics, Laboratories and facilities for Radiological diagnosis facilities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine, to award the Procurement to construct buildings for the Outdoor Patients Division (OPD), Laboratory, Radiology Unit and Wards at the National Institute of Infectious Diseases in Angoda to M/s George Steuart Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd., as recommended by the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Procurement of Lubricating Oil for the Barge Mounted Power Plant of the Ceylon Electricity Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9492",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development to award the procurement for the supply of 750,000 liters of Cylinder Lubricating Oil and 175,000 liters of System Lubricating Oil required for the Barge Mounted Power Plant of the Ceylon Electricity Board for the year 2018/2019 to M/s Chevron Lubricants Lanka PLC, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Procurement of Lubricating oil for the Sapugaskanda Power Plant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9493",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development to award the procurement for purchasing 800,000 litres of lubricating oil Taro 40 XL 40 for Pielstick  plant of Sapugaskanda and 300,000 litres of lubricating oil Taro 40 XL 40 for the MAN plant of Sapugaskanda, to M/s Chevron Lubricants Lanka PLC as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Purchase of spare parts necessary for the major Overhauling of the Plants at the Sapugaskanda Power Station according to the prevailing operational pattern",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9494",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Major Overhauling is required in respect of the Engine Nos. 5 to 8 after 12,000 running hours and the Engine Nos. 9 to 12  after 6,000 running hours of the Sapugaskanda Power Station.  Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development, to award the contract for the purchase of the spare parts for the overhauling of the Engines  compulsorily needed after the completion of the said running hours to M/s MAN Energy Solutions SE of Germany, the original manufacturer of these Engines as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Construction of Rural Bridges",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9495",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct 4,000 bridges in the rural areas with the objective of extending the benefits of the national development to the remote areas of the Island as well through the improvement of transportation connectivity by connecting various areas of the Island. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Wajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils & Local Government, to award the contract for the construction of 175 bridges of various sizes, so as to cover the 9 Provinces of the Island to Cleveland Bridge UK Limited in the United Kingdom, for a sum of 37.7 million Sterling Pounds, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-02-05-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2019-02-05",
    "description": "Obtaining Consultancy Services for the Second Integrated Road Investment Programme",
