    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development and Petroleum Resources Development to award the contract for the procurement of Murban Crude oil for a period of 8 months during the year 2019, to M/s Swiss Singapore Overseas Enterprise Pte. Ltd., in accordance with recommendation of the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SSCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-06-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2019-03-06",
    "description": "Declaration of the Thripitaka as a World Heritage",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9585",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- On 05th January 2019, The Thripitaka containing its Commentaries (attakatha) transcribed in Pali and Sinhala languages was declared as a National Heritage by H.E the President at the historical Aluwiharaya in Matale and a Gazette Notification dated 07th February 2019 has been issued to that effect. It has been scheduled to hand over the proposal for the declaration of the Thripitaka as a World Heritage to the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO) on 23rd March 2019 which has already been approved by the Cabinet of Ministers. Accordingly, with a view to making this event a success, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to conduct a countrywide programme named \u201cThripitakabhivandana\u201d with the participation of the public during the period from 16th March to 23rd March, to conduct the National Ceremony related to the declaration of the Thripitaka as a World Heritage in the premises of the Maha Maluwa (Great Terrace) of the Tempe of the Sacred Tooth Relic in Kandy and to make the necessary arrangements in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-06-028-en",
    "num": "28",
    "date_str": "2019-03-06",
    "description": "Taking expeditious measures for the preservation of Archaeological Antiquities and the prevention of their destruction, theft and illicit trafficking",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9586",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Antiquities Ordinance No.9 of 1940 was amended for the last time in the year 1998 and the Government has drawn its attention on the importance of updating the legal provision to confront the present challenges in respect of the preservation of antiquities. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Sajith Premadasa, Minister of Housing, Construction and Cultural Affairs to amend the relevant Acts, to take measures in regard to the destruction of Archaeological Antiquities, expeditious action to prevent theft and illicit exportation and to create public awareness on the crimes committed against Archaeological Antiquities and to induce the public to provide information in this regard and also to increase the penalties charged for inflicting damages to archaeological antiquities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Amendments to the required Acts to facilitate the signing of Bilateral Social Security Agreements between Sri Lanka and India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9587",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the existing Labour Law in Sri Lanka, all foreign workers  employed in Sri Lanka are covered by the Employees' Provident Fund Act, No.15 of 1958 (EPF) and are entitled to claim the total contribution made to the EPF with interest for the period of employment in Sri Lanka on account of cessation of the employment and return to their countries. Nevertheless, according to the existing Labour Law in India, a Sri Lankan worker working in India needs to contribute to the Indian Social Security System and is not entitled to withdraw his contribution until he attains the age of 58 years. In order to resolve this issue, it has been proposed to enter into a Bilateral Social Security Agreement between Sri Lanka and India to provide relief to the Sri Lankan expatriate workers working in India. In terms of this agreement, the Sri Lankan workers who work in India and contribute to the EPF in Sri Lanka will not be required to contribute to the Indian Social Security Fund.  Further, the Sri Lankan workers in India who contribute to the Indian Social Security agreement without contributing to the EPF in Sri Lanka will have the ability to make an application to claim their contribution when they cease their employment in India. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to amend the Employees' Provident Fund Act, No.15 of 1958 enabling Sri Lanka and India to enter into a Social Security Agreement as per the request of the Non\u2011Cabinet Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Increasing of Mahapola Scholarship Installment granted to the students of the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9588",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education is one of the prime institutes established in Sri Lanka for awarding the Higher National Diploma in Technological Education and over 20,000 students presently study at 19 regional centres. The Mahapola and Bursary granted to the students who follow higher education have been increased in the year 2015 and currently a Rs.5000/- monthly installment of Mahapola and a Rs.4000/- monthly installment of Bursary are paid for University students and Rs.1500/- monthly installment of Mahapola is being paid to each student of the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education, to increase the monthly installment of Rs.1500/- being paid to the students of the Sri Lanka Institute of Advanced Technological Education up to Rs.2500/-, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
