    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Procurement of Consultancy Services for the Light Rail Transit Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9605",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development to award the contract for Design, Procurement Assistance, Construction, Supervision and Project Management of the proposed Light Rail Transit from Malabe to Fort, to the Joint Venture comprising of the Oriental Consultants Global Co., Ltd., Japan International Consultants for Transportation Co., Ltd., Chodai Co., Ltd, Nippon Koei Co., Ltd of Japan and Consulting Engineers & Architects Associated (Pvt.) Ltd. of Sri Lanka as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Consultants Procurement Committee (CPCC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-12-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Awarding of the engineering procurement and construction contract of the  Basnagoda Reservoir Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9606",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to implement the Basnagoda Reservoir Project as a part of the Gampaha, Attanagalla, Minuwangoda integrated water supply project implemented under the National Water Supply & Drainage Board, for the supply of drinking water and industrial water required for the areas of Gampaha, Attanagalla, Minuwangoda and Mirigama.\n\n\tIt has been planned to construct the Basnagoda reservoir by constructing a dam across the Basnagoda Oya which is a tributary of the Attanagalu Oya. It is designed to be constructed with a concrete dam of 2.5 m in height and 130 m in length for the storage of a water capacity of 3.5 million Cubic meters (MCM). Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. P. Harison, the Minister of Agriculture, Rural Economic Affairs, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development, to award the Engineering Procurement and Construction contract to the Sinohydro Corporation Ltd. for a sum of Rs.2,347.4 million, in accordance with the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (CAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-12-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Procurement of 03 STS Cranes to increase the Deep Berth Capacity of the Jaya Container Terminal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9607",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- A project has been planned to be implemented by the Sri Lanka Ports Authority to increase the capacity of the Deep Berth Capacity of the Jaya Container Terminal (JCT) to enhance the advantage of handling the larger container vessels arriving at the Port of Colombo. As a component of the said project, approval was granted by the Cabinet to award the contract for the purchase of 3 cranes of Ship to Shore to M/s Shanghai Zhenhua Heavy Industries Co. Ltd., in accordance with the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Appointed Procurement Committee.  According to the said approval, the proposal made by Hon. Sagala Ratnayaka, the Minister of Ports & Shipping and Southern Development, to proceed with the future activities of the procurement procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-12-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2019-03-12",
    "description": "Let's Protect Children - National Trust Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9608",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Persons and Organizations come forward voluntarily to provide the necessary assistance to children who have fallen into misery due to numerous social problems,  in\u2011born injuries and those sustained subsequently, diseases and negligence and unawareness of parents and as such, it has become a timely need for setting up of an institutional structure which could accept their donations in a responsible and a legally acceptable manner.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to establish 'Let's Protect Children - National Trust Fund' under the Chairmanship of the Secretary to the President, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Implementation of the National Drug Prevention Programme: 'A Drug Free Country'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9609",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers had granted its approval previously for the establishment of a National Authority for the rehabilitation of persons addicted to drugs and for importing and making use of the modern equipment for the identification of injurious drugs in order to further extend the activities pertaining to the creation of a drug free country. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to appoint an Advisory Committee for the expeditious implementation of the said programme, until such Authority is established, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Implementation of the Special Programme on Empowering the Differently Abled and the Elderly Community",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9610",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been revealed that, presently, the differently abled and the elderly community in Sri Lanka exceeds 15% of the total population. As such, the necessity of developing a programme has arisen to accord the due dignity to the Differently Abled and the Elderly and thereby making them to contribute to the development of the country without being dependent on another by providing the required facilities for them to meet their needs while minimizing inequalities they are subject to. Paying attention to the same, it has been proposed to implement a special programme for Empowering the Differently Abled and the Elderly Community.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to secure the funds necessary for the implementation of the special programme by the Presidential Secretariat to empower the Differently Abled and the Elderly Community, in collaboration and coordination with all stakeholders, focusing attention on ensuring equality in the usage of common amenities and facilities and the development of infrastructure facilities necessary, making the community aware of empowering them in the context of economic and social conditions without treating them differently within the entire community and in the fields of survey, research and policy formulation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Shilpa Sena Exposition - Sri Lanka's Technological Revolution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9611",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Arrangements are being made to conduct a district level Exposition called the 'Shilpa Sena - the Sri Lanka's Technological Revolution' with the prime objective of creating a platform for research commercialization inclusive of the new inventions introduced by the various local Government Institutions and facilitating the development of technology transfer. By this, it is intended to introduce the low\u2011cost and high\u2011end technologies already developed by the Government Research Institutes, to the local industrialists and entrepreneurs. It is proposed to conduct the exposition in all the districts and the contribution of the Government Institutions including the Export Development Board, Technology Development Board, Government Research Institutes and the Universities, are sought for this purpose. Accordingly, at the request of the Non\u2011Cabinet Minister of Science, Technology & Research, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, to conduct the 'Shilpa Sena' Exposition also to coincide with the similar expositions and programmes to be conducted by the various public and private sector institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Regulations for the royalty payment to the rights holders of songs or musical works",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9612",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of the Intellectual Property Act, No.36 of 2003 amended by the Intellectual Property (Amendment) Act, No.7 of 2018, the rights holders of songs or musical works or the collective societies in which such rights owners hold the membership should be paid the due royalty, for the copyright and the related rights of such creations. However, it has been identified that the royalty payments are still not paid to the right holders of these songs or musical works by those who use them for commercial purposes. Therefore, it has been found that it would be more effective to issue the regulations under the Intellectual Property Act, No.36 of 2003 by repealing the Intellectual Property Regulation, No.01 of 2011 published in the Gazette Notification No.1687/28 dated 2011\u201101\u201105 which stipulates the specific minimum fees as royalty payments to regularize the royalty payment mechanism. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, as per the request made by the Non\u2011Cabinet Minister of Science,Technology & Research, to publish the regulations made by the Legal Draftsman in this regard in the Gazette and thereafter, to present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Empowering the economy by the development of the Mechatronics Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9613",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval previously to the proposal for granting the Long Term Loan Facility under the \u201cEnterprise Sri lanka Programme\u201d proposed to be implemented as one of the components of the Mechatronics Enabled Economic Development Initiative. \n\n\tAccordingly, taking into consideration the benefits that could be accrued through the proposed project, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, at the request of the Non\u2011Cabinet Minister of Science, Technology & Research to implement the proposed project including the Standards Training, Prototyping and Test Facility identified as another component thereto, through the financial allocations provided under the Non-Cabinet Minister of Science, Technology & Research, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Introduction of protected foot bridges for the convenience of transportation of the people living in the remote areas",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9614",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct 1000 protected foot bridges developed by the National Engineering Research and Development Centre, at the identified locations in the remote areas at the Divisional Secretariat Division level where unprotected trunk bridges, suspension bridges or any such locations where safety measures are not used for transportation. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President, at the request of the Hon. Non\u2011Cabinet Minister of Science, Technology & Research to implement the said programme, securing the funds necessary within the 2020 - 2022 Medium Term Budgetary Framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Incorporating the Convention on Cluster Munitions (OSLO Convention) into the Domestic Legislation in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9615",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka will be able to gain reputation as a state which stands for the humanitarian disarmament by acceding to the Convention on the Eradication of Cluster Munitions, embodied in the multiple explosive sub-munitions which cause major destruction. Taking into consideration the contribution to be made for the peace and security of the region as well as in the world, the attention of the Government has been focused to incorporate the Convention on Cluster Munitions or the OSLO Convention into the domestic Legislation in Sri Lanka. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to draft the necessary legislation for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Development of Facilities at the Institute of Peace Support Operations Training in Sri Lanka (IPSOTSL)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9616",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Training Centre functioning at the Office Complex of the Kukuleganga Hydro power project provides necessary training for the Army troops who attend for the Peace Keeping Missions under the United Nations Organization. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Defence, to upgrade the facilities of the training school at an investment of Rs. 811.71 million so as to carry out the said training sessions more qualitatively and up to the standards of the United Nations Organization, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Recruitment of 7,500 Trainee Project Assistants",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9617",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Close monitoring and supervision of the development projects have become an essential factor for the effective implementation of the said projects. It has been proposed to make the unemployed youths who have studied up to the GCE (A/L) as partners in the national development process by making them involved in the said process. Accordingly, it has been planned to recruit 7,500 Trainee Project Assistants to the Ministry of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development and Youth Affairs. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development and Youth Affairs, to appoint the candidates so selected to the posts of Trainee Project Assistants for a period of one year on contract basis and pay them each a monthly allowance of Rs.15,000/-, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Appointment of Members to the Wildlife Conservation Advisory Committee in terms of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance (FFPO)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9618",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Wildlife Conservation which comes under the ambit of the Ministry of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs, has been assigned with the tasks such as ensuring the protection of the endangered wild animals living in the conservation areas as well as outside those, implementation of the National Wildlife Policy and the law, implementation of the wildlife protection environmental policy, conservation of the wildlife resources and taking measures for minimizing the human-elephant conflict. The Department of Botanical Gardens which comes under the purview of this Ministry is entrusted with the management and development of several botanical gardens including the Peradeniya Royal Botanical Gardens. In addition, the Department of National Zoological Gardens of this Ministry undertakes the management of the Deheiwala Zoological Gardens, the Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, the Pinnawala New Zoological Gardens and the Hambantota Safari Park.\n\n\tAccordingly, \tthe proposal made by Hon.\t John Amarathunga, the Minister of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs, to appoint an Advisory Committee comprising of experts in the relevant field, for the purpose of advising the Minister on the said functions, in terms of section 70(I) of the Flora and Fauna Protection Ordinance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Conducting the State Vesak Festival of 2563rd year of Sri Buddhist Era",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9619",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been scheduled to conduct the State Vesak Festival of 2563rd year of Sri Buddhist Era on 17th May 2019 and the Vesak Full Moon Poya Day Programme on 18th May 2019 at Thotagamu Ancient Rathpath Rajamaha Viharaya at Thelwatta, Hikkaduwa in Galle with the State patronage. It has been proposed to conduct a programme for the physical development of the temples located in Galle District, spiritual programmes for creating a society of free of drugs enriched with spiritual development and programmes for making a sound economy and an awakening in literature and arts nurtured by Buddhism, to coincide with this ceremony. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Gamini Jayawickrema Perera, the Minister of Buddhasasana & Wayamba Development to conduct the State Vesak Festival - 2019 at the Thotagamu Ancient Rathpath Rajamaha Viharaya at Thelwatta, Hikkaduwa in Galle District, to declare the week from 15 May 2019 to 21st May 2019 as the Vesak Week and to implement the other said programmes to be conducted in line with that, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Amendments to the Monetary Law Act, No. 58 of 1949",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval previously to draft legislative reforms to update the law relating to Central Banking so as to comply with the developed international best practices. Accordingly, proposed amendments to be made to the Monetary Law Act No.58 of 1949 which is in force at present for the functions of the Central Bank have been taken up for discussion with the Monetary Board and all relevant stake holders. This includes amendments for introducing new flexible inflation targeting the monetary policy framework, enhancing the governance standards in management structure of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, introducing several disclosure requirements and recognizing the Central Bank of Sri Lanka as the macro prudential authority of the country. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance to repeal and replace the Monetary Law Act No. 58 of 1949 with the new law, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Renovation activities further necessary at the Seven-storey building complex of the Negambo District General Hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval previously, to award the contract for the renovation of the seven-storey building complex of the Negambo District General Hospital to the State Development and Construction Corporation at an estimated cost of Rs.500 million.\tWhile the renovation activities are being carried out, the hospital authority has proposed several more renovation activities necessary to be done at the building complex. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine to amend the total cost estimate of the project from Rs.500 million to Rs.692.43 million, to make enable the essential activities such as, the improvements to be made to the theatre and the installation of the waste water drainage system, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Construction of a 100 MW of Floating Solar Power Plant in the Maduru Oya Reservoir",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval previously, to implement the construct of a 100 MW of floating solar power plant as an integrated project joint venture of the Sri Lanka Mahaweli Authority, the Ceylon Electricity Board and the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by H.E. the President Maithripala Sirisena, in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment and Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development, to establish a joint venture with the Canadian Solar Institute to implement the project as a storage project to store solar energy with the use of solar panels in accordance with the proposal made by the Canadian Government and to appoint a joint Working Committee to conduct negotiations in that regard,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Provision of clean drinking water to the people of the Districts affected by the Chronic Kidney Disease",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval previously, to implement the project for upgrading the water treatment plant in Lunugamwehera and Kirindi Oya by utilizing the funds amounting to Rs.298 million under the programme for the provision of clean drinking water to the people of the districts affected by the chronic kidney disease. As such, the joint proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education and Hon. Sajith Premadasa, the Minister of Housing, Construction and Cultural Affairs, to implement the project for the laying of pipe line necessary for the distribution of water by the Kirindi Oya water treatment plant so upgraded, to the 217 housing units constructed at the Hon. Narendra Modi Model Village in the Thissamaharamaya Divisional Secretariat Division by using the funds set apart for the National Housing Programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "The National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development - 2018",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The need has arisen to update the National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development introduced in the year 2004, considering the local and the global trends and the sphere of changes that had since taken place. Accordingly, when the National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development - 2018 was presented to the Cabinet at an earlier occasion, instructions have been given to further update it, taking into consideration the observations made so as to represent the various fields in that regard. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Chandrani Bandara, the Minister of Women & Child Affairs and Dry Zone Development, to implement the National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development amended accordingly, under a proper strategic plan, at National, Provincial, District, Divisional and Rural levels, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Completion of the remaining construction work of the New Court Complex in Matara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers has granted its approval for the construction of the new court complex in Matara and presently, its construction work is in progress. It has been planned to complete the said construction work by May 2019 and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.\t(Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms to secure the funds needed for carrying out further improvements necessary and providing of facilities in order to use the courts complex for the proper commencement of court functions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Enhancement of facilities of Courts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Focus of the Government has been made on enhancing the facilities in the courts, due to the increase in the flow of court cases and the lack of adequate space and other facilities in the buildings used for the purpose. In this respect, it has been planned for the construction of the Walapane District and Magistrate's Court Building, the expansion of the Circuit Court Building in Narammala, the construction of the Vakare and Helboda Circuit Court Buildings, the construction of the production rooms and the record rooms of the District and Magistrate's Courts of Akkaraipattu and Pothuwil and the Magistrate's Courts of Kuliyapitiya and the construction of Official Residences for the District Judge and the Magistrate of Chillaw. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms to carry out these development activities within the Medium Term Budgetary Framework of 2020 - 2022 with an investment of Rs.592.86 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Establishment of the Education Inspection Service Institution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, the Minister of Education for the establishment of an affiliated institution to the Ministry of Education, named as 'Education Inspection Service' to ensure the accountability and responsibility of all stakeholders who deal with education for making a novel inspection and evaluation culture aimed at promoting the qualitative development in the school education system, suited to the present day needs, to establish the same at sub\u2011institutional level in all provinces and to establish an independent 'Education Accreditation Board' to make appropriate recommendations by analyzing the findings made by the Education Inspection Service, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Holding of the Third Meeting of the Asia-Europe Political Forum in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9628",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to hold the 3rd Meeting of the Asia-Europe Political Forum in Colombo from 5th to 8th of April, 2019, under the theme 'The Challenges of Social Security and Employment for increasing aged population in the developing countries'. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by Hon. Thilak Marapana, the Minister of Foreign Affairs and Hon. Daya Gamage, the Minister of Primary Industries and Social Empowerment, for hosting the event and providing other facilities necessary related thereto, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Conducting a Forensic Audit in the entities regulated and supervised by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the recommendations made relating to the Central Bank of Sri Lanka in the report submitted by the Presidential Commission of Inquiry appointed by H.E the President to Investigate and Inquire into and Report on the process of decision making over the Issuance of Treasury Bonds, the Central Bank of Sri Lanka has decided to conduct a forensic audit with regard to the matters pointed out by the said Commission. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance to procure the service of a suitable entity with international experience for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-19-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2019-03-19",
    "description": "Implementation of Phase II of the Anuradhapura South Integrated Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-19",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Phase II of the Anuradhapura South Integrated Water Supply Project had been designed for implementation to be beneficial to the people living in Nachchaduwa, Thalawa, Rambawa, Mihinthale, Thirappane, Kuda Nagaraya, some areas of the Anuradhapura town, Nuwaragampalatha Central and the Eastern Divisional Secretary Divisions. Nevertheless, owing to the problems which had cropped up for getting water from the reservoirs planned for the purpose, it has been proposed to implement the project in such a way as to get the required water from the Nachchaduwa Tank. Presently, it has been planned to construct a new water treatment plant with a capacity of 33,500 m3, 9 storage towers, 6 water sumps, the distribution system and a transmission line from the Nachchaduwa Tank up to Thuruwila, with an investment of Rs.16,936.06 million. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education to appoint a Procurement Committee to make the necessary evaluations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
