  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Declaring Sri Lanka as a Mine Free Country and providing the victims with the necessary support",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9637",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a result of the conflict which prevailed in the Northern and Eastern Provinces, it has been identified that there are around 3,000 victims who have been affected with Anti-Personnel Mines and Explosive Remnants of war. In addition to providing them with the necessary first-aid and medical care, the Government, being a signatory to the Ottawa Convention on the prohibition of the use of anti-personnel mines, is committed to providing the victims with the further necessary support. The measures taken by Sri Lanka, for the significant achievement of making the place mine free, leaving only an area of 25 sq.km. out of the suspected hazardous area which is about 1,302 sq.km., is internationally acclaimed. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ranil Wickremasinghe, the Prime Minister and Minister of National Policies, Economic Affairs, Resettlement & Rehabilitation, Northern Province Development and Youth Affairs, to expedite the national programme on mines in order to take action to clear mines from the suspected areas with remaining mines and to implement programmes to ensure sustainable livelihood support of those who have been affected by land mines, with a view to making Sri Lanka a mine free country by 2020, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Updating of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9638",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance to amend the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017, updating it by incorporating the necessary regulations and the provisions, in order to strengthen the intervention of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka when implementing the Foreign Exchange Act, with a view to ensuring an effective Foreign Exchange Management within Sri Lanka and to effect the regulatory functions in that regard, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Securing of Funds for the establishment of a National Vocational Training Institute at Hingurakgoda",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9639",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has focused its attention on the need for providing a qualitative vocational education and training to the youth aimed at productive employment opportunities for the social and economic development of Sri Lanka. As such, it has been planned to establish a National Vocational Training Centre at Hingurakgoda under the Polonnaruwa Integrated Development Programme with a concessionary financial assistance of Euro 35 million from Netherlands. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance, to enter into loan Agreements with the Cooperative Rabobank U.A. of the Netherlands for the implementation of the project under a concessionary loan inclusive of a Euro 9.7 million grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Obtaining financial assistance for the Construction of the High Altitude Sports Complex in Nuwara Eliya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9640",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- High altitude training provides the athletes to improve the lung capacity together with a sustainable level of endurance and physical fitness. It has been found that this promotes enhanced competitiveness to come out with their skills and achieve success at international level. A high altitude sports training centre has to be constructed at a height of between 1,500 m to 3,500 m from the mean sea level. Presently, such a training centre which is the highest in Asia, has been constructed in China at a height of 1,899 m. Accordingly, it has been planned to construct a training complex at an identified location in Nuwara Eliya at a height of 1,895 m making use of the natural setting of Sri Lanka. In this respect, the Export Financial Institute of the United Kingdom has agreed to provide the necessary funds for the purpose under an export credit facility. The People's Bank has agreed to finance the balance part of the contract price, not covered by the export credit facility and accordingly, the proposal made by Hon.\tMangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance to conduct negotiations with the said bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the construction of 200 Rural Bridges",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9641",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has accorded high priority for the connectivity improvement in the road network, with a view to providing the full benefits from the mainstream development activities in the country to the remote villages as well. It has been planned to construct 200 bridges out of the bridges to be constructed Under the Rural Bridges Project aimed at connecting the rural areas to the more developed regions with a concessionary financial assistance from Netherlands. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance, to enter into loan Agreements with the Cooperative Rabobank U.A. of the Netherlands for the implementation of the project under a concessionary loan inclusive of a Euro 14 million grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Securing of funds for the establishment of a Medical Faculty in the University of Sabaragamuwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9642",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to establish a medical faculty in the University of Sabaragamuwa at an investment of US $ 70.46 million, with a view to expanding the health facilities of high standard within the country creating qualitative health professionals equipped with a sound training thereby and increasing the opportunity for the talented Advanced Level qualified students to be entered into the national university system. Accordingly, it has been planned to implement the project for the purpose under three Stages. It is expected that an amount of US $ 50 million of the total project investment to be obtained as a concessionary loan and the Government to incur the balance amount of approximately US $ 20.46 million. As such, the proposal made by Hon.Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance, to enter into a loan agreement with the Saudi Fund for Development (SFD) to obtain a concessionary loan of US $ 50 million, to implement stage II of the Project for the establishment of a Medical Faculty in the University of Sabaragamuwa, including the construction of the main faculty building and purchase of equipment, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Gazette Notifications issued to impose a Special Commodity Levy for providing relief to the Consumers and the Local Farmers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9643",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of section 7(iii) of the Special Commodity Levy Act No.48 of 2007, approval of Parliment has to be obtained as soon as convenience for the Gazette Notifications published under the said Act by passing a resolution in Parliament. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance, to present the Gazette Notifications No.2104/30 dated 2019\u201101\u201103, No.2108/65 dated 2019\u201102\u201101, No.2109/15 dated 2019\u201102\u201107, No.2109/20 dated 2019\u201102\u201108, No.2111/58 dated 2019\u201102\u201124 and No.2112/48 dated 2019\u201103\u201102, published to impose the  Special Commodity Levy to provide relief to the consumers and the local Farmers, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Construction of the Pre and Para-Clinical Six storeyed building at the Faculty of Medicine in the University of Jaffna",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9644",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Medical Faculty of the University of Jaffna initiated in the year 1978 enrolling 65 students as its first intake, has now expanded as a faculty with 937 students. Even though the annual enrollment of the students with multi ethnic composition had been increased by now, in line with that the infrastructure such as lecture halls, laboratories, tutorial rooms, accommodating facilities have not been developed to facilitate them. The Lyca Group of the United Kingdom has agreed to build a six storeyed building with a 6,500 Sq.M floor area including modern facilities with an investment of Rs.740 million and make the award to the Jaffna University through the Gnanam Foundation of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Rauff Hakeem, the Minister of City Planning, Water Supply and Higher Education to implement the relevant project and enter into Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Development of the National Hospital for Respiratory Diseases at Welisara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9645",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Hospital for Respiratory Diseases situated at Welisara, remains as the only institution solely dedicated for diagnosis and treatment of respiratory diseases in Sri Lanka. This hospital which provides services annually for around 100,000 out door Patients, carries out nearly 1,000 thoracic surgeries annually. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine, to implement a development project in stages, with an investment of Rs.9,180 million to improve the health\u2011care facilities of the hospital to meet the present and the future demand of the patients suffering from respiratory diseases, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Project for the Conservation of Traditional Medical Knowledge - Stage II",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9646",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- There is evidence to prove that our Traditional System of Medicine has been of much help for the cure and prevention of non\u2011communicable as well as other diseases. As such, the Department of Ayurveda has implemented a project for the conservation of the traditional system of medicine and the medical knowledge which presently is going into oblivion, considering the importance of preserving and disseminating the system of traditional medicine. As the initial step of the project, the preparation of a database by collecting information of about 2,500 Doctors, renovation of the old library and the preservation of the record room, ola leave books, preservation and duplication of about 400 ola leave books, drafting legislation to preserve the knowledge on traditional indigenous medicine and the establishment of the audio visual unit necessary for the digital library, have been commenced. As the second stage of the above project, it has been planned to preserve age old treatment practices, curing methods and various behavioral patterns and to get the traditional medical systems subject to research to ensure their scientific aspects aimed at disseminating such knowledge to the future generation. As such the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine, to implement the same in the Medium Term Budgetary Framework with an investment of Rs.350 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Establishment of a Laboratory with diagnostic facilities required for handling of harmful and dangerous micro-organism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9647",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Medical Research Institute (MRI) which has a history of around 116 years, conducts research and diagnosis covering many areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. (Dr.) Rajitha Senaratne, the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine to establish a Bio\u2011Safety Level 3 High Risk Laboratory with an investment of Rs.125 million with a view to developing advance diagnostic facilities for identifying and safe handling of harmful micro-organism in the event of a hazardous outbreak by further expanding the services of the MRI, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Issuance of General Policy Guidelines in respect of the Electricity Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9648",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of section 5 of the Sri Lanka Electricity Act. No.20 of 2009, the Minister has to issue General Policy Guidelines in respect of the Electricity Industry. Accordingly, with a view to addressing the emerging issues in the power sector, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development to issue the new General Policy Guidelines formulated incorporating Fuel diversity and security, Electricity Tariff, Generation, Transmission and Distribution Systems, Financing on Electricity Projects, Environment, Energy Conservation, Consumer Services, Multi-Sector Development, Safety and Exemptions from Licensing, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "The thrift use of electricity to meet the existing power shortage",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9649",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the prevailing drought condition, the generation of electricity to meet the demand for the power consumption of the Island, has become a challenge. Considering the possibility of saving a considerable amount of power through the thrift use of electricity, until such time that the generation of electricity returns to normal, the attention of the Government has been focused to make the public aware of the measures to be taken for the thrift consumption of electricity. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Ravi Karunanayake, the Minister of Power, Energy and Business Development to make use of electricity thriftily, during the forthcoming three months by switching off two electric lamps in all houses, reduction of electricity consumption by around 10% in the public institutions and the religious and commercial establishments, switching off the unnecessary street lamps and switching them off one hour prior to the switching off time in a normal day, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Formalization and Expedition of the Receipt of Court Fines and Stamp Duties Levied on Transfer of Lands to the Local Authorities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9650",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to amend section 19 of the Provincial Councils Act, No.42 of 1987, with a view to making the existing system of crediting the revenue accumulated on the Court fines more efficient and stamp duties charged on the deeds certified on transfer of lands within the administrative areas of Local Authorities to the relevant Local Authorities. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Wajira Abeywardena, the Minister of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils & Local Government, to publish the Bill prepared accordingly in the Government Gazette and to refer it to the Provincial Councils through H.E the President for their views in terms of Article 154G of the Constitution and present the same in Parliament subsequently with amendments if found necessary, was approved b the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Protection of the catchment area of the Nanawaladola water source in Ratnapura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9651",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Nanawaladola water source in Ratnapura supplies water for about 89 acres of paddy lands and the drinking water project operating associated with the same provides water for 140 families. Accordingly, taking into account, the significance to protect and maintain the catchment area of the said water resource, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development to vest the aforesaid land which is in the possession of Urban Development Authority with the Department of Agrarian Development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Construction of a Housing Project for Middle income families in the Ceremonial Drive at Rajagiriya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9652",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has initiated a project to provide 500,000 housing units for the Middle income families inclusive of the Public and Private sector employees at an affordable price. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Patali Champika Ranawaka, the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development to implement a housing project with 177 units and other facilities for Middle income earners in the Ceremonial Drive at Rajagiriya, on the basis of Public Private Partnership, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement between Sri Lanka and Pakistan on the exchange of Sugarcane Breeding Materials",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9653",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Navin Dissanayake, the Minister of Plantation Industries to enter into an Agreement, between the Sugarcane Research Institute of Sri Lanka and the Sugarcane Research and Development Board and the Sugarcane Research Institute of Faisalabad in Pakistan, taking into consideration, the benefits that could be accrued by both countries mutually by the exchange of sugarcane breeding materials, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Rehabilitation and improvement of the Priority Roads",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9654",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. Kabir Hashim, the Minister of Highways & Road Development and Petroleum Resources Development to rehabilitate and improve the additional roads to be selected on priority basis utilizing a balance of US$16.8 million under the Priority Road Project implemented as per the Memorandum of Understanding made between the Government of Sri Lanka and the China Development Bank to provide financial facilities to the infrastructure development project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Renovations of the Kandy-Getambe Court Complex",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9655",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to renovate the Kandy-Getambe Court Complex consisting of 11 courts, by the State Engineering Corporation at an investment of Rs.303.5 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Re-enacting of the Prescription (Special Provisions) Act, to provide a period of relief to enable the persons affected due to the conflict situation, to resort to legal measures in respect of their properties",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9656",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Prescription (Special Provisions) Act, No.05 of 2016 was enacted with a view to providing special legal provisions in respect of persons who were unable to claim their rights in Courts, for the recovery of immovable property including lands, during the conflict situation which prevailed in the past. This Act, provides to exempt disadvantaged persons from the provisions of the Prescription Ordinance and entitles them to institute an action in Courts within a period of two years from the date of coming into operation of the Act. It has been observed that and adequate period of time has to be given to prepare the misplaced documents during the conflict period or to collect the evidence relevant to the ownership of the lands and to make the relevant persons aware of this Act. As such, the proposal made by Hon. (Mrs.) Thalatha Atukorala, the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms, to re\u2011enact the Prescription (Special Provisions) Act to make legislation to extend the period of operation of this Act, by a further period of three years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Providing facilities for the students enrolled under the 13 year Guaranteed Education Programme in Government Schools",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9657",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The students who are enrolled under the 13 year Guaranteed Education Programme and follow the vocational training curriculum should have the second year of their education in a selected vocational stream at an accredited Vocational Institute approved for awarding the NVQ 4 Level Certificate. It has been observed that most of such vocational training institutes are established in the main towns and certain other training institutes are situated only in a particular place and this situation has caused the children to incur an enormous expenditure on transport and accommodation. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Akila Viraj Kariyawasam, Minister of Education, to provide a daily allowance of Rs.500/- for the students enrolled under the school programme to cover their transport and other expenditure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Updating of the Wakf Act No.51 of 1982 according to the timely needs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9658",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Hon. M.H.A. Haleem, Minister of Postal Services & Muslim Religious Affairs to appoint an experts committee and provide facilities to consider the amendments required to be made to the existing Wakf Act according to the needs of the time for the smooth functioning of the Wakf Board and Wakfs Tribunal and to provide the necessary legal guidance to solve the issues and disputes pertaining to the Mosques and the administration of the Muslim Trusts, located countrywide, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Construction of the Boralanda Swimming Pool",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9659",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to construct a swimming pool at a length of 25 meters with 06 lanes in a plot of land belonging to the Boralanda Police Training College, in the close proximity to the Boralanda town in Welimada. The Swimming Pool will be used to conduct the training programmes for the Athletes in the area, School children, Government Servants, Police Officers, School Cadets, Life\u2011saving Swimming instructors and for the apprentice officers of the police and other services. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Harin Fernando, Minister of Telecommunication, Foreign Employment and Sports, to implement the said project at an investment of Rs 50 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-03-26-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2019-03-26",
    "description": "Implementation of a Trade Adjustment Programme to accrue the benefits of the International Liberalized Trade",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9660",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-03-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to enhance the benefits which could be accrued to the Sri Lanka's economy through the competitiveness of the international liberalized trade, a comprehensive trade adjustment programme has been prepared with a wide participation of the parties involved in the field. Accordingly, with the objective of enabling the implemention of this programme in a productive manner, the joint proposal made by Hon. Mangala Samaraweera, the Minister of Finance and Hon. Malik Samarawickrama, the Minister of Development Strategies and International Trade to establish the Trade and Productivity Commission and a Joint Steering Committee as independent bodies that recommend the trade adjustments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
