    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Housing, Construction and Cultural Affairs, to award the contract of the project for the construction of a new hostel block for the National Police Academy at Katana to M/s Weerasooriya Builders (Pvt.) Ltd. for a sum of Rs.310 million, as recommended by the Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Revamping of the entire building complex of the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9974",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Education to obtain a status report, after having examined the entire building complex of the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka and to award the contracts using the National Competitive Bidding System in regard to the constructions relevant to the identified priority renovations and the relevant consultancy services to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Development of an Integrated Tourism Development Project at Dedduwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9975",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to develop the Dedduwa area as a tourist destination through public and private partnership. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Ministers of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs, Lands and Parliamentary Reforms and Ports & Shipping and Southern Development, to obtain the services of a local or international consultancy agency with experience in transaction advisory services for large scale projects and the preparation of Expression of Interest and to call for Expression of Interest and Business proposals from the interested parties in this project, considering the large scale of the proposed development project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Procurement of Thirty (30) Terminal Tractors for the Jaya Container Terminal of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9976",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Ports & Shipping and Southern Development to commence the procurement process for the purchase of Thirty (30) Terminal Tractors for the Jaya Container Terminal of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority under the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, following the International Competitive Bidding Procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Agreement between the Consumer Affairs Authority and the Importers of Milk Powder",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9977",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The information submitted by the Minister of Agriculture, Livestock Development, Irrigation and Fisheries & Aquatic Resources Development as Chairman of the Cabinet Sub Committee on Cost of Living, that the mechanism of regulating the maximum retail price for imported milk power would be implemented hereafter by adopting the methodology introduced by the Consumer Affairs Authority in accordance with the agreement entered into between the Importers of Milk Powder and the Consumer Affairs Authority, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Development of the Plantation Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9978",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by Prime Minister to secure a provision of Rs. 600 million to the Ministry of Plantation Industry for the implementation of the development strategies identified for the development of plantation sector considering the future potential of the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-07-30-024-en",
    "num": "24",
    "date_str": "2019-07-30",
    "description": "Implementation of a short term public relation campaign for the revival and rebuilding 'Sri Lanka Tourism Brand'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9979",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-07-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs for obtaining covering approval to select M/s J Walter Thompson (Pvt.) Ltd., deviating from the National Procurement Guidelines to implement a short term public relation campaign without any delay for the revival and rebuilding 'Sri Lanka Tourism Brand' and to manage the crisis situation with a view to achieving the key objectives to support the economy of the country after Easter Sunday attacks, was taken into consideration by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) in the fields of Science, Technology and Innovation between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Nepal",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9980",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President at the request of the Non-Cabinet Minister of Science, Technology & Research  to enter into  an MoU in the fields of Science, Technology and Innovation between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Nepal on the basis of equality and mutual benefits and with the objective of establishing the cooperation in the said field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Payment of compensation for the houses damaged due to the floods in the \tyear 2016",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Prime Minister to pay an ex gratia payment of Rs.20,000 per housing unit for 8,879 housing units in Kolonnawa Divisional Secretariat Division damaged due to the floods in the year 2016 that has not been assessed as yet but has been recommended by the Kolonnawa Divisional Secretary, through the Ministry of Public Administration, Disaster Management and Livestock Development and to provide the required provisions for the purpose to the said Ministry, was approved by  the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Minimization of greenhouse emission in energy sector as at 2030 in compliance with the Paris Agreement of Climate Change of the United Nations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9982",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka also has signed the Paris Agreement which was adopted in the 21st Summit of the partners of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change held in Paris in the year 2015. Accordingly, Sri Lanka is obliged for the minimization of the greenhouse emission in the year 2030 by 20% comparative to the year 2020. Taking this into consideration, the Cabinet noted the information submitted by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment on the importance of focusing special attention on environmental conservation, public health security and greenhouse emission, and on the significance of taking decisions connected with the matter concerned based only on the observations and recommendations granted through scientific environmental assessments  conducted by following the national environmental laws, in case power stations using non renewable energy sources are constructed during the decade from 2020 to 2030."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Establishment of the Institute of Environmental Professionals of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9983",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Member of Parliament, Mr. Harshana Rajakaruna had submitted a private member's Bill in Parliament on the 19th of February 2016 to incorporate the Institute of Environmental Professionals of Sri Lanka. According to the procedure of reporting to Parliament on a private member's Bill by a Member of Parliament, the Legal Draftsman has amended the draft considering the recommendations of the Attorney General in that regard.  As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Mahaweli Development and Environment to table the draft Bill in Parliament to incorporate the said institution, in order to  provide a social and professional recognition to environmental scientists and professionals with standards and code of ethics, within the global context as it makes provision for them to gain professional recognition locally and internationally through establishment of the said institution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Granting a period of moratorium for the payment of the Tourism Development Levy (TDL) for Tourism Institutions registered with the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9984",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet having considered the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs on granting a moratorium for a certain period of time for the payment of the Tourism Development Levy by the Tourism Institutions registered with the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, since the tourism industry in Sri Lanka has been severely affected due to the Easter Sunday terrorist attack on the 21st of April 2019,  decided to grant a moratorium period of six months from the 01st of January 2019 to pay the Levy and to re charge the same once again in 12 equal installments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Allocation of a land in the Yala Palatupana Tourism Zone to the Sister Company of M/s One Nature (Pvt.) Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9985",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Tourism Development, Wildlife and Christian Religious Affairs, to allocate a land in extent of seven acres in the Yala Palatupana Tourism Zone to the Sister Company of M/s One Nature (Pvt.) Limited for a fifty year lease subject to the upfront payment and the annual lease, as per the value assessed by the Department of Valuation for the development of a tourist resort comprising of 28 fully equipped villas, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notification published under the Excise Ordinance for the approval of Parliamen",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9986",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Finance has taken necessary action for the implementation of the Foolproof Sticker and Sticker Management System as approved in the Budget 2016 and 2017, aimed at preventing the use of tax or duty unpaid liquor and enhancing the protection of excise revenue while deterring the counterfeits.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to table the Excise Notification No.04/2019 published in the Extraordinary Gazette No.2128/30 dated 2019 06 20 in Parliament for  approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Establishment of the Assisted Reproductive Treatment Centre at the Castle Street Hospital for Women, Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9987",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Health, Nutrition & Indigenous Medicine, to establish an Assisted Reproductive Treatment Centre at the Castle Hospital inclusive of a Laboratory and a Theatre with In-Vitro Fertilization facilities in a separate new two storey building to expand its services for infertile couples and secure the provisions necessary for same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Allocation of the lands in the IT Park at Malabe to the Institute of Chemistry Ceylon and the University of Peradeniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=9988",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously, to allocate a land in extent of 01 A - 0 R - 6.40 P in the IT Park at Malabe to the IESL College of Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd. on a 30 year lease. However, due to the non payment of the relevant lease to the Government by the said Institute, the proposal made by the Minister of Megapolis & Western Development to revoke the above decision and allocate the said plot of land to the Institute of Chemistry Ceylon and in addition, to allocate a plot of land in extent of 02 A - 0 R - 7.90 P to the  University of Peradeniya, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-06-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-08-06",
    "description": "Devitalization of the Propagatable Floriculture items to be exported to Australia and the use of Glyphosate for the control of White Leaf Disease in the Sugarcane Cultivation and Weligama Coconut Leaf Wilt Disease",
