    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-08-27",
    "description": "Bilateral Air Service Agreement between Sri Lanka and Hungary",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10045",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The officials of the two countries have reached an Agreement on the draft Agreement prepared by the aeronautical authorities of the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Hungary on the Air Service Agreement after discussions held by them during the International Civil Aviation Negotiation Conference held in Bali, Indonesia in the year 2014. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport & Civil Aviation to sign the initialed Air Service Agreement between the Governments of Sri Lanka and Hungary by an accredited representative of Sri Lanka and thereafter, to take appropriate measures for the effective implementation of the Agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-08-27-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2019-08-27",
    "description": "Increase of Fines for the Offences of the Penal Code",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10046",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-08-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tDue to the vast increase in the incidence of criminal activities in the country, it is a timely need, to resort to stringent measures to counter them. As such, a Committee has been appointed to study and make recommendations as the fines imposed pertaining to the violation of provisions containing in certain Acts and Ordinances are not at all adequate to prevent such violations.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice & Prison Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation in accordance with recommendations of the said Committee to increase the fines for offences of the penal code, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
