    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that it is imperative to develop a specific programme to enhance public awareness on the responsibility of environmental management and thereby to increase the public participation on the same and also to obtain the active participation of the other  relevant stakeholders including the local government institutions. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment and Wildlife Resources for the expeditious implementation of a programme in the name of the 'Pivithurulanka National Environmental Management Programme' to carry out the programmes and actions for the entire environmental management continuously in the whole country, inclusive of the establishment of centres for sorting out the waste, providing incinerators to selected local authorities, providing the necessary facilities for enhancing the compost yards and setting up of new compost yards and implementation of programmes for making the public aware of environmental conservation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-12-04",
    "description": "Establishment of a 'Closed Education Service'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10283",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that it is appropriate to establish a Closed education service consisting of teachers, principals, in-service advisors, teacher educators and Education Administrative Service Officers to resolve their professional problems expeditiously, perform their appraisals systematically and transparently, uplift their professionalism and enhance their job satisfaction, enabling them to deliver their services in an efficient and effective manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to establish an Experts' Committee comprising of  subject professionals and educational experts to make a study of the above matters and prepare recommendations pertaining to same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-12-04",
    "description": "Appointment of Secretaries to the State Ministries",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10284",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President  for the appointment of  Secretaries to State Ministries of the the newly appointed State Ministers under Article 44(1) of the Constitution of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-04-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-12-04",
    "description": "National Policy Framework of the Government - Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour for a Reconstructed Country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10285",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development for the Policy Statement 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour for a  Reconstructed Country' presented by H.E. the President with ten fold policies aimed at achieving the four fold outcomes namely, a productive citizenry, a contented family, a disciplined and just society and a prosperous nation, to be accepted as the National Policy Framework of the Government and to direct all Ministries, Departments, Government Institutions, Provincial Councils and Local Authorities etc, to perform their duties and functions accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-04-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-12-04",
    "description": "The removal of the existing requirement on obtaining permits for the transportation of sand, soil and clay necessary for the local industries and the construction industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10286",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several  Members of the Cabinet pointed out  that difficulties have arisen when securing the necessary raw material for the local industries and as well as the construction industry due to the existing requirement on obtaining permits for the transportation of sand, soil and clay and that various malpractices occur when issuing the relevant permits. Taking these matters into consideration, the Cabinet decided to do away with the the present requirement on obtaining permits for the transportation of sand, soil and clay, with immediate effect."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Milling the paddy stocks purchased under the Government Paddy Purchase Programme of 2018/2019 Maha Season into rice and issue them to the market through the Lanka Sathosa Network",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10287",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the Government Paddy Purchase Programme of 2018/2019 Maha Season, action has been taken during the recent past, to convert a part of the paddy stocks purchased, through the private sector small and medium scale paddy millers. However, since, there is an increasing trend in the price of rice these days, the steps taken to provide relief to the consumer by milling the balance of the paddy stocks of about 42,000 MT out of the paddy stocks purchased and presently remaining in the stores of the Paddy Marketing Board and to provide it to the consumer through the Lanka Sathosa Ltd. outlet network were drawn to the attention of the Cabinet by the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development.\n\n\tSimilarly, taking into consideration the consent given by the major rice mill owners to supply rice within the period of next 2 - 3 months to the market without a scarcity and also to maintain the maximum retail price of rice as Rs.98/- per kg., it was decided by the Cabinet to fix the maximum price of rice as Rs.98/- per kg.  \n\n\tFurther, it was also decided by the Cabinet to grant approval to take necessary action for the importation of wheat flour until the crop harvest of the Maha season is had, to enable the people specially living in the estate and urban areas to obtain wheat flour and the products associated with it, at low prices, during the festive season."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Upgrading of the number of National Schools to be 1,000 within the  school network and the establishment of new Tri lingual Schools covering every District",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10288",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Education has planned to implement a programme to increase the number of National Schools to 1,000 by developing 03 schools equipped with all facilities in each Divisional Secretariat Division and upgrading them as National Schools with the objective of providing a free, equitable and qualitative education to every child. The Ministry of Education has also planned to initiate a State of the Art National School in each District with tri lingual educational opportunities and to initiate 20 such schools in the next two year period. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education for the implementation of the proposed programmes, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Introduction of a new, school based scientific methodology instead of the present district based methodology for selection of students to the State Universities on the Z Score method",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10289",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although it is the primary responsibility of the Government to provide equal opportunities of education to each and every child, it has been found that even at present, there exist various disparities in terms of the educational facilities and the quality of education among the Provinces, Districts and Schools as well. In the circumstances, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to appoint an Experts Committee comprising of competent persons on the subject matter to make recommendations for the introduction of a school based new scientific methodology instead of the present district based Z Score methodology for selection of students to the State Universities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "The proposed programme for the maintenance of the electric fences constructed and follow-up action in order to resolve the Human Elephant conflict",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10290",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Human Elephant conflict which has arisen in the country has become a national issue subject to the focus of all stakeholders. The proposal made by the Minister of Environment and Wildlife Resources, to update the existing electric fences and maintaining them, to provide the human and physical resources necessary for the purpose in order to resolve the problem and to implement the programmes planned to resolve the problem with the assistance inclusive of the District Secretaries and all relevant stakeholders, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Accelerated Programme for State Land Management",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10291",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister of Lands & Land Development presented to the attention of the Cabinet, information in respect of 11 programmes planned to be implemented from the month of December 2019 up to the month of March 2020 by the institutions coming under the purview of the Ministry of Lands & Land Development.  Accordingly, the Minister informed the Cabinet further that the programmes such as issuance of permits, Grants and Leases, in terms of the Land Development Ordinance and the State Land Ordinance after  holding Land Kachcheries, conducting Mobile Days and Field Day programmes, issuance of Title Certificates under the Title Registration Act, regularizing of Land Data System, Launching of the New Edition of the Road Map and the preparation of Land Manual etc. are anticipated to be implemented.\n\n\tThe Cabinet also decided to appoint an Officials' Committee to make recommendations to prepare a simple and a convenient method in respect of the lands given under lease basis enabling the lessees to make their  payments without causing much inconvenience to them."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Appointment of the Cabinet Sub Committee on Cost of Living",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10292",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President to appoint the Cabinet Sub Committee on Cost of Living under the Chairmanship of H.E. the President comprising the following members to make recommendations to the Cabinet regarding the matters concerning the cost of living, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tHon. the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development;\n\n*\tThe Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development and the Minister of Internal Trade, Food Security and Consumer Welfare;\n\n*\tThe Minister of Fisheries & Aquatic Resources; and\n\n*\tThe Minister of Plantation Industries and Export Agriculture\n\nIt was also decided to appoint a Committee comprising of 06 State Ministers and 12 Officials to assist the said Sub Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Establishment of a Multipurpose Development Task Force",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10293",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed by HE the President that there are large numbers of unskilled employment opportunities in Government and the related agencies which are filled without paying any heed to the low income segment of the society and guided by the political patronage. Taking that matter into consideration, the proposal made by HE the President to set up a Multipurpose Development Task Force as a Government Department to provide employment for 100,000 less educated youth from low income families was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\tFurther, it was noted by the Cabinet that it has been planned to commence the recruitment at district level in a transparent manner, to commence the operation of the Department by 15th of January 2020 and the ability of providing services of the said Task Force on a cost recovery basis to the Government, government agencies and the private sector."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Assignment of Subjects and Functions to the State Ministers who are not Members of the Cabinet",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10294",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal submitted by H.E. the President to assign subjects and functions to the State Ministers who are not Members of the Cabinet, in terms of Article 44(5) of the Constitution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-10-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-12-10",
    "description": "Reviewing the Current Scope of the 'Financial City Project'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10295",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 'Colombo Port City Project' was commenced in the year 2014, in association with the Sri Lanka Ports Authority and the Chinese investor, CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd., as an investment made by the private sector. After 2015 01 08, changing the original scope of the said project, a project relevant to that has been implemented as the 'Financial City Project'. At present, with the assistance of the external consultants and  under the guidance of the Legal Draftsman, a draft Bill has been prepared to establish a special economic zone by the name of 'Colombo Financial City'. Accordingly, within the current political, social and environmental context, the need has arisen to review the revised scope of the said project and the process followed to revise the said project and therefore, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister to appoint a committee comprising of subject specific experts, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Drafting of the Sri Lanka National Defence College Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10296",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the absence of  a National Defence College in Sri Lanka for conducting higher level courses on national defence, officers of the Tri-forces have to be directed to National Defence Colleges which conduct such courses, established in China, India, Bangladesh and Pakistan. However, due to the limited number of opportunities for the courses offered by those countries annually, it has not  been possible to train the officers as expected.  In this context, approval of the Cabinet has already been granted for the establishment of a National Defence College in Sri Lanka.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development  and the State Minister of Defence to  draft a Bill for the establishment of a National  National Defence College, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Agreement for the transfer of sentenced persons between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and Czech Republic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10297",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the provisions of the Transfer of Offenders Act, No.5 of 1995, a citizen of another country convicted and sentenced to imprisonment by a court in Sri Lanka can serve his/her sentence in the country of which he claims to be a citizen and a citizen of Sri Lanka imprisoned in any other country can serve  his/her balance period of imprisonment in Sri Lanka. Nevertheless, in order to make the provisions of the Act to be applicable, it is essential for an Agreement to be entered into between Sri Lanka and the respective country.\n\n\tAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Human Rights & Law Reforms to enter into an Agreement on transfer of sentenced persons  between the two countries in conformity with the laws of both the countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Introduction of 1000 Information Technology Certificate / Diploma learning opportunities under the Institution of Technology affiliated to the University of Moratuwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10298",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement an expeditious programme for providing training opportunities for Certificate/Diploma/Advanced Diploma courses for the students who have followed the technology subject streams, other subject streams or the students who have passed the Advanced Level Examination  targeting the job market in the IT Sector which is presently in high demand locally and internationally for software production and internet based job opportunities.  The said programme envisages to commence with 1000 training opportunities in the year 2020 and expects to increase the training opportunities up to 3000 by the year 2022. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation, to conduct such training courses through the Institute of Technology at Diyagama affiliated to the University of Moratuwa and to get the contribution of a Committee of Experts in the field of Information Technology working in the private and public sectors to design the courses, was approved in principle by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "The 72nd National Day Celebrations falling on 04th February, 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10299",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils & Local Government to appoint a Ministerial Committee under the Chairmanship of Hon. Prime Minister, to draw up the relevant programme for the 72nd National Day Celebrations falling on the 04th of February, 2020 and to organize the necessary arrangements, was approved by the Cabinet. The Cabinet also decided to hold the 72nd National Day Celebrations at the Independence Square in Colombo 07."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Obtaining 'Govijana Mandiraya' where the Ministry of Agriculture had been established, to re establish the Ministry of Agriculture",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10300",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government owned building named as 'Govijana Mandiraya' situated at Rajamalwatta Avenue in Battaramulla where the Ministry of Agriculture was previously established, had been given over to the Parliament of Sri Lanka on Cabinet approval with the objective of establishing the Parliamentary Committee System.  However, as of now, the building has not been fully utilized for the purpose. Also, the Government has to incur an expenditure close upon Rs.21 million monthly as rent, as a result of the Ministry of Agriculture being established in another building on a rental basis. Nevertheless, due to the inadequate facilities available in the building both the officers serving in the Ministry and the service recipients have to be subject to various inconveniences. Taking these matters into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development, to re establish the Ministry of Agriculture and the other institutions coming under purview of the Ministry, in the 'Govijana Mandiraya', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Establishment of a Task Force under the Ministry of Education for the implementation of Proposals for New Educational Reforms",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10301",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that the establishment of a 'Task Force pertaining to Education' is essential for providing technological and policy guidelines for the implementation of the proposals for educational reforms, in accordance with the Government policy, in a strategical and transparent manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to appoint a Task Force comprising of a group of experts with the subject specialists in the relevant field in the identification of proposals for educational reforms, programmes and  strategies, and to assist in the implementation of same, provide guidance, monitor and feedback for the relevant institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Implementation of  an Interconnected Modernized Road Network in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10302",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the National Policy Framework named the 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour', the modernization of the Road Network has been identified as a key factor necessary to achieve a high level of economic growth. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Roads and Highways, to implement the priority projects such as the construction of Overtaking Lanes at 3-5 km intervals on the National Highways, minimizing traffic congestion and road traffic crashes in areas identified as bottle necks and re surfacing and modernization of the entire road network in conformity with the international standards, the development of 100,000 km of Alternative Road Network, to facilitate a higher level of access to the main Highways and Expressways and improvement of rural access roads to make access to such an alternative road network, was approved in principle, by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Providing Relief for Small Scale Industrialists in Traditional Tile, Brick and Pottery Industries to procure Clay",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10303",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- Any person or an institution engaged in clay mining should obtain a license for the same in accordance with the Mines and Minerals Act, No.33 of 1992 as amended by Act, No.66 of 2009 and also a license to transport such raw materials to the site of the relevant industry. However, considering the various difficulties the small scale clay industrialists have to undergo, as a result of the complications in the procedure of obtaining the permits, the approval of the Cabinet has already been granted to simplify the process of obtaining permits for the transportation of sand, clay and soil.  As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment and Wildlife Resources, to amend Section 28 and 30 of the Mines and Minerals Act, No.33 of 1992 as appropriate to provide the provision necessary \tto further simplify the existing licensing procedure when obtaining the raw materials and to introduce a more efficient and simple method to facilitate the industrialists engaged in Tile, Brick and Pottery to continue in their production process sustainably and to ensure that no eco sensitive areas such as river banks are affected by the process, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Procurement of food items for the Tri Forces - Supply Year 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10304",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per the recommendation made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC) relating to the Procurement of food items  for the Sri Lanka Army, Sri Lanka Navy and Sri Lanka Air Force for the Supply Year 2020, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development and State Minister of Defence to award the said procurements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notification to fulfill the legal requirement under Import and Export (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 for approval of the Cabinet of Ministers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10305",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "The Government Policy 'Saubhagyaye Dekma' ('Vistas of Prosperity') has recognized the necessity of encouraging the farmer and the manufacturer to cultivate crops and manufacture products that can be produced within the country as much as possible. It is expected to uplift the farmer's economy within the country and to control the outflow of local foreign exchange to the other countries.\n\n\tAs such, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development to table the Gazette Notification issued on 2019 12 06 making provisions under the Import and Export (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 to control the importation of crops such as cardamom, clove, turmeric, pepper, cinnamon, nutmeg, mace, arecanut, tamarind and black gram and the products such as kites, lanterns/Vesak lanterns and incense sticks, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "'Sapiri Gamak' Community Based Rural Development Programme 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10306",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement a community based rural development programme called 'Sapiri Gamak' during the year 2020 with the objective of promoting employment and livelihood opportunities through the upliftment of rural facilities.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Prime Minister and Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development, to implement the said programme commencing from the 01st of January in 2020 in each Grama Niladhari Division by implementing projects amounting to Rs.2,000,000/- covering all the 14,021 Grama Niladhari Divisions Island-wide,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Establishment of the National Policy and Planning Bureau",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10307",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President to establish a National Policy and Planning Bureau for the adaptation of economic policies needed to achieve macro economic goals through National Policy and Planning, State Investment Allocation, National Development Planning, the Procurement Process, Project Analysis and Management with transparency and in a strategically oriented manner, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Establishment of an Inter Ministerial Task Force for Industrial and Entrepreneur Development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10308",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Industries and Supply Chain Management to establish an Inter-Ministerial Task Force for Industrial and Entrepreneur Development under the Chairmanship of H.E. the President and the membership of the Minister of Industries and Supply Chain Management and the participation of other relevant Ministers, Secretaries to Ministries and Officers, with a view to minimizing the delays and problematic situations arising in the process of making policy decisions in the manufacturing industry sector which provides a major contribution to the economic development, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-18-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2019-12-18",
    "description": "Review of the Millennium Challenge Corporation (MCC) Compact Agreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10309",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2019-12-18",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019 10 29 had granted approval to sign a compact Agreement and a Programme Implementation Agreement between the Millennium Challenge Corporation of the USA and the Government of Sri Lanka to obtain the grant funds provided by the Office of the Millennium Challenge Corporation for the implementation of several programmes of the identified fields. However, taking into consideration the views expressed on the project by various parties, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister to appoint a Committee comprising of the following to make a comprehensive study on the Millennium Challenge Corporation Project and submit recommendations to the Government and to suspend taking action in terms of  the Cabinet decision dated 2019 10 29 in this respect, until such time that the Committee makes its recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tProf. Lalithasiri Gunaruwan - (Chairman);\n\n*\tMr. D.S. Jayaweera,\n\tformer Secretary to the Ministry of Transport;\n\n*\tMr. Nihal Jayawardena P.C.; and\n\n*\tMr. Nalaka Jayaweera."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Updating of the National Physical Plan of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10310",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the new approach in the National Spatial System proposed in the policy declaration 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour', it has become necessary to update the National Physical Plan in order to integrate the proposed policy elements. \n\nAccordingly, the key objectives of the process are to provide a broader national level framework to all the development agencies to guide the planning and execution of development activities, which will directly impact upon the physical environment of the country and to establish facilities, amenities and service related infrastructure incidental upon the development of the physical environment and to devise a plan for a physical environment that will facilitate Sri Lanka to become a smart nation and a competitive economy of the world by 2030, and to remain so thereafter.\n\nTaking these matters into consideration, the presentation made by the Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities to the effect that the necessary measures are being taken by the Department of National Physical Planning to update the National Physical Plan of Sri Lanka, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Drinking Water Quality Testing and Monitoring Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10311",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The present pipe borne water supply coverage estimated to be around 51% of which 11% is covered by the water supply schemes managed by community based organizations, protected dug wells, tube wells and a programme has been initiated by the Ministry of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities for water quality testing of such water. The main stakeholders of this programme are the National Water Supply & Drainage Board, the Department of National Community Water Supply, the Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement Project and the China Sri Lanka Research Grant Project.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities to initiate the Programme of Water Quality Testing and Monitoring of the water supply schemes managed by the community based organizations, protected dug wells and tube wells from seven districts covered by the World Bank Funded Water Supply and Sanitation Improvement Project and subsequently, to extend it to the other districts as well, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Expanding of opportunities to enroll in the Interest Free Student Loan Scheme granted for students to pursue Degree Programmes at the Non Governmental Higher Education Institutes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10312",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although an Interest Free Student Loan Scheme is in existence at present, in order to follow the Government recognized degree programmes at the Non\u2011Governmental Higher Education Institutes, it has not been possible to attract students as anticipated. Specially due to the non\u2011availability of a sufficient demand in the job market for the courses selected under the said programme and as such degree programmes do not make an adequate contribution towards the economic development of the country, the said loan scheme has to be redesigned in a more productive manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation to further expand and implement the Interest Free Student Loan Scheme to enable to make 10,000 graduates competent in technology for the job opportunities available in the fields of information technology and technology, in conformity with the five year development strategic policy framework 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "National Policy on Pre School Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10313",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that the pre\u2011schools could make a greater contribution towards the development of the early childhood of the children. It has also been observed that the teachers/matrons of certain pre\u2011schools are devoid of professional competency or adequate educational qualifications. In addition, it has been found that the untrained teachers of pre\u2011schools are also engaged in a teaching process not in conformity with the development of children in the age group of 3-5 years. Taking all these matters into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to implement the National Policy on Pre\u2011School Education, prepared after obtaining the views of the experts in the field, officials and interested parties in the matter, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Establishment of the proposed National e Content Development Centre in  Pitipana area in Homagama",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10314",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to construct a National Content Development Centre for developing subject related contents/software and computer applications at the Narangala Estate in the Kuliyapitiya West Divisional Secretariat Division of the Kurunegala District, to formalize the use of information technology in schools and for education.  Considering the fact that the proposed Centre is situated about 90 km away from Colombo and the practical difficulties to be encountered by establishing the Centre in such a distant place, the proposal made by the Minister of Education, to establish the said Centre at Pitipana in the Divisional Secretariat Division of Homagama, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Tea Sector Revival and Modernization Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10315",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of making the Tea sector a key export industry in the country, it has been scheduled to  implement a programme in association with the Tea Board of Sri Lanka, Department of Commerce and relevant authorities of the Sri Lankan  missions abroad enabling to encourage Ceylon Tea importing countries to increase their imports by at least 10%  per year  from 2020. Nevertheless, difficulties encountered by the tea factory owners who play a vital role in the tea industry, have become an obstacle for the same. It has been observed that specially the restrictive finances, tax procedures implemented over the last couple of years and deregulation of prevalent rules  and regulations permitting the import of tea providing space for re export, have led for the said situation. Under these circumstances, the proposals made by the Minister of Plantation Industries and Export Agriculture pertaining to the implementation of the tea sector revival and modernization programme by converting the tea industry into a stable and competitive export earner in a manner ensuring the job security of a large number of employees engaged connected to the tea sector supply chain, was\n approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Awarding of the Contract for the Rehabilitation and Improvement of the Road Section from Kirulapona to Godagama and the Road Section from Pamankada to Pokunuvita under Southern Road Connectivity Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10316",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids  have been invited under the International Competitive Bidding Procedure  for the Rehabilitation and Improvement of the road section from Kirulapona to Godagama and the road section from Pamankada to Pokunuvita, under the Southern Road Connectivity Project funded by the Asian Development Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Roads and Highways, to award the contract to M/s MAGA Engineering (Pvt.) Ltd; which is the substantially responsive evaluated bidder for a sum of Rs.4,215.15 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Redress to Government and Semi Government employees who were subject to political victimization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10317",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that, in the recent past, charges had been framed targeting several Government and Semi Government officers with the intention of subjecting them to politically harassment and the inquiries concerned have been initiated deviating from the formal legal procedures. Therefore, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019-12-10 has granted approval to appoint a Committee under the chairmanship of the retired Supreme Court Judge Mr. Jagath Balapatabendi to examine such situations and report on same. The proposal made by the Prime Minister to appoint Mr. Sumudu K. Wickramarachchi, Attorney-at-law to function as the Secretary to that Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-02-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-01-02",
    "description": "Withdrawal of the proposed Bill on Counter Terrorism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10318",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet had been granted previously to present the Bill on Counter Terrorism in Parliament with a view to repealing the Prevention of Terrorism (Temporary Provisions) Act, No.48 of 1979 and enacting new legislation on counter terrorism. The said Bill is under consideration of the Sectoral Oversight Committee on International Relations in Parliament. Taking into consideration of the views expressed by various parties pertaining to certain provisions therein, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Relations to withdraw the said Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and the Indonesia Defense University",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10319",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development; Internal Trade, Food Security and Consumer Welfare; and State Minister of Defence, to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University and the Indonesia Defense University to work in collaboration, in matters such as, the promotion of academic cooperation, providing of mutual access to libraries, exchange of academic staff, teachers, researchers and visiting lecturers between the Institutes, providing of mutual educational trips, strategic research offers or offering of scholarships, providing of facilities for the training of academic teachers and researchers, facilities for the exchange of published academic books and records and organizing seminars, workshops, symposiums and exhibitions of mutual interest and encouraging the mutual participation at such events etc., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "'Gamata Geyak - Ratata Hetak' - A comfortable house for every family",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10320",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to commence the housing programme 'Gamata Geyak - Ratata Hetak' from the beginning of the year 2020 itself, as an expedient sustainable development programme to pave the way to achieve sustainable development goals through making every family of Sri Lanka to live in a comfortable home as enunciated in the policy statement 'A reconstructed Country with a Future'.\n\nThis programme is due to be implemented Islandwide effective from January 2020 through community committees consisting of political leadership, public officials, civil security organizations  and  community at the rural level with the coordination of the political leadership and the public officials at  the District and Divisional Secretariat level.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Prime Minister and Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities, to secure the provision required, to construct 14,022 houses, as the initial stage to provide one poor family from every Grama Niladhari Division selected on priority to provide a grant of Rs.600,000/- in installments on the basis of the construction progress of a house constructed anew or for upgrading, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Re commencement of the construction of the Court Complex at Beligaha Junction in Galle",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10321",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Human Rights & Law Reforms to re commence the partly constructed Court Complex at Beligaha Junction where the construction work has been stopped, after assigning the construction work to the State Engineering Corporation under the consultancy of the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau and to establish the Galle Court Complex at the said premises, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Food Production National Programme 2020 - 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10322",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the 'Food Production National Programme' was implemented during the period from 2016-2018 with the objective of ensuring food security, it has not been possible to achieve the targets envisaged due to the non availability of sufficient provision and the unexpected climatic conditions. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development to implement the projects such as, increasing of crop production and productivity, minimizing of post harvest losses, introduction of value added new products, research and development, minimizing of damages to crops by wild animals, increasing of the production of seeds and planting material through farm development, promotion of environment friendly agriculture through the application of traditional knowledge and practices,  promotion of agro tourism and the establishment of 'Saubhagya' Agro Production Cluster Villages, during the period from 2020-2022 at provincial and divisional level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Supply of fertilizer free of charge to paddy farmers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10323",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- Various approaches have been proposed for the empowerment of the local paddy farmer through the new government policy statement 'Saubhagyaye Dakma'. Under this, it has been planned to make an arrangement to provide the farmers with chemical fertilizer and organic fertilizer free of charge required for cultivation instead of the existing subsidized fertilizer scheme.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development to make an arrangement enabling to supply the recommended quantities of Urea, Triple Super Phosphate (T.S.P.) and  Muriate of potash (MoP) up to a maximum of 02 hectares to farmers cultivating paddy from the commencement of the Yala Season of 2020 and to implement the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of 'Multi Activity Development Task Force'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10324",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E. the President to establish a 'Multi Activity Development Task Force' as a Government Department enabling to provide opportunities to recruit 100,000 youths from the low income families with low educational qualifications, was approved by the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019 12 10. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development to create a service in the said Department as the 'Development Oriented Supportive Service' under the said Department and to recruit 100,000 youths to the said service who have passed the Grade Eight (08) from a Government School, was approved by the Cabinet"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Presenting the Gazette Notification in which Motor Traffic (Signs, Signals, Symbols and Road Markings) Regulations were published, in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10325",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Gazette Notification No.1940/21 dated 2015 11 12 has been published to publish the regulations on the road signs, signals, symbols and road markings, in terms of the provisions of the Motor Traffic Act. However, 'a sign to show 'a limited halting place for long distance service omnibuses' had not been introduced therein.  Taking into consideration the inconvenience caused by the bus drivers and as well as the passengers due to the non availability of such a sign, the Gazette Notification No.2128/9 dated 2019 06 18 has been published inclusive of a new sign to publish a limited halting place for long distance service omnibuses. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport Services Management to present the said Gazette Notification in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Proposed activity schedule for the maintenance and follow up activity of the electric fences erected for resolving the human elephant conflict",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10326",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is reported that around 80 human lives and 250 lives of elephants are lost annually due to the human elephant conflict prevalent in Sri Lanka.  In addition, it has also been identified that a considerable economic loss is caused to the country as a result of the damage caused to property and crops.  As such, the proposal made by the Minister o Environment and Wildlife Resources to set up Regulatory Committees at rural, divisional, district and national level with the representation of Government Officers to take necessary action to minimize and control the human elephant conflict and to provide instructions to the relevant District Secretaries and Divisional Secretaries in that regard, through the Secretary, Ministry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils & Local Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Procurement for the supply of 20,000 Vials of Tenecteplase Injection 40mg Vial",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10327",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Healthcare and Indigenous Medical Services to award the procurement for the supply of 20,000 Vials of Tenecteplase Injection 40mg Vial used for the prevention of death of persons suffering from heart attacks, to M/s Boehringer Ingelheim India (Pvt.) Ltd. for a total Cost and Freight price of US$ 8.75 million, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-08-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-01-08",
    "description": "Procurement for the supply of 500,000 Prefilled Syringes of Enoxaparin Sodium Injection, 4,000 IU in 0.4ml",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10328",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-08",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Procurement Appeal Board having considered the recommendations made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee of the Ministry of Healthcare and Indigenous Medical Services, pertaining to the supply of 500,000 prefilled Syringes of Enoxaparin Sodium Injection, 4,000 IU in 0.4ml used for the treatment of heart patients, has submitted its recommendations to the Cabinet in respect of the measures to be taken relating to the said procurement. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Healthcare and Indigenous Medical Services, to award the relevant procurement to M/s ABC Pharma Services (Pvt.) Ltd. at a total cost of Sri Lankan Rs.396.74 million, taking into consideration the said recommendations of the  Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
