    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10346",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Healthcare and Indigenous Medical Services to award the procurement for the supply of HLA Molecular Testing Reagents used for ensuring the  safety in Organ Transplantation, to M/s Emar Pharma (Pvt.) Ltd. at a total cost of Rs.230.69 million (without VAT) as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-14-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-01-14",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10347",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development, to award the procurement for the supply of 15,000 MT of Urea (Granular) to the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd. and the Colombo Commercial Company Fertilizer Ltd. at the rate of US$ 279.68 per MT at a total cost of US$ 4.40 million to M/s Ameropa Asia Pte Ltd. as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee (SCAPC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-14-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-01-14",
    "description": "Closure of the Policy Development Office established under the Prime Minister\u2019s Office",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10348",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Government Policy Declaration enunciated as 'Saubagyaye Dakma', a decision has been taken to implement a programme to recruit suitably qualified individuals for each and every sector in the Public  Service and hence, it has been identified that there is no necessity any further to maintain the Policy Development Office established under the Prime Minister's Office in the year 2015. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development, for the closure of the said office, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-14-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-01-14",
    "description": "Debt Relief Package Provided by the Government for Reviving the Small and Medium-Sized Entrepreneurial Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10349",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The small and Medium-Sized Entrepreneurs in the country have encountered severe problems due to their inability of obtaining new loans to expand their businesses, various fees and additional interests to be paid on non-performing loans due to the inability of serving loans continuously and the auctioning of the collateralized property by banks.\n\n\tA series of proposals has been submitted through the Government policy Framework ''Saubagyaye Dakma'' to re-energize the Small and Medium-Sized Entrepreneurial Sector, which has collapsed due to the complex taxation policies and banking laws and regulations enforced for the past few years, with a special emphasis on it.\n\n\tAccordingly, H.E the President has already directed all the Banks to suspend the legal action taken to recover the loans that have already been defaulted. \n\n\tAs its second phase, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development, to implement a  'Debt Relief Package' to grant a concessionary period to pay the capital moratorium in respect of the performing term loans as at 2019-12-31 borrowed by the Small and Medium-Sized Entrepreneures from licensed banks until 2020\u201112\u201131, upon a written request made by the borrower and to extend the tenure after the moratorium period without increasing the value of installments, to suspend all legal action relating to the recovery of non-performing loans as at 2019\u201112\u201131 and write off the total penal interest thereof, and also to grant new working capital loans, subject to the concessionary conditions, to resume businesses that have been closed due to the inability to pay off the loans, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-14-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-01-14",
    "description": "Death of three Sri Lankan Students in Azerbaijan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10350",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has been informed by the Minister of Foreign Relations that necessary action is being coordinated by the Sri Lanka Missions in Tehran with the Western Caspian University in Azerbaijan and the Embassy of Azerbaijan in Tehran, to bring the human remains of the female students who had lost their lives as a result of a blaze in an apartment in Baku,  the capital of Azerbaijan, to Sri Lanka treating it as a matter of urgency. Further, the concurrence of the Cabinet was given for the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Relations, to bare the approximate cost of Rs.1.5 million by the Government of Sri Lanka,  to bring those bodies to the country, treating this as a special circumstance on humanitarian grounds."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-14-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-01-14",
    "description": "National Programme for the Eradication of Poverty",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10351",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- The eradication of poverty in the country has been identified as one of the top priorities of the Government in order to create an inclusive and suitable development under the National Policy Framework of the Government - \u201cSaubagyaye Dakma\u201d. Further, the Development Goals identified in the said National Policy Framework of the Government are consistent with the 17 Sustainable Development Goals of the United Nations. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E. the President to implement the following proposals on priority basis with a view to eradicating the poverty in the country, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tImplementing a programme ensuring the food security of low income families by providing them with essential food items;\n\n*\tThe programme for providing 100,000 jobs for 100,000 poor families;\n\n*\tImplementing the programme for providing the poor families with houses under the programme of \u201cOne House - One Village\u201d on an accelerated basis;\n\n*\tImplementing the rural road development programme of 100,000 km to provide quality road access facilities for at least 1,000,000 households; and\n\n*\tProviding easy access to credit prioritizing the small business development, self-employment and household needs and household level livelihood development  initiatives."
  },
  {
