    "doc_id": "2020-01-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-01-22",
    "description": "The present situation in the electricity industry of Sri Lanka and the  proposed measures to avert a future power shortage",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10360",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the delay of the planned power plant projects at present, the Ceylon Electricity Board has to face a serious challenge to meet the electricity demand of the country. As such, with a view to ensuring the Sri Lanka's power security and self-sufficiency and taking into consideration of the proposals made by the Minister of Power & Energy to implement the following measures expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tconstruction of a power plant unit with a capacity of 300 x 2 MW as an extension to the Coal Power Plant at Norochcholai.\n\n*\testablishment of a Liquefied  Natural Gas (LNG) plant in the Kerawalapitiya area with a capacity of 300 MW as a joint enterprise between the Ceylon Electricity Board and India/Japan.\n\n*\taccelerating the construction activities of the Liquefied Natural Gas plant with a capacity of 300 MW proposed to be constructed in the Kerawalapitiya area under the Asian Development Bank Funds.\n\n*\taccelerating the construction activities of the hydro-power plants and the renewable energy projects being constructed by the Ceylon Electricity Board.\n\n*\timplementation of the relevant projects expeditiously with the sum of US$ 100 agreed to be provided by the Government of India for generating solar power electricity generation."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-01-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-01-22",
    "description": "The National Policy for the conservation and sustainable use of Mangrove Ecosystems in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10361",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-01-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the Mangroves Ecosystems play a crucial role in the protection of the coastal zone by maintaining its ecological equilibrium, at present such ecosystems are being under threat due to various human activities. Taking this situation into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment and Wildlife Resources, to implement the national policy prepared with a view to ensuring the sustainability of the mangrove ecosystems with the participation of all the stakeholders led by the National Expert Committee on Mangrove Conservation and Sustainable use, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
