    "doc_id": "2020-02-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-02-05",
    "description": "Implementation of the identified projects with the utilization of the  remaining funds of the Climate Resilience Improvement Project (CRIP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10367",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Climate Resilience Improvement Project initiated under the World Bank funds in the year 2014 is due to be completed by 2020\u201106\u201130. The total value of the project is US$ 152 million. In terms of the Agreements pertaining to the project, the goals anticipated are in the process of being achieved. It has been found that there is a saving of about Rs.2,500 million from the provisions allocated to the project after the completion of the activities of its identified components. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development, to allocate funds out of such saving for the constructions found as essential which were not identified at the time of designing the project and also to utilize the provisions remaining further for designing the preliminary activities identified in the Multi Phased Climate Resilience Programme implemented under the World Bank funds, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-02-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-02-05",
    "description": "The Programme for the development of a 100,000 km alternative road system",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10368",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-02-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted by the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019\u201112\u201118 to develop a 100,000 km alternative road system to facilitate a higher level of access to main roads and express ways. Accordingly, the roads to be developed will be identified taking into consideration that no renovation work had been carried out at all during the past 10 years and making use of the criteria based on matters pertaining to the number of families utilizing the ability to access, educational, medical and marketing facilities by making use of the roads.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Roads and Highways, to implement the proposed programme with the participation of the Provincial Councils and to implement certain components identified in the ongoing projects for the development of roads  under foreign funds also under the proposed programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
