    "description": "Revenue Administration Management Information System presently functioning in the Inland Revenue Department - Awarding the Contract  for the software RAMIS 2.0-Part B",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10452",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- interface with the Inland Revenue Department through the web services. Taking into consideration the necessity of expediting the implementation of  the New Inland Revenue Act, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development, to award the contract for changing the remaining part of the software RAMIS 2.0 which has been edited into a newer version as RAMIS 2.0 - Part B, to Singapore Cooperation Enterprise (SCE), to a sum of SDG 15,534,364, as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-02-27-026-en",
    "num": "26",
    "date_str": "2020-02-27",
    "description": "Measures adopted by the Sri Lanka Missions  to ensure safety and\twelfare of Sri Lankans  in Europe, Middle East East Asia regions in the\tcontext of the new Corona Virus COVID - 19 outbreak",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10453",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The new Corona epidemic has currently spread in 44 countries claiming more than 2,700 lives and infecting over 80,000 people. The Acting Minister of Foreign Relations has made aware the Cabinet that it has not been reported that  any Sri Lankan living in those countries has  been infected by the virus and on action taken by the Sri Lanka Missions of the said countries pertaining to their safety and well being. At the same time, the Cabinet noted the further information furnished by the Minister to the effect that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs continues the monitoring process of the evolving situation with a view to taking necessary steps  on any situation that could arise in future."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-02-27-027-en",
    "num": "27",
    "date_str": "2020-02-27",
    "description": "Elimination of Salary Anomalies in Principals' and the Teachers' Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10456",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-02-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the issues prevailing for many years, pertaining to the salaries and service conditions of teachers, principals and other professionals related to the field of education, the National Policy Framework of the Government ''A Reconstructed Country with a Future-Vistas of Prosperity and Splendor'' has pointed out the necessity of formulating a suitable salary structure after preparing a Salary and Service Minute having integrated the Sri Lanka Teacher's Service and all other related services in the field of education.  Even though, the Government has already taken a policy decision to take action accordingly, the Minister of Education has made a detailed clarification to the Cabinet, regarding the situation emerged due to the salary anomalies of the principals and the teachers' services. \n\n\tH.E the President recently has appointed a National Pay Commission to study the salaries in the public sector and formulate a new salary structure enabling  to remove the salary anomalies and the Government anticipates to implement  recommendations of the said Commission through the budget to be submitted in Parliament. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided that action be taken to remove the salary anomalies presently existing in the Principals and the Teachers' Services as well, on the recommendations of the said Commission."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Developing and implementing the National Financial Inclusion Strategy (NFIS) for Sri Lanka to improve the Financial Inclusiveness in the Country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10457",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The concept of 'Inclusive Finance' is about making available the formal financial services timely at an affordable cost to all individuals and enterprises of the economy. The proposed national methodology of financial inclusiveness anticipates to provide opportunities to all citizens of the country to gain access to the financial products and services such as payments, savings, credit, insurance and retirement products.\n\n\tThe Central Bank of Sri Lanka with the technical and financial assistance of the International Finance Corporation, has prepared the National Financial Inclusion Strategy and an Action Plan with the contribution of the relevant stakeholders to improve the financial inclusiveness in Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development, to implement the said National Financial Inclusion Strategy in accordance with the Action Plan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Granting lands of the Kalutara Bodhi premises by a free grant to the Kalutara Bodhi Trust Board as a definitive grant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10458",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Seven plots of lands in extent of about 7.5 acres, developed by the Kalutara Bodhi Trust Board, have been given over to the said Trust Board by the Land Commissioner General on three long term leases and the Trust Board has made a request to the said Department to grant another plot of land on lease basis. Since all the lands given on lease basis have been developed well and also as granting the lands requested to the Kalutara Bodhi Trust will be of great significance to the development of the 'Pooja Area' it has been found that it is appropriate to vest the said plots of land on a free grant. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs, to grant the said plots of land presently given on lease basis to the Kalutara Bodhi Trust Board as a definitive grant and the remaining plots of land which have been developed and utilized presently to be given to the said Bodhi Trust on a long term lease, subject to taking them back without payment of compensation for the extent so acquired, in the event that such lands are required in the future for the development activities of the area, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "'Setting up of a Permanent Institutional Framework for the Conservation and Promotion of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Sri Lanka'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10459",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'The International Convention for Safeguarding of the Intangible Cultural Heritage' has been adopted in the year 2003 with a view to safeguarding the intangible cultural heritage for the future generations and Sri Lanka has given its concurrence to the Convention in the year 2008. Especially, the social customs and formalities, pageants, publications, knowledge, skills, cultural spaces and the items and tools bound thereto, exist as intangible cultural heritage and Sri Lanka is bound, to safeguard these intangible cultural heritage in the face of the challenges posed by westernization, globalization, commercialization and changes, to promote them and to prepare an appropriate approach for same, in terms of the said International Convention.\n\n\tSince, the unavailability of a separate institute for this purpose at present has become a barrier in implementing the terms of the above Convention expeditiously and accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs, to establish a special unit to carry out the activities of the intangible cultural heritage, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Celebration of the 175th Anniversary of the Royal Asiatic Society of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10460",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Royal Asiatic Society of Sri Lanka, established in the year 1845, is an institution set by the then administration of the Grate Britain to fulfill the main objectives of identifying the development and investment feasibility, preparation of the governing structure and launching of the academic research process to get an understanding on the historical and cultural background of the rural community of this country and having analyzed such information has assisted in the matters of the Government by making recommendations in that regard to the Government, during the colonial era. As such, it has functioned as a renowned institution during the colonial times of Grate Britain and the Governor General has functioned as the ex officio patron of the Society.  At the same time, several famous scholars at the time like Sir Ponnambalam Arunachalam, Messers H.C.P. Bell, Pole E. Peiris, P.E.P. Deraniyagala, Senarath Paranawithana, G.C. Mendis, C.E. Godakumbura and G.P. Malalasekara had functioned as active members of the Society.\n\n\tThe 175th Anniversary of this Society fell on the 07th of February this year and a special programme had been prepared to commemorate it. For the appreciation of the remarkable mission and the functions carried out by of the Society in respect of the progress of this country, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs, to allocate a provision amounting to Rs.15 million to cover the cost pertaining to the celebration of this anniversary, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Providing of 150,000 Domestic Drinking Water Connections",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10461",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- At present, the National Water Supply & Drainage Board (NWSDB) has provided 2.4 million water connections covering 41% of the population of Sri Lanka and the NWSDB provides generally 110,000 domestic drinking water connections annually. However, it has been difficult to provide the consumers of some areas with the domestic drinking water connections even when there is an excess of capacity, because of the need of additional pipe extensions to cover the areas/roads that have not been covered by the existing distribution network, need for the consumers to pay the initial connection fee of around Rs.20,000/- and the road reinstatement charges. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities, to launch an accelerated programme for providing 150,000 domestic drinking water connections during the first 2 quarters of the year 2020, taking necessary action to do away with the aforesaid obstacles, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Allocation of the lands belonging to the Urban Development Authority (UDA) for development",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10462",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has decided on 2020 02 07 to confer authority on the Board of Management of the Urban Development Authority for leasing out lands not exceeding 1 acre within the District of Colombo and lands not exceeding 2 acres, outside the District of Colombo, belonging to the Urban Development Authority.  Accordingly, the information provided by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities, regarding the progress made on the 23 plots of land disposed during the period from 2016 to 2019 with the approval of the Minister in charge of the subject under section 18(1) of the Urban Development Authority Act, No.41 of 1978, having approved by the Board of Management of the UDA, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Continuation of the Sri Lanka International Arbitration Centre",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10463",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet had granted approval to establish a Sri Lanka International Arbitration Centre as a regional hub in the year 2012, for resolving disputes arising out of International Commercial Agreements and other International affairs.  Further, the Cabinet had approved to establish the Sri Lanka International Arbitration Centre as a limited guarantee company in the year 2015 and accordingly, the Sri Lanka International Arbitration Centre (Guarantee) Limited Company has been incorporated on 2016 12 20.  \n\n\tWhile certain countries are engaged in generating a colossal sum of income by way of involving in the international arbitration, the establishment of an International Arbitration Centre in Sri Lanka as well and resorting to action to get the international arbitration pertaining to commercial matters in the region attracted to the International Arbitration Centre in Sri Lanka will make it economically beneficial to Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Human Rights & Law Reforms, to continue the International Arbitration Centre independently, was noted by the Cabinet.\n\n\tAt the same time, the Cabinet further decided that when including the provisions related to arbitration in the agreements entered into in future by the Government Institutions, to include the said provisions as well to the effect that arbitration activities should be carried out by the International Arbitration Centre in Sri Lanka."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Construction of Permanent Houses with New Technology Concrete Panels for conflict affected people in the Northern and Eastern Provinces of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10464",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet had granted approval previously, for the construction of 28,000 concrete panel cost effective permanent houses (at a cost of Rs.1,280,000/- per house) for the conflict affected families in the Northern and Eastern Provinces of Sri Lanka and as at its initial stage to construct 7,000 calicut tile roof houses.\n\n\tNevertheless, due to the inability of securing the required funds for the project as expected, the General Treasury had taken the necessary action to get a term loan facility from the Bank of Ceylon to construct 1,000 houses initially.  Accordingly, the information submitted by the Minister of Community Empowerment and Estate Infrastructure Development, that a commercial agreement has already been signed with the contractor, M/s YAPKA Development (Pvt.) Ltd., selected for the construction of the 1,000 houses utilizing the said loan and that the activities of the relevant project has been commenced on 2020 02 21, was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Regulation of the Issuance of Television and Broadcasting Licenses -",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10465",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, license are issued for private broadcasting and telecasting in accordance with the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Act, No.37 of 1966 and the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation Act, No.06 of 1982 for conducting Broadcasting and Telecasting Services. As such, by now 27 private broadcasting licenses and 54 telecasting licenses have been issued. Nevertheless, only 18 broadcasting licenses and 28 telecasting licenses are in use.  A Committee appointed to study the process related to the issuance of licenses, has shown the necessity of having a separate institution to carry out the activities of the broadcasting and telecasting media both and has submitted a draft named as the ''Broadcasting Regulatory Commission''.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Information and Mass Media, to appoint a Committee comprising of experienced intellectuals in the field to review the draft further and make recommendations and to investigate the possibility of amending the provisions of the Sri Lanka Telecommunication Regulatory Commission Act, to enable it to perform the task of the process of issuing Broadcasting and Telecasting Licenses, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Improving the Master Control Room Complex of the Independent Television Network,  pioneer Television Channel of Sri Lanka with the state of the art technology and relocating it",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10466",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Independent Television Network has been inaugurated on the 05th of June 1979 as the first ever television channel of Sri Lanka and in the whole of the 40 year period up to the present, its Master Control Room has been housed in the building constructed initially. At present, a new building has been constructed for the Master Control Room Complex with the required facilities.  As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Information and Mass Media, to take appropriate action to establish the said Master Control Room Complex consisting of the equipment with new technology necessary for digital transmission at the new building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Formulation of a National Fertilizer Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10467",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Fertilizer Act, No.68 of 1988 has provided the necessary legal provision to regulate the importation, production, preparation and distribution of fertilizer. The said Act has not been subject to any amendment so far and although action has already been formulated to upgrade the Act to suite the present needs, the absence of a formal national fertilizer policy declaration up to date, is seen as a major  impediment to the progress of the said field. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development, to appoint a committee comprising of experts in the field to formulate a National Fertilizer Policy and to prepare the final draft, after obtaining the views of the other relevant stakeholders and the general public on the draft so prepared, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-03-04-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-03-04",
    "description": "Food Security for Low Income Earners",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10468",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-03-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- At its meeting held on 2020 01 14, the Cabinet granted approval to the proposal made by H.E. the President to implement a programme called 'The National Programme for eradication of Poverty', to ensure the food security of low income earners by the provision of essential food items. Accordingly, it has been planned to implement the said programme expeditiously as follows and the information provided by the Minister of Internal Trade, Food Security and Consumer Welfare in this respect, was noted by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tprovision of a bag of essential food items to 1,000,000 (one million) beneficiaries including the disabled persons, widows, adults without a permanent source of income and those suffering from chronic diseases.\n>br>\n*\tprovision of food items for the current market value of approximately Rs.1,007/- including tea leaves, nadu rice, flovour (normal), dhal and dry fish/sprats/locally canned salmon fish to the selected beneficiaries for a price of Rs.500/- .\n\n*\timplementation of the programme with the participation of Lanka Sathosa, cooperative trade network and the selected  franchised sales outlets in the rural areas."
  },
  {
