    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Education has been continuously providing free school uniform materials to the students of the Government schools and Government aided schools and also to the student bhikkus and lay students of Government approved pirivenas, since 1993. Instead of providing uniform materials, a system of providing gift vouchers has been implemented for this purpose during the period from 2015-2020.\n\nDue to the COVID 19 pandemic prevailing in the country, the export income has been reduced and therefore, it has been found appropriate to produce school uniforms locally by encouraging local textile manufacturers, taking into consideration that the cost of foreign exchange to be incurred for the purpose is also very high. Accordingly, Cabinet approval was granted to provide uniform materials in future instead of granting vouchers and to obtain required stock of uniform materials from the local textile manufactures that are registered under the Ministry of Industry and Supply Chain Management."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Construction of a new interchange on the Southern Expressway at Bedigama for the Tangalle - Weeraketiya Road",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10505",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found that, there is a possibility of attracting more expressway users by constructing a new interchange at Bedigama, for the road section of Tangalle - Weeraketiya. As such, approval of the Cabinet has been granted to construct the proposed new interchange and to utilize the balance of the amount used for the construction of the Section II of the Southern Expressway."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Introduction of minimum specifications for buses used for public passenger transportation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10506",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Nearly, 26,985 buses are presently being used by the Sri Lanka Transport Board and the Private Sector for passenger transportation and almost all of them are made on truck chassis meant for transportation of goods. It has been observed that passengers are jolted and made uncomfortable when brakes are applied as those are made for transportation of goods. Therefore, Cabinet approval was granted to appoint a Cabinet Sub Committee comprising of the following Ministers in order to further consider the matters mentioned in the report submitted by the Committee appointed to prepare the technical specifications and criteria in order to enable the passengers to travel in comfort, to be considered when importing buses to the country in the future, with the participation of the relevant officials and to submit its recommendations to the Cabinet.\n\n*\tMinister of Transport Service Management\n\n*\tMinister of Industries and Supply Chain Management\n\n*\tMinister of Education"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Tax exemptions for execution of the Railway Track Rehabilitation Project from Maho to Omanthai under the Indian Line of Credit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10507",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval was granted to implement the Railway Track Rehabilitation Project from Maho to Omanthai under the Indian Line of Credit, at the meeting held on 2019 04 02. Now, it has been decided by the Cabinet to declare this Project as a special project to allow exemptions from the payment of the relevant taxes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Obtaining additional provisions for forming infrastructure facilities essential for the e-motoring Project of the Department of the Motor Traffic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10508",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract to implement the e-Motoring Project, which has been planned to transform the departmental services to public centric nature, has been awarded to Metropolitan Advanced Technologies Pvt Limited and agreement thereof has been signed in July 2018. Even though, the Head Office premises at Narahenpita and the District Office premises of the Department have to be appropriately organized in order to implement to the Project, nonreceipt of allocations needed for such infrastructure facilities has resulted in the delay in implementing the same. Therefore, Cabinet approval was granted to provide the necessary allocations through the forthcoming Budget to accomplish the essential and urgent tasks in order to implement the Project as planned."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Implementation of Solar Power Projects under the Indian Lines of Credit",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10509",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has extended its consensus to grant USD 100 million under Indian Lines of Credit through the EXIM Bank of India in order to accomplish the targets of integrating renewable energy to the energy sector in the Country through implementing solar power projects, in line with 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour' policy framework. Accordingly, Cabinet approval was granted to implement the relevant projects by giving the priority for provision of electricity to the government buildings by installation of solar power generation systems on roofs of those buildings and to selected low income families in the Mannar, Trincomalee, Moneragala, Anuradhapura and Hambantota districts and meet their power requirements by provision of solar power generation systems to their housing units."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Release of Pine Plantations belonging to the Department of Forest Conservation and the Land Reforms Commission for Oleoresin extraction on the basis of a charge",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10510",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval was granted to take necessary action for the selection of suitable institutions following the competitive bidding procedure, for Oleoresin extraction in the Pine Plantations belonging to the Department of Forest Conservation and the Land Reforms Commission in extent of 6,200 hectares."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-022-en",
    "num": "22",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Allocation of land near the Mirisawetiya Maha Viharaya, Anuradhapura to the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10511",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Circuit Bungalow of the Forest Department is located in a 2 Acre 22.6 perch land plot adjoining the Mirisawetiya MahaViharaya. The Department of Archaeology has informed that no new constructions should be done there since this land is situated within the Anuradhapura sacred city and it is an area with archaeological ruins. The Chief Incumbent of the Mirisavatiya Viharaya has requested this land for the Miriswetiya Viharaya for the ease of carrying out religious and social activities of the temple in the future as the relevant land plot is situated adjoining the Mirisawetiya Maha Viharaya. Accordingly, the Cabinet approval was given to allocate this land to the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs to be transferred to the Mirisawetiya Maha Viharaya upon the approval of the Sacred Area Development Committee in future when formally declaring the boundaries of the said sacred area."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-10-023-en",
    "num": "23",
    "date_str": "2020-06-10",
    "description": "Granting relief for the tourist industry during the post COVID-19 pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10512",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-10",
    "decision_details_body": "As a redress to minimizing the impact on the tourist industry due to the COVID 19 pandemic conditions and normalizing the industry; approval of the Cabinet of Ministers was granted for implementing a relief programme for institutions and individuals engaged in the tourist industry as follows.\n\n- \tProviding loan facilities on the basis of paying back within a period of 05 years with a 2 year grace period under an interest of 4% for payment of salaries of Rs.20,000/- per head for a period of six months for the staffs of tourist hotels, tour management companies/travel agents registered under the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority.\n\n-\tProviding loan facilities for the payment of Rs.15,000/- each for a period of six months serving in the other institutions related to tourism including restaurants, cafeterias, spa and wellness centres registered under the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority.\n\n-\tOne-off payment of Rs.20,000/- per tour guide registered under the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority to be dispensed by the by Sri Lanka Tourist Development Authority.\n\n-\tOne-off payment of Rs.15,000/- per tourist driver registered under the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority to be dispensed by the Sri Lanka Tourist Development Authority.\n\n-\tProviding facilities to pay the electricity and water bills payable from 01st March 2020 to 31st August from 01st September 2020 in 12 equal installments and not to disconnect power or water supply during that period.\n\n-\tExtending the grace period of 06 months given for payment of vehicle leasing installments related to the tourism industry up to 12 months without any delayed charges."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Utilizing the funds allocated under the Contingent Emergency Response Components of the World Bank Group financed investment projects  for the projects to be implemented on priority basis, due to the COVID 19 pandemic situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10513",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that it is necessary to provide financial assistance for the  uplifting the agricultural sector, implementing the e-education platform, establishment of an online platform for home-based work , disaster management as well as the prevention of spreading the disease while using public transport sectors,  immediately, since the country is facing a wide range of impacts other than the health sector due to COVID-19 pandemic situation. Therefore, the Cabinet of Ministers has approved the proposal submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development for taking necessary measures to enable to utilize  US$ 56 million that has been included under the Contingent Emergency Response Components of (04) investment projects funded by the World Bank Group in the projects to be immediately implemented in the sectors mentioned above."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Programme - 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10514",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Programme is being implemented since the year of 2010 for providing opportunities for the executive level public sector officers to undergo postgraduate courses in the recognized Universities in Japan and under the grant the Government of Japan has given their consent to grant an amount of Japanese Yen 269 million (approximately Rs. 457 million) to facilitate the government officials who are to commence their studies from September 2020.  Accordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development for accepting the aforementioned grant and signing the agreements relating to the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Extension of the period of contract awarded to the State Printing Corporation for printing and supplying new Lottery \"Daru Diri Sampatha\" drawn by the National Lotteries Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10515",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "The agreement period of the contract awarded to the State Printing Corporation for the printing of the \"Daru Diri Sampatha\" lottery ticket by the National Lotteries Board with the objective of raising funds for the \"Save the children National Trust Fund\" has expired on 12.05.2020. However, the procurement procedure commenced for selecting a suitable printer after the said contract period has not yet been completed due to Corona pandemic. Therefore, the proposal made by  the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development to extend the contract awarded to the State Printing Corporation for the printing of lottery tickets, for a further period of 06 months from 2020.05.13 to 2020.11.12, so as to get the work done by the State Printing Corporation itself under the previously agreed  specifications and price, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Japanese Yen 800 million Non project Japanese Grant Aid of for supplying medical equipment required for COVID 19 pandemic prevention activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10516",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Japan has agreed to provide Japanese Yen 800 million (approximately Rs. 1,360 million) under the Japanese non\u2011project grant scheme for the supply of medical equipment required for strengthening the activities pertaining to the prevention of COVID-19 pandemic situation within Sri Lanka. Medical equipment such as MRI Scanner, CT Scanner, Bedside X\u2011Ray Systems, Central Monitors, Bedside Monitors and Defibrillators etc. can be supplied under that. Accordingly, the proposal made by the the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development to obtain the said grant aid as well as to sign the relevant agreements in this regard was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Procurement for the supply of Full Cream Milk Powder to the Sri Lanka Thriposha Limited for the Production of Thriposha for the year 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10517",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the approval of the Cabinet of Ministers, Milco (Pvt.) Ltd. has been awarded the contract for  supplying milk powder required for the manufacturing of Thriposha from the year 2014 to 2019 with the objective of strengthening the economy of the local dairy farmers. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal submitted by the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medical Services for the procurement of 720 metric tons of full cream milk powder required for the production of Thriposha for the year 2020 / 2021 for Sri Lanka Thriposha Ltd., the Cabinet granted approval to procure the said quantity of milk powder from Milco (Pvt.) Ltd. itself."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Temporary suspension of the Tea Promotion and Marketing Levy imposed on the tea exports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10518",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "Continuous maintenance of the operational activities of tea factories, relative decline of the procurement power of most of the countries that import tea, supply chain management issues as well as continuous maintenance of quality in the products are the major issues that were faced by the tea industry amidst the COVID 19 pandemic conditions, prevailing within the country at present. Therefore, the Cabinet of Ministers has approved the proposal forwarded by the Minister of Plantation Industries and Export Agriculture to temporarily suspend the tea promotion and marketing tax of  Rs.3.50 already charged on each kilogram of tea exported from the registered exporters, for a period of 06 months as a financial relief granted to stabilize the tea industry amidst the said difficulties."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-17-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-06-17",
    "description": "Granting the Strategic Project Development Status and incentives for the proposed investment in Colombo Port City by CHEC Port City Colombo (Private) Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10519",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Tri-Partite agreement has been signed in August 2016 between the Government of Sri Lanka, the Urban Development Authority and the locally incorporated CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd. and accordingly actions have been taken to reclaim 440 hectares of land under the said project. In terms of the provisions of the relevant agreement, an extent of 116 hectares of land from the said extent has to be leased to the Project Company CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd. Accordingly, the said Company has submitted a proposal to the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka to implement a mixed development project comprising of 05 pillars / buildings in an area of 6.8 hectares out of the extent of land proposed to be given on lease. The project with an investment of US$ 01 billion is proposed to be implemented in two phases comprised of first phase for US$ 400 million and the second phase for US$ 600 million. Considering the strategic importance and the magnitude of the project, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal submitted by the Minister of Industrial Exports and Investment Promotion for the publication of relevant Gazette Notifications under the Strategic Development Projects Act, enabling to provide incentive allowances relevant for the said investments in terms of the provisions of the Strategic Development Projects (Amendment) Act, No.14 of 2008 and the Sri Lanka Board of Investment (Amendment) Act, No.4 of 1978."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Financing the projects implemented by the Road Development Authority and the National Water Supply and Drainage Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10520",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction activities of Section II of the Central Expressway Project are being carried out at present while measures have been taken to initiate the construction works of the section I of the same. Further, the project activities for the rehabilitation of roads in extent of 100,000km has commenced and are being carried out at present. Accordingly, the Road Development Authority has to secure an amount of Rs. 50 billion in order to make payments relating to the projects carried out by the said Authority. In addition to that, an amount of Rs. 30 billion is also required to settle the essential financial commitments pertaining to the projects undertaken by the National Water supply and Drainage Board. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development to authorize the relevant authorities of the two institutions to obtain funds from the local banks including Bank of Ceylon, People's Bank and National Savings Bank and to issue the Treasury Guarantees for the purpose was approved by the Cabinet ."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Further increase of the Financing Assistance from the International Development Association (IDA) of the World Bank Group (WBG) agreed to be made for COVID-19 Emergency Response",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10521",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The International Development Association of the World Bank Group has agreed for the use of US$ 60 million of uncommitted funds, of the following projects funded by the International Development Association (IDA) to fund for the programs targeted at COVID-19 affected social segments.\n\n* \tTransport Connectivity and Asset Management Project\n* \tEcosystem conservation and management Project\n*\tClimate Smart Irrigated Agriculture Project\n\n\tFurther, The International Development Association (IDA) has agreed to provide US$ 05 million from the Transitional Support Facility of the International Development Association and US$ 1.72 million grant from the Pandemic Emergency Financing Facility. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development to obtain the said funds was approved by the Cabinet of Ministers on June 3, 2020.\n\n\tSubsequently, the International Development Association (IDA) has agreed to provide an additional US$ 22.24 million under the Transitional Support Credit Facility. Accordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal presented by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development to increase the total amount of funds to be obtained up to US$ 87.24 million and to utilize these funds for social security measures targeting the adversely affected segments of the society due to the COVID\u201119 outbreak."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Relief measures taken by the Ministry of Foreign Relations and the Sri Lanka Missions abroad to address the issues related to vulnerable segments of Overseas Sri Lankans amidst the COVID-19 Global Pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10522",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- Minister of Foreign Affairs presented the following measures taken by the Ministry of Foreign Relations and the Sri Lanka Missions abroad to address the issues related to the vulnerable segments of overseas Sri Lankans amidst the COVID-19 Global Pandemic to the attention of the Cabinet.\n\n* 52,401 Sri Lankans in 117 countries have made requests to be repatriated to Sri Lanka by June 16, 2020. \n\n* The Presidential Secretariat together with the COVID Task Force by now, have facilitated in repatriating to Sri Lanka more than 9,580 Sri Lankans from 38 countries.\n\n*\tFurther, Ten flights have been scheduled from 24th June to 7th July to repatriate Sri Lankans from 10 other countries.\n\n*\tOver Rs. 42.6 million have been disbursed to the Sri Lanka Missions abroad for providing dry rations, basic medicines, protective gears and safe transportation to vulnerable segments in the Middle East and other locations.\n\n*\tSteps have been taken to dispatch 5,000 packs worth Rs. 15.5 million containing dry rations and medicines to Maldives, UAE and Qatar where there is a shortage of goods and difficulty in purchasing dry rations.\n\n* \tDiplomatic representations are made by the Sri Lanka Missions on behalf of the Sri Lankans overseas pertaining to their needs and maintain continuous contact with the said Sri Lankans.\n\n*\tNecessary measures have been taken to provide the required services from the nearest Sri Lankan Diplomatic Missions to the Sri Lankans living in countries where the Sri Lankan Missions are not functioning. \n\n\n*\tMeasures are being taken by the Sri Lankan Diplomatic Missions to identify new markets and increase the demand in existing markets in order to mitigate the economic impact to Sri Lanka of the global pandemic and to revive the economy."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Awarding the contract for the construction of buildings and infrastructure facilities of the Faculty of Computing and Technology of the University of Kelaniya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10523",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation to award the contract for the construction of the buildings and infrastructure facilities of the Faculty of Computing and Technology of the University of Kelaniya under the 'Science and Technology Human Resources Development Project' implemented through funds of the Asian Development Bank (ADB), to a sum of Rs 3,032.70 million (without VAT), to M/s Maga - ICC Joint Venture, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Preparation of an arrangement for the proper distribution of chemical fertilizer among farmers required for other crops excluding paddy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10524",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development has implemented several programmes namely \u2018Sawbagye Gewaththa\u2019 and the programme for cultivation of 16 identified field crops within 88,000 hectares so as to avoid the possible inconveniences with regard to the food security due to the restrictive factors imposed on the imports and exports consequent to the COVID - 19 global pandemic situation. Therefore in this context, having informed of the programme expected to be implemented along with the following by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development for the distribution of chemical fertilizer through a rational arrangement without any shortage to the cultivators of other crops except paddy, the Cabinet of Ministers noted the said contents. \n\n* \tEncouraging to use organic fertilizer for the small scale agricultural cultivations including \u2018Sawbagye Gewaththa\u2019 while providing an opportunity to buy less than 10 kilograms of chemical fertilizer from the market only if required.\n\n*\tProviding 50% of the required amount of fertilizer ration approved for non\u2011 paddy crops from the open market while the remaining 50% to be issued through the Agrarian Development Centres.\n\n* \tProviding the chemical fertilizer subsidy required for the vegetable, fruit, and other agricultural cultivations implemented under the supervision of the Department of Agriculture, Provincial Agriculture Departments and the Sri Lanka Mahaweli Authority through the Agrarian Development Centres.\n * Preparation of a methodology to obtain the fertilizer required for the cultivators from the open market based on a receipt issued by the Agricultural Research and Production Assistant when there are no required stocks of fertilizer at the Agrarian Development Centres or when it is apparent to have delays in the required stocks."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Extension of Contract between the Ceylon Shipping Corporation (CSC) and M/s United Shippers Limited on Lightering (Barging) for Discharging of Coal from ships to the jetty of the Lakvijaya Coal Power Plant",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10525",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract agreement between the Ceylon Shipping Corporation and the M/s United Shippers Ltd of India for disembarkation of coal from barges from the ships to Lakwijaya Coal Power Plant has expired from April 2020. Therefore, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Ports and Shipping and the Minister of Power and Energy to extend the said contract agreement for a further period of one year until 2020/2021, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Tax Relief Measures to Facilitate Post COVID 19 Economic Recovery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10526",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- A simple, transparent and efficient tax system was introduced to all stakeholders in the economy including Small and Medium Entrepreneurs by the Cabinet decision dated 26th of November 2019 on the Note to the Cabinet on 'Economic Revival Initiatives' submitted by His Excellency the President. Since the economy is facing a drastic challenge consequent to the COVID-19 pandemic, it has been an essential factor to implement tax administrative measures by giving sufficient space to commence the business operations of especially the Small and Medium Scale Entrepreneurs to ease their tax burden.\n\nAccordingly, Cabinet approval was granted by its decision dated 2020-06-03 to exempt the penalty relating to all type of taxes during the COVID-19 lockdown period and to re\u2011commence the collection of the penalty for late payments from July 2020. \n\nApart from that the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal submitted by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic and Policy Development in regard to providing the following relief measures also to the Small and Medium Scale Entrepreneurs, to amend the legal provisions accordingly and to implement the proposed relief measures with immediate effect until such time the legal provisions are operative. \n\n*\tIf the Commissioner General of Inland Revenue is satisfied that no willful evasion of the payment of tax has been taken place, to waive off the income tax in arrears payable on the assessment issued up to the assessment year 2018 / 2019.\n\n*\tNon\u2011issuance of additional assessments for the assessment year 2019 / 2020 in regard to the Small and Medium Scale Entrepreneurs who paid tax by submitting income tax reports. \n*\tExtension of the period provided for the submission of the bank guarantee or the non\u2011refundable cash payment required to be made when submitting an appeal to the Tax Appeals Commission.\n*\tGranting a grace period to settle the taxes that have already been agreed upon with the Department of Inland Revenue in arrears / default. \n*\tSuspending the implementation of the seizure notices issued to the banks until 30th April 2021.\n*\tEnable the payment or / obtaining of tax reports of a particular tax applicable for the period of 01st March 2020 to 30th June 2020, on the 31st December 2020 or prior to that, and to treat that the relevant payment of tax / submission the report was done on the due date."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-06-24-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-06-24",
    "description": "Approval for the restriction of foreign exchange outflows from the country and to issue orders on the foreign exchange deposit account",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10527",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-06-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers at its meeting held on 01st April 2020 granted approval to temporally suspend certain outward remittances for a period of three (03) months, and accordingly, the relevant Order was issued by the Gazette Notification dated 02nd April 2020 as per the provisions of the section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act.\n\nFurther, approval of the Cabinet of Ministers was granted at the meeting held on 22nd April 2020 for taking necessary measures to encourage the remittance of foreign currency to the country through Special Deposit Accounts.\n\nIn terms of the said Cabinet decisions, relevant Regulations were issued under sections 22 and 29 of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017 by the Gazette Notifications 02.04.2020 and 08.04.2020 respectively. \n\nFurthermore, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the following proposals submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development for taking measures applicable to the said Orders.\n\n* \tExtending the period of the Gazette Notification relating to the Orders applicable to the restrictions of the outward remittances by another six (06) months from 02nd July 2020.\n\n\n\n*\tIssuance of a new Gazette Notification amending the existing Gazette Notification dated 08.04.2020 relating to the Regulations made under section 29 of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017 in order to address constrains prevailing due to the provisions in the laws applicable to Foreign Exchange Act and Anti-Money laundering and Combating the Financing of Terrorism when implementing the methodologies introduced for encouraging the remittance of foreign exchange into the country through the Special Deposit Account."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Loans, Grants and material assistance received by the Government of Sri Lanka (GOSL) in support of COVID 19 response initiatives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10528",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet of Ministers considered the information furnished by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development in relation to the contributions received during the period up to 2020 06 12 as loans, grants and material assistance by the Government of Sri Lanka from several countries and international organizations for the initial steps to be taken in relation to the control of the global pandemic conditions of COVID 19.\n\nAccordingly, the World Bank has agreed to provide US$ 128.6 million for the Sri Lanka COVID 19 Emergency Response and Health Systems Preparedness Project while another US$ 45 million to be provided under the Social Security Network Project.\n\nIt was brought to the attention of the Cabinet of Ministers that US$ 57.5 million out of the agreed amount under the Sri Lanka COVID 19 Emergency Response and Health Systems Preparedness Project as well as the total amount of provision of US$ 45 million agreed under the Social Security Network Project have been received to the country by now.\n\nIn addition to that, the Cabinet of Ministers noted that the donations to the value of approximately US$ 75 million and another stock of material assistance to the value of about US$ 8 million too have been received by the Government up to the above mentioned date."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Obtaining Provisions for the payment of salaries to the employees of the Central Cultural Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10529",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Central Cultural Fund has encountered a grave financial crisis by now and it has led to difficulties in bearing the salaries of the employees and other expenditure. Therefore, the request made by the said Fund for obtaining a provision of Rs.135 million monthly under the prevailing circumstances was brought into the notice of the Cabinet by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Cultural and Religious Affairs. Accordingly, the approval of the Cabinet of Ministers was granted to facilitate in obtaining a Short Term Loan grant from a local bank with the intervention of the General Treasury as a remedy to the issues confronted by the aforementioned Fund and to make necessary arrangement for the settlement of the said loan increasing the income of the Central Cultural Fund once tourism is restored in the country in the time to come."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Purchase of Food Items to the Department of Prisons for the year 2019/2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10530",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the contract to procure food items to the Department of Prisons for the year 2019 / 2020 is due to be expired on 2020 07 31, it has not been able to carry out the procurement procedure for the selection of new suppliers as a result of the COVID 19 pandemic condition. Therefore, considering the present situation experienced by the country as well as the current market conditions, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal furnished by the Minister of Justice, Human Rights and Legal Reforms for awarding the contract for the purchase of food items required by the Department of Prisons to the current supplier itself from 2020 08 01 to 2021 01 31, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Procurement of Fertilizer - 2020 (for the month of July)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10531",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- International competitive bids have been invited for the procurement of fertilizer for the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd (Lak Pohora) and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Ltd. (Commercial Fertilizer) for the requirement of fertilizer during the month of July 2020. The Cabinet having considered the recommendation made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee with regard to the said prices, the covering approval was granted to the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development for awarding the procurement of fertilizer supply as mentioned follows:\n\n*\tTo procure 9,000 + 5% metric tons of Urea (Granular) from Agri Commodities & Finance FZE for a sum of US$ 260.00 per metric ton.\n\n*\tTo procure 6,000 + 5% metric tons of Triple Super Phosphate from Aries Fertilizer Group Pvt. Ltd., for a sum of US$ 249.07 per metric ton."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Establishment of the Ministry of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development in the 'Govijana Mandiraya",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10532",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Necessary actions have been taken by now to re establish the Ministry of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development in the 'Govijana Mandiraya' in terms of the approval granted by the Cabinet of Ministers on 2019 12 18. However, the layout of the building should be re arranged to and the electricity supply system should be renovated to establish the Ministry and carry out its functions. Therefore, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal submitted by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development for the direct awarding of the contract for the consultancy services relevant to the said renovation activities to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau (CECB) and the contract for the construction activities to the Central Engineering Services (Pvt) Limited since the relevant activities should be attended urgently."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Providing an opportunity to buy chemical fertilizer used for paddy, for other agricultural activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10533",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the fertilizer subsidized programme implemented at present, fertilizer is issued for paddy cultivations up to 05 acres while the fertilizer required for the lands exceeding the said extent should be purchased from the open market. Under these circumstances, a shortage of fertilizer used for other crops has been created in the open market since the demand for fertilizer has been increased due to the escalation of the extent of land under cultivation especially as a result of COVID 19 pandemic situation. Therefore, the Cabinet of Ministers noted the information furnished by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development on the action taken for purchasing stocks of remaining fertilizer with the state fertilizer companies imported under the fertilizer subsidized programme for paddy cultivation, by the Agrarian Development Centres and selling a bag of fertilizer of 50kg to a sum of Rs.1000/- to the farmers so that the farmers can purchase the fertilizer stocks required without creating any issues to the government."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-01-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-07-01",
    "description": "Extension of the period of the loan pertaining to the Asian Development Bank funded Northern Road Connectivity Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10534",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-01",
    "decision_details_body": "- Renovation of National Highways and Provincial Roads and newly construction of new selected bridges of the Northern and North Central Provinces are being carried out under the Asian Development Bank funded Northern Road Connectivity Project. For this purpose funds up to US$ 98 million are provided by the Asian Development Bank. Two (02) additional contract packages of the Medavachchiya - Horowpathatna road have been awarded in the month of March 2019 out of the savings of the loan. Although it has been scheduled to complete the construction activities of the said project before the 2020 06 30 which was the loan closing date it has not been possible to complete the same. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Roads and Highways to extend the period of the relevant loan up to 2020 12 31, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
