    "description": "Conducting feasibility studies for the establishment of High-Tech Universities targeting job market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10561",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Asian Development Bank has extended their concurrence to grant assistance to conduct the feasibility studies applicable to establish 10 District High - Tech Universities targeting the expansion of Information Technology, Engineering Technology and Bio Technology opportunities as indicated in the Vistas of Prosperity Development Approach. Accordingly, the Cabinet considered the information submitted by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation that necessary actions have been taken by the University Grants Commission for the commencement of the initial feasibility study process in relation to the 10 districts of Nuwara-Eliya, Kalutara, Hambantota, Matale, Puttalam, Mannar, Mullaitivu, Galle, Polonnaruwa and Kegalle."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-15-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-07-15",
    "description": "Sri Lanka Biotechnology Innovation Park (SLBIP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10562",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The project for the establishment of the Sri Lanka Bio Technology Innovation Park and the Sri Lanka Bio Technology Institute, with the objective of promoting high-tech exports and encouraging the substitute productions of such imports has been designed to implement in stages. The objective of this project is to facilitate the creation of a favourable environment required to work collectively for the biotech companies and biotech researchers to convert their ideas into commercial products. The International Centre for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology (ICGEB) an affiliated entity of the United Nations' Organization has selected Sri Lanka as the Regional Research Centre for South Asia to work in collaboration with the proposed Sri Lanka Bio Technology Institute. Under this, the Organization has given its consent to transfer the technology for the manufacture of 10 biologics including insulin and the growth hormones immediately creating favourable grounds for Sri Lanka.\n\nAccordingly, the Cabinet approved the joint proposal submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development and the Minister of Higher Education, technology and Innovation, for the establishment of a Biotechnology Innovation park and to construct the 'BiotechnoPlex' building in a land in extent of 13.2 acres situated in Aramawatte, Pitipana, Homagama and to appoint a Monitoring Committee co-chaired by the Secretary to the Treasury and the Secretary to the Ministry of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation and a Technical Committee comprising of the experts of the relevant field to take the future steps relating to same and to allocate provisions required for the said project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-15-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-07-15",
    "description": "Media Reports published pertaining to the extraction of high quality Ilmenite in the coastal belt in Mannar",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10563",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister of Industries and Supply Chain Management drew the attention of the Cabinet to a report published in a daily English newspaper indicating that explorations are being conducted pertaining to a project for extracting Illmenite in the coastal belt of the Mannar island in terms to an Agreement entered into between an Australian Company and a local company and such activities are to be expanded in future and also regarding a project report being circulated in the web in this regard. The Minister further stated that the institutions responsible for granting permission for any type of exploration have not given such permission for this purpose. The Cabinet having considered these facts, decided to appoint an Officials' Committee, to study relating to this matter and submit a comprehensive report on the measures to be taken."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-15-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-07-15",
    "description": "Decade of Skills Development 2021-2030",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10564",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is imperative to obtain the participation of the youth as the active pioneers in the endeavour towards the sustainable development efforts for creating a peaceful and a just society and enhance their knowledge, skills and capabilities. For the purpose, the focus on the next generation youth skills development is given foremost attention in the national development agenda; \u2018Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u2019. Accordingly, the Cabinet concurred for the proposal submitted by H.E. the President for declaring the period from 2021 \u2013 2030 as the \u2018 Decade of Skills Development\u2019 of Sri Lanka, expecting to transform the General Education, Higher Education and Professional Education and Vocational Education sectors in order to reduce the population of the unskilled labour to 10% thereby making Sri Lanka the epicentre for human resource development in Asia and with future-fit citizenry who will drive the development agenda of the country."
  },
  {
