    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Modernization and refurbishment of the Lumbini Theatre at Colombo 05",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10567",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The existing facilities of the Lumbini Theatre, built in 1952, are not adequate and the sound control system, seating capacity and sanitation facilities of the theater have not been updated in a timely manner. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development, Water Supply and Housing Facilities to implement the project designed for the modernization and refurbishment of the Lumbini Theatre through the Urban Development Authority and to select a suitable contractor on Design and Build basis by following the National Competitive Procurement procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Further extension of benefits under the Agrahara Insurance Scheme operated for retired Public Officers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10568",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The officers who retired from the public service after 2016\u201101\u201101, have been provided an opportunity to join the Agrahara Insurance Scheme and enjoy its benefits. However, the majority of the retired officers have retired from the public service prior to 2016\u201101\u201101 and the unions of the said retired officers have made requests to grant them also an opportunity to join the Agrahara Insurance Scheme. Accordingly the approval was granted by the Cabinet to the joint proposal made by the Minister of Skills Development, Employment and Labour Relations and the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils & Local Government with regard to the extending of Agrahara benefits which is presently entitled to the public servants retired after 2016\u201101\u201101 also to the public servants retired prior to 2016\u201101\u201101, taking into consideration the concurrence given by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development.\n\n\tFurther, the Cabinet granted approval for taking action, considering the proposals submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development - \n\n* \tto prepare a suitable mechanism to maintain a separate ward in every leading Government hospital covering all the districts, for all public servants and the retired public servants enabling them to obtain high quality health care facilities under the Agrahara Insurance Scheme.\n\t\n* \tto request the National Pay Commission to submit appropriate recommendations to rectify the pension anomalies since it has been observed that pension anomalies still exist among the officers who have retired from the public service."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Manufacturing and marketing of innovative products developed by the Industrial Technology Institute (ITI) designed as an effort to prevent the COVID-19 Pandemic",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10569",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- At the Cabinet meeting held on 2020\u201104\u201120, it was decided to explore the possibility of the Sri Lanka Ayurvedic Drugs Corporation to manufacture the innovative products developed by Industrial Technology Institute (ITI) and the ability to distribute such products through the sales outlets of the Co\u2011operative Wholesale Establishment and other appropriate Government Agencies as an effort to prevent the COVID-19 Pandemic. As such, the Cabinet noted the information submitted by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation that, the Institute of Industrial Technology has entered into an Agreement with the Sri Lanka Ayurvedic Corporation and agreed to provide the required raw materials for the manufacture of Alchohol based Herbal Gel Hand Sanitizer and Alcohol based Liquid Hand Sanitizer and its manufacturing methodology to the Sri Lanka Ayurvedic Corporation and the Co\u2011operative Wholesale Establishment has agreed to distribute the products through its sales outlets."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Promotion of Biofilm Bio-fertilizer Island wide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10570",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- A pilot project on the use of Biofilm Bio-fertilizer has been launched in the year 2018 under the directions of the National Institute of Fundamental Studies. Under the project, the said fertilizer has been introduced for the paddy cultivation in 3500 acres in Hambantota, Polonnaruwa, Kurunegala, Ampara and Mahiyanganaya. It has been expanded up to 4000 acres in the year 2019 and based on the successful results achieved through that, the fertilizer has been applied for of 15000 acres during the Yala season 2020 especially in the Kurunegala and Ampara districts. By next year, it is planned to increase the area under cultivation using this fertilizer up to 120,000 acres. Considering the proposal made by the Minister of Higher Education, Technology and Innovation, the Cabinet approval was granted to further expand and implement the program with a suitable mechanism in collaboration with the Department of Agriculture."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Rural Bridges Project - Extending the Project Period",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10571",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- 'The Rural Bridges Project' for the construction of 1,210 rural bridges has been implemented since 2013 under 03 Phases and under that, construction of 1318 bridges have been completed by July 2019. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to extend the duration of the project until 2020\u201108\u201131, enabling to construct another 250 Rural Bridges under Phase II and another 230 Rural Bridges under Phase III of the project. However, the relevant contracts coming into full force and the implementation of the same have been delayed. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils & Local Government to extend the period of the contract agreements already signed for projects under Phase II and Phase III up to 2021\u201105\u201110 and 2021\u201103\u201105 respectively, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Providing relief measures to house holders affected by the water leaks of the Main Tunnel of the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10572",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Mahaweli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development relating to the payment of the housing rent recommended by the Provincial Assessor further from 2019\u201105\u201131 up to 2020\u201109\u201130 for 46 families still living in rented houses out of the house owners affected by the water leakage in the main tunnel of the Uma Oya Multipurpose Development Project and to construct 118 new houses at another suitable location as a special project with the intervention of the Ministry in charge of the subject of Disaster Management for the families recommended to be evacuated due to the risk of landslides."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Formulation of a mechanism to pay the Depositors who lost their money due to the irregularities of East Hewagam Korale Multipurpose Co operative Society Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10573",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since 2015, on five occasions, the Board of Directors of the East Hewagam Korale Multipurpose Co\u2011operative Society has invested Rs.507.59 million in Treasury Bills through a certain institution, which has been introduced as a primary buying company registered under the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. However, it has been revealed that the said institution is not a primary buyer company approved by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and the depositors have been subjected to a severe injustice due to the inability to recover the relevant money up to date. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Internal Trade, Food Security and Consumer Welfare to appoint a committee comprising of the representatives of the relevant institutions to specifically identify the responsible parties for this incident and to recommend actions to be taken to bring justice to the depositors, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Extension of the Project Completion Date of the Moragolla Hydropower Project and Extension of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) Loan Closing Date",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10574",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Moragolla Hydropower Project is being implemented under the Phase I of the Green Power Development and Energy Efficiency Improvement Investment Programme implemented by Asian Development Funds and due to delays in the implementation of the project, the loan closing date has been extended up to 2021\u201103\u201131. However, due to delays in the relevant procurement process, the project completion date and the loan closing date have to be revised further. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power & Energy to extend the project completion date of the Moragolla Hydropower Project up to 2023\u201110\u201131 and the loan closing date up to 2024\u201107\u201131, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Issuing Free Grants for lands of re located houses in the implementation of the Upper Kothmale Hydro Power Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10575",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Upper Kothmale Hydro Power Project which was inaugurated in 2006, completed its construction works in 2012. By the August 2014, houses for displaced families due to the implementation of the hydro power project and alternative locations for shops and workshops have been constructed and handed over to the beneficiaries and the activities relating to the payment of the compensation too has been completed. However, the right to the lands of the relocated families has not been granted so far. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Power & Energy for transferring the alternative lands provided for the construction of alternative residencies and buildings and for cultivation purposes for the displaced parties due to the construction of Upper Kotmale Hydro Power Plant, to the relevant beneficiaries through free grants, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Extension of the validity period of the Treasury Guarantee issued for the establishment of Letters of Credit to import coal for the Coal Power Plant at Norochcholai",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10576",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The validity period of the Treasury Guarantee issued to the People\u2019s Bank by the General Treasury with regard to the import of coal by the Lanka Coal Company to the value of Rs.11 billion, is to expire on the 2020\u201108\u201131. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Power & Energy to extend of the date of validity of the said Treasury Guarantee by another one year effective from that date, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Winding up of the functions of the Interim Board set up until the Southern Development Bill is passed",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10577",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- At the Cabinet meeting held on 30th March 2016, approval had been granted to appoint an Interim Board comprising of a Chairman and 09 members and recruit the required staff for that Board, until the Southern Development Board is legally constituted by an Act of Parliament. However, the Southern Province Development Board bill has not been tabled in Parliament up to date. Some of the projects implemented by the Interim Board have already been completed while all other remaining projects are scheduled to be completed by the year 2020. Therefore, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal made by the Minister of Industrial Export and Investment Promotion for winding up the functions of the Interim Board set up until the Southern Province Development Board Bill is passed and for obtaining the required allocations for the completion of work of the projects to be completed."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Procurement of Retrocession cover on 30% Compulsory Reinsurance Cession on the Reinsurance programme of the General Insurance Industry of Sri Lanka for the year 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10578",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Insurance Trust Fund provides a 30% Compulsory Reinsurance Cession for the General Insurance Industry of Sri Lanka. Further, the National Insurance Trust Fund obtains a retrocession from reputed reinsurers /reinsurance brokers for the purpose. Accordingly, the international competitive bids have been invited for obtaining the reinsurance cession for the year 2020 / 2021 and the proposal submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development for awarding the reinsurance coverage to M/s J. B. Boda & Co. (S) Pte. Ltd. (Lead Reinsurer - M/s Everest Reinsurance Company) at a total cost of Rs.985.5 million for a period of 18 months from the date of awarding of the relevant contract, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Procurement of Reinsurance cover on Strike, Riot, Civil Commotion and Terrorism Fund for the year 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10579",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Insurance Trust Fund provides an insurance cover for the strike, Riot, Civil Commotion and Terrorism Fund for the General Insurance Companies in Sri Lanka. A reinsurance cover is obtained by the National Insurance Trust Fund from the reputed reinsurers/reinsurance brokers once again for the said insurance cover. Accordingly, international competitive bids have been invited for obtaining the said reinsurance cover for the year 2020 / 2021 and the proposal submitted by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economy and Policy Development for awarding the reinsurance cover for M/s J. B. Boda & Co. (S) Pte. Ltd. (Lead Reinsurer - M/s Chaucer Syndicate 1084) at a total cost of Rs.116.39 million for a period of 18 months from the date of awarding of the relevant contract, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
