    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Procurement of Chemical Fertilizer - Maha season 2020 - (September Supply)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10580",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- International open competitive bids have been invited for the procurement of fertilizer for the Lanka Fertilizer Limited (Lak Pohora) and Colombo Commercial Company Limited (Commercial Fertilizer), for the requirement of the month of September 2020. The Cabinet having considered the recommendation made by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee on those prices, granted covering approval for the proposal submitted by the Minister of Mahaveli, Agriculture, Irrigation and Rural Development for awarding of the procurement for the supply of fertilizer as follows;\n\n*\t60,000 + 5% metric tons of Urea (Granular) to M/s Valency International Pte Limited for an amount of US$ 259.99 per metric ton.\n\n*\t7,318 + 5% metric tons of Urea (Frilled) to Agri Fert Liven International Pvt Limited for an amount of US$ 266.48 per metric ton.\n\n*\t20,000 + 5% metric tons of Murate of Potash (Red / Pinkish / White) to Agricultural Resources and Investments Pte Limited for an amount of US$ 248 per metric ton.\n\n*\t4,700 + 5% metric tons of Murate of Potash (Red / Pinkish) to Agricultural Resources and Investments Pte Limited for an amount of US$ 249 per metric ton."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Appointment of a Committee for the preparation of a strategic mechanism for implementing a Common Watershed Management Approach in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10581",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal submitted by Hon. Prime Minister for the appointment of a committee comprised of experts in the field of water management headed by Prof. C. M. Madduma Bandara, Environmentalist for the preparation of a proposal on making strategies enabling to build up cooperation among all the relevant stakeholders with the view to increasing the available water quantity with better quality for present and future purposes by reviewing all the relevant policies on effective management of watersheds in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Regularizing and make efficient the State Bank system to Strengthen the National Economy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10582",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- State banking system and their affiliated institutions have to operate regularly and effectively in order to overcome the challenges encountered by the Sri Lankan economy amidst COVID-19 pandemic. However, it appears that actions have been taken deviating from the fundamental objectives of establishing said state banks and violating the provisions and procedures stipulated in relevant Acts during the past. The Cabinet granted approval to the proposal submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister for the appointment of a Committee chaired by the former High Court Judge Sisira Ratnayake and comprised of experts in the relevant fields to identify such incidents and to recommend the legal and administrative measures in order to avoid such situations in future."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-07-22-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2020-07-22",
    "description": "Upgrading the General Hospital, Kalutara and the Base Hospital, Homagama as Teaching Hospitals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10583",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-07-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Presently, plans are being made for the establishment of a Medical Faculty of the University of Moratuwa and it is expected to commence the academic activities expeditiously. The proposal submitted by the Minister of Health and Indigenous Medical Services to upgrade the General Hospital, Kalutara and the Base Hospital, Homagama as Teaching Hospitals enabling the establishment of the Professorial Unit of proposed Medical Faculty at General Hospital, Kalutara and the relevant clinical training at the Base Hospital, Homagama, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Appointment of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10584",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E the President to appoint  the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living under the chairmanship of H.E the President and comprising of the Hon. Prime Minister, Minister of Trade, Minister of Agriculture, Minister of Fisheries and Minister of Plantation, in order to maintain the stability of Cost of Living by taking into account the issues such as constant fluctuations in the market \tdemand and supply, climate effects, seasonal changes in production and international prices, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\t\n\tFurther, the Cabinet granted its approval for the following State Ministers to be \tattended to the deliberations of the above Cabinet Sub-Committee.\n\n*\tState Minister of Paddy and Grains, Organic Food, Vegetables, Fruits, Chillies, Onion and Potato Cultivation Promotion, Seed Production and Advanced Technology Agriculture. \n\n*\tState Minister of Co-operative Services, Marketing Development and Consumer Protection.\n\n*\tState Minister of Coconut, Kithul, Palmyrah and Rubber Cultivation Promotion and Related Industrial Product Manufacturing & Export Diversification."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Construction of Flyovers over the Railway Line at Uttharananda Mawatha near \tthe Slave Island Railway Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10585",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- A huge traffic congestion has been observed during peak hours due to the location of  railway lines across Uttharananda Mawatha and Akbhar Mawatha at Slave Island area. Accordingly, a project has been proposed to implement a one-way traffic plan by constructing flyovers\tto avoid the said traffic congestion.  As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Highways to implement the said \tproject and invite bids from qualified domestic contractors for the construction of 03 flyovers under the same, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Submission of reports published by the Ministry of Finance to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10586",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The following reports have been published by the Ministry of Finance and accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to submit the said reports  to Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n i.\tPre-election Budgetary Position Report\n\nIn terms of the provisions of Section 16 (2) of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.3 of 2003, the Pre-election Budgetary Position Report is required to be tabled in Parliament by the Minister of Finance within 02 weeks of the first session of the new Parliament.\n\tii.\tAnnual Report - 2019 of the Ministry of Finance\n\nIn terms of the provisions of Section 13 of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.3 of 2003, the Final Budgetary Position Report is required to be released to the public  by the Minister of Finance prior to lapse of 05 months after the end of the financial year and thereafter tabled in Parliament.\n\n\tiii.\tMid-Year Fiscal Position Report 2020\n\nIn terms of the provisions of Section 10 of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No.3 of 2003, the Mid-Year Fiscal Position Report is required to be released to the public by the Minister of Finance  by the last day of June in each financial year and thereafter tabled in Parliament.\n\n\tiv.\t Annual Report - 2019 of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka\n\nIn terms of the provisions of Section 35 of the Monetary Law Act, the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka should submit a report containing the state of the economy, condition of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and the policies and measures adopted by the Monetary Board during the year to the Minister of Finance within 04 months of the commencement of the following year and thereafter the same should be submitted to Parliament."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Procurement of a Data Management System for Reserve Management of the\tCentral Bank of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10587",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet granted its approval on 2019\u201106\u201107 to procure a new data management system to meet the existing requirements in the management of the foreign reserves of the country and productively facilitate to the future developments as well. Accordingly, bids have been invited through the International Competitive Bidding process to supply, install, commission and maintain the said data management system. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to award the above procurement to SimCorp Pte. Limited of Singapore as per the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee on the said bid, and the views and the recommendations of the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka (ICTA) pertaining to the proposed procurement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
