    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Finance for submission of the Gazette Notifications issued in terms of the provisions of the following Acts, in Parliament was approved by the Cabinet.\n\ni.\tSix (06) Gazette Notifications issued under the Ports and Airports Development Levy Act, No.18 of  2011.\n\nii.\tNine (09) Gazette Notifications issued under the Excise (Special Provisions) Act, No.13 of 1989.\niii.\tTen (10) Gazette Notifications issued under the Excise Ordinance (Chapter 52):\n\niv.\tOne (01) Gazette Notification issued under the Finance Act, No.11 of 2006:\n\nv.\tOne (01) Gazette Notification issued under the Finance Act, No.12 of 2012:\n\nvi.\tFive (05) Gazette Notifications issued under the Finance Act, No.35 of 2018:\n\nvii.\tSix (06) Gazette Notifications issued under the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962:\n\nviii.\tThree (03) Gazette Notifications issued under the Customs Ordinance (Chapter 235):\n\nix.\tThirty One (31) Gazette Notifications issued under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007:\n\nx.\tFive (05) Gazette Notifications issued under the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017:"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Procurement of Chemical Fertilizer - 2020 Maha Season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10589",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- Open competitive bids have been invited for the importation of chemical fertilizer to be distributed during the month of October for Maha Season 2020 by the Ceylon Fertilizer Company Ltd (Lak Pohora) and the Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Ltd. (Commercial Fertilizer). Accordingly, the Cabinet granted its approval  for the proposal submitted by the Minister of Agriculture to award the relevant procurements as follows considering the recommendation of the Standing Cabinet Appointed procurement Committee:\n\n*\tTo procure 20,000+ 5% metric tons of Murate of Potash (Red/Pinkish/White) for the Lak Pohora and Commercial Fertilizer companies from M/s Valency International Trading Pte Ltd., at  US$ 236.44 per metric ton.\n\n*\tTo procure 2,000+ 5% metric tons of Murate of Potash (Red/Pinkish) for the Commercial Fertilizer company from M/s Valency International Trading Pte Ltd., at US$ 236.44 per metric ton.\n\nFurther, the proposal to procure  8,700+ 5% metric tons of Triple Super Phosphate for Lak Pohora and Commercial Fertilizer companies for the month of September of the Maha Season 2020 to M/s Gulf Fert International FZE at US$ 241.00 per metric ton, as recommended by the Procurement Appeal Board, was also approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "Amendment of Tax Legislation - Policy Measures for Economic Revival",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10590",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "Followed by a proposal made by H.E the President, the approval of the Cabinet was granted at its meeting held on the 2019\u201111\u201127 for the introduction of a simple, transparent and efficient tax system to all the stakeholders in the economy including consumers, working population, entrepreneurs and tax paying community. Morefully, the Government has also taken  measures to provide fiscal and monetary stimulus to all the stakeholders in the economy including low - income earners, entrepreneurs, micro, small and medium entrepreneurs, those engaged in tourism and the farmers in order to minimize the adverse impacts caused to the production activities as well as to the employments due to the COVID - 19 pandemic. The Central Bank of Sri Lanka with the intention of easing the financial burden on the entrepreneurs has taken measures to increase the liquidity of the financial market.\n\nIt is expected that these measures will bring back the economy to normalcy in the second part of the year 2020. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to publish the Bills drafted by the Legal Draftsman to amend the following Acts in compliance with the above, in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\ni. \tNation Building Tax Act, No.9 of 2009\nii. \tEconomic Services Charge Act, No.13 of 2006\niii. \tPorts and Airports Development Levy Act, No.18 of 2011 \niv.  \tFinance Act, No.35 of 2018\n\nFurther, the Cabinet approved the proposal made to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to amend the following Acts.\n\ni.  Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017.\nii. Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-08-26-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-08-26",
    "description": "The Interim Report in relation to the total power failure in the National Power System on 17th August 2020",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10591",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-08-26",
    "decision_details_body": "- The interim report of the Committee appointed by the Minister of Power to examine and report the total power failure which occurred in the national power system on 2020\u201108\u201117 was brought to the notice of the Cabinet. The Committee has identified the non\u2011availability of a risk management mechanism for operations and maintenance and further submitted 11 more recommendations including the urgency of having a more reliable operational and maintenance mechanism for risk prevention. Further, the Committee has reported that the cause for the total power interruption on 2020\u201108\u201117 was due to a mistake made by the officer\u2011in\u2011charge of the general maintenance at the Kerawalapitiya Grid Sub Station, at that time.\n\nThe Cabinet further noted the information submitted by the Minister of Power, that an in\u2011depth study is being conducted on the matters stated in the above committee report and expeditious action will be taken to make aware the Cabinet of Ministers of the activities recommended in such study and the estimated investment  required for the implementation of such activities."
  },
  {
