    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-09-16",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports\t(Control ) Act, No.01 of 1969 in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10607",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet granted approval at its meeting held on 2020\u201104\u201101 for the proposals made by H.E. The President pertaining to streamlining the imports and restoring the economic activities with a view to easing the pressure caused to the foreign exchange due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Accordingly, H.E. the President appointed the Tariff Determination Committee to submit recommendations on action to be taken pertaining to strengthening and reviving the national economy pursuant to the policy statement of \u201cVistas of Prosperity and Splendor\u201d and as per the recommendations of the said Committee, the importing goods were classified into 03 categories to streamline the import as an interim measure and action was taken as follows:\n\n*\ttemporary suspension of the importation of non-essential goods  and commodities that could be cultivated or manufactured domestically and motor vehicles.\n\n*\tallowing importation of selected commodities under the suppliers' credit facility or on no foreign exchange basis.\n\n*\tallowing importation of selected goods necessary for domestic industries, agriculture, export processing and domestic consumption.\n      \n\tAs such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the\tMinister of Finance to submit four (04) Gazette Extraordinary Notifications\tpublishing the Regulations promulgated under the Imports and Exports\t(Control) Act, No.1 \tof 1969 in Parliament for implementing the aforesaid\tmeasures, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-09-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-09-16",
    "description": "Relief assistance to the affected families of Amphan Cyclone",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10608",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Amphan Cyclone which lasted for 04 days from 16th May, 2020 to 19th May 2020 has severely damaged the banana and papaya plantation of 2,374 farmers in Kopay, Tellipallai and Karaweddi Divisional Secretariat Divisions of the Jaffna District and the District Secretary/Government Agent, Jaffna has reported that the total loss of the damage was Rs.52.98 million. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to implement a mechanism in coordination with the Ministry of Agriculture, the Ministry in charge of the subject of Disaster Management and the District Secretariat, Jaffna and to grant an additional allocation of Rs.52.98 million to the District Secretary/Government Agent, Jaffna, required for the same through the Ministry in charge of the subject of Disaster Management as per the proposal of the Minister of Fisheries to provide relief to the said farmers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
