    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-09-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Trade to submit four Gazette\tExtraordinary Notifications issued for the following purposes under the Sri\tLanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979 in Parliament, was approved\tby the Cabinet.\n\n*\tExemption of the payment of CESS on the importation or importation and supply or importation and donation of products such as medicines, chemicals, health care equipment and machinery required for the prevention of COVID\u201119 on the request of the Ministry of Health, Tri -Forces and the COVID Centre.\n\n*\tLevying the CESS on the importation of Portland Cement on the basis of unit rate in place of advalorem basis.\n\n*\tRemoval of CESS levy on importation of cement clinkers.\n\n*\tImposition of CESS levy on importation of certain parts required for footwear manufacturing, filament bulbs and flexible packaging materials."
