    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet had granted approval at its meeting held on 2019\u201105\u201107 to commence the procurement process for the construction of the Stage 1 of the Import Cargo Terminal Building at the Bandaranaike International Airport. Accordingly, competitive bids have been called. The proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to award the said contract to M/s Nawaloka Construction Company (Pvt.) Ltd at a sum of Rs.2.37 billion, taking into consideration the recommendation made by the of Procurement Appeal Board, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Submission of the Appropriation Bill for the Financial year 2020 in \tParliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10654",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020.08.19 granted approval to draft the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2020. Accordingly, the total recurrent expenditure and the capital expenditure for the financial year 2020 have been estimated as Rs. 2692 billion and Rs.1846 billion respectively. Those estimated provisions also include the following allocation :\n\t\n    \u2022 Provisions allocated by the two Votes on Accounts approved by Parliament before.\n    \u2022 Provisions for estimated expenditure for the year 2020 approved by  H.E. the President in terms of paragraph (3) of Article 150 of the Constitution.\n    \u2022 Provisions for accounting for a sum of Rs. 211 billion incurred in the year 2019 but which has not been accounted.\nAccordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Appropriation Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman for the financial year 2020. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to publish the said draft bill in the Government Gazette and present the same thereafter in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Submission of the Appropriation Bill for the Financial year 2021 in \tParliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10655",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020.09.16 granted approval to draft the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2021. Accordingly, the estimated recurrent expenditure and the capital expenditure for the financial year 2021 is Rs. 2,690 billion and Rs. 2,216 billion respectively. Further, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Appropriation Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to publish the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2021 in the Government Gazette and present the same thereafter in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Purchase of School Uniform Materials \u2013 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10656",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2020\u201109\u201128 has decided to purchase the required school uniform materials for the year 2021 from the local textile manufacturers and to expedite the procurement process already commenced accordingly.\nAs such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to award the contract for manufacturing sorting, packing and distribution of the school uniform materials to the Divisional Education Offices in accordance with the relevant specifications as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee to institutes; Vanguard Industries (Pvt) Company, Dankotuwa Weaving Mills, Prabha Tex Industries and Creative Textile Mills (Pvt) Company, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Minimum number of students in a classroom in a school",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10657",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Principals follow the circular instructions issued by the Ministry of Education for the admission of students to Grade 1. Similarly, admission of students to Grade 6 of the National and Provincial Schools based on the merits of the Scholarship Examination and admission of students to the Advanced Level classes based on qualifications of the Ordinary Level Examination are conducted by the relevant Principals.\nIn addition, as per the Circulars: No.37/2008 and 33/2019, students are enrolled to intermediate classes with the recommendations of the school Principals. The students who qualify to be enrolled into intermediate classes include the groups on the basis of change of residence due to transfers, arrive from abroad, elected to Parliament, Judges in Judicial Service, Government Specialist Medical Officers , Government Medical Officers, employees of schools,  Ministry of Education and in affiliated departments thereof, University Lecturers and Executive Officers, Officers in Sri Lanka Education Administrative Service and Sri Lanka Teacher Educators Service. \nMoreover, students who were subjected to injustice in the admission process and subsequently being found as qualified at the investigations conducted in this regard, students with special needs and children in social welfare centers are groups eligible to enter  to  intermediate classes.\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to revise the existing procedure for admission of students and introduce a more transparent mechanism enabling to increase the number of students that could be admitted to a class, taking into consideration the high demand for admission of students to the schools, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-05-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-10-05",
    "description": "Temporary cancellation of diving permits issued for the collection of sea creatures such as Sea-Cucumber and Conch Shells",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10658",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-05",
    "decision_details_body": "-\tThe Department of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources issues special diving permits for the collection of sea creatures such as Sea Cucumber and Conch Shells in the western coast of the Jaffna peninsula. Accordingly, the diving teams engaged in such activities attend to same while residing temporarily on the coast of that area.\n\nIt has been reported that some of the divers who have obtained permits for this purpose are abusing these permits and engaging in illegal activities with the Indian fishermen who engage in fishing by trawlers in that maritime boarder. It has been observed that in view of the above, there is a severe threat of the spread of COVID- 19 pandemic among the people of Jaffna peninsula. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries, to  temporarily suspend the diving permits issued for the collection of sea creatures such as Sea Cucumber and Conch Shells, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "73rd Independence Day Celebration falling on 04th February 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10659",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-The proposal made by the the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of \tInternal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management to appoint the following Cabinet Sub-Committee to organize and monitor the activities of the 73rd Independence Day Celebration falling on 04th February 2021, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n    \u2022 Hon. Mahinda Rajapaksa\n      Prime Minister - (Chairman)\n      \t\n    \u2022 Hon. (Prof.) G.L. Peiris\n      Minister of Education \n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Dinesh Gunawardena\n      Foreign Minister\n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Janaka Bandara Tennakoon\n      Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils & \n      Local Government\n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Keheliya Rambukwella\n      Minister of Mass Media\n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Chamal Rajapaksa \n      Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management\n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Dullas Alahapperuma \n      Minister of Power\n      \n    \u2022 Hon. Wasudeva Nanayakkara\n      Minister of Water Supply"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Establishment of the Expressway Investment Company",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10660",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Statement at National Policy enunciated in 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour' has clearly identified the necessity of having an interconnected roadnetwork as a key aspect of the economic growth strategy. Accordingly, 100,000km Rural Road Project is now in progress and the Government has given priority to complete the work of the Central Expressway and to initiate the construction of the Ruwanpura Expressway and to complete the work of the Elevated Expressway from Kelaniya to Athurugiriya.\n\nIt has been observed that an investment of 0.5% - 1% of the Gross Domestic Production has to be borne by the National Budget for financing Expressways currently under construction and those are to be constructed. As such, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to incorporate a Company with Secretary to the Treasury as the sole shareholder, bringing all the Expressways under one Company enabling the said Company to raise funds required to construct the Expressways through the funds received as the revenue earned by the toll charged from the users of the Expressways as well as the other sources of income of Expressways , was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Bringing the Vidyalankara International Buddhist Conference Hall to \tservice providing status",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10661",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-Government has spent approximately Rs. 1,200 million for the construction of the Vidyalankara International Buddhist Conference Hall and the Cabinet, having considered the magnitude of the investment and enabling to properly maintain the high efficiency technical equipment installed in the said Conference hall, granted approval to appoint a Board of Trustees on 2019\u201111\u201111. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received in respect of the Deed of Trust prepared in this regard and the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs informed the Cabinet that the Secretary to the Ministry in charge of the subject of Buddhasasana is to sign on behalf of the Government as the First Party of the said Deed of Trust and the Cabinet has given their consent to that."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Construction of multi-storied car parks together with the implementation of mixed development projects in the city of Colombo and other selected cities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10662",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-A programme has been designed to construct and maintain car parks through selected investors by following the open competitive bidding procedure for the purpose of minimizing the traffic congestion caused by the vehicles reaching Colombo and suburbs daily and the vehicles parked on the sides of the roads. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to implement the said project under the following two (02) methods, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n* \tRequest for proposals from Private Sector investors for the construction of multi-storied car parks constructed under general conditions and multi-storied mechanical vehicle parks at 08 locations in the city of Colombo and in Battaramulla, Anuradhapura and Kandy, as a Public-Private Partnership Project.\n\n* \tRequest for proposals to construct multi-storied car parks under general conditions and mechanical car parks including housing units and office spaces and other appropriate projects at Narahenpita, Telecom Parking Land at Pettah, car Park at the land where Otter Sports Club Colombo 07 is located, Kinsey Avenue at Colombo 07, enabling the cost incurred for the project to be generated within the project itself ,on pre-sale basis."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Allocation of a Plot of Land for the Uva Wellassa University",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10663",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-Considering the demand for higher education existing at present, it is essential to improve the infrastructure facilities of the State Universities in order to implement the Government's policy on expanding opportunities for more students to enter into State Universities. Taking into consideration, a proposal made by the Minister of Education, the Cabinet approved to vest a plot of 02 acres from the land located at Kalugalpitiya, Badulla, which is under the purview of the Badulla District Secretary, enabling the Uva Wellassa University to commence degree courses further required in the most appropriate field in addition to the degree courses presently available in the University."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Taking actions regarding the railway employees who reside in the railway reserved lands belonging to the Department of Sri Lanka Railways",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10664",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-The Department of Sri Lanka Railways has about 14,000 acres of reserved lands and about 10% of them have been given on lease to various parties. Further, various persons are in unauthorized possession of about 80% of the remaining lands and officers presently serving in the Department as well as the officers who retired from the departmental service are from among them. These lands are being used for unauthorized purposes such as construction of houses and business premises and cultivation. Some railway employees who have illegally acquired those lands have been evicted from those places by legal proceedings. There have also been instances of disciplinary action been taken against them having to forego their right to pension. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to appoint a Ministerial Committee consisting of the following to study the matters with regard to the said issue and submit recommendations to the Cabinet. \n\n* \tHon. Gamini Lokuge,\n\tMinister of Transport - (Chairman);\n\n* \tHon.Janaka Bandara Tennakoon,\n\tMinister of Public Services, Provincial Councils & \n\tLocal Government;\n\n*\tHon. S.M. Chandrasena,\nMinister of Lands; and \n\n*\tHon. Ajith Nivard Cabraal, \nState Minister of Money & Capital Market and \tState \tEnterprise Reforms."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Amendments to the Intellectual Property Act No.36 of 2003",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10665",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-There are a number of local products that can be promoted as geographical indication and such products have to face a severe competition due to counterfeits both in the local and foreign markets. Therefore, it has been identified that it is appropriate to register such products in Sri Lanka as geographical indications. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a bill to amend the Intellectual Property Act No.36 of 2003 enabling to establish a comprehensive and specific legal framework to register geographical indications in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Importing Basmathi Rice under the Pakistan - Sri Lanka Trade \tAgreement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10666",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-In accordance with the provisions of the Pakistan-Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement, it is possible to import 6000 Metric tons of Basmati rice annually under duty free concession. In recent times, the private sector also had been granted permission to import Basmathi rice under this facility. However, complaints have been received with regard to various irregularities being committed by importing rice not belonging to the specified varieties. Taking into consideration these matters, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to import Basmathi rice only through the Sri Lanka State Trading Corporation and the Co-operative Wholesale Establishment/ Lanka Sathosa ltd., under this facility, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Greater Colombo Water and Wastewater Management Improvement Investment Programme - Tranche 3",
