  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Simplifying Systems and Processes to fast track the implementation of development activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10672",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-The following issues have been identified as some of the impediments to fast track the implementation of development Activities:\n\n*\tMinistries have to take action to obtain the approval from several institutions and finally the Cabinet of Ministers for general matters which are not required as matters of policy or the regulatory requirements.\n\n*\tDelays in payments to be done to private contractors cause delays in development projects and the cost escalation of projects.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to pursue action as follows to fast track the development activities in order to minimize the delays caused as far as possible:\n\n*\tTo submit a report to the Cabinet of Ministers once in three months on the development projects which could be implemented with the approval of the Secretary to the Treasury and the other relevant Authorities, after fulfilling the same expeditiously.\n\n*\tTo introduce a new mechanism to ensure a continuous cash flow for the key development projects by issuing Treasury Guarantee or Facilitation Letters to their banks, enabling to pay the Contractors for their work completed, without delay."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-10-12-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-10-12",
    "description": "Implementation of the recommendations made by the Presidential Commission pertaining to Edirisinghe Trust Investment Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10673",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-10-12",
    "decision_details_body": "-A Presidential Commission under the chairmanship of retired Supreme Court Judge, K.T.Chithrasiri was appointed by H.E the President on 2020.01.09 to investigate, examine and report on the alleged wrongdoings, irregularities and malpractices which are said to have taken place relating to Edirisinghe Trust Investments Limited. The said Commission submitted the report containing its observations and recommendations to H.E the President on 2020\u201110\u201106. The aforesaid Commission, by its observations and recommendations has pointed out that many offenses have been committed under the Companies Act, the Finance Companies Act, Prevention of Money Laundering Act, Financial Reporting Act, the Legal Framework for the transfer of lands to foreigners as well as the Penal Code. Moreover, it has also been pointed out by the above Report of Presidential Commission, the need of fully re-organize the Department of Supervision of Non-Bank Financial Institutions of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, bringing the aforesaid matters to the notice of the Cabinet, the following proposals made by H.E the President, were approved by the Cabinet. \n\n    \u2022 to direct the Attorney General to take legal actions expeditiously to implement the recommendations of the above Report of Presidential Commission pertaining to the irregularities of the financial and property transactions of Edirisinghe Trust Investment Limited.\n      \n    \u2022 to inform the Ministry of Finance to formulate a new institutional structure to regulate Financial Companies by fully re\u2011organizing the Department of Supervision of Non\u2011Bank Financial Institutions of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka.\n      \n    \u2022 to submit the said Report of the Commission and the measures to be taken accordingly in Parliament, through the Minister of Justice."
  },
  {
