    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Model Memorandum of Understanding on Police Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10718",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that entering into bilateral memoranda of understanding with the foreign police organizations who perform their duties in a highly efficient manner with the help of modern technology, will enable our police officers to share their experience, knowledge, skills and internationally recognized practices and standards on modern police duties. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation and State Minister of Internal Security, Home Affairs and Disaster Management to enter into Memoranda of Understanding between the Ministry under which the subject of police falls and the foreign police organizations under the guidance of the Foreign Ministry to establish police cooperation under 17 fields such as terrorist activities, terrorist financing, drug related crimes, human trafficking and smuggling, money laundering, cybercrime etc, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Reservation of Borrow Area for Offshore Sand Mining",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10719",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The requirement of long-term reserving of a borrow area for offshore sand mining has been arisen for mining sand for the construction industry and as well as for the projects implemented by Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation. The institution has satisfied its sand requirement since the year 1994 by mining sand within an offshore area of 61 square kilometers, having obtained exploration license periodically. Considering the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, the Cabinet decided to grant approval to permit the the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation for offshore sand mining from the said borrow area of 61 square kilo meters for a period of 10 years, subject to carrying out an Environmental Impact Assessment."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Construction of a Paediatric Surgical Ward at the Teaching Hospital, Ratnapura",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10720",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Teaching Hospital, Ratnapura is the largest tertiary care hospital in the Sabaragamuwa province thus providing services to a large number of patients from other provinces as well. Adhering to the need of a surgical ward with proper facilities for the pediatric ward complex consisted of 116 beds, it has been planned to construct a paediatric surgical ward in the second storey of the relevant paediatric ward building. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Health for the construction of the proposed paediatric surgical ward with the funding of the donors and to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health and the relevant donors for the said purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Establishment of a Dedicated Pharmaceutical Zone at Arabokka Estate, Hambantota",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10721",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Presidential Task Force for Economic Revival and Poverty Alleviation has identified the pharmaceutical manufacturing industry as one of the potential industries that could attract foreign direct investments as well as earn foreign exchange. Therefore, it has been planned to establish a special pharmaceutical manufacturing zone with modern facilities within an area in extent of 400 acres of the Arabokka estate in Hambantota enabling to attract the world renowned pharmaceutical manufacturing companies. It is expected to declare the said project as a Strategic Development Project and grant concessions and incentives for the investors who invest in the said pharmaceutical manufacturing zone. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health for the establishment of 20 pharmaceutical manufacturing companies in 200 acres as phase I of this Project and another 20 pharmaceutical manufacturing companies in 200 more acres as its phase II and to furnish necessary infrastructure facilities by the Board of Investments of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Providing relief for continuing inter-provincial bus operations in the face of the COVID-19 pandemic situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10722",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to waive off the following charges from the bus operators with effect from March 2020 for continuing inter-provincial bus operations amidst the COVID - 19 pandemic situation. \n\n*\tPermit renewal fees \n*\tLate fees \n*\tTender fees \n*\tLog fees \n*\tEntrance fees \n*\tExpressway temporary permit fees\n\nHowever, it has been identified that the bus operators need to be provided with relief enabling them to provide quality and efficient passenger transport service, since they have confronted with numerous constrains due to re-emergence of the pandemic situation. Accordingly, considering a proposal made by the Minister of Transport, the Cabinet granted approval for further providing the said concessions to the bus operators until the end of this year."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Providing opportunity for sale of products of the Government Institutions in the showroom of the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10723",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is been planned to expand the showroom of the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation which is currently operating at the Narahenpita Dedicated Economic Center and establish a sales center called \u201cRajawasa\u201d in order to facilitate the customers to obtain the products manufactured and sold in the following Government Institutions under one roof at a reasonable price.\n*\t Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation\n*\tCeylon Fisheries Corporation\n*\tEducational Publications Department \n*\t Sri Lanka Tea Board\n*\t State Pharmaceuticals Corporation \n*\t B.B.C. Lanka Limited \n*\t Cooperative Development Department \n*\t Lanka Sathosa Limited\n*\t Ceylon Cashew Corporation\n*\t Mantai Salt Company\n*\t Litro Gas Limited\n*\t State Timber Corporation\n*\t Colombo Commercial Fertilizers Limited\n*\tCeylon Fertilizer Company Limited\n*\t Milco (Pvt.) Ltd\n*\t Coconut Development Authority\n*\t State Printing Corporation \n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to modernize the premises where the showroom of the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation presently located and to establish the proposed \u201cRajawasa\u201d Sales Center, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Supply of necessary scrap metal for the Local Small Scale Industrialists",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10724",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Issues relating to the metal industry had been discussed by the \u201cInter-Ministerial Task Force on Industry and Enterprise\u201d and the \u201cPresidential Task Force on Economic Revival and Poverty Alleviation\u201d at their meetings. As determined at those discussions, steps have been taken to stop the export of Copper, Aluminium, Stainless Steel, High Carbon Steel, Brass, Cast Iron, Aluminium Ingots and Zinc Ingots with immediate effect, with a view to providing sufficient raw materials for the local metal industrialists. According to a research conducted by the Sri Lanka Industrial Development Board and the University of Moratuwa, it has been proved that there is a high demand for scrap Iron, Cast Iron, Aluminium, Copper and Brass by the local industrialists and the demand for Zinc, Manganese, High Carbon Steel and Stainless Steel is also being increased. \n\nThe demand for Scrap Metal is expected to be increased further in line with policies of the Government pertaining to the promotion of local industries. Therefore, it has been found that it is appropriate to reconsider the current permission that has been given for the export of Copper Wire and to suspend the export of Copper Wire in order to encourage production of more value added products.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to use the scrap metal of Iron, Copper, Aluminium, Stainless Steel, High Carbon Steel, Brass , Cast Iron and Aluminium Ingots and Zinc Ingots and Copper Wire only for the local industries and to permit to export the unusable Scrap Metal only on the recommendation of the Sri Lanka Industrial Development Board and the other relevant institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Granting State Lands to Landless War Heroes for Residential Purposes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10725",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the introduction of a new methodology for disposition of state lands to war heroes, having revised the previous policy existed, at the Cabinet meeting held on 2016\u201107\u201118, the some war heroes who have been granted lands under the previous policy are reported to have faced numerous hardships. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Lands to introduce a new methodology to eliminate these inequalities that have occurred in providing relief to the war heroes belonging to the same category, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
