    "description": "Awarding the long term contracts for the importation of Petrol and Diesel for the period of eight months from 2020/11/01 to 2020/06/30",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10735",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet approved the proposals submitted by the Minister of Energy to award the following long term contracts for the importation of Petrol and Diesel for the period of eight months from 2020\u201111\u201101 to 2020\u201106\u201130, as recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee. \n* \tAwarding the procument to M/s ES Energy DMCC,U.A.E to supply 1,800,000 barrels of Petrol (92 Unl) \n*\t Awarding the procument to M/s Swiss Singapore Overseas Enterprises Pte. Ltd., in Singapore to supply 1,680,000 barrels of Diesel that contain maximum sulphur percentage 0.05."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "COVID-19 (Temporary Provisions) Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10736",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has emerged the need of taking a certain temporary measure to provide legal protection to all relevant parties and persons in dispensation of justice on pending court cases due to the COVID - 19 pandemic. Particularly, as per the COVID- 19 pandemic condition, it has become appropriate to make provisions for such measures to be taken deviating to the ordered time limit, when certain persons are ordered to take certain measures within specified time limits. Accordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers approved the proposal submitted by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft the COVID -19 Bill (Temporary Provisions) to impose relevant provisions including such identified matters."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-09-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2020-11-09",
    "description": "Selling of paddy stocks in the possession of the District Secretaries/Government Agents and the paddy stocks belonging to the Paddy Marketing Board through Sathosa outlets by threshing them into rice",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10737",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the facts that the current rice shortage in the market and the reluctance shown by the owners of rice mills to supply sufficient rice stocks under the controlled price, the Cabinet of Ministers granted approval to take necessary measures to sell paddy stocks in the possession of the District Secretaries/Government Agents and the paddy stocks belonging to the Paddy Marketing Board through Sathosa outlets to consumers under the controlled price, after threshing them into rice."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Implementation of the Unique Digital Identity (SL-UDI) Framework and e-NIC Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10739",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government adopts an Unique Digital Identity Framework and a strategy to facilitate the said framework in order to achieve the goal 'Smart Nation' which is one of the ten key goals of the national policy framework 'Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour'.  Further the said programme has been given priority as a national level programme. The Unique Digital Identity Framework for Sri Lanka has been prepared together with the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka and the Department for the Registration of Persons and implementation of the e-NIC project has been identified as one of the components to be implemented under the said Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President to implement the following proposals was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tGranting approval to the Unique Digital Identity Framework for Sri Lanka finalized \tby the Programme Preparation Committee.\n\n*\tAppointment of a Presidential Task Force to provide the necessary guidance to establish the Unique Digital Identity Framework for Sri Lanka.\n\n*\tVesting the responsibility of implementation of the Unique Digital Identity Framework Project for Sri Lanka with the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka.\n\n*\tImplementation of the e-NIC Project together with the Information \tand Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka and the Department for the Registration of Persons.\n\n\n*\tMaking required amendments to the Registration of Persons Act No.32 \tof 1968 to facilitate the implementation of Unique Digital Identity Framework for Sri Lanka and the e-NIC Project.\n\n*\tCompletion of the said project by 2022\u201112\u201131."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Implementing Digital Strategies and empowering the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka (ICTA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10740",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka has been entrusted the responsibility of recommending a National Digital Policy and Strategy to be implemented during the period 2020-2025 under the Government's new policy framework. Accordingly, the said Institution has prepared a National Digital Policy and Implementation Strategies for Sri Lanka. It has been recommended to initiate 03 new programme units by the said programme as follows.\n\ni.\tDigital Government - This unit will carry out programmes for digital transformation process of Government institutions and empowerment of citizens of Sri Lanka.\n\nii.\tDigital Economy - This unit will facilitate innovations, entrepreneurship and starting up new companies by capacity building, introducing new technology and expansion of the industry by creating an environment for foreign direct investment .\n\niii.\tDigital Services - This unit will establish, mange and maintain IT infrastructure required for government services and provide consultancy services to initiate and manage the digital transformation process. \nAs such, the proposal made by H.E the President to restructure the Information and Communication Technology Agency of Sri Lanka enabling to fulfill the aforesaid duties and responsibilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
