    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Presenting an appropriate methodology for determining and identifying \tthe National Heritage of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10745",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Issues have arisen in identifying the Nation Heritages of Sri Lanka due to the absence of specific criteria or mechanism for the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to appoint a Committee comprising of Experts /Scholars in the relevant fields to prepare a methodology in consultation with the views of the general public for the identification of tangible and intangible national heritages which ensures Sri Lankan cultural identity, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Introduction of an Arbitration System to settle the disputes of the Employees in the Public Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10746",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is apparent that there are also instances where protests, demonstrations, strikes etc. conducted by certain employees in the public sector at present,resulting impediments to achieve theNational development goals. Although it is possible to take action to minimize disputes and strikes in the private sector in terms of the provisions of the Labour Dispute Act No.43 of 1950, the Government sector possesses no such methodology. Through the Government's Policy Framework of \u2018Vistas of Prosperity and Splendour\u2019, it has been pointed out that a mechanism similar to the arbitration system adopted by the private sector to solve the employee disputes at present would be introduced to solve the employee disputes in the public sector as well. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils and Local Government, to appoint a committee comprising of relevant Secretaries to ministries and relevant trade union representatives, in order to introduce amechanism fortified with four aspects; dialogue,consultation, mediation and arbitration which can be agreed by all in order to avoid and settle disputes in the public sector, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement between Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation (SLBC) and the Encompass Digital Media Services Limited - London for the transmission of overseas programmmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10747",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The services of the TrincomaleeBroadcasting Station commenced as per the Agreement entered into between the Government of Sri Lanka and Deutsche Welle, the overseas broadcasting service of the Federal Republic of Germanin 1980 andthe operational activities of the said station have been entrusted with the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation in the year 2012. Subsequently, programmes were transmitted through the said station along with foreign media institutions. The Encompass Digital Media Services Limited - London, operating its business activities from Londonhas submitted a business proposal to transmit overseas programmes via short wave and medium wave and accordingly, foreign exchange of US$ 49,000 and US$ 16,000 can be earned respectively by the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation per month by providing its air time to the said Company. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Mediato enter into aBroadcasting Agreement between the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation and the Encompass Digital Media Services Limited - London for the transmission of overseas programmes using TrincomaleeBroadcasting Station of the Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Implementation of the proposed Gin-Nilwala Diversion project for the optimal use of water from the Gin and Nilwala rivers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10748",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The rivers Gin and Nilwala carry 2000 and 1200 cubic meters of water to the ocean, respectively. The Gin -Nilwala project has been proposed to implement for the purpose of diverting the excess water of the said two rivers in order to avoid shortage of drinking and irrigation water in the Hambantota District and also to control the floods in these rivers and studies in this regard are nearing its completion. Taking into consideration the proposals made by the Minister of Irrigation and the need to expedite the project, the Cabinet approval was granted to implement the project in phased out manner, utilizing local funds."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Changing the name of Manthai Salt Limited as 'National Salt Company' and transferring the ownership of all government owned Salterns in the Northern Province to the National Salt Company",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10749",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ceylon Salt Company was established by privatizing the Sri Lanka Salt Corporation in 1990 and all Salterns except the Salterns located in Northern Province were brought under the purview of the said Company. Subsequently, in the year 2001, a State-owned public company called Manthai Salt Ltd. was established and the administrativeand the operational activities of the Salterns located in the Northern Province were brought under the said Company. In accordance with the Extraordinary Gazette Notification No. 2196/27 dated 2020\u201110\u201106, the Manthai Salt Ltd. and the Elephant Pass Saltern have been incorporated as two public enterprises under the purview of the Ministry of Industries. Further, it has been found that maintenance of all Salterns located in the Northern Province under a single administrative structure would be economically and administratively more advantageous other than maintaining those as separate limited companies. Accordingly, taking into account the present needs, the proposal made by the the Minister of Industries to change the company name of Manthai Salt Ltd. functioning as a fully State-owned company under the Ministry of Industries, as \u201cNational Salt Company\u201d and to transfer the ownership, administrative activities and operational activities of the Elephant Pass Saltern located in the Northern Province to the National Salt Company, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Establishment of Centre of Excellence in Robotics Application - CERA",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10750",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2016\u201108\u201109 forthe establishment of Centre of Excellence in Robotics Application. With the establishment of the said Centre, it was expected to function as a technology transfer agency for the design, development and conduct of research with respect to robotic systems and vehicles for Government and industrial customers. Through the applications of this Centre, it is possible to provide services required by many local industries and to raise funds needed for the existence of the Institution. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to establish the Centre of Excellence in Robotics Application as a limited company under the Companies Act No. 7 of 2007 and maintenance of its activities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Use of environmentally-friendly materials to cover the roofs of Schools and Pre-Schools in place of Asbestos roofing sheets",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10751",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified through the studies of the World Health Organization (WHO)that all types of asbestos cause various diseases such as lung cancer and laryngeal cancer at present. Therefore, the use of environmentally-friendlysubstitutes for roofs in buildings of schools and Pre-Schools instead of asbestos enables to prevent school and Pre-School children being exposed to asbestos and it would be an important step that could be taken for the safety of their health. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to use locally manufactured roofing tiles and other environmentally-friendly substitutes forroofs in schools and Pre-Schools to be built in future instead of asbestosroofing sheets considering adverse effects that could be caused by asbestos to the future generation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Transfer of Ownership of the Fertilizer Testing Laboratory of Ceylon Fertilizer Company to the National Fertilizer Secretariat",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10752",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Fertilizer Testing Laboratory of Ceylon Fertilizer Company issues certificates to the relevant institutions after testing fertilizer samples. Since the Ceylon Fertilizer Company is a commercial institute engaged in the fertilizer supply process, it seems inappropriate to engage in the regulatory function of testing samples. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to transfer the ownership of the Fertilizer Testing Laboratory with its all movable and immovable assets to National Fertilizer Secretariat, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Providing production relief for six (06) selected crops under the Saubhagya \tFood \tProduction \tNational Program",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10753",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has been granted to provide guaranteed price for 16 crops and to provide seeds with the intervention of the Government with a view to encouraging local farmers. It seems appropriate to provide government assistance to farmers for obtaining seeds to meet the annual consumption requirement of Maize, Chillie, Big Onion, Red Onion, Potato and Black Gram locally, which are currently restricted to import. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, the Cabinet granted approvalto provide a 50% subsidy for the cost incurred on obtaining seeds up to one (1) acre of Maize and up to 1/2 acre of Chilli, Big Onion, Red Onion, Potato and Black Gram for the Maha season 2020/2021."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Tea Research Institute of Sri Lanka and Council of Scientific and Industrial Research Institute of Himalayan Bio-Resource Technology, India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10754",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Tea Research Institute of Sri Lanka has been awarded a grant to conduct a two year research project under the Indo \u2013 Sri Lanka Joint Research Programme on \u201cHigh throughput genotyping to expedite the genetic characterization and dissection of important agronomic traits of tea\u201d. The main objective of this research is to develop the molecular biology techniques required to accelerate the tea breeding programmes by reducing the time taken for cultivar development. Accordingly,the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Tea Research institute of Sri Lanka and the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research Institute of Himalayan Bio Resource Technology, India, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "The proposed Voluntary Retirement Scheme of Sri Lankan Airlines Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10755",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been decided to implement a Voluntary Retirement Scheme due to the financial crisis of the Sri Lankan Airlines Ltd. and a Three \u2013 Member Committee headed by the Secretary to the State Ministry of Aviation and Export Zones Development has been appointed to examine this matter. The said Committee has recommended to implement the proposed Voluntary Retirement Scheme without any hindrance to the operations of the Company for the next three years. It is expected that approximately 560 employees will be retired under this scheme andit has been estimated that Rs1.46 billion would be the cost on it. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to implement the aforesaid Retirement Scheme, was approved by the Cabinet of Ministers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Eppawala, Rajanganaya, Nochchiyagama & Giribawa Water Supply Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10756",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- A detailed financial proposal has been called from a Swiss Company to implement the Eppawala, Rajanganaya, Nochchiyagama and Giribawa Water Supply Project on the recommendation of the then Cabinet Sub Committee on Economic Management. The cost of the project presented by the said company was found to be very high. Therefore, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply, the Cabinet granted its approval to implement the said project under the local funds within the Medium\u2011Term Budgetary Framework pursuant to the plans prepared by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board by revising the scope of the said project."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-16-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2020-11-16",
    "description": "Purchasing a Maintenance andEmergency Response Vessel (MERV) \tfor The Ceylon Petroleum Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10757",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The fact that hiring a Maintenance and Emergency Response Vessel for the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation was discussed at the Cabinet meeting held on 2020\u201107\u201122 and it was decided at that Cabinet meeting to explore the possibility of providing relevant services by purchasing a Maintenance andEmergency Response Vessel by the Sri Lanka Navy.Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to purchase a new Maintenance and Emergency Response Vessel by the Sri Lanka Navy thereby connecting ships to two Single Point Buoy Moorings of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation, to provide tanker discharging operations and other necessary services and to purchase the said vessel from the Colombo Dockyard Company as agreed during the deliberations with the participation of the Ministry of Energy, Ministry of Defence and officials concerned, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
