    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Programme for the Budget Debate for the Financial Year 2021 prepared by the Office of the Leader of the House of Parliament and the Committee Stage Programme prepared by the Office of the Leader of the Opposition of Parliament, were submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister for the attention of the Cabinet. Accordingly, the Cabinet noted that it has been scheduled to conduct the Budget Speech on 2020\u201111\u201117, the Second Reading of the Budget from 2020\u201111\u201118 to 21, and that 16 days have been allocated for the Committee Stage from 2020\u201111\u201123 to 2020\u201112\u201110 and that the Third Reading Vote will take place on 2020.12.10."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Extending the term of the Committee established to make recommendations to regularize and make efficient the State Banking System to strengthen the National Economy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10759",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201107\u201122 granted approval to establish a Committee to submit appropriate recommendations within 03 months to regularize and make efficient the state banking system to strengthen the National economy. However, due to the prevailing situation in the country, the work of the committee could not be completed as expected. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to extend the term of the Committee for a period of three months with effect from 2020\u201111\u201118, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Extending the validity period of the Order issued under section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act No. 12 of 2017 on restriction of Foreign Exchange Outflows",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10760",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201106\u201124 granted approval to issue an Order valid for a period of 06 months under section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act No. 12 of 2017 to impose restrictions relating to outward foreign exchange capital transactions. Accordingly, the said Order has been imposed by the Gazette Extraordinary Notification dated 2020\u201107\u201102 and its validity period will expire on 2021\u201101\u201101. It has been found that it would be appropriate to extend the period of the same for another 06 months. The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to take necessary action accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Submission of the published Gazette Extraordinary Notifications to Parliament for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10761",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to submit six Gazette Extraordinary Notifications published under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007, one Gazette Extraordinary Notification published under the Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962 and one Gazette Extraordinary Notification issued in respect of imposing Surcharge on customs import duty for imported fuel in terms of the provisions of Customs Ordinance, to Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Acquiring the 48 Waththa land where the Sinhapura Housing Complex has been built to the Urban Settlement Development Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10762",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under two phases of the Sinhapura Housing Scheme Project, housing facilities have been provided to 120 low - income families living amidst minimum facilities within the Colombo Municipal Council area within a block of land in extent of 0.4423 hectares belonging to Wanathamulla of Divisional Secretariat Division, Thimbirigasyaya. The said housing programme has been implemented by an establishment called Real Estate Exchange (Pvt.) Limited which was fallen under the then Ministry which was vested with the subject of Housing, and has spent Rs. 174.15 million of budgetary allocations from the General Treasury for the purpose. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development & Housing for transferring the relevant plot of land to the Urban Development Authority as a free grant, enabling to issue deeds for those low \u2013 income families who have been granted houses, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Construction of the Administrative Complex-Polonnaruwa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10763",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2016\u201110\u201118 for the construction of the administrative complex of Polonnaruwa. The building has been constructed under the supervision of the Urban Development Authority having spent Rs.1,018 million. It has been planned to accommodate 19 Government and Semi \u2013 Government institutions in this building complex. Another Rs.265 million has been estimated to be spent for completion of its construction activities comprised of affixing air conditioning system, installation of electricity generators, completion of remaining work of the auditorium as well as landscaping. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development & Housing to secure required allocations to the State Ministry of Urban Development, Coast Conservation, Waste Disposal and Community Cleanliness for completion of construction work of the said building, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Providing relief to those who have been affected due to Weras Ganga Storm water Drainage and Environment Improvement project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10764",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Construction work of the Weras Ganga Storm water Drainage and Environment Improvement project has been inaugurated in 2013 with the objective of flood control in Colombo and suburbs, improvement of environmental systems, conservation of wetlands, conservation of sanctuaries as well as expanding the cannel system. Actions have been taken to compensate 80% of the value recommended by the Department of Valuation for the buildings and other constructions which will be affected by the said project and to pay a housing rental for obtaining temporary housing facilities for a period of 06 months for the people whose residences are totally evacuated under the project. The lands required for the project have been acquired by now and the construction work is scheduled to be concluded by the year 2020.\n\nThe Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing for further payment of housing rental paid for residing in temporary houses for an additional period until compensation is paid at a time the payment of statutory compensation decided for them is delayed more than 06 months due to unavoidable reasons and to pay 100% of the total estimated amount recommended by the Department of Valuation for the construction houses and buildings that are totally evacuated."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Increasing number of sports schools, development of infrastructure facilities in sports schools and increasing nutrition allowances and other allowances for the sports scholarship holders",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10765",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Measures have been taken in the year 1989 to inaugurate sports schools in all the districts, having one sports school in each district in the island. A programme has been planned collectively by the Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Youth & Sports in order to implement the said concept more productively. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the following joint proposals made by the Minister of Education and the Minister of Youth & Sports.\n\n*\tDevelopment of infrastructure facilities in 26 existing sports schools.\n\n*\t Development of the following schools as special sports schools.\n\ni. \tInauguration and development of a new bi - lingual National School by the name of \u2018Cricket Sports School\u2019 within the premises of Sooriyawewa International Cricket Stadium and enrol students to the grade six (6) from the year 2021.\n\nii.\tDevelopment of Pelwatte Navodya School as a sports school for athletics/ Volleyball.\n\niii. Development of Mahinda Rajapaksha Vidyalaya, Pitipana for athletics.\n\niv. Development of Murunkan Maha Vidyalaya, Mannar for football / athletics.\n\n*\tConstruction of new school hostels in the sport schools where there are no hostels and development of the existing hostels.\n\n*\t Increase of sports scholarships and other allowances to suit the current requirements."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Policy to Collect Sex-and Age- Disaggregated Data and Information",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10766",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The difficulty in obtaining information on gender and age disaggregated data with the exception of a limited number of census and surveys by the Department of Census and Statistics and the surveys of the health sector has become an issue in the policy and planning process. This information is essential for identifying Government-prioritized needs, especially in the field of child and women's development, and for understanding their trends and determining plans and strategies for addressing them. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to make it compulsory to collect information based on gender and age group in all census, surveys and studies conducted by Ministries, Departments and Statutory Institutions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Facilitating the issuance of vehicle number plates and driving licenses to the client public through the speed post courier service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10767",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The vehicle registration certificate, vehicle number plates and a sticker are issued when registering a vehicle. Under the existing system, one has to come to the Department of Motor Traffic spending considerable time and expense in order to obtain them. Further, there seems to be some delay in sending new driver's licenses by registered mail to clients. As a remedy for the issue, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to implement a suitable programme in collaboration with the Postal Department enabling to deliver them to the client's home under the express courier service implemented by the Postal Department, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Issuance of Postal Stamps in Commemoration of 50 years of Sri Lanka-Singapore Diplomatic Relations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10768",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Posts of Sri Lanka and Singapore Post Limited have agreed to issue two stamps each in commemoration of 50 years of Sri Lanka-Singapore diplomatic relations. Accordingly, it is planned to create stamps under a common theme \"Oceanic Bio Conservation\" for both parties and to exchange each 4000 stamps and 1000 commemorative leaflets between the two parties. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to sign a Memorandum of Understanding for the purpose between the two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Implementation of Livestock Development Projects for the year 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10769",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement \u201cSaubhagya\u201d Diary Development Programme and the \"Dairy Development Centres\" project in the year 2021 to increase local milk production under the State Ministry of Livestock, Farm Promotion and Dairy & Egg Related Industries. Activities such as improving efficiency of animal breeding, animal nutrition, animal health conditions and creating eco\u2011friendly farms through animal waste management are planned under the \u201cSauubhagya\u201d Dairy Development Programme. The Dairy Development Centres Establishment Project aims to develop the milk value chain process by upgrading artificial insemination Centres, providing the necessary inputs and training, and networking Veterinary Surgeon's offices. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to secure provisions within the 2021-2023 Medium Term Budget Framework for the implementation of these projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Development and Conservation of the National Art Gallery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10770",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been received on several occasions for the renovation of the National Art Gallery. Although the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2018\u201108\u201121 has granted approval to allocate Rs. 42 million for the purpose, relevant renovations have not been carried out. Main building of the Art Gallery is in a dilapidated condition due to water leaking from the main rain water pipe that was installed to drain the rainwater and it needs to be repaired immediately. Accordingly, the proposal presented by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to obtain the services of the Sri Lanka Navy and carry out the relevant repairs of the National Art Gallery, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Suraksha Student Insurance Coverage 2020/2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10771",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Proposals have been invited from Government-owned insurance companies for \u201cSuraksha\u201d student insurance. In response to the invitation, only the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation has submitted a proposal. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to award the Procurement for the securing of Suraksha Student Insurance Scheme to the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, following the negotiations conducted with the said Corporation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Award of the contract for the supply and distribution of Arial Bundled Conductor Alu. (ABC) 230/400V 3x70+54.6+16 sqmm - 2000km",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10772",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Competitive bids have been called for the supply of Arial Bundled Conductors for distribution zone 2 of the Ceylon Electricity Board. Accordingly, the proposal made by Minister of power to award the contract for the supply and distribution of Arial Bundled Conductor Alu. (ABC) 230/400V 3x70+54.6+16 sqmm - 2000km of the Ceylon Electricity Board to M/s ACL Cables PLC as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Awarding the term contract for the import of Gasoline for a period of eight months from 2020-12-01 to 2021-07-31",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10773",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called from the registered suppliers of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation to import 1,564,500 Bbls +10/-5% of Gasoline (92 Unl) & 535,500 Bbls +10/-5% of Gasoline (95 Unl) during the period of eight months from 2020\u201112\u201101 to 2021\u201107\u201131. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to award the relevant procurement to M/s BB Energy (Asia) pte. Ltd., Singapore, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Construction of the new Court Complex, Kalutara",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10774",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Kaluthara Court Complex which is already being operated within a land and buildings with an archaeological value and the Ministry of Justice has been endowed a plot of land in extent of 1.064 hectares to build a New Court Complex under the Kaluthara Urban Development Project. Therefore the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to award the consultancy service for the construction of the new Court Complex to the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Appointment of a Committee to look into the irregularities that occurred in the Grand Hyatt Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10775",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Grand Hyatt Hotel Project is implemented by the Sino Lanka (Pvt) Ltd, which possesses the ownership of the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation, Employees\u2019 Provident Fund and Litro Gas Lanka Ltd. The hotel was scheduled to open in business activities during the first quarter of 2016 afterwards the completion of construction. Provided that, most of the agreements signed by the previous Government were terminated by the new board of directors of the Sino Lanka (Pvt) Ltd. which was appointed following the 2015 presidential election without any justifiable reason and has been entered into agreements with new contractors for aforementioned work phases. Therefore, some companies have initiated legal proceedings and it has been decided that the Sino Lanka (Pvt) Ltd shall pay approximately a sum of Rs.1.8 billion as compensation. The current cost of the the project, which was originally planned to be completed at an estimated cost of Rs.30 billion , has been re-estimated to be around Rs.60 billion. Therefore, approval has been granted by the Cabinet for proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to appoint a committee to investigate whether the Government has incurred a financial loss as it appears that the situation has arisen due to the irregularities committed by the previous management of the Sino Lanka (Pvt) Ltd."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-11-30-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2020-11-30",
    "description": "Awarding of Construction Contract of 27.7km long Tunnel Section in 95.86km long North Central Main Canal Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10776",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-11-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to construct a 27.7 km tunnel from Koduruwawa to Namalpura via the protected forests and sanctuaries in Minneriya, Girithale and Hurulu as a package of the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme which is implemented under the funds of the Asian Development Bank. For the purpose, international competitive bids have been invited to select a suitable contractor. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to award the relevant contract to the China State Construction Engineering Corporation Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Project to manufacture semi steel radial tyres and all steel radial tyres for export market",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10777",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Shandong Haohua Tire Co. Limited of China has submitted a project proposal to the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka with an investment of US$ 300 million for the establishment of a project within the premises of Hambantota International Port for manufacturing semi - steel radial tyres and total steel radial tyres for the export market. The board of investment of Sri Lanka has given its consent for the implementation of this project as a strategic development project under the Strategic Development Act (Amended) No. 14 of 2008. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to grant the relevant tax concessions as per the provisions furnished by the Strategic Development Act, subject to inauguration of the project within a period of 36 months and export at least 80% of the total production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Submission of the published Gazette Notifications for approval in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10778",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance for the submission of the following Gazette Notifications in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n(i) \tGazette Notifications issued under the Ports and Airports Development Levy Act, No. 18 of 2011;\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2191/25 dated 2020-09-02 \n\n*\t  Gazette Notification No. 2198/57 dated 2020-10-23\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2199/2 dated 2020-10-26\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2203/37 dated 2020-11-28\n\n(ii) \tGazette Notifications issued under the Excise (Special Provisions) Act No. 13 of 1989;\n\n*\tGazette Notification No. 2189/47 dated 2020-08-21\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2197/3 dated 2020-10-12\n\n(iii) \tthe Gazette Notification No. 2194/6 dated 2020-09-21 published under the Finance Act No. 25 of 2003\n\n(iv)\tGazette Notifications under the Strategic Development Projects Act No. 14 of 2008\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2201/6 dated 2020-11-10\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2202/3 dated 2020-11-16\n\n*\t Gazette Notification No. 2203/16 dated 2020-11-24."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Obtaining provisions for the working capital requirements of the Central Cultural Fund",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10779",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The income of the Central Cultural Fund has been declined due to the complete collapsing down of the tourism industry with the expansion of the global Corona pandemic. Although, actions have been taken previously to obtain a loan of Rs.135 million for the activities of the said fund having obtained the Cabinet approval, it has been observed that, the amount obtained is not sufficient for maintaining the institutional activities. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of  Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs for obtaining Rs.50 million from the General Treasury for settling the bills relevant to the conservation and construction activities presently being performed by the institution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Performing essential renovation and rehabilitation activities of the Mahinda Rajapaksa National Tele Cinema Park",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10780",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mahinda Rajapaksha National Tele Cinema Park has been established for earmarking a renaissance in the local cinema and tele creations sector by providing studios and scenic background facilities as well as accommodation and other facilities for artists of the said field, on a concessionary basis. 13 local films, 18 tele dramas and 08 songs for advertisements have been produced up to date since the year 2010. Since this park has not been properly maintained for the past four years, most of the physical resources of the institution are being deteriorated. Therefore, it has been identified that prompt actions should be taken to carry out essential renovations of the tele cinema park and accordingly, the the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs for allocating funds from the General Treasury during the years 2021 and 2022 for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Amendment to the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation Act, No.15 of 1968",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10781",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2015\u201112\u201102 for further amendment of the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation Act, No. 15 of 1968 (Amended) as amended by the Acts, No. 27 of 1976, No. 52 of 1982, No. 35 of 2006 and No. 11 of 2019. Accordingly, clearance from the Attorney General has been received for the draft bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing to publish the said draft bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Amendment of the method of payment of four housing projects implemented with the Indian Government Aid",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10782",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has granted an award of Rs.300 million each for implementing 04 projects for the construction of houses for low \u2013 income families and the relevant projects are being implemented by the National Housing Development Authority. Steps will be taken to release applicable funds followed by a progress report submitted to the Indian High Commission by National Housing Development Authority upon the completion of the relevant construction by the beneficiaries with their cost. However, since the house owners do not have sufficient funds to complete the construction as supposed that the progress of the project lies at a lower level. Therefore the Indian High Commission has agreed to release the initial payment required for the construction at the inauguration of work and continue to release the rest of the instalments on the progress of the construction. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing for taking necessary action to implement the said projects,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Amendment of the Institutional Name of the Children's Secretariat as the 'National Secretariat for Early Childhood Development'",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10783",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The \"Children's Secretariat\" which has been established in the year 1979, functions as the central institution that executes the National Policy on Early Childhood Care and Development. Though the institute also plays a special role in the field of early childhood education, it seems that, the current institutional name of the said Secretariat does not imply that role. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to amend the institutional name of \u201cChildren's Secretariat\u201d as \u201cNational Secretariat for Early Childhood Development\u201d, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Increasing the number of National Schools to 1000",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10784",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Policy approval has been granted by the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2019\u201112\u201110 to implement an appropriate program to establish 1000 new National Schools covering all Divisional Secretariat Divisions. Accordingly, the program is planned to be implemented in three phases and the proposal made by the Minister of Education to implement the relevant programme to develop one selected Provincial Council School as a National School in each of the 123 Divisional Secretariat Divisions in which there are no National Schools as the first phase, to upgrade 673 schools selected on the basis of identified criteria as National Schools under the second phase and to further develop the existing 373 National Schools under the third phase,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Formulating a Long-Term 'Human Resource Development Plan' for the Public Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10785",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Formulation and implementation of a long-term \"Human Resource Development Plan\" has been identified as an urgent programme for enhancing the performance and productivity of the public sector. Public Administration Circular No. 02/2018 dated 2018\u201101\u201124, emphasizes the need of preparing a Human Resource Development Plan by every State Institution. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Services, Provincial Councils and Local Government to formulate a long term \"Human Resource Development Plan\" with the participation of all relevant parties to enhance the efficiency and productivity of the public service, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Securing necessary financial support for the working capital requirement of the Laksala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10786",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Revenue earned by Laksala  has dropped by 90% due to the absence of foreign tourists due to the Covid-19 pandemic, making it difficult to run the institution. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to secure the necessary provisions from the General Treasury for salaries and working capital requirements including other essential expenses required to function the Laksala, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Establishment of the 1000 Acre Fodder Silage Baling Project  at the Polonnaruwa Farm of the National Livestock Development Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10787",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Lack of quality roughage has been identified as a major issue in large scale dairy farms belonging to the National Livestock Development Board and generally, one dairy cow should be fed with roughage of about 10% of her body weight. As a remedy to this situation, it has been planned to commence a Fodder Silage Baling Project within 1000 acres  of the Polonnaruwa farm of the National Livestock Development Board. As its initial stage, it has been planned to cultivate 1000 acres of nutritive maize and sorghum and produce mechanized baled silage and to import 2000 dairy cows and keep them in the farms as the second phase of the project, Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agricultur to obtain 60% of the total capital expenditure estimated for the project as a government contribution, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Increase the quality seed production required to enhance the availability of crop production in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10788",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The \"Food Production National Program\", launched in the Yala season 2020 to reduce imports by cultivating locally grown crops, is now being successfully implemented. Since it is difficult for the Department of Agriculture alone to provide quality seeds to increase harvests and the area of cultivated lands the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to implement a formal program in collaboration with the Provincial and Inter-Provincial Departments of Agriculture and the Seed Producers' Institutions in the Mahaweli areas, enabling the farmers to produce their own  seed requirements in respective areas."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2020-12-07-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2020-12-07",
    "description": "Construction of a Building for the proposed Army Base Hospital at Pallekale",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=10789",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2020-12-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- A new base hospital is designed to be constructed at Pallekele, Kandy to provide basic medical treatment to army personnel serving and residing in Kandy and surrounding districts. For the purpose, it is expected to construct a 3 storey building and the estimated cost is Rs.376.22 million. Accordingly the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence  to complete the construction of the proposed hospital within a year using the labour of other ranks of the Sri Lanka Army Professionals and to secure provisions required for the purpose from the General Treasury, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
