    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11069",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- An agreement has been reached between the Open University of Sri Lanka and the Korea National Open University, South Korea to develop collaboration in the fields of open and distance education, capacity building, ICT applications, use of laboratory services, research and publications and staff exchange programmes. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign an MoU to that effect, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Establishment of a fully equipped Haemodialysis Unit and Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) Clinic with NCD Screening facility at Colombo East Base Hospital, Mulleriyawa",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11070",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- Colombo East Base Hospital located at Mulleriyawa provides secondary healthcare facilities to a large number of people in Colombo district and the Hospital, at present, offers all major specialist consultation services in the fields of medicine, surgery, gynecology and obstetrics and pediatrics. Further, under the ongoing projects, it has been planned to establish new units of National Stroke Centre, Level 2 Accident and Emergency Unit, Intensive Care Unit (ICU), Neo-natal Intensive Care Unit (NICU) and Simulation Centre for this Hospital. In addition, it has been proposed to establish a dialysis unit with 12 dialysis machines and a fully equipped Haemodialysis Unit with necessary surgical equipment which can cater to 20 patients per day and a CKD clinic with Non Communicable Disease (NCD) screening facility, using a grant provided by the District 306 C1 of International Lions Clubs. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Health and the District 306 C1 of International Lions Club for the implementation of the said project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Amendment to the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation Act No. 28 of 1961",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11071",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since some of the provisions of the the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation Act No. 28 of 1961 which are currently in force, are inadequate for the present-day requirements, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to amend the said Act, incorporating the amendments identified for the same and to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a draft Bill for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 in Parliament for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11072",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been observed that certain vehicle importers get a special advantage by registering the imported mobile workshops as dual purpose vehicles. Taking into account the recommendations made by the Committee on Public Accounts to that effect, Regulations to introduce a new Harmonized System Code (HS Code) to levy equal duty on mobile workshops and dual purpose vehicles and to allow to import them based on equal lifetime, have been published in the Gazette Notification dated 2020\u201104\u201123 as per the provisions of the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No. 1 of 1969. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to submit the Regulations so published in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Construction of the Elevated Expressway connecting Athurugiriya Interchange and New Kelani Bridge",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11073",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2020\u201104\u201108 has granted approval to implement the Elevated Expressway connecting Athurugiriya Interchange and New Kelani Bridge on Built, Operate and Transfer (BOT) basis. Accordingly, Bids including technical and financial proposals have been invited from the relevant investors for the proposed project. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport to assign the task of implementing the said project to M/s China Harbor Engineering Corporation (CHEC) as recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Accelerating treatments for COVID-19 patients",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11074",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The critically ill patients among the most of patients diagnosed under the third wave of COVID \u2013 19 are required to be treated under oxygen concentrators. Accordingly, proposals made by the Minister of Health to take expeditious action as follows to ensure the medical oxygen supply for the critically ill patients, were approved by the Cabinet.  \n\t\n    \u2022 Establishment of High Dependency Units with Wall Oxygen Outlets enabling to treat the critically ill patients in 25 Hospitals identified Provincial level covering the whole Island.\n      \n    \u2022 Installation of 15 Oxygen Concentrators in 15 identified hospitals located in remote areas to secure medical oxygen supply required for hospitals.\n      \n    \u2022 Providing 2500 Portable Oxygen Concentrators by 100 machines per each district thereby reducing the requirement of Cylinder-based oxygen supply. \n    \u2022 maintenance of adequate stock of Oxygen in the country having imported 120,000 litres of Liquefied Oxygen monthly in order to meet the increasing demand for medical Oxygen."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-24-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2021-05-24",
    "description": "Purchase of Sinopharm and Oxford-AstraZeneca (OAZ) Vaccines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11075",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-24",
    "decision_details_body": "- The required quantity of vaccines has to be obtained at the earliest in the circumstances where there is no other remedy to combat the COVID - 19 pandemic other than vaccination. The Government has planned to vaccinate 60 % - 70% of the overall population by the end of this year. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to take necessary action to purchase 14 million doses of Sinopharm Vaccine from the relevant manufacturer of China and 1 million doses of Oxford-AstraZeneca vaccine expeditiously, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-31-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2021-05-31",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969, for approval in Parliament",
