    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-31",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of promoting the use of organic fertilizers for agricultural products, the Cabinet decided on 2021\u201104\u201127 to ban the importation of chemical fertilizers, pesticides and herbicides. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to submit the Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations promulgated under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 pertaining to the implementation of the said Cabinet decision, for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-31-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2021-05-31",
    "description": "Payment of compensation to the people affected by the establishment of the Anuradhapura South and Anuradhapura North Multi-Transport Centres",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11077",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-31",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Anuradhapura Joint Urban Development project is carried out by the Ministry of Urban Development & Housing on the funds provided by the French Development Agency (AFD). The prime objective of this project is to improve urban services and public places in the city of Anuradhapura while preserving its cultural heritage. It has been planned under this project to develop the Anuradhapura new bus stand as the Anuradhapura South Multi\u2011Transport Centre and to remove the Anuradhapura old bus stand and the long distance service bus stand from those places and to develop the same as the Anuradhapura North Multi\u2011Transport Centre in close proximity to the Anuradhapura main Railway Station. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing to pay compensation to 302 families to be affected by the said projects subject to the relevant criteria, taking into consideration the nature of the impact, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-31-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2021-05-31",
    "description": "Establishment of a Vessel Monitoring System (VMS) to comply with the local and international legal requirements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11078",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-31",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the Indian Ocean Tuna Commission (IOTC) Resolution 15/03, it is essential to set up a Vessel Monitoring System (VMS) to identify the location of multi\u2011day fishing vessels at sea, to launch Search and Rescue (SAR) Operations at disaster situations and to control illegal and unofficial fisheries activities carried out via maritime passages by using multi\u2011day fishing vessels. In 2015, a VMS using satellite technology was installed in 1,250 multi\u2011day fishing vessels registered under the Department of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources (DFAR). In addition to the said fisheries vessels, 4,200 other such multi\u2011day fishing vessels are required to be fitted with the relevant devices. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries to take necessary action to install the said VMS through a procurement process conducted by the International Organization for Migration (IOM) by using a grant of Australian Dollar 5.38 million provided by the Department of Home Affairs (DOH) of Australia, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-05-31-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2021-05-31",
    "description": "Housing Project of Maliboda Estate - Deraniyagala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11079",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-05-31",
    "decision_details_body": "- In response to a request made at the 'Gama Samaga Pilisandarak' program conducted by H. E. the President at Deraniyagala area, it has been proposed to implement a housing project for the estate workers in Maliboda area. It has been planned to construct 171 houses for the estate workers under the said project. The Government of India has also agreed to provide a grant of Rs.500 million for construction of 480 estate houses including the proposed houses in response to the request made by H. E. the President. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing to implement the project for constructing 171 housing units at Maliboda Estate under the proposed Indian Grant Scheme and to award the contract for constructing 60 houses as its first phase, to the State Engineering Corporation (SEC), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
