    "description": "Submission of the Gazette Notification published under the Value Added Tax Act, No14 of 2002 for approval in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11142",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Gazette Notification No.2228/33 dated 2021\u201105\u201120 has been issued under the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002 enacting a regulation by the Minister of Finance making it compulsory the completion of schedules 6 and 7 that can be obtained from the web portal of the Department of Inland Revenue, enabling to streamline the values of exports declared by exporters with export data submitted to the Sri Lanka Customs. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance to submit the said regulation in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2021-07-05-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2021-07-05",
    "description": "Implementation of New Tax Proposals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11143",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2021-07-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Budget 2021 has proposed to impose legal provisions for the investors to pay only a \u201cTax on Voluntary Disclosure\u201d at the rate of 1%, exempting them from a paying a tax, penalty or interest or from any investigation or prosecution in order to encourage such investors to disclose and invest undisclosed income and assets. Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201102\u201122 to draft the Finance Bill - 2021 in order to make provisions required for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, to publish the draft bill so prepared in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
