    "date_str": "2022-01-03",
    "description": "Draft Bills for amending the Special Goods and Services Tax Bill and the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11388",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed through the Budgets 2021 and 2022 to impose online-managed single Special Goods and Services Tax in place of multiple taxes and levies imposed under several legal statutes to improve the efficiency of tax collection on liquor, cigarette, telecommunication, betting and gaming and vehicles. It has also been proposed by the Budget 2022 to increase Value Added Tax (VAT) charged on financial services and to exempt medical equipment, accessories and chemicals etc. donated to the Government Hospitals and the Ministry of Health to address any pandemic or public health conditions from the Value Added Tax. The clearances of the Attorney General have been received for the Special Goods and Services Tax Bill and the Value Added Tax (Amendment) Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to publish the said draft Bills in the Government Gazette and to submit the same thereafter in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-03-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-01-03",
    "description": "Amending the Public Administration Circular No. 03/2016 pertaining to the removal of Salary Anomalies in the Teachers' and Principals' Services",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11389",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet has granted approval to remove the salary anomalies in the Teachers' and Principals' Services based on the set of proposals submitted to the then National Pay Commission by the Ministry of Education in consultation with the Trade Unions in the year 2018 and action has also been taken to allocate necessary provisions through the Budget proposals for the year 2022 to implement the said proposal. Accordingly, the proposals made by the Minister of Education to amend the Public Administration Circular No. 03/2016 to enable to remove the salary anomalies in the Teachers' and Principals' Services including the salary scales to the Teacher Advisors Service, since the said service had not been established at the time of preparation of the relevant proposals in the year 2018, were approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-03-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-01-03",
    "description": "Programme for promoting the installment of Battery Energy Storage System for the Roof Top Solar Sites",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11390",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has taken a policy decision to take necessary action to generate 70% of the electricity requirement of the country by the renewable energy and to reach carbon neutrality at the electricity generation by the year 2030. The Solar Power Systems installed on roof tops currently provide a capacity of 400 MW to the national grid of the Country. Encouraging consumers to install battery systems for these systems on self-financed investment through a new tariff system will enable the public to secure a more reliable supply of electricity. In this context, An Officials Committee was appointed to identify the technical challenges that could arise in connecting high percentage of electricity receiving from the renewable energy to the national grid and submit recommendation on the same and the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201111\u201123 decided to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee to further study matters on the recommendations of the said Officials Committee. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to implement the proposed programme as per the recommendations submitted by the said Cabinet Sub-Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-03-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-01-03",
    "description": "Trincomalee Oil Tank Farm Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11391",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Both India and Sri lanka have reached an agreement to review the existing three commitments with India pertaining to the Trincomalee Oil Tank Complex and to implement a joint development project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to allocate 24 Oil tanks for the business activities of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation and to allocate 14 Oil tanks in the lower tank farm which are already being used by the Lanka IOC for its business activities and to provide the rest of 61 tanks to the Trinco Petroleum Terminal (Private) Limited which was established holding 51% of the share entitlement to the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation and 49% of the share entitlement to the Lanka IOC, to implement a development project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-03-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-01-03",
    "description": "Economy 2022 and the Way forward",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11392",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-03",
    "decision_details_body": "- Subsequent to the passage of the Budget - 2022 in Parliament, the implementation of the same has been commenced from 01st of January 2022. The following information pertaining to the External Outlook of the Sri Lankan Economy was brought to notice of the Cabinet by the Minister of Finance with a view to achieving the desired objectives of the Budget.\n\n    \u2022 Information on estimated foreign exchange that will flow out of the country in the year 2022, including foreign debt servicing payments and expected import costs of goods and services.\n      \n    \u2022 the expected foreign exchange inflows in the year 2022, including export earnings, earnings from tourism industry, remittances by migrant workers, and foreign direct investments.\n\n    \u2022 Proposed short term- and medium-term measures to cover the expected foreign exchange deficit.\n\n    \u2022 The following reliefs proposed to minimize the economic hardships faced by the people due to the increase in prices of goods and services under the prevailing economic situation.\n\n          (i)\tGranting a monthly allowance of Rs. 5000 for the \tPublic Servants and pensioners from January.\n  \n          (ii)\tTaking action to provide the above concession to \tprivate sector employees as well in consultation with \tprivate sector employers.\n\n          (iii)\tproviding an additional allowance of Rs. 1,000 / - to \tthe Samurdhi beneficiaries entitled the monthly \tallowance of Rs. 3,500/- and giving the same allowance \tto other Samurdhi beneficiaries as well.\n  \n          (iv)\tpayment of an additional amount of Rs. 25/- per 1kg of \tpaddy in addition to the guaranteed price of Rs.50/- \tcurrently being paid per 1kg of paddy, in case of any \treduction in the paddy harvest in the upcoming season.\n  \n          (v)\tbearing the additional amount so paid by the \tGovernment so as not affecting the price of rice in the \tmarket.\n  \n          (vi)\tImplementing a home gardening programme to \tencourage the cultivation of vegetables and fruits \trequired for their self consumption and providing an \tincentive allowance up to a maximum of Rs. 10,000/- \tdepending on the size of the land not more than one \tacre for inputs such as preparing the land, obtaining \tseeds etc. \n  \n          (vii)\tProviding 15kg of wheat flour at a concessionary \tprice of Rs. 80/- per kilogram to a estate sector \temployee's family.\n  \n          (viii)\tfully exempting the all essential food and \tmedicine from \ttax, taking action to protect local farmers and \tproducers whenever necessary.\n  \nThe Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the implementation of the arrangement including the above proposals submitted by the Minister of Finance."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Providing houses to the families affected due to overflowing of the Buthgamuwa Canal during rainy season",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11403",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The programme for resettlement of families residing in areas with landslide risks is being implemented in 14 districts and 1,558 families have been resettled under this programme. Also, although there is no risk of landslides, it has been observed the appropriateness of including such families in the resettlement programme to relocate families who are constantly affected by disasters such as coastal erosion, river bank wahsouts and constant submerging with floods. Accordingly, the requirement of resettling 42 families affected by constant floods due to overflowing of the Buthgamuwa Canal in 514 Welikada East Grama Niladhari Division in Sri Jayawardenapura Kotte Divisional Secretariat Division during rainy season, in another location has been identified. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to remove the said 42 families from their residences and provide them with 42 houses from the housing projects implemented by the Urban Development Authority (UDA) for the persons with low\u2011income, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Implementation of the Projects identified for promotion of Buddhist Heritage between Sri Lanka and India",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11404",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has expressed its concurrence to award a grant of LKR 2.89 billion during a period of five (05) years, to promote cultural and public ties between Sri Lanka and India and to implement projects identified for further strengthening the co\u2011operation of Buddhist Heritage of both countries. It has been planned to implement projects identified in association with the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs and the High Commissioner of India pertaining to development of infrastructure facilities, capacity building, cultural affairs, archaeological collaboration, exhibition of relics of Lord Buddha in Sri Lanka and promotion of Buddhist tours to India. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious & Cultural Affairs to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of India to implement the proposed programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Providing Permanent Houses for families who do not have a house or a land to construct a house and live mainly on rent basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11405",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- In view of providing permanent houses at an affordable price for the low middle income families with true housing requirement who reside in rented houses due to not having either a house or a land to construct a house, the State Ministry of Rural Housing and Construction & Building Material Industries Promotion has planned to implement a housing programme named as \u201cSonduru Mahal Niwasa\u201d through the National Housing Development Authority. Under the programme, the selected beneficiaries should have the ability of making a down\u2011payment of Rs.500,000/- and the remaining value of the house will be charged in installments within a year. The selected beneficiaries will also be given the opportunity to obtain loans from Banks as found necessary. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to implement the said housing programme and to construct 72 houses in a plot of land at Ranpokunugama, belonging to the National Housing Development Authority as its pilot project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Government of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland on Healthcare Cooperation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11406",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been agreed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Sri Lanka and the United Kingdom on the mutually agreed matters including enhancing cooperation between both countries in health sector and ensuring the rights of healthcare professionals serving in the United Kingdom. Specially, it will be possible to receive the employment opportunities being generated in the health sector in the said country to Sri Lanka, subsequent to the breaking up of the United Kingdom from the European Union. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Labour, the Foreign Minister and the Minister of Health to sign the said Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the Ministry of Education of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary to implement a Scholarship Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11407",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to further improving the cooperation between Sri Lanka and Hungary, it has been proposed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to grant scholarships to Sri Lankan students during 2022\u20112024 under the 'STIPENDIUM HUNGARICUM' Scholarship Program for foreign students implemented under the supervision of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary. Under the said programme, Sri Lankan students will be provided with the opportunity to follow 08 Undergraduate Degrees, 08 Postgraduate Degrees and 04 Doctoral Degrees. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to sign the said MoU between the Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Establishment of Weli Oya Sugar Factory attached to Lanka \tSugar Company (Pvt.) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11408",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Annual requirement of Sugar in the Country is around 600,000 MT.  Approximately 85% out of the same is imported spending about Rs. 45 billion annually. Local sugar production in the year 2020 was 54,000 MT and necessary arrangements have been made to increase that quantity further. Accordingly, it has been proposed to establish a new sugar factory based in Weli Oya at Monaragala district under  Lanka Sugar Company (Pvt.) Ltd. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation to implement the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-01-10-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-01-10",
    "description": "Industry Support Scheme for Global Promotions by Local Destination Management Companies, Hoteliers and Online Travel Agents",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11409",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-01-10",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau has made arrangements to implement an industry support scheme for global promotions made by  local destination management companies, hoteliers and online travel agents under the post COVID - 19 situation. It is expected to provide the said relief for the institutions qualified under the above programme for a maximum period of 06 months, in the year 2022. The Board of Management of the  Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau has granted approval to allocate Rs. 400 million for the proposed programme under its funds. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to implement the proposed industry support scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
