    "date_str": "2022-02-21",
    "description": "Operation of the Weuda Factory owned by the Ceylon Ceramics Corporation through a private investor",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11485",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Manufacturing activities of the Weuda Tile Factory belonging to the Ceylon Ceramics Corporation, located in Mawathagama in Kurunegala district, have been suspended in the year 2010 due to the issue of securing raw materials. The Sri Lanka Navy has thereafter used this factory to manufacture bricks required for the Sandahiru Seya in Anuradhapura and the said activities have also been suspended since the year 2017. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to call for Expressions of Interest (EoI) from the investors showing an interest to start and maintain a clay related industry in the Weuda factory in the extent of 09 Acres 01 Rood and 31 Perches and provide the same on lease basis to an investor who confirms a higher viability, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-21-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-02-21",
    "description": "Market-Oriented Dairy (MOD) Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11486",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- With a view to utilizing the best practices to improve the productivity of the dairy manufacturers and the quality of their products, the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) has agreed to provide financial assistance to implement a Market\u2011Oriented Dairy (MOD) Project. The said Department has also agreed to provide funds required for this project up to September 2024. It has been planned through the proposed project to continue their capacity building programmes with 38 key stakeholders in the Government and Private Dairy Manufacturing Sector. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the United States Department of Agriculture and the Ministry of Agriculture of Sri Lanka for the implementation of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-21-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-02-21",
    "description": "Granting a monthly allowance for Athletes and Coaches under the High Performance Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11487",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- Targeting the 2024 and 2028 Olympic Games, the National Sports Council has recommended to implement an encouragement programme so as to grant a financial support to the athletes with special talents who have been selected according to their performance based qualifications, undergoing a long term systematic training, anticipating medals to accomplish their training requirements and also a financial allowance to their coaches.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Youth and Sports to pay a monthly allowance of Rs.100,000/-  each to the selected athletes in the pool of high talents and Rs.50,000/- each for their coaches, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-02-21-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-02-21",
    "description": "Obtaining the services of  Youths as \u201cCommunity Assistants (Voluntary)\u201d at the level of Grama Niladhari Divisions",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11488",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-02-21",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Community Police Service functioning in the countries such as Japan and Singapore, has been found possible to reduce the rate of minor crimes committed at the community level. Based on the success of such programmes, the Ministry of Public Security together with the State Ministry of Community Police Service and the Sri Lanka Police have taken action to attach two police officers for each Grama Niladhari Division, under the Community Police Service, commencing from May 2021, on full time basis. Accordingly, two young people residing in each Grama Niladhari Division have been planned to attach  as \u201cCommunity Assistants (Voluntary)\u201d, in order to obtain the required support to have community participation to accomplish the duties of the police officers. Youths over the age of 18 years and permanent residents of  relevant Grama Niladhari Divisions and who have served as prefects in their schools and holding the membership of youth clubs and other volunteer groups can apply for this. They may provide a honorable service whereas they are not entitled to any allowance or any other right. The Sri Lanka Police will issue them a volunteer identity card and after the expiry of 6 months period they will be awarded a service certificate on \u201cCommunity Leadership\u201d. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the arrangement presented by the Minister of Public Security on the implementation of the proposed programme."
  },
  {
