    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- An area of 400 acres belonging to the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation, located in the Muthurajawela Industrial Zone has been developed by pumping sea sand. A number of blocks of land out of the said land have been vested with public and private sector investors for the projects of national importance. Emergent Cold (Pvt) Ltd has made a request to allocate a block of land from the said land for cold store facilities and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka has informed that the said Company has fulfilled the basic qualifications under section 17 of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Act, to obtain the relevant block of land. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development & Housing to provide a block of land in the extent of 04 Acres 02 Roods that has been identified as appropriate for the proposed project, to the said Company for a period of 30 years on long term lease basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "BIMSTEC Convention on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11500",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to sign the BIMSTEC Convention on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters. As such, the matters submitted by the Foreign Minister that his Ministry has taken necessary action to have the said Convention signed by the Ministry of Justice with each member states of the BIMSTEC Organization  during the Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economical Co operation (BIMSTEC) summit scheduled to be held on 2022 03 30, were noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "BIMSTEC Memorandum of Association (MoA) for the establishment of the Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC) Technology Transfer facility",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11501",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously to enter into the Memorandum of Association for the establishment of the BIMSTEC Technology Transfer Facility. As such, the matters submitted by the Foreign Minister that action is being taken by his Ministry to have the said Convention signed by the State Ministry of Skills Development, Vocational Education, Research and Innovation with each member states of the BIMSTEC Organization  during the Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economical Co operation (BIMSTEC) summit scheduled to be held on 2022 03 30, were noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Donation of wheelchairs and other mobility aid to the Rheumatology and Rehabilitation Hospital (RRH), Ragama",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11502",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been reported that nearly 1,500 people suffer with spinal injuries per year. The Rheumatology and Rehabilitation Hospital (RRH), Ragama is the national centre where patients in need of such rehabilitation treatment services are referred to. Annually, about 200 wheelchairs, 350 walking aid and 100 prosthetic kits are required for the patients in the said Hospital. A global humanitarian aid organization, Latter Day Saint Charities (LDSC) in the United States of America has agreed to provide a donation of Rs.43.70 million to provide training to the staff of the Hospital and to supply mobility aid comprising 564 wheelchairs, 370 walking aid and 410 prosthetic kits. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to sign an Agreement with the relevant institution to accept the said donation, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Acquisition of a land to establish a new police station in Nooriya in the Deraniyagala Police Division",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11503",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- A portion of land called Nooriya Watta at No.110, Dodawatta Grama Niladhari Division in the Deraniyagala Divisional Secretariat Division in Kegalle District, has been identified to establish the Nooriya Police Division. With the establishment of the said police station, it will be able to render an efficient service to the general public in the area while ensuring security by curbing crimes and corruption taking place in the area. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to acquire a land in extent of 02 acres from the Nooriya watta land belonging to the Janatha Estate Development Board under the Ministry of Agriculture, for the establishment of the said police station, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Employment of an Independent Consultant for the SPMC -Lotus Pharma Project of the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11504",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021 03 08 to establish the SPMC Lotus Pharma Project of the State Pharmaceuticals Manufacturing Corporation, in Millewa, Horana. The Cabinet has granted approval on 2021 10 25 to follow international competitive bidding procedure to select a Consultant/ Consultant Firm to implement that project. Accordingly, bids have been called on international competitive  basis and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee has recommended to award the relevant procurement to M/s Meridian Engineers & Consultancy Services, India who is the lowest evaluated substantially responsive bidder. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to appoint the said firm as the Consultant of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Post Office Security Fund Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11505",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Post Office Security Fund has been established under the Post Office Security Fund Ordinance No.1 of 1931. Although the approval of the Cabinet had been granted previously to amend the Post Office Security Fund Ordinance so as to provide a more productive service to the members of the Department of Posts, relevant drafting process has not yet been finalized. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to draft the said Bill through the Legal Draftsman, incorporating relevant provisions to suit the present day requirements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Amendment to the Civil Procedure Code (Chapter 101) (Repeal of Chapter XLII)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11506",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sub-Committee to draft the Matrimonial Causes Bill has been appointed as one of the Sub-Committees of the Special Unit of the Ministry of Justice formed with the approval of the Cabinet for bringing a widespread reform of the law. The said Sub-Committee has prepared a draft incorporating the preliminary provisions on the grounds for divorce, separation and nullity, the procedure for matrimonial actions and the matters that should be taken into account in granting the custody of children. Chapter XLII of the Civil Procedure Code contains the procedure in relation to the matrimonial actions and with the coming into operation of the proposed Matrimonial Causes Act, that Chapter will be redundant. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to instruct the Legal Draftsman to repeal the Chapter XLII of the Civil Procedure Code and draft a Bill for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Conducting of Inquiries into Complaints made with regard to Missing Persons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11507",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Office on Missing Persons was established, in terms of the provisions of the Act No.14 of 2016. The said office has established its regional offices in the areas of Matara, Mannar, Jaffna, Batticaloa and Kilinochchi and about 14,988 complaints on missings have been received to such offices. The Office on Missing Persons is charged with a range of functions and duties including the issuance of reports to the relatives of missing persons, after conducting formal inquiries, in terms of the provisions of the said Act. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to implement an accelerated programme having appointed 25 panels for the purpose of finalizing the inquiries related to those complaints, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Approval for submitting Orders published in the Gazette Notification to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11508",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Four Special Commodity Orders have been issued under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No. 48 of 2007 to implement the Government policy decisions with a view to providing relief to consumers through the stabilization of market price of essential commodities and protecting local farmers. Further, another Order has been issued by the Minister of Finance under the Revenue Protection Act, No. 19 of 1962 to give effect to the HS Code National Subdivisions and revision of Custom Import Duty on selected commodities.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to submit the said Orders to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Securing necessary equipment for the National Plant Quarantine Service under Japanese Non-Project Grant Aid",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11509",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- International movement of healthy plants and plant products is essential for the development of the agriculture and related trade industries. The National Plant Quarantine Service has been established to facilitate such trading activities. The Government of Japan is in agreement to grant equipment worth of JPY 500 million (Approximately Rs.880 Mn) for the activities of the National Plant Quarantine Services through the Non-Project Grant Aid under the Economic and Social Development Programme for the Financial Year 2022/2023. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance to sign the Exchange of Notes with Government of Japan to obtain the said grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Granting incentives for the Promotion of Remittances from Migrant Workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11510",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approximately US$ 7-8 billion is remitted annually to the country through the foreign employment sector which is a main source from where Sri Lanka is receiving  foreign exchange. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour to increase the incentive paid for remittances from its present rate of Rs 10  per dollar to Rs. 38 per dollar with a view to encouraging remittance of the foreign exchange earnings by the migrant workers during the forthcoming festival season, evaluating migrant workers and providing more economical benefits to them and their dependents, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-07-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2022-03-07",
    "description": "Implementation of an Incentive Scheme based on Progress of the Exports",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11511",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-07",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planed to implement a scheme to encourage exporters with a view to minimizing difficulties encountered by the them such as high inflation, severe  foreign exchange deficit, restrictions on imports of raw materials and high operating cost and encouraging exporters to make progress in this year beyond the export performance achieved in the last year. It is anticipated to earn an additional income of US$ 5,500 million in the year 2022 through the implementation of the proposed scheme than the export income in the year 2021.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade to pay an incentive of Rs 30/- per dollar earned in excess to the corresponding quarter of the previous year, to the institutions which have achieved at least 10% export growth compared to the previous corresponding quarter, under the proposed scheme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University (KDU) and the UFA State Aviation Technical University (USATU) of the Russian Federation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11512",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University (KDU) and the UFA State Aviation Technical University (USATU) of the Russian Federation with the objectives of further strengthening the good relationship between the two countries, enhancing the Academic and Research Cooperation in the field of Aviation and Aeronautical Engineering, exchange of scholars and scientists for conducting research in the areas of mutual interest as well as the exchange of information, academic materials and publications in the aforesaid areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to sign the said MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Providing a housing unit to Mr. Herath Mudiyanselage Dinesh Priyantha Herath, the gold medalist in the Javelin Throw event at the 2020 Paralympic Games",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11513",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mr. Herath Mudiyanselage Dinesh Priyantha Herath was competent enough to win a gold medal by making a world record in the Javelin Throw event at the 2020 Paralympic Games, held in Tokyo, Japan, bringing Sri Lanka a glory. As an appreciation to the commitment rendered by him in bringing that glory to the country, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to grant Mr. Dinesh Priyantha Herath a housing unit worth of Rs.14.2 million as a free grant from the Metro Homes Housing Project, Slave Island, implemented by the Urban Development Authority, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Providing a block of land from Narahenpita area to the Sri Lanka Air Force to construct a hospital",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11514",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- A land lot with an extent of 7 acres and 39.9 perches has been vested with the Urban Development Authority to carry out urban development projects. The Sri Lanka Air Force has requested the Urban Development Authority to provide them a land lot in extent of 03 acres of the said land to construct a hospital. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing, to vest a land lot of 03 acres from the said land with the Sri Lanka Air Force, as a free grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Granting the Tunnel Muck removed during the excavation of the tunnel connecting Kaluganga - Moragahakanda which is implemented under the North Central Province Maha Ela Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11515",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Tunnel Muck removed during the excavation of the tunnel connecting Kaluganga - Moragahakanda, a component of the North Central Province Maha Ela Project, which is being implemented under the Mahaweli Water Security Investment Programme with the Asian Development Bank funding, is temporarily accumulated in the reserved lands owned by the Department of Forest Conservation. This muck is comprised of gravel, which cannot be directly used for construction purposes. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to utilize that tunnel muck so as to produce Aggregate Base Course (ABC) required for the rehabilitation and 9.3 km long road from Illukkumbura to Laggala which has to be rehabilitated and developed due to the constructions of the aforesaid tunnel way and also for the construction of 100,000 km road project, implemented by the Government, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "The project to establish an Enhanced Transparency Framework for Agriculture, Forestry and other Land Use Sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11516",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka functions as a party of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC) since 1993, and has ratified the Paris Agreement  in 2016. The Ministry of Environment acts as the national focal point of the UNFCCC. In terms of the provisions of the said agreement, Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) of Sri Lanka have been submitted to the  UNFCCC on 2021\u201107\u201130 and under that Agriculture and Forestry have been identified as 02 key sectors.  According to the section 13 of the Paris Agreement, the partners shall report the progress of the climate change related activities in a transparent manner. Therefore, a project has been designed in collaboration with the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations under the consultation of the Ministry of Environment with a grant of the Global Environment Facility (GEF) in order to formulate the framework with enhanced transparency for the sectors of agriculture, forestry and other land use. The Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations has expressed its willingness to provide a grant of US$ 863,242 under the Global Environment Facility to implement the said project.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, to implement the said project and to sign an agreement with the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations in order to obtain the relevant grant for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Leasing out of two blocks of land located adjacent to the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport (MRIA), to establish 02 Airport Hotels and operate the same",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11517",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although Hambantota area where  the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport is located is a famous tourist destination, only few hotels are being operated in that area. It has been identified that construction of 02 hotels of 4 star category in the close proximity of the airport would attract tourists and it may create a more favorable environment.  For the purpose, two land lots each in extent of 15 hectares located on the right side of the Terminal Building of the Airport have been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism to Request for Proposals from the investors for the establishment of the proposed 02 hotels, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Making a lump sum payment for the revival of families of missing persons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11518",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Policies have been formulated to rebuild and restore the lives of persons who aggrieved from grievances under various circumstances, in terms of policies and guidelines on reparations. Accordingly, the relevant families should be provided with donations in keeping with the already prepared policies, enabling to promote the reconciliation for wellbeing and protection of all Sri Lankans including future generations. In terms of the Office on Missing Persons Act, No.14 of 2016, issuance of Certificate of Death or a Certificate of Absence is recommended to the Registrar General after conducting a proper investigation on missing persons. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice to make a lump sum payment of Rs.100,000/- to the next of kin of the missing person holding a Certificate of Absence issued by the Registrar General  based on the matters uncovered by the Office on Missing Persons, for the revival of the family, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Project for the construction of 408 Housing Units at Millagahawatta, Wattala",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11519",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited following the National Competitive Bidding to implement the Project for Designing  and Construction of  408 Housing Units at Millagahawatta, Wattala. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to award the relevant contract to International Construction Consortium (Pvt.) Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Augmentation of Nadukuda, Chunnakam and Aniyakanda Grid Substations under an Asian Development Bank Loan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11520",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited following the International Competitive Bidding to select a suitable contractor to implement this Project. The Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee has recommended to award the relevant contract to the Joint Venture of TBEA Shenyang Transformer Group and Ceylex Engineering Ltd. Concurrence of the Asian Development Bank has been received for the said recommendation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power to award the relevant contract, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Awarding the Term Contract for the Import of Diesel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11521",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited from the registered suppliers to award the term contract for  importing Diesel (0.05% M.S.) for a period of 08 months from 2022\u201103\u201101 to 2022\u201110\u201131. Awarding the relevant procurement to the Coral Energy DMCC has been recommended by the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to award the relevant procurement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-14-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-03-14",
    "description": "Procurement for Supply of 1,900,000 vials of Biphasic Isophane Insulin Injection BP, 30/70, 1000IU/10ml",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11522",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-14",
    "decision_details_body": "- International Competitive Bids have been invited for the purchase of this Injection which is used for the treatment of diabetic patients. The Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee has recommended the award of the bid to the lowest evaluated substantially responsive bidder, Wockhardt Limited, India. The said recommendation has been confirmed by the Procurement Appeal Board. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the contract for supplying only 1.5 million doses  of the relevant drug to Wockhardt Limited, India, and to purchase the rest in future depending on the actual consumption in the year 2022, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
