    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Research Projects of five (05) Sri Lankan Women Scientists have been selected for providing research grants considering those as suitable Research Projects for the Early Career Followship Programme implemented by the 'Organization for Women in Science for the Developing World' operating under the UNESCO. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to enter into Memoranda of Understanding between the Universities in which the relevant  Scientists serve and the UNESCO  for obtaining the relevant grants and enter into Grant Agreements between the said women scientists and the UNESCO, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-28-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-03-28",
    "description": "Providing relief to the house owners affected by the water leakage of the Uma Oya Multi-purpose Development Project and alternative lands for the acquired lands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11550",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- All construction activities of the Uma Oya Multi\u2011purpose Development Project are nearing completion and it has also been planned to finalize the provision of relief to the parties affected due to the project within the next six (06) months period. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Irrigation to award free grants under the State Lands Ordinance for the alternative blocks of land provided to the house owners who were affected by the water leakage occurred due to the excavation of the tunnel of this Multi\u2011purpose Development Project, pay compensation expeditiously for the houses which have been recommended for removal by the National Building and Research Organization (NBRO) owing to the landslide risk and are entitled to be paid with the full compensation and to provide the opportunity for cultivation under specific conditions, on the original residential lands of the house owners to be resettled, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-03-28-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-03-28",
    "description": "Email and Collaboration Platform for the Digital Government",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11551",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-03-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Creation of a Technology Based Society (Smart Nation) is one of the key objectives of the National Policy Framework of the Government. Under this, setting up of a Citizen Centric Digital Government and digitally empowered economy have been identified as strategies for achieving the vision of the Government. As such, it has been identified the necessity of creating a secured Communication Platform of which the capacity is scalable and suits with the present needs for the use of Government offices. Under this, it has been planned to implement a comprehensive E\u2011mail and Collaboration Solution Platform which is centrally governed and specially employed for the use of the Government. As such, the proposal made by H.E. the President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology to start 100,000 E\u2011mail and Collaborative Solution User Accounts for the Government Institutions under this arrangement and take necessary action to start 30,000 User Accounts expeditiously as its first phase, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
