  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Global Fund \u2013 Framework Agreement for the period 2022-2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11586",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The \u201cGlobal Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria\u201d has been established in the year 2002 in order to combat against 3 infectious diseases namely AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria. Since 2003, the said Global Fund has entered into 24 agreements for securing an amount of US $ 114 million to Sri Lanka. Of the said, the Ministry of Health has signed 15 Agreements where as other Agreements have been signed by the Sri Lanka Jathika Sarvodaya Sangamaya, the Tropical and environmental Diseases and Health Associates and the Sri Lanka Family Planning Association. The Ministry of Health has entered into Agreements to obtain grants amounting to US $ 88.3 million. Of such grant, around US $ 71 million has already been disbursed by 2021\u201110\u201131. The Global Fund has extended its willingness to make an another grant of US$ 9.4 million for the period from 2022-2024. Accordingly, the Minister of Health informed the Cabinet on the measures already taken with regard to the entering into the Agreements to secure that grant and the Cabinet granted its concurrence for the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Deployment of Dry - Bulk Carrier Ships of the Ceylon Shipping Corporation during South \u2013 West Monsoon Period in 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11587",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Expression of Interest (EOI) has been called for the deployment of the two vessels; Mv. Ceylon Breeze and Mv. Ceylon Princess belonging to the Ceylon Shipping Corporation in the service of the international charter market during the South-West Monsoon Period in 2022. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the contract for the deployment of the said two vessels in service during the prescribed period under the Commercial Management System, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee to M/s Wallem Shipping Pte Ltd., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Making Payments to the Suppliers who have submitted bids for the supply of Laboratory Equipments, consumables and reagents",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11588",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into account the sudden increase in the exchange rates due to the prevailing economic situation in the country, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2022\u201104\u201125 to make payments as per the exchange rates prevailing to the date of clearance of pharmaceuticals and surgical instruments for which Letters of Credit have already been opened. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved proposal made by the Minister of Health to make payments also for the suppliers who have opened Letters of credit for the import of laboratory equipment, consumables and reagents, following the said system and to make payments for the other relevant suppliers including the procurement of which quotations have been invited and for which bids have been opened by the State Pharmaceutical Corporation, based on the foreign exchange rate prevailing to the date on which relevant payments are made to the Letters of credit."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Amendments to the Termination of Employment of workmen (Special Provisions) Act, No.45 of 1971 and The Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11589",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201103\u201108 to amend the Termination of Employment of workmen (Special Provisions) Act, No.45 of 1971 and The Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950 so that relevant provisions could be imposed to the effect that a security could be furnished in case where appeals, revisions and writ applications can be filled against the awards and decrees granted under those Acts. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the bills drafted by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to publish the said bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter submit the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Submission of Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No. 1 of 1969 in Parliament for Approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11590",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Central Bank of Sri lanka has proposed to introduce limitations on selected certain payment terms with a view to curbing the expansion of grey foreign exchange market operations and avoiding under -invoicing of importation at the point of Customs clearance. Accordingly, the Gazette Notification dated 2022\u201105\u201106 has been issued imposing 'Import Control Regulations on Payment Terms No. 07 of 2022' under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act No. 1 of 1969 enabling to limit the Open Account Payment terms, Consignment Account Payment terms, Documents against payment term and Documents against Acceptance payment term. Such regulation promulgated under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act shall be submitted for approval of Parliament with the approval of the Cabinet of Ministers within one month from the date of its publication. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to submit the Import Control Regulations on Payment Terms No. 07 of 2022, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Submission of a Supplementary Estimate to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11591",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- \tAt the beginning of the year 2022, the Government introduced a relief package for Samurdhi beneficiaries, Estate community, Pensioners and Public Servants to minimize as far as possible, the hardships faced by the people due to the adverse economic condition in the country. It has been decided to submit a Supplementary Estimate to Parliament to secure funds required to incur the expenditure for the same and to continue the essential public services without hindrance. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to submit a Supplementary Estimate to Parliament to secure an allocation of Rs 695 billion under the \u201c Supplementary Support Services and Contingent Liabilities Project of the Department of National Budget, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Revenue Mobilization for Economic Stabilization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11592",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The decision made by the Government to reduce tax rates of Value Added Tax, Personnel Income Tax and Corporate Income Tax by introducing a low tax regime in late 2019 and to narrow tax bases of Value Added Tax and Personnel Income Tax has resulted in a significant loss in the Government revenue. Further, the said decision has led to an increase in the budget deficit and public debt as a percentage of the Gross Domestic Product. Under the circumstance, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to amend the following Acts with a view to increasing the Government revenue, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n    \u2022 Inland Revenue Act, No. 24 of 2017\n    \u2022 Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2022\n    \u2022 Telecommunication Levy Act, No. 21 of 2011\n    \u2022 Betting and Gaming Levy Act, No. 40 of 1988\n    \u2022 Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No. 3 of 2003"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-05-30-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-05-30",
    "description": "Calculation of Gross Domestic Product (GDP)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11593",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-05-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into consideration the matters such as ascertaining the real structure of the economy accurately, calculating the economic growth of the country more accurately and adhering to the new recommendations and methodologies imposed by the international agencies who are responsible for national Accounts Statistics, the Department of Census and Statistics update the base year of making National Accounts Estimates once in every five years. Accordingly, it has been decided to apply the year 2015 as the base year in lieu of 2010 which is currently being used in preparation of National Accounts. The Department of Census and Statistics has prepared Quarterly and Annual National Accounts Estimates from the year 2015 to 2021 utilizing the year 2015 as the base year. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to publish the said Reports and to issue National Accounts Estimates from the first quarter 2022 onwards under the new base year of 2015."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Amending the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation Act, No.06 of 1982",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11600",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021 01 04 to amend the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation Act, No.06 of 1982, incorporating the provisions enabling to appoint a representative of the General Treasury and the Secretary, in charge of the subject or his representative to the Board of Directors of the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media to publish the said bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Amending to the Rubber Control Act, No.11 of 1956 and the Rubber \tReplanting Subsidy Act, No.36 of 1953",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11601",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Public Administration Circular No.423, instructions have been given to the effect that necessary laws be amended to liquidate the dormant statutory funds. Accordingly, measures have been taken to liquidate the Rubber Control Fund established under the Rubber Control Act, No.11of 1956 and the Rubber Replanting Fund established under the Rubber Replanting Subsidy Act, No.36 of 1953. Since the provisions relating to the Rubber Control Fund and the Rubber Replanting Fund incorporated in the said two Acts are no longer required, it is necessary to amend those Acts. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation Industries to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to amend the Rubber Control Act, No.11of 1956 and the Rubber Replanting Subsidy Act, No.36 of 1953, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Amending the section 46 of the Industrial Disputes Act, No, 43 of 1950",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11602",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- Labour tribunals since the inception have granted opportunities to representatives of trade unions and representatives who are not attorneys at law to appear in labour tribunals, on an equal basis as lawyers, representing their parties. However, during the recent times, several issues have been emerged in the instances where representatives who are not attorneys-at-law appear in labour tribunals. In order to prevent the occurrence of such incidents, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2017 02 21 to amend the Industrial Disputes Act, No.43 of 1950, so that a representative conferred by relevant parties could appear before the Commissioner of Labour or any authorized officer, arbitrator, industrial court or labour tribunal. Clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Procurement of Chemical and Organic Fertilizer required for the Paddy Cultivation of Maha Season 2022/23",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11603",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is expected to cultivate 800,000 hectares of paddy in the Maha Season 2022/23 and action needs to be taken to provide fertilizer for that purpose. It has been estimated that 150,000 MT of Urea, 45,000 MT of Muriate of Potash and 36,000 MT of Triple Super Phosphate are required for the paddy cultivation in Maha Season 2022/23. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to import the required stock of fertilizer through Ceylon Fertilizer Company Limited and Colombo Commercial Fertilizers Limited and distribute to the same to farmers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding for the implementation of the Volunteer Cooperation Programme 2020 - 2027 with the World University Service of Canada",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11604",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The World University Service of Canada implements a Volunteer Cooperation Programme to create opportunities for education, employment and empowerment for underprivileged youth and women worldwide. The said Programme has been implemented in Sri lanka for about 30 years and under an MoU signed between two parties, Programme has been implemented under the same during the period from the year 2015 to 2020 as well. The said Programme has not been implemented in Sri Lanka within last two years due to the travel restrictions imposed pertaining to the COVID-19 pandemic and it has been proposed to sign an MoU to re-implement the said Programme. Accordingly, the proposal made by  Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to sign a Memorandum of Understanding to implement the relevant Programme through a Grant of CAD 2.76 million under 10 Government and Non-Government Organizations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Obtaining US$ 55 Million Credit Line from Indian EXIM Bank for the Procurement of Urea fertilizer",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11605",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India is in agreement to provide US$ 55 Million Credit Line through Indian EXIM Bank for the procurement of Urea fertilizer required for Maha Season 2022/23. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to sign the relevant Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-06-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-06-06",
    "description": "Amendment to the Appropriation Act for the Year 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11606",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has decided to submit an amended Appropriation Bill to Parliament in lieu of the Appropriation Act No. 30 of 2021 due to the fact that expenses had to be borne for the other essential activities apart from the functions for which allocations had been made under Appropriation Act from the middle of the first quarter of 2022 in view of prevailing worst economic situation and that the structure of Ministries that existed at the time of passing the Appropriation Bill for the year 2022 has changed significantly at present. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a draft to amend the Appropriation Bill No. 30 of 2021, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Admission of School children into Grade One of Schools - 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11607",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Considering the matters submitted by the principals, the Circular Revision Committee, the Investigation Unit of the Ministry, the Commission to Investigate Bribery or Corruption and the Election Commission relating to the issues which have arisen during the implementation of the Circular issued previously for admission of school children into Grade One of schools and the Court Orders granted in that regard, the Ministry of Education has prepared a new revised circular. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to make applicable the provisions in the said revised circular for admission of school children into Grade One of schools, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Submission of Orders published in the Gazette, for approval in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11608",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit two (02) Gazette Notifications containing Orders issued under the Sri Lanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979, six (06) Gazette Notifications issued under the Special Commodity Levy Act, No.48 of 2007 imposing Orders and a Gazette Notification issued under Revenue Protection Act, No.19 of 1962 imposing Revenue Protection Order No.02/2022, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Issuance of a new Order under Section 22 of Foreign Exchange Act, No.22 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11609",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201112\u201106 for issuance of an Order under Section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017 to impose restrictions for a period of 06 months relating to certain capital transactions which outflow foreign exchange. The validity period of the Order imposed by the Gazette Notification issued accordingly is to be expired on 2022\u201107\u201101. The Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka has recommended that issuance of a new Order would be appropriate to further continue the restrictions imposed by such Order. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to issue a new Order under Section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017 and thereafter submit the said Order for approval in Parliament, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Social Security Contribution Levy Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11610",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal for the introduction of a Social Security Fund through Budget Proposals - 2022 was passed by Parliament. Accordingly, it has been decided to introduce the Social Security Contribution Levy as a new Levy under a rate of 2.5% for Importers, Manufacturers, Service providers, Wholesalers and Retailers whose turnover exceeds Rs. 120 million per year. The draft prepared by the Legal Draftsman for the purpose has been received the clearance of the Attorney General. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same, thereafter in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Conservation and Promotion of Angam Martial Art",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11611",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ministry of Sports and Youth Affairs has taken action to promote Angam Martial Arts which is significant as a traditional sport in the country, a Martial Art as well as a cultural heritage. Even though, approval of the Cabinet has been granted in the year 2019 to lift the ban imposed on the Angampora Martial Art, the relevant Gazette Notification has not yet been published. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Sports and Youth Affairs to publish the removal of ban imposed by the English Colonial rulers, through a Gazette Notification in view of conserving and protecting Angampora Martial Art, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Granting No Pay Leaves to employ or to engage in any other Productive Economic Activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11612",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- In accordance with the existing provisions, a public officer is entitled to no pay leave for a maximum period of 05 years during their service period for academic and foreign employment. Nevertheless, Public servants are less interested in obtaining such leaves due to the non consideration of that period in the calculation of pension, impact caused to the seniority and other conditions. Taking into account the current economic situation in the country, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government to issue the relevant Circular instructions revising the existing provisions, enabling the public officials to obtain no pay foreign leaves for a period of five (05) years without any prejudice to their seniority and pension to employ in abroad or to engage in any other productive activity, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-13-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-06-13",
    "description": "Encouraging public officials to engage in Agricultural and Farming Activities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11613",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Public transportation has been disrupted due to the prevailing fuel shortage which has made it difficult for public officials to access their transport facilities. In this context, it seems appropriate to grant leave for public officials for one working day of the week and provide them with the necessary facilities to engage in agricultural activities in their home garden or elsewhere as a solution to food shortage which could arise in the near future. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government to close Public institutions on Fridays for the period of next three months other than those providing essential services such as Water, Electricity, Health, Defence Services, Education, Transport, Ports and Airport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Implementation of the \u201cNational Single Window Project\u201d to facilitate international trade",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11614",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Trade Facilitation Agreement of the World Trade Organization is in operation since February, 2017 and Sri Lanka is also a party to the Agreement. According  to the said Trade Agreement, Sri lanka is obliged to initiate and maintain a single place (Single Window) to submit documents and data requirements by traders on their border trade flows (importation, exportation and transshipment) to the participatory border trade regulating authorities. A formal plan relating to the project has been developed in the year 2018 under the financial assistance of the World Bank. The estimated cost of this project to be implemented under three stages as per the said plan is approximately US$ 15 million and it is expected to secure the funds required for the purpose from the World bank and other development stakeholders. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to implement the proposed \u201cNational Single Window Project\u201d, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Submission of the Annual Report (Final Budget Position Report) of the  Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies for the year 2021 to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11615",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Annual Report (Final Budget Position Report) of the  Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies should be issued prior to the expiry of 05 months at the end of relevant Financial year in terms of the provisions of the Fiscal Management (Responsibility) Act, No. 03 of 2003. Accordingly, the said Annual Report for the year 2021 has been published in the official website of the Ministry. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization & National Policies to table the said Report in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Establishment of the Export Oriented Sea Cucumber Production Villages in the Shallow Seas of the Northern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11616",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- A significant amount of foreign exchange has been able to earn through the export of sea cucumber harvested from natural marine environment. Based on the experienced gained through that, the National Aquaculture Development Authority of Sri Lanka has initiated a commercial sea cucumber farming project with a view to building sea cucumber breeding centres, expanding sea cucumber farming areas, establishing export oriented sea cucumber production villagers as a commercial farming thereby increasing foreign exchange earnings and enhancing the livelihood of the fishing community. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries to establish sea cucumber production and export villagers consisting of 100 acres by identifying 5000 acres from Jaffna, Mannar, Kilinochchi and Batticaloa Districts and establish sea cucumber production farms with 1 acre each thereby further expanding the relevant project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Providing Railway reservations on temporary basis for cultivation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11617",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The total railway reservations belonging to the Sri Lanka Railway is approximately 14,000 acres in extent, out of which about 10% lands has been provided for various purposes on lease basis. It has been identified as suitable to provide the  lands which are not urgently required for the development activities of the  Department of Railways and those suitable for cultivation which are allotted as railway reserves in the vicinity of railway tracks and stations, from the rest of reserves for the use of cultivation on temporary lease basis. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport & Highways to take necessary action to provide those lands, on lease basis for a period of one year, giving priority to the farmers already engaged in the cultivation of the relevant areas and residents near by  railway tracks and low income families, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Vesting a block of land in extent of 10 acre located at Muthurajawela to the Ceylon Electricity Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11618",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Director Board of the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation has granted approval to provide a block of land in extent of 10 acre located adjacent to the Yugadanavi Power Plant at Muthurajawela to the Ceylon Electricity Board for the construction of a 300MW LNG Power Plant and approval of the Director Board of the Ceylon Electricity Board  has also been received to purchase the said land block. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to transfer the said block of land to the Ceylon Electricity Board by levying the market value of the said land block estimated by the Chief Government Valuer, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Approval of the National Environment Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11619",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- \u201cThe National Environmental Policy and Strategy\u201d which was declared in the year 2003 by the then Ministry of Environment and Natural Resources, has been the existing key policy document that guided to take decisions on the environmental issues in Sri Lanka. During the previous years, several considerable changes which affected nationally and globally to the environment have emerged. Further, the economic, social and cultural factors which contribute to the climatic change and the scientific knowledge on environment have considerably changed. Taking those circumstances into consideration, the Ministry of Environment has taken measures to update the \u201cThe National Environmental Policy and Strategy\u201d which was declared in the year 2003, so as to suit to the present day requirements, having obtained the consultations of the experts and stakeholders in the field of environment as well as the views of general public. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to implement the National Environment Policy formulated accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Revise the minimum age policy for Sri Lankan women for domestic and \tdomestic related work abroad",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11620",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The current minimum age limit for Sri Lankan women to engage in domestic and domestic related work abroad is 25 years for Saudi Arabia, 23 years for other Middle Eastern countries and 21 years for other countries.  The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201106\u201106 decided to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee headed by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to study on the revision of age limits, in view of a proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment, and submit the recommendations to the Cabinet. Accordingly, considering the recommendations made by the said Sub-Committee, Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to revise the minimum age limit for Sri Lankan women to engage in domestic and domestic related work abroad is 21 years."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Procurement for obtaining security services to the National Savings Bank",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11621",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been called to obtain security services for the head office of the National Savings Bank and its branches  located island wide, following the National Competitive Bidding procedure. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to award the relevant contracts to the security services providing agencies qualified under each category, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Installation of a Modern Surveillance System for the Securities and \tExchange Commission of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11622",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The  existing Surveillance System used by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka was installed in the year 2008 and, the need has been found to modernize the said system so as to suit to the present day requirements. It is possible to secure funds required for the purpose under the World Bank funded Financial Sector Modernization Project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to call for a proposal as a direct procurement from the Millennium IT  Software (Pvt) Ltd., a member of the London Stock Exchange Group Technology, which installed the existing  Surveillance System and take necessary action to modernize the said system, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "Implementation of a Mixed Development Project within the Anuradhapura \tPost Office Premises",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11623",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Urban Settlement Development Authority has planned to implement a mixed development project in the land in extent of 99 perches where the Anuradhapura post office is located. The Postal Department has extended its willingness to release the said land, subject to obtaining a new office premises for the said Department to suit to the present value of the land.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to acquire the said land to the Urban Settlement Development Authority as a free grant, in terms of the section 6(1) of the State Land Ordinance  and  implement the said project as a Public-Private Partnership project having selected a suitable investor by calling for Expression of Interest under national or international competitive bidding procedure, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-20-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-06-20",
    "description": "22nd Amendment to the Constitution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11624",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-20",
    "decision_details_body": "- Requests have been made to reintroduce the constructive factors of the 19th Amendment to the Constitution in view of the sensational situation arisen in the country due to the powers vested with the Executive Presidential system by the 20th Amendment to the Constitution. Under this backdrop, taking into consideration the existing crisis situation the country is faced with, it has been identified that  the Constitution has to be amended by vesting a certain power in the Cabinet of Ministers which is collectively responsible to Parliament and the Public and the Constitutional Council thereby creating a certain balance of power on the Executive President and the Parliament. Accordingly, the preliminary draft submitted by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "\u201cA Democratic, Prosperous, and Resilient Sri Lanka Programme\u201d",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11625",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Two Agreements have been signed between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of the United States of America in 2011, to secure funds for  the programmes of \u201cstrengthened partnership for Democratic Governance and Social Cohesion\u201d and \u201cSustained and Inclusive Economic Growth\u201d and the said two programmes have been implemented accordingly. A proposal has been made to enter into a new agreement for securing a grant of US$ 57 million awarded by the United State Agency for International Development (USAID), in order to implement a new programme with the name of \u201cDemocratic, Prosperous, and Resilient Sri Lanka\u201d to be effective until 2026, mainly focusing attention on the areas of effective democratic governance, inclusive, market driven growth and resilience of resources to shocks and stresses. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to conduct negotiations for securing the said grant, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Resumption of International Operations of Jaffna International Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11626",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though, the international operations of the Jaffna International Airport were commenced on 2019\u201111\u201111 after certifying the initial international regulatory requirements, its operations have been temporarily suspended from 2020\u201103\u201115 due to Covid-19 pandemic situation. Internationally and locally established airlines have requested at present to operate charter flights and scheduled flights to South Indian destinations from the Jaffna International Airport. Accordingly, Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence for the measures taken by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to resume the international operations of the Jaffna International Airport from 2022\u201107\u201101."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Revision of Railway Transport Fares",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11627",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Sri Lanka Railways adopts a concessionary fare scheme for passenger transport in line with the Government policies. However, with the rapid hike of fuel prices, the recurrent loss of the Department of Railways is escalating and therefore it has been essential to raise the income generated by the Department so that a satisfactory railway service could be maintained. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to revise the railway passenger transport fare which has not been revised for more than five (05) years and the railway charges for providing wagons for freight transport, mail transport and other goods which have not been increased for nearly 14 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "'Ekwa Wawamu-Rata Dinawamu' - The Crop Production National Drive - 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11628",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- As an expedite solution to the crisis emerged in the country on food security, it has been planned to implement an accelerated food production drive island wide under the auspices of the Ministry of Agriculture in collaboration with the other ministries including the Ministry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government and the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs. The entire programme is to be carried out under the coordination of the Ministry of Agriculture under the technical contribution of the Department of Agriculture and the Provincial Departments of Agriculture. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the joint proposal made by the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government; the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to implement the said programme called 'Ekwa Wawamu-Rata Dinawamu'- The Crop Production National Drive utilizing the lands approximately in extent of 250,000 hectares belonging to Buddhist temples and places of worship, Christian churches, Mosques and Hindu Kovils."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Eliminate the need for a Family Background Report for female migrant \tworkers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11629",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several international reports published on the protection of womens' rights have pointed out that making mandatory the submission of a 'Family Background Report' in view of ensuring that the children of female migrant workers who go abroad for domestic work are not less than 05 years of age, has adversely impacted on womens' rights. Also, it has been reported that women who are anticipating to go abroad are inconvenienced by certain officers, by delaying the reports on several grounds, in spite that women have duly qualified to be issued that report. It has further been reported that some women who are not qualified to submit the said report have gone abroad through other illegal ways without any supervision and faced various problems. Taking into consideration the matters submitted to the Cabinet by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment in this regard, the Cabinet decided to exempt women who have children of two (02) years of age or above from the compulsory requirement to submit a Family Background Report when going abroad for employment."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Amending the Children and Young Persons Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11630",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- A person under the age of 18 has been defined as a child by the Convention on the Rights of the Child. Accordingly, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2020\u201109\u201116 to amend the Children and Young Persons Ordinance, incorporating relevant provisions while adhering to the said convention. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman as per the said decision. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Introduction of new laws on Child Protection and Justice",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11631",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2015\u201102\u201118 to draft the Children (Judicial Protection) Bill so that Courts can be established to exercise jurisdiction and other forms of jurisdiction over children to hear cases relating to children in need of care and protection or to prosecute a child who violates the law. Accordingly, the preliminary draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman has been studied by two committees of experts and further proposals have been submitted. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare the final draft Bill incorporating the proposals of the said committees also in the preliminary draft Bill that has already been prepared, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Amendment to the Prevention of Frauds Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11632",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Taking into account the necessity of making certain consequential amendments to the Prevention of Frauds Ordinance in line with the amendments recommended to be made to the Notaries Ordinance and the Wills Ordinance, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201110\u201118 decided to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a draft for that purpose. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney general has been received for the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Amendment to the Powers of Attorney Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11633",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201107\u201119 has granted approval to introduce amendments to the Powers of Attorney Ordinance with a view to minimizing the fraudulent activities carried out using the forged and illegal powers of attorney. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Introduction of a New Law on Contempt of Court",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11634",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the absence of a definition on the offense of contempt of court in Sri Lanka, there is no clear and uniform procedure for hearing and determining such cases at present. Therefore, it has been found difficult to understand limits of interference for the administration of justice and the limits under freedom of expression. Further, in considering the cases on contempt of court which have been severely criticized in the recent past, it has appeared that it is appropriate to reassess the relevant law. Accordingly, the Law Commission of Sri Lanka having studied the matters, has prepared a preliminary draft with a view to introducing appropriate laws. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a draft Bill to enact a new Law based on the preliminary draft, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Amendments to the Notaries Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11635",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201107\u201119 has granted approval to amend the  Notaries Ordinance for introducing new provisions with a view to preventing unlawful activities pertaining to the land frauds. Accordingly, the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman based on the preliminary draft prepared by the Notarial Advisory Committee while obtaining the views of the Registrar General has been received the clearance of the Attorney General. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same, thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Amendment to the Registration of Documents Ordinance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11636",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201107\u201119 has granted approval to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislations to amend the Registration of Documents Ordinance for introducing new provisions to prevent irregularities and frauds in respect of lands. Accordingly, the draft prepared by the Legal Draftsman has been received the clearance of the Attorney General. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same, thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Twenty Second Amendment to the Constitution",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11637",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The policy approval has been received at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201106\u201120 for the preliminary draft on the Twenty Second Amendment to the Constitution. Accordingly, the Legal Draftsman has prepared the draft Bill on Twenty Second Amendment to the Constitution and the Attorney General has assured that the said draft Bill is not inconsistent with the Constitution. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the draft Bill on the Twenty Second Amendment to the Constitution in the Government Gazette and submit the same, thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Obtaining fuel from the companies established in the petroleum producing countries based on long-term Agreements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11638",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Ceylon Petroleum Corporation contributes about 90% of the total fuel supply of the country and the Indian Oil Company supplies the rest of 10%. Due to the prevailing foreign exchange crisis in the country, ensuring an uninterrupted fuel supply in the country has become a major challenge. In this context, it has been observed that it would be appropriate to provide opportunities to the fuel companies established in the fuel producing countries to import and sell fuel with long term agreements with such companies, using the funds of those companies without any pressure to the foreign exchange issue in the country. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to provide the opportunity to the fuel companies selected using the formal procedure to import, distribute and sell fuel to Sri lanka with long-term Agreements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-06-27-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2022-06-27",
    "description": "Identification of new suppliers to ensure the continues supply of Jet A-1 Aviation fuel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11639",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-06-27",
    "decision_details_body": "- Daily requirement of aviation fuel for aircraft in and outside Sri Lanka is approximately 1.2 million litres and under the current situation in the country, the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation has been unable to provide at least the minimum quantity of fuel required to sustain the operations of domestic and foreign airlines as well. Under this circumstance, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation and the Minister of Power and Energy to grant permission for the Bunkers registered under the Sri Lanka Ports Authority to import, supply and sell Jet A-1 aviation fuel in order to continue the airline services without any hindrance, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Re-constitution of the Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living and the Appointment of the Food Security Committee",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11640",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by H.E the President to re-establish the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee on Cost of Living to make recommendations to the Cabinet on policy and practical solutions required for maintaining the stability of the cost of living, was approved by the Cabinet. Accordingly, the composition of the  Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living is as follows.\n\n*\tH.E the President - (Chairman)\n\n* \tHon. Prime Minister\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Fisheries\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Transport and Highways\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Agriculture\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Plantation Industries\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Power and Energy\n\n*\tHon. Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security\n\nFurther, the Cabinet also granted approval to appoint a Food Security Committee chaired by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security and with the participation of the relevant Ministry Secretaries to assist the activities of the above Cabinet Sub-Committee on Cost of Living."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Alternative options to avoid the shortage of Ammonium Nitrate explosives used for various Industries in the country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11641",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The monopoly for import/storage and distribution of Ammonium Nitrate explosives used for Cement/Water gel/Emulsion manufacturing industries and granite blasting industries has been vested with Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Ltd. There is a shortage of Ammonium Nitrate explosives in the country due to the current foreign exchange deficit in the country and inability of suppliers who supplied the said explosives to  Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Ltd for a long period to supply the same. This has severely affected to the activities of industries using the said explosives. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to take necessary action expeditiously to import Ammonium Nitrate explosives to the country with the intervention of the Ministry of Defence for short period as a solution to the above issue, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Signing a Letter of Intent for Developing Defence Cooperation between the Ministry of Defence of the Republic of Indonesia and the Ministry of Defence of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11642",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- An inter-institutional cooperation has been proposed to be established to develop the Defence cooperation between the Ministry of Defence of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Defence of the Republic of Indonesia. The Government of Indonesia has proposed to sign a Letter of Intent to initiate negotiations between two countries for the said purpose and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the draft Letter of Intent. Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to sign the said Letter of Intent, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Treaty on Extradition between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11643",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Treaty on Extradition has been signed in the year 2014 between the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the United Arab Emirates with the intention of strengthening judicial corporation in the field of extradition.  Accordingly, the proposal made by H.E the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to rectify the said Treaty on Extradition by re-amending the Provisions of section 5(1) of the said Treaty to suit with the legal system of both countries and to submit the same thereafter to Parliament as per the provisions of the Extradition Law No.8 of 1978, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Prgramme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11644",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Japan has introduced the Japanese Grant Aid for Human Resources Development Scholarship Prgramme in the year 2010 to provide opportunities to the executive grade officers in the Public Sector to follow Postgraduate degree courses in the recognized Universities in Japan. 195 opportunities to follow Postgraduate degree courses and 10 opportunities to follow PhDs have been granted under the said programme so far. It has been agreed to provide a grant of Japan Yen 282 million (Approximately Rs. 761 million) for the year 2022 under this programme. As such, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to sign the Exchange of Notes for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Establishment of Constituency Office under the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to facilitate the Board Director of Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11645",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Board of Directors of Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank consists of non\u2011resident Directors and they represent 12 Constituencies comprising one or more member countries. Sri Lanka as a founding member of the said Bank represents its 11th Constituency. Indonesia is the major shareholder of that constituency. Sri Lanka, Cambodia, Myanmar, Laos and Timor-Leste are the other  member countries. According to the Memorandum of Understanding signed among those Constituency members in the year 2016, the Director and the Alternate Director positions relating to that Constituency are exchanged according to a rotation scheme. Accordingly, Sri Lanka has got the opportunity to lead that constituency and hold the Director position during the period of 2022 - 2024 and a Deputy Secretary to the Treasury has been nominated for the same. It is more important for Sri Lanka to get that position in this instance and it is required to provide necessary facilities for the Board level tasks since that Board of Directors functions as a non-resident Board. Accordingly, the proposal made by Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to establish a Constituency Office of the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank under the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Establishment of a Flight Training Institute at the Batticaloa Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11646",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the Sri Lanka Air Force and the Road Development Authority have developed the Batticaloa Airport as a domestic flight destination in the year 2018, the said Airport does not generate any income since it has been exempted from the landing and parking charges. Taking into consideration this situation, it has been found that it would be appropriate to use the space of the said Airport for any other productive purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to invite Requests for Proposals to establish a Flight Training Institute at that Airport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "International day to commemorate air crash victims and their families - Civil Aviation Authority of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11647",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Council of the International Civil Aviation Organization at its 5th meeting of the 224th Session has decided to declare 20th February of each year as the International day to commemorate air crash victims and their families. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to declare 20th February of each year in Sri Lanka also as the Day to commemorate air crash victims and their families, adhering to the above decision, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Agricultural Crop Cultivation Programmes launched by the Department \tof Prisons and the Bureau of the Commissioner General of \tRehabilitation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11648",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Department of Prisons has planned to implement a crop cultivation programme named \u201cSarusara - From Prisons to Farm\u201d, with a view to deriving the labour contribution of the prison inmates for the agricultural development of the country, considering them as a part of nation's human resource, instead of retaining them in prison cells. It is envisaged from this programme to cultivate high yield crops in the open prison camps and working prison camps under the guidance of the Department of Agriculture and utilize the harvest so yielded for the consumption needs of the inmates.\n\nIn addition to that, Agricultural Development Programmes have been initiated under 03 rehabilitation centres which is maintained by the Bureau of Commissioner General of Rehabilitation to rehabilitate drug addicts and in order to expand further the said agricultural activities, it has been planned to obtain 1000 Acres of uncultivated lands situated at Kandakadu and Nawasenapura areas in the Eastern Province, which belong to the Mahaweli  Authority of Sri Lanka and the National Livestock Development Board and cultivate maize in an area of 500 acres and cultivate grains, vegetables and fruits endemic to the area in the remaining portion of land utilizing the labour of those who are being rehabilitated. Cabinet took into notice the information submitted by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional reforms on the said programmes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Streamlining the Casino Industry in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11649",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Casino Business (Regulation) Act, No.17 of 2010 and the the Betting and Gaming Levy Act, No.40 of 1988 have laid down the provisions to regulate  the Casino Industry in Sri Lanka. Even though, licenses should be issued for the operation of Casino industries in Sri Lanka under the Casino Business (Regulation) Act, No.17 of 2010, no licenses have been issued for any casino businesses under the said Act up to now, since regulations to enforce the provisions of the said Act have not been issued so far. Under this circumstance, it has been difficult to collect relevant taxes properly from the institutions currently engaged in casino business. Therefore, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to take necessary action to issue regulations under the Casino Business (Regulation) Act, No.17 of 2010 and introduce appropriate amendments to the Betting and Gaming Levy Act, No.40 of 1988, with a view to regulating the establishments engaged in the Casino business and collecting the due taxes to be received to the Government."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Amending the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No.2 of 1996",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11650",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been recognized that the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act presently in force should be amended, enabling to give effect to Agreements to which Sri Lanka is bounded regionally and internationally and introducing provisions for the sustainable management and conservation of fisheries resources. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to amend the Fisheries and Aquatic Resources Act, No.2 of 1996, so as to suit to the present day requirements, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2022-07-04-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2022-07-04",
    "description": "Amendment to the Civil Procedure Code (Chapter 101) (Revoking Chapter LXVI)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11651",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2022-07-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2021\u201109\u201127 to revoke Chapter LXVI of the Civil Procedure Code containing procedural provisions on Small Claims Courts, taking into account the drafting of a separate law introducing a special procedure for Small Claims Courts and the amendments added to the Judicature Act, No.2 of 1978 for the establishment of Small Claims Courts. Accordingly, clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
