    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11839",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the following Regulations issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969, for approval of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet:\n\n\t* Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations No.23 of 2022  published in\tthe  \tGazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2309/40 dated 2022\u201112\u201109.\n\n\t* Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations No.24 of 2022, published in the \t    Gazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2311/08 dated 2022\u201112\u201119.\n\n\t* Imports Control Regulations on Payment Terms No.25 of 2022, published in \t   the  Gazette Extraordinary Notification No. 2311/18 dated 2022\u201112\u201121."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-02-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-01-02",
    "description": "Importation of Eggs as a remedy to the existing egg shortage in the local \tmarket",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11840",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet decided to import eggs with the intervention of the Government, if necessary, as a solution to the inconvenience faced by the customers due to the current shortage of eggs in the local market and the tendency of hiking the prices of eggs."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "National Energy Potentials, Strategies and the Roadmap for the next \tdecade",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11841",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee has been appointed under the chairmanship of the Hon. Prime Minister at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201130 to identify the policies and strategies to be adopted to develop the Energy sector in a sustainable manner and submit appropriate recommendations to the Cabinet and provide necessary guidance for the expeditious implementation of the decisions to be taken by the Cabinet based on the said recommendations and follow up the same. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister to implement the Roadmap inclusive of recommendations and  the milestones relating to the Energy sector stated in the Report submitted by the said Sub\u2011Committee having conducted several discussions with the stakeholder institutions, professionals and academia in the field, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "75th Independence Day Commemoration Ceremony",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11842",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 75th Independence Day commemoration ceremony which falls on February 04, 2023 and the programme organized to be held concurrently, including the tasks and responsibilities to be performed by the respective institutions was submitted to the Cabinet by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government. Cabinet decided to grant its concurrence to implement the said programme."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Proposal for the revision of Electricity Tariff 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11843",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet considered the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies; and the Minister of Power and Energy on the revision of electricity tariff. Cabinet further considered that the General Treasury is no longer possible to provide required funds to the Ceylon Electricity Board within the existing fiscal space and as such there is no alternative other than the revision of the existing electricity tariff in order to cover only the cost incurred for the supply of electricity while minimizing the impact caused to the electricity consumers as much as possible in order to ensure an uninterrupted supply of power in the country. After discussion, it was decided to grant approval:\n\n* \tThe Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka to further study on the proposed electricity tariff revision submitted by the Sri Lanka Electricity Board in consultation with the relevant parties, and if any revisions are to be made, submit the same on or before 2023\u201102\u201115.\n\n* \tUntil then, the Ceylon Electricity Board and the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka to take necessary action jointly to implement the Electricity Tariff \tamendment proposed by the Ceylon Electricity Board to be effective from \t01\u201101\u20112023 as an interim measure in accordance with the amendments of the Policy Guidelines currently in force regarding the electricity industry.\n\n* \tIf any amendments will be presented by the Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka, the Ceylon Electricity Board to take necessary action to implement those amendments and make the necessary adjustments by the next monthly electricity bills."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Invitation for the Expression of Interest to commence business activities  by \tusing the facilities of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11844",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the layout of the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport, there is a potential for converting the said Airport into a multi-purpose business center by implementing business opportunities related to aviation and as well as non-aviation related activities. Therefore, attention has been focused on taking measures to effectively utilize the facilities and assets in the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport by creating public-private partnership investment opportunities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to invite Expressions of Interest from investors and strategic entrepreneurs in direct and indirect aviation related ventures to carry out aeronautical and non-aeronautical businesses at the Mattala Rajapaksa International Airport, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Implementation of a Community-based Tourism Development Project \tfocusing on the Central, Northern and Eastern regions of Sri Lanka \tUnder a financial grant of the Korea Tourism Organization",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11845",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority has proposed to implement a \"Community\u2011based Tourism Project\" under the financial assistance of the Korea Tourism Organization, focusing the Kuchchaweli Tourism Development Zone owned by the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority. A delegation of the Korea Tourism Organization has conducted a feasibility study on the relevant project proposal and extended its willingness to grant a financial assistance of  2.172 billion Korean Won for the implementation of the proposed entire project. A consensus has also been reached to provide a sum of  of 400 million  Korean won for preparation of the overall plan of the relevant Tourism Development Project, training program and for the implementation of a pilot training program as its first phase. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands to enter into an agreement between the Korea Tourism Organization and the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority for the implementation of the proposed project, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Liberalization of the Sri Lankan Lubricant Market and Selection of New \tEntrants",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11846",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister in charge of the subject of Petroleum Resources Development has been vested with powers by the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation Act, No. 28 of 1961 and its subsequent amended provisions to select new applicants anticipating to enter to the lubricant oil industry and grant licenses in line with that. Accordingly, the Minister in charge of Petroleum Resources Development has fully opened the lubricant oil market of the country. At present, 26 licensed institutions including the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation are engaged in the lubricant oil industry. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to call for Request for Qualifications for the selection of new entrants to the Lubricant Market of Sri Lanka enabling to provide the opportunity for the high quality, innovative and competitive products to be entered to the domestic market providing the opportunity to the consumers to purchase lubricants at competitive prices, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Establishment of Export Oriented Petroleum Refinery and Associated Product Processing Centre in Hambantota area",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11847",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that there is a high potential for establishing an  export oriented petroleum refinery and associated product processing center in Hambantota area. Various parties and local and foreign investors are interested in utilizing the said investment opportunity. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to issue calling for Expression of Interest to select a suitable investor to establish a Petroleum Processing Centre and obtain detailed proposals from those investors who fulfill the  basic qualifications, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Amendments to the National Policy on Management of Chemicals",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11848",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the Environment Programme of United Nations, around 350,000 chemicals exist in the market at present. Exposure to the chemicals causes deaths for about 2 million per year according to the World Health Organization. Further, it has been confirmed that people suffer from various diseases due to improper management of the chemicals. Taking into consideration the negative impact caused to the environment and to health due to the use of chemicals, \u201cEnvironmentally Sound Management of Toxic Chemicals\u201d has been identified in the Agenda 21 of the United Nations as one of the global priorities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to implement the National Policy on Management of Chemicals prepared after negotiating with the relevant main government institutions and Non Government Organizations giving due consideration to the management of chemicals  in order to pursue action adhering to the International Conventions signed by Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Procurement for the supply of raw food items to the National Hospital, Kandy for the year 2022/2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11849",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- National Competitive Bids have been invited for the procurement for the supply of raw food items to the National Hospital, Kandy for the year 2022/2023. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the relevant contract to Janatha Food Suppliers Private Limited as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Procurement for the purchase of Intra Ocular Lens, foldable, hydrophobic (1-7 Items)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11850",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- International Competitive Bids have been invited for this procurement. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to award the relevant contract to M/s Vision Solutions Lanka (Pvt) Ltd., as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Balapitiya Sri Rahularama Purana Viharastha Samanera Akalpa Sangwardena  Bhikshu  Vidyalaya  (Incorporation)  Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11851",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- Balapitiya Sri Rahularama Purana Viharastha Samanera Akalpa Sangwardena Bhikshu Vidyalaya (Incorporation) Bill has been submitted by the Hon. Gayantha Karunathilaka, Member of Parliament, as a Private Member's Bill. The relevant Bill has properly been prepared by the Legal Draftsman and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received to the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to submit a Report to Parliament recommending the relevant Bill as per the provisions of the Standing Order 52(6) of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-09-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-01-09",
    "description": "Next 25 Years",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11852",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-09",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. President apprised the Cabinet that the following action is expected to be taken with a view to achieving the progress of economic, social, cultural and political sectors in Sri Lanka within the next 25 years.\n\n\t(i)\tEstablishment of the following Institutions:\n\n\t\t*\tInstitute of History\n\t\t*\tInstitute of Economics and Trade\n\t\t*\tInstitute for Women and Gender\n\t\t*\tUniversity of Government and Public Policy\n\t\t*\tUniversity of Agro Technology\n\t\t*\tClimate Change University\n\t\t*\tSports University\n\n\t(ii)\tIntroducing new legislation for the following:\n \n\t\t*\tNational Commission on Women's Act\n\t\t*\tGender Equality Act\n\t\t*\tWomen's Empowerment Act\n\t\t*\tChild Care Act\n\t\t*\tClimate Change Act\n\t\t*\tSocial Justice Commission  Act\n\t\t*\tReforestation and Tree Cover Act\n\t\t*\tLiving Entity Act\n\t\tMahaweli River\n\t\tSinharaja\n\t\tSripada Adaviya /Peak Wilderness\n\t\tHorton Plains\n\t\tKnuckles\n\t\tAdam's Bridge\n\t\t*\tLaw for Ocean Resources Exploration and Management  \t\t\t(within the Exclusive Economic Zone/ (EEZ)\n\t\t*\tMuthurajawela (Preservation) Act\n\t\t*\tProtection of Persons with Special Needs Act\n\n\t(iii)\tImplementation of the following New Projects \n\n\t\t*\t75 Urban Forests\n\t\t*\t1996 Houses in Colombo for Low Income Families \n\t\t*\tNational Youth Platform Projects and Programmes"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Establishment of the International Trade Office",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11853",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet was granted at its meeting held on 2022\u201110\u201103 to establish the International Trade Office. At the beginning it is expected to establish the said office under the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies and subsequently amalgamate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft the Bill for the International Trade Office, based on the preliminary draft that has already been drafted, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the Centre for \tAtmospheric and Oceanic Sciences (CAOS), affiliated to the Indian \tInstitute of Science, India and the National Aquatic Resources \tResearch \tand Development \tAgency (NARA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11854",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- A proposal has been made to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding between the Centre for Atmospheric and Oceanic Sciences, affiliated to the Indian Institute of Science, India and the National Aquatic Resources Research and Development Agency for mutually agreed functions such as research exchange programmes, capacity building of Sri Lankan Scientists in predicting ocean-related disasters and providing training opportunities for forecasting fishing zones. Clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have been received for the draft Memorandum of Understanding prepared for the purpose. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries to sign the proposed Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Allotment of a plot of land from the Hambantota area for the Ceylon \tElectricity Board on lease basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11855",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approved the joint proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing and the Minister of Power and Energy for the allotment of a land area of 3 acres 1 rood and 10.65 perches in the Keliyapura area of Hambantota which has been vested with the Urban Development Authority under section 6(1) of the State Land Ordinance, to the Ceylon Electricity Board to be used as an electricity pole yard, for a period of 30 years, on lease basis."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Entering into a Host Country Agreement between the Government of Sri \tLanka and the Global Green Growth Institute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11856",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Global Green Growth Institute has been established in the year 2012 as an inter-governmental organization by the agreement of the stakeholder parties at the United Nations Rio +20 summit. The objectives of establishing the said Institute are to promote the green growth strategies of the developing countries, formulation of green growth plans with the participation of stakeholders and provide relevant parties with necessary support. The said institute functions under the major themes such as renewable energy, green cities and sustainable landscapes. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to sign the relevant agreement, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Granting tax concessions for the World Bank funded Inclusive Connectivity \tand Development Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Inclusive Connectivity and Development Project is being implemented in order to empower the communities in selected districts in Sri Lanka aiming to supply a safe, efficient and climate resilient connectivity and strengthen the agricultural supply chain. Under the said project, it has been planned to develop 3000 km of rural roads island wide, in its initial stage. Taking into account the existing economic situation, it has been recognized that it is appropriate to exempt the payment of taxes relating to the project  so that the foreign currency component under the project can be fully used for the project activities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to declare this project as a Specified Project to be eligible for tax exemption through the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Amending the name of Sri Lanka Institute of Taxation as\tChartered \tInstitute of Taxation of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11858",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Institute of Taxation is a body incorporated under the Sri Lanka Institute of Taxation (Incorporation) (Amendment) Act No. 21 of 2000. The said Institute provides tax education to the public through the conduction of courses and provides membership to professionals in taxation by empowering them to perform as recognized tax consultants, authorized representatives and authorized agents under the Inland Revenue Act No. 24 of 2017. Hon. Madhura Withanage, Member of Parliament has presented a Private Member Bill in Parliament to amend the name of the said institute as Chartered Institute of Taxation of Sri Lanka. Accordingly the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit a Report to Parliament recommending the relevant Bill as per the provisions of Parliamentary Standing Orders 52(6), was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Civil Aviation (Charges for the use of Aerodromes) Regulations",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11859",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister in charge of the subject of Civil Aviation has been vested with the power  by section 117(2) (q) of the Civil Aviation Act No.14 of 2010 to determine the fees and charges to be levied by the Civil Aviation Authority for the Aerodromes in Sri Lanka. The fees charged for the use of Aerodromes at the airports have been revised and the Regulations related thereto have been published through the Gazette Notification dated 2022\u201110\u201126. Further, the Gazette Notification dated 2022\u201111\u201102 has been issued for adopting the same Regulations for the Jaffna International Airport as well. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to table the said Regulations in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Truth and Reconciliation Mechanism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11860",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been found necessary to introduce an independent domestic mechanism of truth seeking as a meaningful way to advance and secure peace achieved after  the end of three decades of conflict. Sri Lanka has established several independent commissions of inquiry to look into post conflict reconciliation. Full implementation of recommendations  of such commissions has to be achieved. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Hon. President; the Hon. Prime Minister; the Minister of Fisheries; the Minister of Education; the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms; the Minister of Urban Development and Housing and the Minister of Foreign Affairs  to implement the concept on truth and reconciliation mechanism prepared accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Establishment of the proposed Agency to promote Exports & Investments",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11861",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal for the establishment of a single institution to promote investments and exports in a coherent and combined manner was submitted through the Budget proposals 2023. Accordingly, it has been planned to establish a new agency instead of Board of Investment and the Export Development Board. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint an Oversight Committee to manage and provide guidance to the task of establishing the said Agency, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Government Paddy Purchasing Programme for the Maha Season 2022/23",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11862",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been reported that there may be a surplus of paddy in the Maha Season 2022/23 according to the data of the Department of Agriculture and the Department of Agrarian Development. Accordingly, in order to protect both farmer and consumer, it has been identified the necessity of the Government intervention to purchase some extent of paddy outside the traditional paddy purchasing system. It has been planned to implement the proposed paddy purchasing programme enabling to provide an additional relief to the identified low income families to maintain their living standard under the prevailing economic situation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to implement the Government Paddy Purchasing Programme 2022/23 through  District Secretaries and Divisional Secretaries with the participation of small and medium scale paddy millers so as to provide each family with 10kg of rice per month for a period of two months, covering two (02) million identified families, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Payment of Salaries of Public Officers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11863",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Implementation of new revenue proposals of the Government for the year 2023 has commenced and since it takes certain period of time to collect income generated through that, the Government expenditure has to be managed for the next few months from January to be suited with the limits of Government cash flow. Accordingly, the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies brought to the notice of the Cabinet the steps taken by the General Treasury pertaining to the payment of monthly salaries of Non-executive officers on due date and the payment of the salaries of executive officers few days later to the due date and the Cabinet granted its concurrence to the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Freezing 6% of the Recurrent Provisions in the Government \tExpenditure Estimates approved for the year 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11864",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201101\u201109 decided to freeze 5% of recurrent provisions in the Government Expenditure Estimates approved for year 2023 enabling to control the Government expenditure within the limited fiscal space and to ensure adequate financial provisions  for essential and key functions. In order to implement this decision, the strategies expected to be taken by the General Treasury were submitted to the Cabinet by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance,Economic Stabilization and National policies. Accordingly, the Cabinet decided at the discussion held, to freeze 6% of recurrent provisions in the approved Government Expenditure Estimates, instead of 5% from the recurrent provisions and to allocate an amount equivalent to 1% out of which to the Ministry of Health as additional provisions for purchasing essential pharmaceuticals."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-16-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-01-16",
    "description": "Providing relief for low income families",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11865",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-16",
    "decision_details_body": "- Attention of the Government has been drawn on the speedy initiation of a new  Scheme to pay welfare benefits and a survey to identify beneficiaries using latest qualifications and criteria has now been commenced and is being implemented island-wide. Necessary provisions have been allocated through the Budget 2023 to provide financial concessions within the first four (4) months of the year 2023 to prevent any difficulties that may encountered by the vulnerable families in the face of economic crisis prevailing at present. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National policies to provide necessary provisions to extend the  financial relief proposed through the Budget 2023 for vulnerable families of the society including Samurdhi beneficiaries, by another period of 5 months from May to September, 2023 until the completion of the ongoing Survey and introducing of new proposed scheme for the payment of welfare benefits, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-23-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-01-23",
    "description": "Implementation of an e-License System for the Department of Imports\tand Exports Control",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11866",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Generally, the Department of Imports and Exports Control issues around 17,000 licenses in a year and that process functions with a minimal technical support and a very high intervention. It has been found the necessity of introducing information technology methodologies in order to implement the said license issuance process more efficiently and with a minimal human intervention. As such, it has been planned to enhance the transparency and efficiency of the said process by automating the aforementioned process with the participation of Regulatory Authorities relevant with the licensing process such as the Sri Lanka Customs, Department of Excise, Department of Motor Traffic as well as the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, National Medicines Regulatory Authority and the Sri Lanka Standard Institute. For the purpose, the Bureau of the Export Control and Related Border Security Programme (EXBS) operated under the Embassy of the United States of America has extended its willingness to grant the STRATLINK information technology programme worth of US$ 280,000 with the complete source code to the Department of Imports and Exports Control as a donation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to implement the e-License programme of the Department of Imports and Exports Control, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-23-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-01-23",
    "description": "South Asia Commercial and Logistics Hub Project",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11867",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Port of Colombo which is the largest Port in Sri Lanka, is also the main hub Port in the South Asian Region. Converting the Port of Colombo into a Logistics Hub is one of the basic strategic goals of the National Port Master Plan of the Sri Lanka Ports Authority. The service supply areas of Battenberg area and Bloemendhal area of the Colombo South Port have been identified to be developed under Public-private Partnership. As such a proposal made by the Colombo International Container Terminal (CICT) to implement the first phase of the proposed project with an investment of US $ 150 million, has been evaluated by a Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee.  Accordingly, based on the recommendations made by the said Committee, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to implement the proposed project as a public-private partnership project between China Merchant Port Company (CM Port), Colombo International Container Terminals (CICT) Company and the Sri Lanka Port Authority, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-23-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-01-23",
    "description": "Proclaiming a Day on Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crime\tand Witnesses",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11868",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crimes and Witnesses Act, No.4 of 2015 has been introduced to create a proper mechanism to identify and promote rights and entitlements of victims and witnesses. Accordingly, National Authority for the Victims of Crime and Witnesses was established. Considering the number of persons particularly the women and children victimized as a result of rise in crimes in Sri Lanka, it has been identified that it is appropriate to proclaim a day on assistance to and protection of victims of crime and witnesses with the purpose of making the society aware of protection of victims of crime and witnesses as well as sensitizing Public Institutions and public officials. Accordingly, the proposal directed by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to proclaim 07th of March, the day on which Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crimes and Witnesses Act, No.4 of 2015 was enacted as the Day on Assistance to and Protection of Victims of Crimes and Witnesses, was granted approval by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-01-23-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-01-23",
    "description": "Revision of En-Route Navigation Charges levied on International Flights\tOverflying Colombo Flight Information Region",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11869",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-01-23",
    "decision_details_body": "- Collection of En-route Navigation charges on International Flights Overflying Colombo Flight Information Region comes under the purview of Airport and Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) Limited and the charges have not been revised since year 1985. Therefore, the proposal directed by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to revise the charges for Overflying aircraft for the use of Air Navigation Services from 2023\u201102\u201101 with immediate effect, was granted approval by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
