    "doc_id": "2023-02-06-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-02-06",
    "description": "Maintaining essential Public Services in the most difficult financial circumstances",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11895",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government revenue has dropped down to a value of 8.3% of the Gross Domestic Product due to the prevailing economic crisis. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Secretary to the Treasury to take necessary action to release imprest only for the most essential recurrent expenditure to be incurred to maintain public services until the condition returns to normalcy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-06-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-02-06",
    "description": "Rationalization of Government Expenditure through a Systematic Review",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11896",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-06",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies has proposed through the Budget 2023 to introduce the Zero Based Budgeting in view of rationalization of Government expenditure. Duplication in expenditure programmes, wasters, low priority activities and efficient and effective methods of utilizing existing allocations will be identified through a systematic review under the Zero-Based Budgeting approach. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to appoint 10 Officials' Committees under the Chairmanship of a Deputy Secretary to the Treasury or a Senior Officer of the Treasury to carry out a systematic review on the following Ministries for which a higher portion of provisions is allocated through the Annual Budgetary Estimates, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tMinistry of Transport and Highways\n*\tMinistry of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government\n*\tMinistry of Education\n*\tMinistry of Health\n*\tMinistry of Agriculture\n*\tMinistry of Plantation Industries\n*\tMinistry of Defence\n*\tMinistry of Public Security\n*\tMinistry of Irrigation\n*\tMinistry of Urban Development and Housing"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-13-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-02-13",
    "description": "Third Round of Negotiations of the Sri Lanka - Thailand Free Trade \tAgreement held in Colombo during 09th and 10th January 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11897",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Preliminary work has been started in the year 2016 to embark a Free Trade Agreement between Sri Lanka and Thailand with the expectation of increasing the existing bilateral trade value of US$ 550 million to US$ 1.5 billion through strengthening the economic corporation of two parties in number of sectors thereby recognizing the economic potentials and complementary economic structures which can be further improved. Accordingly, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2018\u201107\u201103 to commence negotiations of the proposed Sri Lanka Thailand Free Trade Agreement covering Goods, Rules of Origin, Services, Investment, Economic Cooperation, Trade Remedy, Custom Procedures and Trade Facilitation and Intellectual Property. The first round of negotiations was held in July 2018 in Sri Lanka and the second round of negotiations has been held in September 2018 in Bangkok, Thailand. Its third round of negotiations has been held in 09th and 10th January, 2023 at Colombo and the information furnished by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies on the progress of those negotiations was noted by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-02-13-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-02-13",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between the National Search and \tRescue Agency of the Republic of Indonesia and the Civil Aviation \tAuthority of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11898",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-02-13",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka, as a signatory state to the Chicago Convention of International Civil Aviation Organization, is obliged and responsible to provide Air Navigation Services/Air Traffic Services, Flight Information Services and Alerting Services for all aircraft flying across the airspace of this country. Sri Lanka and Indonesia are neighboring states that share the south-eastern boundary of the Colombo Flight Information Region. The responsibilities of search and rescue operations in that region have been vested with Sri Lanka. According to the Chicago Convention of International Civil Aviation Organization, in order to strengthen the cooperation and coordination of search and rescue activities, it is necessary for adjacent States to enter into agreements with neighboring countries setting forth the conditions for entry of search and rescue units into their respective territories. As such, a Memorandum of Understanding has been signed for a period of 05 years between the Civil Aviation Authority of Sri Lanka and the National Search and Rescue Agency of the Republic of Indonesia in the year 2018 and the said period has now become ended. The proposal made by the Minister Ports, Shipping and Aviation to extend the period of said MoU for a further period of 05 years with effect from 2023\u201101\u201123, in order to continue the corporation between the two parties, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
