    "date_str": "2023-04-17",
    "description": "Amending the existing Air Transport Agreement between Sri Lanka and Israel",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11980",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-04-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- Sri Lanka and Israel have entered into an Air Transport Agreement on 2003\u201108\u201124 and the two party has reached to a consensus to amend the said agreement at the International Civil Air Services Negotiations Conference held on 2016\u201112\u201106 in Nassau, Bahamas. Although, approval of the Cabinet has been granted previously at its meeting held on 2021\u201101\u201111 to sign the Protocol for the purpose, it has not yet been signed. The clearance of the Attorney General and the concurrence of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs have been received for the relevant draft Protocol. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to sign the Protocol for amending the Air Transport Agreement that has already been signed between Sri Lanka and Israel and to authorize Ambassador of Sri Lanka to Israel to sign the said Protocol on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-04-17-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-04-17",
    "description": "Allocating the Galle Face Green for the General Public only to spend their leisure time",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=11981",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-04-17",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Ports Authority has undertaken the task of developing the Galle Face Green as a Corporate Social Responsibility Project and the said authority has incurred around Rs.220 million for the development activities so far carried out. An amount of Rs.6.6 million has been spent to repair the damages caused during the recent struggle period. Although this premises should be maintained so that public can freely spend their leisure time, the premises is constantly damaged and maintaining beauty and the scenic nature thereof has become difficult owing to allocating the same for musical shows and other activities where public gather largely. Therefore, Cabinet decided not to grant permission with effect from 2023\u201104\u201120, to utilize the Galle Face Green for musical shows, political meetings or any other activity which damage or could damage the scenic beauty of its premises, except for religious activities."
  },
