    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at its meeting held on 2022\u201109\u201105 to establish the State-Owned Enterprises Restructuring Unit under the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies in order to provide guidance and assist pertaining to the restructuring of State-Owned Enterprises. Accordingly, the  State-Owned Enterprises Restructuring Policy has been prepared aiming to improve the quality, price and accessibility of goods and services provided by the state owned Enterprises, eliminate the fiscal burden caused to the General Treasury by the said enterprises and create a competitive and market based business environment to attract private investments. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and national Policies to take future action on the restructuring of State\u2011Owned enterprises based on the said policy, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-15-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-05-15",
    "description": "Declaration of National Industry Day",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12025",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- Necessary Plans have been prepared to increase the contribution of the industrial sector to the Gross Domestic Product which is 28% at present, up to 30% and to increase the contribution of the manufacturing industry to the Gross National Product which is 15% at present, up to 25%, by the year 2030. Further, it is expected to increase the percentage of entrepreneurs up to 10% which is currently 2.8% and to increase the contribution of micro, small and medium-scale industries to the Gross National Product from 52% to 70% , by the year 2030. In order to meet the said goals, 06 industry sectors have been identified and the Ministry of Industries has taken action to ensure a unified approach to provide the infrastructure and other facilities required for the said sectors. Accordingly, taking into consideration the proposal made by the Minister of Industries, the Cabinet granted approval to conduct an Industry Exhibition Week annually in order to encourage and uplift the promotion of domestic industries and attract foreign investors and industrialists and to conduct the said Exhibition from 22nd to 25th June of this year as the initial step of the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-15-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-05-15",
    "description": "Importation of Urea Fertilizer for paddy cultivation in the Yala Season 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12026",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that 25,000 MT of Urea fertilizer should be further imported  for the Yala Season 2023 when taking into consideration the available quantity of fertilizer with the two Government fertilizer companies and the private sector and those remaining in the Agrarian Services Centres. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to import the said quantity of fertilizer as 60% by the Ceylon Fertilizer Company and 40% by Colombo Commercial Fertilizer Company Ltd., was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-15-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-05-15",
    "description": "Hiring a Maintenance and Emergency Response Vessel (MERV) for the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12027",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201111\u201121 has granted approval to obtain a Maintenance and Emergency Response Vessel for the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation on hiring basis following the International Competitive Bidding Procedure. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the contract for operating a Maintenance and Emergency Response Vessel (MERV) to M/s Sri Lanka Shipping Company Limited on hiring basis for a period of two years from 2023\u201106\u201101 as per the recommendation of the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-15-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-05-15",
    "description": "Scheme for granting permits to import fully electric vehicles for Sri Lankans  \temployed abroad",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12028",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the view of encouraging migrant workers to remit income earned abroad to Sri Lanka through legal channels, the Cabinet has previously approved the scheme of granting permits for the importation of fully electric vehicles to Sri Lankans employed abroad.  Accordingly, the import of an electric vehicle will be based on the amount of foreign exchange remitted by the migrant workers to Sri Lanka during the period from 2022-05-01 to 2022-12-31. However, it is apparent that the amount of foreign exchange remitted during that period does not make space for them to import the desired electric vehicles. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to extend the period in which the amount of foreign currency remitted to Sri Lanka is considered in obtaining a vehicle import permit under the scheme up to 09-15-2023, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-15-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-05-15",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Foreign Affairs Office of the\tPeople's Government of Yunnan Province of the People's Republic of \tChina\tand the Department of External Resources of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12029",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-15",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the visit of Mr. Wang Yubo, Governor of Yunnan Province of the People's Republic of China, to Sri Lanka, from 16 to 20 May, 2023, it is proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Foreign Affairs Office of the People's Government of Yunnan Province of the People's Republic of China and the Department of Foreign Resources of Sri Lanka. The Memorandum of Understanding is expected to provide support to Sri Lanka in the fields of mutual travel, economy, trade and commerce, education, tourism, agriculture, people-to-people and cultural exchange, people's livelihood and health. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policy to sign the said Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Establishment of a National Development Committee for the appraisal of new development projects/programmes",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12030",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Owing to the commencement of development projects/programmes without proper identification and systematic appraisal, it appears that some of the projects implemented during the past have failed to achieve desired results. As such, a proposal for the establishment of a National Development Committee for the methodical appraisal of new development projects/programmes was made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance through the Budget Speech for the year 2023. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint a Committee headed by Mr. Daya Liyanage, a former Deputy Secretary to the Treasury in order to submit its recommendations on the projects/programmes with the estimated cost  considered by the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committees or higher than that, to the Cabinet, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Green Bond Framework",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12031",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government's intention to move towards green financing was stated in the Budget 2023. The proceeds of such bond issuances may be utilized in the areas such as Renewable Energy, Energy Efficiency, Green Buildings, Clean Transportation, Sustainable Water and Wastewater Management, Pollution Prevention, Control and Circular Economy, Climate Change Adaptation, Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Management of Natural Resources and Land Use. The United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and the Global Green Growth Institute (GGGI) have expressed their consent to assist the Government in establishing an internationally accepted framework to access financing through Green/Blue and Sustainable instruments and accordingly a Green Bond Framework has been drafted at present. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to obtain a Second Party Opinion  enabling to validate the presently drafted Green Bond Framework, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Formulation of a Policy Framework for Logistics Service Development including the Shipping Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12032",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Competitiveness of the logistics service industry including Shipping industry is a key factor of the economic development of any country and considering the experiences gained by countries like Singapore and Hong Kong, it is more relevant for an island economy like Sri Lanka. However, it is observed that the existing policy and regulatory framework related to the logistics service industry including the Shipping Industry in Sri Lanka is more protective and not sufficient either to attract investments for development of the said industry or to create a conducive environment to supply competitive/cost efficient logistic services to the users of such services. Considering this situation, the need to prepare a policy framework on logistics service industry was also proposed through the Budget 2023. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to appoint a committee consisting of the representatives of other relevant institutions under the chairmanship of the Secretary to the Treasury to study the existing policies and regulations related to logistics services including the shipping industry and prepare a Logistic Development Programme covering the period of 2023-2027 in accordance with international best practices."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Granting exemptions and incentives in relation to Businesses of Strategic Importance under the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No.11 of 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12033",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Colombo Port City was established as a Special Economic Zone by the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No.11 of 2021. In order to achieve the objectives of modernizing Sri Lanka, creating economic stability and transforming the country into a leader in the export of services, it has been identified the necessity of developing the Port City of Colombo to create a business enabling environment that is internationally competitive. According to the provisions of the Act, the Commission in consultation with the President or the Minister in\u2011charge of the Colombo Port City may identify the businesses designated as Businesses of Strategic Importance and recommend the granting of exemptions or incentives for the same. Two categories have been identified as Primary Businesses of Strategic Importance and Secondary Businesses of Strategic Importance for granting the relevant exemptions and incentives. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to grant the said exemptions and incentives, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "\"Venturing into New Frontiers\" - First International Mining and Mineral\tConference, \tInvestor Forum and Exhibition",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12034",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the aim of providing a platform to all stakeholders involved in the current and future mineral industry in Sri Lanka, the International Mining and Mineral Conference, Investor Forum and Exhibition named \"Venturing into New Frontiers\" has been planned to be held at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall. Through that it is expected to build global brand value for the Sri Lankan mineral industry and create large-scale investment and economic opportunities. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to conduct the proposed International Mining and Mineral Conference, Investor Forum and Exhibition in October 2023, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Amendment of the Ayurveda Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12035",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201110\u201131 for the amendment of the Ayurveda Act, No.31 of 1961, in order to achieve the sustainable development goals and meet the current needs. The Attorney General's clearance has been received for the draft Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. The proposal made by the Minister of Health to publish the said draft Bill in the Government Gazette and present the same in Parliament thereafter, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Implementation of Western Region Megapolis Master Plan 2048 in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12036",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2023-05-08 to award the review of the Western Region Megapolis Master Plan prepared by the Urban Development Authority in 2015 to M/s Surbana Jurong (Pvt) Ltd in Singapore. Accordingly, the said plan will be reviewed and the \"Western Region Megapolis Master Plan - 2048\" will be prepared enabling to implement projects that have been identified so far under the original Master Plan, on priority basis. The joint proposal made by Hon. President; Hon. Prime Minister; and the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to appoint a Ministerial Committee under the chairmanship of the Hon. Prime Minister to provide necessary guidance and coordinate the facilities to implement the said plan prepared as such, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Taking steps to name \u201cKompanna Veediya\u201d Grama Niladhari Division of\tColombo Divisional Secretariat Division in the same manner in all three\tlanguages",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12037",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- \u201cKompanna Veediya\u201d Grama Niladhari Division of Colombo Divisional Secretariat Division has been declared as \"\u0d9a\u0ddc\u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0da4\u0dca\u0da4 \u0dc0\u0dd3\u0daf\u0dd2\u0dba\" in Sinhala, \"\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0bb2\u0bc7\u0bb5\u0bcd\u0b90\u0bb2\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bcd\" in Tamil and \"Slave Island\" in English. It has been suggested that it would be more appropriate to name the Grama Niladhari Division as \u201cKompanna Veediya\u201d in all three languages. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government to declare \u201cKompanna Veediya\u201d as it is in all three languages through a fresh Gazette Notification revising the respective Gazette Extraordinary notification No.743/5 dated 1992\u201112\u201101, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding Regarding Political Consultations between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12038",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Political Consultations between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. It is expected to promote bilateral ties while enhancing the positive roles of other international organizations and regional and global affairs, political developments and topics of mutual interests. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to sign the said MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Carbon Credits between Sri Lanka and Singapore",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12039",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Article 6 of the Paris Agreement has provided the countries with the opportunity to cooperate for the purpose of reducing greenhouse gas emissions in a more cost\u2011effective manner under the International carbon trading.  Accordingly, it has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Carbon Credits between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of Singapore within the framework referred to in the Paris Agreement. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to sign the said MoU, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Awarding the Contract for the Ground Handling Services for SriLankan Airlines at the Doha International Airport and Cargo Warehouse Handling Services at the Dubai International Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12040",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited for Ground Handling Services at the Doha International Airport and Cargo Warehouse Handling Services at Dubai International Airport. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the contract for Ground Handling Services at the Doha International Airport to Qatar Aviation Services W.L.L and to award the contract for Cargo Warehouse Handling Services at the Dubai International Airport to Dnata Company as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-22-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-05-22",
    "description": "Establishment of a Monument for the Commemoration of those who died as a result of the Armed Conflict, Political Unrest or Civil Disturbances in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12041",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-22",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since independence, Sri Lanka has experienced a history of civil disturbances, political unrest, communal clashes and a long-drawn armed conflict, during which citizens of all ethnicities, religions, professions and other identities were subject to perils and sufferings innumerable times. Bitter experiences of the past have proved that any form of conflict based on ethnicity, religion, political ideology or other reasons is highly detrimental to the well-being of the citizens and hampers the progress of the nation. However, the trend of such incidents continues thereby endangering the peace and security of citizens and disrupting social and economic systems. The Office of Reparations Act, No.34 of 2018 recognizes the provision of collective reparations in the form of memorials and other infrastructure as the right to redress for communities or groups of aggrieved persons. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to erect a monument in an appropriate location in Colombo as a symbol of healing and reconciliation to commemorate all persons including civilians, members of Tri\u2011forces and the police and ex\u2011combatants who died as a result of armed conflict, political unrest or civil disturbances in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation and Mutual Assistance on Customs Matters between Sri Lanka and Maldives",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12042",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation and Mutual Assistance on Customs Matters between Sri Lanka and Maldives with a view to strengthening, promoting and developing cooperation and mutual assistance on matters relating to the customs and strengthening mutual understating and communication.  The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Memorandum of Understanding drafted for that purpose.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, to sign the proposed Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "Signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on the Field of Health Cooperation between Maldives and Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12043",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding on the Field of Health Cooperation between Maldives and Sri Lanka with a view to improving health care services, promoting research and development and enhancing the overall well being between the two countries thereby strengthening and formalizing the health cooperation between the two countries. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the proposed draft Agreement. Accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Health to sign the said  Memorandum of Understanding, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "Extension of the period of validity of the Memorandum of Understanding signed between the Sri Lanka Council for Agricultural Research \tPolicy and the Malaysian Agricultural Research and Development Institute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12044",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Memorandum of Understanding has been signed between the Sri Lanka Council for Agricultural Research Policy and the Malaysian Agricultural Research and Development Institute in 2016 for a period of 05 years, with the objective of continuing the scientific cooperation in the field of agriculture between Sri Lanka and Malaysia. The validity period of the said Memorandum of Understanding has now expired and both parties have agreed to extend the said Agreement for another 5 years. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture to extend the period of the Memorandum of Understanding for another five (05) years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "Establishment of Truth and Reconciliation Mechanism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12045",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- On the invitation of Minister of International Relations and Cooperation of South Africa, the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms and the Minister of Foreign Affairs have visited South Africa for a preliminary study on their Truth and Reconciliation Commission. During the visit, meetings have been held with a number of heads of the Government of South Africa including the President and the Minister of International Relations and Cooperation. Accordingly, the joint proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms and the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish the Truth and Reconciliation Commission in Sri Lanka, taking into consideration the functioning of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission of South Africa, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "International Conference on Qualifications Framework and the Recognition of Qualifications and Credentials in Higher Education",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12046",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the increasing internationalization of opportunities for higher education, it has to be entered into Agreements and Conventions which facilitate to mutually recognize the qualifications and credentials awarded according to each country's qualifications framework. Accordingly, the University of Ruhuna and Wayamba University of Sri Lanka in collaboration with the Ministry of Education have initiated several activities through \u201cRegional Cooperation in the field of Recognition among Asian Countries (RecoAsia)\u201d co-funded by the European Union under its \u201cErasmus+\u201d Programme. Further, Sri Lanka has also engaged with the SARRC qualifications Framework Project under the guidance of the International Labour Organization. Under this backdrop, the Ministry of Education has planned to conduct an International Conference on Qualifications Frameworks and the Recognition of Qualifications and Credentials in Higher Education during the two days of 28th and 29th June 2023 with the financial assistance of the RecoAsia and the International Labour Organization. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to conduct the said Conference, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-05-29-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-05-29",
    "description": "Conducting the 45th Asian Conference on Remote Sensing in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12047",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-05-29",
    "decision_details_body": "- Realizing the importance of Remote Sensing Technology in national development activities, countries of the Asian - Pacific Region have formed the Asian Association on Remote Sensing. This Organization in which Sri Lanka is also a founding member is comprised of several member groups such as ordinary members, associate members and sustaining members. It has been proposed to hold the 45th Asian Conference on Remote Sensing throughout 05 days in Colombo during October-November 2024. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism and Lands, to hold the said conference in Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Establishment of an Independent Regulatory Institution for the advancement of Cinema and Television Industry",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12048",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The State Film Corporation was established by the State Film Corporation Act, No.47 of 1971 for the revival of the advancement of the local film industry and in the year 1980 it was renamed as the 'National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka'. At present, the Film Industry is facing many problems and suffers a severe drawback. Therefore, the need to establish an independent regulatory institution to revive the industry has been identified. Also, it has been found appropriate to have an independent institution to regulate the television industry to provide necessary guidance for the advancement of the said industry. Accordingly, taking into consideration a proposal made by the Minister of Mass Media, Cabinet decided to grant approval to take necessary action to establish an independent regulatory institution enabling to facilitate and provide guidance for the revival of the Cinema and Television Industry."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "The National Policy and the Strategic Framework for Prevention and Control of Chronic Non-communicable Diseases in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12049",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Heart diseases, stroke, cancer, chronic respiratory diseases and diabetic are the leading causes to a large percentage of deaths in Sri Lanka caused by non-communicable diseases accounting to approximately 120,000 deaths in each year. Use of tobacco, harmful use of alcohol, obesity, high blood pressure, raised blood sugar level, raised blood cholesterol level have been found as main factors for such diseases. Therefore, the health system should be strengthened to provide screening services for early detection and timely treatment. The first National Policy for prevention of Non-communicable Diseases was declared in 2009 and the revised new policy has been drafted with the participation of all relevant parties after evaluating and reviewing the said policy. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to implement the National Policy and the Strategic Framework for Prevention and Control of Chronic Non-communicable Diseases in Sri Lanka and publish the same in the Government Gazette, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Ratification of the Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty (CTBT)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12050",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Comprehensive Nuclear\u2011Test\u2011Ban Treaty was adopted by the United Nations General Assembly on 1996\u201109\u201110. By the said Agreement, the Member States have agreed to prohibit \u201cany nuclear weapon test explosion or any other nuclear explosion\u201d anywhere in the world. So far, 186 countries have signed the said treaty whereas 177 countries have ratified the same. Sri Lanka has signed the Comprehensive Nuclear\u2011Test\u2011Ban Treaty on 1996\u201110\u201124. Currently, Sri Lanka cooperates with the Comprehensive Nuclear\u2011Test\u2011Ban Treaty Organization in the areas of training, capacity building, data and information sharing. Sri Lanka's ratification of the said Treaty will recognize the diplomatic role of Sri Lanka as an active proponent of international peace and security in a nuclear weapons free world and enable to obtain useful data for civil and scientific purposes benefiting many developing countries including Sri Lanka such as tsunami warning and climate change and earth studies. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to ratify the said Treaty and take necessary action to draft legislation to enforce the provisions of the said Treaty."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Updating the Regulations pertaining to the Company Secretaries under the Companies Act No. 07 of 2007",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12051",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since all the services rendered by the Department of Registrar of Companies are provided through online system, it has been identified the necessity to amend the Regulations pertaining to Company Secretaries made by the Minister in charge  under the provisions of the Companies Act No. 17 of 1982 in order to maintain the said activities properly. Accordingly, taking into consideration the views and suggestions of the relevant stakeholders and Advisory Committee, amended Regulations pertaining to Company Secretaries have been published through the Gazette Notification No. 2323/41 dated 2023\u201103\u201117. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Industries to submit the said Regulations to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Order published under the provisions of the Measurement Units, Standards and Service Act, No. 35 of 1995",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12052",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Maintaining national measurement standards in Sri Lanka in conformity with the international measurements standards, providing metrological services for various fields, ensuring justice through regulatory and service activities based on measurements are the main functions of the Department of Measurement Units, Standard and Services. Accordingly,  National Measurement Laboratory has been established under sub\u2011section 3(b) of the Measurement Units, Standards and Services Act No. 35 of 1995 and an Order has been published through the Gazette Notification No. 2294/54 dated 2022\u201108\u201126 by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security as per the provisions of the Act, declaring the Post of Metrology Experimental Officer to be effective from 2022\u201106\u201116 for the activities of the said Laboratary. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of  Trade, Commerce and Food Security to submit the said Order to Parliament, for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Rationalization of Value Added Tax (VAT) Exemptions and Repealing the Simplified VAT (SVAT)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12053",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Two major reforms with regard to Value Added Tax  have to be introduced as per the Extended Fund Facility (EFF) arrangement of the International Monetary Fund (IMF). Under this, it is required to revamp the Value Added Tax System by removing majority exemptions and to abolish the SVAT system. It is possible to increase the tax revenue approximately by 1.2% of the Gross Domestic Product  through the re-rationalization of  existing VAT exemptions. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft a Bill to amend the relevant provisions in the Value Added Tax Act, enabling to remove the vast majority of  exemptions of VAT by retaining exemptions on the fields of education, health and agriculture and also exemptions which soften the impact on the low-income households and protect key sectors in economy and to abolish the existing  SVAT system with effect from 2024\u201101\u201101 by introducing a more proper mechanism for the refund of VAT, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Contempt of Court, Tribunal or Institution Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12054",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the cabinet meeting held on 2022-06-27 to introduce a new law on \"Contempt of Court\" consisting of clear and specific provisions on the offense of \"Contempt of Court\" and defenses, sentencing and the procedure to be followed in mitigating circumstances. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman. The proposal made by the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter submit to the Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-008-en",
