    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Awarding the Contract for the Repair of Honeywell Auxilliary Power Units \tat SriLankan Airlines (SLA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12056",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- SriLankan Airlines has invited Bids for the repair of Honeywell Auxilliary Power Units following the Limited International Competitive Bidding procedure. Three bids have been received for the purpose and the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the contract for the repair of Honeywell Auxilliary Power Units for a period of 02 years at an estimated cost of USD 15.3 Mn to Honeywell International SARL which has submitted the substantially responsive lowest evaluated bid based on the recommendations of the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-05-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-06-05",
    "description": "Reduction in the price of Essential Medicines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12057",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-05",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Medicines Regulatory Authority established under the National Medicines Regulatory Authority Act No. 5 of 2015 acts as the regulator for all the matters related to the pricing of medicines. Taking into account the depreciation of the Rupee against the United States Dollar, the Ministry of Health has granted approval to increase the maximum retail price of medicines up to 97% in several occasions. As a result of the current economic stabilization program followed by the Government, the value of the United States Dollar has decreased in a considerable amount. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Health to reduce the maximum retail price of 60 types of medicinal products by 16% with effect from 15th June, 2023 and to review the prices of the medicinal products every three months, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "Promotion of the Tourism Industry for Economic Revival",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12058",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201130 has decided to appoint a Cabinet Sub-Committee under the Chairmanship of the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Civil Aviation and with the participation of another six (06) Ministers to identify the existing impediments and opportunities for the promotion of tourism industry for economic revival and submit recommendations to the Cabinet on action be taken to make use of the prevailing opportunities most effectively by removing the said impediments. Accordingly, the Minister of Tourism and Lands brought the Report containing 25 recommendations submitted by the said Cabinet Sub-Committee, to the attention of the Cabinet and the Cabinet granted its concurrence for the implementation of the said recommendations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "Elections (Special Provisions) Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12059",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201112\u201112 has granted approval to amend the Parliamentary Election Act No. 1 of 1981 to take relevant action in case of violation of the Code of Conduct by political parties/independent groups and candidates contesting for an election and to establish special polling stations for specially identified voters who are unable to vote at the prescribed polling station on the election day. Similarly, Cabinet approval has been granted on 2022\u201112\u201112 also to amend the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance, Presidential Elections (Special Provisions) Act, Parliamentary Elections Act and the Provincial Council Elections Act so as to take legal action in case of violation of Media Guidelines when an election has been declared. Accordingly, Legal Draftsman has initiated the drafting amending legislation for the above purpose. However, it has been found the appropriateness of introducing a new Act in the name of Elections (Special Provisions) Act instead of amending the relevant Election Acts separately by incorporating aforementioned amendments. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce a new Act by incorporating the relevant amendments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "The Order under section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12060",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies has issued Orders from time to time under the Foreign Exchange Act, No.12 of 2017  temporarily suspending/limiting outward remittances related to certain capital transactions and current transfers with effect from April 2020, as per the recommendation of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka. Accordingly, the Order which was last issued on 2022\u201112\u201122 in that regard is to be expired on 2023\u201106\u201130. Therefore,  the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, to publish an Order under the provisions of section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act No. 12 of 2017, to extend the said Order for a further period of 06 months as per the recommendation of the Monetary Board of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "Repealing the Bread Ordinance No.13 of 1864",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12061",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Bread Ordinance has been introduced incorporating the provisions to regulate the sale of bread and to prevent the adulteration of bread offered for sale. It has been identified that it is not necessary to implement the said Ordinance further, since there are instances where issues are arisen with the certain provisions of the same when implementing the provisions of the Consumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 2003. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft legislation to repeal the said Ordinance, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
