    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "Amendment to the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12062",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2018\u201103\u201106 to draft a Bill to amend the Prevention of Domestic Violence Act, No.34 of 2005. Clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Prevention of Domestic Violence (Amendment) Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman as per the said approval. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President, in his capacity as the Minster of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-06-12-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-06-12",
    "description": "Amendment to the Parliamentary Elections Act, Presidential Elections Act,\tProvincial Councils Elections Act and Local Authorities Elections Ordinance \tin consequence to the Regulation of Election Expenditure Act No. 3 of 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12063",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-06-12",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified the necessity to make the incidental amendments to the Parliamentary Elections Act, Presidential Elections Act, Provincial Councils Elections Act and Local Authorities Elections Ordinance, with the enactment of the provisions of the Regulation of Election Expenditure Act No. 3 of 2023, and the approval has been granted to make the said amendments at the Cabinet meeting held on 2023-01-23. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the relevant Bill in the Government Gazette and present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
