    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-08-28",
    "decision_details_body": "- Limited International Competitive Bids have been invited for ground handling services for SriLankan Airlines at Delhi and Trichy International Airports in India, Beijing International Airport in China and Kuwait International Airport. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the relevant procurements respectively to the following bidders as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tCelebi Airport Services India Pvt. Ltd.\n\n*\tBird Airport Services (Trichy) Pvt. Ltd.\n\n*\tBeijing Aviation Ground Services Company Limited \n\n*\tNational Aviation Services W.L.L."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Working under an Integrated approach treating the need for water management as an emergency situation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12165",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- A report released on 2023\u201108\u201122 by the National Disaster Relief Centre has shown that owing to the prevailed dry weather condition, around 84,000 families in 70 divisional secretariat divisions belonging to 17 districts of the Island have to face a shortage of drinking water. Under that backdrop, the existing limited water capacities should be utilized and managed in an optimal manner until an adequate capacity of water is collected in the reservoir systems in the country. According to the National Water Resources Policy approved by the Cabinet on 2023\u201107\u201110, priority should be given to providing drinking water, and the government is also committed to protect other water stakeholders. Accordingly, the proposals stated in the joint Cabinet Memorandum submitted by the Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government; the Minister of Irrigation and the Minister of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development to treat the supply of drinking water as an urgent and priority requirement until there is a sufficient rainfall and to function the National Water Resources Council proposed by the National Water Resources Policy as an Urgent Action Committee in order to take necessary action for the purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "The progress of the Mega Scale Development Projects at the end of the \tSecond Quarter of 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12166",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet considered the report submitted by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies on the progress achieved by 202 mega scale development projects implemented by line Ministries by the end of the second quarter of 2023. Cabinet noted that, the progress of the most of the projects is below the expected level by the end of the second quarter of 2023 owing to the fact that the funds related to the projects implemented on foreign funds cannot be used until the debt restructuring process that has been started is completed, and the release of domestic funds is limited. Accordingly, Cabinet decided to allocate provisions in the year 2024, giving priority to the projects that can contribute to achieve the Government's 2048 development goals and as a solution to the current economic crisis, until it becomes possible to use foreign funds after completion of the debt restructuring process."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Promotion of Tertiary Education through Vocational Guidance",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12167",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- A program has been designed to provide opportunities for the students who complete G.E.C. (O/L) until they start studies for G.E.C. (A/L) or those who complete the G.E.C. (A/L) examination until they embark upon vocational Education, to complete a curriculum that covers five basic areas related to vocational education while retaining them within the school system. The program is mainly expected to develop Information Technology and English language which are generally important for professional education and also develop soft skills in parallel with the same. The proposal made by the Minister of Education to implement the said project as a pilot project for a period of 3-4 months in 320 selected schools covering every educational division of the Island, and thereafter to implement the said programme as a national programme from the year 2024 onwards based on the results of the pilot programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Leasing out of the servient right of several land lots located in Muthurajawela owned by the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation, for laying of an underground pipeline system of the Ceylon Electricity Board",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12168",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- A land in extent of 69-acres in Muthurajawela owned by the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation, was set apart by means of selling to the Ceylon Electricity Board in 1997, and the Yugadanavi Power Plant has been built in a potion of the said land. The new Sobadhanavi power plant is currently being built in the remaining portion of the said land. The need for the construction of underground cooling pipelines and underground fuel pipelines for those fuel plants have been identified. For that purpose, several other plots of land in Muthurajawela owned by the Sri Lanka Land Development Corporation have been identified, and accordingly the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to lease out the servient right of those plots along with the right to sub-lease, to the Ceylon Electricity Board on lease basis, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Granting a plot of land located at D.M. Colombage Mawatha, Kirulapone to the Warakagoda Sri Gnanarathana Social Welfare Foundation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12169",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- A request has been made by the Mahanayaka Thero of Kandy Asgiri Maha Viharaya to provide a plot of land suitable for construction of a designated monastery in order to provide accommodation facilities to monks visiting from distant regions for the national and religious events held in Colombo and its suburbs and for other requirements as well. A block of land in extent of 27 perches owned by the Urban Development Authority located at D.M. Colombage Mawatha, Kirulapana has been identified for that purpose and the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to vest the said block of land with the Warakagoda Sri Gnanarathana Social Welfare Foundation through a free grant, for the construction of a monastery, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Establishment of Diplomatic Relations by the Government of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka with the Union of the Comoros and the Democratic Republic of S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9 and Pr\u00edncipe",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12170",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The African region consists of 54 sovereign States recognized by the United Nations. Out of which, Sri Lanka has established diplomatic relations with 46 countries and is awaiting concurrence from 6 more countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish diplomatic relations with the Union of the Comoros consisting of a group of islands situated in the Eastern Africa of the African Region and the S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9 and Pr\u00edncipe, an African island located in Gulf of Guinea, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "National Policy and Action Plan on Migration for Employment Sri Lanka \t2023 - 2027",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12171",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The first policy of Sri Lanka on labor migration has been formulated in the year 2008 as the National Labor Migration Policy.  The said Policy has been reviewed by obtaining views of all stakeholders in the labor migration sector including relevant Ministries, migrant workers and their family members, foreign employment agencies, private sector, civil society organizations, trade unions, academia, research institutions and development partners, international non-governmental organizations and United Nations Agencies and the National Policy and Action Plan on Migration for Employment Sri Lanka 2023 - 2027 has been drafted. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Labour and Foreign Employment to implement the said Policy and Action Plan 2023\u20112027 formulated in accordance with the national and international legal and policy frameworks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Making provisions for the registration of electric-powered motor tricycles \t(Three-wheelers)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12172",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified that in the production of electric-powered motor tricycles and in the conversion of motor tricycles powered by petrol or diesel into electric motor tricycles, the tare weight of such tricycles may exceed 500 kilograms since electric-charged batteries are used for that. Also, according to the interpretation of the Motor Traffic Act, the tare weight of a motor tricycle must not exceed 500kg and the gross weight must not exceed 1000kg. Accordingly, the Cabinet at its meeting held on 2022\u201108\u201108 has granted approval to amend the Motor Traffic Act by removing prevailing impediments to register electric-powered tricycles. Clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman as per the said approval. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Repeal of the Rent Act, No.7 of 1972 and introduction of the Protection of Occupants Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12173",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- Even though the Rent Act, No.7 of 1972 which was introduced with the objective of determining the rights and the duties of landlords and tenants, was amended at several occasions, it is observed that the intended objectives of the Act are not being met. The Advisory Committee on Rent Law set up under the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms has examined the matters with this regard and has proposed that it would be appropriate to introduce a new law with the aim of safeguarding the rights of the landlord and the tenant equally. Taking\tthese proposals into consideration, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to repeal the Rent Act, No.7 of 1972 and to introduce a fresh Act namely, the Protection of Occupants Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Amendment to the Promotion of Export Agriculture Act, No.46 of 1992",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12174",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified the necessity of amending the Promotion of Export Agriculture Act, No.46 of 1992 in keeping up with the current needs. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantation Industries to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the said Act, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Online Safety Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12175",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Online Safety Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman with the objective of protecting the civil society from damages caused by online falsehoods and manipulation. The following actions have been interpreted as offenses through the provisions of this Act, as indicated in the Part III of the Bill.\n\n*\tCommunication of false statements of facts in Sri Lanka\n\n*\tMaking false statements amounting to contempt\n\n*\tWantongly giving provocation by false statement to cause riot\n\n*\tDisturbing a religious assembly by a false statement\n\n*\tCommunicating a false statement with deliberate intent to wound religious feelings\n\n*\tDeliberate and malicious communication of false statement to outrage religious feelings\n\n*\tCheating\n\n*\tCheating by personation\n*\tIntentional insult by false statement with intent to provoke a breach of peace\n\n*\tCirculating false report with intent to cause mutiny or an offence against the state etc.\n\n*\tCommunicating statements of fact to cause harassment.\n\n*\tChild abuse\n\n*\tMaking or altering bots to commit an offence\n  \nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit the same to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-04-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-09-04",
    "description": "Anti-Terrorism Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12176",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-04",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has been granted on 2022-09-05 to publish the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman to introduce the Anti\u2011Terrorism Act by repealing the Prevention of Terrorism (Temporary Provisions) Act in the Government Gazette and thereafter present it in the Parliament according to which the said Bill was published in the Government Gazette on 2023-03-22. Subsequently, several interested parties (local and International) have submitted their views on certain sections of the Bill. Accordingly, the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms has formally invited opinions and suggestions from the interested parties through electronic and electronic media, and the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms has held discussions with some parties. Hence, taking into consideration all the opinions and suggestions that have been submitted, necessary action has been taken to    re-revise the original Bill published in the Government Gazette and prepare a fresh Bill through the Legal Draftsman. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the said fresh Bill.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, submit the same to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Implementing  a Pilot Project for Beire Lake Water Quality Improvement",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12177",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- As per a proposal submitted by Groepo Pte Ltd (GPL), a Singapore company with Japanese ownership, approval in principle of the Cabinet was granted at the Meeting held on 2023\u201107\u201117 to pursue action to implement a Pilot Project together with several Government Institutions to improve the water quality of the Beire Lake using micro-nano bubble technology, carbon fiber biofilm technology and eco\u2011friendly enzymes. Accordingly, Cabinet approved the joint proposal made by Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies and the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to implement the  proposed pilot project for a period of 05 years, subject to providing necessary guidance to implement the said project by an Experts Committee comprising of experts in the field of water quality in all universities of the country and representatives of all relevant research and other agencies, taking into account the further information presented by the project investor, and thereafter, arrive at a decision regarding the further implementation of the project, based on the outcome achieved."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Vesting a plot of land which contains a storied housing complex owned by the Urban Development Authority, with the University of Colombo",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12178",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Board of Management of the Urban Development Authority has granted approval to vest the land in extent of 0.2761 hectares containing a storied housing complex with 144 housing units located at Kalinga Mawatha, Narahenpita, with the University of Colombo. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development and Housing to vest the said plot of land with storied housing complex with the University of Colombo, as a free grant, to be utilized to provide hostel facilities, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Investment Proposal for a Solar Power/Battery Storage Project at Poonakary Tank in Kilinochchi",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12179",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Cabinet approval has been granted to call for Expressions of Interest from prospective investors to develop renewable energy projects with a capacity of 50 MW or more in order to support the implementation of expeditious renewable energy development programmes in the country. Accordingly, United Solar Energy SL (Pvt.) Ltd. has submitted a proposal to develop a solar power plant of 700 MW with a battery energy storage system, at Poonkari Tank, Kilinochchi enabling to provide a power supply of 134 MW. It has been proposed to implement the proposed project with a total investment of US$ 1,727 million and as a 100% foreign direct investment, out of which US$ 500 million will be allocated to be utilized for local project components. As a part of the proposed project, the project proponent company has proposed to construct 03 barrages around the Poonkari tank at a cost of US $13.5 million to prevent the sea water intrusion and to rehabilitate the tank. Instead, the Northern Provincial Council, the Northern Provincial Irrigation Department and the Department of Agrarian Development have already agreed to provide 1,080 acres of the shallow area of the tank to the said company on a 35-year lease agreement for the installation of the 700 MW solar power plant. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to accept the project proposal submitted by United Solar Energy SL (Pvt.) Ltd. in principle and to appoint a Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee to evaluate the said proposal and submit recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Term contract for the procurement of 04 shipments of Gasoline of 92 Unl within the next four months period",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12180",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited for a term contract from the registered suppliers of the Ceylon Petroleum Corporation to purchase 04 shipments of Gasoline 92 Unl for a period of 04 months from 2023\u201109\u201121 to 2024\u201101\u201121. For the purpose, 04 companies have submitted bids. The proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the said procurement to M/s. Vitol Asia Pte. Ltd, as per the recommendation of the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Submission of an Order published in terms of the provisions of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979, for approval in Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12181",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- According to the existing duty structure, the duty levied on the importation of certain raw materials used by local printing ink manufacturers for ink manufacturing is higher  than the printing ink imported as finished products thereby causing a disadvantageous situation to local printing ink manufacturers. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to present the Order published in the Government Gazette dated 2023\u201107\u201121 in terms of the provisions of the Sri Lanka Export Development Act, No.40 of 1979 in order to rectify the same, in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka and the State of Kuwait on the Establishment of a Bilateral Consultation Mechanism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12182",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the discussions held between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the State of Kuwait, an agreement has been reached regarding the establishment of a bilateral consultation mechanism  between the two countries. Accordingly, aiming to promote friendly relations and cooperation in the political, economic and other fields between the two countries, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to sign a Memorandum of Understanding on the establishment of a bilateral consultation mechanism in parallel with the 78th Session of the United Nations General Assembly to be held in New York in September 2023, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Accession to the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12183",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting on 2021-12-20 to take necessary action to sign the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to sign he Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons by Sri Lanka at the Conference held with related to the said Treaty in parallel to the UN General Assembly scheduled to be conducted in New York in September 2023,  was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Bill on Gender Equality",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12184",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- It is evident  that Sri Lanka is lagging behind with regard to Gender equality in Sri Lanka and the Ministry of Women, Child Affairs and Social Empowerment is taking measures to minimize the gender imbalances. Accordingly, approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022-09-05 to prepare a Bill to introduce the necessary legal provisions with the objective of Gender equality and women empowerment. Accordingly, the said Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman was submitted to the Cabinet by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Women, Children Affairs and Social Empowerment and it was decided to grant concurrence of the Cabinet in principle, for the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Bill on the Establishment of National Women's Commission",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12185",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022-09-05 to establish an independent commission named as National Women's Commission through an Act of Parliament, enabling to make necessary recommendations to Parliament through the Minister-in-charge to provide leadership for women's rights and gender equality and intervene for the issues related to gender equity and equality. Accordingly, the said Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman was submitted by the Hon. President in  his capacity as the Minister of Women, Children Affairs and Social Empowerment to the Cabinet and it was decided to grant concurrence of the Cabinet in principle for the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Committee Stage amendments of the Bill of Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of\t2002",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12186",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to submit the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman in Parliament, to amend the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002 as well as the abolition of Simplified Value Added Tax (SVAT) System  from 2024-01-01.  Representations have been made by the relevant parties that if the Simplified Value Added Tax (SVAT) System  is removed without having a robust value added refund system, it will create serious cash flow issues for the present registered persons under the  SVAT system, especially the exporters. Therefore, it seems appropriate to phase out the Simplified Value Added Tax System, until a robust tax refund mechanism is established. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit a proposal to revise the effective date of the relevant provisions relating to removal of the Simplified Value Added Tax System at the Committee Stage of the Value Added Tax (Amendment) Bill in Parliament, as 2025-04-01, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Incentivizing assembly of Electric Vehicles",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12187",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- Many Asian countries have adopted a more favorable approach by imposing a tariff rate of zero per cent (0%) on the assembly and production of Electric Vehicles (EV) and Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles (PHEV). Through this attractive incentive, it will be able to attract investors and manufacturers as well as focus on future export potential while also complying with global imperative of environmental protection. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to impose flat zero per cent (0%) tariff on the CIF (Cost, Insurance and Freight) when importing brand new Semi-Knocked-Down (SKD) kits for the assembly of Electric Vehicles with a power rating of up to 500kW, Electric Two\u2011Wheelers and Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles with engine capacities of up to 3000cc, by the companies which have already entered into Agreements and new companies entering into Agreements with the Board of Investment of Sri lanka that make a minimum investment of US$ 50 million in the Electric Vehicles and Plug-in Hybrid Electric Vehicles assembly industry, with a view to promoting  the Electric Vehicle manufacturing locally, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-11-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-09-11",
    "description": "Permission to import Electric Rechargeable Vehicles on duty free basis to attract  investments",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12188",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-11",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to grant permission to import one electric rechargeable vehicle, brand new with CIF value not exceeding US$ 30,000 on duty free basis for projects fulfilling the following  qualifying criteria in order to attract investments under the \"Investor Retention and Expansion Programme for Re-investments of Existing BOI Companies\" and 100 \"BOI IT/ITES Companies Programme\", was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\t1.\tInvestor Retention and Expansion Programme for Re-investments of \tExisting BOI Companies\n\n    \u2022 The relevant Company should be in operation for not less than 05 years having registered under section 17 of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Act.\n  \n    \u2022 Minimum proposed investment for expansion of the business should be US$ 3 Mn.\n  \n    \u2022 Generation of minimum 50 employment opportunities under the expansion programme of the project.\n  \n\t2.\t100 BOI IT/ ITES Companies Programme \n\n    \u2022 An enterprise should generate 50 new local employment opportunities and out of which 15 employees should be technically qualified. \n\n    \u2022 Minimum Investment should be US$ 250,000."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Taking steps to prevent and control forest fires",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12189",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Given the man-made fires in the forests, there is a tendency to increase the risk of forest fires rapidly especially during dry whether conditions.  This situation commonly can be seen in the districts of Badulla, Kandy, Nuwara Eliya, Matale, Monaragala, Polonnaruwa, Kurunegala, Puttalam and Rathnapura.  About 150 forest fires have been reported so far this year and in consequence of that, approximately 2,600 hectares of forests have been destroyed. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Resources Conservation to implement a programme to prevent and extinguish the forest fires with the assistance of the Government mechanism and other relevant parties from national level to village level, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Memorandum of Understanding between the Bandaranaike International Diplomatic Training Institute and the Levan Mikeladze Diplomatic Training and Research Institute of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Georgia",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12190",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the Bandaranaike International Diplomatic Training Institute coming under the purview of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Levan Mikeladze Diplomatic Training and Research Institute of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Georgia to establish cooperation pertaining to sharing of expertise, exchange of academic staff, exchange of students, joint research programmes as well as sharing of teaching methodologies and other relevant areas. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to sign the said proposed Memorandum of Understanding between the two parties in parallel with the 25th anniversary celebrations of the establishment of diplomatic relations between two countries, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Procurement of Accessories for Buoy Mooring used for offloading petroleum in the sea near Muthurajawela",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12191",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited according to the International Competitive Bidding Procedure to procure 26 marine hoses and relevant accessories required for Buoy Mooring which is used to offload shiploads of petroleum in the sea near Muthurajawela and only one bid has been received. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the relevant procurement to M/s. Industrial Products Asia Pacific (Pte) Ltd. as recommended by the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee that evaluated the said bid, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Procurement of 04 shipments of Gas oil within the next four (04) months period",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12192",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited under term contract basis for procurement of 04 shipments of gas oil for Ceylon Petroleum Corporation within the next four (04) months period from 2023-11-01 to 2024-02-29. It has been received 05 bids for that.  The proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the relevant procurement to M/s Petrochina International (Singapore) Pte.Ltd based on the\trecommendation of the Special Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "28th Session of the Conference of Parties to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change in Dubai, UAE",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12193",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The 28th Session of the Conference of Parties to the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP 28) is scheduled to be held in Dubai, United Arab Emirates from 2023.11.30 to 2023.12.12. In that Conference, Sri Lanka, together with most vulnerable countries due to climate change, expects to present a proposal to create platform named as \"Climate Justice Forum\" that will lead developing countries to have a common voice regarding their concerns and unlock the pledges and commitments of developed countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to maintain a Country Pavilion during the conference for the active participation of the delegations participating in the 28th Conference of Parties to the United Nations Framework Convention and showcase the national level initiatives related to climate change in the pavilion, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Amendments to the Inland Revenue Act, No.24 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12194",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of ensuring that the well-being of disabled children in the society is  prioritized and they receive comprehensive care, it has been proposed that it is appropriate to make amendments to the Inland Revenue Act so that any charitable organization established as a legal entity or registered under any law enforced for the registration of social service organizations that provides health facilities to children in collaboration with Government health care/education system can claim tax relief. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Acting Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the Inland Revenue Act by incorporating the necessary legal provisions for that purpose, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Obtaining policy based special lending facility from the Asian Development Bank for the Financial Sector Stability and Reform Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12195",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka has conducted initial discussions with the Asian Development Bank to obtain 02 policy based lending facilities amounting to US$ 200 million each for implementing two sub-programmes under the  Financial Sector Stability and Reform Programme. Under the said first Sub-programme, it has been proposed to implement immediate reforms to enhance the crisis management regulatory framework and stabilize the financial sector, and under the second Sub-programme, it has been proposed to build a resilient and inclusive financial system. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to enter into a loan agreement with the Asian Development Bank to obtain US$ 200 million for the first Sub-programme at an interest rate of 2% per annum, with a repayment period of 25 years including a grace period of 05 years, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Establishment of a Public Debt Management Institution (PDMA)",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12196",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Importance of establishing an independent Public Debt Management Institution as an institutional reform has been emphasized through the Interim Budget of the year 2022 and improving debt management and transparency have also been identified as priority areas under the Extended Fund Facility of the International Monetary Fund. The International Monetary Fund and the World Bank have provided technical assistance for the establishment of the proposed Public Debt Management Institution. After consultation with relevant stakeholders, the debt management reform plan, debt management institutional framework and legal framework have now been designed. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Acting Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to instruct the Legal Draftsman to draft the  Public Debt Management Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-09-25-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-09-25",
    "description": "Submission of the Appropriation Bill for the year 2024 to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12197",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-09-25",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the Cabinet Meeting held on 2023\u201107\u201131 to prepare the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2024. Accordingly, clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2024 prepared by the Legal Draftsman. As such, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Regulation of Chemical Substances affecting National Security",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12198",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- A large number of different chemical substances are used in Sri Lanka for peaceful uses such as industrial, agricultural, medical and research purposes. It has been observed that, out of which some chemical substances such as Nitric Acid, Chlorine, Hydrogen Peroxide, Potassium Cyanide, Sodium Cyanide, Nitromethane and Sodium Azide have a dual-use nature that can be used for peaceful as well as illicit purposes. It has been recognized that there is a risk of using those chemicals which are used in various industries such as dairy, beverages, oil related industries, water purification for harmful activities that threaten the national security. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence to enact legal provisions to regulate such chemical substances to prevent their misuse, and to vest that regulatory role with the National Authority for Implementation of the Chemical Weapons Convention, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Establishment of a University on Education by upgrading the National \tColleges of Education to the status of Campuses of Universities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12199",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- In terms of the Cabinet decision dated 2019\u201112\u201104, a Committee of Experts has been appointed under the chairmanship of Senior Professor Gunapala Nanayakkara for the purpose of submitting recommendations on administrative and legal procedures to be followed in upgrading the existing National Colleges of Education to the status of the campuses of the universities, with the aim of establishing all graduate teacher cadre in Lanka.  As per the recommendations of the said Committee, the proposal made by the Minister of Education to instruct the Legal Draftsman to take necessary action to draft a new Bill for imposing legal provisions to upgrade 19 out of the 20 existing National Colleges of Education to the status of campuses and to establish a new university called Sri Lanka University of Education, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Granting State owned lands for a Solar Power Project of 100 MW, on lease \tbasis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12200",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal to take over a land in extent of 219.72 hectares located in the Siyambalanduwa Divisional Secretariat Division of the Monaragala District to the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority for a 100 MW solar power project was taken up for discussion at the  Cabinet meeting held on 2023\u201108\u201107, and a decision was taken to discuss with the Ministry of  Tourism and Lands in that regard and submit information related thereto, to the Cabinet. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to lease out the relevant extent of land to the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority for a period of 25 years, along with the provisions enabling to sub\u2011lease the said land to the selected renewable energy developer, as per the recommendation of the Ministry of Tourism and Lands."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Streamlining the inquiries conducted into consumer complaints received \tby the Consumer Affairs Authority",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12201",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the provisions of the Consumer Affairs Authority Act, No.9 of 2003, legal provisions have been provided for the Consumer Affairs Authority to intervene in consumer complaints. Also, the Department of Measurement, Standards and Services established by the Measurement Units, Standards and Services Act, No.35 of 1995 conducts market raids together with the Consumer Affairs Authority with a view to protecting the consumer rights.  Accordingly, the Minister of Trade, Commerce and Food Security having informed the Cabinet on the programme planned to implement to educate consumers and manufacturers regarding the protection of consumer rights and fair trade practices as one of the important steps to reduce the time and effort spent on investigating consumer complaints and giving decisions thereto, to decentralize the investigation procedure and make provisions to conduct them district level in order to make the process of investigating complaints more efficient, and to establish a National Operations Centre aiming to conduct the special raids through an integrated programme, decided to grant the concurrence of the Cabinet for the same."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Providing facilities at the Oluwil Fishery Harbour to carry out fish \tprocessing activities by Tess (Pvt) Ltd.",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12202",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The approval of the Cabinet has previously been granted to provide facilities at the Oluwil Fishery Harbour to carry out fish processing activities by Tess (Pvt) Ltd. re-activating the fish processing plant which has been idle on the premises of the Oluvil Fishery Harbour. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries to provide the fish processing plant located at the Oluwil Fishery Harbour to Tess (Pvt) Ltd., on lease basis for a period of 10 years, subject to levying the relevant lease rental recommended by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee monthly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Increasing inland fish production through stocking of fish seeds in reservoirs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12203",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The inland fisheries and aquaculture sector plays a significant role in the rural economy of Sri Lanka and highly contributes to the increase of food security and nutrition and for providing employment opportunities. In order to carry out  economically effective inland fish production with high growth in the reservoirs of the country, approximately 500 million fish fingerlings should be continuously stocked annually. However, it has not yet been able to fully utilize the potential of the existing reservoirs for culture-based fisheries due to the insufficient fish seed stocking. Although, 230 million fish fingerlings and 80 million freshwater prawn post larvae were initially planned to be stocked in the reservoirs in the year 2023, the said plan had to be changed due to the drying up of the reservoirs owing to the dry weather condition which prevailed in the recent past. Accordingly,  taking into account the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries  to secure budgetary provisions required for the implementation of the programme for producing 100 million fish fingerlings and 50 million freshwater prawn post larvae and stocking into the reservoirs during the remaining period of this year, by revising the said plan, the Cabinet approved the provision of additional allocations of Rs. 100 million for the said tasks for the year 2023."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Establishment of a New Commercial High Court",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12204",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Necessary action needs to be taken to maintain more conducive investment atmosphere in the country in achieving the development targets.  Considering the situation, the necessity of establishing a new Commercial High Court has been identified in order to ensure the expeditious resolution of the current high volume of cases pending with regard to commercial matters. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to establish the relevant Commercial High Court at No. 80, Adhikarana Mawatha, Colombo 12, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-008-en",
    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Construction of 1996 housing units for low income families under the Chinese Aid Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12205",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of China has concurred to grant financial aid of Yuan 552 million to the Government of Sri Lanka to construct 1996 housing units as an assistance to the Urban Regeneration Project which is being implemented as per the decision made to relocate residents from settlements with limited facilities in the Western Province and settle them in the housing Units of Urban Housing Schemes with improved amenities. The Government of Sri Lanka, under the entire project, will carry out the land development activities and provide necessary infrastructure up to the boundary of the work sites.  Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minster of Urban Development and Housing  to sign the implementation Agreement of the relevant project with the Government of China, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-02-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2023-10-02",
    "description": "Establishment of 70MW, Alternative Current (AC) ground mounted solar Photovoltanic (PV) power plants with 1-5 MW capacity on build, own and operate basis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12206",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-02",
    "decision_details_body": "- Proposals have been called from prospective investors interested in establishing 70MW, Alternative Current (AC) ground mounted solar Photovoltanic (PV) power plants with 1-5 MW capacity on build, own and operate basis  with 20 year operational period so as to connect 11 grid substations. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to grant approval to the relevant investors to implement projects for 08 grid substations of Ampara, Anuradhapura, Galle, Habarana, Kurunegala Madampe, Maho and Matara, based on the recommendations submitted by the Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee after evaluation of their proposals, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
