    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "Conducting a Series of Programmes for the full integration of Upcountry Tamils into the Sri Lankan Society",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12246",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government has planned to implement a national programme to mark 200 years for the Sri Lankan Plantation Community and several other programmes in the future for the betterment of the said community. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint a Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee chaired by the Hon. Prime Minister to provide necessary guidance and monitor the effective and efficient implementation of the relevant programmes in collaboration with the Ministry of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development and other relevant Government and Non\u2011Government Institutions, enabling to develop educational and health facilities, create economic and vocational opportunities and provide a high living standard with permanent residence, towards the betterment of plantation community who are Sri Lankan citizens, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "Submission of the National Education Policy Framework to Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12247",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- A Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee chaired by the Hon. President and a Committee of Experts chaired by the Secretary to the Prime Minister and comprising of 25 members to assist the said Sub-Committee have been appointed to take necessary action to prepare a National Education Policy Framework and submit the same to Parliament and the said Committee of Experts paying attention to the relevant specific areas and subject matters, has drafted the National Education Policy Framework. The \"National Education Policy Framework - 2023-2033\" has been prepared by further developing the said draft incorporating the observations and recommendations presented by the Cabinet Sub\u2011Committee to the said Bill. Accordingly, the proposal made by the the Hon. President to refer the said National Education Policy Framework to the Parliamentary Sectoral Oversight Committee on Education and to table the same thereafter, in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "Tax Policy Reforms to strengthen Revenue-based Fiscal Consolidation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12248",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- A number of progressive and broad\u2011based tax policy proposals have been implemented since June 2022 to achieve revenue-based fiscal consolidation with view to ensuring debt sustainability and as a result of that tax revenue has increased by 51% within the first 9 months in the year 2023 compared to the year 2022. Nevertheless, it has not yet been able to meet the tax collection targets agreed with the International Monetary Fund. Accordingly, the Cabinet granted approval to amend the relevant laws to increase the existing Value Added Tax (VAT) rate up to 18% with effect from 2024\u201101\u201101 and to implement new tax proposals including the imposition of VAT for certain goods and services to which VAT is not applicable at present, in order to meet tax revenue and primary balance targets as agreed with the International Monetary Fund."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-10-30-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-10-30",
    "description": "The revision of the existing General Policy Guidlines in respect of the supply of electricity",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12249",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-10-30",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Minister in-charge of Electricity has been vested with the power to prepare General Policy Guidelines on supply of electricity subject to the approval of the Cabinet as per the provisions of the Electricity Act, No. 20 of 2009. Accordingly, as per the existing General Policy Guidelines, the tariff review period has been determined as six (06) months. The joint proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies and the Minister of Power and Energy to revise the tariff review period as three (03) months taking into consideration the difficulties faced by the general public due to pursuing action accordingly and to revise the existing General Policy Guidelines, enabling to conduct Energy Dispatch Audit of the Ceylon Electricity Board and to improve the predictions of electricity with the assistance of the Department of Meteorology, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
