    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2021\u201109\u201127 has granted approval to amend the \tCode of Criminal Procedure Act, No. 15 of 1979 to make legal provisions \tenabling a criminal court to decide whether the requirement of personal \tattendance of suspect/accused persons in courts under certain identified \tcircumstances could \tbe dispensed with even during the trial. Several \tinterested\tparties have submitted further matters for the Bill prepared accordingly, prior to \tthe submission of the same to Parliament. As such, the proposal made by the \tMinister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the \tLegal Draftsman to draft a new Bill to amend the Code of Criminal Procedure \tAct, No. 15 of 1979 \tby further developing the Bill already drafted, taking also \tinto consideration the aforesaid matters, was approved by the Cabinet."
