    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Delegation of powers to District Secretaries to carry out the functions of the National Disaster Relief Services Centre more effectively and efficiently",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12291",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Disaster Management Center has been established in 1996, under the then Ministry of Social Services and Social Welfare, in order to plan and implement relief, rehabilitation and reconstruction activities, and the said Centre has been renamed as the National Disaster Relief Service Center from 2007\u201101\u201101 and so far it has been functioning as a Government institution. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Ministry of Defense to delegate the necessary powers to the District Secretaries/Government Agents so that the functions of the said Center can be carried out more effectively and efficiently, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Entering into a Treaty on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters \tbetween the Republic of Korea and Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12292",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been proposed to sign a Treaty between the Republic of Korea and the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters. Accordingly, a draft Treaty has been prepared jointly by a group of representatives consisting of senior officials of the Ministry of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Attorney General's Department and a group of representatives of relevant institutions of the Republic of Korea. It is expected to improve the effectiveness of crime prevention, investigation, prosecution and suppression of crime in both States. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to sign the said Treaty between the two parties and then ratify the same by respective Diplomatic Missions of the two countries,was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Signing a Record of Discussion (RoD) for the full implementation of the\tCommunity-Based Tourism Development Project focusing on the Central,\tNorthern and Eastern Provinces",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12293",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the Meeting held on 2023\u201101\u201109 to enter into a Record of Discussion between the Korea Tourism Organization and the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority for the implementation of a pilot project related to the implementation of a community-based tourism development project focusing on the Central, Northern and Eastern Provinces of Sri Lanka under a grant of 2.172 billion Korean Won.  Although, it had been planned to implement the entire project based on the success of the pilot project, after its implementation, the representatives of the Korea Tourism Organization after visiting the relevant provinces have agreed to implement the entire project as scheduled instead of a pilot project. Accordingly, the Cabinet having considered the matters submitted by the Minister of Tourism and Lands on the measures taken to enter into a revised Agreement between two parties enabling to implement the project, decided to grant the concurrence of the Cabinet to pursue action accordingly."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Establishment of an Inter-Ministerial Standing Committee on Human\tRights",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12294",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The necessity of appointing an Inter-Ministerial Standing Committee on Human Rights has been identified, enabling to act as a Standing National Framework for an effective domestic process of follow-up and reporting on Sri Lanka's undertakings on human rights and reconciliation. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish an Inter-Ministerial Standing Committee on Human Rights with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs acting as the coordinating/lead agency, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Establishment of a mechanism for expeditious decision making for the\timplementation of Renewable Energy Projects",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12295",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to meet the nationally determined contribution targets by the year 2030, the need to accelerate the implementation of renewable energy projects has been identified. At the Cabinet Meeting held on 2023\u201111\u201120, it was decided that a new mechanism should be introduced for the speedy implementation of renewable energy projects, taking into account the time it takes to implement such projects following the existing processes, as well as the inconveniences faced by the interested investors while working in accordance with such processes. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to appoint a Joint Standing Committee representing the following institutions to take decisions regarding renewable energy projects and to monitor the efficient and prompt implementation of those decisions by the relevant institutions:\n\n*\tPresidential Secretariat- (Chairman)\n\n*\tPrime Minister's Office\n\n*\tMinistry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies\n\n*\tMinistry of Investment Promotions\n\n*\tMinistry of Wildlife and Forest Resources Conservation\n\n*\tMinistry of Environment\n\n*\tMinistry of Tourism and Lands\n\n*\tMinistry of Industries\n\n*\tMinistry of Power and Energy\n*\tMinistry of Irrigation \n\n*\tMinistry of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development\n\n*\tSri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority\n\n*\tCeylon Electricity Board"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Appointment of an Authorized Representative to submit online Visa\tapplications of foreigners who visit Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12296",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- At the Cabinet Meeting held on 2023\u201109\u201111, it was decided to appoint an Evaluation Committee to evaluate the proposal submitted by GBS Technology Services & IVS Global - FZCO and VFS VF Worldwide Holdings Ltd., to act as an authorized representative for the online submission of visa applications for foreigners who visit Sri Lanka. The Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to pursue action as per the recommendations of the Report submitted by the Evaluation Committee appointed accordingly and to sign the relevant Agreement drafted as per the observations submitted by the Attorney General."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Acquisition of a land plot to the Sri Lanka Police for the establishment of \tthe Rangala Police Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12297",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Currently, the Rangala Police Station, which is run on rental basis in a building belonging to the Getagahawela Plantation Company, has found it difficult for the officers on duty to carry out their duties properly since it is not spacious enough. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Public Security to acquire a land plot of 02 acres from the Duckwariya Estate belonging to the Udapussellawa Plantation company to the Sri Lanka Police for the establishment of the Rangala Police Station, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
