    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- National competitive bids have been invited for the procurement of purchasing oil and lubricants for the Sri Lanka Transport Board. The Cabinet Appointed Standing Procurement Committee has recommended the purchase of respective oils and lubricants from Lanka IOC PLC and Chevron Lubricant Lanka PLC, based on each item. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport and Highways to award the relevant procurements to those two companies, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Conducting an investigation over the assassination of Mr. Edward Henry\tPedris 108 years ago by a judgment of the Colonial Military Court",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12300",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Mr. Edward Henry Pedris who was 27 years at the time, has been brought before a Court Martial on charges of inciting riots and treason against the Government by the colonial administration of Sri Lanka and convicted of treason and executed on 1915\u201107\u201107 without considering any appeal. The body of the late Mr. Henry Pedris has been cremated in an undisclosed premise following the procedure prescribed for the cremation of a convicted criminal under the Martial Law. His assassination has been later identified as a result of a plan carried out by the senior officers who administered the country at that time. Accordingly, the Cabinet approved the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint a committee comprising of three members which is chaired by retired Supreme Court Judge Mr. Anil Goonaratne, to disclose actual information related to the said execution, study relevant information and submit a Report with recommendations to the Cabinet in order to bring justice to him."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Amending the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance No.2 of 1937",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12301",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- More than 680 plant species belonging to 121 genera have been declared as protected plants in accordance with the plant classification systems coming under the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance No.2 of 1937 as was last amended by the Fauna and Flora Protection (Amendment) Act No.7 of 2022. However, the necessity to amend the said Schedule to suit the current day needs has been identified. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Resources Conservation to appoint a Committee consisting of experts in the fields of plant taxonomy and nomenclature, ecology, wildlife conservation and ethanobotany and to amend the Schedule VIII of the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance as per the recommendations of the said Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Amendments to the Partition Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12302",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201109\u201125 has granted approval to introduce appropriate amendments to the Partition Act in order to conclude the partition cases expeditiously. The clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill prepared by the Legal Draftsman accordingly. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and submit the same thereafter to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Introducing legal provisions to house arrest as an alternative to remand",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12303",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Overcrowding in prisons in Sri Lanka has been identified as a long-standing problem. As a remedy to that problem, a Committee headed by a Judge of the Supreme Court has been appointed to make suitable recommendations to introduce legal provisions to detain in appropriate cases suspects and convicts under House Arrest as an alternative to remand/imprisonment. The proposal made by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to introduce appropriate laws, based on the Report submitted by the said Official's Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Submission of the Order published in the Gazette under the Special Commodity Levy Act No.48 of 2007 to Parliament for approval",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12304",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201110\u201130 has granted approval to increase the Special Commodity Levy on importation of sugar from 25 cents to Rs.50/- per Kg. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to submit the Order imposed through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2356/20 dated 2023\u201111\u201101 under the provisions of section 2 of the Special Commodity Levy Act No.48 of 2007 to Parliament for approval in order to give effect the said decision, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "The 'Urumaya Programme' which endows Land Permit and Grant Holders the Absolute Ownership of State Lands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12305",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The General Public mainly the farmer community who have been given permits and grants under the Land Development Ordinance, have to encounter various issues in using the relevant land for human and development needs due to the absence of absolute ownership for the said land they possess or have developed. Therefore, the Hon. President, in the Budget Speech 2024, proposed to implement a programme called 'Urumaya Programme', enabling to take necessary action within the existing legal framework to grant the absolute ownerships of such lands to the general public mainly consisting of farmer community in order to minimize those issues and to commence the said arrangements at the beginning of the year 2024 and fully complete the same within few years. The said programme is planned to be implemented under three stages whereby the absolute ownership of residential and agricultural lands are expected to be given for two million families. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Tourism & Lands to issue a Grant with the absolute ownership under section 2 of the Land Development Ordinance for blocks of land for which Permits and Grants have been provided under the Land Development Ordinance by following the relevant steps, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Construction of Hybrid Renewable Energy Systems in Jaffna Small Islands",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12306",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of India has expressed its consent to provide a partial grant of US$ 11 million to provide electricity supply for occupants in the islands of Delft, Nainathivu and Analathivu in the Jaffna Peninsula. Accordingly, bids have been invited only from Indian Contractors to implement the said project as per the conditions of the Agreement entered into. As such, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the said Contract to M/s U-Solar Clean Energy Solutions (Pvt) Ltd., based on the recommendations submitted by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee by evaluating the proposal submitted for that, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-017-en",
    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "700MW Solar Power Project proposed to be installed on the surface of the Poonakary Tank",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12307",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201109\u201111 has granted approval to accept in principle the proposal submitted by M/s United Solar Energy SL (Pvt) Ltd,. to develop 700MW solar power plant with 100% Battery Energy Storage System including the construction of necessary transmission lines from the Poonakary tank to new Kilinochchi Grid Substation and to appoint a Cabinet Appointed Negotiating Committee in order to evaluate the project proposal and to submit recommendations to the Cabinet to determine the power purchasing charges. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to implement the proposed project with M/s United Solar Energy SL (Pvt) Ltd,. based on the recommendations submitted by the Negotiating Committee and to sign a power purchasing agreement related to that, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-018-en",
    "num": "18",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Amendments to the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12308",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2023\u201110\u201130 to amend the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002, making provisions to reduce the Value Added Tax registration threshold, the total value of the supplies that tax can be charged per year from Rs.80 million to Rs.60 million and to increase the VAT rate from 15% to 18%, with effect from 2024\u201101\u201101. The Legal Draftsman has drafted the amending Bill having incorporated relevant amendments and the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to publish the said amending Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-019-en",
    "num": "19",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Awarding the contract for the supply of Aviation Fuel for SriLankan \tAirlines Limited at Dammam (DMM) Airport",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12309",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract for the supply of aviation fuel at the Dammam Airport for the aircraft of SriLankan Airlines Limited is due to expire on 2023\u201112\u201131. Quotations have been called from Modern Consortium for Refueling Aircraft Co. Ltd., the only aviation fuel supplier there at present. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the relevant contract as a direct contract, as recommended by the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-020-en",
    "num": "20",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Awarding the Contracts for Supplying aviation fuel for SriLankan\tAirlines Limited at 09 Airports worldwide",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12310",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contracts for the supply of aviation fuel to Sri Lankan Airlines Limited at the airports of Bangkok, Beijing, Dubai, Hyderabad, Karachi, Male and Riyadh are to be expired on 2024\u201102\u201129, and the contracts for the supply of aviation fuel at the airports of Kuala Lumpur and Jakarta are due to expire on 2024\u201103\u201131. International competitive bids have been invited for the supply of fuel at those airports. Eleven (11) aviation fuel supply companies have submitted bids and one bid for Karachi airport and 02 or more bids for the remaining 8 airports. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the relevant contracts to the lowest evaluated substantially responsive bidders, as per the recommendations of the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-11-021-en",
    "num": "21",
    "date_str": "2023-12-11",
    "description": "Issuance of a New Order under section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act,\tNo.12 of 2017",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12311",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted to issue an Order under section 22 of the Foreign Exchange Act No.12 of 2017 enabling to temporarily suspend/limit certain outward remittances related to certain capital transactions and current transfers commencing from April 2020. After that, measures have been taken to extend the validity period of the said Order on several occasions, and the validity period of the current Order is due to expire on 2023\u201112\u201127. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to issue a new Order for a further period of 06 months to be effective from 2023\u201112\u201128 removing the existing suspension on making investment in Employee Share Ownership Plans or Employee Share Option Schemes by individual residents through Outward Investment Accounts while maintaining the suspensions/limitations stipulated in the prevailing Order, and to present the said Order for approval in Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-18-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2023-12-18",
    "description": "Entering into an Agreement with the British Council for a Pilot Project of training English Teachers in the Sabaragamuwa Province",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12312",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been planned to implement a capacity development program together with the British Council to provide formal training for English teachers in the Sabaragamuwa province and enhance their language knowledge and teaching skills. Under the said programme, it is expected to select 700 teachers and provide them with a formal training through the Teaching Knowledge Test (TKT) course affiliated with the Cambridge University. The proposed training program is to be implemented with the funds of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council, and a sum of Rs.51 million has been estimated for the purpose. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in his capacity as the Minister of Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Council and Local Government to enter into an Agreement between the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council and the British Council for the implementation of the said programme, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-18-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2023-12-18",
    "description": "Segregation of Insurance Business of the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12313",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet at its meeting held on 2023\u201103\u201113 has granted approval to take necessary action to operate the life and general insurance businesses of the Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation as separate legal entities in compliance with the provisions of the Regulation of Insurance Industry (Amendment) Act No. 3 of 2011 under the State enterprises restructuring. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to segregate the life and general insurance businesses of Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation Limited to the fully owned subsidiaries of the said Corporation, Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation Life Limited and Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation General Limited, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
