    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Due to the absence of sufficient stocks of maize in the open market, there is a shortage of raw materials required for the production of poultry feed. As a temporary measure, the Department of Animal Production and Health has issued the required license to Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Limited to import 15,000 Metric Tons of maize. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Development to procure maize from registered foreign suppliers by the Sri Lanka State Trading (General) Corporation Limited, subject to a maximum of 15,000 Metric Tons, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-18-006-en",
    "num": "6",
    "date_str": "2023-12-18",
    "description": "Granting compensation to the selected families who were deprived of lands owing to construction of Yan Oya Reservoir and the Left Bank Canal, in place of alternative paddy lands to be granted",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12317",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the construction of the Yan Oya Reservoir, lands belonging to the Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Horowpathana and Gomarankadawala have been acquired and the lands belonging to the Divisional Secretariat Divisions of Horowpathana, Padaviya and Sri-pura have been acquired during the construction of Left Bank Canal. Alternative paddy lands have been granted to a part of the families who have deprived their lands and owing to the non availability of lands in the surrounding area to develop as paddy lands, approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2023\u201103\u201120 to grant an additional compensation to the land owners whose lands have been acquired. Accordingly, approval of the Cabinet was granted to implement the following proposals made by the Minister of Irrigation.\n\n* \tSince it is not possible to get released sufficient lands to be granted as alternative paddy lands for the selected families who lost their houses owing to the construction of the Yan Oya Reservoir, for development purposes, payment of a compensation of Rs.1.8 million each, in place of lands for the families to whom alternative paddy lands have not been given so far and who are residing in other areas and whose livelihood is not farming. \n\n*\tSince it is not possible to get released sufficient lands to be granted a alternative paddy lands for the selected families who lost their house owing to the construction of the Left Bank Canal, for development purposes, payment of compensation of 1.8 million rupees in lieu of a 1 1/2 acre paddy field."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2023-12-18-007-en",
    "num": "7",
    "date_str": "2023-12-18",
    "description": "Establishing Training/Migration Resource Centres in Jaffna, Homagama and Ampara areas for Overseas Job Seekers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12318",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2023-12-18 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment conducts accelerated, host\u2011country specific training programmes for overseas job seekers. Currently, these training programmes are conducted under minimum facilities at rented out buildings in islandwide. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Labor and Foreign Employment to establish Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment's training centres in the areas of Jaffna, Homagama and Ampara to provide necessary training for overseas job seekers, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
