    "doc_id": "2024-01-01-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2024-01-01",
    "description": "Development of 61 oil storage tanks in the Upper Tank Farm at China Bay, Trincomalee on Build, Operate and Transfer (BOT) basis Business Model",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12341",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Upper Tank Farm at China Bay, Trincomalee consists of 99 fuel storage tanks, and as decided at the Cabinet meeting held on 2022\u201101\u201103, approval has been granted to lease out 61 tanks from among them to Trinco Petroleum Terminal (Pvt.) Ltd., for a period of 50 years. The initial steps have already been commenced including carrying out a feasibility study for the development of said 61 oil tanks. The feasibility study has recommended to develop this project under 07 phases within 16 years, and under the first phase, it has been planned to refurbish 09 tanks which are economically viable, installation of a pipeline with a length of 1.75 km, and construct other allied facilities. It has been proposed to follow the business model of Build, Operate and Transfer (BOT) for the implementation of this project. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to follow the relevant procurement process in order to select a suitable investor to implement the proposed development plan to be carried out under the first phase, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-01-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2024-01-01",
    "description": "Implementation of the Electronic Transactions (e-Grama Niladari Information System) Regulations No.01 of 2022",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12342",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Electronic Transactions (e\u2011Grama Niladari Information System) Regulations No. 01 of 2022 made by the Minister of Technology under the provisions of the Electronic Transactions Act No.19 of 2006 have been published in the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2311/40 dated 2022\u201112\u201122. According to the said Regulations, facilities will be provided to use electronic documents and electronic records for the efficient delivery of services through the respective District Secretariats, Divisional Secretariats and the Grama Niladhari Officers. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Technology to submit the said Regulation to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-01-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2024-01-01",
    "description": "Preparation of the Reforestation and Tree Cover Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12343",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, Sri Lanka has agreed to increase the forest cover of Sri Lanka to 32% of its total land area by the year 2030, and to increase the amount of carbon sequestrated by forests by 7% over the current situation. For that purpose, afforestation, replacement of degraded forests, and increase of forest cover in Government and private lands outside the forest are currently being carried out. These tree planting programmes are carried out with the participation of various parties, and although their benefits accrue to the entire nation, it has been recognized that the benefits of tree planting should be shared among all the parties who contributed to it, in order to encourage them. Currently, there are no legal provisions to provide products such as fruits, leaves, flowers, wood, resin obtained by tree planting in public places to the stakeholders who contributed to tree planting. Also, it has been identified the suitability of establishing a National Tree Planting Fund in order to have the support of the private sector, non-Governmental organizations and international organizations to obtain funds for the implementation of tree planting activities more effectively. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Wildlife and Forest Resources Conservation to introduce a new Act called \"Reforestation and Tree Cover Act\" incorporating provisions relating to the said tasks, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-01-015-en",
    "num": "15",
    "date_str": "2024-01-01",
    "description": "Implementation of an International Application to Person (A2P) SMS Digital Hub",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12344",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- A2P is a communication model and an application, typically a computer programme or software that sends messages or notifications to individuals or end\u2011users. Short Message Service (SMS) is a critical communication medium for citizens, businesses and government agencies and is widely used for a various purposes, including business and transaction evaluations. These messages are delivered to a mobile device by an individual through an application or system, such as text messages (SMS), multimedia messages (MMS) or other forms of messaging. It has been observed that the widespread use of SMS services leads to fraud, spam and unauthorized activities. In order to face such challenges, it has been found the necessity of having a centralized SMS Firewall solution for the regulation of SMS exchanges. Accordingly, Infobip, a private company based in the United Kingdom, has submitted a proposal for the implementation of an international A2P digital SMS hub and the proposal made by the Hon. President to appoint a Technical Committee comprising of representatives from the Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policy, Ministry of Technology and the Telecommunications Regulatory Commission of Sri Lanka to evaluate the said proposal and submit recommendations, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "The recommendations submitted to the Hon. President by the Finance \tCommission for 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12345",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Finance Commission has been established in terms of the Article 154R of the Constitution to assess the funds adequate for the Provincial Councils and to submit recommendations to apportioning the funds allocated for the Provincial Councils from the National Budget more meaningfully among the Provincial Councils  with the aim of achieving a balanced regional development in the country. The Cabinet granted approval for the following recommendations submitted to the Hon. President by the Commission for 2024.\n\n    \u2022 Recommendations pertaining to the assessment of provincial capital and recurrent needs for 2024.\n    \u2022 Recommendations pertaining to the apportionment of public grants among the Provincial Councils for 2024.\n    \u2022 Policy recommendations pertaining to meaningful allocation of resources for the Provincial Councils and use of such resources more effectively.\n\n      In addition, the Cabinet approval was also granted to submit the Report of the Finance Commission with recommendations submitted by the same Commission for 2024 to the Parliament in terms of the provisions of paragraph (7) of Article 154R of the Constitution."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-002-en",
    "num": "2",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "The Anuradhapura Maha Vihara Development Plan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12346",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Since the Maha Viharaya in Anuradhapura is a place with significant religious and historical importance in Sri Lanka, it has been identified the need to implement the exploration and conservation activities of the Maha Viharaya in a formal manner within a specific time frame. Accordingly, upon the notification of Hon. President,  Prof. Robbin Coningham, a senior foreign expert with international experience in the field of archaeology has submitted a project report on implementation of  the exploration, excavation and conservation project of the Maha Vihara. Through the said project report, it has been proposed to implement this project within a time period of 6 years from 2024 to 2029. The proposal made by the Hon. President to implement the exploration, excavation and conservation activities of the Maha Viharaya as per the project report of Prof. Robbin Coningham, jointly by the Presidential Secretariat and the Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural affairs under the direct supervision of the Department of Archaeology and the Central Cultural Fund, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-003-en",
    "num": "3",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of a University of Science and Teachnology in Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12347",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- With the objective of preparing the foundation to create a cadre of skilled\tprofessionals to take the leadership in critical sectors of new scientific \tdiscoveries, technological  innovation and sustainable development, it has been \tidentified the appropriateness of establishing a University of Science and \tTechnology in collaboration with a renowned university in United States of \tAmerica. Such a university will cater to utilize cutting-edge methodologies, \tfoster global \tacademic connections and create an environment for research and \tdevelopment. The  proposal made by the Hon. President to select one partner \tuniversity from among several identified universities including UC Berkeley, \tUC Riverside, UC Davis, University of Michigan and establish the proposed \tUniversity of Science and Technology as a Public-Private Partnership in \tcollaboration with the said university, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-004-en",
    "num": "4",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of new Investment Zones",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12348",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In the Budget Speech 2022, it was emphasized the need to create an integrated mechanism between the public and private sectors to build up an export-oriented economy. Accordingly, it has been identified the appropriateness of developing the new Investment Zones as follows.\n\n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in the Northern, Eastern, North-Western and Southern Provinces.\n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in Mankulam, Paranthan Chemicals Company premises and Kankesanthurai Cement Corporation premises. \n    \u2022 Establishment of new Investment Zones in Iranawila and Trincomalee areas.\n    \u2022 Expansion of the existing Investment Zones in Bingiriya and Hambantota.\n\nThe Asian Development Bank has agreed to provide technical assistance for the establishment of the proposed economic zones. Accordingly,  the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Investment Promotion to develop the said Investment Zones based on a suitable Public-Private Partnership model, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2024-01-08-005-en",
    "num": "5",
    "date_str": "2024-01-08",
    "description": "Establishment of a Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12349",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-01-08 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to further develop the existing diplomatic relations between Kazakhstan and Sri Lanka, it has been recognized that it is appropriate to establish a Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan. The establishment of the  Secretariat of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) in Kazakhstan and Sri Lanka being a member of that Conference provide Sri Lanka a great opportunity to engage with the Central Asian Region. Also, since there it indicates a significant increase in tourist arrivals from Kazakhstan to Sri Lanka, the establishment of an embassy of Sri Lanka in Astana will help to further promote tourism and cultural cooperation between the two countries. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to establish the proposed Sri Lankan Embassy in Astana, Kazakhstan, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
