    "num": "8",
    "date_str": "2024-03-11",
    "description": "Donation of Japanese Yen One Thousand and Six Hundred Million (JPY1600 million) by the Government of Japan under the Japanese Economic and Social Development Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12442",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-03-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- During the present economic crisis in Sri Lanka, the Government of Japan has extended its cooperation by providing instant humanitarian assistance for the affected community and empowering the public sector. Accordingly, the  Government of Japan has agreed to award Japanese Yen One Thousand and Six Hundred Million (approximately LKR 3.3 billion) in order to implement the following projects under the Japanese Economic and Social Development Programme.\n\n\t\ti.\tThe project for improving oil spill response and management of \t\tthe Sri Lanka coast guard\n\n\t\tii.\tThe project for the provision of supportive equipment for \t\t\tmaternal and pediatric care at major hospitals in the Northern \t\tProvince and equipping dressmaker courses at vocational training \t\tcentres in the Northern Province.\n\n\t\tiii.\tThe project for the provision of supportive equipment for the \t\tsafety of fishermen in the Northern and Eastern Provinces.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to sign the Exchange of Notes and other related documents with the Government of Japan to obtain grant assistance under the Japanese Economic and Social Development Programme. for the implementation of the above projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
