    "description": "Payment of Wages for Plantation Workers",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12557",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-05-22 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the Government has recently announced an increase in daily wage for plantation workers, some plantation companies have made representations to the Government on the inability to pay the increased wages. Taking into consideration the said situation, the proposal made by the Hon. President to take the  following measures, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n(i) \tTo estimate the minimum wage be paid to a plantation worker by the \tMinistry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, \ttaking \tinto account the current cost of living and the impact of the recent \teconomic crisis.\n\n(ii)\tTo appoint a Committee to examine the capacity of each Plantation \tCompany \ton the payment of the salary so estimated.\n\n(iii)\tFurther, if any company fails to pay salaries due to its poor management,\tto \ttake necessary action to introduce laws enabling to cancel the Land \tLease \tAgreements entered into with such companies."
  },
