    "description": "Issuance of Import Control Regulations under Imports and Export (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 to enable the import of selected spices for reprocessing and re-exporting for businesses approved by the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12579",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-06-11 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Secretary, Ministry of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies, the Secretary, Ministry of Investment Promotion and the Secretary, Ministry of Agriculture and Plantation Industries have been informed to re-review the Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations No.03 of 2024 issued under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 and submit a Comprehensive Report, at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024 03 18. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to implement the following recommendations included in the above Report, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tAllow importation of selected spices for processing and re exporting for BOI approved enterprises under the Procedure for Importation and Processing of selected spices and re exporting in the form of oil extracts, Oleoresins and Spent.\n\n*\tPromulgate Imports and Exports (Control) Regulations under the provisions of the Imports and Exports (Control) Act, No.1 of 1969 for the above purpose."
  },
