    "description": "Completion of the remaining works of the Construction Projects of the Sri Lanka Police",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12615",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-06-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although a number of construction projects have been started with the aim of providing the necessary infrastructure for the Sri Lanka Police, the following projects scheduled to be completed in the years 2021 - 2023 could not be completed as expected due to the spread of COVID - 19 pandemic in the year 2020 and the economic crisis which has arisen in the country:\n\n*\tProject for the construction of Married Quarters for Junior Police Officers at Kumaran Ratnam Road, Colombo 02.\n\n*\tProject for the construction of Resident Building at the Katana National Police Academy.\n\n*\tProject for the completion of remaining works of the building in the Kollupitiya Police Station.\n\n\tThe proposal made by Minister of Public Security to revise the total cost estimate \tand to extend time period of completing projects up to 2024\u20112027, so as to \tcomplete the remaining works of the said projects, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
