    "num": "17",
    "date_str": "2024-07-01",
    "description": "Third Amendment of the Assistance Agreement No.383-128 signed with the Government of the United States of America",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12635",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-01 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Government of Sri Lanka and the Government of the United States of\tAmerica have entered into an Assistance Agreement on 2022-08-31 to obtain a\tGrant to finance the \u201cProgramme for a Democratic, Prosperous and Resilient\tSri Lanka\u201d and has granted USD 9.069 million to Sri Lanka accordingly. The\tvalue of the grant has been revised up to USD 28.299 million in 2023, in 02\toccassions.The United States Agency for International Development (USAID)\thas proposed to further increase the value of the Grant up to USD 52.835\tmillion. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity\tas the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to\tamend the Assistance Agreement by increasing the Grant Fund under the\t\u201cProgramme for a Democratic, Prosperous and Resilient Sri Lanka\u201d up to USD \t52.835 million, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
