    "description": "Commission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka Bill",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12713",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-07-29 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2024\u201107\u201115 to prepare a new Bill by amending the Commission for Truth, Unity and Reconciliation in Sri Lanka Bill, taking into account the  facts presented by the interested parties regarding the said Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. Therefore, the joint proposal made by the President in his capacity as the Minister of Defence; the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and Constitutional Reforms; and the Minister of Foreign Affairs, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter, present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
