    "description": "Revision of Water Tariff",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12753",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-12 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Water Supply and Drainage Board has been implementing the existing water Tariff from 2023\u201108\u201101 and approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2024\u201107\u201115 to review the tariff system and implement the tariff policy and formula. Since the electricity charges have been reduced by the Ceylon Electricity Board from 2024\u201107\u201116 and considering the reduction in the cost of fuel, chemicals and interest, there is a possibility of reducing the water charges by a certain percentage. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Water Supply and Estate Infrastructure Development to revise the water charges as mentioned below, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\n\nNo\nTariff Group\nproposed average reduction (%)\n\n\n\n\n1\nDomestic other than Samurdhi Recipients and Tenement Garden\n7\n\n\n2\nGovernment Hospitals\n4.5\n\n\n3\nSchools and Charitable Institutions\n6.3\n\n\n\n\nOverall Average Reduction\n5.94"
  },
