    "description": "Awarding Contracts for Passenger and Ramp Handling Services of SriLankan Airlines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12759",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The contract for passenger and Ramp Handling Services at Dammam, Jeddah and Riyadh airports in Saudi Arabia is due to expire on 2024\u201112\u201131, while the contract for passenger and Ramp Handling Services at the Guangzhou Airport in China is due to expire on 2025\u201101\u201131. Therefore, bids have been called under the limited international bidding procedure to select suitable service providers. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the relevant contracts to the following service providers who have substantially responded for a contract period of 03 years, as recommended by the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, having evaluated the bids received, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tto award the contracts for Dammam, Jeddah and Riyadh in Saudi Arabia to Swissport Saudi Arabia Limited.\n\n*\tto award the contract for Guangzhou Airport in China to Guangzhoe International Airport Co. Ltd."
  },
