    "description": "Entering into a Memorandum of Undertanding between the United\tNations Institute for Training and Research and the Ministry of Foreign\tAffairs",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12775",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-08-26 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The proposal made by the Minister of Foreign Affairs to enter into a Memorandum of Undertanding between the United Nations Institute for Training and Research and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for a period of 03 years with the aim of establishing a cooperative framework necessary for facilitation of mutual benefits in the following areas, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n* \tTraining and learning support related to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.\n\n* \tTraining of Diplomats in areas such as conferences, diplomacy and multilateral negotiations, skills development in communication, mediation and leadership, content-based workshops and specialized courses in climate change and human rights.\n\n* \tConducting Trainings by the UNITAR Operational Satellite Applications Programme (UNOSAT) on the use of Geo\u2011information technologies (GIS) for disaster risk reduction and crisis management."
  },
