    "description": "Awarding the Contracts for supplying of Aviation fuel for SriLankan Airlines",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12790",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-02 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The current operational contracts for aviation fuel supply at Frankfurt (FRA),\tIncheon (ICN), Melbourne (MEL) and Sydney (SYD) airports are due to expire on 31 \tOctober 2024. Therefore, limited international bids have been\tinvited to select the \tsuitable suppliers of the said airports for a period of 02 years and for which 08 \taviation fuel supplying companies have submitted bids. Accordingly, the proposal \tmade by the Minister of Ports, Shipping and Aviation to award the aircraft fuel supply \tcontracts as follows, based on the\trecommendations of the Technical Evaluation \tCommittee and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was \tapproved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\n\nAirport\nName of Contractor\n\n\n\n\n* Frankfurt (FRA)\nVitol Aviation BV\n\n\n* Incheon (ICN)\nWorld Fuel Services Trading DMCC\n\n\n* Sydney (SYD)\nVitol Aviation BV\n\n\n* Melbourne (MEL)\nVitol Aviation BV"
  },
