    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited for the development of projects up to 165MW for 20 grid substations, and the approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201109\u201102 to award the contracts for other locations except for Anuradhapura, Galle and Deniyaya grid substations. The appeals submitted by the unsuccessful bidders for the Anuradhapura, Galle and Deniyaya grid substations have been rejected by the Procurement Appeal Board. Accordingly, based on the recommendations of the Cabinet Appointed Negotiation Committee, the proposal made by the Minister of Power and Energy to award the relevant contracts as mentioned below, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\n\nLocation\nCapacity (MW)\nContractor\n\n\n\n\nAnuradhapura grid substation\n3\nFentons Smart Facilities (Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\n3\nHayleys Fentons Limited\n\n\n2\nNanila Publication (Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\n2\nCeylex Renewables (Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\nGalle grid substation\n1\nAustral Solar (Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\nDeniyaya grid substation\n3\nFortune Green (Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\n5\nSolar One Asia(Pvt) Ltd.\n\n\n2\nAustral Solar (Pvt) Ltd."
