    "description": "Removal of the temporary suspension on the importation of Motor Vehicles",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12825",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-09-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- As a measure to reduce the increasing pressure on the country's foreign exchange market and to ensure the distribution of available foreign exchange for the importation of essential goods including medicine, fuel and food, the importation of non-essential goods has been temporarily suspended from March 2020. In view of the recovery of the economy with the reform measures agreed under the Extended Fund Facility Programme of the International Monetary Fund, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization and National Policies to lift the temporary import suspension related to the importation of motor vehicles and non-motorized goods classified under 304 HS Codes, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import vehicles used for public passenger transportation, vehicles used for special purposes and other non\u2011motorized goods to be effective from 2024\u201110\u201101.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import vehicles used for commercial or goods transportation to be effective from 2024\u201112\u201101.\n\n*\tGranting permission to import motor vehicles used for personal purpose (Cars, Vans, Sport Utility Vehicles, Pickups etc.) to be effective from 2025\u201102\u201101."
  },
