    "description": "Programme for the revival of the fishery sector by mitigating the impact caused to the fishery industry due to the economic crisis",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12857",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-10-14 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although the approval had been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2024\u201108\u201121 to address the adverse impact caused to the fishery industry due to the significant increase of fuel price, the said decision has not been implemented as of now. Therefore, the proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Agriculture, lands, Livestock, Irrigation, Fisheries and Aquatic Resources to provide the following concessions for a period of 06 months effective from 2024\u201110\u201101, with a view to uplifting the economic condition of fishermen, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tTo grant \u201can allowance for the revival of the fishery industry\u201d for the vessel owners who use diesel as fuel in such a way as to receive a sum of R.25/- per liter of diesel they purchase, subject to a maximum of Rs. 300,000/- per month.\n\n*\tTo grant \u201can allowance for the revival of the fishery industry\u201d for the vessel owners who use kerosene as a fuel in such a way as to receive a sum of R.25/- per each liter they purchase, subject to a maximum of 15 liters per day and for a maximum period of 25 days in a month, limiting it only for working days.\n\n*\tTo maintain this programme so that fishermen receive a maximum concession of 7.5% for diesel from market price and a maximum concession of 12.5% for kerosene from market price for a maximum period of 6 months, subject to the limit of maximum concessionary price of Rs. 150 for kerosene and a maximum concessionary price of Rs. 250 for diesel, whenever the prices of diesel and kerosene are revised."
  },
