    "doc_id": "2024-10-28-001-en",
    "num": "1",
    "date_str": "2024-10-28",
    "description": "Introduction of a Dispute Prevention and Resolution Mechanism to the Public Service",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12874",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-10-28 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval of the Cabinet has been granted at the meeting held on 2023\u201111\u201120 to introduce a Dispute Prevention and Resolution Mechanism in the Public Service. Accordingly, the Public Administration Circular No. 05/2024 has been issued to implement the Dispute Resolution Mechanism in the entire Public Service. By the aforesaid Cabinet decision, approval has been granted to obtain technical and expert assistance of the International Labour Organization and in order to implement the said Mechanism, the International Labour Organization has requested project support from the United Nations Secretary General's Fund for Peacebuilding. Accordingly, US$ 2 million has been granted for the two programmes called \u201cPublic Sector Social Dialogue Programme\u201d and \u201cSocial Dialogue Promotion Programme in the Private and Informal Economic Sectors\u201d under the new project named \u201cSocial Dialogue for Peace and Crisis Prevention in Sri Lanka\u201d. Cabinet noted the facts submitted by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Justice, Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Labour stating that measures are being taken to implement the said programmes by an Inter-Sectoral Steering Committee co-chaired by the Secretary, Ministry of Justice, Public Administration, Home Affairs, Provincial Councils, Local Government and Labour and the Resident Coordinator of the United Nations."
  },
