    "description": "Procurement for the operation of Currency Exchange Counters at the Departure Walkway of the Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12883",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2024-11-05 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Bids have been invited from Licensed Commercial Banks, Licensed Specialized Banks and Limited Registered Dealers in Foreign Currency Business approved by the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, following the Limited National Competitive Bidding Procedure in order to operate 05 Currency Exchange Counters at the Departure Walkway of the Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake. Bids have been submitted by 05 Institutions for the same. Accordingly, the recommendation made by the Minister of Transport, Highways and Civil Aviation to assign the operation of Currency Exchange Counters to the following Institutions for a period of 03 years, based on the recommendations of the Technical Evaluation Committee and the Standing Cabinet Appointed Procurement Committee, was approved by the Cabinet. \n\n*\tCounter No:25 - Bank of Ceylon for a sum of LKR 798.028 million + Taxes\n\n*\tCounter No:02 - Sampath Bank PLC for a sum of LKR 633.662 million + Taxes\n\n*\tCounter No:04 - Commercial Bank of Ceylon PLC for a sum of LKR 381.364 million + Taxes\n\n*\tCounter No:10 - Thomas Cook Lanka (Pvt) Limited for a sum of LKR 299.064 million + Taxes\n\n*\tCounter No:11- Hatton National Bank PLC for a sum of LKR 225.689 million + Taxes"
  },
