    "date_str": "2025-01-06",
    "description": "Granting of incentives for the promotion of International Airports in the Country",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=12974",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-01-06 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Airport & Aviation Services (Sri Lanka) (Pvt.) Ltd. has introduced Concessionary Schemes for International Airlines with the aim of attracting International Airlines to Jaffna International Airport, Colombo International Airport (Ratmalana) and Mattala Rajapakse International Airport. Under this, the proposal made by the Minister of Transport, Highways, Ports and Civil Aviation to further extend the concessions provided for the Embarkation Levy for these Airports as follows, was approved by the Cabinet.\n* Extension of the concession of 50% of the existing Embarkation Levy for the Airlines operating scheduled flights to Jaffna International Airport for another 01 year up to 2026-01-30.\n* Extension of the concession of 50% of the existing Embarkation Levy for the Airlines operating scheduled flights to Colombo International Airport (Ratmalana) for a period of one year from 2025-03-27.\n* Extension of the full concession of the existing Embarkation Levy for the \tAirlines operating scheduled flights to Mattala Rajapakse International Airport for another year from 2024\u201112\u201129."
  },
  {
