    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-21 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Anti-Corruption Act, No.9 of 2023, has been enacted to give effect to certain provisions of the United Nations Convention against Corruption and other internationally recognized norms, standards and best practices and to provide for the establishment of an independent Commission to detect and investigate allegations of bribery, corruption and offenses related to the declaration of assets and liabilities and associated offenses. The Minister shall make Regulations in consultation with the Commission, in respect of matters required by the Act to be prescribed or in respect of which Regulations are authorized to be made. Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2025\u201103\u201117 to publish the Regulations so made in consultation with the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, in the Government Gazette. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Justice and National Integration to submit the Anti-Corruption (Declaration of Assets and Liabilities) Regulations 2025 published through the Extraordinary Gazette Notification No.2428/43 dated 2025\u201103\u201120, for approval of Parliament, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
