    "date_str": "2025-04-28",
    "description": "Introducing new Laws and amendments to the existing Acts in respect of the scope of the Ministry of Plantation and Community Infrastructure",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13144",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-04-28 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- It has been identified the need of amending the existing Acts and formulation of new Acts within the year 2025 in accordance with the priorities of Government policies related to the scope of the Ministry of Plantations and Community Infrastructure. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Plantations and Community Infrastructure to incorporate the introducing of the following new laws and the amendment of the Acts, in the Legislation Programme of the Government for the year 2025, was approved by the Cabinet:\n\n* Amendments to the Tea, Rubber and Coconut Estates (Control of Fragmentation) Act, No. 2 of 1958\n* Amendments to the Saumyamoorthi Thondaman Memorial Foundation Act, No. 19 of 2005\n* Amendments to the Tea Shakthi Fund Act, No. 47 of 2000\n* Amendments to the Tea Control Act, No. 51 of 1957\n* Amendments to the Rubber Control Act, No. 11 of 1956\n* Introduction of a new Act as the Plantation Management Act\n* Introduction of a new Act to assign the authority of the Thurusaviya\t Societies to the Rubber Development Department\n* Making amendments to the Coconut Development Act, No. 46 of 1971 enabling to introduce new Regulations to the Act, based on the current needs.\n* Making amendments to the Sri Lanka Tea Board Act, No. 14 of 1975 and related Regulations."
  },
