    "description": "Amendment of the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects (SLIA) Law No.1 of 1976",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13226",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-06-09 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Sri Lanka Institute of Architects, the sole body established in Sri Lanka for the profession of Architecture, its practice and education of Architecture has been incorporated by the provisions of the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects Law, No. 1 of 1976, amended by the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects (Amendment) Act, No. 14 of 1996. In order to cope with the current context of professional practices, the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects has proposed to amend the relevant sections of the Principal Act, \u201cPractice in Architecture and Membership and Use of Titles\u201d. Accordingly, approval has been granted by the Cabinet of Ministers on 2023-04-17 to prepare a Bill for the relevant purpose. As per the said approval, the proposal made by the Minister of Urban Development, Construction and Housing to grant policy approval of the present Cabinet of Ministers to complete the preparation of the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects (Amendment) Bill, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
