    "description": "Declaration of \"a National Children's Day Week\"",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13435",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-15 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Many countries, including Sri Lanka, celebrate 1st October as the \"World Children's Day\". This year, under the theme \"Protect with Love - To Conquer the World\", all institutions dealing with children have jointly planned to implement a series of national programmes for World Children's Day under the guidance of the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs and organization of the Department of Probation and Child Protection Services. The proposal made by the Minister of Women and Child Affairs to declare a \"National Children's Day Week\" starting from 2025-09-25 ending as at 2025-10-01, including the main national celebration and to implement the following programmes under the same, in parallel to national programmes for World Children's Day, was approved by the Cabinet.\n\n\n\nDate\nProgramme\n\n\n\n\n2025-09-25\nRaising awareness on the role of Principals in safeguarding children's rights - (Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education)\n\n\n2025-09-26\nInspection of vehicles transporting school children islandwide and application of stickers - (Sri Lanka Police, National Child Protection Authority, National Transport Commission)\n\nEstablishment and reorganization of school child protection committees - (Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education, National Child Protection Authority)\n\n\n2025-09-27\nRaising awareness among school authorities on the role of teachers in safeguarding children's rights - (National Secretariat for Early Childhood Development)\n\n\n2025-09-28\nRaising community awareness on preventing children from substance abuse - (Sri Lanka Police, National Dangerous Drugs Control Board, Alcohol and Drug Information Centre)\n\n\n2025-09-29\nRaising awareness on the role of religious leaders in safeguarding children's rights - (Ministry of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs)\n\n\nConducting family-based recreational programmes - (Department of Cultural Affairs)\n\n\n2025-09-30\nHealth promotion programmes (Grade 1-5) - (Ministry of Health and Mass Media, Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education)\n\n\n2025-10-01\nNational Celebration of World Children's Day\n\n\nDuring the entire week\nIdentification of vulnerable children and conducting relevant inspections of street children - (Sri Lanka Police)"
  },
