    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-10-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Students of the Faculty of Medicine of the Wayamba University of Sri Lanka, established in Kuliyapitiya, carry out their hospital\u001ebased training at the Kurunegala Teaching Hospital. Since the Wayamba University does not have a hostel in the vicinity of the Kurunegala Teaching Hospital to provide hostel facilities to the Medical Students belonging to 03 academic groups, those students have to arrange residential facilities by themselves. Therefore, construction of a hostel in a safe place where those students can have easy access to the Kurunegala Teaching Hospital during the day and night has become a prime requirement. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister in her capacity as the Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education to vest a state-owned block of land in extent of 80 perches located in the Kurunegala West Grama Niladhari Division of the Kurunegala Divisional Secretariat Division, which has been identified for the construction of the said hostel, with the Wayamba University of Sri Lanka as a free Grant under section 6(1) of the State Land Ordnance, was approved by the Cabinet."
