    "description": "Development of the product filling facilities at Zone 7 at the Kolonnawa Installation of Ceylon Petroleum Storage Terminals Limited",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13491",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-10-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Board of Directors of Ceylon Petroleum Terminal Company Limited has approved the development of the product filling facilities in Zone 7 at the Kolonnawa Terminal of Ceylon Petroleum Terminal Company Limited under 03 phases. The Department of National Planning has recommended the implementation of the proposed project. It has been estimated that, the cost for the total design of the state-of-the-art filling facilities for petrol, diesel and kerosene in Zone 7 at the Kolonnawa Terminal and construction of the Gasoline Filling facility Phase -1 at the said zone, as Rs.1.455 million + taxes. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to implement Phase- 1 of the project of the Development of the product filling facilities at Zone 7 at the Kolonnawa Terminal and to commence the procurement process for the said project as an Engineering, Procurement, Construction and Commissioning contract, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-10-13-016-en",
    "num": "16",
    "date_str": "2025-10-13",
    "description": "Amendments to the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No.11 of 2021",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13492",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-10-13 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Colombo Port City has been established as a Special Economic Zone under the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No.11 of 2021. The Colombo Port City Economic Commission has identified the legal amendments required to achieve the objectives of the Act, such as making the said zone a globally competitive Special Economic Zone, attracting foreign direct investments and strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s overall global ranking in the ease of doing business. Accordingly, the approval of the Cabinet had been granted on 2024\u001e07\u001e29 for amending the relevant Act, and several new amendments to be made have been identified as of now. Furthermore, since the strategic Business Regulations that granted very important incentives and exemptions to investors in the Port City have been repealed with effect from 2025\u001e08\u001e04, the proposed new provisions are also expected to directly address the problems of those investors. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to amend the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act, No. 11 of 2021, incorporating the newly identified amendments, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-10-13-017-en",
