    "description": "Signing of the End-User and Handover Agreement between the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC) and the Ministry of Defence for the Provision of Satellite Communication Intercept Equipment to the Sri Lanka Navy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13537",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime with financial and technical support of the Government of Japan and expertise from the Japan Coast Guard, is implementing the project titled \u2018Strengthening Maritime Security and the Rule of Law at Sea in the Indo-Pacific Region\u2019 from 2024. Under the said Project, it has been agreed to provide \u2018Cognyte S12\u2019 Satellite Communication Interception System to the Sri Lanka Navy. Enhancing the maritime security activities through preventing, countering and disrupting terrorist activities, organized crimes, drug trafficking and other serious illegal activities are expected through this. Further, this will enable to strengthen the Sri Lanka\u2019s contribution towards regional and international maritime security initiatives. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister Defence to sign the End-User and Handover Agreement between the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime and the Ministry of Defence to obtain the said System to the country, was approved by the Cabinet."
