    "date_str": "2025-11-03",
    "description": "Amendment of the National Tariff Policy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13548",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2024 06 11, has granted approval for the National Tariff Policy aimed at establishing a transparent and predictable tariff regime to position Sri Lanka as a competitive trade and investment hub. The National Tariff Policy Committee was established on 2025 05 15 to implement the said policy. In the light of the subsequent Government policy amendments, the National Tariff Policy Committee has identified the need to amend certain provisions of the National Tariff Policy to ensure alignment with certain tax legislation and to eliminate ambiguities. The proposal made by the Hon. President in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning and Economic Development to amend the National Tariff Policy based on the amendments identified accordingly, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-03-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2025-11-03",
    "description": "Procedure of granting provisions for selected project proposals under the \u2018National Initiative for Research and Development Commercialization\u2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13549",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- In order to expedite the implementation of the production economy policy of the present government, a provision of Rs. 01 billion has been allocated in the 2025 Budget for the commercialization of processes that bring forth new ideas, methods, products, services or solutions with a significant positive impact and value through research and development. Accordingly, a dedicated unit called the \u2018National Initiative for Research and Development Commercialization' has been established under the Presidential Secretariat, enabling to evaluate the technical and economic potential of the projects and set up a proper investor friendly path for the implementation of those projects thereby contributing to the development of the country. As of now, applications worth about Rs. 2.2 billion have been submitted by local researchers and entrepreneurs to the said unit. The unit has taken steps to prepare a methodology called \u2018National Initiative for Research and Development Commercialization' to evaluate project proposals under 02 main phases namely Technical Evaluation and Administrative Evaluation in order to select the most economically, socially and environmentally effective projects from among the applications. Accordingly, measures will be taken to classify unique and essential projects through the proposed evaluation process as well as to identify projects that make a high contribution to economic progress. Based on the viability of the projects selected from the projects thus evaluated, Grants will be provided as follows:\n\n*\tThe maximum Grant amount is Rs.50 million\n\n*\tA Grant amount to a maximum of Rs.10 million will be granted from the approved Grant amount, depending on the viability of the project.\n\n*\tThe balance provided in addition to the grant amount should be settled as 25% of from the annual net profit after a grace period of one year.\n\n*\tThe relevant Grant amount will be jointly provided by the Bank of Ceylon and the Department of Development Finance of the General Treasury to the selected researchers and entrepreneurs.\n\nAccordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. President to implement the proposed methodology for providing Grants to project proposals selected under the \u2018National Initiative for Research and Development Commercialization', was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-10-001-en",
