    "doc_id": "2025-11-10-011-en",
    "num": "11",
    "date_str": "2025-11-10",
    "description": "Annulment of the National Film Corporation of Sri Lanka Act, No.47 of 1971 and introduction of a new Act",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13560",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-10 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Almost five decades have lapsed since the establishment of the National Film Corporation and significant changes in the social, political and economic sectors as well as technology related to the film industry have occurred during that period. The need to revise the institutional structure and functions of the National Film Corporation to suit the present has been identified. An initial draft has been prepared regarding the structure and the functions of the National Cinema Council of Sri Lanka proposed to be established with the aim of creating a strategic direction in areas which are not covered by the National Film Corporation Act and carrying out the functions of film regulation and promotion of film culture. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to instruct the Legal Draftsman to prepare a Bill to repeal the Sri Lanka National Film Corporation Act No.47 of 1971 also incorporating the provisions for the establishment of the Sri Lanka National Film Council, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-10-012-en",
    "num": "12",
    "date_str": "2025-11-10",
    "description": "Amending the Universities Act, No.16 of 1978",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13561",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-10 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2025-06-16 to amend the Universities Act No.16 of 1978. Accordingly, the clearance of the Attorney General has been received for the Bill drafted by the Legal Draftsman. The proposed amendments to the Universities Act No.16 of 1978 will enable to create a merit-based selection process by expanding the criteria with regard to the qualifications for appointment to the post of Dean. The proposed amendments are intended to broaden the pool of eligible candidates for key academic administrative positions in the university system, thereby strengthening institutional governance. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Hon. Prime Minister, in her capacity as the Minister of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education, to publish the said Bill in the Government Gazette and thereafter present the same in Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-10-013-en",
    "num": "13",
    "date_str": "2025-11-10",
    "description": "Implementation of Pilot Demonstration Models in order to introduce Piped Irrigation Modalities as a novel approach for Sri Lanka\u2019s irrigation sector",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13562",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-10 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The persistent decline in crop yields due to prolonged droughts and the damages caused to the earthen canal systems as a result of increasing the intensity of rainfall have been identified as two major challenges faced by smallholder farmers in the dry zone of Sri Lanka. Therefore, it has been proposed to introduce piped irrigation water distribution systems instead of open type earthen canals which operate at low conveyance efficiency, as a solution to these challenges. Accordingly, a detailed technical study has been carried out to implement 04 pilot projects under 03 different piped irrigation modalities, covering an area of about 877 hectares, to demonstrate them as models. With the use of piped irrigation water distribution systems, it is expected to reduce the wastage of irrigation water from traditional open type canal irrigation systems, provide relief to farmers affected by water scarcity, direct smallholder farmers to high-value food crop cultivation, and increase women's participation in agriculture. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation to implement 03 pilot demonstration models in the Northwestern Province and another pilot demonstration model in the Uva Province, using the funds provided by the Japan Foundation for Prosperous and Resilient Asia and the Pacific (JFPR) for the benefit of the developing member countries of the Asian Development Bank and the funds amounting to USD 3.3 million provided\u00a0 by the Asian Development Bank and another USD 1.68 million of the Government of Sri Lanka, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-10-014-en",
    "num": "14",
    "date_str": "2025-11-10",
