    "description": "Completion of 74 bridges identified under the Rural Bridges Programme",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13568",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-17 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Cabinet, at its meeting held on 2021\u201102\u201108, has granted approval to award 326 contracts for the construction of bridges located island\u2011wide, to the State Development and Construction Corporation under the Rural Bridges Programme. It was decided in 2022 to stop the construction works of 184 bridges where constructions had not been commenced by then and construction works of 45 of the remaining 142 bridges have been completed by now. Works of another 23 bridges have been assigned to the Road Development Authority. The proposal made by the Minister of Transport, Highways and Urban Development to have the works of 74 remaining bridges initiated by the State Development and Construction Corporation and expeditiously complete the constructions thereof, with a view to alleviating the difficulties encountered by the public in the relevant areas, was approved by the Cabinet."
