    "date_str": "2025-11-24",
    "description": "Conducting remaining development activities of the Kelaniya Vidyalankara International Buddhist Conference Hall",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13584",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The Vidyalankara International Buddhist Conference Hall building has been constructed as a sponsorship contribution by the Government for the national, religious, social and educational mission carried out by the Vidyalankara Pirivena in this country. Approval has been granted at the Cabinet meeting held on 2025\u201106\u201123 to provide an amount of Rs.137.11 million for the year 2025, to restore the electric system of the said building. The restoration works of the electric system by the Central Engineering Consultancy Bureau, utilizing the said amount, is nearing completion, and it has been reported that there is a balance of the provisions allocated for that work. The proposal made by the Minister of Buddhasasana, Religious and Cultural Affairs to complete all other essential components of the said building, including the fire extinguisher system, air conditioner system, construction of the security fence, within this year by managing the balance provisions, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-24-009-en",
    "num": "9",
    "date_str": "2025-11-24",
    "description": "Construction of Norochcholai - Wariyapola Transmission Line and Wariyapola Switching Station",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13585",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Several Transmission Development projects have been identified in the 2025-2034 Long-Term Transmission Plan prepared by the Ceylon Electricity Board and are scheduled to be implemented on priority basis. The Norochcholai - Wariyapola Transmission Development Project has been identified as a priority project to be implemented to utilize the renewable energy sources in the North Western region of the country. It is estimated that there is a renewable energy potential of more than 750 MW in the North Western region, and the objectives of this proposed Transmission Development Project are to establish a main transmission network to facilitate the integration of the variable renewable energy sources in that region into the national grid and to reduce congestion in the transmission network by transmitting possible bulk electricity generation around Puttalam. The estimated cost for the construction under the proposed project is Rs.24.06 billion, and the Department of National Planning has recommended that the project be implemented within the medium-term budgetary framework. It is expected to secure necessary funds for the project from the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Energy to implement the Norochcholai \u2011 Wariyapola Transmission Development Project and to pursue action to secure funds required for the purpose from the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_cabinet_decisions",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-24-010-en",
    "num": "10",
    "date_str": "2025-11-24",
    "description": "Submission of the Registration and Licensing of Medicines (fees) Regulations, No.02 of 2017, as amended for approval of Parliament",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13586",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-11-24 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- The National Medicines Regulatory Authority Act, No.5 of 2015, provides for the Minister in charge of the subject to make Regulations in respect of the procedure and the manner in which any medicine, medical device or borderline product should be registered, the terms and conditions applicable to such registration and licensing, and the fees to be charged for such registration or licensing. It has been found necessary to revise the Registration and Licensing of Medicines (fees) Regulations due to the reasons such as, changes in economic and financial values \u200b\u200bthat have occurred in Sri Lanka after 2019, the introduction of new technologies and testing methods, the expansion of the range of regulatory services, the maintenance of transparency of the National Medicines Regulatory Authority and the protection of international equivalence. Accordingly, measures have been taken to publish the Registration and Licensing of Medicines (fees) Regulations, No.02 of 2017, as amended, published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2023/30 dated 2017\u201106\u201114 by further amending the same, having published through the Gazette Extraordinary Notification No.2452/39 dated 2025-09-04. The proposal made by the Minister of Health and Mass Media to submit the said amended Regulation as per the provisions of the National Medicines Regulatory Authority Act No. 5 of 2015, to Parliament for approval, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
