    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-12-10 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Although many countries interested in environmental conservation have assessed and accounted the natural capital values, Sri Lanka has not yet assessed or accounted the natural capital values properly and quantitatively. Approval from the Global Environment Facility has been received for the implementation of the project proposal titled 'Integrating Natural Capital Values \u200b\u200bin Coastal and Marine Ecosystems of Sri Lanka into Sustainable Development Planning' prepared by the International Union for Conservation of Nature and the Ministry of Environment, with the support of other stakeholders, under the Seventh Assistance Programme of the Global Environment Facility, taking into account the said situation. The activities of the said project have been planned to be implemented within a period of 04 years in the coastal areas identified in the districts of Galle, Mannar, Puttalam and Trincomalee, and a financial grant of USD 2.66 million is to be received for the same. Accordingly, the proposal made by the Minister of Environment to implement the said project using the financial grant provided by the Global Environment Facility and to sign the Memorandum of Understanding for the same between the Ministry of Environment and the International Union for Conservation of Nature, was approved by the Cabinet."
